window.TWG_S1C={"level":1,"track":"spirits","exam":{"questions":30,"minutes":45,"pass":70,"written":false,"tasting":false,"trueFalse":true},"ch":{"p1":{"it":"I quattro passaggi e gli alambicchi","fr":"Les quatre étapes et les alambics","en":"Four steps and two stills"},"p2":{"it":"Gusto, dolcezza e colore","fr":"Goût, douceur et couleur","en":"Flavour, sweetness and colour"},"s1":{"it":"Cognac","fr":"Cognac","en":"Cognac"},"s2":{"it":"Vodka","fr":"Vodka","en":"Vodka"},"s3":{"it":"Whisky scozzese","fr":"Whisky écossais","en":"Scotch whisky"},"s4":{"it":"Whiskey americano e altri whisky","fr":"Whiskey américain et autres whiskies","en":"American and other whiskies"},"s5":{"it":"Rum dei Caraibi","fr":"Rhum des Caraïbes","en":"Caribbean rum"},"s6":{"it":"Tequila","fr":"Tequila","en":"Tequila"},"s7":{"it":"Distillati aromatizzati e liquori","fr":"Spiritueux aromatisés et liqueurs","en":"Flavoured spirits and liqueurs"},"s8":{"it":"Vini aromatizzati","fr":"Vins aromatisés","en":"Aromatised wines"},"t1":{"it":"Degustare un distillato","fr":"Déguster un spiritueux","en":"Tasting a spirit"},"t2":{"it":"Il cocktail equilibrato","fr":"Le cocktail équilibré","en":"A balanced cocktail"},"t3":{"it":"Famiglie di cocktail","fr":"Familles de cocktails","en":"Cocktail families"}},"groups":[{"k":"p","w":5,"n":{"it":"Come si fa un distillato","fr":"Comment on fait un spiritueux","en":"How a spirit is made"},"c":["p1","p2"]},{"k":"s","w":20,"n":{"it":"Le grandi famiglie di distillati","fr":"Les grandes familles de spiritueux","en":"The main spirit families"},"c":["s1","s2","s3","s4","s5","s6","s7","s8"]},{"k":"t","w":5,"n":{"it":"Degustare e miscelare","fr":"Déguster et mélanger","en":"Taste and mix"},"c":["t1","t2","t3"]}],"bank":[{"id":"s1760c5f3","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Quale definizione descrive meglio un distillato?","Quelle définition décrit le mieux un spiritueux ?","Which definition best describes a spirit?"],"o":[["Una bevanda alcolica resa più forte dalla distillazione","Une boisson alcoolisée rendue plus forte par la distillation","An alcoholic drink made stronger by distillation"],["Una bevanda alcolica resa più forte dalla fermentazione","Une boisson alcoolisée rendue plus forte par la fermentation","An alcoholic drink made stronger by fermentation"],["Una bevanda alcolica sempre invecchiata in rovere","Une boisson alcoolisée toujours vieillie en fût de chêne","An alcoholic drink that is always aged in oak"],["Una bevanda alcolica a cui si aggiunge sempre zucchero","Une boisson alcoolisée à laquelle on ajoute toujours du sucre","An alcoholic drink that always has sugar added"]],"e":["È la distillazione ad alzare il grado alcolico e a trasformare un liquido fermentato in distillato.","C'est la distillation qui augmente le degré et transforme un liquide fermenté en spiritueux.","Distillation is what raises the alcohol level and turns a fermented liquid into a spirit."],"d":["La fermentazione crea l'alcol ma si ferma intorno all'8–10%: da sola dà una bevanda come vino o birra, non un distillato. Molti distillati non vedono mai il rovere, come la vodka, e la maggior parte non riceve zucchero. Solo la distillazione è comune a tutti.","La fermentation crée l'alcool mais s'arrête vers 8–10 % : seule, elle donne une boisson comme le vin ou la bière, pas un spiritueux. Beaucoup de spiritueux ne voient jamais le chêne, comme la vodka, et la plupart ne reçoivent pas de sucre. Seule la distillation est commune à tous.","Fermentation creates the alcohol but stops at around 8–10%: on its own it gives a drink like wine or beer, not a spirit. Many spirits, vodka for example, never see oak, and most receive no sugar. Only distillation is shared by every spirit."]},{"id":"s18d823af","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["In quale ordine avvengono le quattro tappe della produzione di un distillato?","Dans quel ordre se déroulent les quatre étapes de la production d'un spiritueux ?","In which order do the four steps of spirit production happen?"],"o":[["Materia prima, fermentazione, distillazione, fase finale","Matière première, fermentation, distillation, étape finale","Raw material, fermentation, distillation, post-distillation"],["Materia prima, distillazione, fermentazione, fase finale","Matière première, distillation, fermentation, étape finale","Raw material, distillation, fermentation, post-distillation"],["Fermentazione, materia prima, distillazione, fase finale","Fermentation, matière première, distillation, étape finale","Fermentation, raw material, distillation, post-distillation"],["Materia prima, fase finale, fermentazione, distillazione","Matière première, étape finale, fermentation, distillation","Raw material, post-distillation, fermentation, distillation"]],"e":["Prima si ottiene un liquido zuccherino, poi lo si fa fermentare, lo si distilla e infine lo si rifinisce.","On obtient d'abord un liquide sucré, puis on le fait fermenter, on le distille et enfin on le finit.","First a sugary liquid is made, then fermented, then distilled, and finally finished."],"d":["La distillazione ha bisogno di un liquido che contenga già alcol, quindi non può precedere la fermentazione. E la fermentazione ha bisogno di zucchero, che arriva dalla materia prima lavorata. Invecchiamento, dolcificazione o diluizione arrivano solo dopo che il distillato è uscito dall'alambicco.","La distillation a besoin d'un liquide qui contient déjà de l'alcool : elle ne peut donc pas précéder la fermentation. Et la fermentation a besoin de sucre, qui vient de la matière première transformée. Vieillissement, sucrage ou dilution n'arrivent qu'une fois l'eau-de-vie sortie de l'alambic.","Distillation needs a liquid that already contains alcohol, so it cannot come before fermentation. Fermentation, in turn, needs sugar, which comes from the processed raw material. Ageing, sweetening or dilution only happen once the spirit has left the still."]},{"id":"s17ac77b2","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Qual è lo scopo principale della lavorazione della materia prima?","Quel est le but principal de la transformation de la matière première ?","What is the main aim of processing the raw material?"],"o":[["Ottenere un liquido zuccherino che possa fermentare","Obtenir un liquide sucré qui pourra fermenter","To create a sugary liquid that can ferment"],["Ottenere un liquido già alcolico da distillare","Obtenir un liquide déjà alcoolisé à distiller","To create an already alcoholic liquid for distilling"],["Togliere tutti gli aromi della pianta","Retirer tous les arômes de la plante","To remove all the plant's aromas"],["Dare colore al futuro distillato","Donner de la couleur au futur spiritueux","To give colour to the future spirit"]],"e":["Senza un liquido zuccherino i lieviti non hanno nulla da trasformare in alcol.","Sans liquide sucré, les levures n'ont rien à transformer en alcool.","Without a sugary liquid, yeast has nothing to turn into alcohol."],"d":["L'alcol arriva solo con la fermentazione, la tappa successiva. Gli aromi della materia prima non si eliminano: anzi, ogni pianta lascia la sua impronta nel distillato. Il colore, quando c'è, si decide molto più tardi, dopo la distillazione.","L'alcool n'apparaît qu'avec la fermentation, l'étape suivante. Les arômes de la matière première ne sont pas supprimés : chaque plante laisse au contraire son empreinte dans le spiritueux. La couleur, quand il y en a, se décide bien plus tard, après la distillation.","Alcohol only appears with fermentation, the next step. The raw material's aromas are not removed: on the contrary, each plant leaves its mark on the spirit. Colour, when there is any, is decided much later, after distillation."]},{"id":"s16adfb67","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Quale affermazione sulle materie prime dei distillati è corretta?","Quelle affirmation sur les matières premières des spiritueux est correcte ?","Which statement about the raw materials for spirits is correct?"],"o":[["Devono essere di origine vegetale","Elles doivent être d'origine végétale","They must be of plant origin"],["Devono essere per forza cereali","Ce doivent obligatoirement être des céréales","They must always be cereals"],["Devono contenere zucchero già pronto","Elles doivent contenir du sucre déjà prêt","They must already contain ready sugar"],["Devono crescere in un clima caldo","Elles doivent pousser sous un climat chaud","They must grow in a hot climate"]],"e":["Qualsiasi pianta può in teoria servire, ma deve trattarsi di un vegetale.","En théorie n'importe quelle plante peut servir, mais il doit s'agir d'un végétal.","In theory any plant can be used, but it has to be a plant."],"d":["Uva, canna da zucchero, agave e patate mostrano che i cereali non sono l'unica scelta. Alcune piante, come i cereali, non contengono zucchero e vanno lavorate per crearlo, quindi lo zucchero già pronto non è obbligatorio. Il clima caldo serve alla canna da zucchero, non a tutte le materie prime.","Raisin, canne à sucre, agave et pommes de terre montrent que les céréales ne sont pas le seul choix. Certaines plantes, comme les céréales, ne contiennent pas de sucre et doivent être transformées pour en créer : le sucre tout prêt n'est donc pas obligatoire. Le climat chaud convient à la canne à sucre, pas à toutes les matières premières.","Grapes, sugar cane, agave and potatoes show that cereals are not the only option. Some plants, cereals among them, contain no sugar and must be processed to create it, so ready-made sugar is not a requirement. A hot climate suits sugar cane, not every raw material."]},{"id":"s157c0105","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Un distillatore lavora con una materia prima che non contiene zucchero. Che cosa deve fare?","Un distillateur travaille une matière première qui ne contient pas de sucre. Que doit-il faire ?","A distiller is using a raw material that contains no sugar. What must happen?"],"o":[["Lavorarla per creare zucchero prima della fermentazione","La transformer pour créer du sucre avant la fermentation","Process it to create sugar before fermentation"],["Distillarla direttamente senza fermentarla","La distiller directement sans la faire fermenter","Distil it directly without fermenting it"],["Aggiungere più lieviti, che sostituiscono lo zucchero","Ajouter plus de levures, qui remplacent le sucre","Add extra yeast, which replaces the sugar"],["Invecchiarla in rovere per sviluppare zucchero","La vieillir en fût de chêne pour développer du sucre","Age it in oak so it develops sugar"]],"e":["La fermentazione richiede zucchero, quindi va creato dalla materia prima stessa.","La fermentation exige du sucre : il faut donc le créer à partir de la matière première elle-même.","Fermentation needs sugar, so it has to be created from the raw material itself."],"d":["Senza fermentazione non c'è alcol da concentrare, quindi distillare subito non avrebbe senso. I lieviti non sostituiscono lo zucchero: lo mangiano. Il rovere arriva dopo la distillazione e non crea zucchero da fermentare.","Sans fermentation, il n'y a pas d'alcool à concentrer : distiller tout de suite n'aurait aucun sens. Les levures ne remplacent pas le sucre, elles le consomment. Le chêne intervient après la distillation et ne crée pas de sucre à fermenter.","Without fermentation there is no alcohol to concentrate, so distilling straight away would make no sense. Yeast does not replace sugar: it eats it. Oak comes after distillation and creates no sugar to ferment."]},{"id":"s1860890c","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Durante la fermentazione i lieviti trasformano lo zucchero in…","Pendant la fermentation, les levures transforment le sucre en…","During fermentation, yeast turns sugar into…"],"o":[["etanolo e anidride carbonica","éthanol et dioxyde de carbone","ethanol and carbon dioxide"],["etanolo e acqua pura","éthanol et eau pure","ethanol and pure water"],["anidride carbonica e caramello","dioxyde de carbone et caramel","carbon dioxide and caramel"],["amido e ossigeno","amidon et oxygène","starch and oxygen"]],"e":["I lieviti producono l'alcol che serve, l'etanolo, e un gas di scarto, l'anidride carbonica.","Les levures produisent l'alcool recherché, l'éthanol, et un gaz de déchet, le dioxyde de carbone.","Yeast produces the alcohol that is wanted, ethanol, and a waste gas, carbon dioxide."],"d":["L'acqua è già presente nel liquido zuccherino, non la creano i lieviti. Il caramello è un colorante che si aggiunge eventualmente alla fine. L'amido è ciò che alcuni cereali contengono prima di essere trasformati in zucchero: è un punto di partenza, non un risultato.","L'eau est déjà présente dans le liquide sucré, ce ne sont pas les levures qui la créent. Le caramel est un colorant éventuellement ajouté à la fin. L'amidon est ce que contiennent certaines céréales avant d'être transformées en sucre : c'est un point de départ, pas un résultat.","Water is already in the sugary liquid; yeast does not create it. Caramel is a colouring that may be added at the very end. Starch is what some cereals contain before it is turned into sugar: a starting point, not a product."]},{"id":"s16b85152","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Quale grado alcolico ha di solito un liquido appena fermentato?","Quel degré a généralement un liquide qui vient de fermenter ?","What strength does a freshly fermented liquid usually have?"],"o":[["Tra l'8% e il 10% vol.","Entre 8 % et 10 % vol.","Between 8% and 10% abv"],["Tra il 25% e il 30% vol.","Entre 25 % et 30 % vol.","Between 25% and 30% abv"],["Circa il 40% vol.","Environ 40 % vol.","About 40% abv"],["Tra l'1% e il 2% vol.","Entre 1 % et 2 % vol.","Between 1% and 2% abv"]],"e":["La fermentazione dà un liquido debole, intorno all'8–10%, che la distillazione renderà più forte.","La fermentation donne un liquide faible, autour de 8–10 %, que la distillation rendra plus fort.","Fermentation gives a weak liquid of around 8–10%, which distillation will then make stronger."],"d":["Circa il 25% è il grado tipico dopo la prima passata in un alambicco discontinuo, non dopo la fermentazione. Il 40% è il grado più comune in bottiglia, ottenuto diluendo il distillato. L'1–2% sarebbe troppo poco: i lieviti producono molto più alcol di così.","Environ 25 % est le degré typique après le premier passage dans un alambic à repasse, pas après la fermentation. 40 % est le degré le plus courant en bouteille, obtenu en diluant l'eau-de-vie. 1–2 % serait trop peu : les levures produisent bien plus d'alcool.","About 25% is typical after the first pass through a pot still, not after fermentation. 40% is the most common bottling strength, reached by diluting the spirit. 1–2% would be far too low: yeast produces much more alcohol than that."]},{"id":"s11aaea89","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Oltre all'alcol, che cosa aggiunge la fermentazione al futuro distillato?","En plus de l'alcool, qu'apporte la fermentation au futur spiritueux ?","Apart from alcohol, what does fermentation add to the future spirit?"],"o":[["Nuovi aromi, soprattutto fruttati","De nouveaux arômes, surtout fruités","New aromas, especially fruity ones"],["Aromi di vaniglia e di cocco","Des arômes de vanille et de noix de coco","Vanilla and coconut aromas"],["Un colore dorato","Une couleur dorée","A golden colour"],["Dolcezza che resta nel distillato","Une douceur qui reste dans le spiritueux","Sweetness that stays in the spirit"]],"e":["I lieviti, oltre all'alcol, creano aromi, in particolare fruttati.","En plus de l'alcool, les levures créent des arômes, en particulier fruités.","Besides alcohol, yeast creates aromas, fruity ones in particular."],"d":["Vaniglia e cocco sono aromi tipici del rovere, quindi arrivano con l'invecchiamento. Anche il colore dorato viene dal rovere o dal caramello. I lieviti consumano lo zucchero, e comunque ogni distillato appena fatto è secco: la dolcezza si aggiunge solo dopo.","Vanille et noix de coco sont des arômes typiques du chêne : ils viennent du vieillissement. La couleur dorée vient elle aussi du chêne ou du caramel. Les levures consomment le sucre, et de toute façon toute eau-de-vie qui vient d'être distillée est sèche : la douceur s'ajoute seulement après.","Vanilla and coconut are typical oak aromas, so they come from ageing. A golden colour also comes from oak or caramel. Yeast eats the sugar, and in any case every newly made spirit is dry: sweetness can only be added later."]},{"id":"s14cf2c14","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Qual è lo scopo principale della distillazione?","Quel est le but principal de la distillation ?","What is the main aim of distillation?"],"o":[["Concentrare l'etanolo del liquido fermentato","Concentrer l'éthanol du liquide fermenté","To concentrate the ethanol in the fermented liquid"],["Trasformare lo zucchero in alcol","Transformer le sucre en alcool","To turn sugar into alcohol"],["Dare colore e aromi di legno","Donner de la couleur et des arômes de bois","To add colour and woody aromas"],["Abbassare il grado per renderlo bevibile","Baisser le degré pour le rendre buvable","To lower the strength so it is drinkable"]],"e":["La distillazione separa e concentra l'alcol già creato dalla fermentazione.","La distillation sépare et concentre l'alcool déjà créé par la fermentation.","Distillation separates and concentrates the alcohol that fermentation has already created."],"d":["Trasformare lo zucchero in alcol è il lavoro dei lieviti, durante la fermentazione. Colore e aromi di legno arrivano con il rovere, dopo la distillazione. Abbassare il grado è invece il compito della diluizione con acqua prima dell'imbottigliamento: l'esatto contrario della distillazione.","Transformer le sucre en alcool est le travail des levures pendant la fermentation. La couleur et les arômes boisés viennent du chêne, après la distillation. Baisser le degré est le rôle de la dilution avant la mise en bouteille : exactement le contraire de la distillation.","Turning sugar into alcohol is yeast's job, during fermentation. Colour and woody aromas come from oak, after distillation. Lowering the strength is the role of dilution with water before bottling: the exact opposite of distillation."]},{"id":"s160a4af2","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Perché scaldando un liquido fermentato si possono raccogliere vapori più alcolici?","Pourquoi, en chauffant un liquide fermenté, recueille-t-on des vapeurs plus alcoolisées ?","Why does heating a fermented liquid give vapours that are richer in alcohol?"],"o":[["Perché l'etanolo bolle a una temperatura più bassa dell'acqua","Parce que l'éthanol bout à une température plus basse que l'eau","Because ethanol boils at a lower temperature than water"],["Perché l'acqua bolle a una temperatura più bassa dell'etanolo","Parce que l'eau bout à une température plus basse que l'éthanol","Because water boils at a lower temperature than ethanol"],["Perché il calore trasforma lo zucchero rimasto in alcol","Parce que la chaleur transforme le sucre restant en alcool","Because heat turns the remaining sugar into alcohol"],["Perché il condensatore aggiunge alcol ai vapori","Parce que le condenseur ajoute de l'alcool aux vapeurs","Because the condenser adds alcohol to the vapours"]],"e":["Bollendo prima, l'etanolo passa nei vapori in proporzione maggiore rispetto all'acqua.","Comme il bout plus tôt, l'éthanol passe dans les vapeurs en plus grande proportion que l'eau.","Because it boils first, ethanol makes up a bigger share of the vapours than water does."],"d":["Se l'acqua bollisse prima, i vapori sarebbero più acquosi, non più alcolici. Il calore non crea nuovo alcol: l'alcol nasce solo con i lieviti. Il condensatore si limita a raffreddare i vapori e a farli tornare liquidi.","Si l'eau bouillait la première, les vapeurs seraient plus aqueuses, pas plus alcoolisées. La chaleur ne crée pas d'alcool : l'alcool ne naît que grâce aux levures. Le condenseur se contente de refroidir les vapeurs pour les faire redevenir liquides.","If water boiled first, the vapours would be more watery, not more alcoholic. Heat creates no new alcohol: alcohol only comes from yeast. The condenser simply cools the vapours so they turn back into liquid."]},{"id":"s1a3956e6","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Su un'etichetta si legge 40% vol. Che cosa significa?","Une étiquette indique 40 % vol. Qu'est-ce que cela signifie ?","A label reads 40% abv. What does this mean?"],"o":[["Che il 40% del liquido è alcol","Que 40 % du liquide est de l'alcool","That 40% of the liquid is alcohol"],["Che il 40% del liquido è zucchero","Que 40 % du liquide est du sucre","That 40% of the liquid is sugar"],["Che il distillato ha 40 mesi di invecchiamento","Que le spiritueux a vieilli 40 mois","That the spirit has been aged for 40 months"],["Che il 40% del liquido è acqua","Que 40 % du liquide est de l'eau","That 40% of the liquid is water"]],"e":["La sigla indica la percentuale di alcol presente nel volume del liquido.","La mention indique le pourcentage d'alcool contenu dans le volume du liquide.","The abbreviation gives the percentage of alcohol in the volume of liquid."],"d":["Il grado misura l'alcol, non lo zucchero né l'età. Se il 40% è alcol, la parte restante, circa il 60%, è soprattutto acqua: per questo l'ultima opzione inverte i conti.","Le degré mesure l'alcool, pas le sucre ni l'âge. Si 40 % est de l'alcool, le reste, environ 60 %, est surtout de l'eau : la dernière option inverse donc les chiffres.","The figure measures alcohol, not sugar or age. If 40% is alcohol, the rest, around 60%, is mostly water, so the last option gets the numbers the wrong way round."]},{"id":"s14589871","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Che legame c'è tra il grado di distillazione e l'intensità aromatica?","Quel lien y a-t-il entre le degré de distillation et l'intensité aromatique ?","How is distillation strength linked to aroma intensity?"],"o":[["Più il grado è basso, più gli aromi sono intensi","Plus le degré est bas, plus les arômes sont intenses","The lower the strength, the more intense the aromas"],["Più il grado è alto, più gli aromi sono intensi","Plus le degré est élevé, plus les arômes sont intenses","The higher the strength, the more intense the aromas"],["Il grado non influisce sugli aromi","Le degré n'a aucun effet sur les arômes","Strength has no effect on aromas"],["Solo il grado in bottiglia influisce sugli aromi","Seul le degré en bouteille influe sur les arômes","Only the bottling strength affects the aromas"]],"e":["Distillando a grado basso si conservano più aromi; a grado alto se ne perdono.","En distillant à bas degré on garde plus d'arômes ; à haut degré on en perd.","Distilling to a low strength keeps more aromas; distilling to a high strength strips them away."],"d":["Il rapporto è inverso: un distillato a 96% è così povero di aromi da essere detto neutro. Il grado di distillazione è quindi decisivo. La diluizione prima dell'imbottigliamento usa acqua pura e non aggiunge aromi: lo stile si decide prima, nell'alambicco.","Le rapport est inverse : une eau-de-vie à 96 % est si pauvre en arômes qu'on la dit neutre. Le degré de distillation est donc décisif. La dilution avant la mise en bouteille utilise de l'eau pure et n'ajoute aucun arôme : le style se décide avant, dans l'alambic.","The link is inverse: a spirit at 96% abv is so low in aroma that it is called neutral, so distillation strength clearly matters. Dilution before bottling uses pure water and adds no aroma: the style is set earlier, in the still."]},{"id":"s146cb7dc","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Come si chiama un distillato portato al 96% vol. e quasi privo di aromi?","Comment appelle-t-on une eau-de-vie distillée à 96 % vol. et presque sans arômes ?","What is a spirit distilled to 96% abv, with almost no aroma, called?"],"o":[["Neutro","Neutre","Neutral"],["Aromatizzato","Aromatisé","Flavoured"],["Invecchiato","Vieilli","Aged"],["Liquore","Liqueur","Liqueur"]],"e":["A quel grado resta così poco aroma che il distillato si definisce neutro.","À ce degré il reste si peu d'arômes que l'eau-de-vie est dite neutre.","At that strength so little aroma remains that the spirit is called neutral."],"d":["Un distillato aromatizzato ha ricevuto aromi aggiunti, e un liquore è anche dolcificato: entrambe cose che avvengono dopo la distillazione. Invecchiato indica il passaggio in rovere, che aggiunge aromi invece di toglierli.","Un spiritueux aromatisé a reçu des arômes ajoutés, et une liqueur est en plus sucrée : deux choses qui se font après la distillation. Vieilli indique un passage en fût de chêne, qui ajoute des arômes au lieu d'en retirer.","A flavoured spirit has had flavours added, and a liqueur has been sweetened as well: both happen after distillation. Aged means time in oak, which adds aromas rather than removing them."]},{"id":"s16395d56","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Entro quale intervallo varia il grado di un distillato appena uscito dall'alambicco?","Dans quelle fourchette varie le degré d'une eau-de-vie qui sort de l'alambic ?","Within what range does the strength of a newly made spirit vary?"],"o":[["Da circa il 60% al 96% vol.","D'environ 60 % à 96 % vol.","From about 60% to 96% abv"],["Da circa il 40% al 60% vol.","D'environ 40 % à 60 % vol.","From about 40% to 60% abv"],["Da circa l'8% al 40% vol.","D'environ 8 % à 40 % vol.","From about 8% to 40% abv"],["Da circa il 90% al 100% vol.","D'environ 90 % à 100 % vol.","From about 90% to 100% abv"]],"e":["I distillati appena fatti vanno da circa il 60%, i più aromatici, al 96%, i neutri.","Les eaux-de-vie qui viennent d'être distillées vont d'environ 60 %, les plus aromatiques, à 96 %, les neutres.","Newly made spirits run from about 60%, the most aromatic, up to 96%, the neutral ones."],"d":["Il 40% è il grado tipico in bottiglia, dopo la diluizione, non all'uscita dall'alambicco. L'8–10% è il grado del liquido fermentato, prima della distillazione. Il 96% è il massimo: il 100% non si raggiunge, e molti distillati aromatici escono ben al di sotto del 90%.","40 % est le degré typique en bouteille, après dilution, pas à la sortie de l'alambic. 8–10 % est le degré du liquide fermenté, avant la distillation. 96 % est le maximum : on n'atteint pas 100 %, et beaucoup d'eaux-de-vie aromatiques sortent bien en dessous de 90 %.","40% is the usual bottling strength after dilution, not the strength leaving the still. 8–10% is the fermented liquid, before distillation. 96% is the ceiling: 100% is not reached, and many aromatic spirits come off the still well below 90%."]},{"id":"s1f3d9d79","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Quale affermazione sull'alambicco discontinuo è corretta?","Quelle affirmation sur l'alambic à repasse est correcte ?","Which statement about the pot still is correct?"],"o":[["Va svuotato e pulito dopo ogni distillazione","Il faut le vider et le nettoyer après chaque distillation","It must be emptied and cleaned after each distillation"],["Può funzionare in continuo senza mai fermarsi","Il peut fonctionner en continu sans jamais s'arrêter","It can run continuously without ever stopping"],["Produce facilmente distillati neutri al 96%","Il produit facilement des eaux-de-vie neutres à 96 %","It easily produces neutral spirits at 96% abv"],["È una struttura verticale divisa in molti piani","C'est une structure verticale divisée en nombreux plateaux","It is a vertical structure divided into many sections"]],"e":["L'alambicco discontinuo lavora a lotti: finito un lotto, si svuota e si pulisce.","L'alambic à repasse travaille par lots : une fois le lot terminé, on le vide et on le nettoie.","A pot still works in batches: once a batch is finished, it is emptied and cleaned."],"d":["Il funzionamento continuo, i gradi neutri e la struttura verticale a piani sono tutte caratteristiche della colonna. L'alambicco discontinuo, per quante volte si distilli, non arriva mai a un distillato neutro ad altissimo grado.","Le fonctionnement continu, les degrés neutres et la structure verticale à plateaux sont des caractéristiques de la colonne. L'alambic à repasse, même avec de nombreuses distillations, n'arrive jamais à une eau-de-vie neutre à très haut degré.","Continuous running, neutral strengths and a tall structure divided into sections all describe the column still. However many times it is used, a pot still never reaches a very high-strength neutral spirit."]},{"id":"s1d56c049","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["In una doppia distillazione in alambicco discontinuo, quale sequenza di gradi è la più realistica?","Lors d'une double distillation à l'alambic à repasse, quelle suite de degrés est la plus réaliste ?","In double pot still distillation, which sequence of strengths is most realistic?"],"o":[["Circa 10% → circa 25% → circa 75%","Environ 10 % → environ 25 % → environ 75 %","About 10% → about 25% → about 75%"],["Circa 10% → circa 40% → circa 96%","Environ 10 % → environ 40 % → environ 96 %","About 10% → about 40% → about 96%"],["Circa 25% → circa 50% → circa 75%","Environ 25 % → environ 50 % → environ 75 %","About 25% → about 50% → about 75%"],["Circa 2% → circa 10% → circa 40%","Environ 2 % → environ 10 % → environ 40 %","About 2% → about 10% → about 40%"]],"e":["Si parte da un liquido fermentato di circa il 10%, si sale a circa il 25% e poi a circa il 75%.","On part d'un liquide fermenté d'environ 10 %, on monte à environ 25 %, puis à environ 75 %.","It starts from a fermented liquid of about 10%, rises to about 25%, then to about 75%."],"d":["Un alambicco discontinuo non può arrivare al 96%: quel grado è tipico delle colonne più alte. Il liquido di partenza non è al 25%, perché la fermentazione si ferma intorno all'8–10%. E un risultato finale al 40% corrisponde al grado di imbottigliamento, non a un distillato appena fatto.","Un alambic à repasse ne peut pas atteindre 96 % : ce degré est typique des colonnes les plus hautes. Le liquide de départ n'est pas à 25 %, car la fermentation s'arrête vers 8–10 %. Et 40 % en fin de parcours correspond au degré de mise en bouteille, pas à une eau-de-vie qui sort de l'alambic.","A pot still cannot reach 96%: that strength is typical of the tallest column stills. The starting liquid is not 25%, since fermentation stops around 8–10%. And finishing at 40% matches bottling strength, not a newly made spirit."]},{"id":"s1f56264a","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["In un alambicco discontinuo, quale parte riporta i vapori allo stato liquido?","Dans un alambic à repasse, quelle partie refait passer les vapeurs à l'état liquide ?","In a pot still, which part turns the vapours back into liquid?"],"o":[["Il condensatore","Le condenseur","The condenser"],["La caldaia","La chaudière","The pot"],["La fonte di calore","La source de chaleur","The heat source"],["Il collo dell'alambicco","Le chapiteau","The still head"]],"e":["Nel condensatore i vapori passano in una serpentina raffreddata e tornano liquidi.","Dans le condenseur, les vapeurs traversent un serpentin refroidi et redeviennent liquides.","In the condenser, the vapours pass through a cooled coil and become liquid again."],"d":["La caldaia contiene il liquido da distillare e la fonte di calore lo fa bollire: entrambe creano i vapori, non li raffreddano. Il collo dell'alambicco serve solo a far salire i vapori verso il condensatore.","La chaudière contient le liquide à distiller et la source de chaleur le fait bouillir : toutes deux créent les vapeurs, elles ne les refroidissent pas. Le chapiteau sert seulement à faire monter les vapeurs vers le condenseur.","The pot holds the liquid and the heat source boils it: both create the vapours rather than cooling them. The still head simply carries the rising vapours towards the condenser."]},{"id":"s1d6261cf","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Quali due esigenze hanno portato all'invenzione dell'alambicco a colonna?","Quels deux besoins ont conduit à l'invention de la colonne à distiller ?","Which two needs led to the invention of the column still?"],"o":[["Lavorare in continuo e raggiungere gradi molto alti","Travailler en continu et atteindre des degrés très élevés","Running continuously and reaching very high strengths"],["Lavorare a lotti e ottenere più aromi","Travailler par lots et obtenir plus d'arômes","Working in batches and getting more aroma"],["Invecchiare più in fretta e colorare il distillato","Vieillir plus vite et colorer l'eau-de-vie","Ageing faster and colouring the spirit"],["Fermentare e distillare nello stesso recipiente","Fermenter et distiller dans le même récipient","Fermenting and distilling in the same vessel"]],"e":["L'alambicco discontinuo si ferma a ogni lotto e non arriva a gradi alti: la colonna risolve entrambi i limiti.","L'alambic à repasse s'arrête à chaque lot et n'atteint pas les hauts degrés : la colonne règle ces deux limites.","The pot still stops after every batch and cannot reach high strengths: the column solves both limits."],"d":["Lavorare a lotti è proprio il limite dell'alambicco discontinuo, e una colonna alta dà meno aromi, non di più. La colonna non ha nulla a che fare con l'invecchiamento o il colore, che arrivano dopo. La fermentazione resta una tappa separata, che precede la distillazione.","Le travail par lots est justement la limite de l'alambic à repasse, et une colonne haute donne moins d'arômes, pas plus. La colonne n'a rien à voir avec le vieillissement ou la couleur, qui viennent après. La fermentation reste une étape distincte, avant la distillation.","Working in batches is exactly the pot still's limitation, and a tall column gives less aroma, not more. The column has nothing to do with ageing or colour, which come later. Fermentation remains a separate step before distillation."]},{"id":"s1c569041","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["In un alambicco a colonna, dove si trova il liquido con il grado alcolico più alto?","Dans une colonne à distiller, où se trouve le liquide le plus alcoolisé ?","In a column still, where is the liquid with the highest alcohol level?"],"o":[["Sul piano più alto","Sur le plateau le plus haut","On the top section"],["Sul piano più basso","Sur le plateau le plus bas","On the bottom section"],["A metà colonna","Au milieu de la colonne","Halfway up the column"],["È uguale su tutti i piani","Il est identique sur tous les plateaux","It is the same on every section"]],"e":["Più il vapore sale, più si arricchisce di alcol: il piano più alto è il più forte.","Plus la vapeur monte, plus elle s'enrichit en alcool : le plateau du haut est le plus fort.","The higher the vapour rises, the richer in alcohol it gets: the top section is the strongest."],"d":["Il piano più basso, dove entra il vapore caldo, contiene al contrario il liquido meno alcolico. Il grado non è uniforme né si ferma a metà: cresce gradualmente salendo, ed è per questo che il distillato esce dall'alto.","Le plateau du bas, où entre la vapeur chaude, contient au contraire le liquide le moins alcoolisé. Le degré n'est ni uniforme ni maximal au milieu : il augmente progressivement en montant, et c'est pourquoi l'eau-de-vie sort par le haut.","The bottom section, where hot vapour enters, holds the weakest liquid. Strength is neither uniform nor highest in the middle: it rises step by step, which is why the spirit leaves from the top."]},{"id":"s1f3f94cf","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Un distillatore vuole lavorare in continuo ma ottenere un distillato con aromi medi o pronunciati, simile a quello di un alambicco discontinuo. Che cosa sceglie?","Un distillateur veut travailler en continu mais obtenir une eau-de-vie aux arômes moyens ou prononcés, proche de celle d'un alambic à repasse. Que choisit-il ?","A distiller wants continuous production but a spirit with medium or pronounced aromas, similar to a pot still spirit. What should be chosen?"],"o":[["Una colonna corta con pochi piani","Une colonne courte avec peu de plateaux","A short column with few sections"],["Una colonna molto alta con molti piani","Une colonne très haute avec beaucoup de plateaux","A very tall column with many sections"],["Un alambicco discontinuo usato tre volte","Un alambic à repasse utilisé trois fois","A pot still used three times"],["Una colonna alta e poi la diluizione con acqua","Une colonne haute puis une dilution à l'eau","A tall column followed by dilution with water"]],"e":["Una colonna corta lavora in continuo ma si ferma a un grado più basso, conservando aromi.","Une colonne courte travaille en continu mais s'arrête à un degré plus bas, en gardant des arômes.","A short column runs continuously but stops at a lower strength, keeping aromas."],"d":["Una colonna molto alta raggiunge gradi elevati e dà distillati leggeri o neutri. L'alambicco discontinuo lavora a lotti, quindi non risponde all'esigenza di continuità. Diluire con acqua abbassa il grado ma non riporta aromi: l'acqua usata è pura e non aggiunge gusto.","Une colonne très haute atteint des degrés élevés et donne des eaux-de-vie légères ou neutres. L'alambic à repasse travaille par lots : il ne répond pas au besoin de continuité. Diluer à l'eau baisse le degré mais ne rend pas d'arômes : l'eau utilisée est pure et n'ajoute aucun goût.","A very tall column reaches high strengths and gives light or neutral spirits. A pot still works in batches, so it does not meet the need for continuous production. Diluting with water lowers the strength but brings back no aroma: the water is pure and adds no flavour."]},{"id":"s1d0555bf","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Un produttore deve ottenere un distillato al 95% vol. Quale attrezzatura serve?","Un producteur doit obtenir une eau-de-vie à 95 % vol. De quel équipement a-t-il besoin ?","A producer needs a spirit at 95% abv. Which equipment is required?"],"o":[["Un alambicco a colonna molto alto","Une colonne à distiller très haute","A very tall column still"],["Un alambicco discontinuo e una doppia distillazione","Un alambic à repasse et une double distillation","A pot still and double distillation"],["Una colonna corta con pochi piani","Une colonne courte avec peu de plateaux","A short column with few sections"],["Una lunga fermentazione con molti lieviti","Une longue fermentation avec beaucoup de levures","A long fermentation with lots of yeast"]],"e":["Solo le colonne più alte, con il maggior numero di piani, arrivano al 95–96%.","Seules les colonnes les plus hautes, avec le plus de plateaux, atteignent 95–96 %.","Only the tallest columns, with the most sections, reach 95–96% abv."],"d":["La doppia distillazione in alambicco discontinuo si ferma intorno al 75%, e nessun numero di passaggi porta a un distillato neutro. Una colonna corta dà distillati di grado più basso e più aromatici. La fermentazione, per quanto lunga, non supera l'8–10% circa.","La double distillation à l'alambic à repasse s'arrête autour de 75 %, et aucun nombre de passages ne mène à une eau-de-vie neutre. Une colonne courte donne des eaux-de-vie plus basses en degré et plus aromatiques. La fermentation, même longue, ne dépasse guère 8–10 %.","Double pot still distillation stops at around 75%, and no number of passes will produce a neutral spirit. A short column gives lower-strength, more aromatic spirits. Fermentation, however long, only reaches around 8–10%."]},{"id":"s1d397e44","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Perché la maggior parte di chi usa l'alambicco discontinuo distilla due volte?","Pourquoi la plupart des utilisateurs d'alambic à repasse distillent-ils deux fois ?","Why do most pot still distillers distil twice?"],"o":[["Perché un solo passaggio non basta a ottenere un distillato","Parce qu'un seul passage ne suffit pas pour obtenir un spiritueux","Because a single pass is not enough to make a spirit"],["Perché la seconda passata rende il distillato neutro","Parce que le second passage rend l'eau-de-vie neutre","Because the second pass makes the spirit neutral"],["Perché la prima passata serve solo a pulire l'alambicco","Parce que le premier passage sert seulement à nettoyer l'alambic","Because the first pass only cleans the still"],["Perché la seconda passata aggiunge zucchero e colore","Parce que le second passage ajoute du sucre et de la couleur","Because the second pass adds sugar and colour"]],"e":["Dal liquido fermentato, una passata arriva solo a circa il 25%: serve la seconda per avere un distillato.","À partir du liquide fermenté, un passage n'atteint qu'environ 25 % : il en faut un second pour obtenir un spiritueux.","From the fermented liquid, one pass only reaches about 25%: a second is needed to make a spirit."],"d":["Anche dopo due passate il distillato resta intorno al 75% e pieno di carattere: non diventa neutro. La pulizia si fa tra un lotto e l'altro, non con una distillazione. E ogni distillato esce incolore e secco: zucchero e colore si aggiungono solo dopo, se si vuole.","Même après deux passages, l'eau-de-vie reste autour de 75 % et pleine de caractère : elle ne devient pas neutre. Le nettoyage se fait entre deux lots, pas par une distillation. Et toute eau-de-vie sort incolore et sèche : sucre et couleur ne s'ajoutent qu'ensuite, si on le souhaite.","Even after two passes the spirit stays around 75% and full of character: it does not become neutral. Cleaning happens between batches, not through a distillation. And every spirit leaves the still colourless and dry: sugar and colour can only be added afterwards."]},{"id":"s194565e9","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Com'è un distillato appena uscito dall'alambicco?","Comment est une eau-de-vie qui vient de sortir de l'alambic ?","What is a newly made spirit like as it leaves the still?"],"o":[["Incolore e secco","Incolore et sèche","Colourless and dry"],["Dorato e secco","Dorée et sèche","Golden and dry"],["Incolore e leggermente dolce","Incolore et légèrement sucrée","Colourless and slightly sweet"],["Ambrato e dolce","Ambrée et sucrée","Amber and sweet"]],"e":["Ogni distillato nasce trasparente e senza zucchero; colore e dolcezza arrivano solo dopo.","Toute eau-de-vie naît transparente et sans sucre ; couleur et douceur n'arrivent qu'après.","Every spirit is born clear and sugar-free; colour and sweetness only come later."],"d":["Il colore dorato o ambrato viene dal rovere o dal caramello, quindi dalla fase dopo la distillazione. Lo zucchero non passa con i vapori nell'alambicco: per questo qualsiasi dolcezza deve essere aggiunta in seguito.","La couleur dorée ou ambrée vient du chêne ou du caramel, donc de l'étape après la distillation. Le sucre ne passe pas avec les vapeurs dans l'alambic : toute douceur doit donc être ajoutée ensuite.","A golden or amber colour comes from oak or caramel, so from the post-distillation stage. Sugar does not travel with the vapours through the still, which is why any sweetness must be added afterwards."]},{"id":"s1be6b200","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Qual è lo scopo principale della fase dopo la distillazione?","Quel est le but principal de l'étape après la distillation ?","What is the main aim of the post-distillation stage?"],"o":[["Regolare colore, aromi, dolcezza e grado secondo lo stile","Ajuster couleur, arômes, douceur et degré selon le style","Adjusting colour, aroma, sweetness and strength to suit the style"],["Trasformare l'alcol rimasto in zucchero","Transformer l'alcool restant en sucre","Turning the remaining alcohol into sugar"],["Alzare il grado fino al 96%","Monter le degré jusqu'à 96 %","Raising the strength up to 96%"],["Far ripartire la fermentazione","Relancer la fermentation","Restarting fermentation"]],"e":["Dopo l'alambicco si sistemano colore, aromi, dolcezza e grado in base al distillato voluto.","Après l'alambic, on règle couleur, arômes, douceur et degré selon le spiritueux voulu.","After the still, colour, aroma, sweetness and strength are adjusted for the spirit being made."],"d":["L'alcol non torna zucchero: la dolcezza, se serve, si aggiunge. Il grado dopo la distillazione di solito scende, con la diluizione, invece di salire. E la fermentazione appartiene a una tappa precedente, prima dell'alambicco.","L'alcool ne redevient pas du sucre : la douceur, si on la veut, s'ajoute. Après la distillation, le degré baisse en général avec la dilution au lieu de monter. Et la fermentation appartient à une étape antérieure, avant l'alambic.","Alcohol does not turn back into sugar: sweetness, if wanted, is added. After distillation the strength usually goes down through dilution rather than up. And fermentation belongs to an earlier step, before the still."]},{"id":"s12bf6c0a","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Dove riposa per breve tempo un distillato non invecchiato?","Où repose brièvement une eau-de-vie non vieillie ?","Where does an unaged spirit rest for a short time?"],"o":[["In serbatoi di acciaio inox","En cuves inox","In stainless steel tanks"],["In botti di rovere nuove","En fûts de chêne neufs","In new oak barrels"],["In botti di rovere usate","En fûts de chêne usagés","In used oak barrels"],["Nella caldaia dell'alambicco","Dans la chaudière de l'alambic","In the pot of the still"]],"e":["L'acciaio inox non cede colore né aromi, quindi il distillato resta com'era.","L'inox ne cède ni couleur ni arômes : l'eau-de-vie reste telle qu'elle était.","Stainless steel adds no colour or aroma, so the spirit stays as it was."],"d":["Qualsiasi botte di rovere, nuova o usata, aggiunge colore e aromi: è proprio la definizione di invecchiamento. La caldaia serve a distillare, non a conservare il distillato finito.","Tout fût de chêne, neuf ou usagé, ajoute couleur et arômes : c'est justement la définition du vieillissement. La chaudière sert à distiller, pas à conserver l'eau-de-vie finie.","Any oak barrel, new or used, adds colour and aroma: that is exactly what ageing means. The pot of the still is for distilling, not for storing the finished spirit."]},{"id":"s11770c11","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["In quale ordine cambia il colore di un distillato man mano che invecchia in rovere?","Dans quel ordre change la couleur d'un spiritueux au fil du vieillissement en chêne ?","In what order does a spirit's colour change as it ages in oak?"],"o":[["Limone → oro → ambra → marrone","Citron → or → ambre → brun","Lemon → gold → amber → brown"],["Oro → limone → marrone → ambra","Or → citron → brun → ambre","Gold → lemon → brown → amber"],["Ambra → oro → limone → marrone","Ambre → or → citron → brun","Amber → gold → lemon → brown"],["Limone → ambra → marrone → oro","Citron → ambre → brun → or","Lemon → amber → brown → gold"]],"e":["Il colore si scurisce gradualmente dal limone all'oro e all'ambra, e solo raramente al marrone.","La couleur fonce peu à peu du citron à l'or puis à l'ambre, et rarement jusqu'au brun.","Colour darkens gradually from lemon to gold to amber, and only rarely to brown."],"d":["Le altre sequenze mescolano l'ordine: il rovere scurisce sempre, quindi un distillato non torna da ambra a limone o da marrone a oro. Il marrone è il punto d'arrivo e si vede solo in casi molto rari.","Les autres suites mélangent l'ordre : le chêne fonce toujours, une eau-de-vie ne repasse donc pas de l'ambre au citron ni du brun à l'or. Le brun est le point d'arrivée et ne se voit que très rarement.","The other sequences jumble the order: oak always darkens a spirit, so it never goes back from amber to lemon or from brown to gold. Brown is the end point and is seen only very rarely."]},{"id":"s1a27cd45","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Quale botte cede più aromi a un distillato?","Quel fût cède le plus d'arômes à un spiritueux ?","Which barrel gives the most aroma to a spirit?"],"o":[["Una botte di rovere nuova, mai usata","Un fût de chêne neuf, jamais utilisé","A new oak barrel that has never been used"],["Una botte usata già due volte","Un fût déjà utilisé deux fois","A barrel already used twice"],["Una botte usata molte volte","Un fût utilisé de nombreuses fois","A barrel used many times"],["Un serbatoio di acciaio inox","Une cuve inox","A stainless steel tank"]],"e":["La botte nuova ha ancora tutti i suoi aromi da cedere.","Le fût neuf a encore tous ses arômes à céder.","A new barrel still has all of its aromas to give."],"d":["A ogni utilizzo una botte cede meno aromi, quindi una botte usata due volte o molte volte dà sempre meno di una nuova. L'acciaio inox non cede nulla: si usa proprio per mantenere il distillato invariato.","À chaque usage un fût cède moins d'arômes : un fût utilisé deux fois ou de nombreuses fois donne toujours moins qu'un neuf. L'inox ne cède rien : on l'utilise justement pour garder l'eau-de-vie intacte.","Each time a barrel is used it gives less aroma, so a barrel used twice or many times always gives less than a new one. Stainless steel gives nothing at all: that is precisely why it is used to keep a spirit unchanged."]},{"id":"s1a42e7c4","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Quale gruppo di aromi viene tipicamente dal rovere?","Quel groupe d'arômes vient typiquement du chêne ?","Which group of aromas typically comes from oak?"],"o":[["Vaniglia, cannella, chiodi di garofano, cocco","Vanille, cannelle, clou de girofle, noix de coco","Vanilla, cinnamon, cloves, coconut"],["Erba tagliata, oliva, pepe","Herbe coupée, olive, poivre","Cut grass, olive, pepper"],["Mela, limone, fiori bianchi","Pomme, citron, fleurs blanches","Apple, lemon, white flowers"],["Ginepro, coriandolo, scorza di agrumi","Genièvre, coriandre, zeste d'agrumes","Juniper, coriander, citrus peel"]],"e":["Vaniglia, spezie dolci e cocco sono la firma classica del rovere.","Vanille, épices douces et noix de coco sont la signature classique du chêne.","Vanilla, warm spices and coconut are oak's classic signature."],"d":["Erba, oliva e pepe ricordano piuttosto una materia prima come l'agave. Mela e fiori evocano frutta e fermentazione, non il legno. Ginepro e coriandolo sono piante aggiunte per aromatizzare un distillato come il gin.","Herbe, olive et poivre évoquent plutôt une matière première comme l'agave. Pomme et fleurs rappellent le fruit et la fermentation, pas le bois. Genièvre et coriandre sont des plantes ajoutées pour aromatiser un spiritueux comme le gin.","Grass, olive and pepper point to a raw material such as agave. Apple and flowers suggest fruit and fermentation, not wood. Juniper and coriander are plants added to flavour a spirit such as gin."]},{"id":"s1373bffb","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Perché un distillato diventa più concentrato con un lungo invecchiamento?","Pourquoi un spiritueux devient-il plus concentré avec un long vieillissement ?","Why does a spirit become more concentrated during long ageing?"],"o":[["Perché acqua ed etanolo evaporano attraverso la botte","Parce que l'eau et l'éthanol s'évaporent à travers le fût","Because water and ethanol evaporate through the barrel"],["Perché il rovere aggiunge zucchero al distillato","Parce que le chêne ajoute du sucre à l'eau-de-vie","Because the oak adds sugar to the spirit"],["Perché il grado alcolico sale ogni anno","Parce que le degré monte chaque année","Because the alcohol level rises every year"],["Perché nella botte riprende la fermentazione","Parce que la fermentation reprend dans le fût","Because fermentation restarts in the barrel"]],"e":["Con l'evaporazione di acqua ed etanolo, gli aromi restanti si concentrano.","Avec l'évaporation de l'eau et de l'éthanol, les arômes restants se concentrent.","As water and ethanol evaporate, the remaining aromas become concentrated."],"d":["Il rovere dà colore e aromi, non zucchero: la dolcezza si aggiunge a parte. Il punto non è un aumento del grado, perché evapora anche l'etanolo. E nella botte non c'è più zucchero da far fermentare.","Le chêne donne couleur et arômes, pas de sucre : la douceur s'ajoute à part. Il ne s'agit pas d'une hausse du degré, puisque l'éthanol s'évapore lui aussi. Et dans le fût, il n'y a plus de sucre à faire fermenter.","Oak gives colour and aroma, not sugar: sweetness is added separately. The point is not a rising strength, since ethanol evaporates too. And there is no sugar left in the barrel to ferment."]},{"id":"s16c1ef0f","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Un distillato è rimasto in botte per alcuni decenni. Quali aromi è più probabile trovare?","Un spiritueux est resté plusieurs décennies en fût. Quels arômes a-t-on le plus de chances d'y trouver ?","A spirit has spent several decades in barrel. Which aromas are most likely?"],"o":[["Torta di frutta, frutta secca, cuoio, cera per mobili","Cake aux fruits, fruits secs, cuir, cire à meubles","Fruit cake, dried fruit, leather, wood polish"],["Erba fresca, mela verde, fiori bianchi","Herbe fraîche, pomme verte, fleurs blanches","Fresh grass, green apple, white flowers"],["Nessun aroma: il distillato diventa neutro","Aucun arôme : l'eau-de-vie devient neutre","No aroma at all: the spirit becomes neutral"],["Solo vaniglia leggera, come dopo pochi mesi","Seulement une vanille légère, comme après quelques mois","Only light vanilla, as after a few months"]],"e":["Con un invecchiamento lunghissimo compaiono aromi complessi di frutta secca, cuoio e cera.","Avec un très long vieillissement apparaissent des arômes complexes de fruits secs, de cuir et de cire.","Very long ageing brings complex aromas of dried fruit, leather and polish."],"d":["Erba fresca e mela verde ricordano un distillato giovane. Il rovere aggiunge aromi invece di toglierli, quindi il distillato non diventa neutro. Una leggera vaniglia è tipica di un invecchiamento breve, mentre decenni portano concentrazione e nuove sfumature.","Herbe fraîche et pomme verte évoquent une eau-de-vie jeune. Le chêne ajoute des arômes au lieu d'en retirer : l'eau-de-vie ne devient pas neutre. Une vanille légère est typique d'un vieillissement court, alors que des décennies apportent concentration et nouvelles nuances.","Fresh grass and green apple suggest a young spirit. Oak adds aromas rather than removing them, so the spirit does not become neutral. A light vanilla note is typical of short ageing, whereas decades bring concentration and new layers."]},{"id":"s16bbded4","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Quali sono i due obiettivi principali dell'assemblaggio di distillati invecchiati?","Quels sont les deux objectifs principaux de l'assemblage des spiritueux vieillis ?","What are the two main aims of blending oak-aged spirits?"],"o":[["Costanza e complessità","Constance et complexité","Consistency and complexity"],["Dolcezza e colore","Douceur et couleur","Sweetness and colour"],["Grado più alto e meno aromi","Degré plus élevé et moins d'arômes","Higher strength and less aroma"],["Invecchiamento più rapido e meno botti","Vieillissement plus rapide et moins de fûts","Faster ageing and fewer barrels"]],"e":["Si assembla per avere lo stesso gusto a ogni bottiglia e per dare profondità.","On assemble pour retrouver le même goût dans chaque bouteille et pour donner de la profondeur.","Blending keeps every bottle tasting the same and builds depth."],"d":["Dolcezza e colore si regolano con zucchero e caramello, gesti distinti dall'assemblaggio. Mescolare botti non alza il grado né toglie aromi. L'assemblaggio non accorcia l'invecchiamento e richiede anzi molte botti diverse.","Douceur et couleur se règlent avec sucre et caramel, des gestes distincts de l'assemblage. Mélanger des fûts n'augmente pas le degré et ne retire pas d'arômes. L'assemblage ne raccourcit pas le vieillissement et demande au contraire de nombreux fûts différents.","Sweetness and colour are adjusted with sugar and caramel, separate steps from blending. Mixing barrels neither raises the strength nor strips aroma. Blending does not shorten ageing; in fact it needs many different barrels."]},{"id":"s1e5a2b4e","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Perché chi assembla aggiunge piccole quantità di caramello colorante?","Pourquoi l'assembleur ajoute-t-il de petites quantités de caramel colorant ?","Why does a blender add small amounts of caramel colouring?"],"o":[["Per dare a ogni lotto lo stesso colore","Pour donner la même couleur à chaque lot","To give every batch the same colour"],["Per rendere il distillato più dolce","Pour rendre l'eau-de-vie plus douce","To make the spirit sweeter"],["Per aggiungere aromi di vaniglia","Pour ajouter des arômes de vanille","To add vanilla aromas"],["Per alzare il grado alcolico","Pour augmenter le degré","To raise the alcohol level"]],"e":["Le botti danno tonalità diverse; il caramello uniforma il colore da un lotto all'altro.","Les fûts donnent des teintes différentes ; le caramel uniformise la couleur d'un lot à l'autre.","Barrels give different shades; caramel evens out the colour from batch to batch."],"d":["Il caramello colorante non è dolce e, usato correttamente, non aggiunge aromi: la vaniglia viene dal rovere. Non contiene alcol, quindi non può alzare il grado. Serve solo all'aspetto.","Le caramel colorant n'est pas sucré et, bien utilisé, n'ajoute aucun arôme : la vanille vient du chêne. Il ne contient pas d'alcool et ne peut donc pas augmenter le degré. Il ne sert qu'à l'aspect.","Caramel colouring is not sweet and, used properly, adds no aroma: vanilla comes from oak. It contains no alcohol, so it cannot raise the strength. It is there purely for appearance."]},{"id":"s14a10f8c","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Un cliente dice: «Questo distillato è scuro, quindi è per forza invecchiato a lungo». Che cosa si risponde?","Un client affirme : « Ce spiritueux est foncé, il a donc forcément longtemps vieilli. » Que lui répondre ?","A customer says: 'This spirit is dark, so it must have been aged for a long time.' What is the best reply?"],"o":[["Non per forza: il colore può venire quasi tutto dal caramello","Pas forcément : la couleur peut venir presque entièrement du caramel","Not necessarily: the colour can come almost entirely from caramel"],["Sì, solo il rovere può dare colore a un distillato","Oui, seul le chêne peut colorer un spiritueux","Yes, only oak can colour a spirit"],["Sì, perché il colore scuro indica sempre una botte nuova","Oui, car une couleur foncée indique toujours un fût neuf","Yes, because a dark colour always means a new barrel"],["No, perché i distillati invecchiati sono sempre chiari","Non, car les spiritueux vieillis sont toujours clairs","No, because aged spirits are always pale"]],"e":["Alcuni distillati prendono tutto o quasi il colore dal caramello, quindi il colore non prova l'età.","Certains spiritueux tirent toute ou presque toute leur couleur du caramel : la couleur ne prouve pas l'âge.","Some spirits get all or nearly all their colour from caramel, so colour does not prove age."],"d":["Il rovere non è l'unica fonte di colore: esistono caramello e altri coloranti. Una botte nuova dà più colore, ma un colore scuro può avere molte altre cause. E i distillati invecchiati non sono sempre chiari: anzi, il rovere tende a scurirli col tempo.","Le chêne n'est pas la seule source de couleur : il existe le caramel et d'autres colorants. Un fût neuf colore davantage, mais une couleur foncée peut avoir bien d'autres causes. Et les spiritueux vieillis ne sont pas toujours clairs : le chêne les fonce au contraire avec le temps.","Oak is not the only source of colour: there is caramel and other colourings. A new barrel does give more colour, but dark colour can have other causes. And aged spirits are not always pale: oak tends to darken them over time."]},{"id":"s17c379b2","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Da dove viene la dolcezza che si avverte in bocca in un distillato?","D'où vient la douceur que l'on perçoit en bouche dans un spiritueux ?","Where does the sweetness you taste in a spirit come from?"],"o":[["Da zucchero aggiunto dopo la distillazione","Du sucre ajouté après la distillation","From sugar added after distillation"],["Dallo zucchero della materia prima che passa nell'alambicco","Du sucre de la matière première qui traverse l'alambic","From the raw material's sugar passing through the still"],["Dal caramello colorante","Du caramel colorant","From caramel colouring"],["Dall'acqua usata per la diluizione","De l'eau utilisée pour la dilution","From the water used for dilution"]],"e":["Ogni distillato esce secco, quindi la dolcezza va aggiunta dopo, di solito come zucchero.","Toute eau-de-vie sort sèche : la douceur doit donc être ajoutée ensuite, en général sous forme de sucre.","Every spirit leaves the still dry, so sweetness has to be added later, usually as sugar."],"d":["Lo zucchero della materia prima viene consumato dai lieviti e comunque non passa con i vapori. Il caramello colorante non è dolce. L'acqua di diluizione è pura e non porta né gusto né zucchero.","Le sucre de la matière première est consommé par les levures et ne passe de toute façon pas avec les vapeurs. Le caramel colorant n'est pas sucré. L'eau de dilution est pure et n'apporte ni goût ni sucre.","The raw material's sugar is eaten by yeast and does not travel with the vapours anyway. Caramel colouring is not sweet. Dilution water is pure and brings neither flavour nor sugar."]},{"id":"s158f30a5","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Un whiskey senza zucchero aggiunto ha profumi intensi di vaniglia e frutta. Come va descritto in bocca?","Un whiskey sans sucre ajouté a des arômes intenses de vanille et de fruits. Comment le décrire en bouche ?","A whiskey with no added sugar has intense vanilla and fruit aromas. How should its palate be described?"],"o":[["Secco, perché dolce indica solo il sapore dello zucchero","Sec, car doux désigne seulement le goût du sucre","Dry, because sweet refers only to the taste of sugar"],["Dolce, perché vaniglia e frutta sono aromi dolci","Doux, car vanille et fruits sont des arômes doux","Sweet, because vanilla and fruit are sweet aromas"],["Dolce, perché il rovere aggiunge zucchero","Doux, car le chêne ajoute du sucre","Sweet, because oak adds sugar"],["Neutro, perché non ha zucchero","Neutre, car il n'a pas de sucre","Neutral, because it has no sugar"]],"e":["Senza zucchero aggiunto il distillato resta secco, anche se il naso sembra goloso.","Sans sucre ajouté le spiritueux reste sec, même si le nez semble gourmand.","With no added sugar the spirit is dry, even if the nose smells sweet."],"d":["Chiamare dolci gli aromi di vaniglia e frutta crea confusione: la dolcezza è un sapore, legato allo zucchero. Il rovere non aggiunge zucchero. Neutro descrive invece un distillato quasi privo di aromi, l'opposto di questo whiskey.","Qualifier de doux les arômes de vanille et de fruits crée la confusion : la douceur est une saveur, liée au sucre. Le chêne n'ajoute pas de sucre. Neutre décrit au contraire un spiritueux presque sans arômes, l'inverse de ce whiskey.","Calling vanilla and fruit aromas sweet causes confusion: sweetness is a taste, tied to sugar. Oak adds no sugar. Neutral, on the other hand, describes a spirit with almost no aroma, the opposite of this whiskey."]},{"id":"s14ea3ce0","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Perché la maggior parte dei distillati viene diluita al 40% vol. prima dell'imbottigliamento?","Pourquoi la plupart des spiritueux sont-ils dilués à 40 % vol. avant la mise en bouteille ?","Why are most spirits diluted to 40% abv before bottling?"],"o":[["Per renderli bevibili: troppo alcol anestetizza il palato","Pour les rendre buvables : trop d'alcool anesthésie le palais","To make them drinkable: too much alcohol numbs the palate"],["Per aggiungere aromi tramite l'acqua","Pour ajouter des arômes grâce à l'eau","To add aromas through the water"],["Per renderli più dolci","Pour les rendre plus doux","To make them sweeter"],["Per dare loro un colore più chiaro e uniforme","Pour leur donner une couleur plus claire et uniforme","To give them a paler, even colour"]],"e":["A gradi molto alti non si riesce a sentire né a godere il gusto.","À très haut degré, on ne peut ni percevoir ni apprécier le goût.","At very high strength it is impossible to taste or enjoy the spirit."],"d":["L'acqua usata è completamente pura e non aggiunge aromi né zucchero. Il colore si regola con il rovere o con il caramello, non con l'acqua. La diluizione serve solo ad abbassare il grado.","L'eau utilisée est parfaitement pure et n'ajoute ni arôme ni sucre. La couleur se règle avec le chêne ou le caramel, pas avec l'eau. La dilution sert uniquement à baisser le degré.","The water is completely pure and adds no aroma or sugar. Colour is managed with oak or caramel, not water. Dilution only lowers the strength."]},{"id":"s1e40167f","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Quale tra questi passaggi non aggiunge nessun aroma al distillato?","Laquelle de ces étapes n'ajoute aucun arôme au spiritueux ?","Which of these steps adds no aroma to the spirit?"],"o":[["La diluizione con acqua pura","La dilution à l'eau pure","Dilution with pure water"],["L'invecchiamento in una botte nuova","Le vieillissement en fût neuf","Ageing in a new barrel"],["La macerazione di erbe e spezie","La macération d'herbes et d'épices","Macerating herbs and spices"],["La fermentazione con i lieviti","La fermentation avec les levures","Fermentation with yeast"]],"e":["L'acqua pura abbassa solo il grado e non porta gusto.","L'eau pure baisse seulement le degré et n'apporte aucun goût.","Pure water only lowers the strength and brings no flavour."],"d":["Una botte nuova è la fonte più ricca di aromi del rovere. La macerazione serve proprio a estrarre gli aromi delle piante. E la fermentazione, oltre all'alcol, crea aromi fruttati.","Un fût neuf est la source la plus riche d'arômes de chêne. La macération sert justement à extraire les arômes des plantes. Et la fermentation, en plus de l'alcool, crée des arômes fruités.","A new barrel is the richest source of oak aroma. Maceration exists precisely to draw flavour out of plants. And fermentation creates fruity aromas as well as alcohol."]},{"id":"s1511b400","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Quali sono le tre tecniche più comuni per dare a un distillato aromi diversi dal legno?","Quelles sont les trois techniques les plus courantes pour donner à un spiritueux d'autres arômes que le bois ?","What are the three most common ways to give a spirit flavours other than oak?"],"o":[["Ridistillazione, macerazione, aggiunta di aromi","Redistillation, macération, ajout d'arômes","Redistillation, maceration, adding flavourings"],["Fermentazione, assemblaggio, diluizione","Fermentation, assemblage, dilution","Fermentation, blending, dilution"],["Caramello, zucchero, acqua","Caramel, sucre, eau","Caramel, sugar, water"],["Botte nuova, botte usata, acciaio inox","Fût neuf, fût usagé, cuve inox","New barrel, used barrel, stainless steel"]],"e":["Si ridistilla con le piante, le si lascia in infusione o si aggiungono aromi già pronti.","On redistille avec les plantes, on les laisse macérer ou on ajoute des arômes tout prêts.","The spirit is redistilled with plants, steeped with them, or given ready-made flavourings."],"d":["Assemblaggio e diluizione non aggiungono aromi nuovi, e la fermentazione precede l'alambicco. Caramello e acqua non portano aromi, lo zucchero dà dolcezza. Le botti danno proprio gli aromi del legno, e l'acciaio non ne dà alcuno.","L'assemblage et la dilution n'apportent pas de nouveaux arômes, et la fermentation précède l'alambic. Le caramel et l'eau n'apportent pas d'arômes, le sucre apporte de la douceur. Les fûts donnent justement des arômes de bois, et l'inox n'en donne aucun.","Blending and dilution add no new flavours, and fermentation comes before the still. Caramel and water bring no aroma, while sugar brings sweetness. Barrels give exactly the oak flavours being excluded, and steel gives none."]},{"id":"s1ff642e3","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Quale tecnica di aromatizzazione dà al distillato anche colore?","Quelle technique d'aromatisation donne aussi de la couleur au spiritueux ?","Which flavouring technique also gives the spirit colour?"],"o":[["La macerazione","La macération","Maceration"],["La ridistillazione","La redistillation","Redistillation"],["La diluizione","La dilution","Dilution"],["La distillazione in colonna","La distillation en colonne","Column distillation"]],"e":["Lasciando le piante in infusione, passano nel distillato sia gli aromi sia il colore.","En laissant macérer les plantes, les arômes comme la couleur passent dans l'alcool.","When plants steep in the spirit, both flavour and colour pass into it."],"d":["La ridistillazione con le piante dà un liquido aromatizzato ma incolore, perché il colore non passa con i vapori. La diluizione usa acqua pura. La colonna serve a distillare, non ad aromatizzare.","La redistillation avec les plantes donne un liquide aromatisé mais incolore, car la couleur ne passe pas avec les vapeurs. La dilution utilise de l'eau pure. La colonne sert à distiller, pas à aromatiser.","Redistilling with plants gives a flavoured but colourless liquid, because colour does not travel with the vapours. Dilution uses pure water. A column still is for distilling, not flavouring."]},{"id":"s1de7ae2d","c":"p2","p":0,"q":["Quale affermazione sulle scelte dopo la distillazione è corretta?","Quelle affirmation sur les choix après la distillation est correcte ?","Which statement about post-distillation choices is correct?"],"o":[["Lo Scotch deve passare in rovere, la Tequila può anche non farlo","Le whisky écossais doit passer en fût, la Tequila peut s'en passer","Scotch must be oak-aged, while Tequila may be aged or not"],["La Tequila deve passare in rovere, lo Scotch può anche non farlo","La Tequila doit passer en fût, le whisky écossais peut s'en passer","Tequila must be oak-aged, while Scotch may be aged or not"],["Il produttore è sempre libero, la legge non interviene mai","Le producteur est toujours libre, la loi n'intervient jamais","Producers are always free: the law never steps in"],["Tutti i distillati devono passare almeno un anno in rovere","Tous les spiritueux doivent passer au moins un an en fût","Every spirit must spend at least a year in oak"]],"e":["Le leggi locali limitano le scelte: lo Scotch va invecchiato, la Tequila può essere giovane o invecchiata.","Les lois locales limitent les choix : le whisky écossais doit vieillir, la Tequila peut être jeune ou vieillie.","Local laws limit the options: Scotch must be aged, Tequila can be young or aged."],"d":["La seconda opzione inverte i due casi. La legge interviene spesso, quindi il produttore non è sempre libero. E molti distillati, come la vodka, non vedono mai il rovere: nessuna regola impone un anno a tutti.","La deuxième option inverse les deux cas. La loi intervient souvent : le producteur n'est donc pas toujours libre. Et beaucoup de spiritueux, comme la vodka, ne voient jamais le chêne : aucune règle n'impose un an à tous.","The second option swaps the two cases. The law often steps in, so producers are not always free. And many spirits, vodka for one, never see oak: no rule imposes a year on all of them."]},{"id":"s112de3bc","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è un brandy d'uva come il Cognac?","Qu'est-ce qu'un brandy de raisin comme le Cognac ?","What is a grape brandy such as Cognac?"],"o":[["Un vino distillato","Un vin distillé","A distilled wine"],["Un succo d'uva distillato senza fermentazione","Un jus de raisin distillé sans fermentation","Grape juice distilled without fermentation"],["Un vino rinforzato con alcol neutro","Un vin renforcé avec de l'alcool neutre","A wine strengthened with neutral spirit"],["Un distillato di cereali aromatizzato all'uva","Une eau-de-vie de céréales aromatisée au raisin","A grain spirit flavoured with grapes"]],"e":["Il succo d'uva fermenta in vino, e questo vino viene distillato.","Le jus de raisin fermente en vin, et ce vin est distillé.","Grape juice is fermented into wine, and that wine is distilled."],"d":["Senza fermentazione non c'è alcol da distillare, quindi il succo deve prima diventare vino. Aggiungere alcol a un vino non è distillarlo. E il Cognac nasce dall'uva, non da cereali aromatizzati.","Sans fermentation, il n'y a pas d'alcool à distiller : le jus doit d'abord devenir du vin. Ajouter de l'alcool à un vin, ce n'est pas le distiller. Et le Cognac naît du raisin, pas de céréales aromatisées.","Without fermentation there is no alcohol to distil, so the juice must first become wine. Adding spirit to a wine is not distilling it. And Cognac is made from grapes, not flavoured grain spirit."]},{"id":"s124749f3","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Da dove devono provenire le uve del Cognac?","D'où doivent provenir les raisins du Cognac ?","Where must the grapes for Cognac come from?"],"o":[["Da una zona del sud-ovest della Francia, a nord di Bordeaux","D'une zone du sud-ouest de la France, au nord de Bordeaux","From an area of south-west France, north of Bordeaux"],["Da qualsiasi vigneto francese","De n'importe quel vignoble français","From any vineyard in France"],["Da una zona del sud-est della Francia, vicino al Mediterraneo","D'une zone du sud-est de la France, près de la Méditerranée","From an area of south-east France, near the Mediterranean"],["Da qualsiasi paese, purché distillato in Francia","De n'importe quel pays, s'il est distillé en France","From any country, as long as it is distilled in France"]],"e":["Il Cognac richiede uve di una zona precisa del sud-ovest francese, a nord di Bordeaux.","Le Cognac exige des raisins d'une zone précise du sud-ouest de la France, au nord de Bordeaux.","Cognac requires grapes from a specific area of south-west France, north of Bordeaux."],"d":["Non basta che l'uva sia francese: deve venire da quell'area delimitata. Il sud-est della Francia è un'altra regione. E non conta solo il luogo di distillazione: è l'uva stessa a dover nascere nella zona.","Il ne suffit pas que le raisin soit français : il doit venir de cette zone délimitée. Le sud-est de la France est une autre région. Et le lieu de distillation ne suffit pas : c'est le raisin lui-même qui doit naître dans la zone.","It is not enough for the grapes to be French: they must come from that defined area. South-east France is a different region. And the place of distillation alone does not count: the grapes themselves must be grown in the area."]},{"id":"s18ca661c","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi portano al Cognac le sue uve?","Quels arômes les raisins apportent-ils au Cognac ?","Which aromas do the grapes bring to Cognac?"],"o":[["Fruttati e floreali","Fruités et floraux","Fruity and floral"],["Vaniglia e pane tostato","Vanille et pain grillé","Vanilla and toast"],["Erbacei e pepati","Herbacés et poivrés","Herbal and peppery"],["Cereali e fumo","Céréales et fumée","Cereal and smoke"]],"e":["La materia prima uva dà al Cognac le note fruttate e floreali.","Le raisin, matière première, donne au Cognac ses notes fruitées et florales.","Grapes, the raw material, give Cognac its fruity and floral notes."],"d":["Vaniglia e tostato ci sono, ma vengono dal rovere, non dall'uva. Le note erbacee e pepate sono tipiche dell'agave. Cereali e fumo fanno pensare a un whisky di malto, non a un distillato di vino.","La vanille et le grillé sont bien là, mais ils viennent du chêne, pas du raisin. Les notes herbacées et poivrées sont typiques de l'agave. Céréales et fumée évoquent un whisky de malt, pas une eau-de-vie de vin.","Vanilla and toast are there, but they come from oak, not grapes. Herbal and peppery notes are typical of agave. Cereal and smoke suggest a malt whisky, not a wine spirit."]},{"id":"s1f689581","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Che cosa succede al succo appena pressato destinato al Cognac?","Que devient le jus fraîchement pressé destiné au Cognac ?","What happens to the freshly pressed juice destined for Cognac?"],"o":[["Fermenta subito e diventa vino","Il fermente tout de suite et devient du vin","It is fermented straight away into wine"],["Si distilla subito, prima di fermentare","On le distille tout de suite, avant fermentation","It is distilled at once, before fermenting"],["Si cuoce per creare zucchero","On le cuit pour créer du sucre","It is cooked to create sugar"],["Si invecchia in rovere per due anni","On le vieillit deux ans en fût de chêne","It is aged in oak for two years"]],"e":["Il succo d'uva è già ricco di zucchero, quindi fermenta subito in vino.","Le jus de raisin est déjà riche en sucre : il fermente donc tout de suite en vin.","Grape juice is already full of sugar, so it is fermented into wine right away."],"d":["Distillare prima della fermentazione non darebbe alcol da concentrare. La cottura per creare zuccheri serve a materie prime come l'agave, non all'uva. I due anni in rovere riguardano il distillato, dopo l'alambicco, non il succo.","Distiller avant la fermentation ne donnerait aucun alcool à concentrer. La cuisson pour créer des sucres concerne des matières premières comme l'agave, pas le raisin. Les deux ans en fût concernent l'eau-de-vie, après l'alambic, pas le jus.","Distilling before fermentation would leave no alcohol to concentrate. Cooking to create sugar is for raw materials like agave, not grapes. The two years in oak apply to the spirit after distillation, not to the juice."]},{"id":"s1cf01a1f","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Come deve essere distillato il Cognac per legge?","Comment le Cognac doit-il être distillé selon la loi ?","How must Cognac be distilled by law?"],"o":[["Due volte in un alambicco discontinuo","Deux fois dans un alambic à repasse","Twice in a pot still"],["Una volta in un alambicco a colonna alto","Une fois dans une colonne haute","Once in a tall column still"],["Una sola volta in un alambicco discontinuo","Une seule fois dans un alambic à repasse","Only once in a pot still"],["In continuo, fino al 96% vol.","En continu, jusqu'à 96 % vol.","Continuously, up to 96% abv"]],"e":["La legge impone la doppia distillazione in alambicco discontinuo.","La loi impose la double distillation à l'alambic à repasse.","The law requires double distillation in a pot still."],"d":["La colonna e la distillazione in continuo fino al 96% darebbero un distillato leggero o neutro, lontano dallo stile del Cognac. Un solo passaggio in alambicco discontinuo non basta a ottenere un distillato dal vino.","La colonne et la distillation en continu jusqu'à 96 % donneraient une eau-de-vie légère ou neutre, loin du style du Cognac. Un seul passage à l'alambic à repasse ne suffit pas pour obtenir une eau-de-vie à partir du vin.","A column and continuous distillation to 96% would give a light or neutral spirit, far from the Cognac style. A single pass through a pot still is not enough to make a spirit from wine."]},{"id":"s16d2d8f1","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Perché per il Cognac si usa l'alambicco discontinuo?","Pourquoi utilise-t-on l'alambic à repasse pour le Cognac ?","Why is a pot still used for Cognac?"],"o":[["Dà un distillato di grado basso, ricco di gusto e carattere","Il donne une eau-de-vie de bas degré, riche en goût et en caractère","It gives a low-strength spirit full of flavour and character"],["Dà un distillato neutro, facile da aromatizzare","Il donne une eau-de-vie neutre, facile à aromatiser","It gives a neutral spirit that is easy to flavour"],["Lavora in continuo ed è molto veloce","Il fonctionne en continu et va très vite","It runs continuously and is very fast"],["Aggiunge da solo colore e dolcezza","Il ajoute de lui-même couleur et douceur","It adds colour and sweetness by itself"]],"e":["Il grado basso conserva gli aromi dell'uva e dà un distillato di carattere.","Le bas degré préserve les arômes du raisin et donne une eau-de-vie de caractère.","The low strength keeps the grape aromas and gives a characterful spirit."],"d":["L'alambicco discontinuo non può fare un distillato neutro: quello è compito delle colonne più alte. Lavora a lotti, quindi è lento, non continuo. E ogni distillato esce incolore e secco: colore e dolcezza arrivano dopo.","L'alambic à repasse ne peut pas produire d'alcool neutre : c'est le rôle des colonnes les plus hautes. Il travaille par lots, il est donc lent, pas continu. Et toute eau-de-vie sort incolore et sèche : couleur et douceur viennent après.","A pot still cannot make a neutral spirit: that is the job of the tallest columns. It works in batches, so it is slow rather than continuous. And every spirit leaves the still colourless and dry: colour and sweetness come later."]},{"id":"s129296ea","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Come si scaldano tradizionalmente gli alambicchi del Cognac?","Comment chauffe-t-on traditionnellement les alambics du Cognac ?","How are Cognac pot stills traditionally heated?"],"o":[["Con bruciatori a gas","Avec des brûleurs à gaz","With gas burners"],["Con serpentine a vapore","Avec des serpentins à vapeur","With steam coils"],["Con resistenze elettriche","Avec des résistances électriques","With electric elements"],["Con il calore del sole","Avec la chaleur du soleil","With heat from the sun"]],"e":["Gli alambicchi del Cognac usano ancora bruciatori a gas.","Les alambics du Cognac utilisent encore des brûleurs à gaz.","Cognac stills still use gas burners."],"d":["Il vapore, con camicie o serpentine, è il sistema di molti alambicchi moderni, ed è proprio per questo una trappola: il Cognac fa eccezione. Resistenze elettriche e calore solare non sono il metodo tradizionale.","La vapeur, par double paroi ou serpentin, équipe beaucoup d'alambics modernes, et c'est justement le piège : le Cognac fait exception. Les résistances électriques et la chaleur solaire ne sont pas la méthode traditionnelle.","Steam, through jackets or coils, heats many modern pot stills, which is exactly why it is the trap: Cognac is the exception. Electric elements and solar heat are not the traditional method."]},{"id":"s1650fbd5","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Per quanto tempo minimo un distillato deve restare in rovere per chiamarsi Cognac?","Combien de temps au minimum une eau-de-vie doit-elle rester en fût pour s'appeler Cognac ?","What is the minimum time in oak before a spirit can be called Cognac?"],"o":[["Due anni","Deux ans","Two years"],["Sei mesi","Six mois","Six months"],["Quattro anni","Quatre ans","Four years"],["Dieci anni","Dix ans","Ten years"]],"e":["La legge impone almeno due anni in botti di rovere.","La loi impose au moins deux ans en fût de chêne.","The law requires at least two years in oak barrels."],"d":["Sei mesi non bastano. Quattro anni è il minimo per la menzione VSOP e dieci anni quello per XO: sono età più alte, legate a categorie specifiche, non la soglia minima per poter usare il nome.","Six mois ne suffisent pas. Quatre ans est le minimum de la mention VSOP et dix ans celui de XO : ce sont des âges plus élevés, liés à des catégories précises, pas le seuil minimal pour utiliser le nom.","Six months is not enough. Four years is the minimum for VSOP and ten years for XO: these are higher ages tied to specific categories, not the threshold for using the name at all."]},{"id":"s108b5a46","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi dà il rovere a un Cognac giovane?","Quels arômes le chêne donne-t-il à un Cognac jeune ?","Which aromas does oak give a young Cognac?"],"o":[["Vaniglia e pane tostato","Vanille et pain grillé","Vanilla and toast"],["Fiori e frutta fresca","Fleurs et fruits frais","Flowers and fresh fruit"],["Fumo di torba","Fumée de tourbe","Peat smoke"],["Erba e oliva","Herbe et olive","Grass and olive"]],"e":["Il passaggio in botte aggiunge al Cognac note di vaniglia e di tostato.","Le passage en fût ajoute au Cognac des notes de vanille et de grillé.","Time in barrel adds vanilla and toasty notes to Cognac."],"d":["Fiori e frutta fresca vengono dall'uva, non dal legno. Il fumo di torba si trova in alcuni whisky di malto. Erba e oliva sono note tipiche dell'agave.","Les fleurs et les fruits frais viennent du raisin, pas du bois. La fumée de tourbe se trouve dans certains whiskies de malt. L'herbe et l'olive sont des notes typiques de l'agave.","Flowers and fresh fruit come from the grapes, not the wood. Peat smoke is found in some malt whiskies. Grass and olive are typical agave notes."]},{"id":"s1f1a5cdf","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Un Cognac molto vecchio mostra aromi di torta di frutta e cuoio. Da dove vengono?","Un très vieux Cognac montre des arômes de cake aux fruits et de cuir. D'où viennent-ils ?","A very old Cognac shows fruit cake and leather aromas. Where do they come from?"],"o":[["Da un lungo invecchiamento in botte","D'un long vieillissement en fût","From long ageing in barrel"],["Dalla fermentazione del succo","De la fermentation du jus","From the fermentation of the juice"],["Dalla doppia distillazione","De la double distillation","From double distillation"],["Dal caramello colorante","Du caramel colorant","From caramel colouring"]],"e":["Molti anni in rovere concentrano il distillato e fanno nascere questi aromi complessi.","De nombreuses années en fût concentrent l'eau-de-vie et font naître ces arômes complexes.","Many years in oak concentrate the spirit and develop these complex aromas."],"d":["La fermentazione crea soprattutto aromi fruttati freschi, non note evolute come il cuoio. La doppia distillazione conserva gli aromi dell'uva ma non crea quelli dell'età. Il caramello, usato correttamente, non aggiunge aromi.","La fermentation crée surtout des arômes fruités frais, pas des notes évoluées comme le cuir. La double distillation préserve les arômes du raisin mais ne crée pas ceux de l'âge. Le caramel, bien utilisé, n'ajoute aucun arôme.","Fermentation mainly creates fresh fruity aromas, not evolved notes like leather. Double distillation keeps the grape aromas but does not create the aromas of age. Caramel, used properly, adds no aroma."]},{"id":"s1db7e9df","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Quale affermazione sul Cognac è corretta?","Quelle affirmation sur le Cognac est correcte ?","Which statement about Cognac is correct?"],"o":[["Quasi tutti i Cognac sono assemblaggi","Presque tous les Cognacs sont des assemblages","Nearly all Cognacs are blends"],["Quasi tutti i Cognac vengono da una sola botte","Presque tous les Cognacs viennent d'un seul fût","Nearly all Cognacs come from a single barrel"],["Il Cognac non può mai essere assemblato","Le Cognac ne peut jamais être assemblé","Cognac may never be blended"],["Il Cognac si assembla solo con vodka","Le Cognac ne s'assemble qu'avec de la vodka","Cognac is only blended with vodka"]],"e":["Unire distillati di età diverse dà al Cognac complessità, e quasi tutti sono assemblaggi.","Marier des eaux-de-vie d'âges différents apporte de la complexité, et presque tous les Cognacs sont des assemblages.","Combining spirits of different ages adds complexity, and nearly all Cognacs are blends."],"d":["I Cognac da singola botte sono un'eccezione, non la regola. L'assemblaggio non è vietato, anzi è la norma. E si assemblano distillati di Cognac tra loro, non con altri distillati come la vodka.","Les Cognacs d'un seul fût sont l'exception, pas la règle. L'assemblage n'est pas interdit, c'est même la norme. Et on assemble des eaux-de-vie de Cognac entre elles, pas avec d'autres spiritueux comme la vodka.","Single-barrel Cognacs are the exception, not the rule. Blending is not forbidden; it is the norm. And Cognac spirits are blended with each other, not with other spirits such as vodka."]},{"id":"s1f8e71f4","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Quali ritocchi sono comuni nel Cognac prima della diluizione e dell'imbottigliamento?","Quelles retouches sont courantes pour le Cognac avant dilution et mise en bouteille ?","Which adjustments are common for Cognac before dilution and bottling?"],"o":[["Un po' di caramello colorante e una leggera dolcificazione","Un peu de caramel colorant et un léger sucrage","A little caramel colouring and slight sweetening"],["L'aggiunta di erbe in macerazione","L'ajout d'herbes en macération","Adding herbs by maceration"],["Una terza distillazione in colonna","Une troisième distillation en colonne","A third distillation in a column"],["Il filtraggio al carbone per togliere il colore","La filtration au charbon pour retirer la couleur","Charcoal filtering to remove the colour"]],"e":["Molti produttori usano caramello per uniformare il colore e addolciscono un poco il Cognac.","Beaucoup de producteurs utilisent du caramel pour uniformiser la couleur et sucrent un peu leur Cognac.","Many producers use caramel to even out the colour and sweeten their Cognac slightly."],"d":["Macerare erbe trasformerebbe il Cognac in un distillato aromatizzato. La distillazione avviene solo in alambicco discontinuo, mai in colonna. Togliere il colore con il carbone non ha senso per un distillato che si apprezza proprio per la tonalità data dal rovere.","Faire macérer des herbes transformerait le Cognac en spiritueux aromatisé. La distillation se fait uniquement à l'alambic à repasse, jamais en colonne. Retirer la couleur au charbon n'aurait pas de sens pour une eau-de-vie appréciée justement pour la teinte apportée par le chêne.","Macerating herbs would turn Cognac into a flavoured spirit. Distillation happens only in pot stills, never columns. Stripping colour with charcoal would make no sense for a spirit valued precisely for the shade oak gives it."]},{"id":"s11c6e825","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Che cosa garantisce la menzione VS su un Cognac?","Que garantit la mention VS sur un Cognac ?","What does the term VS guarantee on a Cognac?"],"o":[["Almeno 2 anni di invecchiamento","Au moins 2 ans de vieillissement","At least 2 years of ageing"],["Almeno 4 anni di invecchiamento","Au moins 4 ans de vieillissement","At least 4 years of ageing"],["Almeno 10 anni di invecchiamento","Au moins 10 ans de vieillissement","At least 10 years of ageing"],["Almeno 6 mesi di invecchiamento","Au moins 6 mois de vieillissement","At least 6 months of ageing"]],"e":["VS corrisponde al minimo legale: almeno 2 anni.","VS correspond au minimum légal : au moins 2 ans.","VS matches the legal minimum: at least 2 years."],"d":["4 anni è il minimo per VSOP e 10 anni quello per XO. Sei mesi sono sotto il minimo di legge: un distillato così giovane non può nemmeno chiamarsi Cognac.","4 ans est le minimum pour VSOP et 10 ans celui pour XO. Six mois sont en dessous du minimum légal : une eau-de-vie aussi jeune ne peut même pas s'appeler Cognac.","4 years is the minimum for VSOP and 10 years for XO. Six months is below the legal minimum: a spirit that young cannot even be called Cognac."]},{"id":"s15a183d9","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Qual è l'età minima garantita dalla menzione VSOP?","Quel âge minimum garantit la mention VSOP ?","What minimum age does VSOP guarantee?"],"o":[["4 anni","4 ans","4 years"],["2 anni","2 ans","2 years"],["6 anni","6 ans","6 years"],["10 anni","10 ans","10 years"]],"e":["VSOP garantisce che il distillato più giovane abbia almeno 4 anni.","VSOP garantit que l'eau-de-vie la plus jeune a au moins 4 ans.","VSOP guarantees the youngest spirit is at least 4 years old."],"d":["2 anni corrisponde a VS e 10 anni a XO. 6 anni non è una soglia legata a nessuna di queste tre menzioni: è un numero plausibile ma inventato.","2 ans correspond à VS et 10 ans à XO. 6 ans ne correspond à aucune de ces trois mentions : c'est un chiffre plausible mais inventé.","2 years is VS and 10 years is XO. 6 years is not tied to any of the three terms: it sounds plausible but is made up."]},{"id":"s1f3beaf4","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Un cliente cerca il Cognac con l'invecchiamento minimo più lungo. Quale menzione deve cercare?","Un client cherche le Cognac avec le vieillissement minimum le plus long. Quelle mention doit-il chercher ?","A customer wants the Cognac with the longest minimum ageing. Which term should they look for?"],"o":[["XO, almeno 10 anni","XO, au moins 10 ans","XO, at least 10 years"],["VSOP, almeno 4 anni","VSOP, au moins 4 ans","VSOP, at least 4 years"],["VS, almeno 2 anni","VS, au moins 2 ans","VS, at least 2 years"],["XO, almeno 6 anni","XO, au moins 6 ans","XO, at least 6 years"]],"e":["Tra le tre menzioni, XO garantisce l'età minima più alta: 10 anni.","Parmi les trois mentions, XO garantit l'âge minimum le plus élevé : 10 ans.","Of the three terms, XO guarantees the highest minimum age: 10 years."],"d":["VSOP e VS garantiscono rispettivamente 4 e 2 anni, quindi meno. L'ultima opzione indica la menzione giusta ma con un'età sbagliata: per XO il minimo è 10 anni.","VSOP et VS garantissent respectivement 4 et 2 ans, donc moins. La dernière option cite la bonne mention mais avec un âge faux : pour XO, le minimum est de 10 ans.","VSOP and VS guarantee 4 and 2 years respectively, so less. The last option names the right term with the wrong age: the XO minimum is 10 years."]},{"id":"s1ff2fdeb","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["A quale distillato si riferisce l'età indicata da VS, VSOP o XO?","À quelle eau-de-vie se rapporte l'âge indiqué par VS, VSOP ou XO ?","Which spirit does the age shown by VS, VSOP or XO refer to?"],"o":[["Al distillato più giovane dell'assemblaggio","À l'eau-de-vie la plus jeune de l'assemblage","The youngest spirit in the blend"],["Al distillato più vecchio dell'assemblaggio","À l'eau-de-vie la plus vieille de l'assemblage","The oldest spirit in the blend"],["All'età media dei distillati","À l'âge moyen des eaux-de-vie","The average age of the spirits"],["Agli anni passati in bottiglia","Aux années passées en bouteille","The years spent in the bottle"]],"e":["La menzione garantisce l'età minima, cioè quella del distillato più giovane.","La mention garantit l'âge minimum, c'est-à-dire celui de l'eau-de-vie la plus jeune.","The term guarantees a minimum age, which means the age of the youngest spirit."],"d":["Se contasse il distillato più vecchio, basterebbe una goccia antica per alzare la menzione. Anche una media permetterebbe di nascondere distillati troppo giovani. Il tempo in bottiglia non conta: l'invecchiamento avviene in botte.","Si l'on comptait l'eau-de-vie la plus vieille, une goutte ancienne suffirait à monter de catégorie. Une moyenne permettrait aussi de cacher des eaux-de-vie trop jeunes. Le temps en bouteille ne compte pas : le vieillissement se fait en fût.","If the oldest spirit counted, a single old drop could lift the category. An average would also let very young spirits hide in the blend. Time in bottle does not count: ageing happens in barrel."]},{"id":"s18887aeb","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Un assemblaggio contiene Cognac di 5, 8 e 15 anni. Quale menzione d'età più alta può portare?","Un assemblage contient des Cognacs de 5, 8 et 15 ans. Quelle mention d'âge la plus élevée peut-il porter ?","A blend contains Cognacs aged 5, 8 and 15 years. What is the highest age term it can carry?"],"o":[["VSOP","VSOP","VSOP"],["XO","XO","XO"],["VS soltanto","VS seulement","VS only"],["Nessuna menzione","Aucune mention","No age term"]],"e":["Conta il distillato più giovane, 5 anni: supera i 4 della VSOP ma non i 10 della XO.","C'est l'eau-de-vie la plus jeune qui compte, 5 ans : elle dépasse les 4 ans du VSOP mais pas les 10 ans du XO.","The youngest spirit counts, 5 years: that beats VSOP's 4 years but not XO's 10."],"d":["XO richiederebbe che anche il distillato più giovane avesse almeno 10 anni, e qui ne ha solo 5. VS sarebbe consentito, ma non è la menzione più alta possibile. Il Cognac supera ampiamente i 2 anni minimi, quindi può portare una menzione.","XO exigerait que même l'eau-de-vie la plus jeune ait au moins 10 ans, or elle n'en a que 5. VS serait autorisé, mais ce n'est pas la mention la plus élevée possible. L'assemblage dépasse largement les 2 ans minimum : il peut donc porter une mention.","XO would need even the youngest spirit to be at least 10, and here it is only 5. VS would be allowed, but it is not the highest possible term. The blend is well past the 2-year minimum, so it can carry a term."]},{"id":"s1fd5220f","c":"s1","p":0,"q":["Un distillato di vino della zona del Cognac, distillato secondo le regole, è rimasto 18 mesi in rovere. Si può vendere come Cognac?","Une eau-de-vie de vin de la zone Cognac, distillée selon les règles, a passé 18 mois en fût. Peut-on la vendre comme Cognac ?","A wine spirit from the Cognac area, distilled by the rules, has spent 18 months in oak. Can it be sold as Cognac?"],"o":[["No, deve passare almeno due anni in rovere","Non, il doit passer au moins deux ans en fût","No, it needs at least two years in oak"],["Sì, come VS","Oui, comme VS","Yes, as a VS"],["Sì, basta che sia stato distillato due volte","Oui, il suffit qu'il ait été distillé deux fois","Yes, as long as it was distilled twice"],["Sì, se gli si aggiunge caramello","Oui, si on lui ajoute du caramel","Yes, if caramel is added"]],"e":["Sotto i due anni in rovere il nome Cognac non è consentito.","En dessous de deux ans en fût, le nom Cognac n'est pas autorisé.","With less than two years in oak, the name Cognac is not allowed."],"d":["VS è la menzione più giovane ma richiede comunque almeno 2 anni. La doppia distillazione è obbligatoria ma non sostituisce l'invecchiamento. Il caramello cambia solo il colore, non l'età.","VS est la mention la plus jeune, mais elle exige quand même au moins 2 ans. La double distillation est obligatoire mais ne remplace pas le vieillissement. Le caramel ne change que la couleur, pas l'âge.","VS is the youngest term but still requires at least 2 years. Double distillation is compulsory but does not replace ageing. Caramel only changes the colour, not the age."]},{"id":"s17dce680","c":"s2","p":0,"q":["Che cosa fa di un distillato una vodka?","Qu'est-ce qui fait d'un spiritueux une vodka ?","What makes a spirit a vodka?"],"o":[["Il grado di distillazione","Le degré de distillation","Its distillation strength"],["La materia prima utilizzata","La matière première utilisée","The raw material used"],["Il paese di produzione","Le pays de production","The country of production"],["Il tempo passato in botte","Le temps passé en fût","The time spent in barrel"]],"e":["La vodka è definita dal suo grado di distillazione, molto alto.","La vodka est définie par son degré de distillation, très élevé.","Vodka is defined by its very high distillation strength."],"d":["La materia prima può essere qualsiasi e la vodka si può produrre in qualunque paese, quindi né la pianta né il luogo la definiscono. La vodka non passa in botte: resta non invecchiata.","La matière première peut être n'importe laquelle et la vodka peut être produite dans n'importe quel pays : ni la plante ni le lieu ne la définissent. La vodka ne passe pas en fût : elle reste non vieillie.","The raw material can be anything and vodka can be made in any country, so neither plant nor place defines it. Vodka does not go into barrels: it stays unaged."]},{"id":"s1c79c516","c":"s2","p":0,"q":["Con quale materia prima si può fare la vodka?","Avec quelle matière première peut-on faire de la vodka ?","Which raw material can vodka be made from?"],"o":[["Con qualsiasi materia prima vegetale","Avec n'importe quelle matière première végétale","Any plant-based raw material"],["Solo con le patate","Uniquement avec des pommes de terre","Potatoes only"],["Solo con la segale","Uniquement avec du seigle","Rye only"],["Solo con l'uva","Uniquement avec du raisin","Grapes only"]],"e":["La vodka non ha una materia prima obbligatoria: va bene qualsiasi pianta.","La vodka n'a pas de matière première obligatoire : n'importe quelle plante convient.","Vodka has no required raw material: any plant will do."],"d":["Patate e segale sono materie prime apprezzate per le vodka di qualità, ma non sono obbligatorie. L'uva è possibile anch'essa, ma non è l'unica scelta: nessun ingrediente è imposto.","Les pommes de terre et le seigle sont appréciés pour les vodkas de qualité, mais ils ne sont pas obligatoires. Le raisin est possible lui aussi, mais ce n'est pas le seul choix : aucun ingrédient n'est imposé.","Potatoes and rye are favoured for premium vodka, but they are not compulsory. Grapes are possible too, but they are not the only choice: no ingredient is required."]},{"id":"s142b07b7","c":"s2","p":0,"q":["Dove si può produrre la vodka?","Où peut-on produire de la vodka ?","Where can vodka be made?"],"o":[["In qualsiasi paese del mondo","Dans n'importe quel pays du monde","In any country in the world"],["Solo in Russia e in Polonia","Uniquement en Russie et en Pologne","Only in Russia and Poland"],["Solo nell'Europa del Nord","Uniquement en Europe du Nord","Only in northern Europe"],["Solo dove si coltivano patate","Uniquement là où l'on cultive des pommes de terre","Only where potatoes are grown"]],"e":["La vodka non ha una zona d'origine obbligatoria.","La vodka n'a pas de zone d'origine obligatoire.","Vodka has no required area of origin."],"d":["Alcuni paesi hanno una lunga tradizione di vodka, ma la legge non limita la produzione a loro né a una regione. E poiché la materia prima è libera, non serve coltivare patate per farla.","Certains pays ont une longue tradition de vodka, mais la loi ne limite la production ni à eux ni à une région. Et comme la matière première est libre, nul besoin de cultiver des pommes de terre pour en faire.","Some countries have a long vodka tradition, but the law does not restrict production to them or to any region. And since the raw material is free, there is no need to grow potatoes to make it."]},{"id":"s1a3aefe9","c":"s2","p":0,"q":["Quali materie prime sono spesso associate alle vodka di qualità più alta?","Quelles matières premières sont souvent associées aux vodkas haut de gamme ?","Which raw materials are often linked with premium vodka?"],"o":[["Cereali come orzo, frumento e segale, e patate","Céréales comme l'orge, le blé et le seigle, et pommes de terre","Cereals such as barley, wheat and rye, and potatoes"],["Canna da zucchero e melassa","Canne à sucre et mélasse","Sugar cane and molasses"],["Agave blu e mais","Agave bleu et maïs","Blue agave and corn"],["Uva e mele","Raisin et pommes","Grapes and apples"]],"e":["Cereali, soprattutto orzo, frumento e segale, e patate sono le materie prime classiche della vodka di qualità.","Les céréales, surtout l'orge, le blé et le seigle, et les pommes de terre sont les matières premières classiques de la vodka de qualité.","Cereals, especially barley, wheat and rye, plus potatoes are the classic premium vodka raw materials."],"d":["Canna da zucchero e melassa fanno pensare al rum. L'agave blu è la materia prima della Tequila. Uva e mele si possono usare, ma non sono quelle associate alla vodka di qualità.","La canne à sucre et la mélasse évoquent le rhum. L'agave bleu est la matière première de la Tequila. Le raisin et les pommes peuvent servir, mais ce ne sont pas eux qu'on associe à la vodka de qualité.","Sugar cane and molasses point to rum. Blue agave is Tequila's raw material. Grapes and apples can be used, but they are not the ones linked with premium vodka."]},{"id":"s18ea1ad2","c":"s2","p":0,"q":["A quale grado minimo deve essere distillato un distillato neutro?","À quel degré minimum doit être distillé un alcool neutre ?","To what minimum strength must a neutral spirit be distilled?"],"o":[["Al 95% o al 96% vol., secondo la legge del paese","À 95 % ou 96 % vol., selon la loi du pays","95% or 96% abv, depending on national law"],["Al 40% vol., come in bottiglia","À 40 % vol., comme en bouteille","40% abv, as in the bottle"],["Al 75% vol., come dopo una doppia distillazione","À 75 % vol., comme après une double distillation","75% abv, as after double distillation"],["Al 60% vol. in tutti i paesi","À 60 % vol. dans tous les pays","60% abv in every country"]],"e":["Un distillato neutro deve arrivare almeno al 95% o al 96%, a seconda della legge locale.","Un alcool neutre doit atteindre au moins 95 % ou 96 %, selon la loi locale.","A neutral spirit must reach at least 95% or 96%, depending on local law."],"d":["Il 40% è il grado dopo la diluizione, non quello di distillazione. Il 75% circa è tipico della doppia distillazione in alambicco discontinuo, con molti aromi. Il 60% è il grado più basso dei distillati appena fatti, i più aromatici: l'opposto del neutro.","40 % est le degré après dilution, pas celui de la distillation. Environ 75 % est typique de la double distillation à l'alambic à repasse, avec beaucoup d'arômes. 60 % est le degré le plus bas des eaux-de-vie à la sortie de l'alambic, les plus aromatiques : l'inverse du neutre.","40% is the strength after dilution, not the distillation strength. Around 75% is typical of double pot still distillation, with plenty of aroma. 60% is the lowest strength for newly made spirits, the most aromatic ones: the opposite of neutral."]},{"id":"s1a5a2e53","c":"s2","p":0,"q":["Quale tipo di alambicco è indispensabile per fare la vodka?","Quel type d'alambic est indispensable pour faire de la vodka ?","Which type of still is essential for making vodka?"],"o":[["L'alambicco a colonna","La colonne à distiller","The column still"],["L'alambicco discontinuo","L'alambic à repasse","The pot still"],["Nessun alambicco: basta la fermentazione","Aucun alambic : la fermentation suffit","No still: fermentation is enough"],["Una botte di rovere nuova","Un fût de chêne neuf","A new oak barrel"]],"e":["Solo la colonna può raggiungere il 95–96% richiesto per un distillato neutro.","Seule la colonne peut atteindre les 95–96 % exigés pour un alcool neutre.","Only a column still can reach the 95–96% needed for a neutral spirit."],"d":["Alcuni produttori usano alambicchi discontinui in una parte del processo, ma da soli non arrivano a un distillato neutro. La fermentazione si ferma intorno all'8–10%. Una botte non è un alambicco, e la vodka non passa in rovere.","Certains producteurs utilisent des alambics à repasse pour une partie du processus, mais seuls ils n'atteignent pas l'alcool neutre. La fermentation s'arrête vers 8–10 %. Un fût n'est pas un alambic, et la vodka ne passe pas en chêne.","Some producers use pot stills for part of the process, but on their own they cannot reach a neutral spirit. Fermentation stops at around 8–10%. A barrel is not a still, and vodka is not aged in oak."]},{"id":"s1465f3e5","c":"s2","p":0,"q":["Perché il distillato alla base della vodka si chiama neutro?","Pourquoi l'alcool à la base de la vodka est-il dit neutre ?","Why is the spirit behind vodka called neutral?"],"o":[["Perché a quel grado non ha quasi nessun aroma","Parce qu'à ce degré il n'a presque aucun arôme","Because at that strength it has almost no aroma"],["Perché non contiene alcol","Parce qu'il ne contient pas d'alcool","Because it contains no alcohol"],["Perché ha lo stesso grado dell'acqua","Parce qu'il a le même degré que l'eau","Because it has the same strength as water"],["Perché si può vendere in qualsiasi paese","Parce qu'on peut le vendre dans n'importe quel pays","Because it can be sold in any country"]],"e":["Distillato al 95–96%, l'alcol perde quasi tutti gli aromi e diventa neutro.","Distillé à 95–96 %, l'alcool perd presque tous ses arômes et devient neutre.","Distilled to 95–96%, the spirit loses almost all aroma and becomes neutral."],"d":["Neutro si riferisce agli aromi, non all'alcol: anzi, è uno dei distillati più forti. Non ha niente a che vedere con l'acqua o con il luogo di vendita: descrive un profumo quasi assente.","Neutre se rapporte aux arômes, pas à l'alcool : c'est même l'un des alcools les plus forts. Cela n'a rien à voir avec l'eau ni avec le lieu de vente : le mot décrit une odeur presque absente.","Neutral refers to aroma, not alcohol: in fact it is one of the strongest spirits. It has nothing to do with water or where it can be sold; it describes an almost absent smell."]},{"id":"s1334efe8","c":"s2","p":0,"q":["Che cosa succede alla vodka dopo la distillazione?","Que se passe-t-il pour la vodka après la distillation ?","What happens to vodka after distillation?"],"o":[["Resta non invecchiata e si diluisce, di solito al 40% vol.","Elle reste non vieillie et on la dilue, en général à 40 % vol.","It stays unaged and is diluted, usually to 40% abv"],["Invecchia almeno due anni in rovere","Elle vieillit au moins deux ans en fût","It ages for at least two years in oak"],["Si imbottiglia al 96% vol. senza diluizione","On la met en bouteille à 96 % vol. sans dilution","It is bottled at 96% abv without dilution"],["Si addolcisce sempre con zucchero","On la sucre toujours","It is always sweetened with sugar"]],"e":["La vodka non passa in botte e viene ridotta con acqua al grado di imbottigliamento.","La vodka ne passe pas en fût et est ramenée à son degré de mise en bouteille avec de l'eau.","Vodka skips the barrel and is brought down to bottling strength with water."],"d":["I due anni in rovere ricordano il Cognac, non la vodka. Al 96% sarebbe imbevibile: l'alcol così forte anestetizza il palato. La dolcificazione non fa parte della ricetta di base della vodka.","Les deux ans en fût rappellent le Cognac, pas la vodka. À 96 %, elle serait imbuvable : un alcool aussi fort anesthésie le palais. Le sucrage ne fait pas partie de la recette de base de la vodka.","Two years in oak describes Cognac, not vodka. At 96% it would be undrinkable, as such strong alcohol numbs the palate. Sweetening is not part of vodka's basic recipe."]},{"id":"s1312cd44","c":"s2","p":0,"q":["Perché la vodka è così diffusa nei drink miscelati e nei cocktail?","Pourquoi la vodka est-elle si répandue dans les boissons mélangées et les cocktails ?","Why is vodka so popular in mixed drinks and cocktails?"],"o":[["Perché la sua neutralità la rende versatile","Parce que sa neutralité la rend polyvalente","Because its neutrality makes it versatile"],["Perché è più dolce degli altri distillati","Parce qu'elle est plus sucrée que les autres spiritueux","Because it is sweeter than other spirits"],["Perché ha un grado più basso degli altri distillati","Parce qu'elle a un degré plus bas que les autres spiritueux","Because it is lower in alcohol than other spirits"],["Perché ha aromi di rovere molto marcati","Parce qu'elle a des arômes de chêne très marqués","Because it has strong oak aromas"]],"e":["Quasi senza profumo, la vodka si adatta a molti ingredienti senza coprirli.","Presque sans odeur, la vodka s'accorde avec de nombreux ingrédients sans les masquer.","With almost no aroma, vodka works with many ingredients without masking them."],"d":["La vodka non è dolce: come ogni distillato esce secca e di norma non viene addolcita. Di solito si imbottiglia al 40%, come molti altri distillati. E non passa in botte, quindi non ha aromi di rovere.","La vodka n'est pas sucrée : comme tout spiritueux elle sort sèche et n'est normalement pas sucrée ensuite. Elle est en général embouteillée à 40 %, comme beaucoup d'autres spiritueux. Et elle ne passe pas en fût : elle n'a donc pas d'arômes de chêne.","Vodka is not sweet: like every spirit it leaves the still dry and is not normally sweetened. It is usually bottled at 40%, like many other spirits. And it is not aged in barrels, so it has no oak aromas."]},{"id":"s151fa460","c":"s2","p":0,"q":["Una vodka mostra al naso un leggero accenno di cereale. Come va classificata?","Une vodka montre au nez une légère note de céréale. Comment la classer ?","A vodka shows a faint hint of grain on the nose. How should it be classed?"],"o":[["Ancora neutra, ma con un po' di carattere","Toujours neutre, mais avec un peu de caractère","Still neutral, but with a little character"],["Non più vodka, perché non è neutra","Plus une vodka, car elle n'est pas neutre","No longer vodka, because it is not neutral"],["Una vodka aromatizzata","Une vodka aromatisée","A flavoured vodka"],["Un whisky giovane","Un whisky jeune","A young whisky"]],"e":["Lievi note della materia prima sono ammesse: la vodka resta correttamente neutra.","De légères notes de matière première sont possibles : la vodka reste à juste titre neutre.","Faint raw-material notes are allowed: the vodka is still correctly called neutral."],"d":["Alcune vodka conservano un filo di carattere senza smettere di essere vodka. Una vodka aromatizzata ha aromi aggiunti, mentre qui il cereale viene dalla materia prima. Un whisky avrebbe aromi molto più intensi e passerebbe in rovere.","Certaines vodkas gardent une pointe de caractère sans cesser d'être des vodkas. Une vodka aromatisée a des arômes ajoutés, alors qu'ici la céréale vient de la matière première. Un whisky aurait des arômes bien plus intenses et passerait en fût de chêne.","Some vodkas keep a hint of character without ceasing to be vodka. A flavoured vodka has added flavourings, whereas here the grain note comes from the raw material. A whisky would be far more intense and aged in oak."]},{"id":"s10552583","c":"s2","p":0,"q":["Al bancone si vuole rendere più alcolico un drink alla frutta senza cambiarne il gusto. Quale distillato scegliere?","Au bar, on veut rendre un drink aux fruits plus alcoolisé sans en changer le goût. Quel spiritueux choisir ?","A bartender wants to make a fruit drink stronger without changing its taste. Which spirit fits best?"],"o":[["Una vodka neutra","Une vodka neutre","A neutral vodka"],["Un Cognac XO","Un Cognac XO","An XO Cognac"],["Un whisky di malto torbato","Un whisky de malt tourbé","A peated malt whisky"],["Una Tequila invecchiata","Une Tequila vieillie","An aged Tequila"]],"e":["La vodka neutra aggiunge alcol quasi senza aggiungere aromi.","La vodka neutre ajoute de l'alcool presque sans ajouter d'arômes.","Neutral vodka adds alcohol while adding almost no aroma."],"d":["Un Cognac XO ha aromi intensi di frutta secca, cuoio e rovere. Il whisky torbato porta note di fumo. Una Tequila invecchiata unisce agave e rovere: tutti cambierebbero il gusto del drink.","Un Cognac XO a des arômes intenses de fruits secs, de cuir et de chêne. Le whisky tourbé apporte des notes fumées. Une Tequila vieillie associe agave et chêne : tous changeraient le goût du drink.","An XO Cognac has intense dried fruit, leather and oak aromas. A peated whisky brings smoke. An aged Tequila combines agave and oak: all of them would change the drink's flavour."]},{"id":"s1db2e224","c":"s2","p":0,"q":["Un produttore ha solo alambicchi discontinui e distilla più volte. Può ottenere il distillato neutro della vodka?","Un producteur n'a que des alambics à repasse et distille plusieurs fois. Peut-il obtenir l'alcool neutre de la vodka ?","A producer has only pot stills and distils several times. Can this produce vodka's neutral spirit?"],"o":[["No, il 95–96% si raggiunge solo con la colonna","Non, les 95–96 % ne s'atteignent qu'avec une colonne","No, 95–96% can only be reached with a column still"],["Sì, basta distillare tre volte","Oui, il suffit de distiller trois fois","Yes, three distillations are enough"],["Sì, se poi diluisce con acqua","Oui, s'il dilue ensuite avec de l'eau","Yes, if water is added afterwards"],["Sì, se usa patate come materia prima","Oui, s'il utilise des pommes de terre","Yes, if potatoes are the raw material"]],"e":["Per quante volte si distilli, l'alambicco discontinuo non arriva al grado di un distillato neutro.","Même en multipliant les distillations, l'alambic à repasse n'atteint pas le degré d'un alcool neutre.","However many times it is used, a pot still cannot reach neutral-spirit strength."],"d":["Il numero di passaggi non basta: serve l'alambicco a colonna, eventualmente affiancato da alambicchi discontinui per una parte del processo. Diluire abbassa il grado, non lo alza. E la materia prima non cambia il limite dell'alambicco.","Le nombre de passages ne suffit pas : il faut une colonne, éventuellement complétée par des alambics à repasse pour une partie du processus. Diluer baisse le degré, cela ne l'augmente pas. Et la matière première ne change pas la limite de l'alambic.","The number of passes is not enough: a column still is needed, possibly alongside pot stills for part of the process. Diluting lowers the strength rather than raising it. And the raw material does not change the still's limit."]},{"id":"s163046e1","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Con quale materia prima si fa il whisky?","Avec quelle matière première fait-on le whisky ?","What raw material is whisky made from?"],"o":[["Cereali","Des céréales","Grains"],["Uva","Du raisin","Grapes"],["Canna da zucchero","De la canne à sucre","Sugar cane"],["Patate","Des pommes de terre","Potatoes"]],"e":["Il whisky è per definizione un distillato di cereali invecchiato in rovere.","Le whisky est par définition une eau-de-vie de céréales vieillie en chêne.","By definition, whisky is an oak-aged spirit made from grain."],"d":["Si può immaginare il whisky come una birra distillata: si parte da cereali come orzo, mais o segale. L'uva è la base dei brandy come il Cognac, la canna da zucchero quella del rum. Le patate possono servire per la vodka, ma non per il whisky.","On peut voir le whisky comme une bière distillée : on part de céréales comme l'orge, le maïs ou le seigle. Le raisin est la base des brandies comme le Cognac, la canne à sucre celle du rhum. Les pommes de terre peuvent servir pour la vodka, mais pas pour le whisky.","Whisky can be pictured as distilled beer: it starts from grains such as barley, corn or rye. Grapes are the base of brandies like Cognac, and sugar cane is the base of rum. Potatoes can be used for vodka, but not for whisky."]},{"id":"s1cccbe47","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Perché i cereali devono essere trattati prima della fermentazione?","Pourquoi faut-il traiter les céréales avant la fermentation ?","Why do grains need processing before fermentation?"],"o":[["Contengono amido, che va trasformato in zucchero","Elles contiennent de l'amidon, à transformer en sucre","They hold starch, which must be turned into sugar"],["Contengono troppo zucchero per i lieviti","Elles contiennent trop de sucre pour les levures","They hold too much sugar for the yeast"],["Contengono già alcol, che va eliminato","Elles contiennent déjà de l'alcool, à éliminer","They already hold alcohol, which must be removed"],["Contengono acidi che bloccano i lieviti","Elles contiennent des acides qui bloquent les levures","They hold acids that stop the yeast working"]],"e":["I lieviti si nutrono di zucchero, ma i cereali secchi contengono soprattutto amido.","Les levures se nourrissent de sucre, mais les céréales sèches contiennent surtout de l'amidon.","Yeast feed on sugar, but dry grains mostly contain starch."],"d":["I chicchi sono duri, secchi e pieni di amido. Senza la conversione in zucchero i lieviti non avrebbero nulla da trasformare in alcol. Il problema non è un eccesso di zucchero, che anzi manca, né la presenza di alcol, che compare solo con la fermentazione.","Les grains sont durs, secs et remplis d'amidon. Sans conversion en sucre, les levures n'auraient rien à transformer en alcool. Le problème n'est pas un excès de sucre, qui au contraire manque, ni la présence d'alcool, qui n'apparaît qu'avec la fermentation.","Grains are hard, dry and full of starch. Without converting it to sugar, the yeast would have nothing to turn into alcohol. The problem is not too much sugar, since sugar is actually missing, nor alcohol, which only appears during fermentation."]},{"id":"s15c908e7","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Durante la maltazione, che cosa produce l'orzo mentre germoglia?","Pendant le maltage, que produit l'orge en germant ?","During malting, what does barley produce as it grows?"],"o":[["Enzimi capaci di trasformare l'amido","Des enzymes capables de transformer l'amidon","Enzymes that can convert starch"],["Lieviti che avviano la fermentazione","Des levures qui lancent la fermentation","Yeast that starts the fermentation"],["Alcol in piccole quantità","De l'alcool en petite quantité","Small amounts of alcohol"],["Aromi affumicati naturali","Des arômes fumés naturels","Natural smoky aromas"]],"e":["Germogliando, il chicco crea enzimi che più tardi convertiranno l'amido in zucchero.","En germant, le grain crée des enzymes qui convertiront plus tard l'amidon en sucre.","As it sprouts, the grain makes enzymes that later convert starch into sugar."],"d":["Gli enzimi entrano davvero in azione quando l'orzo macinato si mescola con l'acqua. I lieviti invece si aggiungono dopo, al liquido zuccherino. Il fumo non nasce dalla germinazione: arriva solo se si brucia torba mentre si scalda l'orzo.","Les enzymes entrent vraiment en action quand l'orge broyée est mélangée à l'eau. Les levures, elles, sont ajoutées plus tard au liquide sucré. La fumée ne vient pas de la germination : elle n'apparaît que si l'on brûle de la tourbe en chauffant l'orge.","The enzymes really get to work once the crushed barley is mixed with water. Yeast, by contrast, is added later to the sugary liquid. Smoke does not come from sprouting: it only appears if peat is burned while the barley is heated."]},{"id":"s1763f97d","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Come si ferma la crescita dell'orzo alla fine della maltazione?","Comment stoppe-t-on la croissance de l'orge à la fin du maltage ?","How is the barley's growth stopped at the end of malting?"],"o":[["Con aria calda","Avec de l'air chaud","With hot air"],["Con acqua ghiacciata","Avec de l'eau glacée","With ice-cold water"],["Aggiungendo lieviti","En ajoutant des levures","By adding yeast"],["Filtrando con carbone","En filtrant sur charbon","By charcoal filtering"]],"e":["Il calore asciuga il chicco e blocca la germinazione: si ottiene l'orzo maltato.","La chaleur sèche le grain et bloque la germination : on obtient l'orge maltée.","Heat dries the grain and halts sprouting, giving malted barley."],"d":["È proprio in questa fase di riscaldamento che, in alcune distillerie, si brucia la torba per dare il fumo. L'acqua serve più tardi, quando l'orzo macinato si mescola per liberare lo zucchero. I lieviti e la filtrazione al carbone appartengono a fasi diverse della produzione.","C'est justement pendant ce chauffage que certaines distilleries brûlent de la tourbe pour apporter la fumée. L'eau intervient plus tard, quand l'orge broyée est mélangée pour libérer le sucre. Les levures et la filtration au charbon appartiennent à d'autres étapes de la production.","This heating stage is exactly when some distilleries burn peat to add smoke. Water comes in later, when the crushed barley is mixed to release its sugar. Yeast and charcoal filtering belong to other stages of production altogether."]},{"id":"s1a8c3d25","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Qual è l'invecchiamento minimo per qualsiasi Scotch whisky?","Quel est le vieillissement minimum de tout Scotch whisky ?","What is the minimum ageing for any Scotch whisky?"],"o":[["Tre anni, in Scozia","Trois ans, en Écosse","Three years, in Scotland"],["Due anni, in qualsiasi paese","Deux ans, dans n'importe quel pays","Two years, in any country"],["Tre anni, ovunque nel Regno Unito","Trois ans, partout au Royaume-Uni","Three years, anywhere in the UK"],["Dieci anni, in Scozia","Dix ans, en Écosse","Ten years, in Scotland"]],"e":["Tutto lo Scotch è distillato in Scozia e lì invecchiato per almeno tre anni.","Tout Scotch est distillé en Écosse et y vieillit au moins trois ans.","All Scotch is distilled in Scotland and aged there for at least three years."],"d":["Il luogo dell'invecchiamento conta quanto la durata: maturare altrove nel Regno Unito non basta. Due anni è il minimo del Cognac, non dello Scotch. Dieci anni ricorda la menzione XO del Cognac e non è un obbligo per il whisky scozzese.","Le lieu du vieillissement compte autant que sa durée : vieillir ailleurs au Royaume-Uni ne suffit pas. Deux ans, c'est le minimum du Cognac, pas du Scotch. Dix ans rappelle la mention XO du Cognac et n'est pas une obligation pour le whisky écossais.","Where the whisky ages matters as much as how long: maturing elsewhere in the UK is not enough. Two years is the minimum for Cognac, not Scotch. Ten years recalls the XO term for Cognac and is not a rule for Scotch."]},{"id":"s1ee1bfdb","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Quale combinazione definisce un Single Malt Scotch whisky?","Quelle combinaison définit un Single Malt Scotch whisky ?","Which combination defines a Single Malt Scotch whisky?"],"o":[["100% orzo maltato, alambicchi discontinui, una distilleria","100 % orge maltée, alambics, une seule distillerie","100% malted barley, pot stills, one distillery"],["Orzo maltato e altri cereali, colonna, una distilleria","Orge maltée et autres céréales, colonne, une distillerie","Malted barley and other grains, column still, one distillery"],["100% orzo maltato, alambicchi discontinui, più distillerie","100 % orge maltée, alambics, plusieurs distilleries","100% malted barley, pot stills, several distilleries"],["Almeno 51% orzo, qualsiasi alambicco, una distilleria","Au moins 51 % d'orge, tout appareil, une distillerie","At least 51% barley, any still, one distillery"]],"e":["Un Single Malt usa solo orzo maltato, alambicchi discontinui e una sola distilleria.","Un Single Malt n'utilise que de l'orge maltée, des alambics et une seule distillerie.","A Single Malt uses only malted barley, pot stills and one distillery."],"d":["Tutte e tre le condizioni devono essere vere insieme. Altri cereali e la colonna descrivono il whisky di cereali. Malti di più distillerie non sarebbero più 'single'. La soglia del 51% appartiene alle regole americane, come quella del Bourbon.","Les trois conditions doivent être réunies. D'autres céréales et la colonne décrivent le whisky de grain. Des malts de plusieurs distilleries ne seraient plus « single ». Le seuil de 51 % appartient aux règles américaines, comme celle du Bourbon.","All three conditions must be true together. Other grains and a column still describe grain whisky. Malts from several distilleries would no longer be 'single'. The 51% threshold belongs to American rules such as those for Bourbon."]},{"id":"s147ed1dc","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Da dove viene il sapore affumicato di alcuni Single Malt?","D'où vient le goût fumé de certains Single Malts ?","Where does the smoky flavour of some Single Malts come from?"],"o":[["Dalla torba bruciata mentre si scalda l'orzo maltato","De la tourbe brûlée pendant le chauffage de l'orge maltée","Peat burned while the malted barley is heated"],["Dalle botti nuove bruciate all'interno","Des fûts neufs brûlés à l'intérieur","New barrels charred on the inside"],["Dal whisky finito esposto al fumo","Du whisky fini exposé à la fumée","Finished whisky exposed to smoke"],["Da un filtro di carbone dopo la distillazione","D'un filtre à charbon après la distillation","A charcoal filter after distillation"]],"e":["Il fumo della torba profuma i chicchi durante il riscaldamento finale della maltazione.","La fumée de tourbe parfume les grains pendant le chauffage final du maltage.","Peat smoke flavours the grains during the final heating of malting."],"d":["Il fumo entra nel whisky prima ancora della fermentazione, attraverso l'orzo. Le botti nuove carbonizzate sono tipiche del Bourbon e portano vaniglia e cocco, non torba. La filtrazione al carbone del Tennessee whiskey toglie impurità e non aggiunge alcun sapore.","La fumée entre dans le whisky avant même la fermentation, par l'orge. Les fûts neufs brûlés sont typiques du Bourbon et apportent vanille et noix de coco, pas de tourbe. La filtration au charbon du Tennessee whiskey retire des impuretés et n'ajoute aucun goût.","The smoke enters the whisky before fermentation even begins, through the barley. New charred barrels are typical of Bourbon and give vanilla and coconut, not peat. The charcoal filtering of Tennessee whiskey removes impurities and adds no flavour."]},{"id":"s10f449c9","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Quale affermazione sui Single Malt torbati è vera?","Quelle affirmation sur les Single Malts tourbés est vraie ?","Which statement about peaty Single Malts is true?"],"o":[["Sono pochi, e alcuni hanno un fumo molto marcato","Ils sont peu nombreux, et certains sont très fumés","Only a few exist, and some are very smoky"],["La legge impone la torba a tutti i Single Malt","La loi impose la tourbe à tous les Single Malts","The law requires peat in every Single Malt"],["Quasi tutti i Single Malt sono torbati","Presque tous les Single Malts sont tourbés","Almost every Single Malt is peaty"],["La torba si aggiunge in bottiglia come aroma","La tourbe est ajoutée en bouteille comme arôme","Peat is added in the bottle as a flavouring"]],"e":["Solo una minoranza di Single Malt è torbata, a volte in modo intenso.","Seule une minorité de Single Malts est tourbée, parfois intensément.","Only a minority of Single Malts are peaty, sometimes intensely."],"d":["Il fumo è un tratto famoso ma non la regola: la maggior parte dei Single Malt sa di cereale, frutta, fiori e miele senza note affumicate. Nessuna legge rende obbligatoria la torba. E la torba non è un aroma da aggiungere: si brucia durante la maltazione.","La fumée est un trait célèbre, mais pas la règle : la plupart des Single Malts évoquent céréale, fruits, fleurs et miel, sans notes fumées. Aucune loi n'impose la tourbe. Et la tourbe n'est pas un arôme qu'on ajoute : on la brûle pendant le maltage.","Smoke is a famous trait but not the rule: most Single Malts show cereal, fruit, flowers and honey with no smoky notes. No law makes peat compulsory. And peat is not a flavouring added later; it is burned during malting."]},{"id":"s16fed636","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Come si descrive il whisky di cereali (grain whisky) scozzese?","Comment décrire le whisky de grain écossais ?","How is Scottish grain whisky best described?"],"o":[["Distillato in colonna, leggero e morbido","Distillé en colonne, léger et souple","Column-distilled, light and smooth"],["Distillato in alambicco, intenso e torbato","Distillé à l'alambic, intense et tourbé","Pot-distilled, intense and peaty"],["Fatto solo di orzo maltato, molto aromatico","Fait uniquement d'orge maltée, très aromatique","Made only from malted barley, very aromatic"],["Non invecchiato e imbottigliato subito","Non vieilli et mis en bouteille aussitôt","Unaged and bottled straight away"]],"e":["Il grain whisky esce dalla colonna con un profumo leggero e una consistenza morbida.","Le whisky de grain sort de la colonne avec un nez léger et une texture souple.","Grain whisky comes off the column still with a light aroma and smooth texture."],"d":["Si fa con orzo maltato e altri cereali, quindi non solo con orzo maltato come il Single Malt. L'intensità e il carattere tipici dell'alambicco discontinuo appartengono ai malti. Ed essendo Scotch deve invecchiare almeno tre anni, quindi non può essere imbottigliato subito.","On le fait avec de l'orge maltée et d'autres céréales, donc pas seulement avec de l'orge maltée comme le Single Malt. L'intensité et le caractère de l'alambic appartiennent aux malts. Et comme c'est du Scotch, il doit vieillir au moins trois ans : impossible de le mettre en bouteille tout de suite.","It is made from malted barley plus other grains, so not from malted barley alone like Single Malt. The intensity and character of pot stills belong to the malts. And because it is Scotch, it must age for at least three years, so it cannot be bottled straight away."]},{"id":"s12aa894e","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è un Blended Scotch whisky?","Qu'est-ce qu'un Blended Scotch whisky ?","What is a Blended Scotch whisky?"],"o":[["Malti e whisky di cereali di distillerie diverse","Des malts et whiskies de grain de distilleries différentes","Malt and grain whiskies from different distilleries"],["Più malti di una stessa distilleria","Plusieurs malts d'une même distillerie","Several malts from the same distillery"],["Solo whisky di cereali di varie età","Uniquement des whiskies de grain d'âges variés","Grain whiskies only, of various ages"],["Scotch mescolato con whiskey irlandese","Du Scotch mélangé à du whiskey irlandais","Scotch mixed with Irish whiskey"]],"e":["Il Blended unisce i due tipi di whisky scozzese, presi da più distillerie.","Le Blended réunit les deux types de whisky écossais, venant de plusieurs distilleries.","A blend combines both types of Scottish whisky from several distilleries."],"d":["Le due componenti sono indispensabili: i malti danno carattere, il whisky di cereali leggerezza e morbidezza. Più malti di una sola distilleria non formano un Blended Scotch. E per essere Scotch ogni componente deve essere distillata e invecchiata in Scozia, quindi niente whiskey irlandese.","Les deux composantes sont indispensables : les malts apportent le caractère, le whisky de grain la légèreté et la souplesse. Plusieurs malts d'une seule distillerie ne forment pas un Blended Scotch. Et pour être du Scotch, chaque composant doit être distillé et vieilli en Écosse : pas de whiskey irlandais.","Both parts are essential: malts bring character, grain whisky brings lightness and smoothness. Several malts from one distillery do not make a Blended Scotch. And to be Scotch, every part must be distilled and aged in Scotland, so Irish whiskey cannot be included."]},{"id":"s15eba9de","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Un cliente chiede uno Scotch morbido e facile, senza fumo. Che cosa conviene proporre di solito?","Un client veut un Scotch souple et facile, sans fumée. Que proposer en général ?","A customer wants a smooth, easy-going Scotch with no smoke. What is usually the best suggestion?"],"o":[["Un Blended Scotch whisky","Un Blended Scotch whisky","A Blended Scotch whisky"],["Un Single Malt molto torbato","Un Single Malt très tourbé","A heavily peated Single Malt"],["Un Single Malt vecchio e intenso","Un Single Malt âgé et intense","An old, intense Single Malt"],["Un whisky distillato in alambicco","Un whisky distillé à l'alambic","A pot-distilled whisky"]],"e":["Grazie al whisky di cereali, i Blended sono in genere più morbidi dei Single Malt.","Grâce au whisky de grain, les Blended sont en général plus souples que les Single Malts.","Thanks to grain whisky, blends are usually smoother than Single Malts."],"d":["Il grain whisky, leggero e morbido, ammorbidisce l'insieme. Un malto torbato porta proprio il fumo che il cliente vuole evitare. Malti vecchi e intensi, così come i distillati d'alambicco in generale, puntano su carattere e potenza più che sulla morbidezza.","Le whisky de grain, léger et souple, adoucit l'ensemble. Un malt tourbé apporte justement la fumée que le client veut éviter. Les malts âgés et intenses, comme les distillats d'alambic en général, misent sur le caractère et la puissance plutôt que sur la souplesse.","The light, smooth grain whisky softens the whole blend. A peaty malt brings exactly the smoke the customer wants to avoid. Old, intense malts, like pot-still spirits in general, aim for character and power rather than smoothness."]},{"id":"s1cf1379f","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["A che cosa serve soprattutto il whisky di cereali scozzese?","À quoi sert surtout le whisky de grain écossais ?","What is Scottish grain whisky mainly used for?"],"o":[["A creare i Blended Scotch","À élaborer les Blended Scotch","Making Blended Scotch"],["A essere venduto come Single Malt","À être vendu comme Single Malt","Being sold as Single Malt"],["A dare il fumo ai malti torbati","À donner la fumée aux malts tourbés","Giving smoke to peaty malts"],["A diluire lo Scotch prima dell'imbottigliamento","À diluer le Scotch avant la mise en bouteille","Diluting Scotch before bottling"]],"e":["Raramente venduto da solo, il grain whisky è la base leggera dei Blended.","Rarement vendu seul, le whisky de grain est la base légère des Blended.","Rarely sold on its own, grain whisky is the light backbone of blends."],"d":["Non può essere un Single Malt, perché contiene altri cereali e passa in colonna. Il fumo viene dalla torba, non da un altro whisky. La diluizione prima della bottiglia si fa con acqua pura, non con un altro distillato.","Il ne peut pas être un Single Malt, car il contient d'autres céréales et passe en colonne. La fumée vient de la tourbe, pas d'un autre whisky. La dilution avant la mise en bouteille se fait avec de l'eau pure, pas avec un autre spiritueux.","It cannot be a Single Malt, because it contains other grains and is column-distilled. Smoke comes from peat, not from another whisky. Dilution before bottling is done with pure water, not with another spirit."]},{"id":"s1789f37b","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Quale gruppo di aromi è tipico di un Single Malt non torbato?","Quel groupe d'arômes est typique d'un Single Malt non tourbé ?","Which set of aromas is typical of an unpeated Single Malt?"],"o":[["Cereale, frutta, fiori, miele, spezie dolci","Céréale, fruits, fleurs, miel, épices douces","Cereal, fruit, flowers, honey, sweet spice"],["Erba fresca, note vegetali e di canna","Herbe fraîche, notes végétales et de canne","Fresh grass, vegetal and cane notes"],["Ginepro, agrumi e radici","Genièvre, agrumes et racines","Juniper, citrus and roots"],["Quasi nessun aroma, stile neutro","Presque aucun arôme, style neutre","Almost no aroma, a neutral style"]],"e":["Il Single Malt è un whisky espressivo, con note di cereale, frutta, fiori, miele e spezie.","Le Single Malt est expressif, avec des notes de céréale, fruits, fleurs, miel et épices.","Single Malt is expressive, with cereal, fruit, flower, honey and spice notes."],"d":["Con l'età in botte si aggiungono anche note di torta di frutta secca. Le note erbacee di canna descrivono il rum da succo di canna, il ginepro è la firma del gin. Lo stile neutro è quello della vodka, distillata ad altissima gradazione.","Avec l'âge en fût s'ajoutent aussi des notes de cake aux fruits. Les notes herbacées de canne décrivent le rhum de jus de canne, le genièvre est la signature du gin. Le style neutre est celui de la vodka, distillée à très haut degré.","With age in the barrel, fruit cake notes join them too. Grassy cane notes describe rum made from cane juice, and juniper is the signature of gin. A neutral style belongs to vodka, distilled to a very high strength."]},{"id":"s1a3be247","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Un whisky è distillato in Scozia e poi invecchiato quattro anni in Inghilterra. Può chiamarsi Scotch?","Un whisky est distillé en Écosse puis vieilli quatre ans en Angleterre. Peut-il s'appeler Scotch ?","A whisky is distilled in Scotland, then aged four years in England. Can it be called Scotch?"],"o":[["No: anche l'invecchiamento deve avvenire in Scozia","Non : le vieillissement doit aussi avoir lieu en Écosse","No: the ageing must also take place in Scotland"],["Sì: conta solo il luogo di distillazione","Oui : seul le lieu de distillation compte","Yes: only the place of distillation counts"],["Sì, purché sia fatto con orzo maltato","Oui, à condition d'être fait d'orge maltée","Yes, as long as it is made from malted barley"],["No: lo Scotch deve invecchiare dieci anni","Non : le Scotch doit vieillir dix ans","No: Scotch must age for ten years"]],"e":["Lo Scotch deve essere sia distillato sia invecchiato in Scozia, per almeno tre anni.","Le Scotch doit être à la fois distillé et vieilli en Écosse, au moins trois ans.","Scotch must be both distilled and aged in Scotland, for at least three years."],"d":["Quattro anni sarebbero sufficienti per la durata, ma il luogo non è quello giusto. Il cereale usato non cambia questa regola, che vale per tutti gli Scotch. Il minimo è tre anni, non dieci: il problema qui è solo geografico.","Quatre ans suffiraient pour la durée, mais le lieu n'est pas le bon. La céréale utilisée ne change rien à cette règle, valable pour tous les Scotch. Le minimum est de trois ans, pas dix : ici, le problème est uniquement géographique.","Four years would be long enough, but the place is wrong. The grain used does not change this rule, which applies to every Scotch. The minimum is three years, not ten: the only problem here is geography."]},{"id":"s1a4b649b","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Su un'etichetta si legge 'Single Malt Scotch Whisky'. Che cosa si sa con certezza?","Une étiquette indique « Single Malt Scotch Whisky ». Que peut-on affirmer avec certitude ?","A label reads 'Single Malt Scotch Whisky'. What can you be sure of?"],"o":[["Viene da una sola distilleria e solo da orzo maltato","Il vient d'une seule distillerie et uniquement d'orge maltée","It comes from one distillery and only malted barley"],["Proviene da un'unica botte, senza assemblaggi","Il provient d'un seul fût, sans assemblage","It comes from a single barrel, with no blending"],["Ha un sapore affumicato di torba","Il a un goût fumé de tourbe","It has a smoky peat flavour"],["È invecchiato almeno dieci anni","Il a vieilli au moins dix ans","It has been aged at least ten years"]],"e":["'Single' significa una distilleria; 'Malt' significa solo orzo maltato, distillato in alambicco.","« Single » signifie une distillerie ; « Malt », uniquement de l'orge maltée distillée à l'alambic.","'Single' means one distillery; 'Malt' means only malted barley, pot-distilled."],"d":["Un Single Malt può comunque essere un assemblaggio di molte botti della stessa distilleria: 'single' non vuol dire una botte. Solo pochi Single Malt sono torbati, quindi il fumo non è garantito. L'età minima è tre anni, come per ogni Scotch.","Un Single Malt peut tout à fait assembler de nombreux fûts de la même distillerie : « single » ne veut pas dire un seul fût. Seuls quelques Single Malts sont tourbés, la fumée n'est donc pas garantie. L'âge minimum est de trois ans, comme pour tout Scotch.","A Single Malt can still be a blend of many barrels from the same distillery: 'single' does not mean one barrel. Only a few Single Malts are peaty, so smoke is not guaranteed. The minimum age is three years, as for every Scotch."]},{"id":"s163688dd","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Perché chi produce Blended Scotch mescola whisky di botti e distillerie diverse?","Pourquoi les producteurs de Blended Scotch assemblent-ils des whiskies de fûts et distilleries différents ?","Why do Blended Scotch producers combine whiskies from different barrels and distilleries?"],"o":[["Per ottenere costanza e complessità","Pour obtenir régularité et complexité","To achieve consistency and complexity"],["Per aumentare il grado alcolico finale","Pour augmenter le degré final","To raise the final alcohol strength"],["Per rendere il whisky incolore","Pour rendre le whisky incolore","To make the whisky colourless"],["Per accorciare l'invecchiamento obbligatorio","Pour raccourcir le vieillissement obligatoire","To shorten the required ageing time"]],"e":["L'assemblaggio rende ogni lotto simile al precedente e aggiunge profondità.","L'assemblage rend chaque lot semblable au précédent et ajoute de la profondeur.","Blending keeps each batch like the last and adds depth."],"d":["Ogni botte è unica, quindi solo mescolando si ottiene un gusto costante; unire caratteri diversi crea complessità. Il grado si regola con l'acqua, non con l'assemblaggio. Il colore non sparisce mescolando, e i tre anni minimi restano obbligatori per ogni componente.","Chaque fût est unique : seul l'assemblage donne un goût constant, et réunir des caractères différents crée de la complexité. Le degré se règle avec de l'eau, pas par l'assemblage. La couleur ne disparaît pas en assemblant, et les trois ans minimum restent obligatoires pour chaque composant.","Every barrel is unique, so blending is the way to a consistent taste, and combining different characters creates complexity. Strength is adjusted with water, not by blending. Blending does not remove colour, and the three-year minimum still applies to every component."]},{"id":"s1127fb58","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Perché il whisky viene spesso descritto come una 'birra distillata'?","Pourquoi décrit-on souvent le whisky comme une « bière distillée » ?","Why is whisky often described as 'distilled beer'?"],"o":[["Perché si distilla un liquido fermentato da cereali","Parce qu'on distille un liquide fermenté issu de céréales","Because a fermented grain liquid is distilled"],["Perché si aggiunge birra prima di imbottigliare","Parce qu'on ajoute de la bière avant la mise en bouteille","Because beer is added before bottling"],["Perché invecchia in botti usate per la birra","Parce qu'il vieillit dans des fûts ayant contenu de la bière","Because it ages in old beer barrels"],["Perché ha lo stesso grado alcolico della birra","Parce qu'il a le même degré que la bière","Because it has the same strength as beer"]],"e":["Come la birra, il whisky parte da cereali fermentati; poi quel liquido viene distillato.","Comme la bière, le whisky part de céréales fermentées ; ce liquide est ensuite distillé.","Like beer, whisky starts from fermented grain; that liquid is then distilled."],"d":["L'immagine descrive il processo: zucchero ricavato dai cereali, fermentazione, distillazione. Nessuna birra viene aggiunta al whisky finito, e la frase non parla di botti. Dopo la distillazione e la diluizione il whisky è molto più forte di qualsiasi birra, di solito 40% vol.","L'image décrit le procédé : sucre tiré des céréales, fermentation, distillation. Aucune bière n'est ajoutée au whisky fini, et l'expression ne parle pas de fûts. Après distillation et dilution, le whisky est bien plus fort que n'importe quelle bière, en général 40 % vol.","The image describes the process: sugar from grain, fermentation, distillation. No beer is added to finished whisky, and the phrase says nothing about barrels. After distilling and diluting, whisky is far stronger than any beer, usually 40% abv."]},{"id":"s18ac31ff","c":"s3","p":0,"q":["Chi assembla uno Scotch aggiunge una minuscola quantità di caramello. Qual è lo scopo?","Un assembleur ajoute une infime quantité de caramel à un Scotch. Dans quel but ?","A blender adds a tiny amount of caramel to a batch of Scotch. What is the purpose?"],"o":[["Mantenere lo stesso colore da un lotto all'altro","Garder la même couleur d'un lot à l'autre","To keep the colour the same from batch to batch"],["Rendere il whisky leggermente dolce","Rendre le whisky légèrement sucré","To make the whisky slightly sweet"],["Aggiungere un aroma di toffee","Ajouter un arôme de caramel au beurre","To add a toffee aroma"],["Accelerare l'invecchiamento in botte","Accélérer le vieillissement en fût","To speed up ageing in the barrel"]],"e":["Il colorante caramello serve solo a uniformare il colore tra lotti diversi.","Le colorant caramel sert seulement à uniformiser la couleur entre les lots.","Caramel colour is used only to even out colour between batches."],"d":["Ogni botte dà un colore leggermente diverso, e il caramello corregge queste differenze. Usato correttamente non è dolce e non aggiunge aromi, quindi non porta né zucchero né note di toffee. Non ha alcun effetto sulla maturazione, che dipende dal legno e dal tempo.","Chaque fût donne une couleur un peu différente, et le caramel corrige ces écarts. Bien utilisé, il n'est pas sucré et n'ajoute aucun arôme : ni sucre ni notes de caramel au beurre. Il n'a aucun effet sur la maturation, qui dépend du bois et du temps.","Each barrel gives a slightly different colour, and caramel corrects those differences. Used correctly it is not sweet and adds no aroma, so it brings neither sugar nor toffee notes. It has no effect on maturation, which depends on wood and time."]},{"id":"s19996f5c","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Quale cereale deve costituire almeno il 51% della ricetta di un Bourbon?","Quelle céréale doit représenter au moins 51 % de la recette d'un Bourbon ?","Which grain must make up at least 51% of a Bourbon's recipe?"],"o":[["Mais","Le maïs","Corn"],["Segale","Le seigle","Rye"],["Orzo","L'orge","Barley"],["Frumento","Le blé","Wheat"]],"e":["Il Bourbon è un whiskey a maggioranza di mais, almeno il 51%.","Le Bourbon est un whiskey à majorité de maïs, au moins 51 %.","Bourbon is a corn-majority whiskey, at least 51%."],"d":["Orzo e segale compaiono spesso nella ricetta, ma solo come cereali secondari. Se la segale arriva al 51% il whiskey diventa un Rye. L'orzo maltato al 100% è invece la regola del Single Malt scozzese.","L'orge et le seigle figurent souvent dans la recette, mais seulement comme céréales secondaires. Si le seigle atteint 51 %, le whiskey devient un Rye. L'orge maltée à 100 % est la règle du Single Malt écossais.","Barley and rye often appear in the recipe, but only as secondary grains. If rye reaches 51%, the whiskey becomes a Rye. 100% malted barley is the rule for Scottish Single Malt."]},{"id":"s1e13f16f","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Dove si può produrre il Bourbon?","Où peut-on produire du Bourbon ?","Where can Bourbon be made?"],"o":[["Ovunque negli Stati Uniti","Partout aux États-Unis","Anywhere in the USA"],["Solo in Kentucky","Uniquement au Kentucky","Only in Kentucky"],["Solo in Kentucky e Tennessee","Uniquement au Kentucky et au Tennessee","Only in Kentucky and Tennessee"],["Ovunque in Nord America","Partout en Amérique du Nord","Anywhere in North America"]],"e":["Il Bourbon si può fare in tutti gli Stati Uniti, anche se il Kentucky è lo stato leader.","Le Bourbon peut être fait dans tous les États-Unis, même si le Kentucky domine.","Bourbon can be made across the USA, though Kentucky leads production."],"d":["L'associazione con il Kentucky è forte perché lì se ne produce di più, ma non è un obbligo. È il Tennessee whiskey a essere legato a un solo stato. Fuori dagli Stati Uniti, per esempio in Canada, non si può fare Bourbon.","L'association avec le Kentucky est forte parce qu'on y en produit le plus, mais ce n'est pas une obligation. C'est le Tennessee whiskey qui est lié à un seul État. Hors des États-Unis, au Canada par exemple, on ne peut pas faire de Bourbon.","The link with Kentucky is strong because most Bourbon is made there, but it is not a requirement. It is Tennessee whiskey that is tied to one state. Outside the USA, in Canada for example, Bourbon cannot be made."]},{"id":"s166fc8f5","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["In quali botti deve invecchiare il Bourbon?","Dans quels fûts le Bourbon doit-il vieillir ?","What barrels must Bourbon be aged in?"],"o":[["Rovere nuovo carbonizzato","Chêne neuf brûlé","New charred oak"],["Rovere usato in precedenza","Chêne ayant déjà servi","Previously used oak"],["Ex botti di Cognac","Anciens fûts de Cognac","Former Cognac barrels"],["Rovere nuovo non tostato","Chêne neuf non brûlé","New uncharred oak"]],"e":["La legge impone botti di rovere nuovo, bruciate all'interno.","La loi impose des fûts de chêne neuf, brûlés à l'intérieur.","The law requires new oak barrels charred on the inside."],"d":["Le botti usate cedono meno aromi a ogni utilizzo, quindi non sono ammesse per il Bourbon. Anche una botte nuova non basta se non è carbonizzata. Questa scelta spiega il colore intenso e le note marcate di vaniglia e cocco del Bourbon.","Les fûts usagés cèdent moins d'arômes à chaque utilisation : ils ne sont pas admis pour le Bourbon. Même un fût neuf ne suffit pas s'il n'est pas brûlé. Ce choix explique la couleur intense et les notes marquées de vanille et de noix de coco du Bourbon.","Used barrels give less aroma each time they are used, so they are not allowed for Bourbon. Even a new barrel is not enough unless it is charred. This choice explains Bourbon's deep colour and strong vanilla and coconut notes."]},{"id":"s18e6108c","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi sono tipici di un Bourbon?","Quels arômes sont typiques d'un Bourbon ?","Which aromas are typical of a Bourbon?"],"o":[["Mais dolce, vaniglia, cocco, frutta","Maïs doux, vanille, noix de coco, fruits","Sweetcorn, vanilla, coconut, fruit"],["Fumo di torba, cereale, miele","Fumée de tourbe, céréale, miel","Peat smoke, cereal, honey"],["Erba, vegetale, canna fresca","Herbe, végétal, canne fraîche","Grass, vegetal, fresh cane"],["Agave, pepe, oliva","Agave, poivre, olive","Agave, pepper, olive"]],"e":["Il mais dà le note di mais dolce; le botti nuove carbonizzate vaniglia e cocco.","Le maïs donne les notes de maïs doux ; les fûts neufs brûlés, vanille et coco.","Corn gives sweetcorn notes; new charred barrels give vanilla and coconut."],"d":["Il fumo di torba appartiene ad alcuni Single Malt scozzesi. Le note erbacee di canna sono tipiche del rum da succo di canna. Agave, pepe e oliva descrivono la Tequila.","La fumée de tourbe appartient à certains Single Malts écossais. Les notes herbacées de canne sont typiques du rhum de jus de canne. Agave, poivre et olive décrivent la Tequila.","Peat smoke belongs to some Scottish Single Malts. Grassy cane notes are typical of rum made from cane juice. Agave, pepper and olive describe Tequila."]},{"id":"s18500fe7","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Come si distilla di solito il Bourbon?","Comment le Bourbon est-il généralement distillé ?","How is Bourbon usually distilled?"],"o":[["In colonna, fino a una gradazione bassa","En colonne, jusqu'à un degré bas","In a column still, to a low strength"],["In colonna, fino a 96% vol","En colonne, jusqu'à 96 % vol","In a column still, up to 96% abv"],["Due volte in alambicco discontinuo per legge","Deux fois à l'alambic, par obligation légale","Twice in a pot still, by law"],["In colonna corta, poi filtrato su carbone","En colonne courte, puis filtré au charbon","In a short column, then charcoal filtered"]],"e":["Si usa di solito la colonna, ma fermandosi a bassa gradazione per conservare il sapore.","On utilise d'habitude la colonne, mais à bas degré pour garder le goût.","A column still is normal, but stopped at low strength to keep flavour."],"d":["A 96% vol si otterrebbe uno spirito neutro, come quello della vodka, e il Bourbon perderebbe il suo carattere intenso. La doppia distillazione in alambicco obbligatoria è la regola del Cognac. La filtrazione su carbone d'acero è il passaggio distintivo del Tennessee whiskey.","À 96 % vol, on obtiendrait un spiritueux neutre comme celui de la vodka, et le Bourbon perdrait son caractère intense. La double distillation obligatoire à l'alambic est la règle du Cognac. La filtration sur charbon d'érable est l'étape distinctive du Tennessee whiskey.","At 96% abv you would get a neutral spirit like vodka's, and Bourbon would lose its pronounced character. Compulsory double pot distillation is the rule for Cognac. Maple charcoal filtering is the signature step of Tennessee whiskey."]},{"id":"s1cc66202","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Un cliente dice che il Bourbon 'sa di dolce'. Quale spiegazione è corretta?","Un client trouve que le Bourbon « fait sucré ». Quelle explication est correcte ?","A customer says Bourbon 'tastes sweet'. Which explanation is correct?"],"o":[["Non ha zucchero aggiunto: vaniglia e frutta danno quell'impressione","Il n'a pas de sucre ajouté : vanille et fruits donnent cette impression","It has no added sugar; vanilla and fruit aromas create that impression"],["Dopo l'invecchiamento si aggiunge sempre zucchero","On ajoute toujours du sucre après le vieillissement","Sugar is always added after ageing"],["Lo zucchero del mais sopravvive alla distillazione","Le sucre du maïs survit à la distillation","Sugar from the corn survives distillation"],["Le botti nuove cedono zucchero al whiskey","Les fûts neufs cèdent du sucre au whiskey","New barrels release sugar into the whiskey"]],"e":["Il Bourbon è secco: la 'dolcezza' percepita viene da aromi, non da zucchero.","Le Bourbon est sec : la « douceur » perçue vient d'arômes, pas de sucre.","Bourbon is dry: the perceived 'sweetness' comes from aromas, not sugar."],"d":["Ogni distillato appena uscito dall'alambicco è secco, e nel Bourbon non si aggiunge zucchero dopo. Le botti cedono colore e aromi come vaniglia e cocco, che il naso associa ai dolci, ma non zucchero.","Tout spiritueux qui sort de l'alambic est sec, et on n'ajoute pas de sucre au Bourbon ensuite. Les fûts cèdent couleur et arômes comme la vanille et la noix de coco, que le nez associe aux desserts, mais pas de sucre.","Every spirit is dry when it comes off the still, and no sugar is added to Bourbon afterwards. Barrels give colour and aromas such as vanilla and coconut, which the nose links with desserts, but not sugar."]},{"id":"s1218027f","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Rispetto a una botte già usata, una botte nuova cede allo spirito...","Par rapport à un fût déjà utilisé, un fût neuf donne au spiritueux...","Compared with a used barrel, a new barrel gives a spirit..."],"o":[["più colore e più aromi","plus de couleur et d'arômes","more colour and more aroma"],["meno colore e meno aromi","moins de couleur et d'arômes","less colour and less aroma"],["più zucchero e più dolcezza","plus de sucre et de douceur","more sugar and sweetness"],["solo colore, senza aromi","seulement de la couleur, sans arômes","only colour, no aroma"]],"e":["Una botte mai usata è quella che cede di più; ogni riutilizzo ne riduce l'effetto.","Un fût jamais utilisé est celui qui cède le plus ; chaque réemploi réduit son effet.","A never-used barrel gives the most; each reuse weakens its effect."],"d":["Per questo il Bourbon, che deve usare botti nuove, ha colore e aromi di rovere così evidenti. Le botti non aggiungono zucchero: la dolcezza viene solo da zucchero aggiunto dopo la distillazione. E una botte nuova porta sempre anche aromi, come vaniglia e cocco.","C'est pourquoi le Bourbon, obligé d'utiliser des fûts neufs, a une couleur et des arômes boisés si marqués. Les fûts n'ajoutent pas de sucre : la douceur ne vient que du sucre ajouté après la distillation. Et un fût neuf apporte toujours aussi des arômes, comme la vanille et la noix de coco.","That is why Bourbon, which must use new barrels, shows such clear oak colour and aromas. Barrels do not add sugar: sweetness only comes from sugar added after distillation. And a new barrel always brings aromas too, such as vanilla and coconut."]},{"id":"s16fcac66","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Che cosa distingue il Tennessee whiskey dal Bourbon nella produzione?","Qu'est-ce qui distingue le Tennessee whiskey du Bourbon dans la production ?","What sets Tennessee whiskey apart from Bourbon in production?"],"o":[["Una filtrazione su carbone d'acero prima della botte","Une filtration sur charbon d'érable avant le fût","Maple charcoal filtering before the barrel"],["Una ricetta con almeno il 51% di segale","Une recette avec au moins 51 % de seigle","A recipe with at least 51% rye"],["L'invecchiamento in botti già usate","Le vieillissement en fûts déjà utilisés","Ageing in previously used barrels"],["La doppia distillazione in alambicco","La double distillation à l'alambic","Double distillation in a pot still"]],"e":["Il distillato nuovo passa nel carbone d'acero prima di entrare in botte.","Le distillat neuf passe sur charbon d'érable avant d'entrer en fût.","The new spirit runs through maple charcoal before it goes into the barrel."],"d":["Per il resto il Tennessee whiskey segue le regole del Bourbon: maggioranza di mais, colonna a bassa gradazione, botti nuove carbonizzate. La segale al 51% definisce il Rye. Botti usate e doppia distillazione in alambicco non fanno parte delle sue regole.","Pour le reste, le Tennessee whiskey suit les règles du Bourbon : majorité de maïs, colonne à bas degré, fûts neufs brûlés. Le seigle à 51 % définit le Rye. Les fûts usagés et la double distillation à l'alambic ne font pas partie de ses règles.","Otherwise Tennessee whiskey follows Bourbon's rules: mostly corn, low-strength column distillation, new charred barrels. 51% rye defines Rye whiskey. Used barrels and double pot distillation are not part of its rules."]},{"id":"s14d0d269","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Qual è l'effetto della filtrazione su carbone d'acero del Tennessee whiskey?","Quel est l'effet de la filtration sur charbon d'érable du Tennessee whiskey ?","What does the maple charcoal filtering of Tennessee whiskey do?"],"o":[["Toglie impurità e lo rende più morbido, senza aggiungere sapore","Retire des impuretés et l'assouplit, sans ajouter de goût","Removes impurities and smooths it, adding no flavour"],["Aggiunge un leggero sapore di sciroppo d'acero","Ajoute un léger goût de sirop d'érable","Adds a light maple syrup flavour"],["Aggiunge note affumicate simili alla torba","Ajoute des notes fumées proches de la tourbe","Adds smoky, peat-like notes"],["Toglie tutto il colore dato dalla botte","Retire toute la couleur donnée par le fût","Removes all the colour from the barrel"]],"e":["Il carbone trattiene parte delle impurità e ammorbidisce, ma non dà aromi.","Le charbon retient une partie des impuretés et assouplit, sans donner d'arômes.","The charcoal holds back some impurities and smooths, but adds no aroma."],"d":["Il nome 'acero' trae in inganno: il carbone non trasmette alcun gusto di sciroppo né di fumo. Inoltre la filtrazione avviene prima della botte, sul distillato ancora incolore, quindi non può togliere un colore che non c'è ancora.","Le mot « érable » est trompeur : le charbon ne transmet aucun goût de sirop ni de fumée. De plus, la filtration a lieu avant le fût, sur un distillat encore incolore : elle ne peut donc pas retirer une couleur qui n'existe pas encore.","The word 'maple' is misleading: the charcoal passes on no syrup or smoke flavour. Also, the filtering happens before the barrel, on a spirit that is still colourless, so it cannot remove colour that is not there yet."]},{"id":"s1a136449","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Dove si può produrre il Tennessee whiskey?","Où peut-on produire du Tennessee whiskey ?","Where can Tennessee whiskey be made?"],"o":[["Solo nello stato del Tennessee","Uniquement dans l'État du Tennessee","Only in the state of Tennessee"],["Ovunque negli Stati Uniti","Partout aux États-Unis","Anywhere in the USA"],["In Tennessee o in Kentucky","Au Tennessee ou au Kentucky","In Tennessee or Kentucky"],["Ovunque, se filtrato su carbone d'acero","Partout, s'il est filtré sur charbon d'érable","Anywhere, if maple charcoal filtered"]],"e":["Il nome è legato allo stato: il Tennessee whiskey si fa solo in Tennessee.","Le nom est lié à l'État : le Tennessee whiskey ne se fait qu'au Tennessee.","The name is tied to the state: it can only be made in Tennessee."],"d":["È il Bourbon a poter essere prodotto in tutti gli Stati Uniti. Il Kentucky è il cuore del Bourbon, non del Tennessee whiskey. La filtrazione su carbone è necessaria ma non sufficiente: senza il luogo giusto il nome non si può usare.","C'est le Bourbon qui peut être produit dans tous les États-Unis. Le Kentucky est le cœur du Bourbon, pas du Tennessee whiskey. La filtration au charbon est nécessaire mais pas suffisante : sans le bon lieu, le nom ne peut pas être utilisé.","It is Bourbon that can be made anywhere in the USA. Kentucky is the heart of Bourbon, not of Tennessee whiskey. Charcoal filtering is necessary but not enough: without the right place, the name cannot be used."]},{"id":"s13d23463","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Che cosa definisce un Rye whiskey americano?","Qu'est-ce qui définit un Rye whiskey américain ?","What defines an American Rye whiskey?"],"o":[["Almeno 51% segale; aromi speziati e pepati","Au moins 51 % de seigle ; arômes épicés et poivrés","At least 51% rye; spicy, peppery aromas"],["100% segale e note affumicate","100 % seigle et notes fumées","100% rye and smoky notes"],["Almeno 51% mais; note di cocco","Au moins 51 % de maïs ; notes de coco","At least 51% corn; coconut notes"],["Almeno 51% segale; note erbacee di canna","Au moins 51 % de seigle ; notes herbacées de canne","At least 51% rye; grassy cane notes"]],"e":["Il Rye ha almeno il 51% di segale, che dà un carattere speziato e pepato.","Le Rye contient au moins 51 % de seigle, qui donne un caractère épicé et poivré.","Rye has at least 51% rye grain, giving a spicy, peppery character."],"d":["La soglia è il 51%, non il 100%, e il fumo non c'entra. Il 51% di mais definisce il Bourbon. Le note erbacee di canna appartengono al rum da succo di canna, non a un whiskey di cereali.","Le seuil est de 51 %, pas de 100 %, et la fumée n'a rien à voir. Les 51 % de maïs définissent le Bourbon. Les notes herbacées de canne appartiennent au rhum de jus de canne, pas à un whiskey de céréales.","The threshold is 51%, not 100%, and smoke has nothing to do with it. 51% corn defines Bourbon. Grassy cane notes belong to rum made from cane juice, not to a grain whiskey."]},{"id":"s111784b9","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Chi lavora al bar vuole un whiskey americano dal carattere speziato e pepato. Quale scegliere?","Au bar, on cherche un whiskey américain au caractère épicé et poivré. Lequel choisir ?","A bartender wants an American whiskey with a spicy, peppery character. Which should they choose?"],"o":[["Rye whiskey","Un Rye whiskey","Rye whiskey"],["Bourbon","Un Bourbon","Bourbon"],["Tennessee whiskey","Un Tennessee whiskey","Tennessee whiskey"],["Un whiskey irlandese leggero","Un whiskey irlandais léger","A light Irish whiskey"]],"e":["La segale, cereale principale del Rye, dà aromi speziati e pepati.","Le seigle, céréale principale du Rye, donne des arômes épicés et poivrés.","Rye grain, the main grain in Rye whiskey, gives spicy, peppery aromas."],"d":["Bourbon e Tennessee whiskey sono a maggioranza di mais, quindi più orientati su mais dolce, vaniglia e cocco. Un whiskey irlandese leggero e morbido non è americano e non ha questo profilo pepato.","Le Bourbon et le Tennessee whiskey sont à majorité de maïs, donc plutôt tournés vers le maïs doux, la vanille et la noix de coco. Un whiskey irlandais léger et souple n'est pas américain et n'a pas ce profil poivré.","Bourbon and Tennessee whiskey are mostly corn, so they lean towards sweetcorn, vanilla and coconut. A light, smooth Irish whiskey is not American and does not have this peppery profile."]},{"id":"s19c9ca89","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Qual è l'unica regola che separa il Rye whiskey americano dal Bourbon?","Quelle est la seule règle qui sépare le Rye whiskey américain du Bourbon ?","What is the only rule that separates American Rye whiskey from Bourbon?"],"o":[["Il cereale principale della ricetta","La céréale principale de la recette","The main grain in the recipe"],["Il tipo di botte usata","Le type de fût utilisé","The type of barrel used"],["Il tipo di alambicco usato","Le type d'appareil de distillation","The type of still used"],["Lo stato in cui si produce","L'État où il est produit","The state where it is made"]],"e":["Il Rye si fa esattamente come il Bourbon, ma con la segale al posto del mais.","Le Rye se fait exactement comme le Bourbon, mais avec du seigle à la place du maïs.","Rye is made exactly like Bourbon, but with rye instead of corn."],"d":["Entrambi usano botti di rovere nuovo carbonizzato e, di solito, la colonna a bassa gradazione. Nessuno dei due è legato a un solo stato: è il Tennessee whiskey ad avere un vincolo geografico. Cambia solo il cereale che supera il 51%.","Les deux utilisent des fûts de chêne neuf brûlé et, en général, la colonne à bas degré. Aucun n'est lié à un seul État : c'est le Tennessee whiskey qui a une contrainte géographique. Seule change la céréale qui dépasse 51 %.","Both use new charred oak barrels and usually low-strength column distillation. Neither is tied to one state; it is Tennessee whiskey that has a geographical limit. Only the grain that makes up 51% changes."]},{"id":"s11de22c9","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Come si fa la maggior parte dei whiskey irlandesi?","Comment la plupart des whiskeys irlandais sont-ils faits ?","How are most Irish whiskeys made?"],"o":[["Unendo distillati d'alambicco e di colonna","En assemblant distillats d'alambic et de colonne","By blending pot-still and column-still spirits"],["Solo con orzo maltato e torba","Uniquement avec de l'orge maltée et de la tourbe","Only from malted barley and peat"],["Con il 51% di mais in botti nuove","Avec 51 % de maïs en fûts neufs","With 51% corn in new barrels"],["Senza invecchiamento in rovere","Sans vieillissement en chêne","Without any oak ageing"]],"e":["La maggior parte dei whiskey irlandesi unisce spiriti d'alambicco e di colonna.","La plupart des whiskeys irlandais assemblent distillats d'alambic et de colonne.","Most Irish whiskeys combine pot-still and column-still spirits."],"d":["Il risultato tipico è un whiskey leggero e morbido. La torba è legata ad alcuni Single Malt scozzesi, il 51% di mais con botti nuove al Bourbon. Come tutti i whisky, anche quelli irlandesi invecchiano in rovere.","Le résultat typique est un whiskey léger et souple. La tourbe est liée à certains Single Malts écossais, les 51 % de maïs en fûts neufs au Bourbon. Comme tous les whiskies, les irlandais vieillissent en chêne.","The typical result is a light, smooth whiskey. Peat belongs to some Scottish Single Malts, and 51% corn with new barrels to Bourbon. Like all whiskies, Irish whiskeys are aged in oak."]},{"id":"s1466cf92","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Quale carattere dà l'orzo non maltato ad alcuni whiskey irlandesi d'alambicco?","Quel caractère l'orge non maltée donne-t-elle à certains whiskeys irlandais d'alambic ?","What character does unmalted barley give some Irish pot-still whiskeys?"],"o":[["Note di frutta secca e consistenza oleosa","Notes de fruits secs et texture huileuse","Nutty notes and an oily texture"],["Note affumicate e medicinali","Notes fumées et médicinales","Smoky, medicinal notes"],["Note speziate e pepate","Notes épicées et poivrées","Spicy, peppery notes"],["Note di mais dolce e cocco","Notes de maïs doux et de coco","Sweetcorn and coconut notes"]],"e":["L'orzo non maltato porta un carattere di frutta secca e una texture oleosa.","L'orge non maltée apporte un caractère de fruits secs et une texture huileuse.","Unmalted barley brings a nutty character and an oily texture."],"d":["È un ingrediente insolito, usato solo in alcuni whiskey irlandesi distillati in alambicco. Il fumo viene dalla torba, il pepe dalla segale, mais dolce e cocco da mais e botti nuove come nel Bourbon.","C'est un ingrédient inhabituel, utilisé seulement dans certains whiskeys irlandais distillés à l'alambic. La fumée vient de la tourbe, le poivre du seigle, le maïs doux et la noix de coco du maïs et des fûts neufs comme dans le Bourbon.","It is an unusual ingredient, used only in some Irish whiskeys made in pot stills. Smoke comes from peat, pepper from rye, and sweetcorn and coconut from corn and new barrels as in Bourbon."]},{"id":"s158cbf8b","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Qual è il sapore distintivo dei migliori whisky canadesi?","Quelle est la saveur signature des meilleurs whiskies canadiens ?","What is the signature flavour of the best Canadian whiskies?"],"o":[["La segale","Le seigle","Rye"],["La torba","La tourbe","Peat"],["Il mais","Le maïs","Corn"],["L'orzo non maltato","L'orge non maltée","Unmalted barley"]],"e":["La segale, speziata e pepata, è la firma dei whisky canadesi migliori.","Le seigle, épicé et poivré, est la signature des meilleurs whiskies canadiens.","Spicy, peppery rye is the signature of the best Canadian whiskies."],"d":["Il Canada usa molti cereali diversi, ma è la segale a dare il carattere più riconoscibile. La torba è tipica di alcuni malti scozzesi. Il mais domina il Bourbon, l'orzo non maltato è una particolarità irlandese.","Le Canada utilise beaucoup de céréales différentes, mais c'est le seigle qui donne le caractère le plus reconnaissable. La tourbe est typique de certains malts écossais. Le maïs domine le Bourbon, l'orge non maltée est une particularité irlandaise.","Canada uses many different grains, but rye gives the most recognisable character. Peat is typical of some Scottish malts. Corn dominates Bourbon, and unmalted barley is an Irish speciality."]},{"id":"s1d38d311","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Quale descrizione corrisponde a un tipico whisky canadese?","Quelle description correspond à un whisky canadien typique ?","Which description fits a typical Canadian whisky?"],"o":[["Molti cereali; miscela di spiriti ad alta e bassa gradazione","Plusieurs céréales ; assemblage de spiritueux à haut et bas degré","Many grains; a blend of high- and low-strength spirits"],["Solo orzo maltato, alambicco, una distilleria","Uniquement orge maltée, alambic, une distillerie","Malted barley only, pot still, one distillery"],["51% mais e filtrazione su carbone d'acero","51 % de maïs et filtration au charbon d'érable","51% corn and maple charcoal filtering"],["Distillato neutro a 96% e non invecchiato","Distillat neutre à 96 % et non vieilli","Neutral spirit at 96%, unaged"]],"e":["Il Canada usa più cereali e unisce spiriti leggeri e spiriti più saporiti.","Le Canada utilise plusieurs céréales et assemble spiritueux légers et plus savoureux.","Canada uses several grains and blends lighter and more flavourful spirits."],"d":["Solo orzo maltato da una distilleria descrive un Single Malt. Mais più carbone d'acero è il profilo del Tennessee whiskey. Uno spirito neutro non invecchiato è la base della vodka, mentre ogni whisky passa in rovere.","Uniquement de l'orge maltée d'une distillerie, c'est un Single Malt. Maïs plus charbon d'érable, c'est le profil du Tennessee whiskey. Un spiritueux neutre non vieilli est la base de la vodka, alors que tout whisky passe en chêne.","Malted barley only from one distillery describes a Single Malt. Corn plus maple charcoal is the profile of Tennessee whiskey. An unaged neutral spirit is the base of vodka, while every whisky spends time in oak."]},{"id":"s1744cb93","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["A quale paese si è ispirata l'industria del whisky giapponese?","Sur quel pays l'industrie du whisky japonais s'est-elle modelée ?","Which country was Japanese whisky production modelled on?"],"o":[["La Scozia","L'Écosse","Scotland"],["Gli Stati Uniti","Les États-Unis","The USA"],["L'Irlanda","L'Irlande","Ireland"],["Il Canada","Le Canada","Canada"]],"e":["Il whisky giapponese segue il modello scozzese, con malti e blended.","Le whisky japonais suit le modèle écossais, avec malts et blends.","Japanese whisky follows the Scottish model, with malts and blends."],"d":["Come in Scozia, in Giappone si producono whisky di malto e whisky blended. Gli Stati Uniti hanno un modello diverso, basato su mais o segale e botti nuove. Irlanda e Canada hanno tradizioni proprie, con miscele di spiriti diversi.","Comme en Écosse, le Japon produit des whiskies de malt et des blends. Les États-Unis ont un modèle différent, fondé sur le maïs ou le seigle et les fûts neufs. L'Irlande et le Canada ont leurs propres traditions, avec des assemblages de spiritueux différents.","As in Scotland, Japan makes malt whiskies and blended whiskies. The USA has a different model based on corn or rye and new barrels. Ireland and Canada have their own traditions of blending different spirits."]},{"id":"s12d09691","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Come si descrive lo stile tradizionale del whisky giapponese?","Comment décrire le style traditionnel du whisky japonais ?","How is the traditional style of Japanese whisky described?"],"o":[["Elegante e raffinato","Élégant et raffiné","Elegant and refined"],["Molto dolce per lo zucchero aggiunto","Très sucré grâce au sucre ajouté","Very sweet from added sugar"],["Pepato, a base di segale","Poivré, à base de seigle","Peppery and rye-based"],["Neutro, quasi senza aromi","Neutre, presque sans arômes","Neutral, with almost no aroma"]],"e":["Tradizionalmente i whisky giapponesi sono eleganti e raffinati.","Traditionnellement, les whiskies japonais sont élégants et raffinés.","Traditionally, Japanese whiskies are elegant and refined."],"d":["Oggi molti produttori esplorano anche stili nuovi, ma l'impronta classica resta l'eleganza. Lo zucchero aggiunto non fa parte del profilo tipico. La segale è la firma del Canada e del Rye americano, e uno stile neutro descrive la vodka.","Aujourd'hui, beaucoup de producteurs explorent aussi de nouveaux styles, mais la marque classique reste l'élégance. Le sucre ajouté ne fait pas partie du profil typique. Le seigle est la signature du Canada et du Rye américain, et un style neutre décrit la vodka.","Today many producers are also exploring new styles, but the classic hallmark remains elegance. Added sugar is not part of the typical profile. Rye is the signature of Canada and American Rye, and a neutral style describes vodka."]},{"id":"s1be04f56","c":"s4","p":0,"q":["Un whiskey del Kentucky: 70% mais, colonna a bassa gradazione, rovere nuovo carbonizzato, nessuna filtrazione su carbone. Che cos'è?","Un whiskey du Kentucky : 70 % de maïs, colonne à bas degré, chêne neuf brûlé, pas de filtration au charbon. Qu'est-ce que c'est ?","A Kentucky whiskey: 70% corn, low-strength column still, new charred oak, no charcoal filtering. What is it?"],"o":[["Un Bourbon","Un Bourbon","A Bourbon"],["Un Tennessee whiskey","Un Tennessee whiskey","A Tennessee whiskey"],["Un Rye whiskey","Un Rye whiskey","A Rye whiskey"],["Un whisky canadese","Un whisky canadien","A Canadian whisky"]],"e":["Maggioranza di mais, botti nuove carbonizzate e prodotto negli USA: tutte le regole del Bourbon.","Majorité de maïs, fûts neufs brûlés, produit aux États-Unis : toutes les règles du Bourbon.","Mostly corn, new charred barrels, made in the USA: every Bourbon rule is met."],"d":["Per essere Tennessee whiskey servirebbero la filtrazione su carbone d'acero e la produzione in Tennessee: qui mancano entrambe. Con il 70% di mais non può essere un Rye, che richiede il 51% di segale. E il Kentucky non è in Canada.","Pour être un Tennessee whiskey, il faudrait la filtration au charbon d'érable et une production au Tennessee : ici, les deux manquent. Avec 70 % de maïs, ce ne peut pas être un Rye, qui exige 51 % de seigle. Et le Kentucky n'est pas au Canada.","To be Tennessee whiskey it would need maple charcoal filtering and to be made in Tennessee; both are missing here. With 70% corn it cannot be a Rye, which needs 51% rye. And Kentucky is not in Canada."]},{"id":"s14bb30be","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Qual è la materia prima del rum?","Quelle est la matière première du rhum ?","What is the raw material of rum?"],"o":[["La canna da zucchero","La canne à sucre","Sugar cane"],["I cereali","Les céréales","Grains"],["L'agave blu","L'agave bleu","Blue agave"],["L'uva","Le raisin","Grapes"]],"e":["Il rum si ricava dalla canna da zucchero, come succo o come melassa.","Le rhum est issu de la canne à sucre, sous forme de jus ou de mélasse.","Rum comes from sugar cane, used as juice or as molasses."],"d":["I cereali sono la base del whisky, l'agave blu quella della Tequila e l'uva quella dei brandy come il Cognac. La canna può essere usata fresca, spremendone il succo, oppure sotto forma di melassa.","Les céréales sont la base du whisky, l'agave bleu celle de la Tequila et le raisin celle des brandies comme le Cognac. La canne peut être utilisée fraîche, en pressant son jus, ou sous forme de mélasse.","Grains are the base of whisky, blue agave of Tequila and grapes of brandies such as Cognac. Cane can be used fresh, by crushing out its juice, or in the form of molasses."]},{"id":"s1540c8d2","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Perché la produzione di rum si concentra in zone come i Caraibi?","Pourquoi la production de rhum se concentre-t-elle dans des régions comme la Caraïbe ?","Why is rum production centred on places like the Caribbean?"],"o":[["La canna da zucchero cresce nei climi caldi","La canne à sucre pousse en climat chaud","Sugar cane grows in hot climates"],["Solo lì sono permesse le colonne","Seules les colonnes y sont autorisées","Column stills are only allowed there"],["La legge vieta il rum fuori dai Caraibi","La loi interdit le rhum hors de la Caraïbe","The law bans rum outside the Caribbean"],["Il caldo accelera l'invecchiamento","La chaleur accélère le vieillissement","Heat speeds up ageing"]],"e":["Il rum si produce dove cresce la canna, cioè nei paesi caldi.","On produit le rhum là où pousse la canne, donc dans les pays chauds.","Rum is made where cane grows, which means hot countries."],"d":["La ragione è agricola: la materia prima ha bisogno di calore. Non esiste una legge che riservi il rum ai Caraibi, e le colonne si usano in tutto il mondo. L'idea dell'invecchiamento più rapido non è il motivo per cui il rum nasce in queste zone.","La raison est agricole : la matière première a besoin de chaleur. Aucune loi ne réserve le rhum à la Caraïbe, et les colonnes sont utilisées partout dans le monde. L'idée d'un vieillissement plus rapide n'explique pas pourquoi le rhum naît dans ces régions.","The reason is agricultural: the raw material needs heat. No law reserves rum for the Caribbean, and column stills are used all over the world. The idea of faster ageing is not why rum is made in these areas."]},{"id":"s155d3a51","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è la melassa?","Qu'est-ce que la mélasse ?","What is molasses?"],"o":[["Un sottoprodotto nero e denso della produzione di zucchero","Un sous-produit noir et épais de la fabrication du sucre","A black, sticky by-product of sugar-making"],["Il succo fresco della canna appena spremuta","Le jus frais de la canne fraîchement pressée","The fresh juice of just-crushed cane"],["Un vino di canna già fermentato","Un vin de canne déjà fermenté","A cane wine that has already fermented"],["Il colorante caramello usato nei rum","Le colorant caramel utilisé dans les rhums","The caramel colouring used in rums"]],"e":["La melassa resta quando si trasforma il succo di canna in zucchero.","La mélasse reste quand on transforme le jus de canne en sucre.","Molasses is left over when cane juice is turned into sugar."],"d":["È nera e appiccicosa e va diluita con acqua prima della fermentazione. Il succo fresco è l'altra materia prima, quella dei rhum agricole. Non è già fermentata, e non va confusa con il caramello, che si usa solo per correggere il colore.","Elle est noire et collante et doit être diluée avec de l'eau avant la fermentation. Le jus frais est l'autre matière première, celle des rhums agricoles. Elle n'est pas déjà fermentée, et il ne faut pas la confondre avec le caramel, utilisé seulement pour ajuster la couleur.","It is black and sticky and must be mixed with water before fermentation. Fresh juice is the other raw material, used for rhum agricole. Molasses is not already fermented, and it should not be confused with caramel, which is only used to adjust colour."]},{"id":"s1d74ed0e","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Quale sapore hanno spesso i rum da succo di canna?","Quelle saveur ont souvent les rhums de jus de canne ?","What flavour do cane-juice rums often have?"],"o":[["Erbaceo e vegetale, molto marcato","Herbacé et végétal, très marqué","Very pronounced grassy, herbaceous"],["Caramello e zucchero di canna scuro","Caramel et sucre roux","Caramel and brown sugar"],["Fumo di torba","Fumée de tourbe","Peat smoke"],["Ginepro e agrumi","Genièvre et agrumes","Juniper and citrus"]],"e":["Il succo fresco di canna dà ai rum un carattere erbaceo e vegetale.","Le jus de canne frais donne aux rhums un caractère herbacé et végétal.","Fresh cane juice gives rum a grassy, herbaceous character."],"d":["Caramello e zucchero scuro sono il segno dei rum da melassa, la scelta più diffusa nei Caraibi. Il fumo di torba appartiene ad alcuni whisky scozzesi, mentre ginepro e agrumi sono tipici del gin.","Caramel et sucre roux sont la marque des rhums de mélasse, le choix le plus répandu dans la Caraïbe. La fumée de tourbe appartient à certains whiskies écossais, tandis que genièvre et agrumes sont typiques du gin.","Caramel and brown sugar are the mark of molasses rums, the most common choice in the Caribbean. Peat smoke belongs to some Scotch whiskies, while juniper and citrus are typical of gin."]},{"id":"s1747a9c4","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Nei Caraibi, da dove deve provenire il rhum agricole?","Dans la Caraïbe, d'où doit venir le rhum agricole ?","In the Caribbean, where must rhum agricole come from?"],"o":[["Martinica o Guadalupa","Martinique ou Guadeloupe","Martinique or Guadeloupe"],["Giamaica o Cuba","Jamaïque ou Cuba","Jamaica or Cuba"],["Porto Rico o Giamaica","Porto Rico ou Jamaïque","Puerto Rico or Jamaica"],["Da qualsiasi isola caraibica","De n'importe quelle île de la Caraïbe","Any Caribbean island"]],"e":["Nei Caraibi il rhum agricole deve venire dalla Martinica o dalla Guadalupa.","Dans la Caraïbe, le rhum agricole doit venir de Martinique ou de Guadeloupe.","In the Caribbean, rhum agricole must come from Martinique or Guadeloupe."],"d":["Il rhum agricole è il miglior esempio di rum da succo di canna. La Giamaica è nota per i rum molto fruttati, Cuba e Porto Rico per i rum leggeri da colonna alta. Non basta essere un'isola dei Caraibi per usare questa denominazione.","Le rhum agricole est le meilleur exemple de rhum de jus de canne. La Jamaïque est connue pour ses rhums très fruités, Cuba et Porto Rico pour leurs rhums légers de haute colonne. Il ne suffit pas d'être une île de la Caraïbe pour utiliser ce nom.","Rhum agricole is the best example of a cane-juice rum. Jamaica is known for very fruity rums, Cuba and Puerto Rico for light rums from tall columns. Simply being a Caribbean island is not enough to use this name."]},{"id":"s17e8389e","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Quale materia prima usa la maggior parte dei distillatori caraibici?","Quelle matière première utilisent la plupart des distillateurs de la Caraïbe ?","Which raw material do most Caribbean distillers use?"],"o":[["La melassa","La mélasse","Molasses"],["Il succo fresco di canna","Le jus de canne frais","Fresh cane juice"],["Lo zucchero bianco raffinato","Le sucre blanc raffiné","Refined white sugar"],["Il miele","Le miel","Honey"]],"e":["La melassa è la scelta della maggioranza dei distillatori nei Caraibi.","La mélasse est le choix de la majorité des distillateurs de la Caraïbe.","Molasses is the choice of most Caribbean distillers."],"d":["Il succo fresco è usato soprattutto per i rhum agricole, una parte più piccola della produzione. Lo zucchero raffinato è il prodotto principale dell'industria da cui la melassa deriva, non la materia prima del rum. Il miele non c'entra con il rum.","Le jus frais sert surtout aux rhums agricoles, une part plus réduite de la production. Le sucre raffiné est le produit principal de l'industrie dont vient la mélasse, pas la matière première du rhum. Le miel n'a rien à voir avec le rhum.","Fresh juice is used mainly for rhum agricole, a smaller share of production. Refined sugar is the main product of the industry that leaves molasses behind, not rum's raw material. Honey has nothing to do with rum."]},{"id":"s1bd6806b","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Quali sapori sono tipici di un rum da melassa?","Quelles saveurs sont typiques d'un rhum de mélasse ?","Which flavours are typical of a molasses rum?"],"o":[["Caramello e zucchero di canna scuro","Caramel et sucre roux","Caramel and brown sugar"],["Erba fresca e note vegetali","Herbe fraîche et notes végétales","Fresh grass and vegetal notes"],["Mais dolce e cocco","Maïs doux et noix de coco","Sweetcorn and coconut"],["Agave, oliva e pepe","Agave, olive et poivre","Agave, olive and pepper"]],"e":["La melassa porta nel rum note di caramello e zucchero scuro.","La mélasse apporte au rhum des notes de caramel et de sucre roux.","Molasses brings caramel and brown sugar notes to rum."],"d":["Le note erbacee e vegetali sono tipiche del succo di canna fresco. Mais dolce e cocco ricordano il Bourbon, agave, oliva e pepe la Tequila. Ogni materia prima lascia il suo insieme di aromi.","Les notes herbacées et végétales sont typiques du jus de canne frais. Maïs doux et noix de coco évoquent le Bourbon, agave, olive et poivre la Tequila. Chaque matière première laisse sa propre série d'arômes.","Grassy, vegetal notes are typical of fresh cane juice. Sweetcorn and coconut recall Bourbon, and agave, olive and pepper recall Tequila. Each raw material leaves its own set of aromas."]},{"id":"s17e2a84e","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Che cosa bisogna fare alla melassa prima che possa fermentare?","Que faut-il faire à la mélasse avant qu'elle puisse fermenter ?","What must be done to molasses before it can ferment?"],"o":[["Mescolarla con acqua","La mélanger à de l'eau","Mix it with water"],["Farla germogliare","La faire germer","Let it sprout"],["Cuocerla in forno","La cuire au four","Cook it in ovens"],["Filtrarla con il carbone","La filtrer au charbon","Filter it through charcoal"]],"e":["La melassa è troppo densa: va diluita con acqua per poter fermentare.","La mélasse est trop épaisse : il faut la diluer avec de l'eau pour qu'elle fermente.","Molasses is too thick: it must be mixed with water to ferment."],"d":["La germinazione appartiene alla maltazione dei cereali per il whisky. La cottura in forno serve a creare zucchero dai cuori di agave per la Tequila. La filtrazione al carbone si usa dopo la distillazione, per esempio per togliere colore al rum.","La germination appartient au maltage des céréales pour le whisky. La cuisson au four sert à créer du sucre à partir des cœurs d'agave pour la Tequila. La filtration au charbon intervient après la distillation, par exemple pour retirer la couleur du rhum.","Sprouting belongs to malting grain for whisky. Cooking in ovens is how sugar is created from agave cores for Tequila. Charcoal filtering comes after distillation, for example to remove colour from rum."]},{"id":"s1cdc26ce","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Da quale fase vengono soprattutto gli intensi aromi di frutta tropicale di alcuni rum?","De quelle étape viennent surtout les arômes intenses de fruits tropicaux de certains rhums ?","Which stage mainly creates the intense tropical fruit aromas of some rums?"],"o":[["La fermentazione","La fermentation","Fermentation"],["L'invecchiamento in rovere","Le vieillissement en chêne","Oak ageing"],["La filtrazione al carbone","La filtration au charbon","Charcoal filtering"],["La diluizione con acqua","La dilution à l'eau","Dilution with water"]],"e":["I lieviti, durante la fermentazione, possono creare intensi aromi di frutta tropicale.","Pendant la fermentation, les levures peuvent créer d'intenses arômes de fruits tropicaux.","During fermentation, yeast can create intense tropical fruit aromas."],"d":["Il rovere aggiunge piuttosto vaniglia e spezie dolci. La filtrazione al carbone toglie colore, non aggiunge frutta. L'acqua usata per diluire è pura e non porta alcun sapore.","Le chêne ajoute plutôt vanille et épices douces. La filtration au charbon retire de la couleur, elle n'ajoute pas de fruit. L'eau de dilution est pure et n'apporte aucun goût.","Oak adds vanilla and sweet spice instead. Charcoal filtering removes colour; it does not add fruit. The water used for dilution is pure and brings no flavour."]},{"id":"s1ca02a4c","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Per quale stile di rum sono famosi i distillatori della Giamaica?","Pour quel style de rhum les distillateurs de la Jamaïque sont-ils célèbres ?","Which rum style are Jamaican distillers famous for?"],"o":[["Rum intensamente fruttati","Des rhums intensément fruités","Intensely fruity rums"],["Rum leggeri da colonna alta","Des rhums légers de haute colonne","Light rums from tall columns"],["Rum erbacei da succo di canna","Des rhums herbacés de jus de canne","Grassy cane-juice rums"],["Rum neutri a 96% vol","Des rhums neutres à 96 % vol","Neutral rums at 96% abv"]],"e":["In Giamaica si sfrutta la fermentazione per creare rum carichi di frutta tropicale.","En Jamaïque, on exploite la fermentation pour créer des rhums chargés de fruits tropicaux.","In Jamaica, fermentation is used to create rums loaded with tropical fruit."],"d":["I rum leggeri da colonna alta sono associati a Cuba e Porto Rico. I rum erbacei da succo di canna sono i rhum agricole di Martinica e Guadalupa. Un rum neutro a 96% non avrebbe quasi più aroma, l'opposto dello stile giamaicano.","Les rhums légers de haute colonne sont associés à Cuba et Porto Rico. Les rhums herbacés de jus de canne sont les rhums agricoles de Martinique et de Guadeloupe. Un rhum neutre à 96 % n'aurait presque plus d'arômes, l'inverse du style jamaïcain.","Light rums from tall columns are linked to Cuba and Puerto Rico. Grassy cane-juice rums are the rhum agricole of Martinique and Guadeloupe. A neutral rum at 96% would have almost no aroma, the opposite of the Jamaican style."]},{"id":"s1b9c8de7","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Come si producono i rum dal profumo leggero di Cuba e Porto Rico?","Comment produit-on les rhums au nez léger de Cuba et de Porto Rico ?","How are the light-aroma rums of Cuba and Puerto Rico made?"],"o":[["In colonne alte, ad alta gradazione","En hautes colonnes, à haut degré","In tall columns, to a high strength"],["In alambicchi discontinui, a bassa gradazione","À l'alambic, à bas degré","In pot stills, to a low strength"],["In colonne corte, come il rhum agricole","En colonnes courtes, comme le rhum agricole","In short columns, like rhum agricole"],["Senza distillazione, solo fermentati","Sans distillation, seulement fermentés","With no distillation, only fermented"]],"e":["Colonne alte e gradazione elevata danno rum con un aroma leggero.","Hautes colonnes et degré élevé donnent des rhums au nez léger.","Tall columns and high strength give rums with a light aroma."],"d":["Più alta è la gradazione di distillazione, meno aroma resta. Alambicco e colonna corta danno invece spiriti saporiti e di carattere. Senza distillazione non si avrebbe un rum ma un liquido fermentato a bassa gradazione.","Plus le degré de distillation est élevé, moins il reste d'arômes. L'alambic et la colonne courte donnent au contraire des spiritueux savoureux et de caractère. Sans distillation, on n'aurait pas un rhum mais un liquide fermenté peu alcoolisé.","The higher the distillation strength, the less aroma remains. Pot stills and short columns give flavourful, characterful spirits instead. Without distillation you would not have rum at all, just a low-strength fermented liquid."]},{"id":"s1581ea8d","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Una distilleria vuole un rum intenso e ricco di carattere. Quale alambicco può scegliere?","Une distillerie veut un rhum intense et plein de caractère. Quel appareil peut-elle choisir ?","A distillery wants a pronounced, characterful rum. Which still could it choose?"],"o":[["Un alambicco discontinuo","Un alambic","A pot still"],["Una colonna alta ad alta gradazione","Une haute colonne à haut degré","A tall column run to high strength"],["Una colonna fino a 96% vol","Une colonne jusqu'à 96 % vol","A column still taken to 96% abv"],["Nessuno: basta filtrare con il carbone","Aucun : il suffit de filtrer au charbon","None: charcoal filtering is enough"]],"e":["L'alambicco discontinuo dà uno spirito di bassa gradazione, intenso e di carattere.","L'alambic donne un spiritueux de bas degré, intense et de caractère.","A pot still gives a low-strength, pronounced, characterful spirit."],"d":["Anche una colonna corta potrebbe funzionare, ma tra queste opzioni solo l'alambicco va nella direzione giusta. Le colonne alte e la gradazione di 96% portano a spiriti leggeri o neutri. La filtrazione al carbone non crea carattere: semmai toglie colore.","Une colonne courte pourrait aussi convenir, mais parmi ces options seul l'alambic va dans le bon sens. Les hautes colonnes et le degré de 96 % mènent à des spiritueux légers ou neutres. La filtration au charbon ne crée pas de caractère : elle retire plutôt de la couleur.","A short column could also work, but among these options only the pot still points the right way. Tall columns and 96% abv lead to light or neutral spirits. Charcoal filtering does not create character; if anything, it removes colour."]},{"id":"s1c79fb28","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Con quale tipo di alambicco si distilla tipicamente il rhum agricole?","Avec quel type d'appareil distille-t-on typiquement le rhum agricole ?","What type of still is typically used for rhum agricole?"],"o":[["Una colonna corta","Une colonne courte","A short column still"],["Una colonna molto alta","Une très haute colonne","A very tall column still"],["Un doppio alambicco obbligatorio","Une double distillation obligatoire à l'alambic","A compulsory double pot still"],["Un alambicco con filtro d'acero","Un alambic avec filtre d'érable","A pot still with a maple filter"]],"e":["Il rhum agricole si distilla in colonne corte, che danno uno spirito saporito.","Le rhum agricole est distillé en colonnes courtes, qui donnent un spiritueux savoureux.","Rhum agricole is distilled in short columns, which give a flavourful spirit."],"d":["Una colonna corta, con poche sezioni, conserva molta intensità, simile a quella di un alambicco discontinuo. Le colonne molto alte servono per i rum leggeri. La doppia distillazione obbligatoria in alambicco è la regola del Cognac, e il carbone d'acero è legato al Tennessee whiskey.","Une colonne courte, avec peu de sections, garde beaucoup d'intensité, proche de celle d'un alambic. Les très hautes colonnes servent aux rhums légers. La double distillation obligatoire à l'alambic est la règle du Cognac, et le charbon d'érable est lié au Tennessee whiskey.","A short column with few sections keeps plenty of intensity, similar to a pot still. Very tall columns are used for light rums. Compulsory double pot distillation is the rule for Cognac, and maple charcoal belongs to Tennessee whiskey."]},{"id":"s1e22d140","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["In un paese dove il rum deve invecchiare in botte, come si può ottenere un rum incolore?","Dans un pays où le rhum doit vieillir en fût, comment obtenir un rhum incolore ?","In a country where rum must be oak-aged, how can a colourless rum be made?"],"o":[["Filtrandolo con il carbone dopo la botte","En le filtrant au charbon après le fût","By charcoal filtering it after the barrel"],["Aggiungendo caramello","En ajoutant du caramel","By adding caramel"],["Diluendolo con più acqua","En le diluant avec plus d'eau","By diluting it with more water"],["Aggiungendo zucchero","En ajoutant du sucre","By adding sugar"]],"e":["La filtrazione al carbone toglie il colore preso dal legno.","La filtration au charbon retire la couleur prise au bois.","Charcoal filtering removes the colour picked up from the wood."],"d":["Il caramello aggiunge colore invece di toglierlo. L'acqua abbassa il grado ma lascia il colore quasi invariato, e lo zucchero cambia la dolcezza, non la tinta. L'altro modo per avere un rum bianco, dove la legge lo consente, è non invecchiarlo e conservarlo in acciaio.","Le caramel ajoute de la couleur au lieu d'en retirer. L'eau abaisse le degré mais laisse la couleur presque inchangée, et le sucre change la douceur, pas la teinte. L'autre façon d'obtenir un rhum blanc, là où la loi le permet, est de ne pas le vieillir et de le garder en acier.","Caramel adds colour rather than removing it. Water lowers the strength but leaves the colour almost unchanged, and sugar changes sweetness, not shade. The other way to get a white rum, where the law allows, is not to age it and to keep it in steel."]},{"id":"s1d3a7912","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Molte distillerie caraibiche hanno sia alambicchi discontinui sia colonne. Perché è utile?","Beaucoup de distilleries de la Caraïbe ont à la fois alambics et colonnes. Pourquoi est-ce utile ?","Many Caribbean distilleries own both pot stills and columns. Why is that useful?"],"o":[["Per avere spiriti di intensità diverse da assemblare","Pour avoir des spiritueux d'intensités différentes à assembler","To have spirits of different intensities to blend"],["Perché la legge impone due distillazioni","Parce que la loi impose deux distillations","Because the law requires two distillations"],["Perché le colonne servono per invecchiare","Parce que les colonnes servent au vieillissement","Because columns are used for ageing"],["Perché l'alambicco serve per addolcire","Parce que l'alambic sert à sucrer","Because the pot still is used to sweeten"]],"e":["Due tipi di alambicco danno spiriti leggeri e intensi, utili per comporre stili diversi.","Deux types d'appareils donnent des spiritueux légers et intenses, utiles pour composer des styles différents.","Two kinds of still give light and pronounced spirits for building different styles."],"d":["Con più tipi di spirito, chi assembla può creare prodotti molto diversi, anche combinando età e distillerie differenti. Nessuna regola generale caraibica impone due distillazioni. Le colonne servono a distillare, non a invecchiare, e lo zucchero si aggiunge dopo, non nell'alambicco.","Avec plusieurs types de spiritueux, on peut créer des produits très différents, en combinant aussi des âges et des distilleries différents. Aucune règle générale de la Caraïbe n'impose deux distillations. Les colonnes servent à distiller, pas à vieillir, et le sucre est ajouté après, pas dans l'alambic.","With several types of spirit, blenders can create very different products, also combining different ages and distilleries. No general Caribbean rule requires two distillations. Columns are for distilling, not ageing, and sugar is added afterwards, not in the still."]},{"id":"s12e89d78","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi aggiunge l'invecchiamento in rovere a un rum?","Quels arômes le vieillissement en chêne ajoute-t-il à un rhum ?","Which aromas does oak ageing add to a rum?"],"o":[["Vaniglia e spezie dolci","Vanille et épices douces","Vanilla and sweet spice"],["Erba fresca e note vegetali","Herbe fraîche et notes végétales","Fresh grass and vegetal notes"],["Frutta tropicale intensa","Fruits tropicaux intenses","Intense tropical fruit"],["Fumo di torba","Fumée de tourbe","Peat smoke"]],"e":["Il legno di rovere cede al rum vaniglia e spezie dolci, oltre al colore.","Le chêne cède au rhum vanille et épices douces, en plus de la couleur.","Oak gives rum vanilla and sweet spice, as well as colour."],"d":["Le note erbacee vengono dal succo di canna, cioè dalla materia prima. La frutta tropicale intensa nasce in fermentazione. Il fumo di torba si crea durante la maltazione dei cereali, quindi non riguarda il rum.","Les notes herbacées viennent du jus de canne, donc de la matière première. Les fruits tropicaux intenses naissent pendant la fermentation. La fumée de tourbe se crée pendant le maltage des céréales : elle ne concerne pas le rhum.","Grassy notes come from cane juice, the raw material. Intense tropical fruit is born in fermentation. Peat smoke is created while malting grain, so it has nothing to do with rum."]},{"id":"s1a880993","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Quale affermazione sull'aggiunta di zucchero al rum è corretta?","Quelle affirmation sur l'ajout de sucre au rhum est correcte ?","Which statement about adding sugar to rum is correct?"],"o":[["È comune in America Centrale e del Sud, vietata in alcuni paesi","Courant en Amérique centrale et du Sud, interdit dans certains pays","Common in Central and South America, banned in some countries"],["È obbligatoria per tutti i rum caraibici","Obligatoire pour tous les rhums de la Caraïbe","Required for every Caribbean rum"],["È vietata ovunque nel mondo","Interdit partout dans le monde","Banned everywhere in the world"],["Avviene da sola durante l'invecchiamento","Se produit tout seul pendant le vieillissement","Happens on its own during ageing"]],"e":["Alcuni rum vengono addolciti: pratica diffusa in America Centrale e del Sud, ma non ovunque permessa.","Certains rhums sont sucrés : pratique courante en Amérique centrale et du Sud, mais pas permise partout.","Some rums are sweetened: common in Central and South America, but not allowed everywhere."],"d":["Le regole cambiano da paese a paese, quindi né obbligo né divieto valgono ovunque. Ogni distillato appena fatto è secco: la dolcezza arriva solo da zucchero aggiunto dopo la distillazione, non dalla botte.","Les règles changent d'un pays à l'autre : ni obligation ni interdiction ne valent partout. Tout spiritueux qui sort de l'alambic est sec : la douceur ne vient que du sucre ajouté après la distillation, pas du fût.","The rules change from country to country, so neither a requirement nor a ban applies everywhere. Every spirit is dry when it leaves the still: sweetness only comes from sugar added after distillation, not from the barrel."]},{"id":"s12ac13e7","c":"s5","p":0,"q":["Un rum ha un colore ambrato scuro. Che cosa se ne può dedurre con certezza?","Un rhum a une couleur ambrée foncée. Que peut-on en déduire avec certitude ?","A rum has a deep amber colour. What can you conclude for certain?"],"o":[["Nulla sull'età: il colore può venire dal caramello","Rien sur l'âge : la couleur peut venir du caramel","Nothing about age: the colour may come from caramel"],["Che è invecchiato almeno dieci anni","Qu'il a vieilli au moins dix ans","That it was aged at least ten years"],["Che è fatto con succo di canna fresco","Qu'il est fait de jus de canne frais","That it was made from fresh cane juice"],["Che è stato distillato in alambicco","Qu'il a été distillé à l'alambic","That it was distilled in a pot still"]],"e":["Molti rum ricevono caramello, a volte per quasi tutto il colore, quindi la tinta non prova l'età.","Beaucoup de rhums reçoivent du caramel, parfois pour presque toute leur couleur : la teinte ne prouve pas l'âge.","Many rums get caramel, sometimes for almost all their colour, so shade proves nothing about age."],"d":["Ecco perché classificare il rum per colore funziona male. Il colore non dice nulla nemmeno sulla materia prima o sul tipo di alambicco: queste informazioni dipendono dalle fasi di produzione, non dalla tinta nel bicchiere.","Voilà pourquoi classer le rhum par couleur fonctionne mal. La couleur ne dit rien non plus sur la matière première ni sur le type d'appareil : ces informations dépendent des étapes de production, pas de la teinte dans le verre.","This is why sorting rum by colour works badly. Colour also says nothing about the raw material or the type of still: those depend on the production stages, not on the shade in the glass."]},{"id":"s1d08a532","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Da quale pianta si ottiene la Tequila?","De quelle plante est tirée la Tequila ?","Which plant is Tequila made from?"],"o":[["Agave blu","L'agave bleu","Blue agave"],["Canna da zucchero","La canne à sucre","Sugar cane"],["Mais","Le maïs","Corn"],["Patata","La pomme de terre","Potato"]],"e":["Per legge la Tequila deve essere prodotta con l'agave blu, pianta originaria del Messico.","Par la loi, la Tequila doit être produite à partir de l'agave bleu, plante originaire du Mexique.","By law, Tequila must be made from blue agave, a plant native to Mexico."],"d":["L'agave blu è l'unica pianta ammessa e dà alla Tequila i suoi aromi erbacei e pepati. La canna da zucchero è la materia prima del rum, il mais è il cereale principale del Bourbon e la patata è una delle materie prime classiche della vodka.","L'agave bleu est la seule plante autorisée et donne à la Tequila ses arômes herbacés et poivrés. La canne à sucre est la matière première du rhum, le maïs la céréale principale du Bourbon, et la pomme de terre l'une des matières premières classiques de la vodka.","Blue agave is the only plant allowed and gives Tequila its herbaceous, peppery aromas. Sugar cane is the raw material of rum, corn is the main grain in Bourbon, and potato is one of the classic raw materials for vodka."]},{"id":"s1fc3bda0","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Dove si può produrre la Tequila?","Où peut-on produire de la Tequila ?","Where can Tequila be made?"],"o":[["Solo in alcuni stati del Messico","Seulement dans certains États du Mexique","Only in certain states of Mexico"],["In qualsiasi stato del Messico","Dans n'importe quel État du Mexique","In any state of Mexico"],["In tutta l'America centrale","Dans toute l'Amérique centrale","Anywhere in Central America"],["Ovunque cresca l'agave blu","Partout où pousse l'agave bleu","Wherever blue agave grows"]],"e":["La legge limita la produzione ad alcuni stati messicani ben definiti.","La loi limite la production à certains États mexicains bien définis.","The law limits production to certain named Mexican states."],"d":["Non basta essere in Messico: solo alcuni stati sono autorizzati. Coltivare agave blu altrove non dà diritto al nome Tequila, e l'America centrale non rientra nella zona. È una differenza importante rispetto alla vodka, che si può produrre ovunque.","Il ne suffit pas d'être au Mexique : seuls certains États sont autorisés. Cultiver de l'agave bleu ailleurs ne donne pas droit au nom Tequila, et l'Amérique centrale n'en fait pas partie. C'est une grande différence avec la vodka, qu'on peut produire partout.","Being in Mexico is not enough: only certain states are allowed. Growing blue agave elsewhere does not earn the name Tequila, and Central America is outside the zone. This is a key difference from vodka, which can be made anywhere."]},{"id":"s11f3f45c","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Perché i cuori d'agave vengono cotti in forno?","Pourquoi cuit-on les cœurs d'agave au four ?","Why are agave cores cooked in ovens?"],"o":[["Per ammorbidirli e creare zuccheri","Pour les attendrir et créer des sucres","To soften them and create sugars"],["Per dare un aroma affumicato","Pour leur donner un arôme fumé","To give them a smoky aroma"],["Per eliminare il loro colore","Pour éliminer leur couleur","To remove their colour"],["Per uccidere i lieviti naturali","Pour tuer les levures naturelles","To kill the natural yeasts"]],"e":["La cottura rende il cuore morbido e vi forma gli zuccheri necessari alla fermentazione.","La cuisson attendrit le cœur et y forme les sucres nécessaires à la fermentation.","Cooking softens the core and forms the sugars needed for fermentation."],"d":["Come i cereali, l'agave appena raccolto non ha zuccheri pronti: senza cottura non ci sarebbe nulla da fermentare. Il fumo non è l'obiettivo (pensate piuttosto alla torba di alcuni whisky scozzesi), il colore non c'entra e i lieviti servono proprio dopo, per la fermentazione.","Comme les céréales, l'agave fraîchement récolté n'a pas de sucres prêts : sans cuisson, il n'y aurait rien à fermenter. La fumée n'est pas le but (pensez plutôt à la tourbe de certains whiskies écossais), la couleur n'a rien à voir et les levures sont justement utiles ensuite, pour la fermentation.","Like grains, freshly harvested agave has no sugar ready to use: without cooking there would be nothing to ferment. Smoke is not the goal (that is more the peat in some Scotch whiskies), colour is irrelevant, and yeast is needed right afterwards for fermentation."]},{"id":"s1983e804","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Su un'etichetta di Tequila si legge «Silver». Che cosa indica?","Une étiquette de Tequila porte la mention « Silver ». Qu'est-ce que cela indique ?","A Tequila label says ‘Silver’. What does that tell you?"],"o":[["Che è una Tequila non invecchiata, come la Blanco","Que c'est une Tequila non vieillie, comme la Blanco","It is an unaged Tequila, the same as Blanco"],["Che è invecchiata da 2 a 12 mesi","Qu'elle a vieilli de 2 à 12 mois","It has been aged for 2 to 12 months"],["Che è fatta con il 100% di agave","Qu'elle est faite à 100 % d'agave","It is made from 100% agave"],["Che è stata colorata con caramello","Qu'elle a été colorée au caramel","It has been coloured with caramel"]],"e":["Silver è un altro nome per Blanco: Tequila non invecchiata.","Silver est un autre nom de la Blanco : une Tequila non vieillie.","Silver is another name for Blanco: unaged Tequila."],"d":["Blanco e Silver indicano lo stesso stile, incolore e dal profilo d'agave puro. Il periodo da 2 a 12 mesi corrisponde alla Reposado; la dicitura «100% agave» è un'informazione separata, e il caramello è tipico invece della Joven/Oro.","Blanco et Silver désignent le même style, incolore et au profil d'agave pur. La période de 2 à 12 mois correspond à la Reposado ; la mention « 100 % agave » est une information distincte, et le caramel est plutôt typique de la Joven/Oro.","Blanco and Silver name the same style, colourless with a pure agave profile. The 2–12 month period belongs to Reposado; ‘100% agave’ is a separate piece of information, and caramel is typical of Joven/Oro instead."]},{"id":"s16fafc92","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Quale quota minima di zuccheri deve provenire dall'agave blu in qualsiasi Tequila?","Quelle part minimale des sucres doit provenir de l'agave bleu dans toute Tequila ?","What minimum share of the sugars in any Tequila must come from blue agave?"],"o":[["51%","51 %","51%"],["25%","25 %","25%"],["75%","75 %","75%"],["100%","100 %","100%"]],"e":["Almeno il 51% degli zuccheri fermentati deve venire dall'agave blu.","Au moins 51 % des sucres fermentés doivent provenir de l'agave bleu.","At least 51% of the fermented sugars must come from blue agave."],"d":["Il produttore può aggiungere altri zuccheri, ma l'agave deve restare maggioritario. Il 100% non è obbligatorio: è la condizione per poter scrivere «100% agave» in etichetta. Il 25% e il 75% non corrispondono a nessuna regola.","Le producteur peut ajouter d'autres sucres, mais l'agave doit rester majoritaire. Le 100 % n'est pas obligatoire : c'est la condition pour pouvoir écrire « 100 % agave » sur l'étiquette. Les valeurs de 25 % et 75 % ne correspondent à aucune règle.","The producer may add other sugars, but agave must stay in the majority. 100% is not compulsory: it is the condition for writing ‘100% agave’ on the label. The 25% and 75% figures match no rule."]},{"id":"s1bf4fe3a","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Che cosa garantisce la dicitura «100% agave» su una Tequila?","Que garantit la mention « 100 % agave » sur une Tequila ?","What does ‘100% agave’ on a Tequila label guarantee?"],"o":[["Nessuno zucchero diverso dall'agave blu","Aucun sucre autre que celui de l'agave bleu","No sugar other than blue agave was used"],["Una distillazione solo in alambicco","Une distillation uniquement en alambic","Distillation in pot stills only"],["Un invecchiamento minimo in rovere","Un vieillissement minimal en chêne","A minimum period in oak"],["L'assenza di caramello e additivi","L'absence de caramel et d'additifs","No caramel or other additives"]],"e":["Significa che per il liquido zuccherino è stato usato solo agave blu.","Cela signifie que seul l'agave bleu a servi à préparer le liquide sucré.","It means only blue agave was used to make the sugary liquid."],"d":["La dicitura riguarda solo l'origine degli zuccheri. Non dice nulla sul tipo di alambicco né sull'invecchiamento: esistono Tequile «100% agave» sia non invecchiate sia invecchiate. Non garantisce nemmeno l'assenza di caramello, che può essere usato nelle versioni invecchiate.","La mention concerne seulement l'origine des sucres. Elle ne dit rien du type d'alambic ni du vieillissement : il existe des Tequilas « 100 % agave » non vieillies comme vieillies. Elle ne garantit pas non plus l'absence de caramel, qui peut être utilisé dans les versions vieillies.","The term is only about where the sugars came from. It says nothing about the type of still or about ageing: there are both unaged and aged ‘100% agave’ Tequilas. Nor does it promise no caramel, which may be used in aged versions."]},{"id":"s1f2e4264","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Un cliente cerca la Tequila con l'espressione d'agave più pura possibile. Quale proporre?","Un client cherche la Tequila à l'expression d'agave la plus pure possible. Laquelle proposer ?","A customer wants the purest possible expression of agave. Which Tequila would you suggest?"],"o":[["Una Blanco 100% agave","Une Blanco 100 % agave","A Blanco labelled 100% agave"],["Una Añejo 100% agave","Une Añejo 100 % agave","An Añejo labelled 100% agave"],["Una Joven/Oro","Une Joven/Oro","A Joven/Oro"],["Una Reposado senza altre diciture","Une Reposado sans autre mention","A Reposado with no other label terms"]],"e":["La Blanco non passa in legno e il «100% agave» esclude altri zuccheri: l'agave è protagonista assoluto.","La Blanco ne passe pas en fût et le « 100 % agave » exclut les autres sucres : l'agave est seul en scène.","Blanco sees no oak, and ‘100% agave’ rules out other sugars: agave has the stage to itself."],"d":["Due scelte vanno nella stessa direzione: niente legno e solo zuccheri d'agave. La Añejo aggiunge note di rovere, la Joven/Oro ha caramello e additivi che ne ammorbidiscono la consistenza, e una Reposado senza la dicitura «100% agave» può contenere altri zuccheri oltre a un passaggio in legno.","Deux choix vont dans le même sens : pas de bois et uniquement des sucres d'agave. L'Añejo ajoute des notes de chêne, la Joven/Oro contient du caramel et des additifs qui adoucissent sa texture, et une Reposado sans la mention « 100 % agave » peut contenir d'autres sucres en plus de son passage en fût.","Two choices point the same way: no oak and only agave sugars. Añejo adds oak notes, Joven/Oro has caramel and additives that soften its texture, and a Reposado without ‘100% agave’ may contain other sugars on top of its time in oak."]},{"id":"s15ab2088","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Come vengono distillate le migliori Tequile?","Comment les meilleures Tequilas sont-elles distillées ?","How are the best Tequilas distilled?"],"o":[["Due volte in alambicco discontinuo, a bassa gradazione","Deux fois en alambic à repasse, à faible degré","Twice in pot stills, to a low strength"],["Una volta in colonna alta, a 96% vol.","Une fois en grande colonne, à 96 % vol.","Once in a tall column, to 96% abv"],["Tre volte in colonna, ad alta gradazione","Trois fois en colonne, à degré élevé","Three times in columns, to a high strength"],["Una volta in alambicco, poi filtrate su carbone","Une fois en alambic, puis filtrées au charbon","Once in a pot still, then charcoal filtered"]],"e":["La doppia distillazione in alambicco a bassa gradazione conserva i profumi dell'agave.","La double distillation en alambic à faible degré préserve les arômes de l'agave.","Double pot distillation to a low strength keeps the agave aromas."],"d":["Più bassa è la gradazione, più profumo resta nel distillato. Una colonna alta che arriva a 96% vol. produce uno spirito neutro, l'opposto di ciò che si cerca. La filtrazione su carbone non fa parte del metodo tipico della Tequila: la si incontra piuttosto nel whiskey del Tennessee o in alcuni rum bianchi.","Plus le degré est bas, plus le spiritueux garde d'arômes. Une grande colonne qui atteint 96 % vol. donne un alcool neutre, l'inverse de ce qu'on cherche. La filtration au charbon ne fait pas partie de la méthode typique de la Tequila : on la rencontre plutôt dans le whiskey du Tennessee ou certains rhums blancs.","The lower the strength, the more aroma stays in the spirit. A tall column reaching 96% abv makes a neutral spirit, the opposite of what is wanted. Charcoal filtering is not part of the typical Tequila method; it belongs rather to Tennessee whiskey or some white rums."]},{"id":"s18733c3c","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Quali profumi sono tipici dell'agave blu?","Quels arômes sont typiques de l'agave bleu ?","Which aromas are typical of blue agave?"],"o":[["Erbacei, terrosi e pepati","Herbacés, terreux et poivrés","Herbaceous, earthy and peppery"],["Cereali, miele e fumo","Céréales, miel et fumée","Cereal, honey and smoke"],["Caramello e zucchero di canna","Caramel et sucre roux","Caramel and brown sugar"],["Vaniglia, cocco e mais dolce","Vanille, noix de coco et maïs doux","Vanilla, coconut and sweetcorn"]],"e":["L'agave blu porta note erbacee, vegetali, di oliva, di terra e di pepe.","L'agave bleu apporte des notes herbacées, végétales, d'olive, de terre et de poivre.","Blue agave brings herbaceous, vegetal, olive, earthy and peppery notes."],"d":["Ogni materia prima lascia la sua firma. Cereali, miele e fumo fanno pensare a un single malt scozzese torbato, caramello e zucchero di canna a un rum da melassa, vaniglia, cocco e mais dolce a un Bourbon in rovere nuovo.","Chaque matière première laisse sa signature. Céréales, miel et fumée évoquent un single malt écossais tourbé, caramel et sucre roux un rhum de mélasse, vanille, noix de coco et maïs doux un Bourbon élevé en chêne neuf.","Every raw material leaves its signature. Cereal, honey and smoke point to a peated Scotch single malt, caramel and brown sugar to a molasses rum, and vanilla, coconut and sweetcorn to a Bourbon aged in new oak."]},{"id":"s13af47e8","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Per quanto tempo invecchia in rovere una Tequila Reposado?","Combien de temps une Tequila Reposado vieillit-elle en chêne ?","How long is a Reposado Tequila aged in oak?"],"o":[["Da 2 a 12 mesi","De 2 à 12 mois","Between 2 and 12 months"],["Almeno 12 mesi","Au moins 12 mois","At least 12 months"],["Almeno 2 anni","Au moins 2 ans","At least 2 years"],["Non invecchia affatto","Elle ne vieillit pas du tout","It is not aged at all"]],"e":["La Reposado riposa in rovere tra 2 e 12 mesi.","La Reposado repose en chêne entre 2 et 12 mois.","Reposado rests in oak for 2 to 12 months."],"d":["Almeno 12 mesi è la regola della Añejo; nessun invecchiamento vale per Blanco e Joven. Almeno 2 anni è un numero che ricorda il minimo del Cognac (VS), non una regola della Tequila.","Au moins 12 mois est la règle de l'Añejo ; aucun vieillissement concerne la Blanco et la Joven. Au moins 2 ans rappelle le minimum du Cognac (VS), pas une règle de la Tequila.","At least 12 months is the Añejo rule; no ageing applies to Blanco and Joven. At least 2 years recalls the Cognac minimum (VS), not a Tequila rule."]},{"id":"s187d6a29","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Quale stile di Tequila passa almeno 12 mesi in rovere?","Quel style de Tequila passe au moins 12 mois en chêne ?","Which Tequila style spends at least 12 months in oak?"],"o":[["Añejo","Añejo","Añejo"],["Reposado","Reposado","Reposado"],["Joven","Joven","Joven"],["Blanco","Blanco","Blanco"]],"e":["La Añejo invecchia almeno 12 mesi e unisce agave e rovere.","L'Añejo vieillit au moins 12 mois et associe agave et chêne.","Añejo is aged for at least 12 months and combines agave and oak."],"d":["La Reposado si ferma tra 2 e 12 mesi. Blanco e Joven non sono invecchiate: la Joven può sembrare matura per il colore dorato, ma quel colore viene dal caramello, non dalla botte.","La Reposado s'arrête entre 2 et 12 mois. La Blanco et la Joven ne sont pas vieillies : la Joven peut sembler âgée à cause de sa couleur dorée, mais cette couleur vient du caramel, pas du fût.","Reposado stops at between 2 and 12 months. Blanco and Joven are unaged: Joven may look mature because of its golden colour, but that colour comes from caramel, not from a barrel."]},{"id":"s180a8d0c","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Da dove viene il colore dorato di una Tequila Joven (Oro)?","D'où vient la couleur dorée d'une Tequila Joven (Oro) ?","Where does the golden colour of a Joven (Oro) Tequila come from?"],"o":[["Dal caramello aggiunto","Du caramel ajouté","Added caramel"],["Da qualche mese in rovere","De quelques mois en chêne","A few months in oak"],["Da una varietà d'agave dorata","D'une variété d'agave dorée","A golden variety of agave"],["Da una cottura più lunga","D'une cuisson plus longue","A longer cooking time"]],"e":["La Joven non è invecchiata: è colorata con caramello e ammorbidita con altri additivi.","La Joven n'est pas vieillie : elle est colorée au caramel et adoucie par d'autres additifs.","Joven is unaged: it is coloured with caramel and softened with other additives."],"d":["È un tranello frequente: l'aspetto dorato fa pensare al legno, ma la Joven non passa in botte. La Tequila si fa solo con agave blu, non con varietà «dorate», e la cottura serve a creare zuccheri, non a colorare il distillato, che esce sempre incolore dall'alambicco.","C'est un piège classique : l'aspect doré fait penser au bois, mais la Joven ne passe pas en fût. La Tequila se fait uniquement avec de l'agave bleu, pas avec une variété « dorée », et la cuisson sert à créer des sucres, pas à colorer un spiritueux qui sort toujours incolore de l'alambic.","It is a classic trap: the golden look suggests wood, but Joven never goes into a barrel. Tequila is made only from blue agave, not a ‘golden’ variety, and cooking creates sugars rather than colour; the spirit always leaves the still colourless."]},{"id":"s1e1a1d2f","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Quale affermazione sulla Tequila Reposado è corretta?","Quelle affirmation sur la Tequila Reposado est exacte ?","Which statement about Reposado Tequila is true?"],"o":[["È più morbida, ma l'agave resta protagonista","Elle est plus souple, mais l'agave reste au premier plan","It is softer, but agave stays in the lead"],["Il gusto del legno domina su quello dell'agave","Le goût du bois domine celui de l'agave","Oak flavours dominate the agave"],["È sempre prodotta con 100% agave","Elle est toujours produite à 100 % d'agave","It is always made from 100% agave"],["Passa almeno due anni in botte","Elle passe au moins deux ans en fût","It spends at least two years in barrel"]],"e":["Il breve passaggio in legno la ammorbidisce senza cancellare l'agave.","Le court passage en fût l'assouplit sans effacer l'agave.","Its short time in oak softens it without erasing the agave."],"d":["Tra 2 e 12 mesi il rovere raramente si impone, quindi l'agave resta intensa: due anni sarebbero ben oltre il limite. Una Reposado può essere «100% agave» o semplice «Tequila», come ogni altro stile.","Entre 2 et 12 mois, le chêne s'impose rarement : l'agave reste donc intense, et deux ans dépasseraient largement la limite. Une Reposado peut être « 100 % agave » ou simplement « Tequila », comme tout autre style.","With 2–12 months in oak, the wood rarely takes over, so the agave stays pronounced; two years would be well beyond the limit. A Reposado can be ‘100% agave’ or plain ‘Tequila’, like any other style."]},{"id":"s1e3e6c01","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Perché le Tequile invecchiate raramente restano molto a lungo in botte?","Pourquoi les Tequilas vieillies restent-elles rarement très longtemps en fût ?","Why are aged Tequilas rarely matured for very long?"],"o":[["Per non coprire il carattere dell'agave con il legno","Pour ne pas masquer le caractère de l'agave sous le bois","To keep oak from masking the agave character"],["Perché la legge vieta più di un anno in botte","Parce que la loi interdit plus d'un an en fût","Because the law forbids more than a year in oak"],["Perché l'agave rende la botte inutilizzabile","Parce que l'agave rend le fût inutilisable","Because agave ruins the barrels"],["Perché il clima messicano fa evaporare tutto","Parce que le climat mexicain fait tout évaporer","Because the Mexican climate evaporates it all"]],"e":["Il produttore cerca un equilibrio tra vaniglia e spezie del rovere e l'agave.","Le producteur cherche un équilibre entre la vanille et les épices du chêne et l'agave.","Producers want a balance between oak's vanilla and spice and the agave."],"d":["È una scelta di stile, non un divieto: la Añejo, per esempio, ha solo un minimo di 12 mesi e nessun massimo. Le altre due risposte non hanno fondamento: l'obiettivo è che il rovere accompagni l'agave senza dominarlo.","C'est un choix de style, pas une interdiction : l'Añejo, par exemple, n'a qu'un minimum de 12 mois et aucun maximum. Les deux autres réponses n'ont pas de fondement : le but est que le chêne accompagne l'agave sans le dominer.","It is a style choice, not a ban: Añejo, for example, has a 12-month minimum and no maximum. The other two answers have no basis: the aim is for oak to support the agave, not dominate it."]},{"id":"s13cb2221","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Quale affermazione sulle etichette della Tequila è corretta?","Quelle affirmation sur les étiquettes de Tequila est exacte ?","Which statement about Tequila labels is true?"],"o":[["Ogni stile può essere «Tequila» o «100% agave»","Chaque style peut être « Tequila » ou « 100 % agave »","Any style can be ‘Tequila’ or ‘100% agave’"],["Solo la Añejo può essere «100% agave»","Seule l'Añejo peut être « 100 % agave »","Only Añejo can be ‘100% agave’"],["La Blanco deve essere sempre «100% agave»","La Blanco doit toujours être « 100 % agave »","Blanco must always be ‘100% agave’"],["Una «100% agave» deve essere invecchiata","Une « 100 % agave » doit être vieillie","A ‘100% agave’ Tequila must be aged"]],"e":["Origine degli zuccheri e invecchiamento sono due informazioni indipendenti.","L'origine des sucres et le vieillissement sont deux informations indépendantes.","Sugar source and ageing are two independent pieces of information."],"d":["Blanco, Joven, Reposado e Añejo possono tutte essere «100% agave» oppure semplice «Tequila». Le altre risposte legano per errore la dicitura sugli zuccheri a uno stile o all'invecchiamento, cosa che la legge non fa.","Blanco, Joven, Reposado et Añejo peuvent toutes être « 100 % agave » ou simplement « Tequila ». Les autres réponses lient à tort la mention sur les sucres à un style ou au vieillissement, ce que la loi ne fait pas.","Blanco, Joven, Reposado and Añejo can all be either ‘100% agave’ or plain ‘Tequila’. The other answers wrongly tie the sugar term to one style or to ageing, which the law does not do."]},{"id":"s11a94b40","c":"s6","p":0,"q":["Qual è l'ordine corretto delle prime fasi di produzione della Tequila?","Quel est l'ordre correct des premières étapes de production de la Tequila ?","What is the correct order of the first steps in making Tequila?"],"o":[["Tagliare le foglie, cuocere, schiacciare, fermentare","Couper les feuilles, cuire, broyer, fermenter","Cut the leaves, cook, crush, ferment"],["Schiacciare, cuocere, tagliare le foglie, fermentare","Broyer, cuire, couper les feuilles, fermenter","Crush, cook, cut the leaves, ferment"],["Tagliare le foglie, fermentare, cuocere, schiacciare","Couper les feuilles, fermenter, cuire, broyer","Cut the leaves, ferment, cook, crush"],["Cuocere, fermentare, schiacciare, tagliare le foglie","Cuire, fermenter, broyer, couper les feuilles","Cook, ferment, crush, cut the leaves"]],"e":["Si isola il cuore, lo si cuoce per creare zuccheri, lo si schiaccia per estrarre il succo e poi si fermenta.","On isole le cœur, on le cuit pour créer des sucres, on le broie pour extraire le jus, puis on fermente.","The core is freed, cooked to create sugars, crushed to release juice, then fermented."],"d":["La logica aiuta: la fermentazione ha bisogno di un liquido zuccherino, quindi gli zuccheri devono già esistere (cottura) ed essere estratti (schiacciatura). Un cuore crudo è troppo duro da schiacciare in modo utile, e fermentare prima di cuocere non avrebbe zuccheri su cui lavorare.","La logique aide : la fermentation a besoin d'un liquide sucré, donc les sucres doivent déjà exister (cuisson) et être extraits (broyage). Un cœur cru est trop dur pour être broyé utilement, et fermenter avant de cuire ne donnerait aucun sucre à transformer.","Logic helps: fermentation needs a sugary liquid, so the sugars must already exist (cooking) and be extracted (crushing). A raw core is too hard to crush usefully, and fermenting before cooking would leave no sugar to work on."]},{"id":"s1f138a1c","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Da che cosa parte di solito un produttore di distillati aromatizzati?","De quoi part généralement un producteur de spiritueux aromatisés ?","What does a flavoured-spirit producer usually start from?"],"o":[["Da uno spirito neutro acquistato","D'un alcool neutre acheté","A bought-in neutral spirit"],["Da frutta raccolta e fermentata in casa","De fruits récoltés et fermentés sur place","Fruit harvested and fermented on site"],["Da un brandy invecchiato in rovere","D'un brandy vieilli en chêne","An oak-aged brandy"],["Da un mosto di cereali maltati","D'un moût de céréales maltées","A mash of malted grain"]],"e":["La maggior parte compra lo stesso spirito neutro che diventa vodka.","La plupart achètent le même alcool neutre qui devient de la vodka.","Most buy in the same neutral spirit that becomes vodka."],"d":["Per questi distillati non serve partire da una materia prima: il lavoro sta nell'aromatizzazione. Rum, whisky o brandy vengono usati solo occasionalmente come base, e fermentare frutta o cereali in proprio non è la regola.","Pour ces spiritueux, inutile de partir d'une matière première : le travail se fait dans l'aromatisation. Le rhum, le whisky ou le brandy ne servent de base qu'occasionnellement, et faire fermenter soi-même fruits ou céréales n'est pas la règle.","These spirits do not need to start from a raw material: the work lies in the flavouring. Rum, whisky or brandy are only occasionally used as a base, and fermenting fruit or grain in-house is not the norm."]},{"id":"s15c4cafb","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Che cosa si ottiene ridistillando uno spirito neutro con dei botanici?","Qu'obtient-on en redistillant un alcool neutre avec des botaniques ?","What do you get by redistilling neutral spirit with botanicals?"],"o":[["Un distillato aromatizzato e incolore","Un spiritueux aromatisé et incolore","A flavoured, colourless spirit"],["Un distillato aromatizzato e colorato","Un spiritueux aromatisé et coloré","A flavoured, coloured spirit"],["Un distillato dolce e colorato","Un spiritueux sucré et coloré","A sweet, coloured spirit"],["Uno spirito di nuovo neutro","Un alcool de nouveau neutre","A spirit that is neutral again"]],"e":["Il vapore porta con sé i profumi ma non il colore dei botanici.","La vapeur emporte les arômes mais pas la couleur des botaniques.","The vapour carries the botanicals' aromas but not their colour."],"d":["Tutto ciò che esce da un alambicco è incolore e secco, quindi né colore né dolcezza. Il colore arriva con la macerazione, la dolcezza con lo zucchero aggiunto. I profumi però passano: per questo il risultato non è affatto neutro.","Tout ce qui sort d'un alambic est incolore et sec : ni couleur ni douceur. La couleur vient avec la macération, la douceur avec le sucre ajouté. Les arômes, en revanche, passent : le résultat n'est donc pas du tout neutre.","Everything that leaves a still is colourless and dry, so there is no colour and no sweetness. Colour comes from maceration, sweetness from added sugar. The aromas do come through, though, so the result is far from neutral."]},{"id":"s13fc9666","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è la macerazione?","Qu'est-ce que la macération ?","What is maceration?"],"o":[["Lasciare i botanici in infusione nello spirito","Laisser infuser les botaniques dans l'alcool","Steeping botanicals in the spirit"],["Distillare lo spirito insieme ai botanici","Distiller l'alcool avec les botaniques","Distilling the spirit with botanicals"],["Aggiungere essenze concentrate","Ajouter des essences concentrées","Adding concentrated essences"],["Invecchiare lo spirito in botti usate","Vieillir l'alcool dans des fûts usagés","Ageing the spirit in used barrels"]],"e":["Nella macerazione i botanici restano immersi e cedono sapore e colore.","Dans la macération, les botaniques restent immergés et cèdent saveur et couleur.","In maceration the botanicals soak and release flavour and colour."],"d":["Distillare con i botanici è la ridistillazione, aggiungere essenze è il terzo metodo, quello degli aromi acquistati. Il passaggio in botte è invecchiamento: dà aromi di legno, non quelli di frutta, erbe e spezie.","Distiller avec les botaniques, c'est la redistillation ; ajouter des essences, c'est la troisième méthode, celle des arômes achetés. Le passage en fût est un vieillissement : il apporte des arômes de bois, pas ceux de fruits, d'herbes et d'épices.","Distilling with botanicals is redistillation, and adding essences is the third method, bought-in flavourings. Time in barrel is ageing: it gives oak aromas, not those of fruit, herbs and spices."]},{"id":"s17e510bb","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Un produttore vuole estrarre più sapore, più in fretta, durante la macerazione. Che cosa può fare?","Un producteur veut extraire plus de saveur, plus vite, pendant la macération. Que peut-il faire ?","A producer wants to extract more flavour, faster, during maceration. What can they do?"],"o":[["Riscaldare leggermente lo spirito","Chauffer légèrement l'alcool","Gently heat the spirit"],["Raffreddare lo spirito","Refroidir l'alcool","Chill the spirit"],["Aggiungere caramello","Ajouter du caramel","Add caramel"],["Filtrare su carbone","Filtrer au charbon","Filter it through charcoal"]],"e":["Un leggero calore accelera l'estrazione del sapore.","Une légère chaleur accélère l'extraction de la saveur.","Gentle heat speeds up flavour extraction."],"d":["Come per un tè, il calore aiuta a estrarre: il freddo rallenta. Il caramello dà colore ma non sapore, e la filtrazione su carbone serve a togliere qualcosa (impurità o colore), non ad aggiungere aromi.","Comme pour un thé, la chaleur aide à extraire ; le froid ralentit. Le caramel apporte de la couleur mais pas de saveur, et la filtration au charbon sert à retirer quelque chose (impuretés ou couleur), pas à ajouter des arômes.","As with tea, heat helps extraction and cold slows it. Caramel adds colour but no flavour, and charcoal filtering removes things (impurities or colour) rather than adding aroma."]},{"id":"s175057b1","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Perché alcuni produttori usano aromi acquistati invece dei botanici?","Pourquoi certains producteurs utilisent-ils des arômes achetés plutôt que des botaniques ?","Why do some producers use bought-in flavourings instead of botanicals?"],"o":[["Soprattutto per ragioni di costo","Surtout pour des raisons de coût","Mostly for reasons of cost"],["Perché la legge lo impone per il gin","Parce que la loi l'impose pour le gin","Because the law requires it for gin"],["Per dare colore al distillato","Pour donner de la couleur au spiritueux","To give the spirit colour"],["Perché aumentano la gradazione","Parce qu'ils augmentent le degré","Because they raise the strength"]],"e":["Gli aromi acquistati, molto concentrati, sono di solito una scelta economica.","Les arômes achetés, très concentrés, sont en général un choix économique.","Concentrated bought-in flavourings are usually a cost-driven choice."],"d":["La legge non obbliga il gin a usarli: anzi, i gin migliori sono ridistillati con botanici veri. Gli aromi si usano in piccole dosi per il sapore, non per il colore, e non hanno nulla a che fare con la gradazione.","La loi n'oblige pas le gin à les utiliser : au contraire, les meilleurs gins sont redistillés avec de vraies botaniques. Les arômes s'utilisent en petites doses pour la saveur, pas pour la couleur, et n'ont rien à voir avec le degré.","The law does not make gin use them: in fact the best gins are redistilled with real botanicals. Flavourings are used in small doses for taste, not colour, and have nothing to do with strength."]},{"id":"s19d45567","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Che cosa si intende per «botanici»?","Que désigne-t-on par « botaniques » ?","What are ‘botanicals’?"],"o":[["Frutta, semi, erbe e spezie usati per aromatizzare","Fruits, graines, herbes et épices servant à aromatiser","Fruits, seeds, herbs and spices used for flavour"],["Aromi artificiali molto concentrati","Des arômes artificiels très concentrés","Highly concentrated artificial flavours"],["I lieviti che avviano la fermentazione","Les levures qui lancent la fermentation","The yeasts that start fermentation"],["Le piante usate per fare le botti","Les plantes qui servent à faire les fûts","The plants used to make barrels"]],"e":["Sono gli ingredienti naturali che danno sapore ai distillati aromatizzati.","Ce sont les ingrédients naturels qui donnent leur saveur aux spiritueux aromatisés.","They are the natural ingredients that flavour flavoured spirits."],"d":["Gli aromi artificiali sono proprio l'alternativa ai botanici, non la stessa cosa. I lieviti trasformano lo zucchero in alcol e il rovere delle botti dà aromi di invecchiamento: nessuno dei due rientra nella definizione.","Les arômes artificiels sont justement l'alternative aux botaniques, pas la même chose. Les levures transforment le sucre en alcool et le chêne des fûts apporte des arômes de vieillissement : aucun des deux n'entre dans la définition.","Artificial flavours are the alternative to botanicals, not the same thing. Yeast turns sugar into alcohol and barrel oak gives ageing aromas: neither fits the definition."]},{"id":"s1a658fef","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Quale sapore deve dominare in un gin?","Quelle saveur doit dominer dans un gin ?","Which flavour must lead in a gin?"],"o":[["Ginepro","Le genièvre","Juniper"],["Coriandolo","La coriandre","Coriander"],["Scorza di limone","Le zeste de citron","Lemon peel"],["Genziana","La gentiane","Gentian"]],"e":["Per definizione il gin deve avere il ginepro come sapore predominante.","Par définition, le gin doit avoir le genièvre comme saveur dominante.","By definition, gin must have juniper as its main flavour."],"d":["Coriandolo e scorza di agrumi sono botanici frequenti nel gin, ma restano comprimari. La genziana è un classico botanico amaro, tipico dei distillati amari e dei vini aromatizzati, non il cuore del gin.","La coriandre et les zestes d'agrumes sont des botaniques fréquentes dans le gin, mais restent au second plan. La gentiane est une botanique amère classique, typique des spiritueux amers et des vins aromatisés, pas le cœur du gin.","Coriander and citrus peel are common gin botanicals, but they play supporting roles. Gentian is a classic bitter botanical, typical of bitter spirits and aromatised wines, not the heart of gin."]},{"id":"s1f501c15","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Che cosa indica la dicitura «London Dry Gin»?","Qu'indique la mention « London Dry Gin » ?","What does the term ‘London Dry Gin’ tell you?"],"o":[["Che gli aromi sono stati dati con la ridistillazione","Que les arômes ont été apportés par redistillation","The flavours were added by redistillation"],["Che il gin è stato prodotto a Londra","Que le gin a été produit à Londres","The gin was made in London"],["Che il gin è invecchiato in rovere","Que le gin a vieilli en chêne","The gin has been aged in oak"],["Che il gin non contiene ginepro","Que le gin ne contient pas de genièvre","The gin contains no juniper"]],"e":["È un'indicazione di metodo: aromi aggiunti durante la ridistillazione.","C'est une indication de méthode : arômes apportés pendant la redistillation.","It is a method term: flavours added during redistillation."],"d":["Il nome trae in inganno, ma non è un luogo: si può produrre ovunque. Il gin tipico non è invecchiato, e un gin senza ginepro dominante non sarebbe un gin.","Le nom est trompeur, mais ce n'est pas un lieu : on peut le produire partout. Le gin typique n'est pas vieilli, et un gin sans genièvre dominant ne serait pas un gin.","The name is misleading, but it is not a place: it can be made anywhere. Typical gin is unaged, and a gin without leading juniper would not be gin at all."]},{"id":"s1f139e45","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Quale gruppo elenca botanici tipici del gin oltre al ginepro?","Quel groupe cite des botaniques typiques du gin en plus du genièvre ?","Which group lists typical gin botanicals besides juniper?"],"o":[["Coriandolo, angelica, iris, scorza di agrumi","Coriandre, angélique, iris, zestes d'agrumes","Coriander, angelica, orris, citrus peel"],["Genziana, chinino, assenzio, arancia amara","Gentiane, quinine, absinthe, orange amère","Gentian, quinine, wormwood, bitter orange"],["Vaniglia, cannella, chiodi di garofano, cocco","Vanille, cannelle, clou de girofle, coco","Vanilla, cinnamon, cloves, coconut"],["Menta, lime, zucchero di canna, panna","Menthe, citron vert, sucre de canne, crème","Mint, lime, cane sugar, cream"]],"e":["Semi di coriandolo, radice di angelica, radice di iris e scorza di agrumi sono botanici classici del gin.","Graines de coriandre, racine d'angélique, racine d'iris et zestes d'agrumes sont des botaniques classiques du gin.","Coriander seed, angelica root, orris root and citrus peel are classic gin botanicals."],"d":["Il secondo gruppo riunisce botanici amari, tipici di amari e vini aromatizzati. Vaniglia, cannella, chiodi di garofano e cocco ricordano gli aromi dati dal rovere. Il quarto gruppo somiglia agli ingredienti di un cocktail o di un liquore cremoso.","Le deuxième groupe réunit des botaniques amères, typiques des amers et des vins aromatisés. Vanille, cannelle, clou de girofle et coco rappellent les arômes apportés par le chêne. Le quatrième groupe ressemble aux ingrédients d'un cocktail ou d'une liqueur à la crème.","The second group is made of bitter botanicals, typical of bitter spirits and aromatised wines. Vanilla, cinnamon, cloves and coconut recall the aromas oak gives. The fourth group looks like cocktail ingredients or a cream liqueur."]},{"id":"s1b675375","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Come si presenta, di solito, un gin?","Comment se présente généralement un gin ?","What is a typical gin like?"],"o":[["Incolore e non invecchiato","Incolore et non vieilli","Colourless and unaged"],["Dorato e invecchiato in rovere","Doré et vieilli en chêne","Golden and oak-aged"],["Incolore e zuccherato","Incolore et sucré","Colourless and sweetened"],["Ambrato e colorato con caramello","Ambré et coloré au caramel","Amber and coloured with caramel"]],"e":["Il gin tipico non passa in legno e resta trasparente.","Le gin typique ne passe pas en fût et reste limpide.","Typical gin sees no oak and stays clear."],"d":["Il colore dorato o ambrato farebbe pensare a botte o caramello, che non fanno parte del gin tipico. Un gin incolore ma zuccherato sarebbe più vicino a un liquore: la dolcezza non è una caratteristica del gin.","Une couleur dorée ou ambrée ferait penser au fût ou au caramel, qui ne font pas partie du gin typique. Un gin incolore mais sucré serait plus proche d'une liqueur : la douceur n'est pas une caractéristique du gin.","A golden or amber colour would suggest oak or caramel, neither of which belongs to typical gin. A colourless but sweetened gin would be closer to a liqueur: sweetness is not a feature of gin."]},{"id":"s13dff997","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Come si producono di solito le vodke aromatizzate?","Comment produit-on généralement les vodkas aromatisées ?","How are flavoured vodkas usually made?"],"o":[["Vodka neutra più aromi acquistati","Vodka neutre et arômes achetés","Neutral vodka plus bought-in flavourings"],["Macerazione lunga in botti di rovere","Longue macération en fûts de chêne","Long maceration in oak barrels"],["Distillazione diretta della frutta","Distillation directe des fruits","Distilling the fruit directly"],["Aggiunta di zucchero e caramello","Ajout de sucre et de caramel","Adding sugar and caramel"]],"e":["Quasi sempre si aggiungono aromi acquistati a una vodka neutra; qualcuno ridistilla.","Le plus souvent, on ajoute des arômes achetés à une vodka neutre ; certains redistillent.","Most add bought-in flavourings to neutral vodka; some redistil."],"d":["La base è la stessa vodka neutra, non un distillato di frutta. Il rovere non c'entra, e zucchero e caramello porterebbero verso un liquore colorato, non verso una vodka aromatizzata.","La base est la même vodka neutre, pas une eau-de-vie de fruits. Le chêne n'a rien à voir, et le sucre et le caramel mèneraient vers une liqueur colorée, pas vers une vodka aromatisée.","The base is the same neutral vodka, not a fruit spirit. Oak plays no part, and sugar plus caramel would lead to a coloured liqueur, not a flavoured vodka."]},{"id":"s1371883c","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Che cosa hanno in comune tutti i distillati amari?","Qu'ont en commun tous les spiritueux amers ?","What do all bitter spirits have in common?"],"o":[["Almeno un botanico amaro, come la genziana","Au moins une botanique amère, comme la gentiane","At least one bitter botanical, such as gentian"],["Un invecchiamento minimo in rovere","Un vieillissement minimal en chêne","A minimum time in oak"],["Una base di rum scuro","Une base de rhum brun","A dark rum base"],["Un livello minimo di zucchero per legge","Un niveau minimal de sucre fixé par la loi","A legal minimum sugar level"]],"e":["Genziana, chinino o arancia amara danno l'amaro a questi distillati.","Gentiane, quinine ou orange amère donnent leur amertume à ces spiritueux.","Gentian, quinine or bitter orange provide the bitterness."],"d":["Non serve alcun passaggio in legno né una base di rum. La dolcezza minima per legge è la regola dei liquori, non dei distillati amari.","Aucun passage en fût ni aucune base de rhum ne sont nécessaires. La douceur minimale imposée par la loi est la règle des liqueurs, pas des spiritueux amers.","No oak or rum base is needed. The legal minimum sweetness is the rule for liqueurs, not for bitter spirits."]},{"id":"s1cd04c79","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Durante una degustazione, dove si percepisce l'amaro di un distillato amaro?","Lors d'une dégustation, où perçoit-on l'amertume d'un spiritueux amer ?","When tasting a bitter spirit, where is the bitterness detected?"],"o":[["Solo in bocca","Seulement en bouche","Only on the palate"],["Solo al naso","Seulement au nez","Only on the nose"],["Sia al naso sia in bocca","Au nez comme en bouche","On both nose and palate"],["Già dal colore","Dès la couleur","Already from the colour"]],"e":["L'amaro è un gusto: si sente in bocca, non con l'olfatto.","L'amertume est une saveur : on la perçoit en bouche, pas à l'odorat.","Bitterness is a taste: it is felt in the mouth, not smelled."],"d":["Al naso si colgono i profumi dei botanici, amari e non, ma non l'amarezza in sé. Il colore non rivela il gusto: un distillato amaro può essere colorato come qualsiasi altro.","Au nez, on perçoit les arômes des botaniques, amères ou non, mais pas l'amertume elle-même. La couleur ne révèle pas le goût : un spiritueux amer peut être coloré comme n'importe quel autre.","On the nose you pick up the aromas of the botanicals, bitter or not, but not the bitterness itself. Colour reveals nothing about taste: a bitter spirit can be coloured like any other."]},{"id":"s1d8ebc2a","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Un barman vuole aggiungere complessità a un cocktail usandone solo poche gocce. Che cosa prende?","Pour ajouter de la complexité à un cocktail avec seulement quelques gouttes, que choisir derrière le bar ?","A bartender wants to add complexity to a drink with just a few drops. What do they reach for?"],"o":[["Un bitter da cocktail","Un bitter à cocktail","Cocktail bitters"],["Un liquore alla panna","Une liqueur à la crème","A cream liqueur"],["Un rum speziato","Un rhum épicé","A spiced rum"],["Un gin London Dry","Un London Dry Gin","A London Dry Gin"]],"e":["I bitter da cocktail sono così concentrati che bastano poche spruzzate.","Les bitters à cocktail sont si concentrés que quelques traits suffisent.","Cocktail bitters are so concentrated that a few dashes are enough."],"d":["Liquore alla panna, rum speziato e gin si usano in quantità normali e possono anche essere bevuti da soli. I bitter da cocktail invece non si bevono mai lisci: servono solo a dare profondità a un drink.","La liqueur à la crème, le rhum épicé et le gin s'utilisent en quantités normales et peuvent aussi se boire seuls. Les bitters à cocktail, eux, ne se boivent jamais purs : ils servent seulement à donner de la profondeur à une boisson.","Cream liqueur, spiced rum and gin are used in normal measures and can be drunk on their own. Cocktail bitters are never drunk neat: they are there only to add depth to a drink."]},{"id":"s196ad33b","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Quando si bevevano tradizionalmente i distillati amari?","Quand buvait-on traditionnellement les spiritueux amers ?","When were bitter spirits traditionally drunk?"],"o":[["A inizio o a fine pasto","En début ou en fin de repas","At the start or end of a meal"],["Solo durante la colazione","Seulement au petit-déjeuner","Only with breakfast"],["Solo come ingrediente di cucina","Seulement comme ingrédient de cuisine","Only as a cooking ingredient"],["Solo diluiti in acqua calda","Seulement dilués dans de l'eau chaude","Only diluted in hot water"]],"e":["Tradizionalmente accompagnavano l'inizio o la fine del pasto; oggi si usano soprattutto nei cocktail.","Traditionnellement, on les buvait en début ou en fin de repas ; aujourd'hui, ils servent surtout en cocktail.","Traditionally they opened or closed a meal; today they are mostly used in cocktails."],"d":["Il loro posto classico era attorno al pasto, come aperitivo o digestivo. Le altre risposte descrivono abitudini inventate: oggi il loro uso principale è nella miscelazione.","Leur place classique était autour du repas, en apéritif ou en digestif. Les autres réponses décrivent des habitudes inventées : aujourd'hui, leur principal usage est la mixologie.","Their classic place was around a meal, as an aperitif or digestif. The other answers describe invented habits: today their main use is in mixing."]},{"id":"s1742b99c","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Quale affermazione sul rum speziato è corretta?","Quelle affirmation sur le rhum épicé est exacte ?","Which statement about spiced rum is true?"],"o":[["Spesso parte da un rum leggero non invecchiato","Il part souvent d'un rhum léger non vieilli","It often starts from a light, unaged rum"],["Deve sempre partire da un rum invecchiato","Il doit toujours partir d'un rhum vieilli","It must always start from an aged rum"],["Può essere aromatizzato solo con botanici","Il ne peut être aromatisé qu'avec des botaniques","It may only be flavoured with botanicals"],["Il suo colore viene sempre dal rovere","Sa couleur vient toujours du chêne","Its colour always comes from oak"]],"e":["Molti rum speziati usano un rum leggero non invecchiato, aromatizzato e colorato con caramello.","Beaucoup de rhums épicés utilisent un rhum léger non vieilli, aromatisé et coloré au caramel.","Many spiced rums use a light unaged rum, flavoured and coloured with caramel."],"d":["Solo pochi rum speziati partono da un rum invecchiato in rovere. Si usano sia botanici sia altri aromi, e il colore spesso viene dal caramello: un aspetto ambrato non prova un lungo invecchiamento.","Seuls quelques rhums épicés partent d'un rhum vieilli en chêne. On utilise à la fois des botaniques et d'autres arômes, et la couleur vient souvent du caramel : un aspect ambré ne prouve pas un long vieillissement.","Only a handful of spiced rums start from an oak-aged rum. Both botanicals and other flavourings are used, and the colour often comes from caramel: an amber look does not prove long ageing."]},{"id":"s136defd1","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Che cosa distingue un liquore da un semplice distillato aromatizzato?","Qu'est-ce qui distingue une liqueur d'un simple spiritueux aromatisé ?","What sets a liqueur apart from a plain flavoured spirit?"],"o":[["È stato anche zuccherato","Elle a aussi été sucrée","It has also been sweetened"],["È stato invecchiato in rovere","Elle a vieilli en chêne","It has been aged in oak"],["Contiene sempre panna","Elle contient toujours de la crème","It always contains cream"],["Ha una gradazione più alta","Elle a un degré plus élevé","It has a higher strength"]],"e":["Liquore = distillato aromatizzato più zucchero.","Liqueur = spiritueux aromatisé plus sucre.","Liqueur = flavoured spirit plus sugar."],"d":["L'invecchiamento non fa parte della definizione. La panna compare solo in alcuni liquori, non in tutti. E non c'è nessuna regola che imponga una gradazione più alta: ciò che conta è la dolcezza.","Le vieillissement ne fait pas partie de la définition. La crème n'apparaît que dans certaines liqueurs, pas dans toutes. Et aucune règle n'impose un degré plus élevé : ce qui compte, c'est la douceur.","Ageing is not part of the definition. Cream appears only in some liqueurs, not all. And no rule demands a higher strength: what matters is the sweetness."]},{"id":"s18bcdf70","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Che cosa stabilisce la legge sullo zucchero nei liquori?","Que prévoit la loi sur le sucre dans les liqueurs ?","What does the law say about sugar in liqueurs?"],"o":[["Che ci sia un livello minimo di dolcezza","Un niveau minimal de douceur","There must be a minimum level of sweetness"],["Che lo zucchero sia vietato","Que le sucre soit interdit","Sugar is not allowed"],["Che lo zucchero sia facoltativo","Que le sucre soit facultatif","Sugar is optional"],["Che lo zucchero venga solo dalla frutta","Que le sucre vienne uniquement des fruits","Sugar may only come from fruit"]],"e":["Per chiamarsi liquore, un distillato deve raggiungere una dolcezza minima.","Pour s'appeler liqueur, un spiritueux doit atteindre une douceur minimale.","To be called a liqueur, a spirit must reach a minimum sweetness."],"d":["Lo zucchero non solo è ammesso, è obbligatorio, quindi non può essere vietato né facoltativo. Si aggiunge dopo l'aromatizzazione e non deve per forza venire dalla frutta.","Le sucre n'est pas seulement permis, il est obligatoire : il ne peut donc être ni interdit ni facultatif. On l'ajoute après l'aromatisation, et il ne doit pas forcément venir des fruits.","Sugar is not just allowed but required, so it cannot be banned or optional. It is added after flavouring and does not have to come from fruit."]},{"id":"s1d548ab5","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Quale ingrediente, insolito per un distillato, si trova in alcuni liquori?","Quel ingrédient, inhabituel pour un spiritueux, trouve-t-on dans certaines liqueurs ?","Which ingredient, unusual for a spirit, is found in some liqueurs?"],"o":[["La panna","La crème","Cream"],["Il lievito","La levure","Yeast"],["Il vino rosso","Le vin rouge","Red wine"],["L'acqua di mare","L'eau de mer","Sea water"]],"e":["Alcuni liquori contengono panna, un ingrediente notevole in questa categoria.","Certaines liqueurs contiennent de la crème, un ingrédient remarquable dans cette catégorie.","Some liqueurs contain cream, a notable ingredient in this category."],"d":["Il lievito serve alla fermentazione, prima della distillazione, e non si aggiunge a un liquore. Il vino come base è tipico dei vini aromatizzati, che sono un'altra categoria. L'acqua di mare non ha alcun ruolo.","La levure sert à la fermentation, avant la distillation, et ne s'ajoute pas à une liqueur. Le vin comme base est typique des vins aromatisés, une autre catégorie. L'eau de mer ne joue aucun rôle.","Yeast is for fermentation, before distillation, and is not added to a liqueur. Wine as a base belongs to aromatised wines, a different category. Sea water plays no part."]},{"id":"s1b8130e3","c":"s7","p":0,"q":["Perché molti liquori usano coloranti artificiali?","Pourquoi beaucoup de liqueurs utilisent-elles des colorants artificiels ?","Why do many liqueurs use artificial colourings?"],"o":[["Il colore naturale sbiadisce in fretta","La couleur naturelle pâlit vite","Natural colour fades quickly"],["Rendono il liquore più dolce","Ils rendent la liqueur plus sucrée","They make the liqueur sweeter"],["La legge vieta i coloranti naturali","La loi interdit les colorants naturels","The law bans natural colours"],["Aggiungono profumi di frutta","Ils ajoutent des arômes de fruits","They add fruity aromas"]],"e":["I coloranti artificiali mantengono il colore stabile e offrono più tinte.","Les colorants artificiels gardent une couleur stable et offrent plus de teintes.","Artificial colours keep the colour stable and offer more shades."],"d":["Il colore naturale da macerazione è ammesso, ma tende a perdere vivacità: per questo si preferiscono coloranti più stabili, che permettono anche colori molto accesi. I coloranti non danno dolcezza né aromi: quelli arrivano da zucchero e aromatizzazione.","La couleur naturelle issue de la macération est permise, mais elle perd vite de son éclat : on préfère donc des colorants plus stables, qui permettent aussi des couleurs très vives. Les colorants n'apportent ni douceur ni arômes : ceux-ci viennent du sucre et de l'aromatisation.","Natural colour from maceration is allowed, but it loses its brightness: so more stable colourings are preferred, which also allow very vivid shades. Colourings add neither sweetness nor aroma; those come from sugar and flavouring."]},{"id":"s10b02e3b","c":"s8","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è un vino aromatizzato?","Qu'est-ce qu'un vin aromatisé ?","What is an aromatised wine?"],"o":[["Un vino con aromi, zucchero e un po' di distillato","Un vin additionné d'arômes, de sucre et d'un peu de spiritueux","A wine with flavourings, sugar and a little spirit"],["Un distillato di vino invecchiato in rovere","Une eau-de-vie de vin vieillie en chêne","A wine spirit aged in oak"],["Un liquore a base di spirito neutro","Une liqueur à base d'alcool neutre","A liqueur based on neutral spirit"],["Un vino lasciato ossidare in botte","Un vin qu'on laisse s'oxyder en fût","A wine left to oxidise in barrel"]],"e":["È un prodotto a base di vino, non un distillato, con aromi, zucchero e un po' di spirito.","C'est un produit à base de vin, pas un spiritueux, avec arômes, sucre et un peu d'alcool.","It is wine-based, not a spirit, with flavourings, sugar and a little spirit added."],"d":["Un distillato di vino invecchiato è un brandy, come il Cognac. Un liquore parte da un distillato, non da un vino. L'ossidazione in botte non fa parte della definizione: ciò che conta sono gli aromi, tra cui sempre un elemento amaro.","Une eau-de-vie de vin vieillie est un brandy, comme le Cognac. Une liqueur part d'un spiritueux, pas d'un vin. L'oxydation en fût ne fait pas partie de la définition : ce qui compte, ce sont les arômes, dont toujours un élément amer.","An aged wine spirit is a brandy, such as Cognac. A liqueur starts from a spirit, not a wine. Oxidation in barrel is not part of the definition: what counts is the flavourings, always including something bitter."]},{"id":"s1f64ac91","c":"s8","p":0,"q":["Quale elenco riporta i quattro componenti di ogni vino aromatizzato?","Quelle liste donne les quatre composants de tout vin aromatisé ?","Which list gives the four components of every aromatised wine?"],"o":[["Vino, aromi con un amaro, zucchero, distillato","Vin, arômes avec un amer, sucre, spiritueux","Wine, flavourings incl. a bitter, sugar, spirit"],["Vino, aromi, caramello, acqua gassata","Vin, arômes, caramel, eau gazeuse","Wine, flavourings, caramel, soda water"],["Distillato, zucchero, panna, coloranti","Spiritueux, sucre, crème, colorants","Spirit, sugar, cream, colourings"],["Vino, succo di frutta, zucchero, lievito","Vin, jus de fruits, sucre, levure","Wine, fruit juice, sugar, yeast"]],"e":["Vino di base, aromi (sempre con qualcosa di amaro), zucchero e un po' di distillato.","Vin de base, arômes (toujours avec un élément amer), sucre et un peu de spiritueux.","Base wine, flavourings (always with something bitter), sugar and a little spirit."],"d":["Il caramello è solo facoltativo e l'acqua gassata non c'entra. Distillato, panna e coloranti descrivono piuttosto un liquore cremoso. Succo e lievito non fanno parte della ricetta, mentre manca il distillato, che è obbligatorio.","Le caramel n'est que facultatif et l'eau gazeuse n'a rien à faire là. Spiritueux, crème et colorants décrivent plutôt une liqueur à la crème. Le jus et la levure ne font pas partie de la recette, et il manque le spiritueux, qui est obligatoire.","Caramel is only optional and soda water does not belong. Spirit, cream and colourings describe a cream liqueur instead. Juice and yeast are not part of the recipe, and that list leaves out the spirit, which is required."]},{"id":"s13c3b09b","c":"s8","p":0,"q":["Perché a un vino aromatizzato si aggiunge un po' di distillato?","Pourquoi ajoute-t-on un peu de spiritueux à un vin aromatisé ?","Why is a little spirit added to an aromatised wine?"],"o":[["Per alzare la gradazione e conservarlo più a lungo","Pour relever le degré et le conserver plus longtemps","To raise the alcohol and make it keep longer"],["Per dargli un colore più scuro","Pour lui donner une couleur plus foncée","To give it a darker colour"],["Per renderlo più dolce","Pour le rendre plus sucré","To make it sweeter"],["Per aggiungere note di rovere","Pour ajouter des notes de chêne","To add oak notes"]],"e":["Il distillato alza l'alcol e allunga la vita del prodotto, anche a bottiglia aperta.","Le spiritueux relève l'alcool et prolonge la vie du produit, même bouteille ouverte.","The spirit raises alcohol and extends shelf life, even once opened."],"d":["Si usa quasi sempre uno spirito neutro, quindi non dà colore né note di legno. Uno spirito è secco: la dolcezza arriva dal vino o dallo zucchero aggiunto, il colore eventualmente dal caramello.","On utilise presque toujours un alcool neutre : il n'apporte donc ni couleur ni notes boisées. Un spiritueux est sec : la douceur vient du vin ou du sucre ajouté, la couleur éventuellement du caramel.","A neutral spirit is nearly always used, so it brings no colour or oak notes. Spirits are dry: sweetness comes from the wine or added sugar, and any colour from caramel."]},{"id":"s1a499a65","c":"s8","p":0,"q":["Che tipo di distillato si usa quasi sempre nei vini aromatizzati?","Quel type de spiritueux utilise-t-on presque toujours dans les vins aromatisés ?","Which type of spirit is nearly always used in aromatised wines?"],"o":[["Uno spirito neutro","Un alcool neutre","A neutral spirit"],["Un brandy invecchiato","Un brandy vieilli","An aged brandy"],["Un whisky torbato","Un whisky tourbé","A peated whisky"],["Un rum scuro","Un rhum brun","A dark rum"]],"e":["Lo spirito neutro alza la gradazione senza disturbare gli aromi scelti.","L'alcool neutre relève le degré sans gêner les arômes choisis.","Neutral spirit raises the strength without clashing with the chosen flavours."],"d":["Un distillato con carattere porterebbe aromi propri, come legno, torba o melassa, che entrerebbero in competizione con la ricetta. Il ruolo del distillato qui è tecnico, non aromatico.","Un spiritueux de caractère apporterait ses propres arômes, comme le bois, la tourbe ou la mélasse, qui entreraient en concurrence avec la recette. Ici, le rôle du spiritueux est technique, pas aromatique.","A characterful spirit would bring its own aromas, such as oak, peat or molasses, competing with the recipe. Here the spirit's role is technical, not aromatic."]},{"id":"s195a5071","c":"s8","p":0,"q":["Quale gruppo elenca botanici amari usati nei vini aromatizzati?","Quel groupe cite des botaniques amères utilisées dans les vins aromatisés ?","Which group lists bitter botanicals used in aromatised wines?"],"o":[["Assenzio, genziana, chinino","Absinthe, gentiane, quinine","Wormwood, gentian, quinine"],["Ginepro, coriandolo, angelica","Genièvre, coriandre, angélique","Juniper, coriander, angelica"],["Vaniglia, cocco, cannella","Vanille, coco, cannelle","Vanilla, coconut, cinnamon"],["Menta, lime, zenzero","Menthe, citron vert, gingembre","Mint, lime, ginger"]],"e":["Ogni ricetta include un amaro, come assenzio, genziana o chinino.","Chaque recette comprend un amer, comme l'absinthe, la gentiane ou la quinine.","Every recipe includes a bitter, such as wormwood, gentian or quinine."],"d":["Ginepro, coriandolo e angelica sono i classici del gin, che non sono amari. Vaniglia, cocco e cannella ricordano gli aromi del rovere. Menta, lime e zenzero fanno pensare a un cocktail lungo, non alla ricetta di un vino aromatizzato.","Genièvre, coriandre et angélique sont les classiques du gin, et ne sont pas amers. Vanille, coco et cannelle rappellent les arômes du chêne. Menthe, citron vert et gingembre évoquent un long drink, pas la recette d'un vin aromatisé.","Juniper, coriander and angelica are gin classics, and they are not bitter. Vanilla, coconut and cinnamon recall oak aromas. Mint, lime and ginger suggest a long drink, not an aromatised wine recipe."]},{"id":"s19842c4e","c":"s8","p":0,"q":["Con quale botanico deve essere aromatizzato un vermut?","Avec quelle botanique un vermouth doit-il être aromatisé ?","Which botanical must vermouth be flavoured with?"],"o":[["Assenzio","L'absinthe","Wormwood"],["Ginepro","Le genièvre","Juniper"],["Arancia amara","L'orange amère","Bitter orange"],["Chinino","La quinine","Quinine"]],"e":["L'assenzio è obbligatorio nel vermut.","L'absinthe est obligatoire dans le vermouth.","Wormwood is required in vermouth."],"d":["Il ginepro è la firma del gin. Arancia amara e chinino sono botanici amari che possono comparire in vini aromatizzati e distillati amari, ma la regola del vermut riguarda specificamente l'assenzio.","Le genièvre est la signature du gin. L'orange amère et la quinine sont des botaniques amères qu'on peut trouver dans les vins aromatisés et les spiritueux amers, mais la règle du vermouth concerne précisément l'absinthe.","Juniper is gin's signature. Bitter orange and quinine are bitter botanicals that may appear in aromatised wines and bitter spirits, but the vermouth rule is specifically about wormwood."]},{"id":"s17989ceb","c":"s8","p":0,"q":["Un vermut rosso è prodotto con vino bianco. Da dove viene, di solito, il suo colore?","Un vermouth rouge est élaboré avec du vin blanc. D'où vient généralement sa couleur ?","A red vermouth is made from white wine. Where does its colour usually come from?"],"o":[["Dal caramello","Du caramel","Caramel"],["Dalle bucce dell'uva rossa","Des peaux de raisin noir","Black grape skins"],["Da un lungo invecchiamento in rovere","D'un long vieillissement en chêne","Long ageing in oak"],["Dal ginepro macerato","Du genièvre macéré","Macerated juniper"]],"e":["Con una base bianca, il rosso arriva di solito dal caramello.","Avec une base blanche, le rouge vient généralement du caramel.","With a white base, the red colour usually comes from caramel."],"d":["Se la base è bianca, le bucce rosse non entrano in gioco. Il lungo invecchiamento in rovere non fa parte della ricetta, e il ginepro è un botanico del gin che non tinge di rosso. Il caramello può anche aggiungere un leggero aroma di caramello.","Si la base est blanche, les peaux de raisin noir n'entrent pas en jeu. Un long vieillissement en chêne ne fait pas partie de la recette, et le genièvre est une botanique du gin qui ne colore pas en rouge. Le caramel peut aussi apporter une légère note de caramel.","If the base is white, black grape skins play no part. Long oak ageing is not part of the recipe, and juniper is a gin botanical that does not turn things red. Caramel can also add a light caramel aroma."]},{"id":"s17689050","c":"s8","p":0,"q":["Un cliente chiede un vermut «dry» pensando che sia senza zucchero. Che cosa è corretto rispondere?","Un client demande un vermouth « dry » en pensant qu'il ne contient pas de sucre. Que répondre ?","A customer orders a ‘dry’ vermouth thinking it has no sugar. What is the correct reply?"],"o":[["Che quasi sempre contiene zucchero aggiunto","Qu'il contient presque toujours du sucre ajouté","It nearly always contains added sugar"],["Che per legge non contiene zucchero","Que la loi lui interdit tout sucre","By law it contains no sugar at all"],["Che è più dolce di un vermut rosso","Qu'il est plus sucré qu'un vermouth rouge","It is sweeter than a red vermouth"],["Che è fatto senza vino","Qu'il est fait sans vin","It is made without wine"]],"e":["Anche i vermut «dry» hanno quasi sempre un po' di zucchero aggiunto.","Même les vermouths « dry » ont presque toujours un peu de sucre ajouté.","Even ‘dry’ vermouths nearly always have some added sugar."],"d":["Quasi nessun vino aromatizzato è del tutto secco, e nessuna regola vieta lo zucchero nel «dry». È invece il vermut rosso a essere di solito molto zuccherato. E ogni vermut parte da un vino bianco.","Presque aucun vin aromatisé n'est complètement sec, et aucune règle n'interdit le sucre dans le « dry ». C'est au contraire le vermouth rouge qui est généralement très sucré. Et tout vermouth part d'un vin blanc.","Almost no aromatised wine is fully dry, and no rule bans sugar in ‘dry’. It is red vermouth that is usually heavily sweetened. And every vermouth starts from a white wine."]},{"id":"s1e9e4c02","c":"s8","p":0,"q":["Quali sono le zone più note per la produzione di vini aromatizzati?","Quelles sont les zones les plus connues pour les vins aromatisés ?","Which areas are best known for aromatised wines?"],"o":[["Sud-est della Francia e nord-ovest dell'Italia","Le sud-est de la France et le nord-ouest de l'Italie","South-east France and north-west Italy"],["Nord della Francia e sud dell'Italia","Le nord de la France et le sud de l'Italie","Northern France and southern Italy"],["Scozia e Irlanda","L'Écosse et l'Irlande","Scotland and Ireland"],["Messico e Caraibi","Le Mexique et les Caraïbes","Mexico and the Caribbean"]],"e":["Si producono ovunque, ma le zone celebri sono il sud-est francese e il nord-ovest italiano.","On en produit partout, mais les zones célèbres sont le sud-est français et le nord-ouest italien.","They are made everywhere, but the famous areas are south-east France and north-west Italy."],"d":["La seconda risposta inverte le direzioni. Scozia e Irlanda richiamano il whisky, Messico e Caraibi la Tequila e il rum: sono distillati, mentre qui parliamo di prodotti a base di vino.","La deuxième réponse inverse les directions. L'Écosse et l'Irlande évoquent le whisky, le Mexique et les Caraïbes la Tequila et le rhum : ce sont des spiritueux, alors qu'il s'agit ici de produits à base de vin.","The second answer flips the directions. Scotland and Ireland point to whisky, Mexico and the Caribbean to Tequila and rum: those are spirits, while this is about wine-based products."]},{"id":"s1d001f10","c":"s8","p":0,"q":["Perché i vini aromatizzati sono così utili nei cocktail?","Pourquoi les vins aromatisés sont-ils si utiles en cocktail ?","Why are aromatised wines so useful in cocktails?"],"o":[["Portano dolcezza, amaro e acidità insieme","Ils apportent à la fois douceur, amertume et acidité","They bring sweetness, bitterness and acidity at once"],["Sono la base alcolica più forte del drink","Ce sont la base alcoolique la plus forte de la boisson","They are the strongest spirit in the drink"],["Danno solo colore senza cambiare il gusto","Ils donnent seulement de la couleur sans changer le goût","They add colour without changing the taste"],["Sostituiscono il ghiaccio nella diluizione","Ils remplacent la glace pour la dilution","They replace ice for dilution"]],"e":["Un solo ingrediente aggiunge dolcezza, amaro e acidità al cocktail.","Un seul ingrédient ajoute douceur, amertume et acidité au cocktail.","One ingredient adds sweetness, bitterness and acidity to the drink."],"d":["Sono vini con un po' di distillato, quindi molto meno forti della base alcolica, che di solito ha 40% vol. o più. Cambiano eccome il gusto, e la diluizione resta compito del ghiaccio e degli ingredienti analcolici.","Ce sont des vins additionnés d'un peu de spiritueux, donc bien moins forts que la base alcoolique, qui fait généralement 40 % vol. ou plus. Ils changent nettement le goût, et la dilution reste l'affaire de la glace et des ingrédients sans alcool.","They are wines with a little spirit, so far weaker than the base spirit, which is usually 40% abv or more. They clearly change the taste, and dilution is still the job of ice and non-alcoholic ingredients."]},{"id":"s154b54c6","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Perché si aggiunge acqua al campione durante una degustazione di distillati?","Pourquoi ajoute-t-on de l'eau à l'échantillon lors d'une dégustation de spiritueux ?","Why is water added to the sample when tasting a spirit?"],"o":[["Perché a 40% vol è difficile giudicarlo con precisione","Parce qu'à 40 % vol il est difficile de le juger avec précision","Because at 40% abv it is hard to judge accurately"],["Perché l'acqua cambia il colore e lo rende più leggibile","Parce que l'eau change la couleur et la rend plus lisible","Because water changes the colour and makes it easier to read"],["Perché l'acqua aggiunge zucchero e rende il sorso più morbido","Parce que l'eau ajoute du sucre et adoucit la gorgée","Because water adds sugar and softens the sip"],["Perché il distillato non è mai stato diluito prima","Parce que le spiritueux n'a jamais été dilué auparavant","Because the spirit has never been diluted before"]],"e":["La forza dell'alcol copre molti aromi: diluendo si percepiscono meglio.","La force de l'alcool masque de nombreux arômes : en diluant, on les perçoit mieux.","The strength of the alcohol hides many aromas; diluting reveals them."],"d":["Un distillato in bottiglia è già stato diluito dal produttore, ma a circa 40% vol resta molto forte: l'alcol punge il naso e copre le sfumature. Aggiungere acqua lo rende più facile da giudicare. L'acqua non aggiunge zucchero e non serve a valutare il colore, che si osserva prima della diluizione.","Un spiritueux en bouteille a déjà été dilué par le producteur, mais à environ 40 % vol il reste très fort : l'alcool pique le nez et masque les nuances. Ajouter de l'eau le rend plus facile à juger. L'eau n'apporte pas de sucre et ne sert pas à évaluer la couleur, que l'on observe avant la dilution.","A bottled spirit has already been diluted by the producer, but at around 40% abv it is still very strong: the alcohol stings the nose and masks the details. Adding water makes it easier to judge. Water adds no sugar and is not used to assess colour, which is looked at before diluting."]},{"id":"s1982b93a","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Quanto distillato si versa di solito come campione da degustazione?","Quelle quantité de spiritueux verse-t-on en général comme échantillon de dégustation ?","How much spirit is usually poured as a tasting sample?"],"o":[["Circa 1,5 cL","Environ 1,5 cL","About 1.5 cL"],["Circa 15 cL","Environ 15 cL","About 15 cL"],["Circa 5 cL","Environ 5 cL","About 5 cL"],["Circa 0,1 cL","Environ 0,1 cL","About 0.1 cL"]],"e":["Un campione di circa 1,5 cL basta per osservare, annusare e assaggiare.","Un échantillon d'environ 1,5 cL suffit pour regarder, sentir et goûter.","A sample of about 1.5 cL is enough to look, smell and taste."],"d":["1,5 cL corrisponde più o meno a un cucchiaio: abbastanza per tutte le fasi, poco per non affaticare i sensi. 5 cL è già una dose da bere, 15 cL un bicchiere intero, mentre 0,1 cL sarebbe solo qualche goccia, troppo poco per lavorare.","1,5 cL correspond à peu près à une cuillère à soupe : assez pour toutes les étapes, assez peu pour ne pas fatiguer les sens. 5 cL est déjà une dose à boire, 15 cL un verre entier, tandis que 0,1 cL ne ferait que quelques gouttes, trop peu pour travailler.","1.5 cL is roughly a tablespoon: enough for every step, small enough not to tire your senses. 5 cL is already a drinking measure and 15 cL a full glass, while 0.1 cL would be just a few drops, too little to work with."]},{"id":"s18786a58","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Quale forma di bicchiere è la più adatta per degustare un distillato?","Quelle forme de verre convient le mieux pour déguster un spiritueux ?","Which glass shape is best for tasting a spirit?"],"o":[["Coppa ampia che si stringe verso l'alto","Un large calice qui se resserre vers le haut","A wide bowl that narrows towards the top"],["Bicchiere basso e dritto, molto aperto","Un verre bas et droit, très ouvert","A short, straight, wide-open tumbler"],["Coppa piatta e larga come per lo spumante","Une coupe plate et large comme pour les bulles","A flat, wide saucer like a sparkling-wine coupe"],["Bicchiere alto e stretto con bordo svasato","Un verre haut et étroit au bord évasé","A tall, narrow glass with a flared rim"]],"e":["La coppa ampia libera gli aromi e l'apertura stretta li concentra verso il naso.","Le large calice libère les arômes et l'ouverture étroite les concentre vers le nez.","The wide bowl releases the aromas and the narrow top concentrates them."],"d":["Un bicchiere a tulipano è pensato per raccogliere i profumi. Nei bicchieri molto aperti, come la coppa piatta o il tumbler, gli aromi si disperdono subito. Un bordo svasato fa lo stesso effetto: allarga l'apertura invece di stringerla.","Un verre en forme de tulipe est conçu pour rassembler les parfums. Dans les verres très ouverts, comme la coupe plate ou le gobelet, les arômes s'échappent aussitôt. Un bord évasé produit le même effet : il élargit l'ouverture au lieu de la resserrer.","A tulip-shaped glass is designed to gather the scents. In very open glasses, such as a flat coupe or a tumbler, the aromas escape at once. A flared rim has the same effect: it widens the opening instead of narrowing it."]},{"id":"s1477cff5","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["A che cosa serve una superficie bianca durante la degustazione?","À quoi sert une surface blanche pendant la dégustation ?","What is a white surface used for during a tasting?"],"o":[["A valutare meglio il colore del distillato","À mieux évaluer la couleur du spiritueux","To judge the colour of the spirit better"],["A capire quanto è lungo il finale","À mesurer la longueur de la finale","To work out how long the finish is"],["A ridurre gli odori presenti nella stanza","À réduire les odeurs présentes dans la pièce","To reduce the smells in the room"],["A tenere il campione alla giusta temperatura","À garder l'échantillon à la bonne température","To keep the sample at the right temperature"]],"e":["Uno sfondo bianco permette di vedere il colore senza distrazioni.","Un fond blanc permet de voir la couleur sans distraction.","A white background lets you see the colour without distractions."],"d":["Tenendo il bicchiere davanti a un foglio o una tovaglia bianca, con buona luce naturale, il colore si legge in modo affidabile. La superficie non influisce su odori, temperatura o finale: queste cose dipendono dalla stanza, dal campione e dall'assaggio in bocca.","En tenant le verre devant une feuille ou une nappe blanche, avec une bonne lumière naturelle, on lit la couleur de façon fiable. La surface n'a aucun effet sur les odeurs, la température ou la finale : cela dépend de la pièce, de l'échantillon et de la bouche.","Holding the glass against white paper or a white tablecloth, in good natural light, lets you read the colour reliably. The surface has no effect on smells, temperature or finish: those depend on the room, the sample and the palate."]},{"id":"s14ad83e6","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Poco prima di una degustazione, quale di queste abitudini conviene evitare?","Juste avant une dégustation, quelle habitude vaut-il mieux éviter ?","Just before a tasting, which of these habits is best avoided?"],"o":[["Lavarsi i denti o bere un caffè","Se brosser les dents ou boire un café","Brushing your teeth or drinking coffee"],["Bere un bicchiere d'acqua naturale","Boire un verre d'eau plate","Drinking a glass of still water"],["Sedersi vicino a una finestra luminosa","S'asseoir près d'une fenêtre lumineuse","Sitting near a bright window"],["Preparare un foglio bianco sul tavolo","Préparer une feuille blanche sur la table","Putting a white sheet on the table"]],"e":["Dentifricio e caffè lasciano sapori persistenti che falsano l'assaggio.","Le dentifrice et le café laissent des saveurs persistantes qui faussent la dégustation.","Toothpaste and coffee leave lingering flavours that distort the tasting."],"d":["La bocca deve essere pulita e neutra, senza sapori che restano. Le altre tre abitudini invece aiutano: l'acqua mantiene idratati, la luce naturale e il foglio bianco servono per osservare bene il colore.","La bouche doit être propre et neutre, sans saveurs qui persistent. Les trois autres habitudes, au contraire, aident : l'eau maintient hydraté, la lumière naturelle et la feuille blanche servent à bien observer la couleur.","Your palate should be clean and neutral, with no lingering flavours. The other three habits actually help: water keeps you hydrated, while natural light and white paper help you see the colour properly."]},{"id":"s1b8621ca","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Qual è l'ordine corretto delle fasi di degustazione di un distillato?","Quel est l'ordre correct des étapes de dégustation d'un spiritueux ?","What is the correct order of steps when tasting a spirit?"],"o":[["Occhio e naso, acqua, di nuovo naso, bocca, sputare","Œil et nez, eau, à nouveau nez, bouche, recracher","Eyes and nose, water, nose again, palate, spit"],["Acqua, occhio e naso, bocca, di nuovo naso, sputare","Eau, œil et nez, bouche, à nouveau nez, recracher","Water, eyes and nose, palate, nose again, spit"],["Bocca, occhio e naso, acqua, di nuovo bocca, sputare","Bouche, œil et nez, eau, à nouveau bouche, recracher","Palate, eyes and nose, water, palate again, spit"],["Occhio e naso, bocca, sputare, acqua, di nuovo naso","Œil et nez, bouche, recracher, eau, à nouveau nez","Eyes and nose, palate, spit, water, nose again"]],"e":["Si osserva e si annusa puro, si diluisce, si riannusa, poi si assaggia e si sputa.","On observe et on sent pur, on dilue, on sent à nouveau, puis on goûte et on recrache.","Look and smell neat, dilute, smell again, then taste and spit."],"d":["Il primo esame si fa sul distillato puro, per avere un'impressione di partenza. L'acqua arriva dopo, così si può confrontare il naso prima e dopo la diluizione. L'assaggio viene per ultimo, sul campione diluito, che è più facile da giudicare; mettere la bocca prima dell'acqua o il naso dopo aver sputato rompe questa logica.","Le premier examen se fait sur le spiritueux pur, pour avoir une impression de départ. L'eau vient ensuite, ce qui permet de comparer le nez avant et après dilution. La bouche arrive en dernier, sur l'échantillon dilué, plus facile à juger ; goûter avant d'ajouter l'eau ou sentir après avoir recraché casse cette logique.","The first look and sniff are on the neat spirit, to get a starting impression. Water comes next, so you can compare the nose before and after dilution. Tasting comes last, on the diluted sample, which is easier to judge; tasting before the water or smelling after spitting breaks this logic."]},{"id":"s16b3eabf","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Dopo aver aggiunto l'acqua e annusato di nuovo, si nota che compaiono profumi nuovi. Perché succede?","Après avoir ajouté l'eau et senti à nouveau, de nouveaux parfums apparaissent. Pourquoi ?","After adding water and smelling again, new aromas appear. Why does this happen?"],"o":[["L'alcol, ora meno forte, non copre più alcuni aromi","L'alcool, moins fort, ne masque plus certains arômes","The alcohol, now weaker, no longer masks some aromas"],["L'acqua porta con sé profumi di frutta e fiori","L'eau apporte elle-même des parfums de fruits et de fleurs","The water itself brings fruit and floral aromas"],["Il campione si è scaldato e ha iniziato a invecchiare","L'échantillon s'est réchauffé et a commencé à vieillir","The sample has warmed up and started to age"],["Il bicchiere ha rilasciato gli aromi del campione precedente","Le verre a libéré les arômes de l'échantillon précédent","The glass has released aromas from the previous sample"]],"e":["Con meno forza alcolica, profumi prima nascosti diventano percepibili.","Avec moins de force alcoolique, des parfums cachés deviennent perceptibles.","With less alcoholic strength, hidden aromas become noticeable."],"d":["Diluire in parti uguali dimezza la forza del campione: il pizzico dell'alcol si attenua e lascia emergere sfumature che prima erano coperte. L'acqua di per sé non ha profumo, e pochi minuti nel bicchiere non invecchiano un distillato. Un bicchiere sporco sarebbe un errore di preparazione, non l'effetto normale della diluizione.","Diluer à parts égales divise par deux la force de l'échantillon : le piquant de l'alcool s'atténue et laisse apparaître des nuances jusque-là masquées. L'eau n'a pas d'odeur, et quelques minutes dans le verre ne font pas vieillir un spiritueux. Un verre sale serait une erreur de préparation, pas l'effet normal de la dilution.","Diluting with an equal amount of water halves the strength of the sample: the sting of the alcohol fades and lets hidden details come through. Water has no aroma of its own, and a few minutes in a glass do not age a spirit. A dirty glass would be a preparation mistake, not the normal effect of dilution."]},{"id":"s1556b1d9","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Una vodka non ha quasi nessun profumo. Quale intensità al naso si annota?","Une vodka n'a presque aucune odeur. Quelle intensité au nez note-t-on ?","A vodka has almost no smell at all. Which nose intensity do you record?"],"o":[["Neutra","Neutre","Neutral"],["Leggera","Légère","Light"],["Corta","Courte","Short"],["Semplice","Simple","Simple"]],"e":["«Neutro» è il gradino più basso dell'intensità, per un naso quasi assente.","« Neutre » est le niveau le plus bas d'intensité, pour un nez presque absent.","'Neutral' is the lowest intensity level, for an almost absent nose."],"d":["L'intensità al naso va da neutro a leggero, medio e pronunciato. «Leggero» indica che qualche profumo c'è, anche se delicato. «Corto» descrive il finale in bocca e «semplice» riguarda la complessità: sono termini veri ma usati in un altro punto della nota.","L'intensité au nez va de neutre à léger, moyen et prononcé. « Léger » indique qu'il y a quelques parfums, même discrets. « Court » décrit la finale en bouche et « simple » concerne la complexité : ce sont de vrais termes, mais utilisés ailleurs dans la note.","Nose intensity runs from neutral to light, medium and pronounced. 'Light' means there is some aroma, however delicate. 'Short' describes the finish and 'simple' refers to complexity: real terms, but used in a different part of the note."]},{"id":"s1fd451fb","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["In un brandy invecchiato si notano vaniglia e spezie dolci. Da dove vengono più probabilmente questi aromi?","Dans un brandy vieilli, on perçoit de la vanille et des épices douces. D'où viennent le plus probablement ces arômes ?","In an aged brandy you notice vanilla and sweet spice. Where do these aromas most likely come from?"],"o":[["Dal legno e dall'invecchiamento","Du bois et du vieillissement","From the oak and maturation"],["Dall'uva usata come materia prima","Du raisin utilisé comme matière première","From the grapes used as raw material"],["Dall'acqua aggiunta nel bicchiere","De l'eau ajoutée dans le verre","From the water added in the glass"],["Dallo zucchero aggiunto dopo la distillazione","Du sucre ajouté après la distillation","From sugar added after distillation"]],"e":["Vaniglia e spezie sono tipici aromi che il legno cede durante l'invecchiamento.","La vanille et les épices sont des arômes typiques cédés par le bois pendant le vieillissement.","Vanilla and spice are typical aromas given by oak during maturation."],"d":["Gli aromi si raggruppano per origine: materia prima, lavorazione, legno e invecchiamento. L'uva tende a dare note fruttate, non vaniglia. L'acqua non ha profumo e lo zucchero, se presente, si sente come dolcezza in bocca più che come aroma speziato.","On classe les arômes par origine : matière première, élaboration, bois et vieillissement. Le raisin donne plutôt des notes fruitées, pas de la vanille. L'eau n'a pas d'odeur et le sucre, s'il y en a, se perçoit comme une douceur en bouche plutôt que comme un arôme épicé.","Aromas are grouped by source: raw material, processing, and oak and maturation. Grapes tend to give fruity notes, not vanilla. Water has no smell, and sugar, if present, shows up as sweetness on the palate rather than as a spicy aroma."]},{"id":"s1d3483c4","c":"t1","p":0,"q":["Nella nota di degustazione, che cosa descrive il «finale»?","Dans une note de dégustation, que décrit la « finale » ?","In a tasting note, what does the 'finish' describe?"],"o":[["Quanto a lungo restano i sapori dopo aver sputato","Combien de temps les saveurs persistent après avoir recraché","How long the flavours linger after spitting"],["Il colore del liquido in fondo al bicchiere","La couleur du liquide au fond du verre","The colour of the liquid at the bottom of the glass"],["L'ultimo aroma percepito prima di aggiungere acqua","Le dernier arôme perçu avant d'ajouter l'eau","The last aroma noticed before adding water"],["Il grado alcolico indicato in etichetta","Le degré d'alcool indiqué sur l'étiquette","The alcoholic strength shown on the label"]],"e":["Il finale misura la persistenza dei sapori: corto, medio o lungo.","La finale mesure la persistance des saveurs : courte, moyenne ou longue.","The finish measures how long flavours persist: short, medium or long."],"d":["Il finale è l'ultima osservazione in bocca: dopo aver sputato si conta quanto durano i sapori. Un finale lungo è spesso segno di qualità. Il colore appartiene all'aspetto, gli aromi al naso e il grado alcolico è un dato dell'etichetta, non un'osservazione di degustazione.","La finale est la dernière observation en bouche : après avoir recraché, on mesure combien de temps durent les saveurs. Une finale longue est souvent un signe de qualité. La couleur relève de l'aspect, les arômes du nez, et le degré d'alcool est une donnée d'étiquette, pas une observation de dégustation.","The finish is the last observation on the palate: after spitting, you note how long the flavours last. A long finish is often a sign of quality. Colour belongs to appearance, aromas to the nose, and alcoholic strength is label information, not a tasting observation."]},{"id":"s197c1210","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["In un cocktail, che cosa costituisce la parte «forte»?","Dans un cocktail, qu'est-ce qui constitue la partie « forte » ?","In a cocktail, what makes up the 'strong' element?"],"o":[["Il distillato di base","Le spiritueux de base","The base spirit"],["Il succo di agrumi","Le jus d'agrumes","The citrus juice"],["Lo sciroppo di zucchero","Le sirop de sucre","The sugar syrup"],["Il ghiaccio usato per raffreddare","La glace utilisée pour refroidir","The ice used for chilling"]],"e":["Il distillato di base è la parte forte e il cuore del gusto.","Le spiritueux de base est la partie forte et le cœur du goût.","The base spirit is the strong element and the heart of the flavour."],"d":["La parte forte porta l'alcol e il carattere principale del drink. Gli agrumi forniscono acidità, lo sciroppo dolcezza e il ghiaccio diluizione, quindi appartiene alla parte leggera: sono contrappesi, non la base.","La partie forte apporte l'alcool et le caractère principal de la boisson. Les agrumes donnent l'acidité, le sirop la douceur et la glace la dilution, qui relève donc de la partie légère : ce sont des contrepoids, pas la base.","The strong element brings the alcohol and the main character of the drink. Citrus gives acidity, syrup gives sweetness and ice gives dilution, which belongs to the weak side: they are counterweights, not the base."]},{"id":"s1a2aa17d","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Qual è la gradazione tipica del distillato di base di un cocktail?","Quel est le degré typique du spiritueux de base d'un cocktail ?","What is the typical strength of a cocktail's base spirit?"],"o":[["Di solito 40% vol o più","En général 40 % vol ou plus","Usually 40% abv or higher"],["Di solito tra 12 e 15% vol","En général entre 12 et 15 % vol","Usually between 12 and 15% abv"],["Di solito intorno al 20% vol","En général autour de 20 % vol","Usually around 20% abv"],["Di solito oltre il 90% vol","En général plus de 90 % vol","Usually above 90% abv"]],"e":["La base forte di un cocktail è in genere un distillato al 40% vol o più.","La base forte d'un cocktail est en général un spiritueux à 40 % vol ou plus.","A cocktail's strong base is generally a spirit at 40% abv or more."],"d":["Le gradazioni di 12–15% vol sono tipiche del vino, e intorno al 20% si trovano molti prodotti più leggeri come alcuni vini aromatizzati. Oltre il 90% vol si parla di alcol neutro destinato alla produzione, non di un distillato pronto da miscelare.","Les degrés de 12 à 15 % vol sont typiques du vin, et autour de 20 % on trouve des produits plus légers comme certains vins aromatisés. Au-delà de 90 % vol, il s'agit d'alcool neutre destiné à la production, pas d'un spiritueux prêt à mélanger.","Strengths of 12–15% abv are typical of wine, and around 20% you find lighter products such as some aromatised wines. Above 90% abv you are looking at neutral spirit for production, not a spirit ready for mixing."]},{"id":"s1f536c16","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["In un drink corto mescolato con ghiaccio e servito senza aggiunte, da dove viene la parte «leggera»?","Dans un short drink remué sur glace et servi sans rien ajouter, d'où vient la partie « légère » ?","In a short drink stirred with ice and served with nothing added, where does the 'weak' element come from?"],"o":[["Dall'acqua del ghiaccio che fonde mescolando","De l'eau de la glace qui fond en remuant","From water as the ice melts during stirring"],["Dai bitter aggiunti a gocce","Des bitters ajoutés en quelques gouttes","From the bitters added by the dash"],["Dal distillato di base","Du spiritueux de base","From the base spirit"],["Dalla buccia di agrume usata come guarnizione","Du zeste d'agrume utilisé en décoration","From the citrus peel used as a garnish"]],"e":["Mescolando con ghiaccio, la fusione aggiunge acqua e attenua l'alcol.","En remuant sur glace, la fonte apporte de l'eau et adoucit l'alcool.","Stirring with ice adds meltwater and softens the alcohol."],"d":["Nei drink corti la diluizione arriva quasi solo dal ghiaccio durante la preparazione, mescolando o shakerando. I bitter sono una nota amara, il distillato è la parte forte e una scorza d'agrume dà profumo, ma nessuno dei tre allunga davvero il drink.","Dans les short drinks, la dilution vient presque uniquement de la glace pendant la préparation, en remuant ou en secouant. Les bitters sont une note amère, le spiritueux est la partie forte et un zeste parfume, mais aucun des trois n'allonge vraiment la boisson.","In short drinks, dilution comes almost entirely from ice during mixing, by stirring or shaking. Bitters are a bitter accent, the spirit is the strong part and a citrus peel adds scent, but none of them really lengthens the drink."]},{"id":"s1c091e94","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Come si chiama l'ingrediente che porta una nota amara e/o acida per bilanciare la dolcezza?","Comment appelle-t-on l'ingrédient qui apporte une note amère et/ou acide pour équilibrer le sucré ?","What is the ingredient called that brings a bitter and/or sour note to balance sweetness?"],"o":[["Il modificatore","Le modificateur","The modifier"],["La guarnizione","La garniture","The garnish"],["Il distillato di base","Le spiritueux de base","The base spirit"],["Il dolcificante","L'édulcorant","The sweetener"]],"e":["Il modificatore «condisce» il cocktail con amaro e/o acido.","Le modificateur « assaisonne » le cocktail avec de l'amer et/ou de l'acide.","The modifier 'seasons' the drink with bitterness and/or sourness."],"d":["Spesso un cocktail viene prima addolcito e poi bilanciato da un modificatore, come succo di agrumi o bitter. La guarnizione è soprattutto decorativa o profumata, il distillato di base è la parte forte e il dolcificante è proprio ciò che il modificatore deve controbilanciare.","Souvent, un cocktail est d'abord sucré puis équilibré par un modificateur, comme un jus d'agrume ou des bitters. La garniture est surtout décorative ou parfumée, le spiritueux de base est la partie forte, et l'édulcorant est justement ce que le modificateur doit contrebalancer.","A cocktail is often sweetened first and then balanced by a modifier, such as citrus juice or bitters. A garnish is mainly decorative or aromatic, the base spirit is the strong part, and the sweetener is exactly what the modifier has to offset."]},{"id":"s1d2aa980","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è uno sciroppo semplice?","Qu'est-ce qu'un sirop simple ?","What is simple syrup?"],"o":[["Zucchero sciolto in acqua","Du sucre dissous dans de l'eau","Sugar dissolved in water"],["Succo di limone zuccherato","Du jus de citron sucré","Sweetened lemon juice"],["Un liquore all'arancia","Une liqueur d'orange","An orange liqueur"],["Vermouth ridotto sul fuoco","Du vermouth réduit sur le feu","Vermouth reduced over heat"]],"e":["Lo sciroppo semplice è solo zucchero e acqua, un dolcificante senza aromi.","Le sirop simple, c'est seulement du sucre et de l'eau, un édulcorant sans arôme.","Simple syrup is just sugar and water, an unflavoured sweetener."],"d":["Sciogliere lo zucchero in acqua permette di mescolarlo facilmente in un cocktail freddo. Il succo di limone è un ingrediente acido, il liquore all'arancia è un dolcificante aromatizzato e alcolico, e il vermouth è un vino aromatizzato: nessuno è «semplice».","Dissoudre le sucre dans l'eau permet de l'incorporer facilement à un cocktail froid. Le jus de citron est un ingrédient acide, la liqueur d'orange un édulcorant aromatisé et alcoolisé, et le vermouth un vin aromatisé : aucun n'est « simple ».","Dissolving sugar in water makes it easy to mix into a cold cocktail. Lemon juice is a sour ingredient, orange liqueur is a flavoured, alcoholic sweetener and vermouth is an aromatised wine: none of them is 'simple'."]},{"id":"s11e4ac34","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Un barman assaggia un cocktail e lo trova stucchevole, troppo dolce. Quale correzione è più adatta?","Un barman goûte un cocktail et le trouve écœurant, trop sucré. Quelle correction est la plus adaptée ?","A bartender tastes a cocktail and finds it cloying and too sweet. Which fix makes most sense?"],"o":[["Aggiungere un po' di succo di agrumi o qualche goccia di bitter","Ajouter un peu de jus d'agrume ou quelques gouttes de bitters","Add a little citrus juice or a dash of bitters"],["Aggiungere un cucchiaio di sciroppo semplice","Ajouter une cuillère de sirop simple","Add a spoonful of simple syrup"],["Sostituire il distillato con un liquore","Remplacer le spiritueux par une liqueur","Swap the spirit for a liqueur"],["Servirlo più caldo, senza ghiaccio","Le servir plus chaud, sans glace","Serve it warmer, without ice"]],"e":["Acidità o amaro bilanciano un eccesso di dolcezza.","L'acidité ou l'amertume équilibrent un excès de sucré.","Sourness or bitterness balances too much sweetness."],"d":["Sulla bilancia dolce contro amaro e acido, per compensare troppo zucchero si aumenta il piatto opposto. Altro sciroppo o un liquore aggiungerebbero ancora dolcezza. Togliere il ghiaccio riduce la diluizione e non risolve il problema del dolce.","Sur la balance sucré contre amer et acide, pour compenser un excès de sucre on renforce l'autre plateau. Davantage de sirop ou une liqueur ajouteraient encore du sucré. Supprimer la glace réduit la dilution et ne règle pas le problème de la douceur.","On the sweet-versus-bitter-and-sour scale, you offset too much sugar by adding weight to the other side. More syrup or a liqueur would add even more sweetness. Removing the ice reduces dilution and does nothing about the sweetness."]},{"id":"s1f40c0c5","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Quale ingrediente può portare da solo dolcezza, amaro e acidità in un cocktail?","Quel ingrédient peut apporter à lui seul douceur, amertume et acidité dans un cocktail ?","Which ingredient can bring sweetness, bitterness and acidity to a cocktail on its own?"],"o":[["Un vino aromatizzato come il vermouth","Un vin aromatisé comme le vermouth","An aromatised wine such as vermouth"],["Lo sciroppo semplice","Le sirop simple","Simple syrup"],["L'acqua gassata","L'eau gazeuse","Club soda"],["Un distillato neutro come la vodka","Un spiritueux neutre comme la vodka","A neutral spirit such as vodka"]],"e":["I vini aromatizzati uniscono dolce, amaro e acido in un solo ingrediente.","Les vins aromatisés réunissent sucré, amer et acide en un seul ingrédient.","Aromatised wines combine sweet, bitter and sour in one ingredient."],"d":["Il vermouth parte da un vino, quindi ha acidità, contiene botaniche amare e quasi sempre zucchero: per questo è così utile nei cocktail. Lo sciroppo dà solo dolcezza, l'acqua gassata solo diluizione e la vodka soprattutto forza alcolica.","Le vermouth part d'un vin, il a donc de l'acidité, il contient des plantes amères et presque toujours du sucre : c'est pour cela qu'il est si utile en cocktail. Le sirop n'apporte que du sucré, l'eau gazeuse que de la dilution et la vodka surtout de la force alcoolique.","Vermouth starts from wine, so it has acidity, it contains bitter botanicals and almost always some sugar: that is why it is so useful in cocktails. Syrup gives only sweetness, club soda only dilution and vodka mainly alcoholic strength."]},{"id":"s14c312d4","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Quali due famiglie di cocktail rientrano tra i drink corti?","Quelles deux familles de cocktails font partie des short drinks ?","Which two cocktail families are short drinks?"],"o":[["Spirit-forward e sour corti","Spirit-forward et sours courts","Spirit-forward and short sours"],["Highball e sour lunghi","Highballs et sours longs","Highballs and long sours"],["Highball e spirit-forward","Highballs et spirit-forward","Highballs and spirit-forward"],["Sour corti e sour lunghi","Sours courts et sours longs","Short sours and long sours"]],"e":["Spirit-forward e sour corti sono i due gruppi di drink corti.","Spirit-forward et sours courts sont les deux groupes de short drinks.","Spirit-forward drinks and short sours are the two short groups."],"d":["I drink corti hanno pochi ingredienti e si diluiscono solo con il ghiaccio: è il caso del Manhattan o del Daiquiri. Highball e sour lunghi sono invece drink lunghi, allungati con bibite o succhi. Le opzioni miste mescolano un gruppo corto e uno lungo.","Les short drinks ont peu d'ingrédients et ne sont dilués que par la glace : c'est le cas du Manhattan ou du Daiquiri. Les highballs et les sours longs sont au contraire des long drinks, allongés de sodas ou de jus. Les options mixtes associent un groupe court et un groupe long.","Short drinks have few ingredients and are diluted only by ice, as with a Manhattan or a Daiquiri. Highballs and long sours are long drinks, lengthened with sodas or juices. The mixed options pair a short group with a long one."]},{"id":"s1b27ca00","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Nei drink lunghi, da dove arriva di solito gran parte della parte «leggera»?","Dans les long drinks, d'où vient en général l'essentiel de la partie « légère » ?","In long drinks, where does most of the 'weak' element usually come from?"],"o":[["Da bibite gassate, succhi o latticini","De sodas, de jus ou de produits laitiers","From sodas, juices or dairy"],["Da un secondo distillato aggiunto alla base","D'un second spiritueux ajouté à la base","From a second spirit added to the base"],["Da qualche goccia di bitter","De quelques gouttes de bitters","From a few dashes of bitters"],["Da un liquore dolce","D'une liqueur sucrée","From a sweet liqueur"]],"e":["Bevande analcoliche come bibite e succhi allungano il drink.","Les boissons sans alcool comme les sodas et les jus allongent la boisson.","Non-alcoholic mixers such as sodas and juices lengthen the drink."],"d":["Ciò che distingue un drink lungo è il volume maggiore, ottenuto con ingredienti analcolici: tonica, acqua gassata, succhi, latte o panna. Un secondo distillato aumenterebbe la forza invece di ridurla, i bitter si usano a gocce e un liquore porta soprattutto dolcezza e alcol.","Ce qui distingue un long drink, c'est son volume plus important, obtenu avec des ingrédients sans alcool : tonic, eau gazeuse, jus, lait ou crème. Un second spiritueux augmenterait la force au lieu de la réduire, les bitters s'utilisent en gouttes et une liqueur apporte surtout du sucre et de l'alcool.","What sets a long drink apart is its bigger volume, achieved with non-alcoholic ingredients: tonic, club soda, juice, milk or cream. A second spirit would raise the strength instead of lowering it, bitters are used by the dash and a liqueur mainly adds sugar and alcohol."]},{"id":"s15c48d0f","c":"t2","p":0,"q":["Un Old Fashioned preparato con il rum al posto del whiskey è un esempio di che cosa?","Un Old Fashioned préparé avec du rhum au lieu du whiskey est un exemple de quoi ?","An Old Fashioned made with rum instead of whiskey is an example of what?"],"o":[["Una variante ottenuta cambiando la parte forte","Une variante obtenue en changeant la partie forte","A variation made by changing the strong element"],["Una variante ottenuta cambiando il modificatore","Une variante obtenue en changeant le modificateur","A variation made by changing the modifier"],["Un modo per trasformarlo in un drink lungo","Une façon de le transformer en long drink","A way of turning it into a long drink"],["Un modo per renderlo un sour corto","Une façon d'en faire un sour court","A way of making it a short sour"]],"e":["Si sostituisce il distillato di base, cioè la parte forte.","On remplace le spiritueux de base, c'est-à-dire la partie forte.","The base spirit, the strong element, is replaced."],"d":["Conoscendo i quattro punti di equilibrio, si può modificare una ricetta in modo mirato. Sostituire il whiskey con il rum lascia invariati zucchero e bitter, cioè dolce e modificatore. Il volume non cambia, quindi non diventa un drink lungo, e senza agrumi non diventa un sour.","Quand on connaît les quatre points d'équilibre, on peut modifier une recette de façon ciblée. Remplacer le whiskey par du rhum laisse inchangés le sucre et les bitters, donc le sucré et le modificateur. Le volume ne change pas, ce n'est donc pas un long drink, et sans agrumes ce n'est pas un sour.","Knowing the four points of balance lets you change a recipe in a targeted way. Swapping whiskey for rum leaves the sugar and bitters, the sweet part and the modifier, unchanged. The volume stays the same, so it does not become a long drink, and with no citrus it is not a sour."]},{"id":"s1aab864d","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Qual è il distillato di base del Negroni?","Quel est le spiritueux de base du Negroni ?","What is the base spirit of a Negroni?"],"o":[["Gin","Gin","Gin"],["Vodka","Vodka","Vodka"],["Rum","Rhum","Rum"],["Bourbon","Bourbon","Bourbon"]],"e":["Il Negroni si costruisce sul gin.","Le Negroni se construit sur le gin.","The Negroni is built on gin."],"d":["Il Negroni unisce gin, vermouth rosso dolce e Campari in un drink spirit-forward. La vodka non ha il carattere botanico del gin, il rum è la base di Daiquiri e Mojito, e il Bourbon compare in drink come l'Old Fashioned o il Whiskey Sour.","Le Negroni associe gin, vermouth rouge doux et Campari dans une boisson spirit-forward. La vodka n'a pas le caractère botanique du gin, le rhum est la base du Daiquiri et du Mojito, et le Bourbon apparaît dans des boissons comme l'Old Fashioned ou le Whiskey Sour.","The Negroni combines gin, sweet red vermouth and Campari in a spirit-forward drink. Vodka lacks gin's botanical character, rum is the base of the Daiquiri and Mojito, and Bourbon appears in drinks such as the Old Fashioned or Whiskey Sour."]},{"id":"s1e485b59","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Nel Negroni, quale ingrediente porta soprattutto la nota amara?","Dans le Negroni, quel ingrédient apporte surtout la note amère ?","In a Negroni, which ingredient mainly provides the bitter note?"],"o":[["Il Campari","Le Campari","Campari"],["Il vermouth rosso dolce","Le vermouth rouge doux","Sweet red vermouth"],["Il gin","Le gin","Gin"],["La zolletta di zucchero","Le morceau de sucre","A sugar cube"]],"e":["Il Campari, un distillato amaro rosso, è l'elemento amaro del Negroni.","Le Campari, un spiritueux amer rouge, est l'élément amer du Negroni.","Campari, a red bitter spirit, is the Negroni's bitter element."],"d":["Ogni ingrediente del Negroni ha un ruolo: il gin è la parte forte, il vermouth rosso dolce porta la dolcezza e il Campari l'amaro. Lo zucchero in zolletta appartiene all'Old Fashioned, non al Negroni.","Chaque ingrédient du Negroni a un rôle : le gin est la partie forte, le vermouth rouge doux apporte la douceur et le Campari l'amertume. Le morceau de sucre appartient à l'Old Fashioned, pas au Negroni.","Each Negroni ingredient has a role: gin is the strong part, sweet red vermouth brings sweetness and Campari the bitterness. The sugar cube belongs to the Old Fashioned, not the Negroni."]},{"id":"s188dd3c6","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Old Fashioned e Manhattan usano entrambi whiskey e bitter Angostura. Che cosa rende diverso il Manhattan?","L'Old Fashioned et le Manhattan utilisent tous deux whiskey et bitters Angostura. Qu'est-ce qui distingue le Manhattan ?","The Old Fashioned and the Manhattan both use whiskey and Angostura bitters. What makes the Manhattan different?"],"o":[["Il vermouth rosso dolce al posto dello zucchero","Le vermouth rouge doux à la place du sucre","Sweet red vermouth instead of sugar"],["Il succo di limone al posto dei bitter","Le jus de citron à la place des bitters","Lemon juice instead of bitters"],["L'acqua gassata che lo rende un drink lungo","L'eau gazeuse qui en fait un long drink","Club soda that makes it a long drink"],["La panna che lo rende morbido","La crème qui l'adoucit","Cream that makes it smooth"]],"e":["Nel Manhattan la dolcezza arriva dal vermouth rosso dolce, più complesso dello zucchero.","Dans le Manhattan, la douceur vient du vermouth rouge doux, plus complexe que le sucre.","In the Manhattan, sweetness comes from sweet red vermouth, which is more complex than sugar."],"d":["I due drink condividono la base di whiskey e i bitter Angostura; il Manhattan sostituisce la zolletta di zucchero con il vermouth, che porta anche sfumature amare e acide. Resta un drink corto spirit-forward: niente agrumi, soda o panna, che appartengono rispettivamente ai sour, ai drink lunghi e agli Alexander.","Les deux boissons partagent la base de whiskey et les bitters Angostura ; le Manhattan remplace le morceau de sucre par le vermouth, qui apporte aussi des nuances amères et acides. Il reste un short drink spirit-forward : ni agrumes, ni eau gazeuse, ni crème, qui appartiennent respectivement aux sours, aux long drinks et aux Alexander.","Both drinks share the whiskey base and Angostura bitters; the Manhattan replaces the sugar cube with vermouth, which also brings bitter and sour nuances. It remains a short spirit-forward drink: no citrus, soda or cream, which belong to sours, long drinks and the Alexander family respectively."]},{"id":"s15495b51","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Quale combinazione porta la nota amara in un Sazerac?","Quelle combinaison apporte la note amère dans un Sazerac ?","Which combination provides the bitter note in a Sazerac?"],"o":[["Bitter Peychaud's e assenzio","Bitters Peychaud's et absinthe","Peychaud's bitters and absinthe"],["Bitter Angostura e vermouth dry","Bitters Angostura et vermouth dry","Angostura bitters and dry vermouth"],["Campari e vermouth rosso dolce","Campari et vermouth rouge doux","Campari and sweet red vermouth"],["Succo di pompelmo e ginger ale","Jus de pamplemousse et ginger ale","Grapefruit juice and ginger ale"]],"e":["Il Sazerac si distingue per i bitter Peychaud's e un tocco di assenzio.","Le Sazerac se distingue par les bitters Peychaud's et une touche d'absinthe.","The Sazerac stands out for Peychaud's bitters and a touch of absinthe."],"d":["Il Sazerac usa Cognac o rye, zucchero e, come elemento amaro, bitter Peychaud's con assenzio. Angostura e vermouth dry compaiono in altri classici (Old Fashioned, Manhattan, Martini), Campari e vermouth dolce sono la coppia di Negroni e Americano, mentre pompelmo e ginger ale sono bibite da highball.","Le Sazerac utilise Cognac ou rye, du sucre et, comme élément amer, des bitters Peychaud's avec de l'absinthe. L'Angostura et le vermouth dry apparaissent dans d'autres classiques (Old Fashioned, Manhattan, Martini), Campari et vermouth doux forment le duo du Negroni et de l'Americano, tandis que pamplemousse et ginger ale sont des boissons de highball.","The Sazerac uses Cognac or rye, sugar and, as its bitter element, Peychaud's bitters with absinthe. Angostura and dry vermouth appear in other classics (Old Fashioned, Manhattan, Martini), Campari and sweet vermouth are the Negroni and Americano pair, and grapefruit and ginger ale are highball mixers."]},{"id":"s14df076c","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Un cliente vuole un drink semplice di Scotch whisky addolcito con un liquore. Quale classico gli si propone?","Un client veut une boisson simple à base de Scotch whisky adoucie par une liqueur. Quel classique lui propose-t-on ?","A customer wants a simple drink of Scotch whisky sweetened with a liqueur. Which classic do you suggest?"],"o":[["Rusty Nail","Rusty Nail","Rusty Nail"],["Sazerac","Sazerac","Sazerac"],["Sidecar","Sidecar","Sidecar"],["Horse's Neck","Horse's Neck","Horse's Neck"]],"e":["Il Rusty Nail è Scotch whisky con Drambuie, un liquore.","Le Rusty Nail, c'est du Scotch whisky avec du Drambuie, une liqueur.","The Rusty Nail is Scotch whisky with Drambuie, a liqueur."],"d":["È l'esempio più semplice di spirit-forward con distillato e liquore. Il Sazerac usa Cognac o rye con zucchero, bitter e assenzio; il Sidecar è un sour di Cognac con limone; l'Horse's Neck è un highball di Cognac con ginger ale.","C'est l'exemple le plus simple de spirit-forward associant spiritueux et liqueur. Le Sazerac utilise Cognac ou rye avec sucre, bitters et absinthe ; le Sidecar est un sour au Cognac avec du citron ; le Horse's Neck est un highball au Cognac avec du ginger ale.","It is the simplest example of a spirit-forward drink made of spirit plus liqueur. The Sazerac uses Cognac or rye with sugar, bitters and absinthe; the Sidecar is a Cognac sour with lemon; the Horse's Neck is a Cognac highball with ginger ale."]},{"id":"s1d0ce45c","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Quali sono gli ingredienti di un Martini classico?","Quels sont les ingrédients d'un Martini classique ?","What are the ingredients of a classic Martini?"],"o":[["Gin e vermouth dry","Gin et vermouth dry","Gin and dry vermouth"],["Gin e vermouth rosso dolce","Gin et vermouth rouge doux","Gin and sweet red vermouth"],["Vodka e succo di limone","Vodka et jus de citron","Vodka and lemon juice"],["Gin, Campari e acqua gassata","Gin, Campari et eau gazeuse","Gin, Campari and club soda"]],"e":["Il Martini unisce gin e vermouth dry.","Le Martini associe gin et vermouth dry.","The Martini pairs gin with dry vermouth."],"d":["Nel Martini il vermouth dry fa due lavori insieme: porta un filo di dolcezza (anche il «dry» contiene un po' di zucchero) e una nota amara. Il vermouth dolce va nel Manhattan e nel Negroni; vodka e limone ricordano un sour, e Campari con soda richiama la famiglia degli highball.","Dans le Martini, le vermouth dry fait deux choses à la fois : il apporte un soupçon de douceur (même le « dry » contient un peu de sucre) et une note amère. Le vermouth doux va dans le Manhattan et le Negroni ; vodka et citron évoquent un sour, et Campari avec eau gazeuse renvoie aux highballs.","In the Martini, dry vermouth does two jobs at once: it brings a hint of sweetness (even 'dry' vermouth has a little sugar) and a bitter note. Sweet vermouth goes into the Manhattan and Negroni; vodka and lemon suggest a sour, and Campari with soda points to the highball family."]},{"id":"s18bca2fb","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Che cosa si ottiene aggiungendo panna a un cocktail spirit-forward?","Qu'obtient-on en ajoutant de la crème à un cocktail spirit-forward ?","What do you get by adding cream to a spirit-forward cocktail?"],"o":[["La famiglia degli Alexander, come il Brandy Alexander","La famille des Alexander, comme le Brandy Alexander","The Alexander family, such as the Brandy Alexander"],["La famiglia dei Collins, come il Tom Collins","La famille des Collins, comme le Tom Collins","The Collins family, such as the Tom Collins"],["La famiglia degli Sling, come il Singapore Sling","La famille des Slings, comme le Singapore Sling","The Sling family, such as the Singapore Sling"],["La famiglia dei sour, come il Pisco Sour","La famille des sours, comme le Pisco Sour","The sour family, such as the Pisco Sour"]],"e":["La panna trasforma il drink in un Alexander.","La crème transforme la boisson en Alexander.","Cream turns the drink into an Alexander."],"d":["Gli Alexander sono una modifica dei drink spirit-forward in cui la panna rende tutto più rotondo e vellutato. Collins e Sling sono sour lunghi allungati con soda, e il Pisco Sour è un sour corto la cui morbidezza viene dall'albume, non dalla panna.","Les Alexander sont une variante des spirit-forward dans laquelle la crème rend l'ensemble plus rond et velouté. Collins et Slings sont des sours longs allongés à l'eau gazeuse, et le Pisco Sour est un sour court dont le moelleux vient du blanc d'œuf, pas de la crème.","Alexanders are a twist on spirit-forward drinks in which cream makes everything rounder and velvety. Collinses and Slings are long sours topped with soda, and the Pisco Sour is a short sour whose smoothness comes from egg white, not cream."]},{"id":"s147b4794","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Come si preparano di solito i cocktail spirit-forward?","Comment prépare-t-on en général les cocktails spirit-forward ?","How are spirit-forward cocktails usually prepared?"],"o":[["Direttamente nel bicchiere o mescolati, con ghiaccio per raffreddare e diluire","Directement dans le verre ou remués, avec de la glace pour refroidir et diluer","Built in the glass or stirred, with ice to chill and dilute"],["Shakerati con albume per creare una schiuma","Secoués avec du blanc d'œuf pour créer une mousse","Shaken with egg white to create a foam"],["Allungati con molta acqua gassata in un bicchiere alto","Allongés de beaucoup d'eau gazeuse dans un verre haut","Topped with plenty of club soda in a tall glass"],["Serviti caldi, senza ghiaccio né diluizione","Servis chauds, sans glace ni dilution","Served warm, with no ice or dilution"]],"e":["Si costruiscono nel bicchiere o si mescolano; il ghiaccio raffredda e diluisce.","On les construit dans le verre ou on les remue ; la glace refroidit et dilue.","They are built or stirred; the ice chills and dilutes."],"d":["Mescolare lascia il drink limpido e compatto, adatto a mettere in risalto il distillato. Lo shaker con albume è tipico dei sour corti, la soda in bicchiere alto dei drink lunghi. Senza ghiaccio mancherebbe proprio la parte leggera che rende bevibile un drink così alcolico.","Remuer laisse la boisson limpide et dense, idéale pour mettre le spiritueux en valeur. Le shaker avec blanc d'œuf est typique des sours courts, l'eau gazeuse en verre haut des long drinks. Sans glace, il manquerait justement la partie légère qui rend buvable une boisson aussi alcoolisée.","Stirring keeps the drink clear and dense, ideal for showcasing the spirit. Shaking with egg white is typical of short sours, and soda in a tall glass of long drinks. Without ice you would lose the very weak element that makes such a strong drink pleasant to sip."]},{"id":"s137474d5","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Quali sono i tre elementi di un sour corto classico?","Quels sont les trois éléments d'un sour court classique ?","What are the three elements of a classic short sour?"],"o":[["Distillato, succo di agrumi, sciroppo semplice","Spiritueux, jus d'agrume, sirop simple","Spirit, citrus juice, simple syrup"],["Distillato, vermouth, bitter","Spiritueux, vermouth, bitters","Spirit, vermouth, bitters"],["Distillato, panna, liquore","Spiritueux, crème, liqueur","Spirit, cream, liqueur"],["Distillato, tonica, ghiaccio","Spiritueux, tonic, glace","Spirit, tonic, ice"]],"e":["Il sour corto bilancia forte, acido e dolce: distillato, agrumi, sciroppo.","Le sour court équilibre fort, acide et sucré : spiritueux, agrume, sirop.","The short sour balances strong, sour and sweet: spirit, citrus, syrup."],"d":["La formula base usa un dolcificante senza aroma, come lo sciroppo semplice, e un agrume come lime o limone. Distillato, vermouth e bitter descrivono uno spirit-forward; con panna e liquore si va verso gli Alexander; con tonica si ottiene un highball.","La formule de base utilise un édulcorant neutre, comme le sirop simple, et un agrume comme le citron vert ou jaune. Spiritueux, vermouth et bitters décrivent un spirit-forward ; avec crème et liqueur on va vers les Alexander ; avec du tonic on obtient un highball.","The basic formula uses an unflavoured sweetener such as simple syrup and a citrus fruit such as lime or lemon. Spirit, vermouth and bitters describe a spirit-forward drink; cream and liqueur lead to the Alexander family; tonic gives a highball."]},{"id":"s1e902238","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Quale ricetta corrisponde al Daiquiri?","Quelle recette correspond au Daiquiri ?","Which recipe is a Daiquiri?"],"o":[["Rum, lime, sciroppo semplice","Rhum, citron vert, sirop simple","Rum, lime, simple syrup"],["Rum, cola, lime","Rhum, cola, citron vert","Rum, cola, lime"],["Tequila, lime, triple sec","Tequila, citron vert, triple sec","Tequila, lime, triple sec"],["Rum, lime, zucchero, menta","Rhum, citron vert, sucre, menthe","Rum, lime, sugar, mint"]],"e":["Il Daiquiri è il sour corto classico a base di rum.","Le Daiquiri est le sour court classique à base de rhum.","The Daiquiri is the classic rum-based short sour."],"d":["Il Daiquiri segue lo schema puro del sour: rum, lime, sciroppo, shakerati. Rum, cola e lime è il Cuba Libre, un highball; tequila, lime e triple sec è la Margarita; con menta e un formato lungo si arriva al Mojito.","Le Daiquiri suit le schéma pur du sour : rhum, citron vert, sirop, secoués. Rhum, cola et citron vert, c'est le Cuba Libre, un highball ; tequila, citron vert et triple sec, c'est la Margarita ; avec de la menthe et un format long, on arrive au Mojito.","The Daiquiri follows the pure sour pattern: rum, lime and syrup, shaken. Rum, cola and lime is the Cuba Libre, a highball; tequila, lime and triple sec is the Margarita; add mint and a long format and you reach the Mojito."]},{"id":"s16ec4624","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["In quale cocktail l'albume è considerato indispensabile?","Dans quel cocktail le blanc d'œuf est-il considéré comme indispensable ?","In which cocktail is egg white considered essential?"],"o":[["Pisco Sour","Pisco Sour","Pisco Sour"],["Daiquiri","Daiquiri","Daiquiri"],["Sidecar","Sidecar","Sidecar"],["Margarita","Margarita","Margarita"]],"e":["Il Pisco Sour richiede sempre un albume.","Le Pisco Sour demande toujours un blanc d'œuf.","The Pisco Sour always calls for an egg white."],"d":["Nel Pisco Sour l'albume crea una testa di schiuma e una consistenza setosa, ed è parte integrante della ricetta. Nel Whiskey Sour è facoltativo e nel Clover Club è previsto, mentre Daiquiri, Sidecar e Margarita si fanno normalmente senza.","Dans le Pisco Sour, le blanc d'œuf crée une tête de mousse et une texture soyeuse ; il fait partie intégrante de la recette. Dans le Whiskey Sour il est facultatif et dans le Clover Club il est prévu, tandis que Daiquiri, Sidecar et Margarita se font normalement sans.","In the Pisco Sour, egg white creates a foam head and a silky texture and is an integral part of the recipe. It is optional in the Whiskey Sour and included in the Clover Club, while the Daiquiri, Sidecar and Margarita are normally made without it."]},{"id":"s1dd767d9","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Quale ricetta corrisponde al Sidecar?","Quelle recette correspond au Sidecar ?","Which recipe is a Sidecar?"],"o":[["Cognac, limone, triple sec","Cognac, citron jaune, triple sec","Cognac, lemon, triple sec"],["Cognac, ginger ale, bitter","Cognac, ginger ale, bitters","Cognac, ginger ale, bitters"],["Cognac, limone, sciroppo, Champagne","Cognac, citron jaune, sirop, Champagne","Cognac, lemon, syrup, Champagne"],["Cognac, zucchero, Peychaud's, assenzio","Cognac, sucre, Peychaud's, absinthe","Cognac, sugar, Peychaud's, absinthe"]],"e":["Il Sidecar è un sour di Cognac addolcito con triple sec.","Le Sidecar est un sour au Cognac adouci au triple sec.","The Sidecar is a Cognac sour sweetened with triple sec."],"d":["Il Sidecar è una variante del sour in cui il triple sec, un liquore all'arancia, prende il posto dello sciroppo. Tutte le opzioni contengono Cognac, ma Cognac, ginger ale e bitter è l'Horse's Neck; con Champagne si ha il French 75; con Peychaud's e assenzio il Sazerac.","Le Sidecar est une variante du sour où le triple sec, une liqueur d'orange, remplace le sirop. Toutes les options contiennent du Cognac, mais Cognac, ginger ale et bitters, c'est le Horse's Neck ; avec du Champagne, le French 75 ; avec Peychaud's et absinthe, le Sazerac.","The Sidecar is a sour variation in which triple sec, an orange liqueur, takes the place of syrup. Every option contains Cognac, but Cognac, ginger ale and bitters is the Horse's Neck; with Champagne it is the French 75; with Peychaud's and absinthe, the Sazerac."]},{"id":"s1a4719c8","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Nella Margarita, quale ingrediente porta la dolcezza?","Dans la Margarita, quel ingrédient apporte la douceur ?","In a Margarita, which ingredient provides the sweetness?"],"o":[["Il triple sec","Le triple sec","Triple sec"],["Il sale sul bordo","Le sel sur le bord","The salt rim"],["Il succo di lime","Le jus de citron vert","Lime juice"],["La soda al pompelmo","Le soda au pamplemousse","Grapefruit soda"]],"e":["Il triple sec, liquore all'arancia, è il dolcificante della Margarita.","Le triple sec, liqueur d'orange, est l'édulcorant de la Margarita.","Triple sec, an orange liqueur, is the Margarita's sweetener."],"d":["La Margarita è tequila, lime e triple sec: il lime è la parte acida, non quella dolce. Il bordo di sale è facoltativo e serve a esaltare i sapori. La soda al pompelmo appartiene alla Paloma, un altro drink a base di tequila ma lungo.","La Margarita, c'est tequila, citron vert et triple sec : le citron vert est la partie acide, pas la partie sucrée. Le bord de sel est facultatif et sert à relever les saveurs. Le soda au pamplemousse appartient à la Paloma, une autre boisson à la tequila, mais longue.","The Margarita is tequila, lime and triple sec: the lime is the sour part, not the sweet one. The salt rim is optional and lifts the flavours. Grapefruit soda belongs to the Paloma, another tequila drink, but a long one."]},{"id":"s14062a2e","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Quale sour corto usa gin, limone e sciroppo di lampone?","Quel sour court utilise gin, citron jaune et sirop de framboise ?","Which short sour uses gin, lemon and raspberry syrup?"],"o":[["Clover Club","Clover Club","Clover Club"],["Tom Collins","Tom Collins","Tom Collins"],["Singapore Sling","Singapore Sling","Singapore Sling"],["French 75","French 75","French 75"]],"e":["Il Clover Club è la variante al gin con sciroppo di lampone.","Le Clover Club est la variante au gin avec sirop de framboise.","The Clover Club is the gin variation with raspberry syrup."],"d":["Il Clover Club è un sour corto con un dolcificante aromatizzato, più albume e, a scelta, un po' di vermouth. Gli altri tre contengono gin ma sono sour lunghi: il Tom Collins con sciroppo semplice e soda, il Singapore Sling con liquori e soda, il French 75 con Champagne.","Le Clover Club est un sour court avec un édulcorant aromatisé, plus du blanc d'œuf et, au choix, un peu de vermouth. Les trois autres contiennent du gin mais sont des sours longs : le Tom Collins avec sirop simple et eau gazeuse, le Singapore Sling avec liqueurs et eau gazeuse, le French 75 avec du Champagne.","The Clover Club is a short sour with a flavoured sweetener, plus egg white and optionally a little vermouth. The other three contain gin but are long sours: the Tom Collins with simple syrup and soda, the Singapore Sling with liqueurs and soda, and the French 75 with Champagne."]},{"id":"s1537c36f","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Whiskey Sour e Pisco Sour sono entrambi sour classici. In che cosa differiscono gli agrumi usati?","Le Whiskey Sour et le Pisco Sour sont deux sours classiques. En quoi diffèrent les agrumes utilisés ?","The Whiskey Sour and the Pisco Sour are both classic sours. How do their citrus juices differ?"],"o":[["Il Whiskey Sour usa limone, il Pisco Sour lime","Le Whiskey Sour utilise du citron jaune, le Pisco Sour du citron vert","The Whiskey Sour uses lemon, the Pisco Sour lime"],["Il Whiskey Sour usa lime, il Pisco Sour limone","Le Whiskey Sour utilise du citron vert, le Pisco Sour du citron jaune","The Whiskey Sour uses lime, the Pisco Sour lemon"],["Entrambi usano succo di pompelmo","Les deux utilisent du jus de pamplemousse","Both use grapefruit juice"],["Entrambi usano succo d'arancia","Les deux utilisent du jus d'orange","Both use orange juice"]],"e":["Limone per il Whiskey Sour, lime per il Pisco Sour.","Citron jaune pour le Whiskey Sour, citron vert pour le Pisco Sour.","Lemon for the Whiskey Sour, lime for the Pisco Sour."],"d":["Tra i tre sour classici, solo il Whiskey Sour usa il limone; Pisco Sour e Daiquiri usano il lime. Un trucco per ricordarlo: il whiskey, come il Cognac del Sidecar, va con il limone. Il pompelmo compare in Greyhound e Paloma, non in questi sour.","Parmi les trois sours classiques, seul le Whiskey Sour utilise le citron jaune ; le Pisco Sour et le Daiquiri utilisent le citron vert. Une astuce : le whiskey, comme le Cognac du Sidecar, va avec le citron jaune. Le pamplemousse apparaît dans le Greyhound et la Paloma, pas dans ces sours.","Of the three classic sours, only the Whiskey Sour uses lemon; the Pisco Sour and Daiquiri use lime. A memory tip: whiskey, like the Cognac in a Sidecar, goes with lemon. Grapefruit appears in the Greyhound and the Paloma, not in these sours."]},{"id":"s11daee12","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è un Greyhound?","Qu'est-ce qu'un Greyhound ?","What is a Greyhound?"],"o":[["Vodka e succo di pompelmo","Vodka et jus de pamplemousse","Vodka and grapefruit juice"],["Rum e cola con lime","Rhum et cola avec citron vert","Rum and cola with lime"],["Gin e acqua tonica","Gin et tonic","Gin and tonic water"],["Tequila e soda al pompelmo","Tequila et soda au pamplemousse","Tequila and grapefruit soda"]],"e":["Il Greyhound è un highball di vodka e succo di pompelmo.","Le Greyhound est un highball de vodka et jus de pamplemousse.","The Greyhound is a highball of vodka and grapefruit juice."],"d":["È uno degli highball con un nome proprio, semplice come tutti quelli della famiglia. Rum, cola e lime è il Cuba Libre; gin e tonica non ha un nome speciale; tequila e soda al pompelmo con lime è la Paloma, che però è un sour lungo.","C'est l'un des highballs qui portent un nom, simple comme tous ceux de la famille. Rhum, cola et citron vert, c'est le Cuba Libre ; le gin tonic n'a pas de nom particulier ; tequila et soda au pamplemousse avec citron vert, c'est la Paloma, qui est pourtant un sour long.","It is one of the highballs with its own name, as simple as the rest of the family. Rum, cola and lime is the Cuba Libre; gin and tonic has no special name; tequila and grapefruit soda with lime is the Paloma, which is a long sour."]},{"id":"s1553a687","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Un cliente chiede un highball a base di Cognac con ginger ale e qualche goccia di bitter. Che cosa si prepara?","Un client demande un highball au Cognac avec du ginger ale et quelques gouttes de bitters. Que prépare-t-on ?","A customer asks for a Cognac highball with ginger ale and a few dashes of bitters. What do you make?"],"o":[["Un Horse's Neck","Un Horse's Neck","A Horse's Neck"],["Un Sidecar","Un Sidecar","A Sidecar"],["Un French 75","Un French 75","A French 75"],["Un Americano","Un Americano","An Americano"]],"e":["L'Horse's Neck è Cognac, ginger ale e bitter.","Le Horse's Neck, c'est Cognac, ginger ale et bitters.","The Horse's Neck is Cognac, ginger ale and bitters."],"d":["È un esempio di highball che aggiunge i bitter a distillato e bibita. Sidecar e French 75 contengono Cognac ma sono sour, con limone; l'Americano è un highball senza Cognac, con Campari, vermouth dolce e soda.","C'est un exemple de highball qui ajoute des bitters au spiritueux et au soda. Le Sidecar et le French 75 contiennent du Cognac mais sont des sours, avec du citron ; l'Americano est un highball sans Cognac, avec Campari, vermouth doux et eau gazeuse.","It is an example of a highball that adds bitters to the spirit and mixer. The Sidecar and French 75 contain Cognac but are sours, with lemon; the Americano is a highball with no Cognac, made with Campari, sweet vermouth and soda."]},{"id":"s15ae55ac","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Perché si dice che l'Americano ha una «base divisa»?","Pourquoi dit-on que l'Americano a une « base partagée » ?","Why is the Americano said to have a 'split base'?"],"o":[["La parte alcolica è formata da Campari e vermouth dolce insieme","La partie alcoolisée est formée de Campari et de vermouth doux réunis","Its alcoholic part is Campari and sweet vermouth together"],["Si serve metà in un bicchiere corto e metà in uno lungo","On le sert moitié en verre court, moitié en verre haut","It is served half in a short glass and half in a tall one"],["Usa due tipi di gin diversi","Il utilise deux gins différents","It uses two different gins"],["Mescola succo di limone e succo di lime","Il mélange jus de citron jaune et jus de citron vert","It mixes lemon juice and lime juice"]],"e":["Campari e vermouth rosso dolce condividono il ruolo di parte forte.","Le Campari et le vermouth rouge doux se partagent le rôle de partie forte.","Campari and sweet red vermouth share the role of the strong element."],"d":["Invece di un solo distillato, l'Americano usa due ingredienti alcolici che insieme fanno da base, poi allungati con acqua gassata. Non contiene gin né agrumi: è come un Negroni senza gin e reso lungo con la soda.","Au lieu d'un seul spiritueux, l'Americano utilise deux ingrédients alcoolisés qui forment ensemble la base, puis allongés d'eau gazeuse. Il ne contient ni gin ni agrumes : c'est comme un Negroni sans gin rallongé à l'eau gazeuse.","Instead of a single spirit, the Americano uses two alcoholic ingredients that together form the base, then lengthened with club soda. It contains no gin and no citrus: think of a Negroni without the gin, made long with soda."]},{"id":"s1fe76854","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Come si trasforma un sour corto in un Tom Collins?","Comment transforme-t-on un sour court en Tom Collins ?","How is a short sour turned into a Tom Collins?"],"o":[["Usando gin e allungando con acqua gassata","En utilisant du gin et en allongeant à l'eau gazeuse","By using gin and topping with club soda"],["Usando rum e aggiungendo foglie di menta","En utilisant du rhum et en ajoutant de la menthe","By using rum and adding mint leaves"],["Usando Cognac e completando con Champagne","En utilisant du Cognac et en complétant au Champagne","By using Cognac and topping with Champagne"],["Usando tequila e soda al pompelmo","En utilisant de la tequila et du soda au pamplemousse","By using tequila and grapefruit soda"]],"e":["Il Tom Collins è un sour di gin allungato con acqua gassata.","Le Tom Collins est un sour au gin allongé à l'eau gazeuse.","The Tom Collins is a gin sour lengthened with club soda."],"d":["Gin, limone e sciroppo semplice formano un sour; aggiungendo soda su ghiaccio diventa un Collins, il sour lungo più semplice. Rum e menta portano al Mojito, Cognac e Champagne al French 75, tequila e soda al pompelmo alla Paloma.","Gin, citron jaune et sirop simple forment un sour ; en ajoutant de l'eau gazeuse sur glace, il devient un Collins, le sour long le plus simple. Rhum et menthe mènent au Mojito, Cognac et Champagne au French 75, tequila et soda au pamplemousse à la Paloma.","Gin, lemon and simple syrup make a sour; topped with soda over ice it becomes a Collins, the simplest long sour. Rum and mint lead to the Mojito, Cognac and Champagne to the French 75, and tequila with grapefruit soda to the Paloma."]},{"id":"s1c250a2e","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Con che cosa si completa un French 75?","Avec quoi complète-t-on un French 75 ?","What is a French 75 topped with?"],"o":[["Champagne","Champagne","Champagne"],["Acqua tonica","Tonic","Tonic water"],["Ginger ale","Ginger ale","Ginger ale"],["Cola","Cola","Cola"]],"e":["Il French 75 è un sour frizzante completato con Champagne.","Le French 75 est un sour pétillant complété au Champagne.","The French 75 is a sparkling sour topped with Champagne."],"d":["La base è Cognac o gin, limone e sciroppo semplice; lo Champagne sostituisce la soda e lo rende un sour frizzante. La tonica è tipica di highball come il gin tonic, il ginger ale dell'Horse's Neck e la cola del Cuba Libre.","La base est un Cognac ou un gin, du citron jaune et du sirop simple ; le Champagne remplace l'eau gazeuse et en fait un sour pétillant. Le tonic est typique de highballs comme le gin tonic, le ginger ale du Horse's Neck et le cola du Cuba Libre.","The base is Cognac or gin, lemon and simple syrup; Champagne replaces the soda and makes it a sparkling sour. Tonic is typical of highballs such as the gin and tonic, ginger ale of the Horse's Neck and cola of the Cuba Libre."]},{"id":"s17be08de","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Nella Paloma, che cosa porta insieme dolcezza e bollicine?","Dans la Paloma, qu'est-ce qui apporte à la fois douceur et bulles ?","In a Paloma, what provides both sweetness and bubbles?"],"o":[["Una soda al pompelmo di tipo messicano","Un soda au pamplemousse de type mexicain","A Mexican-style grapefruit soda"],["Il triple sec","Le triple sec","Triple sec"],["Lo Champagne","Le Champagne","Champagne"],["Il ginger ale","Le ginger ale","Ginger ale"]],"e":["La soda al pompelmo addolcisce e allunga la Paloma.","Le soda au pamplemousse adoucit et allonge la Paloma.","Grapefruit soda both sweetens and lengthens the Paloma."],"d":["La Paloma è tequila e lime completati con soda al pompelmo; in alternativa si possono usare succo di pompelmo e acqua gassata. Il triple sec è il dolcificante della Margarita, lo Champagne completa il French 75 e il ginger ale va nell'Horse's Neck.","La Paloma, c'est tequila et citron vert complétés de soda au pamplemousse ; on peut aussi utiliser jus de pamplemousse et eau gazeuse. Le triple sec est l'édulcorant de la Margarita, le Champagne complète le French 75 et le ginger ale va dans le Horse's Neck.","The Paloma is tequila and lime topped with grapefruit soda; alternatively, grapefruit juice and soda water can be used. Triple sec sweetens the Margarita, Champagne tops the French 75 and ginger ale goes into the Horse's Neck."]},{"id":"s1dc08db9","c":"t3","p":0,"q":["Quale ingrediente extra caratterizza il Mojito rispetto a un semplice sour di rum?","Quel ingrédient supplémentaire caractérise le Mojito par rapport à un simple sour au rhum ?","Which extra ingredient sets the Mojito apart from a plain rum sour?"],"o":[["Le foglie di menta","Les feuilles de menthe","Mint leaves"],["L'albume","Le blanc d'œuf","Egg white"],["Il bordo di sale","Le bord de sel","A salt rim"],["La panna","La crème","Cream"]],"e":["La menta, con il lime, rende il Mojito fresco e profumato.","La menthe, avec le citron vert, rend le Mojito frais et parfumé.","Mint, with the lime, makes the Mojito fresh and fragrant."],"d":["Il Mojito è rum, lime e zucchero o sciroppo, arricchito con menta: un sour lungo con un ingrediente extra semplice. L'albume è tipico del Pisco Sour, il sale della Margarita e la panna degli Alexander.","Le Mojito, c'est rhum, citron vert et sucre ou sirop, enrichi de menthe : un sour long avec un ingrédient supplémentaire simple. Le blanc d'œuf est typique du Pisco Sour, le sel de la Margarita et la crème des Alexander.","The Mojito is rum, lime and sugar or syrup, enriched with mint: a long sour with one simple extra ingredient. Egg white is typical of the Pisco Sour, salt of the Margarita and cream of the Alexander family."]}],"lessons":[{"c":"p1","t":["Quattro tappe per ogni distillato","Quatre étapes pour chaque spiritueux","Four steps behind every spirit"],"p":[["Un distillato, detto nel modo più semplice, è una bevanda alcolica che la distillazione ha reso più forte. Ma la distillazione non lavora da sola: dietro ogni bottiglia, che sia una vodka o un cognac, ci sono sempre quattro tappe. Si prepara la materia prima, la si fa fermentare, si distilla e infine si decide che cosa fare del distillato appena uscito dall'alambicco. Conoscere queste quattro tappe permette di capire quasi ogni distillato.","Un spiritueux, dit le plus simplement possible, est une boisson alcoolisée rendue plus forte par la distillation. Mais la distillation ne travaille pas seule : derrière chaque bouteille, vodka ou cognac, on retrouve toujours quatre étapes. On prépare la matière première, on la fait fermenter, on distille, puis on décide quoi faire de l'eau-de-vie qui sort de l'alambic. Connaître ces quatre étapes permet de comprendre presque tous les spiritueux.","Put as simply as possible, a spirit is an alcoholic drink that distillation has made stronger. But distillation never works alone: behind every bottle, whether vodka or Cognac, there are always four steps. The raw material is prepared, it is fermented, it is distilled, and finally the producer decides what to do with the spirit fresh from the still. Knowing these four steps unlocks almost every spirit on the shelf."],["La prima tappa ha un solo obiettivo: ottenere un liquido zuccherino, perché senza zucchero non c'è fermentazione. La materia prima deve essere di origine vegetale. Alcune piante, come la canna da zucchero o l'uva, contengono già zucchero facile da estrarre. Altre, come i cereali, non ne contengono affatto e vanno lavorate per crearlo. In ogni caso la pianta di partenza lascia la sua firma: ogni materia prima regala al distillato aromi propri.","La première étape n'a qu'un but : obtenir un liquide sucré, car sans sucre il n'y a pas de fermentation. La matière première doit être d'origine végétale. Certaines plantes, comme la canne à sucre ou le raisin, contiennent déjà un sucre facile à extraire. D'autres, comme les céréales, n'en contiennent pas et doivent être transformées pour en créer. Dans tous les cas, la plante de départ laisse sa signature : chaque matière première donne au spiritueux ses propres arômes.","The first step has a single goal: to obtain a sugary liquid, because without sugar there is no fermentation. The raw material must come from a plant. Some plants, such as sugar cane or grapes, already hold sugar that is easy to extract. Others, such as cereals, contain none and must be processed to create it. Either way, the starting plant leaves its signature: every raw material gives the spirit its own set of aromas."],["Dopo la fermentazione e la distillazione arriva la quarta tappa, spesso dimenticata ma decisiva. Il distillato appena nato è incolore e secco, quindi il produttore può lasciarlo così, metterlo in botti di rovere, aggiungere aromi, zucchero o colore, e infine diluirlo con acqua. Un'immagine utile: le prime tre tappe costruiscono la casa, la quarta la arreda. Due distillati nati uguali possono uscire molto diversi da questa fase.","Après la fermentation et la distillation vient la quatrième étape, souvent oubliée mais décisive. L'eau-de-vie qui vient de naître est incolore et sèche ; le producteur peut la laisser ainsi, la mettre en fût de chêne, ajouter des arômes, du sucre ou de la couleur, puis la diluer avec de l'eau. Une image utile : les trois premières étapes construisent la maison, la quatrième la meuble. Deux eaux-de-vie identiques au départ peuvent en sortir très différentes.","After fermentation and distillation comes the fourth step, often overlooked but decisive. A newly made spirit is colourless and dry, so the producer can leave it that way, put it into oak barrels, add flavours, sugar or colour, and finally dilute it with water. A handy image: the first three steps build the house, the fourth furnishes it. Two spirits that start out identical can leave this stage tasting very different."]],"k":[["Distillato = bevanda alcolica resa più forte dalla distillazione.","Spiritueux = boisson alcoolisée rendue plus forte par la distillation.","Spirit = an alcoholic drink made stronger by distillation."],["Quattro tappe: materia prima, fermentazione, distillazione, fase dopo la distillazione.","Quatre étapes : matière première, fermentation, distillation, étape après la distillation.","Four steps: raw material, fermentation, distillation, post-distillation."],["La materia prima è sempre vegetale e serve a ottenere un liquido zuccherino.","La matière première est toujours végétale et sert à obtenir un liquide sucré.","The raw material is always a plant and is used to make a sugary liquid."],["Ogni materia prima porta i propri aromi.","Chaque matière première apporte ses propres arômes.","Each raw material brings its own aromas."]]},{"c":"p1","t":["La fermentazione crea l'alcol, la distillazione lo concentra","La fermentation crée l'alcool, la distillation le concentre","Fermentation makes alcohol, distillation concentrates it"],"p":[["I lieviti sono minuscoli organismi viventi che si aggiungono al liquido zuccherino. Si nutrono dello zucchero e lasciano dietro di sé due prodotti: l'etanolo, cioè l'alcol che interessa al distillatore, e l'anidride carbonica, un gas di scarto. Alla fine il liquido fermentato contiene di solito tra l'8% e il 10% di alcol in volume, più o meno come una birra robusta. I lieviti creano anche nuovi aromi, soprattutto fruttati.","Les levures sont de minuscules organismes vivants que l'on ajoute au liquide sucré. Elles se nourrissent du sucre et laissent derrière elles deux produits : l'éthanol, l'alcool qui intéresse le distillateur, et le dioxyde de carbone, un gaz qui part en déchet. À la fin, le liquide fermenté titre en général entre 8 % et 10 % vol., à peu près comme une bière costaude. Les levures créent aussi de nouveaux arômes, surtout fruités.","Yeasts are tiny living organisms added to the sugary liquid. They feed on the sugar and leave two things behind: ethanol, the alcohol the distiller wants, and carbon dioxide, a waste gas. At the end, the fermented liquid usually sits between 8% and 10% abv, roughly the strength of a strong beer. Yeasts also create new aromas, especially fruity ones, so fermentation adds flavour as well as alcohol."],["La distillazione sfrutta un fatto semplice: l'etanolo bolle a una temperatura più bassa dell'acqua. Se si scalda il liquido fermentato fino a farlo bollire, i vapori che si alzano sono più ricchi di alcol del liquido rimasto sotto. Raccolti e raffreddati, questi vapori ritornano liquidi e formano un nuovo liquido più forte. È questa la tappa in cui nasce davvero un distillato.","La distillation profite d'un fait simple : l'éthanol bout à une température plus basse que l'eau. Quand on chauffe le liquide fermenté jusqu'à ébullition, les vapeurs qui montent sont plus riches en alcool que le liquide resté en bas. Recueillies et refroidies, ces vapeurs redeviennent liquides et donnent un nouveau liquide plus fort. C'est à cette étape que naît vraiment un spiritueux.","Distillation relies on one simple fact: ethanol boils at a lower temperature than water. When the fermented liquid is heated to boiling, the vapours rising from it are richer in alcohol than the liquid left behind. Collected and cooled, those vapours turn back into a liquid that is stronger than the one we started with. This is the step where a spirit is truly born."],["Il grado a cui si distilla conta molto. Un distillato appena fatto può andare da circa il 60% fino al 96% di alcol. Più il grado è basso, più gli aromi sono intensi; più il grado è alto, meno aroma resta. A 96% il distillato ha così poco profumo da essere chiamato neutro. Si può immaginare una radio: alzando il volume dell'alcol, la musica degli aromi si sente sempre meno.","Le degré auquel on distille compte beaucoup. Une eau-de-vie qui vient d'être distillée peut aller d'environ 60 % à 96 % vol. Plus le degré est bas, plus les arômes sont intenses ; plus il est haut, moins il reste d'arômes. À 96 %, l'eau-de-vie a si peu d'odeur qu'on la dit neutre. On peut imaginer une radio : plus on monte le volume de l'alcool, moins on entend la musique des arômes.","The strength reached during distillation matters a lot. A newly made spirit can range from about 60% up to 96% abv. The lower the strength, the more intense the aromas; the higher the strength, the less aroma survives. At 96% abv a spirit has so little smell that it is called neutral. Picture a radio: the louder the alcohol, the fainter the music of the aromas."]],"k":[["Lieviti + zucchero → etanolo + anidride carbonica.","Levures + sucre → éthanol + dioxyde de carbone.","Yeast + sugar → ethanol + carbon dioxide."],["Il liquido fermentato ha di solito l'8–10% vol.; i lieviti aggiungono aromi fruttati.","Le liquide fermenté titre en général 8–10 % vol. ; les levures ajoutent des arômes fruités.","Fermented liquid is usually 8–10% abv; yeast adds fruity aromas."],["La distillazione concentra l'etanolo perché bolle prima dell'acqua.","La distillation concentre l'éthanol parce qu'il bout avant l'eau.","Distillation concentrates ethanol because it boils before water."],["Grado basso = più aroma; grado alto = meno aroma; 96% = neutro.","Degré bas = plus d'arômes ; degré élevé = moins d'arômes ; 96 % = neutre.","Low strength = more aroma; high strength = less aroma; 96% = neutral."]]},{"c":"p1","t":["L'alambicco discontinuo","L'alambic à repasse","The pot still"],"p":[["Qualunque sia la sua forma, un alambicco discontinuo ha sempre tre elementi: una caldaia scaldata da una fonte di calore, un condensatore raffreddato e un tubo che li collega. Il liquido bolle nella caldaia, i vapori salgono nel collo dell'alambicco e passano nel condensatore, dove una serpentina immersa in acqua fredda li riporta allo stato liquido. Molti alambicchi moderni si scaldano con il vapore; quelli del Cognac usano ancora bruciatori a gas.","Quelle que soit sa forme, un alambic à repasse comporte toujours trois éléments : une chaudière posée sur une source de chaleur, un condenseur refroidi et un tuyau qui les relie. Le liquide bout dans la chaudière, les vapeurs montent dans le chapiteau puis passent dans le condenseur, où un serpentin plongé dans l'eau froide les refait passer à l'état liquide. Beaucoup d'alambics modernes sont chauffés à la vapeur ; ceux du Cognac utilisent encore des brûleurs à gaz.","Whatever its shape, a pot still always has three parts: a pot sitting on a heat source, a cooled condenser and a pipe linking the two. The liquid boils in the pot, the vapours climb the still head and pass into the condenser, where a coiled tube bathed in cold water turns them back into liquid. Many modern pot stills are heated with steam; those used for Cognac still rely on gas burners."],["L'alambicco discontinuo lavora a lotti, come una lavatrice: si carica, si fa girare il programma, si svuota e si pulisce prima del giro successivo. Non può funzionare senza sosta. Inoltre, con un solo passaggio non si ottiene un distillato a partire dal liquido fermentato. Per questo quasi tutti distillano due volte: da circa il 10% si arriva a circa il 25%, poi a circa il 75%. È la doppia distillazione.","L'alambic à repasse travaille par lots, comme une machine à laver : on le remplit, on lance le cycle, on le vide et on le nettoie avant le suivant. Il ne peut pas fonctionner sans arrêt. De plus, un seul passage ne suffit pas pour obtenir un spiritueux à partir du liquide fermenté. C'est pourquoi presque tous distillent deux fois : d'environ 10 % on passe à environ 25 %, puis à environ 75 %. C'est la double distillation.","A pot still works in batches, much like a washing machine: load it, run the cycle, empty it and clean it before the next round. It cannot run non-stop. What is more, a single pass cannot turn the fermented liquid into a spirit. That is why most distillers run it twice: from about 10% abv to about 25%, then to about 75%. This is known as double pot still distillation."],["Il risultato è un distillato di grado relativamente basso, con un'intensità aromatica da media a pronunciata e tanto carattere e complessità. Ecco perché questo alambicco si usa quando si vuole un distillato ricco di gusto. Il prezzo da pagare è il lavoro: ogni lotto richiede tempo e attenzione, e per quante volte si ridistilli, l'alambicco discontinuo non arriverà mai a un distillato neutro ad altissimo grado.","Le résultat est une eau-de-vie de degré relativement bas, avec une intensité aromatique moyenne à prononcée, beaucoup de caractère et de complexité. Voilà pourquoi on choisit cet alambic quand on veut un spiritueux riche en goût. Le revers, c'est le travail : chaque lot demande du temps et de l'attention, et même en redistillant encore et encore, l'alambic à repasse n'atteindra jamais une eau-de-vie neutre à très haut degré.","The result is a spirit of relatively low strength, with medium to pronounced aroma intensity and plenty of character and complexity. That is why this still is chosen whenever a flavour-packed spirit is the goal. The price is labour: each batch takes time and care, and no matter how many times the spirit is redistilled, a pot still will never reach a very high-strength neutral spirit."]],"k":[["Tre parti: caldaia con fonte di calore, condensatore, tubo di collegamento.","Trois parties : chaudière avec source de chaleur, condenseur, tuyau de liaison.","Three parts: pot with heat source, condenser, linking pipe."],["Lavora a lotti: si svuota e si pulisce dopo ogni distillazione.","Il travaille par lots : on le vide et on le nettoie après chaque distillation.","Batch process: emptied and cleaned after every distillation."],["Di solito due distillazioni: ~10% → ~25% → ~75% vol.","En général deux distillations : ~10 % → ~25 % → ~75 % vol.","Usually two distillations: ~10% → ~25% → ~75% abv."],["Grado basso, aromi da medi a pronunciati, molto carattere; mai neutro.","Degré bas, arômes moyens à prononcés, beaucoup de caractère ; jamais neutre.","Low strength, medium to pronounced aromas, lots of character; never neutral."]]},{"c":"p1","t":["L'alambicco a colonna","La colonne à distiller","The column still"],"p":[["Con il tempo si è voluto un alambicco capace di lavorare senza fermarsi e di arrivare a gradi molto alti, cosa impossibile per l'alambicco discontinuo. La risposta è stata la colonna: una struttura verticale divisa in tanti piani. Il vapore caldo entra dal basso e sale, il liquido scende. È come avere tante distillazioni impilate una sull'altra, che avvengono tutte nello stesso momento.","Avec le temps, on a voulu un alambic capable de travailler sans s'arrêter et d'atteindre des degrés très élevés, ce que l'alambic à repasse ne peut pas faire. La réponse a été la colonne : une structure verticale divisée en nombreux plateaux. La vapeur chaude entre par le bas et monte, le liquide descend. C'est comme si l'on empilait de nombreuses distillations les unes sur les autres, toutes en même temps.","Over time, distillers wanted a still that could run without stopping and reach very high strengths, which the pot still cannot do. The answer was the column: a vertical structure divided into many sections. Hot vapour enters at the bottom and rises, while liquid runs down. It is like stacking many distillations on top of one another, all happening at the same time."],["Più il vapore sale nella colonna, più il suo grado alcolico aumenta: il piano più basso contiene il liquido meno alcolico, quello più alto il più alcolico, ed è da lì che esce il distillato. Poiché le distillazioni avvengono contemporaneamente e la colonna non va svuotata, il lavoro è continuo e veloce. Si può pensare a una scala mobile che non si ferma mai, contro l'ascensore a corse dell'alambicco discontinuo.","Plus la vapeur monte dans la colonne, plus son degré augmente : le plateau du bas contient le liquide le moins alcoolisé, celui du haut le plus alcoolisé, et c'est de là que sort l'eau-de-vie. Comme les distillations ont lieu en même temps et qu'il n'y a pas à vider la colonne, le travail est continu et rapide. On peut penser à un escalator qui ne s'arrête jamais, face à l'ascenseur à trajets de l'alambic à repasse.","The higher the vapour climbs in the column, the higher its alcohol level: the bottom section holds the weakest liquid, the top section the strongest, and that is where the spirit leaves the still. Because the distillations happen simultaneously and the column never needs emptying, production is continuous and fast. Think of an escalator that never stops, compared with the stop-start lift of the pot still."],["Non tutte le colonne sono uguali. Una colonna corta, con pochi piani, dà un distillato di grado più basso, con aromi medi o pronunciati, simile a quello di un alambicco discontinuo. Una colonna alta, con molti piani, raggiunge gradi elevati e dà un distillato leggero. Le colonne più alte in assoluto arrivano al 95% o al 96%: ne esce un distillato neutro, quasi senza profumo, la base di molte vodka.","Toutes les colonnes ne se ressemblent pas. Une colonne courte, avec peu de plateaux, donne une eau-de-vie de degré plus bas, aux arômes moyens ou prononcés, proche de celle d'un alambic à repasse. Une colonne haute, avec beaucoup de plateaux, atteint des degrés élevés et donne une eau-de-vie légère. Les plus hautes de toutes montent à 95 % ou 96 % vol. : on obtient un alcool neutre, presque sans odeur, base de nombreuses vodkas.","Not all columns are alike. A short column with few sections gives a lower-strength spirit with medium or pronounced aromas, close to a pot still spirit. A tall column with many sections reaches high strengths and gives a light spirit. The very tallest reach 95% or 96% abv, producing a neutral spirit with almost no smell, the base of most vodkas."]],"k":[["La colonna lavora in continuo: tante distillazioni impilate e simultanee.","La colonne fonctionne en continu : des distillations empilées et simultanées.","A column still runs continuously: many stacked, simultaneous distillations."],["Il grado più alto si trova in cima alla colonna.","Le degré le plus élevé se trouve en haut de la colonne.","The highest strength is at the top of the column."],["Colonna corta = distillato aromatico, simile all'alambicco discontinuo.","Colonne courte = eau-de-vie aromatique, proche de l'alambic à repasse.","Short column = flavourful spirit, similar to a pot still."],["Colonna alta = distillato leggero; la più alta = neutro al 95–96%.","Colonne haute = eau-de-vie légère ; la plus haute = neutre à 95–96 %.","Tall column = light spirit; tallest = neutral at 95–96%."]]},{"c":"p2","t":["Da dove viene il gusto","D'où vient le goût","Where flavour comes from"],"p":[["Il gusto di un distillato si costruisce passo dopo passo. La materia prima dà la base: l'uva porta note fruttate e floreali, l'agave note erbacee e pepate. La fermentazione aggiunge altri aromi, soprattutto fruttati. Poi la distillazione decide quanto di tutto questo resterà: a grado basso gli aromi rimangono intensi, a grado altissimo quasi spariscono. Ogni tappa è come un filtro che lascia passare più o meno carattere.","Le goût d'un spiritueux se construit pas à pas. La matière première pose la base : le raisin apporte des notes fruitées et florales, l'agave des notes herbacées et poivrées. La fermentation ajoute d'autres arômes, surtout fruités. Puis la distillation décide de ce qui en restera : à bas degré les arômes restent intenses, à très haut degré ils disparaissent presque. Chaque étape agit comme un filtre qui laisse passer plus ou moins de caractère.","A spirit's flavour is built step by step. The raw material lays the foundation: grapes bring fruity and floral notes, agave brings herbal and peppery ones. Fermentation adds further aromas, mostly fruity. Then distillation decides how much of all this survives: at a low strength the aromas stay intense, at a very high strength they almost vanish. Each step works like a filter letting more or less character through."],["Dall'alambicco esce sempre un liquido incolore e secco, cioè senza zucchero. Da qui il produttore sceglie una di tre strade, spesso dettate anche dalla legge. Può lasciarlo non invecchiato, conservandolo per poco tempo in serbatoi d'acciaio inox, così colore e aromi restano quelli originali. Può invecchiarlo in botti di rovere, di solito per anni. Oppure può aromatizzarlo con sapori diversi dal legno, come accade per il gin.","De l'alambic sort toujours un liquide incolore et sec, c'est-à-dire sans sucre. À partir de là, le producteur choisit l'une de trois voies, souvent fixées aussi par la loi. Il peut le laisser non vieilli, en le gardant peu de temps en cuve inox : couleur et arômes restent ceux d'origine. Il peut le vieillir en fût de chêne, en général pendant des années. Ou il peut l'aromatiser avec d'autres saveurs que le bois, comme pour le gin.","What leaves the still is always colourless and dry, meaning it has no sugar. From here the producer takes one of three routes, often set by law as well. The spirit can stay unaged, kept briefly in stainless steel tanks so its colour and aromas stay as they were. It can be aged in oak barrels, usually for years. Or it can be flavoured with something other than wood, as happens with gin."],["La legge spesso decide al posto del produttore. Lo Scotch, per esempio, deve passare in rovere, mentre una Tequila può essere invecchiata oppure no. Per questo conviene sempre chiedersi: questo distillato è non invecchiato, invecchiato o aromatizzato? La risposta spiega già molto del suo colore e del suo profumo, ancora prima di assaggiarlo.","La loi décide souvent à la place du producteur. Le whisky écossais, par exemple, doit passer en fût de chêne, alors qu'une Tequila peut être vieillie ou non. Il est donc utile de toujours se demander : ce spiritueux est-il non vieilli, vieilli ou aromatisé ? La réponse explique déjà beaucoup de sa couleur et de son nez, avant même de le goûter.","The law often makes the choice for the producer. Scotch whisky, for instance, must spend time in oak, while a Tequila may be aged or not. So it always pays to ask: is this spirit unaged, oak-aged or flavoured? The answer already explains a great deal about its colour and its aromas, before it is even tasted."]],"k":[["Il gusto nasce da materia prima, fermentazione e grado di distillazione.","Le goût naît de la matière première, de la fermentation et du degré de distillation.","Flavour comes from raw material, fermentation and distillation strength."],["Ogni distillato appena fatto è incolore e secco.","Toute eau-de-vie qui sort de l'alambic est incolore et sèche.","Every newly made spirit is colourless and dry."],["Tre strade: non invecchiato, invecchiato in rovere, aromatizzato.","Trois voies : non vieilli, vieilli en fût de chêne, aromatisé.","Three routes: unaged, oak-aged, flavoured."],["Spesso è la legge a imporre la strada.","C'est souvent la loi qui impose la voie.","The law often dictates the route."]]},{"c":"p2","t":["Non invecchiato o in rovere","Non vieilli ou en fût de chêne","Unaged or oak-aged"],"p":[["Un distillato non invecchiato riposa poco tempo in acciaio inox, un materiale che non cede nulla: resta trasparente e conserva gli aromi nati nell'alambicco. Il rovere invece lavora. Una botte aggiunge colore, in una sequenza che va dal limone all'oro, poi all'ambra e, in casi molto rari, fino al marrone. Più la botte è giovane e più il distillato ci resta, più il colore si fa profondo.","Une eau-de-vie non vieillie repose peu de temps en cuve inox, un matériau qui ne cède rien : elle reste transparente et garde les arômes nés dans l'alambic. Le chêne, lui, travaille. Un fût ajoute de la couleur, selon une suite qui va du citron à l'or, puis à l'ambre et, très rarement, jusqu'au brun. Plus le fût est jeune et plus l'eau-de-vie y reste longtemps, plus la couleur devient profonde.","An unaged spirit rests briefly in stainless steel, a material that gives nothing away: it stays clear and keeps the aromas born in the still. Oak, on the other hand, does real work. A barrel adds colour in a sequence that goes from lemon to gold, then amber and, very rarely, brown. The newer the barrel and the longer the spirit stays in it, the deeper the colour."],["Il rovere regala anche aromi: vaniglia, cannella, chiodi di garofano, cocco. Una botte nuova, mai usata, ne dà moltissimi. Una botte già usata, detta vecchia, ne dà meno, e a ogni riutilizzo un po' meno ancora, come una bustina di tè messa in infusione più volte. Il produttore sceglie quindi tra botti nuove, per un'impronta forte del legno, e botti usate, per un tocco più discreto.","Le chêne apporte aussi des arômes : vanille, cannelle, clou de girofle, noix de coco. Un fût neuf, jamais utilisé, en donne énormément. Un fût déjà utilisé, dit vieux, en donne moins, et un peu moins encore à chaque nouvel usage, comme un sachet de thé infusé plusieurs fois. Le producteur choisit donc entre fûts neufs, pour une empreinte boisée marquée, et fûts usagés, pour une touche plus discrète.","Oak also brings aromas: vanilla, cinnamon, cloves, coconut. A new barrel that has never been used gives a lot of them. A previously used barrel, called an old barrel, gives less, and a little less again with every reuse, just like a tea bag steeped several times. So the producer chooses between new barrels for a strong oak imprint and used barrels for a gentler touch."],["Anche il tempo conta. Durante l'invecchiamento acqua ed etanolo evaporano lentamente attraverso il legno, e ciò che resta diventa più concentrato. Dopo moltissimi anni, a volte decenni, compaiono aromi nuovi che danno profondità: torta di frutta, frutta secca, cuoio, cera per mobili. È per questo che un distillato invecchiato a lungo sembra stratificato, con tante sfumature che si rivelano una dopo l'altra.","Le temps compte aussi. Pendant le vieillissement, l'eau et l'éthanol s'évaporent lentement à travers le bois, et ce qui reste devient plus concentré. Après de très nombreuses années, parfois des décennies, de nouveaux arômes apparaissent et donnent de la profondeur : cake aux fruits, fruits secs, cuir, cire à meubles. Voilà pourquoi un spiritueux longuement vieilli paraît étagé, avec des nuances qui se révèlent l'une après l'autre.","Time matters too. During ageing, water and ethanol slowly evaporate through the wood, so what remains becomes more concentrated. After many years, sometimes decades, new aromas appear and add depth: fruit cake, dried fruit, leather, wood polish. That is why a long-aged spirit feels layered, with shades of flavour revealing themselves one after another."]],"k":[["Non invecchiato: breve sosta in acciaio inox, nessun colore né aroma aggiunto.","Non vieilli : court passage en cuve inox, ni couleur ni arôme ajoutés.","Unaged: a short rest in stainless steel, no colour or aroma added."],["Colori del rovere: limone → oro → ambra → (raramente) marrone.","Couleurs du chêne : citron → or → ambre → (rarement) brun.","Oak colours: lemon → gold → amber → (rarely) brown."],["Botte nuova = più aromi (vaniglia, spezie, cocco); botte usata = meno.","Fût neuf = plus d'arômes (vanille, épices, coco) ; fût usagé = moins.","New barrel = more aroma (vanilla, spice, coconut); used barrel = less."],["Col tempo: evaporazione, concentrazione e aromi di frutta secca, cuoio, cera.","Avec le temps : évaporation, concentration, arômes de fruits secs, cuir, cire.","Over time: evaporation, concentration, dried fruit, leather, polish aromas."]]},{"c":"p2","t":["Assemblare, aromatizzare, diluire","Assembler, aromatiser, diluer","Blending, flavouring and dilution"],"p":[["Ogni botte è un piccolo mondo a sé: due botti riempite con lo stesso distillato, lo stesso giorno, non daranno mai un risultato identico. Il maestro assemblatore mescola il contenuto di molte botti per due obiettivi. Il primo è la costanza: chi compra di nuovo la stessa bottiglia si aspetta lo stesso gusto. Il secondo è la complessità: unire distillati con caratteri diversi è il modo più semplice per dare profondità.","Chaque fût est un petit monde : deux fûts remplis de la même eau-de-vie, le même jour, ne donneront jamais exactement le même résultat. Le maître de chai assemble le contenu de nombreux fûts avec deux objectifs. Le premier est la constance : qui rachète la même bouteille attend le même goût. Le second est la complexité : marier des eaux-de-vie de caractères différents est le moyen le plus simple de donner de la profondeur.","Every barrel is its own little world: two barrels filled with the same spirit on the same day will never turn out exactly alike. The blender combines the contents of many barrels with two aims. The first is consistency: anyone buying the same bottle again expects the same taste. The second is complexity: bringing together spirits with different characters is the easiest way to create depth."],["Quando si vogliono aromi diversi dal legno, si usano soprattutto tre tecniche. Si può ridistillare il distillato insieme a erbe, semi o spezie, ottenendo un liquido aromatizzato ma incolore. Si possono lasciare le stesse piante in infusione nel distillato, come in una tisana fredda: gli aromi e anche il colore passano piano piano. Oppure si possono aggiungere aromi già pronti, naturali o artificiali.","Quand on veut des arômes autres que le bois, on utilise surtout trois techniques. On peut redistiller l'alcool avec des herbes, des graines ou des épices : on obtient un liquide aromatisé mais incolore. On peut laisser ces mêmes plantes macérer dans l'alcool, comme une tisane froide : les arômes et aussi la couleur passent peu à peu. Ou bien on peut ajouter des arômes tout prêts, naturels ou artificiels.","When flavours other than wood are wanted, three main techniques are used. The spirit can be redistilled together with herbs, seeds or spices, giving a flavoured but colourless liquid. The same plants can be left to soak in the spirit, like a cold herbal tea, so their flavours and colour seep out slowly. Or ready-made flavourings, natural or artificial, can simply be added."],["L'ultimo gesto prima dell'imbottigliamento è quasi sempre la diluizione. Si aggiunge acqua completamente pura e la grande maggioranza dei distillati scende al 40% vol. Il motivo è pratico: un alcol troppo forte anestetizza il palato e impedisce di sentire e apprezzare il gusto. L'acqua non porta nessun aroma: abbassa solo il grado, come aprire una finestra in una stanza troppo calda.","Le dernier geste avant la mise en bouteille est presque toujours la dilution. On ajoute de l'eau parfaitement pure et la grande majorité des spiritueux descend à 40 % vol. La raison est pratique : un alcool trop fort anesthésie le palais et empêche de percevoir et d'apprécier le goût. L'eau n'apporte aucun arôme : elle baisse seulement le degré, comme on ouvre une fenêtre dans une pièce surchauffée.","The last move before bottling is almost always dilution. Completely pure water is added and the vast majority of spirits come down to 40% abv. The reason is practical: alcohol that is too strong numbs the palate, making it impossible to taste or enjoy the spirit. The water brings no aroma; it simply lowers the strength, like opening a window in an overheated room."]],"k":[["L'assemblaggio cerca costanza e complessità.","L'assemblage recherche constance et complexité.","Blending aims for consistency and complexity."],["Tre modi di aromatizzare: ridistillazione, macerazione, aromi aggiunti.","Trois façons d'aromatiser : redistillation, macération, arômes ajoutés.","Three ways to flavour: redistillation, maceration, added flavourings."],["La macerazione dà anche colore; la ridistillazione dà un liquido incolore.","La macération donne aussi de la couleur ; la redistillation donne un liquide incolore.","Maceration also adds colour; redistillation gives a colourless liquid."],["Diluizione con acqua pura, di solito a 40% vol., per rendere il distillato bevibile.","Dilution à l'eau pure, souvent à 40 % vol., pour rendre le spiritueux buvable.","Dilution with pure water, usually to 40% abv, makes the spirit drinkable."]]},{"c":"p2","t":["Dolcezza e colore","Douceur et couleur","Sweetness and colour"],"p":[["Poiché ogni distillato esce secco dall'alambicco, qualsiasi dolcezza che si avverte in bocca è stata aggiunta dopo, di solito semplicemente con zucchero. Attenzione alle parole: qui dolce indica solo il sapore dello zucchero. Un whiskey con profumi di vaniglia e frutta può sembrare dolce al naso, ma se non ha zucchero aggiunto resta secco. Naso goloso e palato dolce non sono la stessa cosa.","Comme toute eau-de-vie sort sèche de l'alambic, la douceur que l'on perçoit en bouche a été ajoutée après, le plus souvent avec du sucre. Attention aux mots : ici, doux désigne seulement le goût du sucre. Un whiskey aux arômes de vanille et de fruits peut sembler doux au nez, mais s'il n'a pas de sucre ajouté, il reste sec. Nez gourmand et bouche sucrée, ce n'est pas la même chose.","Since every spirit leaves the still dry, any sweetness you notice in the mouth was added afterwards, usually simply as sugar. Watch the wording: here, sweet refers only to the taste of sugar. A whiskey with vanilla and fruity aromas may seem sweet on the nose, but with no added sugar it is still dry. A sweet-smelling nose and a sweet palate are not the same thing."],["Il colore può arrivare da più fonti. Il rovere è la più naturale. Poi c'è il caramello colorante: le botti danno tonalità diverse, così chi assembla ne usa piccolissime quantità per avere ogni lotto dello stesso colore. Usato bene, il caramello non è dolce e non aggiunge aromi. Altri distillati, come molti liquori, ricevono coloranti naturali o artificiali, a volte dai toni vivacissimi.","La couleur peut venir de plusieurs sources. Le chêne est la plus naturelle. Il y a ensuite le caramel colorant : les fûts donnent des teintes différentes, alors l'assembleur en utilise de toutes petites quantités pour que chaque lot ait la même couleur. Bien utilisé, le caramel n'est pas sucré et n'ajoute aucun arôme. D'autres spiritueux, comme beaucoup de liqueurs, reçoivent des colorants naturels ou artificiels, parfois très vifs.","Colour can come from several sources. Oak is the most natural one. Then there is caramel colouring: barrels give different shades, so the blender uses tiny amounts to keep every batch the same colour. Used properly, caramel is not sweet and adds no aroma. Other spirits, including many liqueurs, receive natural or artificial colourings, sometimes in very bright shades."],["Da qui una lezione utile per la degustazione: il colore non è una prova dell'età. Alcuni distillati prendono tutto o quasi tutto il colore dal caramello, quindi può esistere un distillato non invecchiato dal colore intenso. Un bicchiere ambrato fa pensare a lunghi anni in botte, ma solo l'etichetta o la conoscenza dello stile possono confermarlo.","D'où une leçon utile pour la dégustation : la couleur ne prouve pas l'âge. Certains spiritueux tirent toute ou presque toute leur couleur du caramel ; un spiritueux non vieilli peut donc être très coloré. Un verre ambré fait penser à de longues années en fût, mais seuls l'étiquette ou la connaissance du style peuvent le confirmer.","This gives a useful tasting lesson: colour is no proof of age. Some spirits get all or nearly all of their colour from caramel, so an unaged spirit can be deeply coloured. An amber glass suggests long years in barrel, but only the label or knowledge of the style can confirm it."]],"k":[["La dolcezza è sempre aggiunta dopo la distillazione, di solito con zucchero.","La douceur est toujours ajoutée après la distillation, en général avec du sucre.","Sweetness is always added after distillation, usually as sugar."],["Dolce = sapore di zucchero, non un profumo goloso.","Doux = goût de sucre, pas un arôme gourmand.","Sweet = taste of sugar, not a sweet-smelling aroma."],["Fonti di colore: rovere, caramello, coloranti naturali o artificiali.","Sources de couleur : chêne, caramel, colorants naturels ou artificiels.","Colour sources: oak, caramel, natural or artificial colourings."],["Il colore non prova l'età: anche un distillato non invecchiato può essere scuro.","La couleur ne prouve pas l'âge : un spiritueux non vieilli peut être foncé.","Colour does not prove age: an unaged spirit can be dark."]]},{"c":"s1","t":["Dall'uva al vino","Du raisin au vin","From grapes to wine"],"p":[["Un brandy d'uva non è altro che vino distillato, e il Cognac è il più famoso di tutti. Nasce nel sud-ovest della Francia, in una zona ben delimitata a nord di Bordeaux. Solo l'uva coltivata lì può diventare Cognac: come per molti prodotti legati a un territorio, il nome è un indirizzo preciso e non una semplice ricetta che si può copiare altrove.","Un brandy de raisin n'est rien d'autre que du vin distillé, et le Cognac est le plus célèbre de tous. Il naît dans le sud-ouest de la France, dans une zone bien délimitée au nord de Bordeaux. Seul le raisin cultivé là peut devenir du Cognac : comme pour beaucoup de produits liés à un terroir, le nom est une adresse précise et non une simple recette que l'on pourrait copier ailleurs.","A grape brandy is simply wine that has been distilled, and Cognac is the most famous of them all. It comes from south-west France, from a clearly defined area north of the town of Bordeaux. Only grapes grown there can become Cognac: as with many products tied to a place, the name is a precise address rather than a recipe that can be copied elsewhere."],["Le uve di questa zona danno al Cognac i suoi aromi di base, fruttati e floreali. Dopo la vendemmia si pressano per liberare il succo, che è ricco di zucchero e quindi non ha bisogno di lavorazioni complicate: si mette a fermentare subito. Il risultato è un vino, ed è proprio questo vino, non l'uva, a entrare nell'alambicco. Prima di essere un distillato, il Cognac è dunque un vino.","Les raisins de cette zone donnent au Cognac ses arômes de base, fruités et floraux. Après la vendange, on les presse pour libérer le jus, riche en sucre, qui n'a donc pas besoin de transformations compliquées : on le met à fermenter tout de suite. On obtient un vin, et c'est ce vin, et non le raisin, qui entre dans l'alambic. Avant d'être une eau-de-vie, le Cognac est donc un vin.","The grapes from this area give Cognac its basic aromas, fruity and floral. After harvest they are pressed to release their juice, which is full of sugar and so needs no complicated processing: it is fermented straight away. The result is a wine, and it is this wine, not the grapes, that goes into the still. Before it is a spirit, then, Cognac is a wine."],["Il Cognac segue con precisione le quattro tappe di ogni distillato: lavorazione dell'uva, fermentazione in vino, distillazione e fase finale in botte. Per orientarsi basta ricordare un'immagine: un grappolo di Cognac attraversa la stessa strada di un grappolo da vino, ma a metà percorso, invece di finire nel bicchiere, prende la deviazione verso l'alambicco.","Le Cognac suit avec précision les quatre étapes de tout spiritueux : transformation du raisin, fermentation en vin, distillation et étape finale en fût. Pour s'y retrouver, il suffit d'une image : une grappe destinée au Cognac emprunte le même chemin qu'une grappe destinée au vin, mais à mi-parcours, au lieu de finir dans le verre, elle bifurque vers l'alambic.","Cognac follows the four steps of every spirit closely: processing the grapes, fermenting them into wine, distilling, and a final stage in barrel. One image helps: a bunch of Cognac grapes travels the same road as a bunch of wine grapes, but halfway along, instead of ending up in the glass, it takes the turning towards the still."]],"k":[["Brandy d'uva = vino distillato; il Cognac è il più noto.","Brandy de raisin = vin distillé ; le Cognac est le plus connu.","Grape brandy = distilled wine; Cognac is the best known."],["Zona delimitata del sud-ovest della Francia, a nord di Bordeaux.","Zone délimitée du sud-ouest de la France, au nord de Bordeaux.","A defined area of south-west France, north of Bordeaux."],["Le uve danno aromi fruttati e floreali.","Les raisins donnent des arômes fruités et floraux.","The grapes give fruity and floral aromas."],["Uve pressate, succo fermentato subito in vino.","Raisins pressés, jus fermenté tout de suite en vin.","Grapes pressed, juice fermented straight away into wine."]]},{"c":"s1","t":["Due passaggi nell'alambicco discontinuo","Deux passages à l'alambic à repasse","Twice through the pot still"],"p":[["Per il Cognac la legge non lascia scelta: il vino deve essere distillato due volte in un alambicco discontinuo. Niente colonna. È un lavoro lento, a lotti, perché dopo ogni distillazione l'alambicco va svuotato e pulito. Gli alambicchi tradizionali del Cognac si scaldano con bruciatori a gas e il condensatore è una serpentina immersa in acqua fredda continuamente rinnovata.","Pour le Cognac, la loi ne laisse pas le choix : le vin doit être distillé deux fois dans un alambic à repasse. Pas de colonne. C'est un travail lent, par lots, car après chaque distillation l'alambic doit être vidé et nettoyé. Les alambics traditionnels du Cognac sont chauffés par des brûleurs à gaz et leur condenseur est un serpentin plongé dans une eau froide sans cesse renouvelée.","For Cognac the law leaves no choice: the wine must be distilled twice in a pot still. No column allowed. It is slow, batch-by-batch work, because after every distillation the still has to be emptied and cleaned. Traditional Cognac stills are heated with gas burners, and the condenser is a coil sitting in cold water that is constantly refreshed."],["Perché tanta fatica? Perché l'alambicco discontinuo dà un distillato di grado relativamente basso, che conserva molto gusto e carattere: proprio ciò che serve a un Cognac. Una colonna alta darebbe un distillato più leggero e meno espressivo, perdendo buona parte dei profumi fruttati e floreali dell'uva. Si può dire che la doppia distillazione protegga l'anima del vino invece di cancellarla.","Pourquoi tant d'efforts ? Parce que l'alambic à repasse donne une eau-de-vie de degré relativement bas, qui garde beaucoup de goût et de caractère : exactement ce qu'il faut à un Cognac. Une colonne haute donnerait une eau-de-vie plus légère et moins expressive, en perdant une bonne partie des arômes fruités et floraux du raisin. On peut dire que la double distillation protège l'âme du vin au lieu de l'effacer.","Why go to so much trouble? Because a pot still gives a spirit of relatively low strength that keeps plenty of flavour and character, exactly what a Cognac needs. A tall column would give a lighter, less expressive spirit and lose much of the grapes' fruity and floral aromas. You could say that double distillation protects the soul of the wine instead of wiping it out."]],"k":[["Per legge: doppia distillazione in alambicco discontinuo.","Par la loi : double distillation à l'alambic à repasse.","By law: double distillation in a pot still."],["Lavoro a lotti, lento e impegnativo.","Travail par lots, lent et exigeant.","Slow, labour-intensive batch work."],["Alambicchi tradizionali scaldati con bruciatori a gas.","Alambics traditionnels chauffés par des brûleurs à gaz.","Traditional stills heated with gas burners."],["Grado basso = molto gusto e carattere.","Degré bas = beaucoup de goût et de caractère.","Low strength = lots of flavour and character."]]},{"c":"s1","t":["Rovere, assemblaggio e menzioni d'età","Chêne, assemblage et mentions d'âge","Oak, blending and age terms"],"p":[["Appena distillato, il futuro Cognac non può ancora chiamarsi così: la legge impone almeno due anni in botti di rovere. Il legno gli dà colore e aromi di vaniglia e di pane tostato. I Cognac migliori restano in botte molto più a lungo, si concentrano e sviluppano note di torta di frutta, cuoio e cera per mobili, segno di una lunga e lenta maturazione.","Tout juste distillé, le futur Cognac ne peut pas encore porter ce nom : la loi impose au moins deux ans en fût de chêne. Le bois lui apporte de la couleur et des arômes de vanille et de pain grillé. Les meilleurs Cognacs restent bien plus longtemps en fût, se concentrent et développent des notes de cake aux fruits, de cuir et de cire à meubles, signe d'une longue et lente maturation.","Fresh from the still, the future Cognac cannot yet use the name: the law requires at least two years in oak barrels. The wood gives it colour and aromas of vanilla and toast. The finest Cognacs stay in barrel far longer, becoming concentrated and developing notes of fruit cake, leather and wood polish, the mark of a long, slow maturation."],["Quasi tutti i Cognac sono assemblaggi di distillati di età diverse: i più giovani portano freschezza, i più vecchi profondità, e insieme danno complessità. Prima della diluizione e dell'imbottigliamento è comune aggiungere un po' di caramello colorante, per avere sempre la stessa tonalità, e una leggera dolcificazione. Un Cognac può quindi essere appena morbido al palato pur nascendo secco dall'alambicco.","Presque tous les Cognacs sont des assemblages d'eaux-de-vie d'âges différents : les plus jeunes apportent de la fraîcheur, les plus vieilles de la profondeur, et ensemble elles donnent de la complexité. Avant la dilution et la mise en bouteille, il est courant d'ajouter un peu de caramel colorant, pour garder toujours la même teinte, et de sucrer légèrement. Un Cognac peut donc être un peu rond en bouche alors qu'il sort sec de l'alambic.","Nearly all Cognacs are blends of spirits of different ages: younger ones bring freshness, older ones depth, and together they create complexity. Before dilution and bottling it is common to add a little caramel colouring, to keep the shade consistent, and a touch of sweetening. So a Cognac can feel slightly rounded on the palate even though it left the still dry."],["Sull'etichetta tre sigle indicano l'età, e si riferiscono sempre al distillato più giovane dell'assemblaggio. VS garantisce almeno 2 anni, VSOP almeno 4 anni, XO almeno 10 anni. Si può pensare a una scala con tre gradini: 2, 4 e 10. Se in un assemblaggio c'è un distillato di 5 anni e uno di 20, conta il 5.","Sur l'étiquette, trois mentions indiquent l'âge, et elles se rapportent toujours à l'eau-de-vie la plus jeune de l'assemblage. VS garantit au moins 2 ans, VSOP au moins 4 ans, XO au moins 10 ans. On peut imaginer un escalier à trois marches : 2, 4 et 10. Si un assemblage contient une eau-de-vie de 5 ans et une de 20 ans, c'est le 5 qui compte.","Three label terms show the age, and they always refer to the youngest spirit in the blend. VS guarantees at least 2 years, VSOP at least 4 years, XO at least 10 years. Picture a staircase with three steps: 2, 4 and 10. If a blend contains a 5-year-old and a 20-year-old spirit, it is the 5 that counts."]],"k":[["Almeno 2 anni in rovere per legge; vaniglia e tostato.","Au moins 2 ans en fût de chêne par la loi ; vanille et grillé.","At least 2 years in oak by law; vanilla and toast."],["Invecchiamento lungo: torta di frutta, cuoio, cera per mobili.","Long vieillissement : cake aux fruits, cuir, cire à meubles.","Long ageing: fruit cake, leather, wood polish."],["Quasi sempre assemblaggi; spesso caramello e un po' di zucchero.","Presque toujours des assemblages ; souvent caramel et un peu de sucre.","Almost always blends; often caramel and a little sugar."],["VS 2+ anni, VSOP 4+ anni, XO 10+ anni: età del distillato più giovane.","VS 2 ans et plus, VSOP 4 ans et plus, XO 10 ans et plus : âge de l'eau-de-vie la plus jeune.","VS 2+ years, VSOP 4+ years, XO 10+ years: age of the youngest spirit."]]},{"c":"s2","t":["Qualsiasi materia prima, ovunque","N'importe quelle matière première, partout","Any raw material, anywhere"],"p":[["La vodka è il distillato più libero di tutti. Si può produrre in qualsiasi paese del mondo e partendo da qualsiasi materia prima vegetale. Non c'è una zona d'origine obbligatoria, come per il Cognac, né un ingrediente imposto, come l'agave per la Tequila. Ciò che fa di un distillato una vodka non è il luogo né la pianta: è il grado a cui viene distillato.","La vodka est le plus libre de tous les spiritueux. On peut la produire dans n'importe quel pays du monde, à partir de n'importe quelle matière première végétale. Pas de zone d'origine obligatoire comme pour le Cognac, ni d'ingrédient imposé comme l'agave pour la Tequila. Ce qui fait d'un spiritueux une vodka, ce n'est ni le lieu ni la plante : c'est le degré auquel il est distillé.","Vodka is the freest spirit of all. It can be made in any country in the world and from any plant-based raw material. There is no compulsory area of origin, as with Cognac, and no required ingredient, as agave is for Tequila. What makes a spirit a vodka is neither the place nor the plant: it is the strength it is distilled to."],["Anche se la scelta è aperta, alcune materie prime sono legate alle vodka di qualità più alta: i cereali, in particolare orzo, frumento e segale, e le patate. Dopo la lavorazione per ottenere un liquido zuccherino, si fa fermentare come per ogni altro distillato. Le prime due tappe sono quindi quelle classiche; la vera particolarità della vodka arriva con la terza.","Même si le choix est ouvert, certaines matières premières sont associées aux vodkas de plus grande qualité : les céréales, en particulier l'orge, le blé et le seigle, et les pommes de terre. Après la transformation pour obtenir un liquide sucré, on fait fermenter comme pour tout autre spiritueux. Les deux premières étapes sont donc classiques ; la vraie particularité de la vodka arrive avec la troisième.","Although the choice is open, some raw materials are linked with premium-quality vodka: cereals, especially barley, wheat and rye, and potatoes. After processing to make a sugary liquid, it is fermented just like any other spirit. So the first two steps are the classic ones; vodka's real distinguishing feature arrives with the third."]],"k":[["La vodka si può fare ovunque, con qualsiasi materia prima.","La vodka peut se faire partout, avec n'importe quelle matière première.","Vodka can be made anywhere, from any raw material."],["La definisce il grado di distillazione, non il luogo né la pianta.","C'est le degré de distillation qui la définit, pas le lieu ni la plante.","It is defined by distillation strength, not place or plant."],["Vodka di qualità: cereali (orzo, frumento, segale) e patate.","Vodkas de qualité : céréales (orge, blé, seigle) et pommes de terre.","Premium vodka: cereals (barley, wheat, rye) and potatoes."]]},{"c":"s2","t":["Un distillato neutro, poi diluito","Un alcool neutre, puis dilué","A neutral spirit, then diluted"],"p":[["La vodka è un distillato neutro diluito. Per essere neutro, il distillato deve raggiungere almeno il 95% o il 96% vol., secondo la legge del paese di produzione. Un grado così alto si ottiene solo con l'alambicco a colonna, anche se alcuni produttori usano alambicchi discontinui in una parte del processo. A quel livello di alcol non resta quasi nessun aroma: da qui il nome neutro.","La vodka est un alcool neutre dilué. Pour être neutre, l'alcool doit atteindre au moins 95 % ou 96 % vol., selon la loi du pays de production. Un degré aussi élevé ne s'obtient qu'avec une colonne, même si certains producteurs utilisent des alambics à repasse pour une partie du processus. À ce niveau d'alcool, il ne reste presque aucun arôme : d'où le nom de neutre.","Vodka is a diluted neutral spirit. To count as neutral, the spirit must reach at least 95% or 96% abv, depending on the law of the producing country. Such a high strength can only be achieved with a column still, although some producers use pot stills for part of the process. At that alcohol level almost no aroma remains, hence the name neutral."],["Dopo la distillazione la vodka non passa in botte: resta non invecchiata e trasparente. Viene poi diluita con acqua pura fino al grado di imbottigliamento, di solito il 40% vol. Si può immaginare come una tela bianca: tutto il lavoro del produttore punta a togliere, non ad aggiungere, così che nel bicchiere resti un alcol pulito e quasi senza profumo.","Après la distillation, la vodka ne passe pas en fût : elle reste non vieillie et transparente. On la dilue ensuite avec de l'eau pure jusqu'au degré de mise en bouteille, en général 40 % vol. On peut l'imaginer comme une toile blanche : tout le travail du producteur vise à retirer, et non à ajouter, pour qu'il reste dans le verre un alcool net et presque sans odeur.","After distillation, vodka does not go into barrels: it stays unaged and clear. It is then diluted with pure water to bottling strength, typically 40% abv. Think of it as a blank canvas: the producer's whole effort goes into taking away rather than adding, so that what reaches the glass is a clean spirit with almost no smell."]],"k":[["Distillato neutro: almeno 95% o 96% vol., secondo la legge del paese.","Alcool neutre : au moins 95 % ou 96 % vol., selon la loi du pays.","Neutral spirit: at least 95% or 96% abv, depending on national law."],["Serve l'alambicco a colonna; il discontinuo solo per una parte.","Il faut une colonne ; l'alambic à repasse seulement pour une partie.","A column still is needed; pot stills only for part of the process."],["Non invecchiata, diluita di solito al 40% vol.","Non vieillie, diluée en général à 40 % vol.","Unaged, usually diluted to 40% abv."]]},{"c":"s2","t":["Neutra o con un po' di carattere","Neutre ou avec un peu de caractère","Neutral or with a little character"],"p":[["La maggior parte delle vodka cerca la neutralità più completa. È proprio questa assenza di profumo a renderla così diffusa nei drink miscelati e nei cocktail: si fonde con succhi, bibite e liquori senza imporre il proprio gusto, aggiungendo alcol ma lasciando la scena agli altri ingredienti. Chi lavora al bancone e vuole rinforzare un drink senza cambiarne il sapore pensa subito a lei.","La plupart des vodkas recherchent la neutralité la plus complète. C'est justement cette absence d'odeur qui la rend si répandue dans les boissons mélangées et les cocktails : elle se fond dans les jus, les sodas et les liqueurs sans imposer son goût, en ajoutant de l'alcool tout en laissant la vedette aux autres ingrédients. Derrière un bar, quand on veut renforcer un drink sans en changer le goût, on pense tout de suite à elle.","Most vodka aims for the most complete neutrality possible. That very lack of aroma is what makes it so popular in mixed drinks and cocktails: it blends into juices, sodas and liqueurs without imposing its own taste, adding alcohol while leaving the spotlight to the other ingredients. A bartender who wants to strengthen a drink without changing its flavour reaches for it first."],["Alcune vodka, però, conservano un filo di carattere. Al naso e in bocca si colgono leggeri accenni della materia prima, per esempio un tocco di cereale o di patata. Restano comunque molto delicate, lontanissime dall'intensità di un whisky o di un brandy, e si descrivono ancora correttamente come neutre. È come la differenza tra acqua minerale e acqua distillata: sottile, ma percepibile.","Certaines vodkas gardent cependant une pointe de caractère. Au nez et en bouche, on perçoit de légères touches de la matière première, par exemple une note de céréale ou de pomme de terre. Elles restent très délicates, bien loin de l'intensité d'un whisky ou d'un brandy, et on les décrit encore à juste titre comme neutres. C'est comme la différence entre une eau minérale et une eau distillée : subtile, mais perceptible.","Some vodkas, however, keep a hint of character. On the nose and palate there are faint touches of the raw material, such as a note of grain or potato. They remain very delicate, nowhere near the intensity of a whisky or a brandy, and are still correctly described as neutral. It is like the difference between mineral water and distilled water: subtle, but noticeable."]],"k":[["La maggior parte delle vodka è il più neutra possibile.","La plupart des vodkas sont aussi neutres que possible.","Most vodka is as neutral as possible."],["La neutralità la rende versatile nei drink e nei cocktail.","Sa neutralité la rend polyvalente dans les drinks et cocktails.","Neutrality makes it versatile in mixed drinks and cocktails."],["Alcune mostrano lievi note della materia prima, ma restano neutre.","Certaines montrent de légères notes de matière première, mais restent neutres.","Some show faint raw-material notes but are still neutral."]]},{"c":"s3","t":["Dal chicco allo zucchero: la maltazione","Du grain au sucre : le maltage","From grain to sugar: malting"],"p":[["Il whisky nasce sempre dai cereali e si può immaginare come una birra passata in alambicco. C'è però un ostacolo: un chicco d'orzo è secco, duro e pieno di amido, non di zucchero. I lieviti non sanno cosa farsene dell'amido, quindi prima di qualunque fermentazione bisogna trasformarlo in zucchero. Il metodo classico lascia fare quasi tutto il lavoro all'orzo stesso.","Le whisky naît toujours de céréales, et on peut le voir comme une bière passée à l'alambic. Il y a pourtant un obstacle : un grain d'orge est sec, dur et rempli d'amidon, pas de sucre. Les levures ne savent rien faire de l'amidon ; avant toute fermentation, il faut donc le changer en sucre. La méthode classique laisse l'orge faire presque tout le travail elle-même.","Whisky always starts with grain, and you can picture it as beer that has been through a still. There is one obstacle, though: a barley grain is dry, hard and packed with starch rather than sugar. Yeast cannot do anything with starch, so it has to be turned into sugar before any fermentation can happen. The classic method lets the barley do almost all of that work itself."],["Il primo passo è la maltazione. Si lascia germogliare l'orzo e, mentre cresce, il chicco produce degli enzimi, piccoli strumenti chimici capaci di trasformare l'amido. Al momento giusto si soffia aria calda per fermare la crescita: da qui in poi si parla di orzo maltato. Il chicco ha ormai tutto ciò che serve, ma lo zucchero non è ancora stato liberato.","La première étape est le maltage. On laisse l'orge germer et, pendant sa croissance, le grain fabrique des enzymes, de petits outils chimiques capables de transformer l'amidon. Au bon moment, on envoie de l'air chaud pour stopper la croissance : on parle alors d'orge maltée. Le grain possède désormais tout ce qu'il faut, mais le sucre n'est pas encore libéré.","The first step is malting. The barley is allowed to start growing, and as it grows the grain makes enzymes, tiny chemical tools that can change starch. At the right moment hot air is blown through to stop the growth, and from then on it is called malted barley. The grain now carries everything it needs, but the sugar has not been released yet."],["Poi l'orzo maltato viene macinato fino a ottenere una farina grossolana, a cui si possono aggiungere anche altri cereali macinati. Il tutto si mescola con acqua: in questo bagno gli enzimi dell'orzo si mettono al lavoro e convertono l'amido in zucchero. Il risultato è un liquido dolce, pronto per i lieviti. Da qui in avanti il percorso è quello di tutti i distillati: fermentazione, distillazione, invecchiamento.","L'orge maltée est ensuite broyée en une farine grossière, à laquelle on peut ajouter d'autres céréales broyées. Le tout est mélangé à de l'eau : dans ce bain, les enzymes de l'orge se mettent au travail et convertissent l'amidon en sucre. On obtient un liquide sucré, prêt pour les levures. La suite est celle de tous les spiritueux : fermentation, distillation, vieillissement.","Next the malted barley is crushed into a rough flour, and other crushed grains can be added too. Everything is mixed with water, and in this bath the barley's enzymes get to work, converting the starch into sugar. The result is a sweet liquid ready for the yeast. From here the path is the one every spirit follows: fermentation, distillation, then what happens after the still."],["Ogni cereale lascia la sua firma nel bicchiere. L'orzo porta note di cereale, il mais ricorda il mais dolce e la segale dà un tocco speziato e pepato. Tutti i whisky passano poi in botti di rovere, vengono assemblati e, dove la legge lo consente, corretti nel colore con il caramello. Quasi sempre si imbottigliano a 40% vol.","Chaque céréale laisse sa signature dans le verre. L'orge apporte des notes céréalières, le maïs rappelle le maïs doux et le seigle donne une touche épicée et poivrée. Tous les whiskies passent ensuite en fûts de chêne, sont assemblés et, si la loi le permet, ajustés en couleur avec du caramel. Ils sont presque toujours mis en bouteille à 40 % vol.","Each grain leaves its own signature in the glass. Barley brings cereal notes, corn recalls sweetcorn and rye adds a spicy, peppery edge. All whiskies then spend time in oak barrels, are blended and, where the law allows, have their colour adjusted with caramel. Most are bottled at 40% abv."]],"k":[["Il whisky si fa solo con cereali: è come una birra distillata.","Le whisky se fait uniquement avec des céréales : c'est une sorte de bière distillée.","Whisky is made only from grain: think of it as distilled beer."],["I cereali contengono amido, non zucchero: va convertito prima della fermentazione.","Les céréales contiennent de l'amidon, pas du sucre : il faut le convertir avant la fermentation.","Grains hold starch, not sugar, so it must be converted before fermentation."],["Maltazione: l'orzo germoglia, crea enzimi, poi l'aria calda ferma la crescita.","Maltage : l'orge germe, crée des enzymes, puis l'air chaud stoppe la croissance.","Malting: barley sprouts, makes enzymes, then hot air stops the growth."],["Orzo macinato + acqua: gli enzimi trasformano l'amido in zucchero.","Orge broyée + eau : les enzymes transforment l'amidon en sucre.","Crushed malt + water: the enzymes turn starch into sugar."]]},{"c":"s3","t":["Le regole comuni a tutto lo Scotch","Les règles communes à tout le Scotch","The rules every Scotch follows"],"p":[["Scotch è il nome del whisky scozzese, e non è solo un'indicazione geografica generica. Per portare questo nome un whisky deve essere distillato in Scozia e poi invecchiato in Scozia per almeno tre anni. Entrambe le condizioni contano: un distillato scozzese che va a maturare oltre confine perde il diritto al nome, anche se è identico in tutto il resto.","Scotch désigne le whisky écossais, et ce n'est pas une simple indication géographique. Pour porter ce nom, un whisky doit être distillé en Écosse puis vieilli en Écosse pendant au moins trois ans. Les deux conditions comptent : un distillat écossais envoyé vieillir de l'autre côté de la frontière perd le droit au nom, même s'il est identique en tout le reste.","Scotch is the name for whisky from Scotland, and it is more than a loose geographical label. To carry the name, a whisky must be distilled in Scotland and then aged in Scotland for at least three years. Both conditions matter: a Scottish spirit sent to mature across the border loses the right to the name, even if everything else about it is identical."],["Il passaggio in rovere è quindi obbligatorio, e lascia il segno. Le botti cedono colore e aromi, e con il tempo lo spirito si concentra perché un po' di acqua e alcol evapora attraverso il legno. Nei whisky più vecchi possono comparire note di torta di frutta secca e di spezie dolci. Dopo la maturazione si assembla, si regola il colore se serve e si diluisce.","Le passage en chêne est donc obligatoire, et il laisse sa marque. Les fûts apportent couleur et arômes, et avec le temps le spiritueux se concentre, car un peu d'eau et d'alcool s'évapore à travers le bois. Dans les whiskies plus âgés peuvent apparaître des notes de cake aux fruits et d'épices douces. Après la maturation, on assemble, on ajuste la couleur si besoin et on dilue.","Time in oak is therefore compulsory, and it leaves its mark. The barrels give colour and aromas, and over the years the spirit becomes more concentrated as a little water and alcohol escape through the wood. Older whiskies can show notes of fruit cake and sweet spice. After maturation the whisky is blended, its colour adjusted if needed, and it is diluted."],["Lo Scotch si divide in due grandi famiglie da conoscere bene: il Single Malt e il Blended. La differenza non sta nel prestigio né nell'età, ma in tre domande semplici: con quali cereali è fatto, in quale tipo di alambicco è stato distillato e da quante distillerie proviene. Rispondere a queste tre domande basta per collocare qualsiasi bottiglia di Scotch.","Le Scotch se divise en deux grandes familles à bien connaître : le Single Malt et le Blended. La différence ne tient ni au prestige ni à l'âge, mais à trois questions simples : avec quelles céréales il est fait, dans quel type d'appareil il a été distillé et de combien de distilleries il provient. Ces trois réponses suffisent pour situer n'importe quelle bouteille de Scotch.","Scotch splits into two big families worth knowing well: Single Malt and Blended. The difference is not about prestige or age but about three simple questions: which grains it is made from, what kind of still it was distilled in, and how many distilleries it comes from. Answer those three and you can place any bottle of Scotch."]],"k":[["Scotch: distillato e invecchiato in Scozia.","Scotch : distillé et vieilli en Écosse.","Scotch: distilled and aged in Scotland."],["Invecchiamento minimo: tre anni, sempre in Scozia.","Vieillissement minimum : trois ans, toujours en Écosse.","Minimum ageing: three years, always in Scotland."],["Due famiglie principali: Single Malt e Blended Scotch.","Deux grandes familles : Single Malt et Blended Scotch.","Two main families: Single Malt and Blended Scotch."],["Le distingue la ricetta: cereali, alambicco, numero di distillerie.","Elles se distinguent par la recette : céréales, appareil, nombre de distilleries.","What separates them: grains, type of still, number of distilleries."]]},{"c":"s3","t":["Il Single Malt e il fumo della torba","Le Single Malt et la fumée de tourbe","Single Malt and peat smoke"],"p":[["Un Single Malt Scotch risponde a tre requisiti. È fatto esclusivamente con orzo maltato, senza altri cereali. È distillato in alambicchi discontinui, gli stessi che lavorano un lotto alla volta. E proviene da una sola distilleria. Il termine 'single' si riferisce proprio a questo: un unico luogo di produzione, non un'unica botte.","Un Single Malt Scotch répond à trois exigences. Il est fait uniquement avec de l'orge maltée, sans autre céréale. Il est distillé dans des alambics, ces appareils qui travaillent un lot à la fois. Et il provient d'une seule distillerie. Le mot « single » renvoie justement à cela : un seul lieu de production, et non un seul fût.","A Single Malt Scotch meets three requirements. It is made only from malted barley, with no other grains. It is distilled in pot stills, the kind that work one batch at a time. And it comes from a single distillery. That is what 'single' refers to: one place of production, not one barrel."],["Gli alambicchi discontinui producono un distillato di gradazione relativamente bassa e ricco di carattere. Per questo i Single Malt sono whisky espressivi: al naso e in bocca si trovano cereale, frutta, fiori, miele e, con il tempo in botte, torta di frutta secca e spezie dolci. Due Single Malt di distillerie diverse possono essere molto lontani tra loro.","Les alambics donnent un distillat de degré relativement bas et plein de caractère. C'est pourquoi les Single Malts sont des whiskies expressifs : au nez et en bouche, on trouve céréale, fruits, fleurs, miel et, avec le temps passé en fût, cake aux fruits et épices douces. Deux Single Malts de distilleries différentes peuvent être très éloignés l'un de l'autre.","Pot stills produce a spirit of fairly low strength that is full of character. That is why Single Malts are expressive whiskies: on the nose and palate you find cereal, fruit, flowers and honey and, with time in the barrel, fruit cake and sweet spice. Two Single Malts from different distilleries can taste very different from each other."],["Alcuni Single Malt hanno un aroma in più: il fumo. Nasce dalla torba, un combustibile naturale che si brucia nel momento in cui si scalda l'orzo alla fine della maltazione. Il fumo avvolge i chicchi e li profuma, e quel profumo arriva fino al bicchiere. Si tratta però di una minoranza: soltanto pochi Single Malt sono torbati, alcuni in modo molto deciso.","Certains Single Malts ont un arôme en plus : la fumée. Elle vient de la tourbe, un combustible naturel que l'on brûle au moment où l'on chauffe l'orge à la fin du maltage. La fumée enveloppe les grains et les parfume, et ce parfum se retrouve jusque dans le verre. Il s'agit cependant d'une minorité : seuls quelques Single Malts sont tourbés, certains de façon très marquée.","Some Single Malts carry one extra aroma: smoke. It comes from peat, a natural fuel that is burned when the barley is heated at the end of malting. The smoke wraps around the grains and flavours them, and that flavour travels all the way to the glass. These whiskies are a minority, though: only a few Single Malts are peaty, some of them very strongly."]],"k":[["Single Malt: 100% orzo maltato, alambicchi discontinui, una sola distilleria.","Single Malt : 100 % orge maltée, alambics, une seule distillerie.","Single Malt: 100% malted barley, pot stills, one distillery."],["Aromi tipici: cereale, frutta, fiori, miele, torta di frutta, spezie dolci.","Arômes typiques : céréale, fruits, fleurs, miel, cake aux fruits, épices douces.","Typical aromas: cereal, fruit, flowers, honey, fruit cake, sweet spice."],["Il fumo viene dalla torba bruciata quando si scalda l'orzo maltato.","La fumée vient de la tourbe brûlée pendant le chauffage de l'orge maltée.","Smoke comes from peat burned while the malted barley is heated."],["Solo pochi Single Malt sono torbati.","Seuls quelques Single Malts sont tourbés.","Only a few Single Malts are peaty."]]},{"c":"s3","t":["Il Blended Scotch e il whisky di cereali","Le Blended Scotch et le whisky de grain","Blended Scotch and grain whisky"],"p":[["Accanto al malto esiste un secondo tipo di whisky scozzese: il whisky di cereali, o grain whisky. Si prepara con orzo maltato insieme ad altri cereali e si distilla in colonna, non in alambicco discontinuo. Ne esce uno spirito dal profumo leggero e dalla consistenza morbida. Da solo arriva raramente sugli scaffali: il suo vero compito è un altro.","À côté du malt, il existe un second type de whisky écossais : le whisky de grain. On le prépare avec de l'orge maltée et d'autres céréales, et on le distille en colonne, pas à l'alambic. Il en sort un spiritueux au nez léger et à la texture douce. On le trouve rarement seul en rayon : sa vraie mission est ailleurs.","Alongside malt there is a second kind of Scottish whisky: grain whisky. It is made from malted barley together with other grains and distilled in a column still rather than a pot still. The result is a spirit with a light aroma and a smooth texture. It rarely reaches the shelf on its own, because its real job lies elsewhere."],["Quella funzione è il Blended Scotch, la categoria più diffusa. Un Blended unisce whisky di malto e whisky di cereali provenienti da distillerie diverse. Si può pensare a un'orchestra: i malti, intensi e caratteriali, sono gli strumenti solisti; il grain whisky, leggero e morbido, è la sezione che lega tutto. Anche whisky di età diverse entrano nella miscela per aggiungere varietà.","Cette mission, c'est le Blended Scotch, la catégorie la plus répandue. Un Blended réunit des whiskies de malt et des whiskies de grain venant de distilleries différentes. On peut penser à un orchestre : les malts, intenses et typés, sont les solistes ; le whisky de grain, léger et souple, est la section qui lie l'ensemble. Des whiskies d'âges différents entrent aussi dans le mélange pour ajouter de la diversité.","That job is Blended Scotch, the most widespread category. A blend brings together malt whiskies and grain whiskies from different distilleries. Think of an orchestra: the malts, intense and characterful, are the soloists, while the light, smooth grain whisky is the section that holds everything together. Whiskies of different ages also go into the mix to add variety."],["Perché mescolare? Per due ragioni. La prima è la costanza: ogni botte è un po' diversa, e chi compra una bottiglia si aspetta lo stesso gusto della volta precedente. La seconda è la complessità: unire spiriti con caratteri diversi è il modo più semplice per creare profondità. Una piccola dose di caramello aiuta poi a mantenere identico il colore da un lotto all'altro.","Pourquoi assembler ? Pour deux raisons. La première est la régularité : chaque fût est un peu différent, et l'on attend d'une bouteille le même goût que la fois précédente. La seconde est la complexité : réunir des spiritueux de caractères différents est le moyen le plus simple de créer de la profondeur. Une petite dose de caramel aide ensuite à garder la même couleur d'un lot à l'autre.","Why blend? For two reasons. The first is consistency: every barrel is slightly different, and people expect a bottle to taste the same as last time. The second is complexity: combining spirits with different characters is the easiest way to build depth. A tiny amount of caramel then helps keep the colour identical from one batch to the next."],["I Blended sono molto vari. Alcuni hanno un'intensità media e uno stile semplice, perfetti da miscelare; altri sono intensi e complessi. In generale, grazie al whisky di cereali, risultano più morbidi dei Single Malt. Non conviene quindi considerarli 'di serie B': sono il frutto di un mestiere preciso, quello di chi assembla.","Les Blended sont très variés. Certains ont une intensité moyenne et un style simple, parfaits en mélange ; d'autres sont intenses et complexes. En général, grâce au whisky de grain, ils sont plus souples que les Single Malts. Inutile donc de les voir comme des whiskies de second rang : ils sont le fruit d'un vrai métier, celui de l'assemblage.","Blends vary a great deal. Some have medium intensity and a simple style, ideal for mixing; others are pronounced and complex. Thanks to the grain whisky they are usually smoother than Single Malts. So there is no reason to see them as second-rate: they are the work of a real craft, the craft of blending."]],"k":[["Grain whisky: orzo maltato + altri cereali, colonna, leggero e morbido.","Whisky de grain : orge maltée + autres céréales, colonne, léger et souple.","Grain whisky: malted barley + other grains, column still, light and smooth."],["Blended Scotch: malto + cereali da distillerie diverse.","Blended Scotch : malt + grain de distilleries différentes.","Blended Scotch: malt + grain whiskies from different distilleries."],["Si assembla per costanza e complessità.","On assemble pour la régularité et la complexité.","Blending gives consistency and complexity."],["Di solito più morbido dei Single Malt; dal semplice al complesso.","En général plus souple que les Single Malts ; du simple au complexe.","Usually smoother than Single Malts; from simple to complex."]]},{"c":"s4","t":["Bourbon: mais e botti nuove","Bourbon : maïs et fûts neufs","Bourbon: corn and new barrels"],"p":[["Il Bourbon è il whiskey americano più famoso. Molti lo associano al Kentucky, e in effetti è lo stato che ne produce di più, ma la legge permette di farlo in qualsiasi parte degli Stati Uniti. Lo stile del Bourbon dipende da tre scelte precise: la ricetta dei cereali, il modo di distillare e il tipo di botte.","Le Bourbon est le whiskey américain le plus célèbre. Beaucoup l'associent au Kentucky, et c'est en effet l'État qui en produit le plus, mais la loi permet de le faire partout aux États-Unis. Son style dépend de trois choix précis : la recette de céréales, la façon de distiller et le type de fût.","Bourbon is the best-known American whiskey. Many people link it to Kentucky, and that is indeed the state that makes the most, but the law allows it to be made anywhere in the United States. Its style comes down to three clear choices: the grain recipe, the way it is distilled and the type of barrel."],["Prima scelta: almeno il 51% dei cereali deve essere mais, completato di solito da orzo e segale. Il mais porta note di mais dolce. Seconda scelta: di solito si distilla in colonna, ma fermandosi a una gradazione bassa, così lo spirito conserva molto carattere. Una colonna, quindi, non produce per forza un distillato leggero: tutto dipende da quanto in alto si spinge la gradazione.","Premier choix : au moins 51 % des céréales doivent être du maïs, complété en général par de l'orge et du seigle. Le maïs apporte des notes de maïs doux. Deuxième choix : on distille d'habitude en colonne, mais jusqu'à un degré bas, pour que le spiritueux garde beaucoup de caractère. Une colonne ne donne donc pas forcément un distillat léger : tout dépend du degré visé.","First choice: at least 51% of the grain must be corn, usually topped up with barley and rye. Corn brings sweetcorn notes. Second choice: it is normally distilled in a column still, but only to a low strength, so the spirit keeps plenty of character. A column still does not have to make a light spirit; it all depends on how high the strength goes."],["Terza scelta: le botti devono essere di rovere nuovo, bruciato all'interno. Una botte mai usata prima è quella che cede più colore e più aromi, e la carbonizzazione aggiunge ancora intensità. Il risultato è un whiskey intenso e complesso, con note di mais dolce, cereale, frutta, vaniglia e cocco.","Troisième choix : les fûts doivent être en chêne neuf, brûlé à l'intérieur. Un fût jamais utilisé est celui qui cède le plus de couleur et d'arômes, et le bousinage ajoute encore de l'intensité. Le résultat est un whiskey intense et complexe, aux notes de maïs doux, de céréale, de fruits, de vanille et de noix de coco.","Third choice: the barrels must be new oak, charred on the inside. A barrel that has never been used gives the most colour and aroma, and the charring adds even more intensity. The result is a pronounced, complex whiskey with notes of sweetcorn, cereal, fruit, vanilla and coconut."],["Una trappola frequente: molti dicono che il Bourbon è 'dolce'. In realtà non contiene zucchero aggiunto ed è secco. L'impressione di dolcezza viene dagli aromi di vaniglia, frutta e cocco, che il naso associa ai dolci. Nel linguaggio della degustazione, 'dolce' indica solo il sapore dello zucchero, percepito in bocca.","Un piège fréquent : on dit souvent que le Bourbon est « sucré ». En réalité, il ne contient pas de sucre ajouté et il est sec. L'impression de douceur vient des arômes de vanille, de fruits et de noix de coco, que le nez associe aux desserts. En dégustation, « sucré » désigne uniquement le goût du sucre, perçu en bouche.","A common trap: people often call Bourbon 'sweet'. In fact it has no added sugar and is dry. The impression of sweetness comes from the vanilla, fruit and coconut aromas, which the nose links with desserts. In tasting language, 'sweet' refers only to the taste of sugar, felt on the palate."]],"k":[["Bourbon: almeno 51% mais; prodotto ovunque negli USA, soprattutto in Kentucky.","Bourbon : au moins 51 % de maïs ; produit partout aux États-Unis, surtout au Kentucky.","Bourbon: at least 51% corn; made anywhere in the USA, mostly Kentucky."],["Di solito distillato in colonna a bassa gradazione.","En général distillé en colonne à bas degré.","Usually column-distilled to a low strength."],["Botti di rovere nuovo carbonizzato: molto colore e aroma.","Fûts de chêne neuf brûlé : beaucoup de couleur et d'arômes.","New charred oak barrels: lots of colour and aroma."],["Mais dolce, vaniglia, cocco, frutta; nessuno zucchero aggiunto: è secco.","Maïs doux, vanille, coco, fruits ; aucun sucre ajouté : il est sec.","Sweetcorn, vanilla, coconut, fruit; no added sugar, so it is dry."]]},{"c":"s4","t":["Tennessee whiskey: il passaggio nel carbone","Tennessee whiskey : le passage au charbon","Tennessee whiskey: through the charcoal"],"p":[["Il Tennessee whiskey è un parente stretto del Bourbon. Si prepara allo stesso modo, con la stessa prevalenza di mais, la stessa distillazione e le stesse botti nuove carbonizzate. Le differenze sono due. La prima è geografica: a differenza del Bourbon, si può produrre soltanto nello stato del Tennessee. La seconda è un passaggio in più, che avviene prima della botte.","Le Tennessee whiskey est un proche parent du Bourbon. On le fait de la même façon, avec la même majorité de maïs, la même distillation et les mêmes fûts neufs brûlés. Il y a deux différences. La première est géographique : contrairement au Bourbon, il ne peut être produit que dans l'État du Tennessee. La seconde est une étape en plus, avant le fût.","Tennessee whiskey is a close relative of Bourbon. It is made the same way, with the same majority of corn, the same distillation and the same new charred barrels. There are two differences. The first is geography: unlike Bourbon, it can only be made in the state of Tennessee. The second is one extra step that happens before the barrel."],["Appena uscito dall'alambicco, lo spirito viene fatto passare attraverso uno strato di carbone di legno d'acero. Non è un filtro finissimo, ma trattiene una parte delle impurità. L'effetto è un whiskey dal carattere più morbido. Questo passaggio non aggiunge alcun sapore: niente acero, niente fumo. Toglie qualcosa, non mette nulla.","Dès sa sortie de l'alambic, le spiritueux passe à travers une couche de charbon de bois d'érable. Ce n'est pas un filtre très fin, mais il retient une partie des impuretés. Le résultat est un whiskey au caractère plus souple. Cette étape n'ajoute aucun goût : ni érable ni fumée. Elle enlève quelque chose, elle n'apporte rien.","As soon as it leaves the still, the new spirit is passed through a bed of maple charcoal. It is not a very fine filter, but it holds back some impurities. The effect is a whiskey with a smoother character. This step adds no flavour at all: no maple, no smoke. It takes something away rather than putting anything in."],["Per ricordarlo, basta un'immagine: il Tennessee whiskey è un Bourbon che fa una doccia prima di entrare in botte. Attenzione all'ordine delle fasi: la filtrazione avviene sul distillato nuovo, incolore, e non sul whiskey già invecchiato. Dopo la filtrazione il percorso torna identico a quello del Bourbon, con le botti nuove carbonizzate che danno colore e aromi.","Pour s'en souvenir, une image suffit : le Tennessee whiskey est un Bourbon qui prend une douche avant d'entrer en fût. Attention à l'ordre des étapes : la filtration se fait sur le distillat neuf, incolore, et non sur le whiskey déjà vieilli. Ensuite, le parcours redevient identique à celui du Bourbon, avec des fûts neufs brûlés qui donnent couleur et arômes.","One image makes it easy to remember: Tennessee whiskey is a Bourbon that takes a shower before going into the barrel. Watch the order of the steps: the filtering is done on the new, colourless spirit, not on whiskey that has already aged. After that, the path is the same as Bourbon's, with new charred barrels giving colour and aroma."]],"k":[["Si produce solo in Tennessee.","Il ne se produit qu'au Tennessee.","Made only in the state of Tennessee."],["Stessa ricetta e stesse botti del Bourbon.","Même recette et mêmes fûts que le Bourbon.","Same recipe and barrels as Bourbon."],["In più: filtrazione su carbone d'acero prima della botte.","En plus : filtration sur charbon d'érable avant le fût.","Extra step: maple charcoal filtering before the barrel."],["Toglie impurità, dà morbidezza, non aggiunge sapore.","Retire des impuretés, apporte de la souplesse, n'ajoute aucun goût.","Removes impurities, adds smoothness, adds no flavour."]]},{"c":"s4","t":["Rye whiskey: la segale piccante","Rye whiskey : le seigle épicé","Rye whiskey: the spicy grain"],"p":[["Il Rye whiskey americano è il gemello speziato del Bourbon. Le regole sono le stesse in tutto, con una sola differenza: il cereale principale. Invece del mais, almeno il 51% della ricetta deve essere segale. Restano quindi la distillazione in colonna a bassa gradazione e l'invecchiamento in botti di rovere nuovo carbonizzato.","Le Rye whiskey américain est le jumeau épicé du Bourbon. Les règles sont les mêmes en tout point, à une différence près : la céréale principale. À la place du maïs, au moins 51 % de la recette doit être du seigle. On retrouve donc la distillation en colonne à bas degré et le vieillissement en fûts de chêne neuf brûlé.","American Rye whiskey is Bourbon's spicy twin. The rules are the same in every way except one: the main grain. Instead of corn, at least 51% of the recipe must be rye. So you still find low-strength column distillation and ageing in new charred oak barrels."],["Quel cambio di cereale basta a cambiare il carattere. La segale porta aromi speziati e pepati, che si sentono bene sia al naso sia in bocca. Dove il Bourbon ricorda il mais dolce e il cocco, il Rye ha un profilo più vivace e piccante. Le note di vaniglia della botte nuova restano, ma fanno da sfondo alla speziatura.","Ce changement de céréale suffit à changer le caractère. Le seigle apporte des arômes épicés et poivrés, bien présents au nez comme en bouche. Là où le Bourbon évoque le maïs doux et la noix de coco, le Rye a un profil plus vif et piquant. Les notes de vanille du fût neuf restent, mais en arrière-plan des épices.","That change of grain is enough to change the character. Rye brings spicy, peppery aromas that show clearly on both nose and palate. Where Bourbon recalls sweetcorn and coconut, Rye has a livelier, sharper profile. The vanilla notes from the new barrel are still there, but they sit behind the spice."],["Un modo semplice per fissare i tre whiskey americani è guardare il cereale e il filtro. Mais in maggioranza: Bourbon. Mais in maggioranza più carbone d'acero e solo Tennessee: Tennessee whiskey. Segale in maggioranza: Rye. Chi cerca un whiskey americano con una nota pepata, per esempio in un cocktail, pensa al Rye.","Un moyen simple de retenir les trois whiskeys américains : regarder la céréale et le filtre. Majorité de maïs : Bourbon. Majorité de maïs, plus charbon d'érable et uniquement au Tennessee : Tennessee whiskey. Majorité de seigle : Rye. Pour un whiskey américain avec une touche poivrée, par exemple dans un cocktail, on pense au Rye.","A simple way to fix the three American whiskeys is to look at the grain and the filter. Mostly corn: Bourbon. Mostly corn, plus maple charcoal, made only in Tennessee: Tennessee whiskey. Mostly rye: Rye. Anyone looking for an American whiskey with a peppery kick, for example in a cocktail, should think of Rye."]],"k":[["Rye: almeno 51% segale.","Rye : au moins 51 % de seigle.","Rye: at least 51% rye."],["Per il resto si fa come il Bourbon: colonna e botti nuove carbonizzate.","Pour le reste, il se fait comme le Bourbon : colonne et fûts neufs brûlés.","Otherwise made like Bourbon: column still and new charred barrels."],["Aromi speziati e pepati.","Arômes épicés et poivrés.","Spicy, peppery aromas."]]},{"c":"s4","t":["Irlanda, Canada e Giappone","Irlande, Canada et Japon","Ireland, Canada and Japan"],"p":[["In Irlanda la maggior parte dei whiskey nasce dall'unione di distillati d'alambicco e distillati di colonna. Lo stile tipico è leggero e morbido, facile da bere. Esistono però anche whiskey irlandesi distillati solo in alambicco, e alcuni usano un ingrediente insolito: l'orzo non maltato. Questo cereale dà una consistenza oleosa e un carattere di frutta secca a guscio, come nocciola.","En Irlande, la plupart des whiskeys naissent de l'union de distillats d'alambic et de distillats de colonne. Le style typique est léger et souple, facile à boire. Il existe aussi des whiskeys irlandais distillés uniquement à l'alambic, et certains utilisent un ingrédient inhabituel : l'orge non maltée. Elle apporte une texture huileuse et un caractère de fruits secs, comme la noisette.","In Ireland, most whiskeys are made by combining pot-still and column-still spirits. The typical style is light and smooth, easy to drink. There are also Irish whiskeys made only in pot stills, and some use an unusual ingredient: unmalted barley. This gives an oily texture and a nutty character."],["Il Canada usa molti cereali diversi e di solito unisce spiriti distillati ad alta gradazione, più leggeri, con spiriti a bassa gradazione, più saporiti. Così si ottengono whisky equilibrati e versatili. Nei whisky canadesi migliori, però, c'è un filo conduttore: la segale. È il sapore che dà la loro firma, speziata e pepata.","Le Canada utilise beaucoup de céréales différentes et assemble en général des spiritueux distillés à haut degré, plus légers, avec des spiritueux à bas degré, plus savoureux. On obtient ainsi des whiskies équilibrés et polyvalents. Dans les meilleurs whiskies canadiens, un fil conducteur se dessine pourtant : le seigle, qui leur donne leur signature épicée et poivrée.","Canada uses many different grains and usually blends high-strength spirits, which are lighter, with low-strength spirits, which have more flavour. The result is balanced, versatile whiskies. In the best Canadian whiskies, though, there is one common thread: rye. It is the signature flavour, spicy and peppery."],["Il Giappone ha costruito la sua industria del whisky prendendo a modello la Scozia. Per questo vi si trovano sia whisky di malto sia blended, proprio come nello Scotch. Lo stile tradizionale è elegante e raffinato, preciso nei dettagli. Negli ultimi anni, però, molti produttori giapponesi esplorano stili e sapori nuovi, e la categoria è in continua evoluzione.","Le Japon a construit son industrie du whisky sur le modèle écossais. On y trouve donc des whiskies de malt et des blends, exactement comme pour le Scotch. Le style traditionnel est élégant et raffiné, précis dans les détails. Ces dernières années, cependant, de nombreux producteurs japonais explorent de nouveaux styles et saveurs, et la catégorie évolue sans cesse.","Japan built its whisky industry using Scotland as the model. That is why you find both malt and blended whiskies there, just as with Scotch. The traditional style is elegant and refined, precise in its details. In recent years, though, many Japanese producers have been exploring new styles and flavours, and the category keeps evolving."]],"k":[["Irlanda: per lo più miscele alambicco + colonna, leggere e morbide.","Irlande : surtout des assemblages alambic + colonne, légers et souples.","Ireland: mostly pot + column blends, light and smooth."],["Orzo non maltato: note di frutta secca e consistenza oleosa.","Orge non maltée : notes de fruits secs et texture huileuse.","Unmalted barley: nutty notes and an oily texture."],["Canada: molti cereali, miscele alta + bassa gradazione; firma della segale.","Canada : nombreuses céréales, assemblages haut + bas degré ; signature du seigle.","Canada: many grains, high + low strength blends; rye is the signature."],["Giappone: modello scozzese, malti e blended eleganti.","Japon : modèle écossais, malts et blends élégants.","Japan: Scottish model, elegant malts and blends."]]},{"c":"s5","t":["Succo di canna o melassa","Jus de canne ou mélasse","Cane juice or molasses"],"p":[["Il rum nasce dalla canna da zucchero, una pianta che ama il caldo. Per questo la sua produzione si concentra nei paesi dal clima caldo, e la sua patria storica sono i Caraibi. La regione però è un mosaico di piccoli paesi, ognuno con tradizioni e regole proprie. Classificare il rum per colore o per lingua parlata funziona poco: conviene invece seguire le quattro fasi di produzione.","Le rhum naît de la canne à sucre, une plante qui aime la chaleur. C'est pourquoi sa production se concentre dans les pays chauds, et sa patrie historique est la Caraïbe. La région est pourtant une mosaïque de petits pays, chacun avec ses traditions et ses règles. Classer le rhum par couleur ou par langue parlée fonctionne mal : mieux vaut suivre les quatre étapes de production.","Rum is made from sugar cane, a plant that loves heat. That is why production is centred on hot countries, and its historic heartland is the Caribbean. The region is a patchwork of small countries, though, each with its own traditions and rules. Sorting rum by colour or by the language spoken works poorly; it is far more useful to follow the four stages of production."],["La prima scelta riguarda la materia prima. Si può spremere la canna appena tagliata e far fermentare subito il suo succo dolce. I rum da succo di canna hanno spesso un sapore erbaceo, vegetale, molto marcato, come di erba appena falciata. Gli esempi migliori sono i rhum agricole, che nei Caraibi devono provenire dalla Martinica o dalla Guadalupa.","Le premier choix concerne la matière première. On peut presser la canne fraîchement coupée et faire fermenter aussitôt son jus sucré. Les rhums de jus de canne ont souvent un goût herbacé, végétal, très marqué, comme de l'herbe fraîchement coupée. Les meilleurs exemples sont les rhums agricoles, qui dans la Caraïbe doivent venir de Martinique ou de Guadeloupe.","The first choice is the raw material. Freshly cut cane can be crushed and its sweet juice fermented straight away. Rums made from cane juice often have a very pronounced grassy, herbaceous flavour, like freshly mown grass. The best examples are rhum agricole, which in the Caribbean must come from Martinique or Guadeloupe."],["La maggior parte dei distillatori caraibici, però, usa la melassa. È una sostanza nera e appiccicosa, il sottoprodotto dell'industria che trasforma il succo di canna in zucchero da cucina. Prima di fermentare va mescolata con acqua. I rum da melassa hanno sapori di caramello e zucchero di canna scuro: un profilo più rotondo rispetto alla freschezza erbacea del succo di canna.","La plupart des distillateurs de la Caraïbe utilisent pourtant la mélasse. C'est une substance noire et collante, le sous-produit de l'industrie qui transforme le jus de canne en sucre. Avant de fermenter, elle doit être mélangée à de l'eau. Les rhums de mélasse ont des saveurs de caramel et de sucre roux : un profil plus rond que la fraîcheur herbacée du jus de canne.","Most Caribbean distillers, however, use molasses. It is a black, sticky substance, the by-product of the industry that turns cane juice into sugar. It has to be mixed with water before fermentation can start. Molasses rums have flavours of caramel and brown sugar, a rounder profile than the grassy freshness of cane juice."]],"k":[["Il rum si fa con la canna da zucchero, che cresce nei climi caldi.","Le rhum se fait avec la canne à sucre, qui pousse en climat chaud.","Rum is made from sugar cane, which grows in hot climates."],["Meglio capirlo con le quattro fasi che con colore o lingua.","Mieux vaut le comprendre par les quatre étapes que par la couleur ou la langue.","Understand it through the four stages, not colour or language."],["Succo di canna: erbaceo; rhum agricole da Martinica e Guadalupa.","Jus de canne : herbacé ; rhum agricole de Martinique et Guadeloupe.","Cane juice: grassy; rhum agricole from Martinique and Guadeloupe."],["Melassa (la scelta più diffusa): caramello e zucchero di canna scuro.","Mélasse (le choix le plus courant) : caramel et sucre roux.","Molasses (the most common choice): caramel and brown sugar."]]},{"c":"s5","t":["La fermentazione e la frutta tropicale","La fermentation et les fruits tropicaux","Fermentation and tropical fruit"],"p":[["In ogni distillato la fermentazione trasforma lo zucchero in alcol, ma fa anche qualcos'altro: crea aromi. Sono soprattutto i lieviti a produrre profumi fruttati. Nel rum questo lavoro può diventare protagonista. Gestendo la fermentazione in un certo modo, si ottengono aromi di frutta tropicale, come banana o ananas, che in alcuni casi diventano molto intensi.","Dans tout spiritueux, la fermentation transforme le sucre en alcool, mais elle fait aussi autre chose : elle crée des arômes. Ce sont surtout les levures qui produisent des parfums fruités. Dans le rhum, ce travail peut passer au premier plan. En conduisant la fermentation d'une certaine façon, on obtient des arômes de fruits tropicaux, comme la banane ou l'ananas, parfois très intenses.","In every spirit, fermentation turns sugar into alcohol, but it also does something else: it creates aromas. Yeast in particular produces fruity scents. In rum this work can take centre stage. By managing fermentation in a certain way, distillers get tropical fruit aromas, such as banana or pineapple, which can become very pronounced."],["Spingendo al massimo il sapore creato in fermentazione si arriva a rum intensamente fruttati, quasi esplosivi al naso. I distillatori della Giamaica sono famosi proprio per questo stile. Se si incontra un rum dal profumo di frutta tropicale molto concentrato, è facile che dietro ci sia una fermentazione curata in questo senso, non un aroma aggiunto.","En poussant au maximum la saveur créée pendant la fermentation, on obtient des rhums intensément fruités, presque explosifs au nez. Les distillateurs de la Jamaïque sont célèbres pour ce style. Face à un rhum au parfum de fruits tropicaux très concentré, il y a de fortes chances qu'une fermentation travaillée dans ce sens en soit la cause, et non un arôme ajouté.","Pushing the flavour created during fermentation as far as it will go produces intensely fruity rums, almost explosive on the nose. Jamaican distillers are famous for exactly this style. When you meet a rum with a very concentrated tropical fruit aroma, the likely cause is a fermentation managed with that aim, not an added flavouring."],["Questa fase mostra bene perché le quattro tappe aiutano più del colore. Due rum entrambi incolori possono essere lontanissimi: uno leggero e discreto, l'altro carico di frutta tropicale. Chiedersi da quale materia prima viene, come è stato fermentato e distillato e che cosa è successo dopo dice molto di più sul bicchiere che guardarne la tinta.","Cette étape montre bien pourquoi les quatre étapes aident plus que la couleur. Deux rhums incolores peuvent être très éloignés : l'un léger et discret, l'autre chargé de fruits tropicaux. Se demander de quelle matière première il vient, comment il a été fermenté et distillé et ce qui s'est passé ensuite en dit bien plus sur le verre que sa teinte.","This stage shows clearly why the four steps help more than colour. Two rums that are both colourless can be worlds apart: one light and discreet, the other loaded with tropical fruit. Asking what it was made from, how it was fermented and distilled and what happened afterwards tells you far more about the glass than its shade does."]],"k":[["La fermentazione crea alcol e anche aromi fruttati.","La fermentation crée de l'alcool et aussi des arômes fruités.","Fermentation creates alcohol and fruity aromas too."],["Nel rum può dare aromi di frutta tropicale molto intensi.","Dans le rhum, elle peut donner des arômes de fruits tropicaux très intenses.","In rum it can give very pronounced tropical fruit aromas."],["La Giamaica è famosa per questo stile intensamente fruttato.","La Jamaïque est réputée pour ce style intensément fruité.","Jamaica is known for this intensely fruity style."]]},{"c":"s5","t":["Alambicco o colonna: intensità su misura","Alambic ou colonne : l'intensité sur mesure","Pot or column: intensity to order"],"p":[["Nei Caraibi quasi ogni distillatore può scegliere il tipo di alambicco, e la scelta decide l'intensità del rum. Chi vuole uno spirito intenso e ricco di carattere può usare l'alambicco discontinuo. Un'alternativa è la colonna corta, con poche sezioni, che dà anch'essa un distillato saporito: è il caso del rhum agricole.","Dans la Caraïbe, presque chaque distillateur peut choisir son appareil, et ce choix décide de l'intensité du rhum. Pour un spiritueux intense et plein de caractère, on peut utiliser l'alambic. Autre solution : la colonne courte, avec peu de sections, qui donne elle aussi un distillat savoureux. C'est le cas du rhum agricole.","In the Caribbean nearly every distiller can choose their still, and that choice decides how intense the rum will be. For a pronounced spirit full of character, a pot still is an option. Another is a short column with few sections, which also gives a flavourful spirit; this is how rhum agricole is made."],["All'estremo opposto ci sono i rum dal profumo leggero. Si producono in colonne alte, con molte sezioni, e si distillano a una gradazione elevata. Più alta è la gradazione, meno aroma resta nello spirito. Esempi di questo stile si trovano a Cuba e a Porto Rico, rum delicati e molto adatti ai cocktail.","À l'opposé, on trouve les rhums au nez léger. Ils sont produits dans de hautes colonnes, avec de nombreuses sections, et distillés à un degré élevé. Plus le degré est haut, moins il reste d'arômes dans le spiritueux. On trouve des exemples de ce style à Cuba et à Porto Rico : des rhums délicats, très à l'aise en cocktail.","At the opposite end are rums with a light aroma. They are made in tall column stills with many sections and distilled to a high strength. The higher the strength, the less aroma remains in the spirit. Examples of this style come from Cuba and Puerto Rico: delicate rums that work very well in cocktails."],["Molte distillerie caraibiche possiedono sia alambicchi discontinui sia colonne, e producono diversi distillati con intensità differenti. È come avere una tavolozza di colori: uno spirito leggero, uno intenso, uno fruttato. Più avanti, al momento dell'assemblaggio, questa varietà permette di comporre rum dallo stile molto diverso partendo dalla stessa distilleria.","Beaucoup de distilleries de la Caraïbe possèdent à la fois des alambics et des colonnes, et produisent plusieurs distillats d'intensités différentes. C'est comme une palette de peintre : un spiritueux léger, un intense, un fruité. Plus tard, au moment de l'assemblage, cette variété permet de composer des rhums de styles très différents à partir de la même distillerie.","Many Caribbean distilleries own both pot stills and column stills and make several spirits of different intensities. It is like a painter's palette: one light spirit, one pronounced, one fruity. Later, at the blending stage, this variety lets them compose rums in very different styles from the same distillery."]],"k":[["Alambicco discontinuo: rum intenso e di carattere.","Alambic : rhum intense et de caractère.","Pot still: pronounced, characterful rum."],["Colonna corta: anche lei saporita; usata per il rhum agricole.","Colonne courte : savoureuse elle aussi ; utilisée pour le rhum agricole.","Short column: also flavourful; used for rhum agricole."],["Colonna alta, alta gradazione: rum leggeri (Cuba, Porto Rico).","Haute colonne, haut degré : rhums légers (Cuba, Porto Rico).","Tall column, high strength: light rums (Cuba, Puerto Rico)."],["Molte distillerie hanno entrambi i tipi di alambicco.","Beaucoup de distilleries ont les deux types d'appareils.","Many distilleries own both types of still."]]},{"c":"s5","t":["Dopo l'alambicco: botte, filtri, zucchero e colore","Après l'alambic : fût, filtres, sucre et couleur","After the still: oak, filters, sugar and colour"],"p":[["Un rum può essere invecchiato o no. Il passaggio in rovere aggiunge aromi di vaniglia e spezie dolci, oltre al colore. In alcuni paesi caraibici un periodo in botte è obbligatorio per legge. Il rum non invecchiato, invece, riposa in contenitori d'acciaio: resta incolore e conserva gli aromi dello spirito appena distillato.","Un rhum peut être vieilli ou non. Le passage en chêne ajoute des arômes de vanille et d'épices douces, ainsi que de la couleur. Dans certains pays de la Caraïbe, un séjour en fût est obligatoire. Le rhum non vieilli repose au contraire en cuves d'acier : il reste incolore et garde les arômes du spiritueux fraîchement distillé.","A rum can be aged or not. Time in oak adds vanilla and sweet spice aromas, as well as colour. In some Caribbean countries a period in the barrel is a legal requirement. Unaged rum, by contrast, rests in steel tanks: it stays colourless and keeps the aromas of the freshly distilled spirit."],["E se un paese impone la botte ma si vuole un rum bianco? La soluzione è filtrare con il carbone, che toglie il colore preso dal legno. Si ottiene così un rum incolore che in realtà ha fatto un periodo in rovere. È uno dei motivi per cui il colore, da solo, non racconta come è stato fatto un rum.","Et si un pays impose le fût mais que l'on veut un rhum blanc ? La solution est la filtration au charbon, qui retire la couleur apportée par le bois. On obtient ainsi un rhum incolore qui a pourtant passé du temps en chêne. C'est l'une des raisons pour lesquelles la couleur, à elle seule, ne dit pas comment un rhum a été fait.","What if a country requires oak but the producer wants a white rum? The answer is charcoal filtering, which removes the colour taken from the wood. The result is a colourless rum that has actually spent time in oak. This is one reason why colour alone cannot tell you how a rum was made."],["Poi si assembla. Chi miscela può combinare spiriti d'alambicco e di colonna, di età diverse e anche di distillerie diverse, per costruire lo stile di ogni prodotto. Infine alcuni rum vengono addolciti: è comune in America Centrale e del Sud, mentre in certi paesi è vietato. Molti rum ricevono anche caramello per il colore, a volte quasi tutto il loro colore.","Vient ensuite l'assemblage. On peut combiner des distillats d'alambic et de colonne, d'âges différents et même de distilleries différentes, pour construire le style de chaque produit. Enfin, certains rhums sont sucrés : c'est courant en Amérique centrale et du Sud, alors que c'est interdit dans certains pays. Beaucoup de rhums reçoivent aussi du caramel pour la couleur, parfois presque toute leur couleur.","Then comes blending. Blenders can combine pot-still and column-still spirits, of different ages and even from different distilleries, to build the style of each product. Finally, some rums are sweetened: this is common in Central and South America, while some countries forbid it. Many rums also receive caramel for colour, sometimes almost all of their colour."],["Ultimo passaggio, come per quasi tutti i distillati: la diluizione con acqua pura fino al grado di imbottigliamento. Il risultato è una famiglia ricchissima, che va dal rum bianco leggero e discreto a quello scuro, intenso e speziato. Per orientarsi basta ripercorrere le quattro fasi: materia prima, fermentazione, distillazione e ciò che succede dopo.","Dernière étape, comme pour presque tous les spiritueux : la dilution à l'eau pure jusqu'au degré de mise en bouteille. Le résultat est une famille très riche, du rhum blanc léger et discret au rhum foncé, intense et épicé. Pour s'y retrouver, il suffit de reparcourir les quatre étapes : matière première, fermentation, distillation et ce qui se passe ensuite.","The last step, as for nearly every spirit, is dilution with pure water down to bottling strength. The result is a hugely varied family, from light, discreet white rum to dark, intense, spicy rum. To find your way, simply walk back through the four stages: raw material, fermentation, distillation and what happens afterwards."]],"k":[["Il rovere dà vaniglia, spezie dolci e colore; in alcuni paesi è obbligatorio.","Le chêne donne vanille, épices douces et couleur ; obligatoire dans certains pays.","Oak gives vanilla, sweet spice and colour; required in some countries."],["Rum bianco: acciaio (non invecchiato) o filtrazione al carbone (invecchiato).","Rhum blanc : acier (non vieilli) ou filtration au charbon (vieilli).","White rum: steel tanks (unaged) or charcoal filtering (aged)."],["Assemblaggio di stili, età e distillerie diverse.","Assemblage de styles, d'âges et de distilleries différents.","Blending of different styles, ages and distilleries."],["Zucchero: comune in America Centrale e del Sud, vietato in alcuni paesi; caramello frequente.","Sucre : courant en Amérique centrale et du Sud, interdit dans certains pays ; caramel fréquent.","Sugar: common in Central and South America, banned in some countries; caramel is common."]]},{"c":"s6","t":["Dall'agave blu al succo dolce","De l'agave bleu au jus sucré","From blue agave to sweet juice"],"p":[["La Tequila è un distillato messicano con un'identità molto precisa: si può produrre solo in alcuni stati del Messico indicati dalla legge e solo a partire dall'agave blu, una pianta originaria di quel paese. Non è un cactus, anche se ci somiglia: ha lunghe foglie appuntite, disposte a rosetta attorno a un grosso cuore duro. È proprio quel cuore la materia prima che interessa al distillatore.","La Tequila est un spiritueux mexicain à l'identité bien définie : on ne peut la produire que dans certains États du Mexique fixés par la loi, et uniquement à partir de l'agave bleu, une plante originaire de ce pays. Ce n'est pas un cactus, même s'il en a l'air : de longues feuilles pointues entourent un gros cœur dur. C'est ce cœur qui intéresse le distillateur.","Tequila is a Mexican spirit with a very clear identity: it can only be made in certain Mexican states named by law, and only from blue agave, a plant native to Mexico. It is not a cactus, even if it looks a bit like one: long, spiky leaves fan out around a large, hard core. That core is the part the distiller actually wants."],["Durante la raccolta le foglie vengono tagliate via e resta solo il cuore. Come accade per i cereali, il cuore d'agave appena raccolto non offre zuccheri pronti da fermentare: va lavorato. Lo si cuoce lentamente in forni, finché diventa morbido e al suo interno si formano zuccheri. Immaginate una patata dura che, dopo la cottura, si schiaccia con una forchetta: il principio è simile.","À la récolte, on coupe les feuilles pour ne garder que le cœur. Comme pour les céréales, ce cœur fraîchement récolté n'offre pas de sucres prêts à fermenter : il faut le transformer. On le cuit lentement dans des fours, jusqu'à ce qu'il devienne tendre et que des sucres se forment. Pensez à une pomme de terre dure qui s'écrase à la fourchette une fois cuite : le principe est proche.","At harvest the leaves are cut away, leaving only the core. As with grains, a freshly harvested agave core has no sugar ready to ferment: it has to be processed first. The cores are cooked slowly in ovens until they turn soft and sugars form inside them. Think of a hard potato that you can mash with a fork once it has been cooked: the idea is much the same."],["Una volta cotti, i cuori vengono schiacciati e rilasciano un succo dolce. Questo succo porta con sé i profumi tipici dell'agave blu, molto riconoscibili: note erbacee e vegetali, sentori di oliva, di terra e una punta di pepe. Sono questi aromi a rendere la Tequila così diversa da un rum o da un whisky, e il produttore cercherà di preservarli nelle fasi successive.","Une fois cuits, les cœurs sont broyés et libèrent un jus sucré. Ce jus porte les arômes typiques de l'agave bleu, très reconnaissables : des notes herbacées et végétales, des touches d'olive, de terre et une pointe de poivre. Ce sont ces arômes qui distinguent si nettement la Tequila d'un rhum ou d'un whisky, et le producteur cherchera à les préserver dans les étapes suivantes.","Once cooked, the cores are crushed and give up a sweet juice. That juice carries the very recognisable aromas of blue agave: herbaceous and vegetal notes, hints of olive and earth, and a touch of pepper. These aromas are what set Tequila so clearly apart from rum or whisky, and the producer will try to protect them through the following steps."]],"k":[["Solo agave blu, solo in alcuni stati del Messico.","Uniquement de l'agave bleu, uniquement dans certains États du Mexique.","Blue agave only, made only in certain Mexican states."],["Si usa il cuore: le foglie si tagliano via.","On utilise le cœur : les feuilles sont coupées.","The core is used; the leaves are cut away."],["Cottura in forno: il cuore si ammorbidisce e si formano zuccheri, poi lo si schiaccia.","Cuisson au four : le cœur s'attendrit et des sucres se forment, puis on le broie.","Oven cooking softens the core and creates sugars; then it is crushed."],["Aromi dell'agave: erbacei, vegetali, oliva, terra, pepe.","Arômes de l'agave : herbacés, végétaux, olive, terre, poivre.","Agave aromas: herbaceous, vegetal, olive, earthy, peppery."]]},{"c":"s6","t":["Tequila o Tequila 100% agave?","Tequila ou Tequila 100 % agave ?","Tequila or Tequila 100% agave?"],"p":[["Il succo d'agave viene allungato con acqua per ottenere un liquido zuccherino pronto per la fermentazione. A questo punto il produttore ha una scelta: può aggiungere anche altri zuccheri, che non vengono dall'agave. La legge però fissa un limite chiaro: almeno il 51% degli zuccheri fermentati deve provenire dall'agave blu. Più della metà, insomma, deve sempre essere agave.","Le jus d'agave est allongé d'eau pour obtenir un liquide sucré prêt à fermenter. À ce stade, le producteur a un choix : il peut ajouter d'autres sucres, qui ne viennent pas de l'agave. La loi fixe toutefois une limite claire : au moins 51 % des sucres fermentés doivent provenir de l'agave bleu. Autrement dit, plus de la moitié doit toujours être de l'agave.","The agave juice is mixed with water to make a sugary liquid ready for fermentation. At this point the producer has a choice: other sugars, not from agave, may be added too. The law sets a clear floor, though: at least 51% of the sugars fermented must come from blue agave. In other words, more than half must always be agave."],["Quando in etichetta compare la dicitura «100% agave», significa che per il liquido zuccherino è stato usato solo agave blu, senza alcun altro zucchero. Il risultato tende ad avere un carattere d'agave più marcato. Tutte le altre Tequile, quelle che sfruttano la possibilità di aggiungere altri zuccheri, portano semplicemente il nome «Tequila», senza altre precisazioni.","Quand l'étiquette indique « 100 % agave », cela signifie que seul l'agave bleu a servi à préparer le liquide sucré, sans aucun autre sucre. Le résultat a souvent un caractère d'agave plus marqué. Toutes les autres Tequilas, celles qui profitent de la possibilité d'ajouter d'autres sucres, s'appellent simplement « Tequila », sans autre précision.","When a label says ‘100% agave’, it means only blue agave was used to make the sugary liquid, with no other sugars at all. The result tends to show a more pronounced agave character. Every other Tequila, the ones that use the option of adding other sugars, is simply labelled ‘Tequila’, with nothing more."],["Attenzione a non confondere questa distinzione con l'invecchiamento: riguarda solo l'origine degli zuccheri. Una Tequila non invecchiata può essere «100% agave» oppure no, e lo stesso vale per una Tequila passata in legno. Davanti a uno scaffale conviene quindi leggere due informazioni separate: da un lato quanto agave c'è, dall'altro quanto tempo il distillato ha riposato.","Attention à ne pas confondre cette distinction avec le vieillissement : elle concerne seulement l'origine des sucres. Une Tequila non vieillie peut être « 100 % agave » ou non, et il en va de même pour une Tequila passée en fût. Devant un rayon, il faut donc lire deux informations distinctes : d'un côté la part d'agave, de l'autre le temps de repos du spiritueux.","Be careful not to mix this up with ageing: it is only about where the sugars came from. An unaged Tequila can be ‘100% agave’ or not, and the same is true of an oak-aged one. So, in front of a shelf, it pays to read two separate pieces of information: how much agave went in, and how long the spirit has rested."]],"k":[["Il succo d'agave si mescola con acqua prima della fermentazione.","Le jus d'agave est mélangé à de l'eau avant la fermentation.","Agave juice is mixed with water before fermentation."],["Almeno il 51% degli zuccheri deve venire dall'agave blu.","Au moins 51 % des sucres doivent venir de l'agave bleu.","At least 51% of the sugars must come from blue agave."],["«100% agave» = nessun altro zucchero, carattere d'agave più marcato.","« 100 % agave » = aucun autre sucre, caractère d'agave plus marqué.","‘100% agave’ = no other sugars, more pronounced agave character."],["Ogni stile, invecchiato o no, può essere «Tequila» o «100% agave».","Chaque style, vieilli ou non, peut être « Tequila » ou « 100 % agave ».","Any style, aged or unaged, can be ‘Tequila’ or ‘100% agave’."]]},{"c":"s6","t":["Distillare per conservare l'agave","Distiller pour garder l'agave","Distilling to keep the agave"],"p":[["Dopo la fermentazione arriva la distillazione. La Tequila si può fare anche in alambicchi a colonna, ma le migliori seguono un'altra strada: vengono distillate due volte in alambicchi discontinui, fermandosi a una gradazione notevolmente bassa. Ricordate la regola generale: più bassa è la gradazione di distillazione, più profumi della materia prima restano nel distillato.","Après la fermentation vient la distillation. On peut faire de la Tequila dans des colonnes, mais les meilleures suivent une autre voie : elles sont distillées deux fois en alambic à repasse, en s'arrêtant à un degré remarquablement bas. Rappelez-vous la règle générale : plus le degré de distillation est bas, plus le spiritueux garde les arômes de sa matière première.","After fermentation comes distillation. Tequila can be made in column stills, but the best ones take another route: they are distilled twice in pot stills and stopped at a notably low strength. Remember the general rule: the lower the distillation strength, the more of the raw material's aromas stay in the spirit."],["Il risultato è un distillato dal carattere deciso, che mette in primo piano quelle note erbacee e pepate dell'agave blu riconoscibili già al primo sorso. È l'esatto contrario di uno spirito neutro come la vodka, che viene spinto in colonna fino a gradazioni altissime proprio per eliminare quasi tutti i profumi.","Le résultat est un spiritueux au caractère affirmé, qui met en avant les notes herbacées et poivrées de l'agave bleu, reconnaissables dès la première gorgée. C'est tout l'inverse d'un alcool neutre comme la vodka, poussé en colonne jusqu'à des degrés très élevés justement pour effacer presque tous les arômes.","The result is a spirit with real personality, putting the herbaceous, peppery notes of blue agave front and centre, easy to spot from the first sip. It is the exact opposite of a neutral spirit such as vodka, which is pushed through a column to very high strength precisely to strip out almost all aroma."],["Un modo semplice per fissare il concetto: alambicco discontinuo, doppia distillazione e bassa gradazione significano «più agave nel bicchiere». Se un esercizio vi chiede come si ottengono le Tequile più espressive, la risposta passa da qui, non dalle colonne alte e dalle gradazioni elevate. Le colonne restano possibili, ma producono in genere Tequile dal carattere meno marcato.","Une façon simple de retenir l'idée : alambic à repasse, double distillation et degré bas signifient « plus d'agave dans le verre ». Si un exercice demande comment on obtient les Tequilas les plus expressives, la réponse passe par là, et non par les grandes colonnes et les degrés élevés. Les colonnes restent permises, mais donnent en général des Tequilas au caractère moins affirmé.","A simple way to lock the idea in: pot still, double distillation and low strength mean ‘more agave in the glass’. If a question asks how the most expressive Tequilas are made, the answer lies here, not with tall columns and high strengths. Columns are still allowed, but they generally give Tequilas with less pronounced character."]],"k":[["Si possono usare le colonne, ma le migliori Tequile sono distillate due volte in alambicco discontinuo.","Les colonnes sont permises, mais les meilleures Tequilas sont distillées deux fois en alambic à repasse.","Columns are allowed, but the best Tequilas are double distilled in pot stills."],["Gradazione di distillazione bassa = più profumi d'agave.","Degré de distillation bas = plus d'arômes d'agave.","Low distillation strength = more agave aroma."],["Risultato: distillato caratteriale, erbaceo e pepato.","Résultat : spiritueux de caractère, herbacé et poivré.","Result: a characterful, herbaceous, peppery spirit."]]},{"c":"s6","t":["Blanco, Joven, Reposado, Añejo","Blanco, Joven, Reposado, Añejo","Blanco, Joven, Reposado, Añejo"],"p":[["Dopo la distillazione il produttore decide se invecchiare la Tequila o lasciarla com'è. Le versioni non invecchiate sono due. La Blanco, chiamata anche Silver, è incolore ed è apprezzata perché esprime l'agave nel modo più puro. La Joven, detta anche Oro o Gold, ha un bel colore dorato ma non è passata in legno: il colore viene dal caramello, e altri additivi ne ammorbidiscono la consistenza.","Après la distillation, le producteur décide de vieillir la Tequila ou de la laisser telle quelle. Il existe deux versions non vieillies. La Blanco, aussi appelée Silver, est incolore et appréciée parce qu'elle exprime l'agave de la façon la plus pure. La Joven, dite aussi Oro ou Gold, a une jolie couleur dorée mais n'est pas passée en fût : sa couleur vient du caramel, et d'autres additifs adoucissent sa texture.","After distillation the producer decides whether to age the Tequila or leave it as it is. There are two unaged versions. Blanco, also called Silver, is colourless and prized for showing agave at its purest. Joven, also called Oro or Gold, has an attractive golden colour but has never seen a barrel: the colour comes from caramel, and other additives soften its texture."],["Le versioni invecchiate in rovere sono altre due. La Reposado («riposata») passa in legno da 2 a 12 mesi: ne esce più morbida, ma raramente il legno si fa sentire molto e i profumi d'agave restano intensi. La Añejo («vecchia») resta in botte almeno 12 mesi e unisce i profumi dell'agave a quelli del rovere, come vaniglia e spezie.","Les versions vieillies en fût de chêne sont au nombre de deux. La Reposado (« reposée ») passe de 2 à 12 mois en fût : elle en ressort plus souple, mais le bois se fait rarement très présent et les arômes d'agave restent intenses. L'Añejo (« vieille ») reste au moins 12 mois en fût et associe les arômes d'agave à ceux du chêne, comme la vanille et les épices.","There are also two oak-aged versions. Reposado (‘rested’) spends between 2 and 12 months in oak: it comes out softer, but the wood rarely shows strongly and the agave aromas stay pronounced. Añejo (‘aged’) spends at least 12 months in barrel and combines agave aromas with oak notes such as vanilla and spice."],["Perché le Tequile invecchiate restano in botte relativamente poco? Perché il produttore cerca un equilibrio: un po' di vaniglia e di spezia, senza coprire il carattere dell'agave che rende unica la Tequila. Le versioni invecchiate vengono poi assemblate e possono ricevere caramello per uniformare il colore, prima di essere diluite con acqua e imbottigliate.","Pourquoi les Tequilas vieillies restent-elles assez peu de temps en fût ? Parce que le producteur cherche un équilibre : un peu de vanille et d'épices, sans masquer le caractère de l'agave qui rend la Tequila unique. Les versions vieillies sont ensuite assemblées et peuvent recevoir du caramel pour harmoniser la couleur, avant d'être diluées à l'eau et mises en bouteille.","Why do aged Tequilas spend fairly little time in barrel? Because the producer is looking for balance: some vanilla and spice, without burying the agave character that makes Tequila unique. Aged versions are then blended and may receive caramel to even out the colour, before being diluted with water and bottled."]],"k":[["Blanco/Silver: non invecchiata, agave allo stato puro.","Blanco/Silver : non vieillie, l'agave à l'état pur.","Blanco/Silver: unaged, agave at its purest."],["Joven/Oro/Gold: non invecchiata, colorata con caramello.","Joven/Oro/Gold : non vieillie, colorée au caramel.","Joven/Oro/Gold: unaged, coloured with caramel."],["Reposado: da 2 a 12 mesi in rovere, più morbida, agave ancora protagonista.","Reposado : de 2 à 12 mois en chêne, plus souple, l'agave reste au premier plan.","Reposado: 2–12 months in oak, softer, agave still in the lead."],["Añejo: almeno 12 mesi in rovere, agave più legno.","Añejo : au moins 12 mois en chêne, agave et bois.","Añejo: at least 12 months in oak, agave plus oak."]]},{"c":"s7","t":["Tre modi per dare sapore a un distillato","Trois façons d'aromatiser un spiritueux","Three ways to flavour a spirit"],"p":[["Per i distillati aromatizzati il punto di partenza è diverso: il produttore di solito non coltiva né fermenta nulla, ma acquista un distillato già pronto. Nella grande maggioranza dei casi è lo stesso spirito neutro che, diluito con acqua, diventa vodka. Ogni tanto si parte invece da un rum, un whisky o un brandy. Il lavoro vero comincia dopo: aggiungere sapori diversi da quelli del legno.","Pour les spiritueux aromatisés, le point de départ est différent : le producteur ne cultive et ne fait généralement rien fermenter, il achète un spiritueux déjà prêt. Dans la grande majorité des cas, c'est le même alcool neutre qui, dilué à l'eau, devient de la vodka. Parfois, on part plutôt d'un rhum, d'un whisky ou d'un brandy. Le vrai travail commence ensuite : ajouter des saveurs autres que celles du bois.","With flavoured spirits the starting point is different: the producer usually grows and ferments nothing, but buys in a ready-made spirit. In the vast majority of cases it is the same neutral spirit that becomes vodka once diluted with water. Now and then the base is a rum, whisky or brandy instead. The real work starts afterwards: adding flavours other than those from oak."],["I migliori prodotti usano ingredienti naturali come frutta, semi, erbe e spezie, chiamati botanici. Il primo metodo è la ridistillazione: lo spirito neutro diluito e i botanici vanno insieme in un alambicco discontinuo e si distillano. Ne esce un distillato profumato e incolore. Il secondo è la macerazione: i botanici restano in infusione nello spirito, come una tisana a freddo, e cedono sapore e anche colore.","Les meilleurs produits utilisent des ingrédients naturels comme des fruits, des graines, des herbes et des épices, appelés botaniques. La première méthode est la redistillation : l'alcool neutre dilué et les botaniques passent ensemble dans un alambic à repasse. On obtient un spiritueux parfumé et incolore. La deuxième est la macération : les botaniques infusent dans l'alcool, comme une tisane à froid, et lui cèdent leur saveur et aussi leur couleur.","The best products use natural ingredients such as fruits, seeds, herbs and spices, known as botanicals. The first method is redistillation: diluted neutral spirit and botanicals go into a pot still together and are distilled. What comes out is fragrant and colourless. The second is maceration: the botanicals steep in the spirit, like a cold herbal tea, giving up flavour and colour too."],["La macerazione può durare pochi giorni o diversi mesi: più è lunga, più sapore si estrae, e un leggero riscaldamento accelera il processo. Il terzo metodo è il più semplice: aggiungere aromi acquistati già pronti, naturali o artificiali, molto concentrati, in piccole quantità. Di solito lo si sceglie per ragioni di costo, al posto dei botanici veri e propri.","La macération peut durer quelques jours ou plusieurs mois : plus elle est longue, plus on extrait de saveur, et un léger chauffage accélère le processus. La troisième méthode est la plus simple : ajouter des arômes achetés tout prêts, naturels ou artificiels, très concentrés, en petites quantités. On la choisit généralement pour des raisons de coût, à la place de vrais botaniques.","Maceration can last a few days or several months: the longer it goes on, the more flavour is drawn out, and gentle heating speeds things up. The third method is the simplest: adding bought-in flavourings, natural or artificial, which are very concentrated and used in small amounts. It is usually chosen for cost reasons, instead of real botanicals."]],"k":[["Base tipica: spirito neutro acquistato (a volte rum, whisky o brandy).","Base typique : alcool neutre acheté (parfois rhum, whisky ou brandy).","Typical base: bought-in neutral spirit (sometimes rum, whisky or brandy)."],["Botanici = frutta, semi, erbe e spezie.","Botaniques = fruits, graines, herbes et épices.","Botanicals = fruits, seeds, herbs and spices."],["Ridistillazione: aromatizzato e incolore. Macerazione: aromatizzato e colorato.","Redistillation : aromatisé et incolore. Macération : aromatisé et coloré.","Redistillation: flavoured and colourless. Maceration: flavoured and coloured."],["Aromi acquistati: concentrati, usati in piccole dosi, spesso per contenere i costi.","Arômes achetés : concentrés, en petites doses, souvent pour réduire les coûts.","Bought-in flavourings: concentrated, used in small doses, often to save cost."]]},{"c":"s7","t":["Vodka aromatizzata e gin","Vodka aromatisée et gin","Flavoured vodka and gin"],"p":[["La vodka aromatizzata è il caso più intuitivo: una base neutra a cui si dà un sapore preciso. Le possibilità sono tantissime: vaniglia, frutta come mela o limone, perfino spezie come il pepe. Quasi sempre i produttori aggiungono aromi acquistati alla loro vodka neutra, anche se qualcuno sceglie la ridistillazione. Il risultato è facile da riconoscere al naso: un solo aroma, netto e diretto.","La vodka aromatisée est le cas le plus intuitif : une base neutre à laquelle on donne une saveur précise. Les possibilités sont nombreuses : vanille, fruits comme la pomme ou le citron, et même des épices comme le poivre. Le plus souvent, les producteurs ajoutent des arômes achetés à leur vodka neutre, même si certains choisissent la redistillation. Le résultat se reconnaît facilement au nez : un arôme unique, net et direct.","Flavoured vodka is the most intuitive case: a neutral base given one clear flavour. The options are endless: vanilla, fruits such as apple or lemon, even spices like pepper. Most producers simply add bought-in flavourings to their neutral vodka, although some use redistillation. The result is easy to spot on the nose: one flavour, clean and direct."],["Il gin è un distillato aromatizzato con una regola fondamentale: il sapore dominante deve essere quello del ginepro, con le sue note resinose e di pino. Accanto al ginepro compaiono spesso semi di coriandolo, radice di angelica, radice di iris e scorza di agrumi. Di solito la base è uno spirito neutro, anche se negli Stati Uniti sono ammessi altri distillati. Il gin tipico è incolore e non invecchiato.","Le gin est un spiritueux aromatisé soumis à une règle essentielle : la saveur dominante doit être celle du genièvre, avec ses notes résineuses de pin. À côté du genièvre, on trouve souvent des graines de coriandre, de la racine d'angélique, de la racine d'iris et des zestes d'agrumes. La base est généralement un alcool neutre, même si d'autres spiritueux sont admis aux États-Unis. Le gin typique est incolore et non vieilli.","Gin is a flavoured spirit with one essential rule: juniper must be the leading flavour, with its resinous, piney notes. Alongside juniper you often find coriander seed, angelica root, orris root and citrus peel. The base is usually neutral spirit, although other distilled spirits are allowed in the USA. A typical gin is colourless and unaged."],["I gin migliori sono di solito ridistillati con i botanici, anche se alcuni aromi molto delicati vengono aggiunti dopo. Altri produttori aggiungono semplicemente aromi acquistati. In etichetta, la dicitura «London Dry Gin» indica che gli aromi sono stati dati durante la ridistillazione. Nonostante il nome, non indica un luogo: un London Dry Gin si può produrre in qualsiasi parte del mondo.","Les meilleurs gins sont en général redistillés avec les botaniques, même si certains arômes très délicats sont ajoutés après. D'autres producteurs se contentent d'ajouter des arômes achetés. Sur l'étiquette, la mention « London Dry Gin » indique que les arômes ont été apportés pendant la redistillation. Malgré son nom, elle n'indique aucun lieu : un London Dry Gin peut être produit n'importe où dans le monde.","The best gins are usually redistilled with their botanicals, although some very delicate flavours are added afterwards. Other producers simply add bought-in flavourings. On a label, ‘London Dry Gin’ means the flavours were added during redistillation. Despite the name, it is not a place: a London Dry Gin can be made anywhere in the world."]],"k":[["Vodka aromatizzata: base neutra + di solito aromi acquistati (a volte ridistillazione).","Vodka aromatisée : base neutre + le plus souvent arômes achetés (parfois redistillation).","Flavoured vodka: neutral base + usually bought-in flavourings (sometimes redistillation)."],["Gin: il ginepro deve dominare.","Gin : le genièvre doit dominer.","Gin: juniper must lead."],["Altri botanici classici: coriandolo, angelica, iris, scorza di agrumi.","Autres botaniques classiques : coriandre, angélique, iris, zestes d'agrumes.","Other classic botanicals: coriander, angelica, orris, citrus peel."],["London Dry = aromi dati in ridistillazione; si può fare ovunque.","London Dry = arômes apportés par redistillation ; peut se faire partout.","London Dry = flavours added by redistillation; can be made anywhere."]]},{"c":"s7","t":["Amari, bitter da cocktail e rum speziato","Amers, bitters à cocktail et rhum épicé","Bitter spirits, cocktail bitters and spiced rum"],"p":[["I distillati amari, come gli amari e i bitter da aperitivo, contengono almeno un botanico amaro: genziana, chinino o arancia amara, per esempio. Un dettaglio curioso: l'amaro si percepisce solo in bocca, perché il naso non sente l'amarezza. I profumi vengono dai botanici amari ma anche da molti altri ingredienti. Un tempo si bevevano a inizio o fine pasto; oggi finiscono soprattutto nei cocktail.","Les spiritueux amers contiennent au moins une botanique amère : gentiane, quinine ou orange amère, par exemple. Un détail curieux : l'amertume ne se perçoit qu'en bouche, car le nez ne la sent pas. Les arômes viennent des botaniques amères mais aussi de nombreux autres ingrédients. Autrefois, on les buvait en début ou en fin de repas ; aujourd'hui, ils servent surtout dans les cocktails.","Bitter spirits contain at least one bitter botanical, such as gentian, quinine or bitter orange. A curious detail: bitterness only shows up in the mouth, because the nose cannot detect it. The aromas come from the bitter botanicals but also from many other ingredients. These spirits were traditionally drunk before or after a meal; today they end up mostly in cocktails."],["I bitter da cocktail sono un'altra cosa: distillati molto concentrati e intensamente amari, che nessuno beve da soli. Si usano a gocce, poche spruzzate in un cocktail, per aggiungere complessità, un po' come il sale e il pepe in cucina. Una bottiglietta dura a lungo dietro al bancone proprio perché ne basta pochissimo.","Les bitters à cocktail sont autre chose : des spiritueux très concentrés et intensément amers, que personne ne boit seuls. On les utilise à la goutte, quelques traits dans un cocktail, pour ajouter de la complexité, un peu comme le sel et le poivre en cuisine. Un petit flacon dure longtemps derrière le comptoir, justement parce qu'il en faut très peu.","Cocktail bitters are something else: highly concentrated, intensely bitter spirits that nobody drinks on their own. They are used by the drop, a few dashes in a cocktail, to add complexity, rather like salt and pepper in cooking. A small bottle lasts a long time behind the bar precisely because so little is needed."],["Il rum speziato, infine, è una famiglia molto varia, sia per il rum di base sia per gli aromi aggiunti. Molti partono da un rum leggero e non invecchiato, che viene aromatizzato e colorato con caramello; solo pochi usano un rum invecchiato in rovere. Si impiegano sia botanici veri sia altri aromi. Quindi, attenzione: un colore ambrato non significa per forza anni di botte.","Le rhum épicé, enfin, est une famille très variée, tant pour le rhum de base que pour les arômes ajoutés. Beaucoup partent d'un rhum léger et non vieilli, aromatisé et coloré au caramel ; seuls quelques-uns utilisent un rhum vieilli en fût de chêne. On emploie à la fois de vraies botaniques et d'autres arômes. Attention donc : une couleur ambrée ne signifie pas forcément des années de fût.","Spiced rum, finally, is a very varied family, both in its base rum and in the flavourings added. Many start from a light, unaged rum that is flavoured and coloured with caramel; only a handful use an oak-aged rum. Both real botanicals and other flavourings are used. So be careful: an amber colour does not necessarily mean years in a barrel."]],"k":[["Distillati amari: almeno un botanico amaro (genziana, chinino, arancia amara).","Spiritueux amers : au moins une botanique amère (gentiane, quinine, orange amère).","Bitter spirits: at least one bitter botanical (gentian, quinine, bitter orange)."],["L'amaro si sente solo in bocca, non al naso.","L'amertume se perçoit seulement en bouche, pas au nez.","Bitterness is felt only on the palate, not the nose."],["Bitter da cocktail: concentratissimi, mai bevuti da soli, usati a gocce.","Bitters à cocktail : très concentrés, jamais bus seuls, utilisés à la goutte.","Cocktail bitters: very concentrated, never drunk alone, used in dashes."],["Rum speziato: spesso rum leggero non invecchiato + aromi + caramello.","Rhum épicé : souvent rhum léger non vieilli + arômes + caramel.","Spiced rum: often light unaged rum + flavourings + caramel."]]},{"c":"s7","t":["Liquori: aromatizzati e dolci","Liqueurs : aromatisées et sucrées","Liqueurs: flavoured and sweet"],"p":[["Un liquore è un distillato aromatizzato a cui è stato aggiunto anche zucchero. È questa la differenza chiave rispetto a un gin o a una vodka aromatizzata, che restano secchi. Lo zucchero si aggiunge dopo l'aromatizzazione e la legge impone un livello minimo di dolcezza: senza raggiungerlo, un prodotto non può chiamarsi liquore.","Une liqueur est un spiritueux aromatisé auquel on a aussi ajouté du sucre. C'est la différence essentielle avec un gin ou une vodka aromatisée, qui restent secs. Le sucre est ajouté après l'aromatisation, et la loi impose un niveau minimal de douceur : sans l'atteindre, un produit ne peut pas s'appeler liqueur.","A liqueur is a flavoured spirit that has also been sweetened. That is the key difference from a gin or a flavoured vodka, which stay dry. Sugar goes in after the flavouring, and the law sets a minimum level of sweetness: without reaching it, a product cannot be called a liqueur."],["La maggior parte dei liquori nasce da uno spirito neutro, ma alcuni partono da distillati con più carattere, come brandy, rum o whisky. Per il resto la libertà è quasi totale: qualsiasi sapore e qualsiasi metodo per aggiungerlo. Si va dagli agrumi al caffè, dalle erbe alle nocciole. Esiste persino un ingrediente sorprendente in alcuni liquori: la panna, che dà una consistenza morbida e vellutata.","La plupart des liqueurs sont faites à partir d'un alcool neutre, mais certaines partent de spiritueux plus caractérisés, comme le brandy, le rhum ou le whisky. Pour le reste, la liberté est presque totale : n'importe quelle saveur et n'importe quelle méthode pour l'apporter. On va des agrumes au café, des herbes aux noisettes. Certaines liqueurs contiennent même un ingrédient surprenant : la crème, qui leur donne une texture douce et veloutée.","Most liqueurs are made from neutral spirit, but some start from more characterful spirits such as brandy, rum or whisky. Beyond that, freedom is almost complete: any flavour and any method of adding it. Think citrus or coffee, herbs or hazelnuts. Some liqueurs even contain a surprising ingredient: cream, which gives them a soft, velvety texture."],["Molti liquori sono anche colorati. Il colore naturale ottenuto con la macerazione è bello ma tende a sbiadire in fretta, così è diffuso l'uso di coloranti artificiali, più stabili. Offrono inoltre una gamma di tinte molto più ampia: ecco perché sugli scaffali si vedono liquori verde brillante, blu elettrico o rosso acceso.","Beaucoup de liqueurs sont aussi colorées. La couleur naturelle obtenue par macération est belle mais a tendance à pâlir vite : on utilise donc largement des colorants artificiels, plus stables. Ils offrent en plus une gamme de teintes bien plus large : voilà pourquoi on voit en rayon des liqueurs vert vif, bleu électrique ou rouge éclatant.","Many liqueurs are coloured as well. Natural colour from maceration is attractive but tends to fade quickly, so artificial colourings, which are more stable, are widely used. They also offer a much wider range of shades, which is why shelves show liqueurs in bright green, electric blue or vivid red."]],"k":[["Liquore = distillato aromatizzato + zucchero.","Liqueur = spiritueux aromatisé + sucre.","Liqueur = flavoured spirit + sugar."],["La legge impone una dolcezza minima.","La loi impose une douceur minimale.","The law requires a minimum sweetness."],["Base neutra o con carattere; qualsiasi sapore, anche la panna.","Base neutre ou de caractère ; toute saveur, même la crème.","Neutral or characterful base; any flavour, even cream."],["Coloranti artificiali: colore stabile e tinte più vivaci.","Colorants artificiels : couleur stable et teintes plus vives.","Artificial colours: stable colour and brighter shades."]]},{"c":"s8","t":["I quattro ingredienti di un vino aromatizzato","Les quatre composants d'un vin aromatisé","The four building blocks of an aromatised wine"],"p":[["I vini aromatizzati non sono distillati, ma si trovano su ogni bancone perché nei cocktail sono preziosi: in un solo ingrediente portano dolcezza, amaro e acidità. La categoria è varia, eppure la ricetta di base è sempre la stessa. Ci sono quattro componenti: un vino di base, degli aromi che includono sempre qualcosa di amaro, dello zucchero e un po' di distillato. A volte si aggiunge anche caramello.","Les vins aromatisés ne sont pas des spiritueux, mais on les trouve dans tous les bars, car ils sont précieux en cocktail : en un seul ingrédient, ils apportent douceur, amertume et acidité. La catégorie est variée, et pourtant la recette de base reste la même. Il y a quatre composants : un vin de base, des arômes qui comprennent toujours quelque chose d'amer, du sucre et un peu de spiritueux. On ajoute parfois du caramel.","Aromatised wines are not spirits, yet every bar has them because they are so useful in cocktails: a single ingredient brings sweetness, bitterness and acidity. The category is varied, but the basic recipe never changes. There are four components: a base wine, flavourings that always include something bitter, sugar and a little spirit. Caramel is sometimes added too."],["Il vino di base è quasi sempre bianco, spesso piuttosto neutro, così da fare da tela per gli aromi aggiunti; alcuni produttori scelgono invece vini aromatici e li bilanciano con la ricetta, e c'è chi usa vino rosso o rosato. Gli aromi si aggiungono direttamente al vino o sotto forma di distillati aromatizzati. Le ricette cambiano molto, ma tutte contengono botanici amari come assenzio, genziana o chinino.","Le vin de base est presque toujours blanc, souvent assez neutre, pour servir de toile de fond aux arômes ajoutés ; certains producteurs choisissent au contraire des vins aromatiques qu'ils équilibrent avec leur recette, et d'autres utilisent du vin rouge ou rosé. Les arômes sont ajoutés directement au vin ou sous forme de spiritueux aromatisés. Les recettes varient beaucoup, mais toutes contiennent des botaniques amères comme l'absinthe, la gentiane ou la quinine.","The base wine is nearly always white, often fairly neutral, so it works as a blank canvas for the added flavours; some producers prefer aromatic wines and balance them with their recipe, and some use red or rosé wine. Flavourings go straight into the wine or are added as flavoured spirits. Recipes vary a lot, but all of them include bitter botanicals such as wormwood, gentian or quinine."],["Il distillato, quasi sempre neutro, si aggiunge in piccola quantità per alzare la gradazione e far durare di più il prodotto, soprattutto dopo l'apertura della bottiglia. Quasi nessun vino aromatizzato è del tutto secco: la dolcezza può venire dal vino stesso o dallo zucchero aggiunto. Il caramello, facoltativo, serve a colorare; nei prodotti rossi fatti con vino bianco può anche dare note di caramello.","Le spiritueux, presque toujours neutre, est ajouté en petite quantité pour relever le degré et prolonger la durée de conservation, surtout une fois la bouteille ouverte. Presque aucun vin aromatisé n'est complètement sec : la douceur peut venir du vin lui-même ou du sucre ajouté. Le caramel, facultatif, sert à colorer ; dans les produits rouges élaborés avec du vin blanc, il peut aussi apporter des notes de caramel.","The spirit, nearly always neutral, is added in a small amount to raise the alcohol and give the product a longer life, especially once the bottle is open. Almost no aromatised wine is fully dry: sweetness can come from the wine itself or from added sugar. Caramel is optional and used for colour; in red products made from white wine it can also add caramel notes."]],"k":[["Quattro componenti: vino di base, aromi con un elemento amaro, zucchero, distillato.","Quatre composants : vin de base, arômes avec un élément amer, sucre, spiritueux.","Four components: base wine, flavourings with something bitter, sugar, spirit."],["Vino di base di solito bianco e piuttosto neutro.","Vin de base généralement blanc et assez neutre.","Base wine usually white and fairly neutral."],["Il distillato (di solito neutro) alza la gradazione e allunga la conservazione.","Le spiritueux (souvent neutre) relève le degré et prolonge la conservation.","The spirit (usually neutral) raises alcohol and extends shelf life."],["Quasi mai del tutto secchi; caramello facoltativo per il colore.","Presque jamais complètement secs ; caramel facultatif pour la couleur.","Almost never fully dry; caramel optional for colour."]]},{"c":"s8","t":["Il vermut","Le vermouth","Vermouth"],"p":[["I vini aromatizzati si possono produrre ovunque nel mondo, ma le zone più celebri sono due: il sud-est della Francia e il nord-ovest dell'Italia. In entrambi i paesi il tipo più diffuso è il vermut. Due regole lo definiscono: nasce da un vino bianco e deve essere aromatizzato con l'assenzio, un botanico dal gusto decisamente amaro.","Les vins aromatisés peuvent être produits partout dans le monde, mais deux zones sont particulièrement célèbres : le sud-est de la France et le nord-ouest de l'Italie. Dans ces deux pays, le type le plus répandu est le vermouth. Deux règles le définissent : il est élaboré à partir d'un vin blanc et doit être aromatisé à l'absinthe, une botanique à l'amertume prononcée.","Aromatised wines can be made anywhere in the world, but two areas are especially famous: south-east France and north-west Italy. In both countries the most widely made type is vermouth. Two rules define it: it is made from a white wine base, and it must be flavoured with wormwood, a botanical with a strongly bitter taste."],["Attenzione alle etichette: un vermut «dry» (secco) contiene quasi sempre zucchero aggiunto, anche se in quantità minore. I vermut rossi, invece, sono in genere molto zuccherati. E il loro colore? Visto che la base è un vino bianco, la tinta rossa arriva di solito dal caramello, che può aggiungere anche un leggero profumo di caramello.","Attention aux étiquettes : un vermouth « dry » (sec) contient presque toujours du sucre ajouté, même en plus petite quantité. Les vermouths rouges, eux, sont en général très sucrés. Et leur couleur ? Comme la base est un vin blanc, la teinte rouge vient généralement du caramel, qui peut aussi apporter une légère note de caramel.","Watch the labels: a vermouth marked ‘dry’ nearly always contains added sugar, just less of it. Red vermouths, on the other hand, are usually heavily sweetened. And their colour? Since the base is a white wine, the red shade usually comes from caramel, which can also add a light caramel aroma."],["Dietro al bancone il vermut è un vero jolly. Un vermut secco può asciugare e profumare un drink a base di gin, mentre uno rosso, dolce e amaricante, arrotonda un cocktail a base di whiskey. In entrambi i casi fa lo stesso lavoro: bilancia dolcezza, amaro e acidità in un solo gesto. Ecco perché conviene conoscerne bene stile e dolcezza prima di usarlo.","Derrière le comptoir, le vermouth est un vrai joker. Un vermouth sec peut assécher et parfumer une boisson à base de gin, tandis qu'un rouge, sucré et légèrement amer, arrondit un cocktail à base de whiskey. Dans les deux cas, il fait le même travail : équilibrer douceur, amertume et acidité en un seul geste. D'où l'intérêt de bien connaître son style et sa douceur avant de l'utiliser.","Behind the bar, vermouth is a real all-rounder. A dry vermouth can add dryness and perfume to a gin-based drink, while a red one, sweet with a bitter edge, rounds out a whiskey cocktail. Either way it does the same job: balancing sweetness, bitterness and acidity in one pour. That is why it pays to know its style and sweetness before reaching for the bottle."]],"k":[["Zone più note: sud-est della Francia e nord-ovest dell'Italia.","Zones les plus connues : sud-est de la France et nord-ouest de l'Italie.","Best-known areas: south-east France and north-west Italy."],["Vermut = vino bianco di base + assenzio obbligatorio.","Vermouth = vin blanc de base + absinthe obligatoire.","Vermouth = white wine base + wormwood, by rule."],["Anche il «dry» ha quasi sempre zucchero; il rosso è molto dolce.","Même le « dry » contient presque toujours du sucre ; le rouge est très sucré.","Even ‘dry’ nearly always has sugar; red is very sweet."],["Il colore del vermut rosso viene di solito dal caramello.","La couleur du vermouth rouge vient généralement du caramel.","Red vermouth usually gets its colour from caramel."]]},{"c":"t1","t":["Preparare il posto e il bicchiere","Préparer le lieu et le verre","Setting the scene and choosing the glass"],"p":[["Degustare un distillato significa osservarlo con attenzione, e per farlo bene serve un metodo da ripetere sempre allo stesso modo. Se ogni campione viene trattato nello stesso modo, le note scritte oggi si potranno confrontare con quelle di domani. Prima ancora di versare, però, conviene sistemare l'ambiente: un buon assaggio dipende tanto da ciò che c'è intorno al bicchiere quanto dal liquido che contiene.","Déguster un spiritueux, c'est l'observer avec attention, et pour bien le faire il faut une méthode que l'on répète toujours de la même façon. Si chaque échantillon est traité de manière identique, les notes prises aujourd'hui pourront être comparées à celles de demain. Avant même de servir, il vaut mieux préparer l'environnement : une bonne dégustation dépend autant de ce qui entoure le verre que du liquide qu'il contient.","Tasting a spirit means looking at it closely, and doing that well needs a method you repeat the same way every time. If every sample is treated identically, the notes you write today can be compared with the ones you write next month. Before pouring anything, though, it pays to prepare the setting: a good tasting depends as much on what surrounds the glass as on the liquid inside it."],["La stanza deve essere libera da odori che distraggono: niente profumi forti, cucina o candele. Serve buona luce naturale e una superficie bianca, come un foglio o una tovaglia, su cui tenere il bicchiere per giudicarne il colore senza riflessi ingannevoli. Anche chi assaggia ha la sua parte: bocca pulita, senza il ricordo di dentifricio o caffè, e il corpo ben idratato.","La pièce doit être libre de toute odeur parasite : pas de parfum puissant, de cuisine ni de bougie. Il faut une bonne lumière naturelle et une surface blanche, une feuille ou une nappe, sur laquelle poser le verre pour juger la couleur sans reflets trompeurs. La personne qui déguste compte aussi : une bouche propre, sans trace de dentifrice ou de café, et un corps bien hydraté.","The room should be free of distracting smells: no strong perfume, cooking or scented candles. You need good natural light and a white surface, such as a sheet of paper or a tablecloth, to hold the glass against so the colour can be judged without misleading reflections. The taster matters too: a clean palate with no lingering toothpaste or coffee, and a well-hydrated body."],["Poi c'è il bicchiere. La forma ideale ha una coppa ampia che si stringe verso l'alto, un po' come un tulipano. La parte larga lascia spazio agli aromi per liberarsi, mentre l'apertura più stretta li raccoglie e li porta dritti al naso. Con un bicchiere dritto e largo, invece, i profumi si disperdono nell'aria e il distillato sembra meno espressivo di quanto sia davvero.","Vient ensuite le verre. La forme idéale présente un large calice qui se resserre vers le haut, un peu comme une tulipe. La partie large laisse aux arômes la place de se libérer, tandis que l'ouverture plus étroite les rassemble et les conduit droit vers le nez. Avec un verre droit et évasé, au contraire, les parfums se dispersent et le spiritueux paraît moins expressif qu'il ne l'est vraiment.","Then comes the glass. The ideal shape has a wide bowl that narrows towards the rim, a little like a tulip. The wide part gives the aromas room to rise, while the narrower opening gathers them and channels them straight to your nose. In a straight, open tumbler, by contrast, the scents drift away and the spirit seems less expressive than it really is."]],"k":[["Un metodo sempre uguale rende le note confrontabili nel tempo.","Une méthode toujours identique rend les notes comparables dans le temps.","A consistent method makes your notes comparable over time."],["Stanza senza odori, luce naturale e superficie bianca per il colore.","Pièce sans odeurs, lumière naturelle et surface blanche pour la couleur.","No stray smells, natural light and a white surface for colour."],["Bocca pulita (niente dentifricio o caffè) e buona idratazione.","Bouche propre (ni dentifrice ni café) et bonne hydratation.","A clean palate (no toothpaste or coffee) and good hydration."],["Bicchiere a coppa ampia che si stringe in alto: concentra gli aromi.","Verre à large calice resserré en haut : il concentre les arômes.","A wide bowl narrowing at the top concentrates the aromas."]]},{"c":"t1","t":["Il metodo passo dopo passo","La méthode pas à pas","The method step by step"],"p":[["Anche se il produttore lo ha già diluito prima dell'imbottigliamento, un distillato resta una bevanda molto forte. A 40% vol l'alcol punge il naso e scalda la bocca, coprendo molte sfumature. Per questo si lavora con un campione piccolo, circa 1,5 cL, cioè più o meno un cucchiaio. Bastano poche gocce per avere tutto ciò che serve, senza stancare i sensi.","Même si le producteur l'a déjà dilué avant la mise en bouteille, un spiritueux reste une boisson très forte. À 40 % vol, l'alcool pique le nez et chauffe la bouche, masquant beaucoup de nuances. On travaille donc avec un petit échantillon, environ 1,5 cL, soit à peu près une cuillère à soupe. Cela suffit largement, sans fatiguer les sens.","Even though the distiller has already diluted it before bottling, a spirit is still a very strong drink. At 40% abv the alcohol stings the nose and warms the mouth, hiding many details. That is why you work with a small sample of about 1.5 cL, roughly a tablespoon. It gives you everything you need without tiring your senses."],["Il percorso è semplice. Prima si guarda il campione e lo si annusa così com'è. Poi si aggiunge la stessa quantità d'acqua, altri 1,5 cL, così il liquido si dimezza di forza. Si annusa di nuovo: spesso compaiono profumi che prima l'alcol nascondeva, come quando si apre una finestra in una stanza affollata. Solo a questo punto si passa all'assaggio.","Le parcours est simple. On regarde d'abord l'échantillon et on le sent tel quel. On ajoute ensuite la même quantité d'eau, soit 1,5 cL de plus, ce qui divise sa force par deux. On sent à nouveau : des arômes que l'alcool cachait apparaissent souvent, comme lorsqu'on ouvre une fenêtre dans une pièce bondée. Ce n'est qu'alors que l'on passe à la bouche.","The route is simple. First you look at the sample and smell it neat. Then you add the same amount of water, another 1.5 cL, which halves its strength. You smell again: aromas the alcohol was hiding often appear, like opening a window in a crowded room. Only then do you move on to tasting."],["In bocca si fa girare il liquido per qualche secondo, si cercano i sapori e poi lo si sputa. Sputare non è scortesia: è ciò che permette di assaggiare più campioni restando lucidi e di giudicare l'ultimo con la stessa attenzione del primo. Riassumendo: poco campione, occhio e naso, acqua in pari quantità, di nuovo naso, bocca, sputare.","En bouche, on fait tourner le liquide quelques secondes, on cherche les saveurs, puis on recrache. Recracher n'a rien d'impoli : c'est ce qui permet de goûter plusieurs échantillons en gardant les idées claires et de juger le dernier avec autant de soin que le premier. En résumé : un petit échantillon, l'œil et le nez, autant d'eau, à nouveau le nez, la bouche, recracher.","In the mouth, you roll the liquid around for a few seconds, look for the flavours and then spit it out. Spitting is not rude: it lets you taste several samples while staying clear-headed and judge the last one as carefully as the first. In short: small sample, eyes and nose, equal water, nose again, palate, spit."]],"k":[["Campione piccolo: circa 1,5 cL.","Petit échantillon : environ 1,5 cL.","Small sample: about 1.5 cL."],["Si guarda e si annusa prima di aggiungere acqua.","On regarde et on sent avant d'ajouter de l'eau.","Look and smell before adding any water."],["Si aggiunge la stessa quantità d'acqua, poi si annusa di nuovo.","On ajoute autant d'eau, puis on sent à nouveau.","Add an equal amount of water, then smell again."],["Si assaggia e poi si sputa.","On goûte puis on recrache.","Taste, then spit."]]},{"c":"t1","t":["Che cosa annotare","Que noter","What to write down"],"p":[["Le note seguono l'ordine dell'assaggio: occhio, naso, bocca. Per l'aspetto basta il colore. Molti distillati non invecchiati sono incolori, mentre quelli passati in legno vanno dal giallo limone all'oro, all'ambra fino al marrone. Alcuni prodotti aromatizzati, soprattutto i liquori, possono avere tinte vivaci: rosa, rosso, verde, blu, perfino nero. Il colore è un primo indizio, non una prova.","Les notes suivent l'ordre de la dégustation : l'œil, le nez, la bouche. Pour l'aspect, la couleur suffit. Beaucoup de spiritueux non vieillis sont incolores, tandis que ceux passés en bois vont du jaune citron à l'or, à l'ambre puis au brun. Certains produits aromatisés, surtout les liqueurs, peuvent afficher des teintes vives : rose, rouge, vert, bleu, voire noir. La couleur est un premier indice, pas une preuve.","Your notes follow the order of the tasting: eyes, nose, palate. For appearance, colour is all you need. Many unaged spirits are colourless, while those that have spent time in wood range from lemon to gold, amber and brown. Some flavoured products, especially liqueurs, can be vivid: pink, red, green, blue, even black. Colour is a first clue, not proof."],["Al naso si giudica prima l'intensità: un distillato può essere neutro, quasi senza profumo come molte vodka, oppure leggero, medio o pronunciato. Poi si descrivono gli aromi raggruppandoli per origine: quelli della materia prima, come frutta o cereali; quelli dovuti alla lavorazione; quelli del legno e dell'invecchiamento, come vaniglia, spezie o note tostate. Chiedersi «da dove viene questo profumo?» aiuta a ordinare le idee.","Au nez, on juge d'abord l'intensité : un spiritueux peut être neutre, presque sans odeur comme beaucoup de vodkas, ou bien léger, moyen ou prononcé. On décrit ensuite les arômes en les classant par origine : ceux de la matière première, comme le fruit ou la céréale ; ceux qui viennent de l'élaboration ; ceux du bois et du vieillissement, comme la vanille, les épices ou le grillé. Se demander « d'où vient cette odeur ? » aide à mettre de l'ordre.","On the nose, you first judge intensity: a spirit can be neutral, with almost no smell like many vodkas, or light, medium or pronounced. Then you describe the aromas grouped by where they come from: the raw material, such as fruit or grain; the way it was made; and the oak and maturation, such as vanilla, spice or toasty notes. Asking 'where does this smell come from?' helps you sort your thoughts."],["In bocca si ritrovano gli stessi gruppi di sapori, più due osservazioni utili: quanto zucchero si percepisce e che consistenza ha il liquido, se scorrevole o più ricco. Dopo aver sputato si misura il finale, cioè quanto a lungo restano i sapori: corto, medio o lungo. Infine si dà un giudizio sulla complessità, da neutro a semplice, fino a molto complesso quando i sapori sono tanti e cambiano.","En bouche, on retrouve les mêmes familles de saveurs, plus deux observations utiles : le niveau de sucre perçu et la texture du liquide, fluide ou plus riche. Après avoir recraché, on mesure la finale, c'est-à-dire combien de temps les saveurs persistent : courte, moyenne ou longue. Enfin, on juge la complexité, de neutre à simple, jusqu'à très complexe lorsque les saveurs sont nombreuses et évoluent.","On the palate you find the same groups of flavours, plus two useful observations: how much sugar you can sense and what the texture is like, thin or richer. After spitting, you measure the finish, meaning how long the flavours linger: short, medium or long. Finally, you judge complexity, from neutral to simple, up to very complex when there are many flavours that keep changing."]],"k":[["Aspetto: il colore, da incolore a marrone, o tinte vivaci nei prodotti aromatizzati.","Aspect : la couleur, d'incolore à brun, ou des teintes vives pour les produits aromatisés.","Appearance: colour, from colourless to brown, or vivid shades in flavoured products."],["Naso: intensità (neutro, leggero, medio, pronunciato) e aromi per origine.","Nez : intensité (neutre, léger, moyen, prononcé) et arômes par origine.","Nose: intensity (neutral, light, medium, pronounced) and aromas by source."],["Origini degli aromi: materia prima, lavorazione, legno e invecchiamento.","Origines des arômes : matière première, élaboration, bois et vieillissement.","Aroma sources: raw material, processing, oak and maturation."],["Bocca: sapori, zucchero, consistenza; poi finale (corto, medio, lungo) e complessità.","Bouche : saveurs, sucre, texture ; puis finale (courte, moyenne, longue) et complexité.","Palate: flavours, sugar, texture; then finish (short, medium, long) and complexity."]]},{"c":"t2","t":["Forte contro leggero","Fort contre léger","Strong versus weak"],"p":[["Buoni ingredienti e strumenti giusti aiutano, ma ciò che trasforma un cocktail discreto in uno memorabile è l'equilibrio. Si può immaginarlo come due bilance. La prima mette su un piatto la parte forte e sull'altro quella leggera; la seconda mette il dolce contro l'amaro e l'acido. Insieme formano quattro punti di equilibrio, e ogni cocktail classico è costruito proprio su questi quattro elementi.","De bons ingrédients et les bons outils aident, mais ce qui transforme un cocktail correct en un cocktail mémorable, c'est l'équilibre. On peut l'imaginer comme deux balances. La première place le fort d'un côté et le léger de l'autre ; la seconde oppose le sucré à l'amer et à l'acide. Ensemble, elles donnent quatre points d'équilibre, et chaque cocktail classique est construit sur ces quatre éléments.","Good ingredients and the right tools help, but what turns a decent cocktail into a memorable one is balance. Picture two sets of scales. The first weighs the strong part against the weak part; the second weighs sweet against bitter and sour. Together they give four points of balance, and every classic cocktail is built from exactly these four elements."],["La parte forte è il distillato di base, di solito al 40% vol o più. È il cuore del gusto: in un Daiquiri è il rum, in un Martini è il gin. Cambiare distillato cambia il cocktail. Anche passare a un altro prodotto della stessa categoria modifica il risultato, e sostituire del tutto la base crea una variante, come un Old Fashioned fatto con il rum invece che con il whiskey.","Le fort, c'est le spiritueux de base, en général à 40 % vol ou plus. C'est le cœur du goût : dans un Daiquiri, c'est le rhum ; dans un Martini, le gin. Changer de spiritueux change le cocktail. Même passer à un autre produit de la même catégorie modifie le résultat, et remplacer complètement la base crée une variante, comme un Old Fashioned au rhum au lieu du whiskey.","The strong part is the base spirit, usually 40% abv or more. It is the heart of the flavour: rum in a Daiquiri, gin in a Martini. Change the spirit and you change the drink. Even switching to another product from the same category alters the result, and replacing the base entirely creates a variation, such as an Old Fashioned made with rum instead of whiskey."],["La parte leggera ammorbidisce la forza dell'alcol. Una fonte c'è sempre: il ghiaccio, che fondendo un po' mentre si mescola o si shakera aggiunge acqua. Altre sono facoltative e analcoliche: succhi di frutta, panna o latte, bibite gassate, acqua gassata, acqua tonica. Pensate a un gin tonic: il gin è la parte forte, la tonica e il ghiaccio fanno da contrappeso.","Le léger adoucit la force de l'alcool. Une source est toujours présente : la glace, qui fond un peu quand on remue ou que l'on secoue, et apporte de l'eau. D'autres sont facultatives et sans alcool : jus de fruits, crème ou lait, sodas, eau gazeuse, tonic. Pensez à un gin tonic : le gin est le fort, le tonic et la glace font contrepoids.","The weak part softens the power of the alcohol. One source is always there: ice, which melts a little as you stir or shake and adds water. Others are optional and non-alcoholic: fruit juices, cream or milk, sodas, club soda and tonic. Think of a gin and tonic: the gin is the strong part, and the tonic and ice balance it."]],"k":[["Due bilance: forte contro leggero, dolce contro amaro e/o acido.","Deux balances : fort contre léger, sucré contre amer et/ou acide.","Two scales: strong vs weak, and sweet vs bitter and/or sour."],["Forte = distillato di base, di solito 40% vol o più.","Fort = spiritueux de base, en général 40 % vol ou plus.","Strong = the base spirit, usually 40% abv or more."],["Leggero = diluizione del ghiaccio più succhi, latticini, bibite o tonica.","Léger = dilution par la glace, plus jus, produits laitiers, sodas ou tonic.","Weak = dilution from ice, plus juices, dairy, sodas or tonic."],["Cambiare il distillato di base crea una variante del cocktail.","Changer le spiritueux de base crée une variante du cocktail.","Swapping the base spirit creates a variation of the drink."]]},{"c":"t2","t":["Dolce contro amaro e acido","Sucré contre amer et acide","Sweet versus bitter and sour"],"p":[["Molti cocktail vengono prima addolciti e poi «condizionati» con un altro ingrediente, chiamato modificatore, che porta una nota amara, acida o entrambe. Il dolce può arrivare in varie forme: zucchero, sciroppo semplice, cioè zucchero sciolto in acqua, oppure un liquore. La dolcezza arrotonda e lega, ma da sola stanca: un cocktail troppo dolce risulta stucchevole e pesante.","Beaucoup de cocktails sont d'abord sucrés puis « assaisonnés » avec un autre ingrédient, appelé modificateur, qui apporte une note amère, acide ou les deux. Le sucré peut prendre plusieurs formes : sucre, sirop simple, c'est-à-dire du sucre dissous dans l'eau, ou une liqueur. La douceur arrondit et lie, mais seule elle lasse : un cocktail trop sucré devient écœurant et lourd.","Many cocktails are first sweetened and then 'seasoned' with another ingredient, called a modifier, which brings a bitter note, a sour note or both. Sweetness can come in several forms: sugar, simple syrup (sugar dissolved in water) or a liqueur. Sweetness rounds things off and binds them together, but on its own it tires the palate: a cocktail that is too sweet tastes cloying and heavy."],["Il contrappeso è l'acidità o l'amaro. L'acido arriva soprattutto dagli agrumi: un po' di succo di lime o di limone rende il sorso vivace. L'amaro arriva in modo evidente dai bitter da cocktail, usati a gocce, ma anche da distillati amari. È come in cucina: un pizzico di sale o una spruzzata di limone fanno risaltare un piatto che sembrava piatto.","Le contrepoids, c'est l'acidité ou l'amertume. L'acide vient surtout des agrumes : un peu de jus de citron vert ou jaune rend la gorgée vive. L'amer vient très nettement des bitters à cocktail, utilisés en quelques gouttes, mais aussi des spiritueux amers. C'est comme en cuisine : une pincée de sel ou un trait de citron réveillent un plat qui semblait fade.","The counterweight is acidity or bitterness. Sourness comes mainly from citrus: a little lime or lemon juice makes the sip lively. Bitterness comes most obviously from cocktail bitters, used by the dash, but also from bitter spirits. It is just like cooking: a pinch of salt or a squeeze of lemon lifts a dish that seemed flat."],["Un singolo ingrediente può giocare più ruoli. I vini aromatizzati, come il vermouth, portano insieme dolcezza, amaro e acidità; un liquore porta alcol e dolcezza. L'obiettivo finale è un insieme coeso, in cui nessuna parte prevale sulle altre: se il cocktail sa solo di zucchero, di limone o di alcol, l'equilibrio non c'è ancora.","Un même ingrédient peut jouer plusieurs rôles. Les vins aromatisés, comme le vermouth, apportent à la fois douceur, amertume et acidité ; une liqueur apporte de l'alcool et du sucre. Le but est un ensemble cohérent, où aucun élément ne domine les autres : si le cocktail ne goûte que le sucre, le citron ou l'alcool, l'équilibre n'est pas encore atteint.","A single ingredient can play several roles. Aromatised wines such as vermouth bring sweetness, bitterness and acidity all at once; a liqueur brings both alcohol and sweetness. The goal is a cohesive whole in which no part dominates the others: if the drink tastes only of sugar, lemon or alcohol, it is not balanced yet."]],"k":[["Il dolce viene da zucchero, sciroppo semplice o liquori.","Le sucré vient du sucre, du sirop simple ou des liqueurs.","Sweetness comes from sugar, simple syrup or liqueurs."],["Troppo dolce = stucchevole.","Trop sucré = écœurant.","Too sweet = cloying."],["Il modificatore porta acido (agrumi) e/o amaro (bitter).","Le modificateur apporte de l'acide (agrumes) et/ou de l'amer (bitters).","The modifier brings sour (citrus) and/or bitter (bitters)."],["I vini aromatizzati possono dare dolce, amaro e acido insieme.","Les vins aromatisés peuvent apporter sucré, amer et acide à la fois.","Aromatised wines can add sweet, bitter and sour at once."]]},{"c":"t2","t":["Drink corti e drink lunghi","Short drinks et long drinks","Short drinks and long drinks"],"p":[["Centinaia di cocktail possono sembrare un labirinto, ma basta una prima divisione per orientarsi: drink corti e drink lunghi. I drink corti hanno pochi ingredienti e un volume ridotto. La loro parte leggera viene quasi solo dall'acqua che il ghiaccio rilascia mentre si mescola o si shakera; poi vengono serviti in un bicchiere piccolo, concentrati e intensi.","Des centaines de cocktails peuvent ressembler à un labyrinthe, mais une première division suffit pour s'orienter : les short drinks et les long drinks. Les short drinks comptent peu d'ingrédients et un petit volume. Leur partie légère vient presque uniquement de l'eau que libère la glace quand on remue ou que l'on secoue ; ils sont ensuite servis dans un petit verre, concentrés et intenses.","Hundreds of cocktails can look like a maze, but one first split is enough to find your way: short drinks and long drinks. Short drinks have few ingredients and a small volume. Their weak part comes almost entirely from the water released by ice while stirring or shaking; they are then served in a small glass, concentrated and intense."],["Tra i drink corti ci sono due famiglie. I cocktail «spirit-forward», dove domina il distillato, come il Manhattan, e i sour corti, che uniscono distillato, agrumi e dolce, come il Daiquiri. I drink lunghi, invece, hanno un volume maggiore: la parte leggera arriva da bibite gassate, succhi, latticini o altre bevande analcoliche. Qui si trovano gli highball e i sour lunghi.","Parmi les short drinks, on trouve deux familles : les cocktails « spirit-forward », où le spiritueux domine, comme le Manhattan, et les sours courts, qui associent spiritueux, agrumes et sucré, comme le Daiquiri. Les long drinks, eux, ont un volume plus important : leur partie légère vient de sodas, de jus, de produits laitiers ou d'autres boissons sans alcool. On y trouve les highballs et les sours longs.","Short drinks include two families: spirit-forward cocktails, where the spirit leads, such as the Manhattan, and short sours, which combine spirit, citrus and sweetness, such as the Daiquiri. Long drinks have a larger volume: their weak part comes from sodas, juices, dairy or other non-alcoholic drinks. This is where highballs and long sours belong."],["Un esempio aiuta a vedere il legame. Un gin sour corto, shakerato e servito in un bicchierino, diventa un drink lungo se lo si versa su ghiaccio e lo si allunga con acqua gassata. Gli ingredienti di base restano gli stessi; cambia la quantità della parte leggera, e con essa la forza, il volume e il momento in cui lo si beve.","Un exemple aide à voir le lien. Un gin sour court, secoué et servi dans un petit verre, devient un long drink si on le verse sur de la glace et qu'on l'allonge d'eau gazeuse. Les ingrédients de base restent les mêmes ; c'est la quantité de partie légère qui change, et avec elle la force, le volume et le moment où on le boit.","An example shows the link. A short gin sour, shaken and served in a small glass, becomes a long drink if you pour it over ice and top it with club soda. The core ingredients stay the same; what changes is the amount of the weak part, and with it the strength, the volume and the moment you might drink it."]],"k":[["Drink corti: pochi ingredienti, diluiti solo dal ghiaccio durante la preparazione.","Short drinks : peu d'ingrédients, dilués seulement par la glace pendant la préparation.","Short drinks: few ingredients, diluted only by ice during mixing."],["Famiglie corte: spirit-forward e sour corti.","Familles courtes : spirit-forward et sours courts.","Short families: spirit-forward and short sours."],["Drink lunghi: più volume, allungati con bibite, succhi o latticini.","Long drinks : plus de volume, allongés de sodas, jus ou produits laitiers.","Long drinks: bigger volume, lengthened with sodas, juices or dairy."],["Famiglie lunghe: highball e sour lunghi.","Familles longues : highballs et sours longs.","Long families: highballs and long sours."]]},{"c":"t3","t":["I cocktail spirit-forward","Les cocktails spirit-forward","Spirit-forward cocktails"],"p":[["Sono i cocktail più alcolici, quelli che mettono in vetrina il distillato. Nella versione più semplice uniscono un distillato a zucchero e bitter, oppure un distillato a un liquore; nelle versioni più elaborate dolce e amaro arrivano da combinazioni di zucchero, vini aromatizzati e bitter. Si preparano direttamente nel bicchiere o mescolando, e il ghiaccio serve sia a raffreddare sia a diluire.","Ce sont les cocktails les plus alcoolisés, ceux qui mettent le spiritueux en vitrine. Dans leur forme la plus simple, ils associent un spiritueux à du sucre et des bitters, ou un spiritueux à une liqueur ; dans les versions plus élaborées, sucré et amer viennent de combinaisons de sucre, de vins aromatisés et de bitters. On les prépare directement dans le verre ou en remuant, et la glace sert à refroidir comme à diluer.","These are the strongest cocktails, the ones that put the spirit on show. In their simplest form they combine a spirit with sugar and bitters, or a spirit with a liqueur; in more elaborate versions, sweetness and bitterness come from mixes of sugar, aromatised wines and bitters. They are built in the glass or stirred, and the ice both chills and dilutes."],["L'Old Fashioned è il modello: whiskey americano, una zolletta di zucchero e bitter Angostura. Il Manhattan usa rye o Bourbon con gli stessi bitter, ma sostituisce lo zucchero con vermouth rosso dolce, che lo rende più complesso. Il Sazerac parte da Cognac o rye, con zucchero, bitter Peychaud's e un tocco di assenzio. Il Rusty Nail è il più semplice: Scotch whisky e Drambuie, un liquore.","L'Old Fashioned est le modèle : whiskey américain, un morceau de sucre et des bitters Angostura. Le Manhattan utilise du rye ou du Bourbon avec les mêmes bitters, mais remplace le sucre par du vermouth rouge doux, ce qui le rend plus complexe. Le Sazerac part d'un Cognac ou d'un rye, avec du sucre, des bitters Peychaud's et une touche d'absinthe. Le Rusty Nail est le plus simple : Scotch whisky et Drambuie, une liqueur.","The Old Fashioned is the template: American whiskey, a sugar cube and Angostura bitters. The Manhattan uses rye or Bourbon with the same bitters, but swaps the sugar for sweet red vermouth, which makes it more complex. The Sazerac starts from Cognac or rye, with sugar, Peychaud's bitters and a touch of absinthe. The Rusty Nail is the simplest: Scotch whisky and Drambuie, a liqueur."],["Con il gin nascono due grandi classici. Il Martini abbina gin e vermouth dry, che da solo porta sia la nota dolce sia quella amara. Il Negroni unisce gin, vermouth rosso dolce e Campari, un distillato amaro rosso: tre ingredienti, tre ruoli chiari. Infine, aggiungendo panna a un drink di questo tipo nasce la famiglia degli Alexander, come il Brandy Alexander.","Avec le gin naissent deux grands classiques. Le Martini associe gin et vermouth dry, qui apporte à lui seul la note sucrée et la note amère. Le Negroni réunit gin, vermouth rouge doux et Campari, un spiritueux amer rouge : trois ingrédients, trois rôles clairs. Enfin, en ajoutant de la crème à ce type de boisson, on obtient la famille des Alexander, comme le Brandy Alexander.","Gin gives two great classics. The Martini pairs gin with dry vermouth, which on its own provides both the sweet and the bitter note. The Negroni combines gin, sweet red vermouth and Campari, a red bitter spirit: three ingredients, three clear roles. Finally, adding cream to this kind of drink creates the Alexander family, such as the Brandy Alexander."]],"k":[["Spirit-forward: i più alcolici, preparati nel bicchiere o mescolati.","Spirit-forward : les plus alcoolisés, préparés dans le verre ou remués.","Spirit-forward: the strongest drinks, built or stirred."],["Old Fashioned e Manhattan: whiskey e Angostura; il Manhattan aggiunge vermouth dolce.","Old Fashioned et Manhattan : whiskey et Angostura ; le Manhattan ajoute du vermouth doux.","Old Fashioned and Manhattan: whiskey and Angostura; the Manhattan adds sweet vermouth."],["Sazerac: Cognac o rye, Peychaud's e assenzio; Rusty Nail: Scotch e Drambuie.","Sazerac : Cognac ou rye, Peychaud's et absinthe ; Rusty Nail : Scotch et Drambuie.","Sazerac: Cognac or rye, Peychaud's and absinthe; Rusty Nail: Scotch and Drambuie."],["Martini: gin e vermouth dry; Negroni: gin, vermouth dolce, Campari. Con panna: Alexander.","Martini : gin et vermouth dry ; Negroni : gin, vermouth doux, Campari. Avec crème : Alexander.","Martini: gin and dry vermouth; Negroni: gin, sweet vermouth, Campari. With cream: Alexander."]]},{"c":"t3","t":["I sour corti","Les sours courts","Short sours"],"p":[["Il sour corto si regge su un trio: forte, acido, dolce. La ricetta base prevede un distillato, un succo di agrumi e un dolcificante neutro come lo sciroppo semplice. Questi drink si shakerano: lo shaker raffredda, mescola, diluisce un po' e dona una consistenza leggera e ariosa, quasi spumosa. È la famiglia da cui derivano moltissimi cocktail di successo.","Le sour court repose sur un trio : fort, acide, sucré. La recette de base associe un spiritueux, un jus d'agrume et un édulcorant neutre comme le sirop simple. Ces boissons se secouent : le shaker refroidit, mélange, dilue un peu et donne une texture légère et aérienne, presque mousseuse. C'est la famille dont découlent de très nombreux cocktails à succès.","The short sour rests on a trio: strong, sour, sweet. The basic recipe is a spirit, a citrus juice and an unflavoured sweetener such as simple syrup. These drinks are shaken: the shaker chills, mixes, dilutes a little and gives a light, airy, almost frothy texture. It is the family behind a huge number of successful cocktails."],["Tre classici mostrano lo schema puro. Il Daiquiri: rum, lime e sciroppo semplice. Il Whiskey Sour: Bourbon o rye, limone e sciroppo, con albume e bitter facoltativi. Il Pisco Sour: pisco, lime e sciroppo, più un albume e qualche goccia di bitter. Qui l'albume è indispensabile: crea una testa di schiuma e una consistenza setosa. Molti bar oggi usano l'aquafaba, l'acqua di cottura dei ceci, come alternativa vegana.","Trois classiques montrent le schéma pur. Le Daiquiri : rhum, citron vert et sirop simple. Le Whiskey Sour : Bourbon ou rye, citron jaune et sirop, avec blanc d'œuf et bitters facultatifs. Le Pisco Sour : pisco, citron vert et sirop, plus un blanc d'œuf et quelques gouttes de bitters. Ici, le blanc d'œuf est indispensable : il crée une tête de mousse et une texture soyeuse. Beaucoup de bars utilisent aujourd'hui l'aquafaba, l'eau de cuisson des pois chiches, comme alternative végane.","Three classics show the pure pattern. The Daiquiri: rum, lime and simple syrup. The Whiskey Sour: Bourbon or rye, lemon and syrup, with optional egg white and bitters. The Pisco Sour: pisco, lime and syrup, plus one egg white and a dash of bitters. Here the egg white is essential: it creates a foam head and a silky texture. Many bars now use aquafaba, the water chickpeas are cooked in, as a vegan alternative."],["Le varianti cambiano il dolcificante, l'acido o entrambi. Nel Sidecar il Cognac incontra limone e triple sec, un liquore all'arancia che sostituisce lo sciroppo. La Margarita usa tequila, lime e triple sec, con il bordo di sale facoltativo. Il Clover Club unisce gin, limone e sciroppo di lampone, con albume e, a piacere, un po' di vermouth: lo stesso schema, un colore tutto diverso.","Les variantes changent l'édulcorant, l'acide ou les deux. Dans le Sidecar, le Cognac rencontre le citron jaune et le triple sec, une liqueur d'orange qui remplace le sirop. La Margarita utilise tequila, citron vert et triple sec, avec un bord de sel facultatif. Le Clover Club associe gin, citron jaune et sirop de framboise, avec blanc d'œuf et, si l'on veut, un peu de vermouth : le même schéma, une tout autre couleur.","Variations change the sweetener, the sour ingredient or both. In the Sidecar, Cognac meets lemon and triple sec, an orange liqueur that replaces the syrup. The Margarita uses tequila, lime and triple sec, with an optional salt rim. The Clover Club brings together gin, lemon and raspberry syrup, with egg white and optionally a little vermouth: the same pattern, a completely different colour."]],"k":[["Sour corto = distillato + agrumi + dolcificante, shakerato.","Sour court = spiritueux + agrume + édulcorant, secoué.","Short sour = spirit + citrus + sweetener, shaken."],["Daiquiri: rum e lime; Whiskey Sour: whiskey e limone; Pisco Sour: pisco, lime e albume.","Daiquiri : rhum et citron vert ; Whiskey Sour : whiskey et citron jaune ; Pisco Sour : pisco, citron vert et blanc d'œuf.","Daiquiri: rum and lime; Whiskey Sour: whiskey and lemon; Pisco Sour: pisco, lime and egg white."],["Albume: schiuma e consistenza setosa; alternativa vegana: aquafaba.","Blanc d'œuf : mousse et texture soyeuse ; alternative végane : aquafaba.","Egg white: foam and a silky texture; vegan alternative: aquafaba."],["Varianti: Sidecar (Cognac), Margarita (tequila), Clover Club (gin, lampone).","Variantes : Sidecar (Cognac), Margarita (tequila), Clover Club (gin, framboise).","Variations: Sidecar (Cognac), Margarita (tequila), Clover Club (gin, raspberry)."]]},{"c":"t3","t":["Gli highball","Les highballs","Highballs"],"p":[["L'highball è il più semplice di tutti i drink miscelati: un distillato e una bevanda analcolica, serviti in un bicchiere lungo con ghiaccio a cubetti. Gin tonic, vodka tonic, whisky e soda sono esempi che quasi tutti conoscono senza sapere che appartengono a una famiglia. La regola è chiara: poco lavoro, tanto volume e la parte leggera affidata alla bibita.","Le highball est le plus simple de tous les mélanges : un spiritueux et une boisson sans alcool, servis dans un verre haut sur des glaçons. Gin tonic, vodka tonic, whisky soda sont des exemples que presque tout le monde connaît sans savoir qu'ils forment une famille. La règle est claire : peu de travail, beaucoup de volume et la partie légère confiée à la boisson gazeuse ou au jus.","The highball is the simplest of all mixed drinks: a spirit and a non-alcoholic mixer, served long over cubed ice. Gin and tonic, vodka and tonic, whisky and soda are examples almost everyone knows without realising they form a family. The rule is clear: little work, plenty of volume, and the weak part handed over to the mixer."],["Alcuni highball hanno un nome proprio. Il Cuba Libre è rum e cola con lime. Il Greyhound è vodka e succo di pompelmo: il succo, leggermente amaro e acido, fa da modificatore. Sono drink da immaginare in un pomeriggio caldo, facili da preparare a casa con ingredienti che si trovano ovunque, eppure costruiti con la stessa logica di equilibrio dei cocktail più complessi.","Certains highballs portent un nom. Le Cuba Libre, c'est rhum et cola avec du citron vert. Le Greyhound, c'est vodka et jus de pamplemousse : le jus, légèrement amer et acide, sert de modificateur. Ce sont des boissons d'après-midi d'été, faciles à préparer chez soi avec des ingrédients que l'on trouve partout, mais construites selon la même logique d'équilibre que les cocktails plus complexes.","Some highballs have their own names. The Cuba Libre is rum and cola with lime. The Greyhound is vodka and grapefruit juice: the slightly bitter, sour juice acts as the modifier. These are summer-afternoon drinks, easy to make at home with ingredients found anywhere, yet built on the same logic of balance as more complex cocktails."],["Altri highball aggiungono un dettaglio. L'Horse's Neck unisce Cognac, ginger ale e bitter: un esempio di highball con una nota amara oltre a distillato e bibita. L'Americano, invece, ha una base divisa: la parte alcolica è formata da Campari e vermouth rosso dolce insieme, completati con acqua gassata. Meno alcolico di un Negroni, ne è quasi una versione allungata senza gin.","D'autres highballs ajoutent un détail. Le Horse's Neck associe Cognac, ginger ale et bitters : un exemple de highball avec une note amère en plus du spiritueux et du soda. L'Americano, lui, a une base partagée : la partie alcoolisée est formée de Campari et de vermouth rouge doux réunis, complétés d'eau gazeuse. Moins alcoolisé qu'un Negroni, il en est presque une version allongée sans gin.","Other highballs add a detail. The Horse's Neck combines Cognac, ginger ale and bitters: a highball with a bitter accent on top of spirit and mixer. The Americano has a split base: its alcoholic part is Campari and sweet red vermouth together, topped with club soda. Lighter than a Negroni, it is almost a lengthened version of it without the gin."]],"k":[["Highball: distillato + bibita analcolica, in bicchiere lungo con ghiaccio.","Highball : spiritueux + boisson sans alcool, en verre haut sur glace.","Highball: spirit + non-alcoholic mixer, served long over ice."],["Cuba Libre: rum, cola e lime. Greyhound: vodka e succo di pompelmo.","Cuba Libre : rhum, cola et citron vert. Greyhound : vodka et jus de pamplemousse.","Cuba Libre: rum, cola and lime. Greyhound: vodka and grapefruit juice."],["Horse's Neck: Cognac, ginger ale e bitter.","Horse's Neck : Cognac, ginger ale et bitters.","Horse's Neck: Cognac, ginger ale and bitters."],["Americano: base divisa di Campari e vermouth dolce, più acqua gassata.","Americano : base partagée de Campari et vermouth doux, plus eau gazeuse.","Americano: split base of Campari and sweet vermouth, plus club soda."]]},{"c":"t3","t":["I sour lunghi","Les sours longs","Long sours"],"p":[["Il sour lungo comprende diverse sottofamiglie: i Collins, gli Sling e i sour frizzanti. Nella forma più semplice è un sour corto reso lungo con acqua gassata. Il Tom Collins ne è l'esempio perfetto: gin, succo di limone e sciroppo semplice, versati su ghiaccio e completati con soda. È rinfrescante, dissetante e mostra bene come un'unica ricetta possa cambiare veste.","Le sour long regroupe plusieurs sous-familles : les Collins, les Slings et les sours pétillants. Dans sa forme la plus simple, c'est un sour court rallongé à l'eau gazeuse. Le Tom Collins en est l'exemple parfait : gin, jus de citron jaune et sirop simple, versés sur glace et complétés d'eau gazeuse. Il est rafraîchissant, désaltérant, et montre bien comment une même recette peut changer d'allure.","The long sour covers several sub-families: Collinses, Slings and sparkling sours. In its simplest form it is a short sour made long with club soda. The Tom Collins is the perfect example: gin, lemon juice and simple syrup, poured over ice and topped with soda. It is refreshing and thirst-quenching, and shows clearly how one recipe can change its outfit."],["Al posto della soda si può usare una bibita aromatizzata o lo Champagne. La Paloma unisce tequila e lime a una soda al pompelmo di tipo messicano, che porta insieme dolcezza e bollicine; in alternativa si usano succo di pompelmo e acqua gassata. Il French 75 parte da Cognac o gin, limone e sciroppo semplice, e si completa con Champagne: un sour frizzante ed elegante.","À la place de l'eau gazeuse, on peut utiliser un soda aromatisé ou du Champagne. La Paloma associe tequila et citron vert à un soda au pamplemousse de type mexicain, qui apporte à la fois sucre et bulles ; on peut aussi employer jus de pamplemousse et eau gazeuse. Le French 75 part d'un Cognac ou d'un gin, de citron jaune et de sirop simple, et se complète au Champagne : un sour pétillant et élégant.","Instead of club soda you can use a flavoured soda or Champagne. The Paloma combines tequila and lime with a Mexican-style grapefruit soda, which brings sweetness and bubbles at once; alternatively, grapefruit juice and soda water are used. The French 75 starts from Cognac or gin, lemon and simple syrup, and is topped with Champagne: an elegant sparkling sour."],["Alcuni sour lunghi si arricchiscono con ingredienti extra. Il Mojito resta semplice: rum, lime e zucchero o sciroppo, con foglie di menta che lo rendono fresco e profumato. Il Singapore Sling è più complesso: gin e lime, addolciti da un liquore alla ciliegia e da un liquore alle erbe, con qualche goccia di bitter Angostura e un'aggiunta finale di acqua gassata.","Certains sours longs s'enrichissent d'ingrédients supplémentaires. Le Mojito reste simple : rhum, citron vert et sucre ou sirop, avec des feuilles de menthe qui le rendent frais et parfumé. Le Singapore Sling est plus complexe : gin et citron vert, adoucis par une liqueur de cerise et une liqueur aux plantes, avec quelques gouttes de bitters Angostura et un complément d'eau gazeuse.","Some long sours are enriched with extra ingredients. The Mojito stays simple: rum, lime and sugar or syrup, with mint leaves that make it fresh and fragrant. The Singapore Sling is more complex: gin and lime, sweetened with a cherry liqueur and a herbal liqueur, with a dash of Angostura bitters and a final top of club soda."]],"k":[["Sour lungo = sour corto allungato; sottofamiglie: Collins, Sling, sour frizzanti.","Sour long = sour court allongé ; sous-familles : Collins, Slings, sours pétillants.","Long sour = a lengthened short sour; sub-families: Collins, Sling, sparkling sour."],["Tom Collins: gin, limone, sciroppo, acqua gassata.","Tom Collins : gin, citron jaune, sirop, eau gazeuse.","Tom Collins: gin, lemon, syrup, club soda."],["Paloma: tequila, lime, soda al pompelmo. French 75: Cognac o gin, limone, sciroppo, Champagne.","Paloma : tequila, citron vert, soda au pamplemousse. French 75 : Cognac ou gin, citron jaune, sirop, Champagne.","Paloma: tequila, lime, grapefruit soda. French 75: Cognac or gin, lemon, syrup, Champagne."],["Mojito: rum, lime, zucchero e menta. Singapore Sling: gin, lime, liquori, bitter, soda.","Mojito : rhum, citron vert, sucre et menthe. Singapore Sling : gin, citron vert, liqueurs, bitters, eau gazeuse.","Mojito: rum, lime, sugar and mint. Singapore Sling: gin, lime, liqueurs, bitters, soda."]]}],"flash":[{"c":"p1","f":["Distillato","Spiritueux","Spirit"],"b":["Bevanda alcolica il cui grado è stato alzato con la distillazione.","Boisson alcoolisée dont le degré a été augmenté par distillation.","An alcoholic drink whose strength has been raised by distillation."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Le quattro tappe","Les quatre étapes","The four steps"],"b":["Materia prima, fermentazione, distillazione, fase dopo la distillazione.","Matière première, fermentation, distillation, étape après la distillation.","Raw material, fermentation, distillation, post-distillation."]},{"c":"p1","f":["% vol.","% vol.","abv"],"b":["Percentuale di alcol nel volume del liquido: 40% vol. = 40% è alcol.","Pourcentage d'alcool dans le volume : 40 % vol. = 40 % d'alcool.","Alcohol by volume: 40% abv means 40% of the liquid is alcohol."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Che cosa fanno i lieviti?","Que font les levures ?","What does yeast do?"],"b":["Mangiano lo zucchero e producono etanolo, anidride carbonica e aromi fruttati.","Elles mangent le sucre et produisent éthanol, dioxyde de carbone et arômes fruités.","Eats sugar, making ethanol, carbon dioxide and fruity aromas."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Grado dopo la fermentazione","Degré après fermentation","Strength after fermentation"],"b":["Di solito tra l'8% e il 10% vol.","En général entre 8 % et 10 % vol.","Usually 8–10% abv."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Grado di distillazione e aromi","Degré de distillation et arômes","Distillation strength and aroma"],"b":["Grado basso = più aromi; grado alto = meno aromi; 96% = neutro.","Degré bas = plus d'arômes ; degré élevé = moins ; 96 % = neutre.","Lower strength = more aroma; higher strength = less; 96% = neutral."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Alambicco discontinuo","Alambic à repasse","Pot still"],"b":["Lavora a lotti, di solito due volte; grado basso, molto carattere.","Travaille par lots, en général deux fois ; degré bas, beaucoup de caractère.","Batch process, usually twice; low strength, lots of character."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Alambicco a colonna","Colonne à distiller","Column still"],"b":["Continuo; corta = aromatico, alta = leggero, la più alta = neutro al 95–96%.","Continue ; courte = aromatique, haute = légère, la plus haute = neutre à 95–96 %.","Continuous; short = flavourful, tall = light, tallest = neutral at 95–96%."]},{"c":"p2","f":["Distillato appena fatto","Eau-de-vie sortant de l'alambic","Newly made spirit"],"b":["Sempre incolore e secco, cioè senza zucchero.","Toujours incolore et sèche, c'est-à-dire sans sucre.","Always colourless and dry, with no sugar."]},{"c":"p2","f":["Botte nuova","Fût neuf","New oak barrel"],"b":["Mai usata: cede il massimo di colore e aromi (vaniglia, spezie, cocco).","Jamais utilisé : cède le maximum de couleur et d'arômes (vanille, épices, coco).","Never used: gives the most colour and aroma (vanilla, spice, coconut)."]},{"c":"p2","f":["Botte vecchia","Vieux fût","Old oak barrel"],"b":["Già usata: cede meno aromi, e meno ancora a ogni riutilizzo.","Déjà utilisé : cède moins d'arômes, et moins encore à chaque usage.","Already used: gives less aroma, and less again with each reuse."]},{"c":"p2","f":["Assemblaggio","Assemblage","Blending"],"b":["Unire più botti per costanza da una bottiglia all'altra e per complessità.","Réunir plusieurs fûts pour la constance d'une bouteille à l'autre et la complexité.","Combining barrels for bottle-to-bottle consistency and for complexity."]},{"c":"p2","f":["Caramello colorante","Caramel colorant","Caramel colouring"],"b":["Uniforma il colore dei lotti; usato bene, non è dolce e non dà aromi.","Uniformise la couleur des lots ; bien utilisé, il n'est pas sucré et n'apporte aucun arôme.","Evens out batch colour; used properly, not sweet and adds no aroma."]},{"c":"p2","f":["Da dove viene la dolcezza?","D'où vient la douceur ?","Where does sweetness come from?"],"b":["Sempre aggiunta dopo la distillazione, di solito come zucchero.","Toujours ajoutée après la distillation, en général sous forme de sucre.","Always added after distillation, usually as sugar."]},{"c":"p2","f":["Diluizione","Dilution","Dilution"],"b":["Ultimo passaggio: acqua pura, di solito fino al 40% vol.; nessun aroma aggiunto.","Dernière étape : eau pure, en général jusqu'à 40 % vol. ; aucun arôme ajouté.","Final step: pure water, usually down to 40% abv; adds no flavour."]},{"c":"s1","f":["Brandy d'uva","Brandy de raisin","Grape brandy"],"b":["Vino distillato; il Cognac è l'esempio più famoso.","Du vin distillé ; le Cognac en est l'exemple le plus célèbre.","Distilled wine; Cognac is the most famous example."]},{"c":"s1","f":["Dove nasce il Cognac?","Où naît le Cognac ?","Where does Cognac come from?"],"b":["Zona delimitata del sud-ovest della Francia, a nord di Bordeaux.","Zone délimitée du sud-ouest de la France, au nord de Bordeaux.","A defined area of south-west France, north of Bordeaux."]},{"c":"s1","f":["Distillazione del Cognac","Distillation du Cognac","Cognac distillation"],"b":["Per legge: due volte in alambicco discontinuo.","Par la loi : deux fois à l'alambic à repasse.","By law: twice in a pot still."]},{"c":"s1","f":["Invecchiamento minimo del Cognac","Vieillissement minimum du Cognac","Cognac minimum ageing"],"b":["Almeno 2 anni in rovere; dà vaniglia e tostato.","Au moins 2 ans en fût de chêne ; apporte vanille et grillé.","At least 2 years in oak; gives vanilla and toast."]},{"c":"s1","f":["VS","VS","VS"],"b":["Distillato più giovane: almeno 2 anni.","Eau-de-vie la plus jeune : au moins 2 ans.","Youngest spirit: at least 2 years old."]},{"c":"s1","f":["VSOP","VSOP","VSOP"],"b":["Distillato più giovane: almeno 4 anni.","Eau-de-vie la plus jeune : au moins 4 ans.","Youngest spirit: at least 4 years old."]},{"c":"s1","f":["XO","XO","XO"],"b":["Distillato più giovane: almeno 10 anni.","Eau-de-vie la plus jeune : au moins 10 ans.","Youngest spirit: at least 10 years old."]},{"c":"s2","f":["Che cosa definisce la vodka?","Qu'est-ce qui définit la vodka ?","What defines vodka?"],"b":["Il grado di distillazione; materia prima e luogo sono liberi.","Le degré de distillation ; matière première et lieu sont libres.","Distillation strength; raw material and place are open."]},{"c":"s2","f":["Distillato neutro","Alcool neutre","Neutral spirit"],"b":["Almeno 95% o 96% vol., in colonna; quasi senza aromi.","Au moins 95 % ou 96 % vol., en colonne ; presque sans arômes.","At least 95% or 96% abv, column-distilled; almost no aroma."]},{"c":"s2","f":["Materie prime della vodka di qualità","Matières premières de la vodka de qualité","Premium vodka raw materials"],"b":["Cereali (orzo, frumento, segale) e patate.","Céréales (orge, blé, seigle) et pommes de terre.","Cereals (barley, wheat, rye) and potatoes."]},{"c":"s2","f":["Vodka dopo la distillazione","Vodka après la distillation","Vodka after distillation"],"b":["Non invecchiata; diluita di solito al 40% vol.","Non vieillie ; diluée en général à 40 % vol.","Unaged; usually diluted to 40% abv."]},{"c":"s2","f":["Vodka con un po' di carattere","Vodka avec un peu de caractère","Vodka with some character"],"b":["Lievi note della materia prima, ma ancora neutra.","Légères notes de matière première, mais toujours neutre.","Faint raw-material notes, yet still neutral."]},{"c":"s3","f":["Maltazione","Maltage","Malting"],"b":["L'orzo germoglia e crea enzimi; l'aria calda ferma la crescita.","L'orge germe et crée des enzymes ; l'air chaud stoppe la croissance.","Barley sprouts and makes enzymes; hot air then stops the growth."]},{"c":"s3","f":["A cosa servono gli enzimi dell'orzo?","À quoi servent les enzymes de l'orge ?","What do barley enzymes do?"],"b":["Nell'acqua trasformano l'amido dei cereali in zucchero fermentabile.","Dans l'eau, ils transforment l'amidon des céréales en sucre fermentescible.","In water, they turn the grain's starch into sugar yeast can ferment."]},{"c":"s3","f":["Scotch: regola base","Scotch : règle de base","Scotch: the basic rule"],"b":["Distillato in Scozia e invecchiato lì almeno tre anni.","Distillé en Écosse et vieilli sur place au moins trois ans.","Distilled in Scotland and aged there for at least three years."]},{"c":"s3","f":["Single Malt Scotch","Single Malt Scotch","Single Malt Scotch"],"b":["100% orzo maltato, alambicchi discontinui, una sola distilleria.","100 % orge maltée, alambics, une seule distillerie.","100% malted barley, pot stills, one distillery."]},{"c":"s3","f":["Torba","Tourbe","Peat"],"b":["Combustibile bruciato scaldando l'orzo maltato: dà fumo a pochi Single Malt.","Combustible brûlé en chauffant l'orge maltée : donne la fumée de quelques Single Malts.","Fuel burned while heating malted barley; gives smoke to a few Single Malts."]},{"c":"s3","f":["Whisky di cereali (grain whisky)","Whisky de grain","Grain whisky"],"b":["Orzo maltato e altri cereali, in colonna: leggero, morbido, raramente venduto da solo.","Orge maltée et autres céréales, en colonne : léger, souple, rarement vendu seul.","Malted barley plus other grains, column-distilled: light, smooth, rarely sold alone."]},{"c":"s3","f":["Blended Scotch","Blended Scotch","Blended Scotch"],"b":["Malti più whisky di cereali di distillerie diverse; di solito più morbido.","Malts et whiskies de grain de distilleries différentes ; souvent plus souple.","Malt plus grain whiskies from different distilleries; usually smoother."]},{"c":"s4","f":["Bourbon: cereale","Bourbon : céréale","Bourbon: grain rule"],"b":["Almeno 51% mais, più di solito orzo e segale.","Au moins 51 % de maïs, plus en général orge et seigle.","At least 51% corn, usually with some barley and rye."]},{"c":"s4","f":["Bourbon: botti","Bourbon : fûts","Bourbon: barrels"],"b":["Rovere nuovo carbonizzato: vaniglia, cocco, colore intenso.","Chêne neuf brûlé : vanille, noix de coco, couleur intense.","New charred oak: vanilla, coconut and deep colour."]},{"c":"s4","f":["Dove si fa il Bourbon?","Où fait-on le Bourbon ?","Where is Bourbon made?"],"b":["Ovunque negli Stati Uniti; il Kentucky è lo stato principale.","Partout aux États-Unis ; le Kentucky est l'État principal.","Anywhere in the USA; Kentucky is the leading state."]},{"c":"s4","f":["Tennessee whiskey","Tennessee whiskey","Tennessee whiskey"],"b":["Come il Bourbon, ma solo in Tennessee e filtrato su carbone d'acero prima della botte.","Comme le Bourbon, mais seulement au Tennessee et filtré au charbon d'érable avant le fût.","Like Bourbon, but made only in Tennessee and maple-charcoal filtered before the barrel."]},{"c":"s4","f":["Rye whiskey americano","Rye whiskey américain","American Rye whiskey"],"b":["Fatto come il Bourbon ma con almeno 51% segale: speziato e pepato.","Fait comme le Bourbon mais avec au moins 51 % de seigle : épicé et poivré.","Made like Bourbon but with at least 51% rye: spicy and peppery."]},{"c":"s4","f":["Whiskey irlandese","Whiskey irlandais","Irish whiskey"],"b":["Per lo più alambicco + colonna, leggero e morbido; a volte orzo non maltato.","Surtout alambic + colonne, léger et souple ; parfois orge non maltée.","Mostly pot + column blends, light and smooth; sometimes unmalted barley."]},{"c":"s4","f":["Whisky canadese","Whisky canadien","Canadian whisky"],"b":["Molti cereali, miscela di spiriti ad alta e bassa gradazione; firma della segale.","Plusieurs céréales, assemblage haut et bas degré ; signature du seigle.","Many grains, high- and low-strength blend; rye is the signature."]},{"c":"s4","f":["Whisky giapponese","Whisky japonais","Japanese whisky"],"b":["Modello scozzese: malti e blended, tradizionalmente eleganti e raffinati.","Modèle écossais : malts et blends, traditionnellement élégants et raffinés.","Scottish model: malts and blends, traditionally elegant and refined."]},{"c":"s5","f":["Melassa","Mélasse","Molasses"],"b":["Sottoprodotto nero e denso dello zucchero; si diluisce con acqua; dà caramello e zucchero scuro.","Sous-produit noir et épais du sucre ; diluée à l'eau ; donne caramel et sucre roux.","Black, sticky sugar by-product; mixed with water; gives caramel and brown sugar."]},{"c":"s5","f":["Rum da succo di canna","Rhum de jus de canne","Cane-juice rum"],"b":["Succo fresco fermentato subito: sapore erbaceo e vegetale molto marcato.","Jus frais fermenté aussitôt : goût herbacé et végétal très marqué.","Fresh juice fermented at once: very pronounced grassy, herbaceous flavour."]},{"c":"s5","f":["Rhum agricole","Rhum agricole","Rhum agricole"],"b":["Da succo di canna, colonna corta; nei Caraibi solo Martinica o Guadalupa.","Jus de canne, colonne courte ; dans la Caraïbe, Martinique ou Guadeloupe.","Cane juice, short column; in the Caribbean, only Martinique or Guadeloupe."]},{"c":"s5","f":["Rum della Giamaica","Rhum de la Jamaïque","Jamaican rum"],"b":["Famoso per aromi di frutta tropicale intensi, creati in fermentazione.","Célèbre pour ses arômes intenses de fruits tropicaux, créés pendant la fermentation.","Known for intense tropical fruit aromas created during fermentation."]},{"c":"s5","f":["Rum leggeri di Cuba e Porto Rico","Rhums légers de Cuba et Porto Rico","Light rums of Cuba and Puerto Rico"],"b":["Colonne alte, alta gradazione: aroma leggero.","Hautes colonnes, haut degré : nez léger.","Tall columns, high strength: light aroma."]},{"c":"s5","f":["Filtrazione al carbone nel rum","Filtration au charbon dans le rhum","Charcoal filtering in rum"],"b":["Toglie il colore del rovere: dà un rum bianco anche se invecchiato.","Retire la couleur du chêne : donne un rhum blanc même vieilli.","Removes oak colour, giving a white rum even after ageing."]},{"c":"s5","f":["Rum addolcito","Rhum sucré","Sweetened rum"],"b":["Comune in America Centrale e del Sud; vietato in alcuni paesi.","Courant en Amérique centrale et du Sud ; interdit dans certains pays.","Common in Central and South America; not allowed in some countries."]},{"c":"s6","f":["Cuore d'agave blu","Cœur d'agave bleu","Blue agave core"],"b":["Si tagliano le foglie, si cuoce in forno per creare zuccheri, poi si schiaccia.","On coupe les feuilles, on le cuit au four pour créer des sucres, puis on le broie.","Leaves cut off; cooked in ovens to create sugars, then crushed."]},{"c":"s6","f":["Tequila vs Tequila 100% agave","Tequila vs Tequila 100 % agave","Tequila vs Tequila 100% agave"],"b":["Almeno 51% di zuccheri d'agave, oppure solo zuccheri d'agave.","Au moins 51 % de sucres d'agave, ou uniquement des sucres d'agave.","At least 51% agave sugars, or agave sugars only."]},{"c":"s6","f":["Come si distillano le migliori Tequile?","Comment distille-t-on les meilleures Tequilas ?","How are the best Tequilas distilled?"],"b":["Due volte in alambicco discontinuo, a bassa gradazione: tanto carattere d'agave.","Deux fois en alambic à repasse, à faible degré : beaucoup de caractère d'agave.","Twice in pot stills to a low strength: lots of agave character."]},{"c":"s6","f":["Blanco / Silver","Blanco / Silver","Blanco / Silver"],"b":["Non invecchiata, incolore: l'agave nella forma più pura.","Non vieillie, incolore : l'agave dans sa forme la plus pure.","Unaged and colourless: agave at its purest."]},{"c":"s6","f":["Joven / Oro / Gold","Joven / Oro / Gold","Joven / Oro / Gold"],"b":["Non invecchiata; colore da caramello, consistenza ammorbidita da additivi.","Non vieillie ; couleur due au caramel, texture adoucie par des additifs.","Unaged; colour from caramel, texture softened by additives."]},{"c":"s6","f":["Reposado vs Añejo","Reposado vs Añejo","Reposado vs Añejo"],"b":["Reposado: 2–12 mesi in rovere. Añejo: almeno 12 mesi.","Reposado : 2 à 12 mois en chêne. Añejo : au moins 12 mois.","Reposado: 2–12 months in oak. Añejo: at least 12 months."]},{"c":"s7","f":["Botanici","Botaniques","Botanicals"],"b":["Ingredienti naturali che aromatizzano: frutta, semi, erbe e spezie.","Ingrédients naturels qui aromatisent : fruits, graines, herbes et épices.","Natural flavouring ingredients: fruits, seeds, herbs and spices."]},{"c":"s7","f":["Ridistillazione","Redistillation","Redistillation"],"b":["Spirito neutro + botanici distillati insieme in alambicco: aromatizzato e incolore.","Alcool neutre + botaniques distillés ensemble en alambic : aromatisé et incolore.","Neutral spirit and botanicals distilled together in a pot still: flavoured, colourless."]},{"c":"s7","f":["Macerazione","Macération","Maceration"],"b":["Botanici in infusione per giorni o mesi; danno sapore e colore. Il calore accelera.","Botaniques infusés des jours ou des mois ; saveur et couleur. La chaleur accélère.","Botanicals steeped for days or months; give flavour and colour. Heat speeds it up."]},{"c":"s7","f":["Gin","Gin","Gin"],"b":["Distillato aromatizzato con il ginepro dominante; di solito incolore e non invecchiato.","Spiritueux aromatisé où domine le genièvre ; en général incolore et non vieilli.","Flavoured spirit led by juniper; usually colourless and unaged."]},{"c":"s7","f":["London Dry Gin","London Dry Gin","London Dry Gin"],"b":["Aromi dati con la ridistillazione. Si può produrre ovunque, non solo a Londra.","Arômes apportés par redistillation. Peut être produit partout, pas seulement à Londres.","Flavours added by redistillation. Can be made anywhere, not just London."]},{"c":"s7","f":["Distillato amaro","Spiritueux amer","Bitter spirit"],"b":["Almeno un botanico amaro (genziana, chinino, arancia amara); l'amaro si sente solo in bocca.","Au moins une botanique amère (gentiane, quinine, orange amère) ; amertume perçue en bouche seulement.","At least one bitter botanical (gentian, quinine, bitter orange); bitterness felt only on the palate."]},{"c":"s7","f":["Bitter da cocktail","Bitters à cocktail","Cocktail bitters"],"b":["Concentratissimi e molto amari; mai bevuti da soli, poche gocce per dare complessità.","Très concentrés et très amers ; jamais bus seuls, quelques gouttes pour la complexité.","Very concentrated and very bitter; never drunk alone, a few drops add complexity."]},{"c":"s7","f":["Liquore","Liqueur","Liqueur"],"b":["Distillato aromatizzato e zuccherato, con dolcezza minima per legge; spesso colorato.","Spiritueux aromatisé et sucré, douceur minimale imposée par la loi ; souvent coloré.","Flavoured, sweetened spirit with a legal minimum sweetness; often coloured."]},{"c":"s8","f":["Vino aromatizzato","Vin aromatisé","Aromatised wine"],"b":["Vino di base + aromi con un amaro + zucchero + un po' di distillato.","Vin de base + arômes avec un amer + sucre + un peu de spiritueux.","Base wine + flavourings with a bitter + sugar + a little spirit."]},{"c":"s8","f":["Perché si aggiunge distillato?","Pourquoi ajouter du spiritueux ?","Why add spirit?"],"b":["Per alzare l'alcol e conservare più a lungo, anche dopo l'apertura.","Pour relever l'alcool et mieux conserver, même après ouverture.","To raise alcohol and extend shelf life, even after opening."]},{"c":"s8","f":["Vermut","Vermouth","Vermouth"],"b":["Vino bianco di base aromatizzato con assenzio; Francia e Italia.","Vin blanc de base aromatisé à l'absinthe ; France et Italie.","White wine base flavoured with wormwood; France and Italy."]},{"c":"s8","f":["Vermut «dry»","Vermouth « dry »","‘Dry’ vermouth"],"b":["Quasi sempre con zucchero aggiunto, solo meno del rosso.","Presque toujours avec du sucre ajouté, simplement moins que le rouge.","Nearly always has added sugar, just less than red."]},{"c":"s8","f":["Colore del vermut rosso","Couleur du vermouth rouge","Red vermouth colour"],"b":["Di solito dal caramello, perché la base è un vino bianco.","Généralement du caramel, car la base est un vin blanc.","Usually from caramel, as the base is a white wine."]},{"c":"t1","f":["Campione per degustare un distillato","Échantillon pour déguster un spiritueux","Sample size for tasting a spirit"],"b":["Circa 1,5 cL, più o meno un cucchiaio.","Environ 1,5 cL, à peu près une cuillère à soupe.","About 1.5 cL, roughly a tablespoon."]},{"c":"t1","f":["Quanta acqua aggiungere?","Combien d'eau ajouter ?","How much water to add?"],"b":["La stessa quantità del campione, dopo il primo esame di occhio e naso.","Autant que l'échantillon, après le premier examen de l'œil et du nez.","The same amount as the sample, after the first look and sniff."]},{"c":"t1","f":["Bicchiere da degustazione ideale","Verre de dégustation idéal","Ideal tasting glass"],"b":["Coppa ampia che si stringe in alto, per concentrare gli aromi.","Large calice resserré en haut, pour concentrer les arômes.","Wide bowl narrowing at the top, to concentrate the aromas."]},{"c":"t1","f":["Livelli di intensità al naso","Niveaux d'intensité au nez","Nose intensity levels"],"b":["Neutro, leggero, medio, pronunciato.","Neutre, léger, moyen, prononcé.","Neutral, light, medium, pronounced."]},{"c":"t1","f":["Due osservazioni in bocca oltre ai sapori","Deux observations en bouche en plus des saveurs","Two palate observations besides flavours"],"b":["Livello di zucchero e consistenza del liquido.","Niveau de sucre et texture du liquide.","Sugar level and the texture of the liquid."]},{"c":"t2","f":["I quattro punti di equilibrio","Les quatre points d'équilibre","The four points of balance"],"b":["Forte, leggero, dolce, amaro e/o acido.","Fort, léger, sucré, amer et/ou acide.","Strong, weak, sweet, bitter and/or sour."]},{"c":"t2","f":["Sciroppo semplice","Sirop simple","Simple syrup"],"b":["Zucchero sciolto in acqua: un dolcificante senza aromi.","Du sucre dissous dans l'eau : un édulcorant sans arôme.","Sugar dissolved in water: an unflavoured sweetener."]},{"c":"t2","f":["Modificatore","Modificateur","Modifier"],"b":["Ingrediente che bilancia il dolce con amaro e/o acido, come agrumi o bitter.","Ingrédient qui équilibre le sucré par de l'amer et/ou de l'acide, comme agrumes ou bitters.","Ingredient that balances sweetness with bitter and/or sour, like citrus or bitters."]},{"c":"t2","f":["Drink corto","Short drink","Short drink"],"b":["Pochi ingredienti, diluito dal ghiaccio mescolando o shakerando.","Peu d'ingrédients, dilué par la glace en remuant ou en secouant.","Few ingredients, diluted by ice when stirred or shaken."]},{"c":"t2","f":["Drink lungo","Long drink","Long drink"],"b":["Più volume, allungato con bibite, succhi o latticini.","Plus de volume, allongé de sodas, jus ou produits laitiers.","Bigger volume, lengthened with sodas, juices or dairy."]},{"c":"t3","f":["Old Fashioned","Old Fashioned","Old Fashioned"],"b":["Whiskey (di solito Bourbon), zolletta di zucchero, bitter Angostura.","Whiskey (souvent Bourbon), morceau de sucre, bitters Angostura.","Whiskey (usually Bourbon), sugar cube, Angostura bitters."]},{"c":"t3","f":["Manhattan","Manhattan","Manhattan"],"b":["Rye o Bourbon, vermouth rosso dolce, bitter Angostura.","Rye ou Bourbon, vermouth rouge doux, bitters Angostura.","Rye or Bourbon, sweet red vermouth, Angostura bitters."]},{"c":"t3","f":["Brandy Alexander","Brandy Alexander","Brandy Alexander"],"b":["Esempio della famiglia Alexander: un drink spirit-forward arricchito con panna.","Exemple de la famille Alexander : un spirit-forward enrichi de crème.","Example of the Alexander family: a spirit-forward drink with cream added."]},{"c":"t3","f":["Whiskey Sour","Whiskey Sour","Whiskey Sour"],"b":["Bourbon o rye, limone, sciroppo semplice; albume e bitter facoltativi.","Bourbon ou rye, citron jaune, sirop simple ; blanc d'œuf et bitters facultatifs.","Bourbon or rye, lemon, simple syrup; optional egg white and bitters."]},{"c":"t3","f":["Aquafaba","Aquafaba","Aquafaba"],"b":["Acqua di cottura dei ceci: alternativa vegana all'albume per la schiuma.","Eau de cuisson des pois chiches : alternative végane au blanc d'œuf pour la mousse.","Chickpea cooking water: a vegan alternative to egg white for foam."]},{"c":"t3","f":["Highball","Highball","Highball"],"b":["Il drink miscelato più semplice: distillato e bibita, lungo, su ghiaccio a cubetti.","Le mélange le plus simple : spiritueux et soda, long, sur glaçons.","The simplest mixed drink: spirit and mixer, served long over cubed ice."]},{"c":"t3","f":["Cuba Libre","Cuba Libre","Cuba Libre"],"b":["Highball di rum e cola con lime.","Highball de rhum et cola avec citron vert.","Highball of rum and cola with lime."]},{"c":"t3","f":["French 75","French 75","French 75"],"b":["Cognac o gin, limone, sciroppo semplice, completato con Champagne.","Cognac ou gin, citron jaune, sirop simple, complété au Champagne.","Cognac or gin, lemon, simple syrup, topped with Champagne."]},{"c":"t3","f":["Singapore Sling","Singapore Sling","Singapore Sling"],"b":["Gin, lime, liquore alla ciliegia e alle erbe, bitter Angostura, acqua gassata.","Gin, citron vert, liqueur de cerise et aux plantes, bitters Angostura, eau gazeuse.","Gin, lime, cherry and herbal liqueurs, Angostura bitters, club soda."]},{"c":"t3","f":["Sottofamiglie del sour lungo","Sous-familles du sour long","Long sour sub-families"],"b":["Collins, Sling e sour frizzanti.","Collins, Slings et sours pétillants.","Collins, Sling and sparkling sour."]}]};
window.TWG_ESX=Object.assign(window.TWG_ESX||{es:{},ar:{}},{});Object.assign(window.TWG_ESX.es,{"Four steps behind every spirit":"Cuatro pasos detrás de cada destilado","Put as simply as possible, a spirit is an alcoholic drink that distillation has made stronger. But distillation never works alone: behind every bottle, whether vodka or Cognac, there are always four steps. The raw material is prepared, it is fermented, it is distilled, and finally the producer decides what to do with the spirit fresh from the still. Knowing these four steps unlocks almost every spirit on the shelf.":"Dicho de la forma más sencilla, un destilado es una bebida alcohólica a la que la destilación ha hecho más fuerte. Pero la destilación nunca trabaja sola: detrás de cada botella, sea vodka o coñac, hay siempre cuatro pasos. Se prepara la materia prima, se fermenta, se destila y, por último, se decide qué hacer con el destilado recién salido del alambique. Conocer estos cuatro pasos permite entender casi cualquier destilado.","The first step has a single goal: to obtain a sugary liquid, because without sugar there is no fermentation. The raw material must come from a plant. Some plants, such as sugar cane or grapes, already hold sugar that is easy to extract. Others, such as cereals, contain none and must be processed to create it. Either way, the starting plant leaves its signature: every raw material gives the spirit its own set of aromas.":"El primer paso tiene un único objetivo: obtener un líquido azucarado, porque sin azúcar no hay fermentación. La materia prima debe ser de origen vegetal. Algunas plantas, como la caña de azúcar o la uva, ya contienen azúcar fácil de extraer. Otras, como los cereales, no tienen y hay que transformarlas para crearlo. En cualquier caso, la planta de partida deja su firma: cada materia prima aporta al destilado sus propios aromas.","After fermentation and distillation comes the fourth step, often overlooked but decisive. A newly made spirit is colourless and dry, so the producer can leave it that way, put it into oak barrels, add flavours, sugar or colour, and finally dilute it with water. A handy image: the first three steps build the house, the fourth furnishes it. Two spirits that start out identical can leave this stage tasting very different.":"Después de la fermentación y la destilación llega el cuarto paso, a menudo olvidado pero decisivo. El destilado recién hecho es incoloro y seco, así que el productor puede dejarlo así, meterlo en barricas de roble, añadirle aromas, azúcar o color y, al final, rebajarlo con agua. Una imagen útil: los tres primeros pasos construyen la casa y el cuarto la amuebla. Dos destilados idénticos al principio pueden salir de esta fase muy distintos.","Spirit = an alcoholic drink made stronger by distillation.":"Destilado = bebida alcohólica hecha más fuerte por la destilación.","Four steps: raw material, fermentation, distillation, post-distillation.":"Cuatro pasos: materia prima, fermentación, destilación, fase posterior a la destilación.","The raw material is always a plant and is used to make a sugary liquid.":"La materia prima siempre es vegetal y sirve para obtener un líquido azucarado.","Each raw material brings its own aromas.":"Cada materia prima aporta sus propios aromas.","Fermentation makes alcohol, distillation concentrates it":"La fermentación crea el alcohol, la destilación lo concentra","Yeasts are tiny living organisms added to the sugary liquid. They feed on the sugar and leave two things behind: ethanol, the alcohol the distiller wants, and carbon dioxide, a waste gas. At the end, the fermented liquid usually sits between 8% and 10% abv, roughly the strength of a strong beer. Yeasts also create new aromas, especially fruity ones, so fermentation adds flavour as well as alcohol.":"Las levaduras son organismos vivos diminutos que se añaden al líquido azucarado. Se alimentan del azúcar y dejan dos productos: el etanol, que es el alcohol que busca el destilador, y el dióxido de carbono, un gas de desecho. Al final, el líquido fermentado suele tener entre un 8% y un 10% vol., más o menos como una cerveza fuerte. Las levaduras también crean nuevos aromas, sobre todo afrutados.","Distillation relies on one simple fact: ethanol boils at a lower temperature than water. When the fermented liquid is heated to boiling, the vapours rising from it are richer in alcohol than the liquid left behind. Collected and cooled, those vapours turn back into a liquid that is stronger than the one we started with. This is the step where a spirit is truly born.":"La destilación aprovecha un hecho sencillo: el etanol hierve a una temperatura más baja que el agua. Al calentar el líquido fermentado hasta que hierve, los vapores que suben son más ricos en alcohol que el líquido que queda abajo. Recogidos y enfriados, esos vapores vuelven a ser líquidos y forman un nuevo líquido más fuerte. Es en este paso donde nace de verdad un destilado.","The strength reached during distillation matters a lot. A newly made spirit can range from about 60% up to 96% abv. The lower the strength, the more intense the aromas; the higher the strength, the less aroma survives. At 96% abv a spirit has so little smell that it is called neutral. Picture a radio: the louder the alcohol, the fainter the music of the aromas.":"El grado al que se destila importa mucho. Un destilado recién hecho puede ir de un 60% a un 96% vol. aproximadamente. Cuanto más bajo es el grado, más intensos son los aromas; cuanto más alto, menos aroma queda. A 96% el destilado tiene tan poco olor que se le llama neutro. Imagina una radio: cuanto más sube el volumen del alcohol, menos se oye la música de los aromas.","Yeast + sugar → ethanol + carbon dioxide.":"Levadura + azúcar → etanol + dióxido de carbono.","Fermented liquid is usually 8–10% abv; yeast adds fruity aromas.":"El líquido fermentado suele tener un 8–10% vol.; las levaduras aportan aromas afrutados.","Distillation concentrates ethanol because it boils before water.":"La destilación concentra el etanol porque hierve antes que el agua.","Low strength = more aroma; high strength = less aroma; 96% = neutral.":"Grado bajo = más aroma; grado alto = menos aroma; 96% = neutro.","The pot still":"El alambique discontinuo","Whatever its shape, a pot still always has three parts: a pot sitting on a heat source, a cooled condenser and a pipe linking the two. The liquid boils in the pot, the vapours climb the still head and pass into the condenser, where a coiled tube bathed in cold water turns them back into liquid. Many modern pot stills are heated with steam; those used for Cognac still rely on gas burners.":"Sea cual sea su forma, un alambique discontinuo siempre tiene tres partes: una caldera sobre una fuente de calor, un condensador refrigerado y un tubo que los une. El líquido hierve en la caldera, los vapores suben por el capitel y pasan al condensador, donde un serpentín sumergido en agua fría los devuelve al estado líquido. Muchos alambiques modernos se calientan con vapor; los del coñac siguen usando quemadores de gas.","A pot still works in batches, much like a washing machine: load it, run the cycle, empty it and clean it before the next round. It cannot run non-stop. What is more, a single pass cannot turn the fermented liquid into a spirit. That is why most distillers run it twice: from about 10% abv to about 25%, then to about 75%. This is known as double pot still distillation.":"El alambique discontinuo trabaja por lotes, como una lavadora: se carga, se pone el programa, se vacía y se limpia antes de la siguiente tanda. No puede funcionar sin parar. Además, con una sola pasada no se consigue un destilado a partir del líquido fermentado. Por eso casi todos destilan dos veces: de un 10% aproximadamente se pasa a un 25% y luego a un 75%. Es la doble destilación.","The result is a spirit of relatively low strength, with medium to pronounced aroma intensity and plenty of character and complexity. That is why this still is chosen whenever a flavour-packed spirit is the goal. The price is labour: each batch takes time and care, and no matter how many times the spirit is redistilled, a pot still will never reach a very high-strength neutral spirit.":"El resultado es un destilado de grado relativamente bajo, con una intensidad aromática de media a pronunciada y mucho carácter y complejidad. Por eso se elige este alambique cuando se busca un destilado lleno de sabor. El precio es el trabajo: cada lote exige tiempo y atención, y por muchas veces que se redestile, el alambique discontinuo nunca llegará a un destilado neutro de grado muy alto.","Three parts: pot with heat source, condenser, linking pipe.":"Tres partes: caldera con fuente de calor, condensador, tubo de unión.","Batch process: emptied and cleaned after every distillation.":"Trabaja por lotes: se vacía y se limpia tras cada destilación.","Usually two distillations: ~10% → ~25% → ~75% abv.":"Normalmente dos destilaciones: ~10% → ~25% → ~75% vol.","Low strength, medium to pronounced aromas, lots of character; never neutral.":"Grado bajo, aromas de medios a pronunciados, mucho carácter; nunca neutro.","The column still":"El alambique de columna","Over time, distillers wanted a still that could run without stopping and reach very high strengths, which the pot still cannot do. The answer was the column: a vertical structure divided into many sections. Hot vapour enters at the bottom and rises, while liquid runs down. It is like stacking many distillations on top of one another, all happening at the same time.":"Con el tiempo se quiso un alambique capaz de trabajar sin parar y de llegar a grados muy altos, algo imposible para el alambique discontinuo. La respuesta fue la columna: una estructura vertical dividida en muchas secciones. El vapor caliente entra por abajo y sube, mientras el líquido baja. Es como apilar muchas destilaciones una encima de otra, todas a la vez.","The higher the vapour climbs in the column, the higher its alcohol level: the bottom section holds the weakest liquid, the top section the strongest, and that is where the spirit leaves the still. Because the distillations happen simultaneously and the column never needs emptying, production is continuous and fast. Think of an escalator that never stops, compared with the stop-start lift of the pot still.":"Cuanto más sube el vapor por la columna, más alto es su grado: la sección de abajo tiene el líquido menos alcohólico, la de arriba el más alcohólico, y de ahí sale el destilado. Como las destilaciones ocurren a la vez y no hay que vaciar la columna, el trabajo es continuo y rápido. Piensa en una escalera mecánica que nunca se detiene, frente al ascensor de viajes sueltos del alambique discontinuo.","Not all columns are alike. A short column with few sections gives a lower-strength spirit with medium or pronounced aromas, close to a pot still spirit. A tall column with many sections reaches high strengths and gives a light spirit. The very tallest reach 95% or 96% abv, producing a neutral spirit with almost no smell, the base of most vodkas.":"No todas las columnas son iguales. Una columna corta, con pocas secciones, da un destilado de grado más bajo, con aromas medios o pronunciados, parecido al de un alambique discontinuo. Una columna alta, con muchas secciones, alcanza grados elevados y da un destilado ligero. Las más altas de todas llegan al 95% o al 96% vol.: sale un destilado neutro, casi sin olor, base de muchos vodkas.","A column still runs continuously: many stacked, simultaneous distillations.":"La columna trabaja en continuo: muchas destilaciones apiladas y simultáneas.","The highest strength is at the top of the column.":"El grado más alto está en lo alto de la columna.","Short column = flavourful spirit, similar to a pot still.":"Columna corta = destilado aromático, parecido al del alambique discontinuo.","Tall column = light spirit; tallest = neutral at 95–96%.":"Columna alta = destilado ligero; la más alta = neutro al 95–96%.","Where flavour comes from":"De dónde viene el sabor","A spirit's flavour is built step by step. The raw material lays the foundation: grapes bring fruity and floral notes, agave brings herbal and peppery ones. Fermentation adds further aromas, mostly fruity. Then distillation decides how much of all this survives: at a low strength the aromas stay intense, at a very high strength they almost vanish. Each step works like a filter letting more or less character through.":"El sabor de un destilado se construye paso a paso. La materia prima pone la base: la uva aporta notas afrutadas y florales, el agave notas herbáceas y a pimienta. La fermentación añade otros aromas, sobre todo afrutados. Luego la destilación decide cuánto de todo eso sobrevive: a grado bajo los aromas siguen intensos, a grado muy alto casi desaparecen. Cada paso funciona como un filtro que deja pasar más o menos carácter.","What leaves the still is always colourless and dry, meaning it has no sugar. From here the producer takes one of three routes, often set by law as well. The spirit can stay unaged, kept briefly in stainless steel tanks so its colour and aromas stay as they were. It can be aged in oak barrels, usually for years. Or it can be flavoured with something other than wood, as happens with gin.":"Del alambique sale siempre un líquido incoloro y seco, es decir, sin azúcar. A partir de ahí el productor elige uno de tres caminos, que a menudo también marca la ley. Puede dejarlo sin envejecer, guardándolo poco tiempo en depósitos de acero inoxidable para que color y aromas sigan intactos. Puede envejecerlo en barricas de roble, normalmente durante años. O puede aromatizarlo con sabores distintos de la madera, como pasa con la ginebra.","The law often makes the choice for the producer. Scotch whisky, for instance, must spend time in oak, while a Tequila may be aged or not. So it always pays to ask: is this spirit unaged, oak-aged or flavoured? The answer already explains a great deal about its colour and its aromas, before it is even tasted.":"La ley a menudo decide por el productor. El whisky escocés, por ejemplo, tiene que pasar por roble, mientras que un tequila puede envejecerse o no. Por eso conviene preguntarse siempre: ¿este destilado es sin envejecer, envejecido o aromatizado? La respuesta ya explica mucho de su color y su aroma, incluso antes de probarlo.","Flavour comes from raw material, fermentation and distillation strength.":"El sabor nace de la materia prima, la fermentación y el grado de destilación.","Every newly made spirit is colourless and dry.":"Todo destilado recién hecho es incoloro y seco.","Three routes: unaged, oak-aged, flavoured.":"Tres caminos: sin envejecer, envejecido en roble, aromatizado.","The law often dictates the route.":"A menudo es la ley la que impone el camino.","Unaged or oak-aged":"Sin envejecer o en roble","An unaged spirit rests briefly in stainless steel, a material that gives nothing away: it stays clear and keeps the aromas born in the still. Oak, on the other hand, does real work. A barrel adds colour in a sequence that goes from lemon to gold, then amber and, very rarely, brown. The newer the barrel and the longer the spirit stays in it, the deeper the colour.":"Un destilado sin envejecer reposa poco tiempo en acero inoxidable, un material que no cede nada: sigue transparente y conserva los aromas nacidos en el alambique. El roble, en cambio, trabaja. Una barrica aporta color siguiendo una secuencia que va del limón al oro, luego al ámbar y, muy rara vez, al marrón. Cuanto más nueva es la barrica y más tiempo pasa dentro el destilado, más profundo es el color.","Oak also brings aromas: vanilla, cinnamon, cloves, coconut. A new barrel that has never been used gives a lot of them. A previously used barrel, called an old barrel, gives less, and a little less again with every reuse, just like a tea bag steeped several times. So the producer chooses between new barrels for a strong oak imprint and used barrels for a gentler touch.":"El roble también aporta aromas: vainilla, canela, clavo, coco. Una barrica nueva, nunca usada, da muchísimos. Una barrica ya usada, llamada vieja, da menos, y un poco menos con cada nuevo uso, como una bolsita de té que se infusiona varias veces. El productor elige, pues, entre barricas nuevas, para una huella de madera marcada, y usadas, para un toque más discreto.","Time matters too. During ageing, water and ethanol slowly evaporate through the wood, so what remains becomes more concentrated. After many years, sometimes decades, new aromas appear and add depth: fruit cake, dried fruit, leather, wood polish. That is why a long-aged spirit feels layered, with shades of flavour revealing themselves one after another.":"El tiempo también cuenta. Durante el envejecimiento, el agua y el etanol se evaporan despacio a través de la madera, y lo que queda se concentra. Tras muchos años, a veces décadas, aparecen aromas nuevos que dan profundidad: bizcocho de frutas, frutos secos, cuero, cera para muebles. Por eso un destilado muy envejecido parece tener capas, con matices que aparecen uno tras otro.","Unaged: a short rest in stainless steel, no colour or aroma added.":"Sin envejecer: breve paso por acero inoxidable, sin color ni aroma añadidos.","Oak colours: lemon → gold → amber → (rarely) brown.":"Colores del roble: limón → oro → ámbar → (raramente) marrón.","New barrel = more aroma (vanilla, spice, coconut); used barrel = less.":"Barrica nueva = más aromas (vainilla, especias, coco); usada = menos.","Over time: evaporation, concentration, dried fruit, leather, polish aromas.":"Con el tiempo: evaporación, concentración, aromas de frutos secos, cuero, cera.","Blending, flavouring and dilution":"Mezclar, aromatizar, diluir","Every barrel is its own little world: two barrels filled with the same spirit on the same day will never turn out exactly alike. The blender combines the contents of many barrels with two aims. The first is consistency: anyone buying the same bottle again expects the same taste. The second is complexity: bringing together spirits with different characters is the easiest way to create depth.":"Cada barrica es un pequeño mundo: dos barricas llenas del mismo destilado el mismo día nunca darán un resultado idéntico. El maestro mezclador combina el contenido de muchas barricas con dos objetivos. El primero es la regularidad: quien vuelve a comprar la misma botella espera el mismo sabor. El segundo es la complejidad: unir destilados de carácter distinto es la forma más sencilla de dar profundidad.","When flavours other than wood are wanted, three main techniques are used. The spirit can be redistilled together with herbs, seeds or spices, giving a flavoured but colourless liquid. The same plants can be left to soak in the spirit, like a cold herbal tea, so their flavours and colour seep out slowly. Or ready-made flavourings, natural or artificial, can simply be added.":"Cuando se buscan aromas distintos de la madera, se usan sobre todo tres técnicas. Se puede redestilar el alcohol junto con hierbas, semillas o especias, y se obtiene un líquido aromatizado pero incoloro. Se pueden dejar esas mismas plantas en remojo en el alcohol, como una infusión en frío: los aromas y también el color pasan poco a poco. O se pueden añadir aromas ya preparados, naturales o artificiales.","The last move before bottling is almost always dilution. Completely pure water is added and the vast majority of spirits come down to 40% abv. The reason is practical: alcohol that is too strong numbs the palate, making it impossible to taste or enjoy the spirit. The water brings no aroma; it simply lowers the strength, like opening a window in an overheated room.":"El último paso antes de embotellar es casi siempre la dilución. Se añade agua totalmente pura y la gran mayoría de los destilados baja al 40% vol. El motivo es práctico: un alcohol demasiado fuerte adormece el paladar e impide percibir y disfrutar el sabor. El agua no aporta ningún aroma: solo baja el grado, como abrir una ventana en una habitación demasiado caldeada.","Blending aims for consistency and complexity.":"La mezcla busca regularidad y complejidad.","Three ways to flavour: redistillation, maceration, added flavourings.":"Tres formas de aromatizar: redestilación, maceración, aromas añadidos.","Maceration also adds colour; redistillation gives a colourless liquid.":"La maceración también da color; la redestilación da un líquido incoloro.","Dilution with pure water, usually to 40% abv, makes the spirit drinkable.":"Dilución con agua pura, normalmente al 40% vol., para hacerlo bebible.","Sweetness and colour":"Dulzor y color","Since every spirit leaves the still dry, any sweetness you notice in the mouth was added afterwards, usually simply as sugar. Watch the wording: here, sweet refers only to the taste of sugar. A whiskey with vanilla and fruity aromas may seem sweet on the nose, but with no added sugar it is still dry. A sweet-smelling nose and a sweet palate are not the same thing.":"Como todo destilado sale seco del alambique, cualquier dulzor que notes en boca se ha añadido después, casi siempre con azúcar. Ojo con las palabras: aquí dulce se refiere solo al sabor del azúcar. Un whiskey con aromas de vainilla y fruta puede parecer dulce en nariz, pero si no lleva azúcar añadido sigue siendo seco. Una nariz golosa y un paladar dulce no son lo mismo.","Colour can come from several sources. Oak is the most natural one. Then there is caramel colouring: barrels give different shades, so the blender uses tiny amounts to keep every batch the same colour. Used properly, caramel is not sweet and adds no aroma. Other spirits, including many liqueurs, receive natural or artificial colourings, sometimes in very bright shades.":"El color puede venir de varias fuentes. El roble es la más natural. Luego está el caramelo colorante: las barricas dan tonos distintos, así que quien mezcla usa cantidades mínimas para que cada lote tenga el mismo color. Bien usado, el caramelo no es dulce y no añade aromas. Otros destilados, como muchos licores, reciben colorantes naturales o artificiales, a veces de tonos muy vivos.","This gives a useful tasting lesson: colour is no proof of age. Some spirits get all or nearly all of their colour from caramel, so an unaged spirit can be deeply coloured. An amber glass suggests long years in barrel, but only the label or knowledge of the style can confirm it.":"De ahí una lección útil para la cata: el color no demuestra la edad. Algunos destilados toman todo o casi todo su color del caramelo, así que puede existir un destilado sin envejecer de color intenso. Una copa ambarina hace pensar en largos años en barrica, pero solo la etiqueta o el conocimiento del estilo pueden confirmarlo.","Sweetness is always added after distillation, usually as sugar.":"El dulzor siempre se añade tras la destilación, normalmente con azúcar.","Sweet = taste of sugar, not a sweet-smelling aroma.":"Dulce = sabor a azúcar, no un aroma goloso.","Colour sources: oak, caramel, natural or artificial colourings.":"Fuentes de color: roble, caramelo, colorantes naturales o artificiales.","Colour does not prove age: an unaged spirit can be dark.":"El color no prueba la edad: un destilado sin envejecer puede ser oscuro.","From grapes to wine":"De la uva al vino","A grape brandy is simply wine that has been distilled, and Cognac is the most famous of them all. It comes from south-west France, from a clearly defined area north of the town of Bordeaux. Only grapes grown there can become Cognac: as with many products tied to a place, the name is a precise address rather than a recipe that can be copied elsewhere.":"Un brandy de uva no es más que vino destilado, y el coñac es el más famoso de todos. Nace en el suroeste de Francia, en una zona bien delimitada al norte de Burdeos. Solo la uva cultivada allí puede convertirse en coñac: como en muchos productos ligados a un territorio, el nombre es una dirección concreta y no una simple receta que se pueda copiar en otro lugar.","The grapes from this area give Cognac its basic aromas, fruity and floral. After harvest they are pressed to release their juice, which is full of sugar and so needs no complicated processing: it is fermented straight away. The result is a wine, and it is this wine, not the grapes, that goes into the still. Before it is a spirit, then, Cognac is a wine.":"Las uvas de esta zona dan al coñac sus aromas de base, afrutados y florales. Tras la vendimia se prensan para liberar el zumo, que es rico en azúcar y por eso no necesita transformaciones complicadas: se pone a fermentar enseguida. El resultado es un vino, y es ese vino, no la uva, lo que entra en el alambique. Antes de ser un destilado, el coñac es, por tanto, un vino.","Cognac follows the four steps of every spirit closely: processing the grapes, fermenting them into wine, distilling, and a final stage in barrel. One image helps: a bunch of Cognac grapes travels the same road as a bunch of wine grapes, but halfway along, instead of ending up in the glass, it takes the turning towards the still.":"El coñac sigue al pie de la letra los cuatro pasos de cualquier destilado: transformación de la uva, fermentación en vino, destilación y fase final en barrica. Para ubicarse basta una imagen: un racimo para coñac recorre el mismo camino que uno para vino, pero a mitad de trayecto, en lugar de acabar en la copa, toma el desvío hacia el alambique.","Grape brandy = distilled wine; Cognac is the best known.":"Brandy de uva = vino destilado; el coñac es el más conocido.","A defined area of south-west France, north of Bordeaux.":"Zona delimitada del suroeste de Francia, al norte de Burdeos.","The grapes give fruity and floral aromas.":"Las uvas aportan aromas afrutados y florales.","Grapes pressed, juice fermented straight away into wine.":"Uvas prensadas, zumo fermentado enseguida en vino.","Twice through the pot still":"Dos pasadas por el alambique discontinuo","For Cognac the law leaves no choice: the wine must be distilled twice in a pot still. No column allowed. It is slow, batch-by-batch work, because after every distillation the still has to be emptied and cleaned. Traditional Cognac stills are heated with gas burners, and the condenser is a coil sitting in cold water that is constantly refreshed.":"Para el coñac la ley no deja elección: el vino debe destilarse dos veces en alambique discontinuo. Nada de columna. Es un trabajo lento, por lotes, porque tras cada destilación hay que vaciar y limpiar el alambique. Los alambiques tradicionales del coñac se calientan con quemadores de gas y su condensador es un serpentín sumergido en agua fría que se renueva sin parar.","Why go to so much trouble? Because a pot still gives a spirit of relatively low strength that keeps plenty of flavour and character, exactly what a Cognac needs. A tall column would give a lighter, less expressive spirit and lose much of the grapes' fruity and floral aromas. You could say that double distillation protects the soul of the wine instead of wiping it out.":"¿Por qué tanto esfuerzo? Porque el alambique discontinuo da un destilado de grado relativamente bajo que conserva mucho sabor y carácter, justo lo que necesita un coñac. Una columna alta daría un destilado más ligero y menos expresivo, y perdería buena parte de los aromas afrutados y florales de la uva. Se podría decir que la doble destilación protege el alma del vino en lugar de borrarla.","By law: double distillation in a pot still.":"Por ley: doble destilación en alambique discontinuo.","Slow, labour-intensive batch work.":"Trabajo por lotes, lento y laborioso.","Traditional stills heated with gas burners.":"Alambiques tradicionales calentados con quemadores de gas.","Low strength = lots of flavour and character.":"Grado bajo = mucho sabor y carácter.","Oak, blending and age terms":"Roble, mezcla y menciones de edad","Fresh from the still, the future Cognac cannot yet use the name: the law requires at least two years in oak barrels. The wood gives it colour and aromas of vanilla and toast. The finest Cognacs stay in barrel far longer, becoming concentrated and developing notes of fruit cake, leather and wood polish, the mark of a long, slow maturation.":"Recién destilado, el futuro coñac aún no puede llamarse así: la ley exige al menos dos años en barricas de roble. La madera le da color y aromas de vainilla y pan tostado. Los mejores coñacs se quedan en barrica mucho más tiempo, se concentran y desarrollan notas de bizcocho de frutas, cuero y cera para muebles, señal de una maduración larga y lenta.","Nearly all Cognacs are blends of spirits of different ages: younger ones bring freshness, older ones depth, and together they create complexity. Before dilution and bottling it is common to add a little caramel colouring, to keep the shade consistent, and a touch of sweetening. So a Cognac can feel slightly rounded on the palate even though it left the still dry.":"Casi todos los coñacs son mezclas de destilados de distintas edades: los más jóvenes aportan frescura, los más viejos profundidad, y juntos dan complejidad. Antes de rebajar y embotellar es habitual añadir un poco de caramelo colorante, para mantener siempre el mismo tono, y endulzar ligeramente. Así, un coñac puede resultar algo redondo en boca aunque salga seco del alambique.","Three label terms show the age, and they always refer to the youngest spirit in the blend. VS guarantees at least 2 years, VSOP at least 4 years, XO at least 10 years. Picture a staircase with three steps: 2, 4 and 10. If a blend contains a 5-year-old and a 20-year-old spirit, it is the 5 that counts.":"En la etiqueta, tres menciones indican la edad, y siempre se refieren al destilado más joven de la mezcla. VS garantiza al menos 2 años, VSOP al menos 4 años y XO al menos 10 años. Imagina una escalera de tres peldaños: 2, 4 y 10. Si una mezcla lleva un destilado de 5 años y otro de 20, cuenta el de 5.","At least 2 years in oak by law; vanilla and toast.":"Al menos 2 años en roble por ley; vainilla y tostado.","Long ageing: fruit cake, leather, wood polish.":"Envejecimiento largo: bizcocho de frutas, cuero, cera para muebles.","Almost always blends; often caramel and a little sugar.":"Casi siempre mezclas; a menudo caramelo y algo de azúcar.","VS 2+ years, VSOP 4+ years, XO 10+ years: age of the youngest spirit.":"VS 2+ años, VSOP 4+ años, XO 10+ años: edad del destilado más joven.","Any raw material, anywhere":"Cualquier materia prima, en cualquier lugar","Vodka is the freest spirit of all. It can be made in any country in the world and from any plant-based raw material. There is no compulsory area of origin, as with Cognac, and no required ingredient, as agave is for Tequila. What makes a spirit a vodka is neither the place nor the plant: it is the strength it is distilled to.":"El vodka es el destilado más libre de todos. Se puede elaborar en cualquier país del mundo y a partir de cualquier materia prima vegetal. No hay una zona de origen obligatoria, como en el coñac, ni un ingrediente impuesto, como el agave en el tequila. Lo que convierte un destilado en vodka no es el lugar ni la planta: es el grado al que se destila.","Although the choice is open, some raw materials are linked with premium-quality vodka: cereals, especially barley, wheat and rye, and potatoes. After processing to make a sugary liquid, it is fermented just like any other spirit. So the first two steps are the classic ones; vodka's real distinguishing feature arrives with the third.":"Aunque la elección es libre, algunas materias primas se asocian con los vodkas de mayor calidad: los cereales, sobre todo cebada, trigo y centeno, y las patatas. Tras transformarlas para obtener un líquido azucarado, se fermenta como cualquier otro destilado. Los dos primeros pasos son, pues, los clásicos; la verdadera particularidad del vodka llega con el tercero.","Vodka can be made anywhere, from any raw material.":"El vodka se puede hacer en cualquier lugar, con cualquier materia prima.","It is defined by distillation strength, not place or plant.":"Lo define el grado de destilación, no el lugar ni la planta.","Premium vodka: cereals (barley, wheat, rye) and potatoes.":"Vodka de calidad: cereales (cebada, trigo, centeno) y patatas.","A neutral spirit, then diluted":"Un destilado neutro, después rebajado","Vodka is a diluted neutral spirit. To count as neutral, the spirit must reach at least 95% or 96% abv, depending on the law of the producing country. Such a high strength can only be achieved with a column still, although some producers use pot stills for part of the process. At that alcohol level almost no aroma remains, hence the name neutral.":"El vodka es un destilado neutro rebajado. Para ser neutro, el destilado debe alcanzar al menos el 95% o el 96% vol., según la ley del país donde se elabora. Un grado tan alto solo se consigue con alambique de columna, aunque algunos productores usan alambiques discontinuos en una parte del proceso. A ese nivel de alcohol casi no queda aroma: de ahí el nombre de neutro.","After distillation, vodka does not go into barrels: it stays unaged and clear. It is then diluted with pure water to bottling strength, typically 40% abv. Think of it as a blank canvas: the producer's whole effort goes into taking away rather than adding, so that what reaches the glass is a clean spirit with almost no smell.":"Tras la destilación, el vodka no pasa por barrica: queda sin envejecer y transparente. Después se rebaja con agua pura hasta el grado de embotellado, normalmente el 40% vol. Piensa en un lienzo en blanco: todo el trabajo del productor busca quitar, no añadir, para que en la copa quede un alcohol limpio y casi sin olor.","Neutral spirit: at least 95% or 96% abv, depending on national law.":"Destilado neutro: al menos 95% o 96% vol., según la ley del país.","A column still is needed; pot stills only for part of the process.":"Hace falta columna; el discontinuo solo en una parte del proceso.","Unaged, usually diluted to 40% abv.":"Sin envejecer, rebajada normalmente al 40% vol.","Neutral or with a little character":"Neutro o con algo de carácter","Most vodka aims for the most complete neutrality possible. That very lack of aroma is what makes it so popular in mixed drinks and cocktails: it blends into juices, sodas and liqueurs without imposing its own taste, adding alcohol while leaving the spotlight to the other ingredients. A bartender who wants to strengthen a drink without changing its flavour reaches for it first.":"La mayoría de los vodkas buscan la neutralidad más completa. Es precisamente esa falta de aroma lo que lo hace tan popular en combinados y cócteles: se funde con zumos, refrescos y licores sin imponer su sabor, aportando alcohol y dejando el protagonismo a los demás ingredientes. Quien está en la barra y quiere reforzar una bebida sin cambiar su sabor piensa enseguida en él.","Some vodkas, however, keep a hint of character. On the nose and palate there are faint touches of the raw material, such as a note of grain or potato. They remain very delicate, nowhere near the intensity of a whisky or a brandy, and are still correctly described as neutral. It is like the difference between mineral water and distilled water: subtle, but noticeable.":"Algunos vodkas, sin embargo, conservan un toque de carácter. En nariz y en boca se perciben ligeras notas de la materia prima, por ejemplo un toque de cereal o de patata. Siguen siendo muy delicados, muy lejos de la intensidad de un whisky o un brandy, y se siguen describiendo correctamente como neutros. Es como la diferencia entre agua mineral y agua destilada: sutil, pero perceptible.","Most vodka is as neutral as possible.":"La mayoría de los vodkas son lo más neutros posible.","Neutrality makes it versatile in mixed drinks and cocktails.":"Su neutralidad lo hace versátil en combinados y cócteles.","Some show faint raw-material notes but are still neutral.":"Algunos muestran ligeras notas de materia prima, pero siguen siendo neutros.","Which definition best describes a spirit?":"¿Qué definición describe mejor un destilado?","An alcoholic drink made stronger by distillation":"Una bebida alcohólica hecha más fuerte por la destilación","An alcoholic drink made stronger by fermentation":"Una bebida alcohólica hecha más fuerte por la fermentación","An alcoholic drink that is always aged in oak":"Una bebida alcohólica siempre envejecida en roble","An alcoholic drink that always has sugar added":"Una bebida alcohólica a la que siempre se añade azúcar","Distillation is what raises the alcohol level and turns a fermented liquid into a spirit.":"Es la destilación la que sube el grado y convierte un líquido fermentado en destilado.","Fermentation creates the alcohol but stops at around 8–10%: on its own it gives a drink like wine or beer, not a spirit. Many spirits, vodka for example, never see oak, and most receive no sugar. Only distillation is shared by every spirit.":"La fermentación crea el alcohol pero se queda en torno al 8–10%: por sí sola da una bebida como el vino o la cerveza, no un destilado. Muchos destilados, como el vodka, nunca pasan por roble, y la mayoría no lleva azúcar. Solo la destilación es común a todos.","In which order do the four steps of spirit production happen?":"¿En qué orden se suceden los cuatro pasos de la producción de un destilado?","Raw material, fermentation, distillation, post-distillation":"Materia prima, fermentación, destilación, fase final","Raw material, distillation, fermentation, post-distillation":"Materia prima, destilación, fermentación, fase final","Fermentation, raw material, distillation, post-distillation":"Fermentación, materia prima, destilación, fase final","Raw material, post-distillation, fermentation, distillation":"Materia prima, fase final, fermentación, destilación","First a sugary liquid is made, then fermented, then distilled, and finally finished.":"Primero se obtiene un líquido azucarado, luego se fermenta, se destila y por último se termina.","Distillation needs a liquid that already contains alcohol, so it cannot come before fermentation. Fermentation, in turn, needs sugar, which comes from the processed raw material. Ageing, sweetening or dilution only happen once the spirit has left the still.":"La destilación necesita un líquido que ya contenga alcohol, así que no puede ir antes de la fermentación. Y la fermentación necesita azúcar, que procede de la materia prima transformada. El envejecimiento, el endulzado o la dilución solo llegan cuando el destilado ha salido del alambique.","What is the main aim of processing the raw material?":"¿Cuál es el objetivo principal de transformar la materia prima?","To create a sugary liquid that can ferment":"Obtener un líquido azucarado que pueda fermentar","To create an already alcoholic liquid for distilling":"Obtener un líquido ya alcohólico para destilar","To remove all the plant's aromas":"Eliminar todos los aromas de la planta","To give colour to the future spirit":"Dar color al futuro destilado","Without a sugary liquid, yeast has nothing to turn into alcohol.":"Sin un líquido azucarado, las levaduras no tienen nada que convertir en alcohol.","Alcohol only appears with fermentation, the next step. The raw material's aromas are not removed: on the contrary, each plant leaves its mark on the spirit. Colour, when there is any, is decided much later, after distillation.":"El alcohol solo aparece con la fermentación, el paso siguiente. Los aromas de la materia prima no se eliminan: al contrario, cada planta deja su huella en el destilado. El color, cuando lo hay, se decide mucho después, tras la destilación.","Which statement about the raw materials for spirits is correct?":"¿Qué afirmación sobre las materias primas de los destilados es correcta?","They must be of plant origin":"Deben ser de origen vegetal","They must always be cereals":"Tienen que ser siempre cereales","They must already contain ready sugar":"Deben contener azúcar ya disponible","They must grow in a hot climate":"Deben crecer en un clima cálido","In theory any plant can be used, but it has to be a plant.":"En teoría puede servir cualquier planta, pero debe ser un vegetal.","Grapes, sugar cane, agave and potatoes show that cereals are not the only option. Some plants, cereals among them, contain no sugar and must be processed to create it, so ready-made sugar is not a requirement. A hot climate suits sugar cane, not every raw material.":"La uva, la caña de azúcar, el agave y la patata demuestran que los cereales no son la única opción. Algunas plantas, como los cereales, no tienen azúcar y hay que transformarlas para crearlo, así que el azúcar ya disponible no es obligatorio. El clima cálido conviene a la caña de azúcar, no a todas las materias primas.","A distiller is using a raw material that contains no sugar. What must happen?":"Un destilador trabaja con una materia prima que no contiene azúcar. ¿Qué debe hacer?","Process it to create sugar before fermentation":"Transformarla para crear azúcar antes de la fermentación","Distil it directly without fermenting it":"Destilarla directamente sin fermentarla","Add extra yeast, which replaces the sugar":"Añadir más levadura, que sustituye al azúcar","Age it in oak so it develops sugar":"Envejecerla en roble para que desarrolle azúcar","Fermentation needs sugar, so it has to be created from the raw material itself.":"La fermentación necesita azúcar, así que hay que crearlo a partir de la propia materia prima.","Without fermentation there is no alcohol to concentrate, so distilling straight away would make no sense. Yeast does not replace sugar: it eats it. Oak comes after distillation and creates no sugar to ferment.":"Sin fermentación no hay alcohol que concentrar, así que destilar directamente no tendría sentido. La levadura no sustituye al azúcar: se lo come. El roble llega después de la destilación y no crea azúcar para fermentar.","During fermentation, yeast turns sugar into…":"Durante la fermentación, las levaduras convierten el azúcar en…","ethanol and carbon dioxide":"etanol y dióxido de carbono","ethanol and pure water":"etanol y agua pura","carbon dioxide and caramel":"dióxido de carbono y caramelo","starch and oxygen":"almidón y oxígeno","Yeast produces the alcohol that is wanted, ethanol, and a waste gas, carbon dioxide.":"Las levaduras producen el alcohol que interesa, el etanol, y un gas de desecho, el dióxido de carbono.","Water is already in the sugary liquid; yeast does not create it. Caramel is a colouring that may be added at the very end. Starch is what some cereals contain before it is turned into sugar: a starting point, not a product.":"El agua ya está en el líquido azucarado; no la crean las levaduras. El caramelo es un colorante que se puede añadir al final. El almidón es lo que contienen algunos cereales antes de convertirse en azúcar: un punto de partida, no un resultado.","What strength does a freshly fermented liquid usually have?":"¿Qué grado suele tener un líquido recién fermentado?","Between 8% and 10% abv":"Entre un 8% y un 10% vol.","Between 25% and 30% abv":"Entre un 25% y un 30% vol.","About 40% abv":"Alrededor del 40% vol.","Between 1% and 2% abv":"Entre un 1% y un 2% vol.","Fermentation gives a weak liquid of around 8–10%, which distillation will then make stronger.":"La fermentación da un líquido flojo, en torno al 8–10%, que la destilación hará más fuerte.","About 25% is typical after the first pass through a pot still, not after fermentation. 40% is the most common bottling strength, reached by diluting the spirit. 1–2% would be far too low: yeast produces much more alcohol than that.":"Alrededor del 25% es el grado típico tras la primera pasada por un alambique discontinuo, no tras la fermentación. El 40% es el grado más habitual en botella, que se logra rebajando el destilado. Un 1–2% sería muy poco: las levaduras producen bastante más alcohol.","Apart from alcohol, what does fermentation add to the future spirit?":"Además del alcohol, ¿qué aporta la fermentación al futuro destilado?","New aromas, especially fruity ones":"Nuevos aromas, sobre todo afrutados","Vanilla and coconut aromas":"Aromas de vainilla y coco","A golden colour":"Un color dorado","Sweetness that stays in the spirit":"Dulzor que permanece en el destilado","Besides alcohol, yeast creates aromas, fruity ones in particular.":"Además de alcohol, las levaduras crean aromas, en particular afrutados.","Vanilla and coconut are typical oak aromas, so they come from ageing. A golden colour also comes from oak or caramel. Yeast eats the sugar, and in any case every newly made spirit is dry: sweetness can only be added later.":"La vainilla y el coco son aromas típicos del roble, así que llegan con el envejecimiento. El color dorado también viene del roble o del caramelo. Las levaduras consumen el azúcar y, de todos modos, todo destilado recién hecho es seco: el dulzor solo se añade después.","What is the main aim of distillation?":"¿Cuál es el objetivo principal de la destilación?","To concentrate the ethanol in the fermented liquid":"Concentrar el etanol del líquido fermentado","To turn sugar into alcohol":"Convertir el azúcar en alcohol","To add colour and woody aromas":"Aportar color y aromas de madera","To lower the strength so it is drinkable":"Bajar el grado para hacerlo bebible","Distillation separates and concentrates the alcohol that fermentation has already created.":"La destilación separa y concentra el alcohol que ya ha creado la fermentación.","Turning sugar into alcohol is yeast's job, during fermentation. Colour and woody aromas come from oak, after distillation. Lowering the strength is the role of dilution with water before bottling: the exact opposite of distillation.":"Convertir el azúcar en alcohol es trabajo de las levaduras, durante la fermentación. El color y los aromas de madera llegan con el roble, tras la destilación. Bajar el grado es tarea de la dilución con agua antes de embotellar: justo lo contrario de destilar.","Why does heating a fermented liquid give vapours that are richer in alcohol?":"¿Por qué al calentar un líquido fermentado se obtienen vapores más alcohólicos?","Because ethanol boils at a lower temperature than water":"Porque el etanol hierve a una temperatura más baja que el agua","Because water boils at a lower temperature than ethanol":"Porque el agua hierve a una temperatura más baja que el etanol","Because heat turns the remaining sugar into alcohol":"Porque el calor convierte el azúcar restante en alcohol","Because the condenser adds alcohol to the vapours":"Porque el condensador añade alcohol a los vapores","Because it boils first, ethanol makes up a bigger share of the vapours than water does.":"Como hierve antes, el etanol pasa a los vapores en mayor proporción que el agua.","If water boiled first, the vapours would be more watery, not more alcoholic. Heat creates no new alcohol: alcohol only comes from yeast. The condenser simply cools the vapours so they turn back into liquid.":"Si el agua hirviera antes, los vapores serían más acuosos, no más alcohólicos. El calor no crea alcohol nuevo: el alcohol solo nace con las levaduras. El condensador se limita a enfriar los vapores para que vuelvan a ser líquidos.","A label reads 40% abv. What does this mean?":"Una etiqueta indica 40% vol. ¿Qué significa?","That 40% of the liquid is alcohol":"Que el 40% del líquido es alcohol","That 40% of the liquid is sugar":"Que el 40% del líquido es azúcar","That the spirit has been aged for 40 months":"Que el destilado tiene 40 meses de envejecimiento","That 40% of the liquid is water":"Que el 40% del líquido es agua","The abbreviation gives the percentage of alcohol in the volume of liquid.":"La indicación da el porcentaje de alcohol en el volumen del líquido.","The figure measures alcohol, not sugar or age. If 40% is alcohol, the rest, around 60%, is mostly water, so the last option gets the numbers the wrong way round.":"El grado mide el alcohol, no el azúcar ni la edad. Si el 40% es alcohol, el resto, alrededor del 60%, es sobre todo agua: la última opción invierte las cifras.","How is distillation strength linked to aroma intensity?":"¿Qué relación hay entre el grado de destilación y la intensidad aromática?","The lower the strength, the more intense the aromas":"Cuanto más bajo el grado, más intensos los aromas","The higher the strength, the more intense the aromas":"Cuanto más alto el grado, más intensos los aromas","Strength has no effect on aromas":"El grado no influye en los aromas","Only the bottling strength affects the aromas":"Solo el grado en botella influye en los aromas","Distilling to a low strength keeps more aromas; distilling to a high strength strips them away.":"Destilando a grado bajo se conservan más aromas; a grado alto se pierden.","The link is inverse: a spirit at 96% abv is so low in aroma that it is called neutral, so distillation strength clearly matters. Dilution before bottling uses pure water and adds no aroma: the style is set earlier, in the still.":"La relación es inversa: un destilado a 96% es tan pobre en aromas que se le llama neutro, así que el grado de destilación es decisivo. La dilución antes de embotellar usa agua pura y no añade aromas: el estilo se decide antes, en el alambique.","What is a spirit distilled to 96% abv, with almost no aroma, called?":"¿Cómo se llama un destilado llevado al 96% vol. y casi sin aromas?","Neutral":"Neutro","Flavoured":"Aromatizado","Aged":"Envejecido","Liqueur":"Licor","At that strength so little aroma remains that the spirit is called neutral.":"A ese grado queda tan poco aroma que el destilado se llama neutro.","A flavoured spirit has had flavours added, and a liqueur has been sweetened as well: both happen after distillation. Aged means time in oak, which adds aromas rather than removing them.":"Un destilado aromatizado ha recibido aromas añadidos, y un licor además está endulzado: ambas cosas ocurren después de la destilación. Envejecido indica paso por roble, que aporta aromas en lugar de quitarlos.","Within what range does the strength of a newly made spirit vary?":"¿Entre qué valores varía el grado de un destilado recién salido del alambique?","From about 60% to 96% abv":"De un 60% a un 96% vol. aproximadamente","From about 40% to 60% abv":"De un 40% a un 60% vol. aproximadamente","From about 8% to 40% abv":"De un 8% a un 40% vol. aproximadamente","From about 90% to 100% abv":"De un 90% a un 100% vol. aproximadamente","Newly made spirits run from about 60%, the most aromatic, up to 96%, the neutral ones.":"Los destilados recién hechos van de un 60%, los más aromáticos, a un 96%, los neutros.","40% is the usual bottling strength after dilution, not the strength leaving the still. 8–10% is the fermented liquid, before distillation. 96% is the ceiling: 100% is not reached, and many aromatic spirits come off the still well below 90%.":"El 40% es el grado típico en botella, tras la dilución, no a la salida del alambique. El 8–10% es el del líquido fermentado, antes de destilar. El 96% es el máximo: no se llega al 100%, y muchos destilados aromáticos salen bastante por debajo del 90%.","Which statement about the pot still is correct?":"¿Qué afirmación sobre el alambique discontinuo es correcta?","It must be emptied and cleaned after each distillation":"Hay que vaciarlo y limpiarlo tras cada destilación","It can run continuously without ever stopping":"Puede funcionar en continuo sin detenerse nunca","It easily produces neutral spirits at 96% abv":"Produce fácilmente destilados neutros al 96%","It is a vertical structure divided into many sections":"Es una estructura vertical dividida en muchas secciones","A pot still works in batches: once a batch is finished, it is emptied and cleaned.":"El alambique discontinuo trabaja por lotes: al terminar uno, se vacía y se limpia.","Continuous running, neutral strengths and a tall structure divided into sections all describe the column still. However many times it is used, a pot still never reaches a very high-strength neutral spirit.":"El funcionamiento continuo, los grados neutros y la estructura vertical por secciones son rasgos de la columna. Por muchas veces que se destile, el alambique discontinuo nunca llega a un destilado neutro de grado muy alto.","In double pot still distillation, which sequence of strengths is most realistic?":"En una doble destilación en alambique discontinuo, ¿qué secuencia de grados es la más realista?","About 10% → about 25% → about 75%":"Aprox. 10% → aprox. 25% → aprox. 75%","About 10% → about 40% → about 96%":"Aprox. 10% → aprox. 40% → aprox. 96%","About 25% → about 50% → about 75%":"Aprox. 25% → aprox. 50% → aprox. 75%","About 2% → about 10% → about 40%":"Aprox. 2% → aprox. 10% → aprox. 40%","It starts from a fermented liquid of about 10%, rises to about 25%, then to about 75%.":"Se parte de un líquido fermentado de un 10%, se sube a un 25% y luego a un 75%.","A pot still cannot reach 96%: that strength is typical of the tallest column stills. The starting liquid is not 25%, since fermentation stops around 8–10%. And finishing at 40% matches bottling strength, not a newly made spirit.":"Un alambique discontinuo no puede llegar al 96%: ese grado es propio de las columnas más altas. El líquido de partida no está al 25%, porque la fermentación se detiene hacia el 8–10%. Y acabar en un 40% corresponde al grado de embotellado, no a un destilado recién hecho.","In a pot still, which part turns the vapours back into liquid?":"En un alambique discontinuo, ¿qué parte devuelve los vapores al estado líquido?","The condenser":"El condensador","The pot":"La caldera","The heat source":"La fuente de calor","The still head":"El capitel","In the condenser, the vapours pass through a cooled coil and become liquid again.":"En el condensador, los vapores pasan por un serpentín refrigerado y vuelven a ser líquidos.","The pot holds the liquid and the heat source boils it: both create the vapours rather than cooling them. The still head simply carries the rising vapours towards the condenser.":"La caldera contiene el líquido y la fuente de calor lo hace hervir: ambas crean los vapores, no los enfrían. El capitel solo conduce los vapores hacia el condensador.","Which two needs led to the invention of the column still?":"¿Qué dos necesidades llevaron a inventar el alambique de columna?","Running continuously and reaching very high strengths":"Trabajar en continuo y alcanzar grados muy altos","Working in batches and getting more aroma":"Trabajar por lotes y obtener más aromas","Ageing faster and colouring the spirit":"Envejecer más rápido y dar color al destilado","Fermenting and distilling in the same vessel":"Fermentar y destilar en el mismo recipiente","The pot still stops after every batch and cannot reach high strengths: the column solves both limits.":"El alambique discontinuo se detiene en cada lote y no llega a grados altos: la columna resuelve ambos límites.","Working in batches is exactly the pot still's limitation, and a tall column gives less aroma, not more. The column has nothing to do with ageing or colour, which come later. Fermentation remains a separate step before distillation.":"Trabajar por lotes es justamente el límite del alambique discontinuo, y una columna alta da menos aroma, no más. La columna no tiene nada que ver con el envejecimiento ni con el color, que llegan después. La fermentación sigue siendo un paso aparte, previo a la destilación.","In a column still, where is the liquid with the highest alcohol level?":"En un alambique de columna, ¿dónde está el líquido con el grado más alto?","On the top section":"En la sección más alta","On the bottom section":"En la sección más baja","Halfway up the column":"A media columna","It is the same on every section":"Es igual en todas las secciones","The higher the vapour rises, the richer in alcohol it gets: the top section is the strongest.":"Cuanto más sube el vapor, más alcohol tiene: la sección más alta es la más fuerte.","The bottom section, where hot vapour enters, holds the weakest liquid. Strength is neither uniform nor highest in the middle: it rises step by step, which is why the spirit leaves from the top.":"La sección de abajo, por donde entra el vapor caliente, tiene en cambio el líquido menos alcohólico. El grado no es uniforme ni máximo a media altura: crece poco a poco al subir, y por eso el destilado sale por arriba.","A distiller wants continuous production but a spirit with medium or pronounced aromas, similar to a pot still spirit. What should be chosen?":"Un destilador quiere trabajar en continuo pero obtener un destilado con aromas medios o pronunciados, parecido al de un alambique discontinuo. ¿Qué elige?","A short column with few sections":"Una columna corta con pocas secciones","A very tall column with many sections":"Una columna muy alta con muchas secciones","A pot still used three times":"Un alambique discontinuo usado tres veces","A tall column followed by dilution with water":"Una columna alta seguida de dilución con agua","A short column runs continuously but stops at a lower strength, keeping aromas.":"Una columna corta trabaja en continuo pero se queda en un grado más bajo y conserva aromas.","A very tall column reaches high strengths and gives light or neutral spirits. A pot still works in batches, so it does not meet the need for continuous production. Diluting with water lowers the strength but brings back no aroma: the water is pure and adds no flavour.":"Una columna muy alta alcanza grados elevados y da destilados ligeros o neutros. El alambique discontinuo trabaja por lotes, así que no cumple la exigencia de continuidad. Rebajar con agua baja el grado pero no devuelve aromas: el agua es pura y no aporta sabor.","A producer needs a spirit at 95% abv. Which equipment is required?":"Un productor necesita un destilado al 95% vol. ¿Qué equipo hace falta?","A very tall column still":"Un alambique de columna muy alto","A pot still and double distillation":"Un alambique discontinuo y una doble destilación","A long fermentation with lots of yeast":"Una fermentación larga con mucha levadura","Only the tallest columns, with the most sections, reach 95–96% abv.":"Solo las columnas más altas, con más secciones, llegan al 95–96%.","Double pot still distillation stops at around 75%, and no number of passes will produce a neutral spirit. A short column gives lower-strength, more aromatic spirits. Fermentation, however long, only reaches around 8–10%.":"La doble destilación en alambique discontinuo se queda en torno al 75%, y ningún número de pasadas da un destilado neutro. Una columna corta da destilados de menor grado y más aromáticos. La fermentación, por larga que sea, ronda solo el 8–10%.","Why do most pot still distillers distil twice?":"¿Por qué la mayoría de quienes usan alambique discontinuo destilan dos veces?","Because a single pass is not enough to make a spirit":"Porque una sola pasada no basta para obtener un destilado","Because the second pass makes the spirit neutral":"Porque la segunda pasada vuelve neutro el destilado","Because the first pass only cleans the still":"Porque la primera pasada solo sirve para limpiar el alambique","Because the second pass adds sugar and colour":"Porque la segunda pasada añade azúcar y color","From the fermented liquid, one pass only reaches about 25%: a second is needed to make a spirit.":"A partir del líquido fermentado, una pasada solo llega a un 25%: hace falta otra para tener un destilado.","Even after two passes the spirit stays around 75% and full of character: it does not become neutral. Cleaning happens between batches, not through a distillation. And every spirit leaves the still colourless and dry: sugar and colour can only be added afterwards.":"Incluso tras dos pasadas el destilado se queda en torno al 75% y lleno de carácter: no se vuelve neutro. La limpieza se hace entre lotes, no con una destilación. Y todo destilado sale incoloro y seco: el azúcar y el color solo se añaden después, si se quiere.","What is a newly made spirit like as it leaves the still?":"¿Cómo es un destilado recién salido del alambique?","Colourless and dry":"Incoloro y seco","Golden and dry":"Dorado y seco","Colourless and slightly sweet":"Incoloro y ligeramente dulce","Amber and sweet":"Ambarino y dulce","Every spirit is born clear and sugar-free; colour and sweetness only come later.":"Todo destilado nace transparente y sin azúcar; el color y el dulzor llegan después.","A golden or amber colour comes from oak or caramel, so from the post-distillation stage. Sugar does not travel with the vapours through the still, which is why any sweetness must be added afterwards.":"El color dorado o ambarino viene del roble o del caramelo, es decir, de la fase posterior a la destilación. El azúcar no pasa con los vapores por el alambique, así que cualquier dulzor debe añadirse después.","What is the main aim of the post-distillation stage?":"¿Cuál es el objetivo principal de la fase posterior a la destilación?","Adjusting colour, aroma, sweetness and strength to suit the style":"Ajustar color, aromas, dulzor y grado según el estilo","Turning the remaining alcohol into sugar":"Convertir el alcohol restante en azúcar","Raising the strength up to 96%":"Subir el grado hasta el 96%","Restarting fermentation":"Reiniciar la fermentación","After the still, colour, aroma, sweetness and strength are adjusted for the spirit being made.":"Tras el alambique se ajustan color, aromas, dulzor y grado según el destilado que se busca.","Alcohol does not turn back into sugar: sweetness, if wanted, is added. After distillation the strength usually goes down through dilution rather than up. And fermentation belongs to an earlier step, before the still.":"El alcohol no vuelve a ser azúcar: el dulzor, si se quiere, se añade. Tras la destilación el grado suele bajar con la dilución, no subir. Y la fermentación pertenece a un paso anterior, antes del alambique.","Where does an unaged spirit rest for a short time?":"¿Dónde reposa brevemente un destilado sin envejecer?","In stainless steel tanks":"En depósitos de acero inoxidable","In new oak barrels":"En barricas de roble nuevas","In used oak barrels":"En barricas de roble usadas","In the pot of the still":"En la caldera del alambique","Stainless steel adds no colour or aroma, so the spirit stays as it was.":"El acero inoxidable no aporta color ni aromas, así que el destilado sigue igual.","Any oak barrel, new or used, adds colour and aroma: that is exactly what ageing means. The pot of the still is for distilling, not for storing the finished spirit.":"Cualquier barrica de roble, nueva o usada, aporta color y aromas: eso es precisamente envejecer. La caldera sirve para destilar, no para guardar el destilado acabado.","In what order does a spirit's colour change as it ages in oak?":"¿En qué orden cambia el color de un destilado a medida que envejece en roble?","Lemon → gold → amber → brown":"Limón → oro → ámbar → marrón","Gold → lemon → brown → amber":"Oro → limón → marrón → ámbar","Amber → gold → lemon → brown":"Ámbar → oro → limón → marrón","Lemon → amber → brown → gold":"Limón → ámbar → marrón → oro","Colour darkens gradually from lemon to gold to amber, and only rarely to brown.":"El color se oscurece poco a poco del limón al oro y al ámbar, y solo rara vez al marrón.","The other sequences jumble the order: oak always darkens a spirit, so it never goes back from amber to lemon or from brown to gold. Brown is the end point and is seen only very rarely.":"Las otras secuencias desordenan los pasos: el roble siempre oscurece, así que un destilado no vuelve del ámbar al limón ni del marrón al oro. El marrón es el final y solo se ve muy rara vez.","Which barrel gives the most aroma to a spirit?":"¿Qué barrica aporta más aromas a un destilado?","A new oak barrel that has never been used":"Una barrica de roble nueva, nunca usada","A barrel already used twice":"Una barrica ya usada dos veces","A barrel used many times":"Una barrica usada muchas veces","A stainless steel tank":"Un depósito de acero inoxidable","A new barrel still has all of its aromas to give.":"La barrica nueva aún tiene todos sus aromas por ceder.","Each time a barrel is used it gives less aroma, so a barrel used twice or many times always gives less than a new one. Stainless steel gives nothing at all: that is precisely why it is used to keep a spirit unchanged.":"Con cada uso una barrica cede menos aromas, así que una usada dos o muchas veces siempre da menos que una nueva. El acero inoxidable no cede nada: por eso se usa para mantener el destilado intacto.","Which group of aromas typically comes from oak?":"¿Qué grupo de aromas procede típicamente del roble?","Vanilla, cinnamon, cloves, coconut":"Vainilla, canela, clavo, coco","Cut grass, olive, pepper":"Hierba cortada, aceituna, pimienta","Apple, lemon, white flowers":"Manzana, limón, flores blancas","Juniper, coriander, citrus peel":"Enebro, cilantro, piel de cítricos","Vanilla, warm spices and coconut are oak's classic signature.":"Vainilla, especias dulces y coco son la firma clásica del roble.","Grass, olive and pepper point to a raw material such as agave. Apple and flowers suggest fruit and fermentation, not wood. Juniper and coriander are plants added to flavour a spirit such as gin.":"La hierba, la aceituna y la pimienta recuerdan más a una materia prima como el agave. La manzana y las flores evocan fruta y fermentación, no madera. El enebro y el cilantro son plantas añadidas para aromatizar un destilado como la ginebra.","Why does a spirit become more concentrated during long ageing?":"¿Por qué un destilado se concentra con un largo envejecimiento?","Because water and ethanol evaporate through the barrel":"Porque el agua y el etanol se evaporan a través de la barrica","Because the oak adds sugar to the spirit":"Porque el roble añade azúcar al destilado","Because the alcohol level rises every year":"Porque el grado sube cada año","Because fermentation restarts in the barrel":"Porque la fermentación se reanuda en la barrica","As water and ethanol evaporate, the remaining aromas become concentrated.":"Al evaporarse el agua y el etanol, los aromas que quedan se concentran.","Oak gives colour and aroma, not sugar: sweetness is added separately. The point is not a rising strength, since ethanol evaporates too. And there is no sugar left in the barrel to ferment.":"El roble da color y aromas, no azúcar: el dulzor se añade aparte. No se trata de que suba el grado, porque el etanol también se evapora. Y en la barrica ya no queda azúcar que fermentar.","A spirit has spent several decades in barrel. Which aromas are most likely?":"Un destilado ha pasado varias décadas en barrica. ¿Qué aromas es más probable encontrar?","Fruit cake, dried fruit, leather, wood polish":"Bizcocho de frutas, frutos secos, cuero, cera para muebles","Fresh grass, green apple, white flowers":"Hierba fresca, manzana verde, flores blancas","No aroma at all: the spirit becomes neutral":"Ningún aroma: el destilado se vuelve neutro","Only light vanilla, as after a few months":"Solo vainilla ligera, como tras unos meses","Very long ageing brings complex aromas of dried fruit, leather and polish.":"Un envejecimiento muy largo trae aromas complejos de frutos secos, cuero y cera.","Fresh grass and green apple suggest a young spirit. Oak adds aromas rather than removing them, so the spirit does not become neutral. A light vanilla note is typical of short ageing, whereas decades bring concentration and new layers.":"La hierba fresca y la manzana verde recuerdan a un destilado joven. El roble añade aromas en lugar de quitarlos, así que el destilado no se vuelve neutro. Una vainilla ligera es típica de un envejecimiento corto, mientras que décadas aportan concentración y nuevos matices.","What are the two main aims of blending oak-aged spirits?":"¿Cuáles son los dos objetivos principales de mezclar destilados envejecidos?","Consistency and complexity":"Regularidad y complejidad","Higher strength and less aroma":"Más grado y menos aromas","Faster ageing and fewer barrels":"Envejecimiento más rápido y menos barricas","Blending keeps every bottle tasting the same and builds depth.":"Se mezcla para que cada botella sepa igual y para dar profundidad.","Sweetness and colour are adjusted with sugar and caramel, separate steps from blending. Mixing barrels neither raises the strength nor strips aroma. Blending does not shorten ageing; in fact it needs many different barrels.":"El dulzor y el color se ajustan con azúcar y caramelo, pasos distintos de la mezcla. Mezclar barricas no sube el grado ni quita aromas. La mezcla no acorta el envejecimiento; al contrario, necesita muchas barricas distintas.","Why does a blender add small amounts of caramel colouring?":"¿Por qué quien mezcla añade pequeñas cantidades de caramelo colorante?","To give every batch the same colour":"Para que cada lote tenga el mismo color","To make the spirit sweeter":"Para hacer el destilado más dulce","To add vanilla aromas":"Para añadir aromas de vainilla","To raise the alcohol level":"Para subir el grado","Barrels give different shades; caramel evens out the colour from batch to batch.":"Las barricas dan tonos distintos; el caramelo iguala el color de un lote a otro.","Caramel colouring is not sweet and, used properly, adds no aroma: vanilla comes from oak. It contains no alcohol, so it cannot raise the strength. It is there purely for appearance.":"El caramelo colorante no es dulce y, bien usado, no añade aromas: la vainilla viene del roble. No contiene alcohol, así que no puede subir el grado. Solo sirve para el aspecto.","A customer says: 'This spirit is dark, so it must have been aged for a long time.' What is the best reply?":"Un cliente dice: «Este destilado es oscuro, así que tiene que estar muy envejecido». ¿Qué se le responde?","Not necessarily: the colour can come almost entirely from caramel":"No necesariamente: el color puede venir casi todo del caramelo","Yes, only oak can colour a spirit":"Sí, solo el roble puede dar color a un destilado","Yes, because a dark colour always means a new barrel":"Sí, porque un color oscuro siempre indica barrica nueva","No, because aged spirits are always pale":"No, porque los destilados envejecidos siempre son claros","Some spirits get all or nearly all their colour from caramel, so colour does not prove age.":"Algunos destilados toman todo o casi todo el color del caramelo, así que el color no prueba la edad.","Oak is not the only source of colour: there is caramel and other colourings. A new barrel does give more colour, but dark colour can have other causes. And aged spirits are not always pale: oak tends to darken them over time.":"El roble no es la única fuente de color: existen el caramelo y otros colorantes. Una barrica nueva da más color, pero un color oscuro puede tener otras causas. Y los destilados envejecidos no siempre son claros: el roble tiende a oscurecerlos con el tiempo.","Where does the sweetness you taste in a spirit come from?":"¿De dónde viene el dulzor que se nota en boca en un destilado?","From sugar added after distillation":"Del azúcar añadido tras la destilación","From the raw material's sugar passing through the still":"Del azúcar de la materia prima que pasa por el alambique","From caramel colouring":"Del caramelo colorante","From the water used for dilution":"Del agua usada para la dilución","Every spirit leaves the still dry, so sweetness has to be added later, usually as sugar.":"Todo destilado sale seco, así que el dulzor se añade después, normalmente como azúcar.","The raw material's sugar is eaten by yeast and does not travel with the vapours anyway. Caramel colouring is not sweet. Dilution water is pure and brings neither flavour nor sugar.":"Las levaduras se comen el azúcar de la materia prima y, de todos modos, no pasa con los vapores. El caramelo colorante no es dulce. El agua de dilución es pura y no aporta ni sabor ni azúcar.","A whiskey with no added sugar has intense vanilla and fruit aromas. How should its palate be described?":"Un whiskey sin azúcar añadido tiene intensos aromas de vainilla y fruta. ¿Cómo se describe en boca?","Dry, because sweet refers only to the taste of sugar":"Seco, porque dulce se refiere solo al sabor del azúcar","Sweet, because vanilla and fruit are sweet aromas":"Dulce, porque la vainilla y la fruta son aromas dulces","Sweet, because oak adds sugar":"Dulce, porque el roble añade azúcar","Neutral, because it has no sugar":"Neutro, porque no tiene azúcar","With no added sugar the spirit is dry, even if the nose smells sweet.":"Sin azúcar añadido el destilado sigue seco, aunque la nariz parezca golosa.","Calling vanilla and fruit aromas sweet causes confusion: sweetness is a taste, tied to sugar. Oak adds no sugar. Neutral, on the other hand, describes a spirit with almost no aroma, the opposite of this whiskey.":"Llamar dulces a los aromas de vainilla y fruta crea confusión: el dulzor es un sabor ligado al azúcar. El roble no añade azúcar. Neutro, en cambio, describe un destilado casi sin aromas, lo contrario de este whiskey.","Why are most spirits diluted to 40% abv before bottling?":"¿Por qué la mayoría de los destilados se rebaja al 40% vol. antes de embotellar?","To make them drinkable: too much alcohol numbs the palate":"Para hacerlos bebibles: demasiado alcohol adormece el paladar","To add aromas through the water":"Para añadir aromas a través del agua","To make them sweeter":"Para hacerlos más dulces","To give them a paler, even colour":"Para darles un color más claro y uniforme","At very high strength it is impossible to taste or enjoy the spirit.":"A grados muy altos es imposible percibir y disfrutar el sabor.","The water is completely pure and adds no aroma or sugar. Colour is managed with oak or caramel, not water. Dilution only lowers the strength.":"El agua es totalmente pura y no aporta aromas ni azúcar. El color se ajusta con roble o caramelo, no con agua. La dilución solo sirve para bajar el grado.","Which of these steps adds no aroma to the spirit?":"¿Cuál de estos pasos no añade ningún aroma al destilado?","Dilution with pure water":"La dilución con agua pura","Ageing in a new barrel":"El envejecimiento en barrica nueva","Macerating herbs and spices":"La maceración de hierbas y especias","Fermentation with yeast":"La fermentación con levaduras","Pure water only lowers the strength and brings no flavour.":"El agua pura solo baja el grado y no aporta sabor.","A new barrel is the richest source of oak aroma. Maceration exists precisely to draw flavour out of plants. And fermentation creates fruity aromas as well as alcohol.":"Una barrica nueva es la fuente más rica de aromas de roble. La maceración sirve precisamente para extraer los aromas de las plantas. Y la fermentación, además de alcohol, crea aromas afrutados.","What are the three most common ways to give a spirit flavours other than oak?":"¿Cuáles son las tres técnicas más comunes para dar a un destilado aromas distintos de la madera?","Redistillation, maceration, adding flavourings":"Redestilación, maceración, adición de aromas","Fermentation, blending, dilution":"Fermentación, mezcla, dilución","Caramel, sugar, water":"Caramelo, azúcar, agua","New barrel, used barrel, stainless steel":"Barrica nueva, barrica usada, acero inoxidable","The spirit is redistilled with plants, steeped with them, or given ready-made flavourings.":"Se redestila con las plantas, se dejan en remojo o se añaden aromas ya preparados.","Blending and dilution add no new flavours, and fermentation comes before the still. Caramel and water bring no aroma, while sugar brings sweetness. Barrels give exactly the oak flavours being excluded, and steel gives none.":"La mezcla y la dilución no añaden aromas nuevos, y la fermentación va antes del alambique. El caramelo y el agua no aportan aromas, el azúcar aporta dulzor. Las barricas dan precisamente aromas de madera, y el acero no da ninguno.","Which flavouring technique also gives the spirit colour?":"¿Qué técnica de aromatización también da color al destilado?","Maceration":"La maceración","Redistillation":"La redestilación","Dilution":"La dilución","Column distillation":"La destilación en columna","When plants steep in the spirit, both flavour and colour pass into it.":"Al dejar las plantas en remojo, pasan al destilado tanto los aromas como el color.","Redistilling with plants gives a flavoured but colourless liquid, because colour does not travel with the vapours. Dilution uses pure water. A column still is for distilling, not flavouring.":"La redestilación con plantas da un líquido aromatizado pero incoloro, porque el color no pasa con los vapores. La dilución usa agua pura. La columna sirve para destilar, no para aromatizar.","Which statement about post-distillation choices is correct?":"¿Qué afirmación sobre las decisiones posteriores a la destilación es correcta?","Scotch must be oak-aged, while Tequila may be aged or not":"El whisky escocés debe pasar por roble; el tequila puede no hacerlo","Tequila must be oak-aged, while Scotch may be aged or not":"El tequila debe pasar por roble; el whisky escocés puede no hacerlo","Producers are always free: the law never steps in":"El productor siempre es libre: la ley nunca interviene","Every spirit must spend at least a year in oak":"Todos los destilados deben pasar al menos un año en roble","Local laws limit the options: Scotch must be aged, Tequila can be young or aged.":"Las leyes locales limitan las opciones: el escocés debe envejecer, el tequila puede ser joven o envejecido.","The second option swaps the two cases. The law often steps in, so producers are not always free. And many spirits, vodka for one, never see oak: no rule imposes a year on all of them.":"La segunda opción invierte los dos casos. La ley interviene a menudo, así que el productor no siempre es libre. Y muchos destilados, como el vodka, nunca pasan por roble: ninguna norma impone un año a todos.","What is a grape brandy such as Cognac?":"¿Qué es un brandy de uva como el coñac?","A distilled wine":"Un vino destilado","Grape juice distilled without fermentation":"Zumo de uva destilado sin fermentar","A wine strengthened with neutral spirit":"Un vino reforzado con alcohol neutro","A grain spirit flavoured with grapes":"Un destilado de cereales aromatizado con uva","Grape juice is fermented into wine, and that wine is distilled.":"El zumo de uva fermenta en vino, y ese vino se destila.","Without fermentation there is no alcohol to distil, so the juice must first become wine. Adding spirit to a wine is not distilling it. And Cognac is made from grapes, not flavoured grain spirit.":"Sin fermentación no hay alcohol que destilar, así que el zumo primero debe convertirse en vino. Añadir alcohol a un vino no es destilarlo. Y el coñac nace de la uva, no de cereales aromatizados.","Where must the grapes for Cognac come from?":"¿De dónde deben proceder las uvas del coñac?","From an area of south-west France, north of Bordeaux":"De una zona del suroeste de Francia, al norte de Burdeos","From any vineyard in France":"De cualquier viñedo francés","From an area of south-east France, near the Mediterranean":"De una zona del sureste de Francia, cerca del Mediterráneo","From any country, as long as it is distilled in France":"De cualquier país, siempre que se destile en Francia","Cognac requires grapes from a specific area of south-west France, north of Bordeaux.":"El coñac exige uvas de una zona concreta del suroeste francés, al norte de Burdeos.","It is not enough for the grapes to be French: they must come from that defined area. South-east France is a different region. And the place of distillation alone does not count: the grapes themselves must be grown in the area.":"No basta con que la uva sea francesa: debe venir de esa zona delimitada. El sureste de Francia es otra región. Y no cuenta solo el lugar de destilación: la propia uva tiene que nacer en la zona.","Which aromas do the grapes bring to Cognac?":"¿Qué aromas aportan las uvas al coñac?","Fruity and floral":"Afrutados y florales","Vanilla and toast":"Vainilla y pan tostado","Herbal and peppery":"Herbáceos y a pimienta","Cereal and smoke":"Cereal y humo","Grapes, the raw material, give Cognac its fruity and floral notes.":"La uva, materia prima, da al coñac sus notas afrutadas y florales.","Vanilla and toast are there, but they come from oak, not grapes. Herbal and peppery notes are typical of agave. Cereal and smoke suggest a malt whisky, not a wine spirit.":"La vainilla y el tostado están, pero vienen del roble, no de la uva. Las notas herbáceas y a pimienta son típicas del agave. El cereal y el humo hacen pensar en un whisky de malta, no en un destilado de vino.","What happens to the freshly pressed juice destined for Cognac?":"¿Qué ocurre con el zumo recién prensado destinado al coñac?","It is fermented straight away into wine":"Fermenta enseguida y se convierte en vino","It is distilled at once, before fermenting":"Se destila enseguida, antes de fermentar","It is cooked to create sugar":"Se cuece para crear azúcar","It is aged in oak for two years":"Se envejece dos años en roble","Grape juice is already full of sugar, so it is fermented into wine right away.":"El zumo de uva ya es rico en azúcar, así que fermenta enseguida en vino.","Distilling before fermentation would leave no alcohol to concentrate. Cooking to create sugar is for raw materials like agave, not grapes. The two years in oak apply to the spirit after distillation, not to the juice.":"Destilar antes de fermentar no daría alcohol que concentrar. La cocción para crear azúcares es para materias primas como el agave, no para la uva. Los dos años en roble se aplican al destilado, tras el alambique, no al zumo.","How must Cognac be distilled by law?":"¿Cómo debe destilarse el coñac por ley?","Twice in a pot still":"Dos veces en alambique discontinuo","Once in a tall column still":"Una vez en una columna alta","Only once in a pot still":"Una sola vez en alambique discontinuo","Continuously, up to 96% abv":"En continuo, hasta el 96% vol.","The law requires double distillation in a pot still.":"La ley impone la doble destilación en alambique discontinuo.","A column and continuous distillation to 96% would give a light or neutral spirit, far from the Cognac style. A single pass through a pot still is not enough to make a spirit from wine.":"La columna y la destilación en continuo hasta el 96% darían un destilado ligero o neutro, lejos del estilo del coñac. Una sola pasada por alambique discontinuo no basta para obtener un destilado a partir del vino.","Why is a pot still used for Cognac?":"¿Por qué se usa alambique discontinuo para el coñac?","It gives a low-strength spirit full of flavour and character":"Da un destilado de grado bajo, lleno de sabor y carácter","It gives a neutral spirit that is easy to flavour":"Da un destilado neutro, fácil de aromatizar","It runs continuously and is very fast":"Funciona en continuo y es muy rápido","It adds colour and sweetness by itself":"Añade por sí solo color y dulzor","The low strength keeps the grape aromas and gives a characterful spirit.":"El grado bajo conserva los aromas de la uva y da un destilado con carácter.","A pot still cannot make a neutral spirit: that is the job of the tallest columns. It works in batches, so it is slow rather than continuous. And every spirit leaves the still colourless and dry: colour and sweetness come later.":"El alambique discontinuo no puede hacer un destilado neutro: eso es cosa de las columnas más altas. Trabaja por lotes, así que es lento, no continuo. Y todo destilado sale incoloro y seco: el color y el dulzor llegan después.","How are Cognac pot stills traditionally heated?":"¿Cómo se calientan tradicionalmente los alambiques del coñac?","With gas burners":"Con quemadores de gas","With steam coils":"Con serpentines de vapor","With electric elements":"Con resistencias eléctricas","With heat from the sun":"Con el calor del sol","Cognac stills still use gas burners.":"Los alambiques del coñac siguen usando quemadores de gas.","Steam, through jackets or coils, heats many modern pot stills, which is exactly why it is the trap: Cognac is the exception. Electric elements and solar heat are not the traditional method.":"El vapor, con camisas o serpentines, calienta muchos alambiques modernos, y por eso es la trampa: el coñac es la excepción. Las resistencias eléctricas y el calor solar no son el método tradicional.","What is the minimum time in oak before a spirit can be called Cognac?":"¿Cuánto tiempo mínimo debe pasar un destilado en roble para llamarse coñac?","Two years":"Dos años","Six months":"Seis meses","Four years":"Cuatro años","Ten years":"Diez años","The law requires at least two years in oak barrels.":"La ley exige al menos dos años en barricas de roble.","Six months is not enough. Four years is the minimum for VSOP and ten years for XO: these are higher ages tied to specific categories, not the threshold for using the name at all.":"Seis meses no bastan. Cuatro años es el mínimo para la mención VSOP y diez años para XO: son edades más altas ligadas a categorías concretas, no el umbral para poder usar el nombre.","Which aromas does oak give a young Cognac?":"¿Qué aromas da el roble a un coñac joven?","Flowers and fresh fruit":"Flores y fruta fresca","Peat smoke":"Humo de turba","Grass and olive":"Hierba y aceituna","Time in barrel adds vanilla and toasty notes to Cognac.":"El paso por barrica añade al coñac notas de vainilla y tostado.","Flowers and fresh fruit come from the grapes, not the wood. Peat smoke is found in some malt whiskies. Grass and olive are typical agave notes.":"Las flores y la fruta fresca vienen de la uva, no de la madera. El humo de turba aparece en algunos whiskies de malta. La hierba y la aceituna son notas típicas del agave.","A very old Cognac shows fruit cake and leather aromas. Where do they come from?":"Un coñac muy viejo muestra aromas de bizcocho de frutas y cuero. ¿De dónde vienen?","From long ageing in barrel":"De un largo envejecimiento en barrica","From the fermentation of the juice":"De la fermentación del zumo","From double distillation":"De la doble destilación","Many years in oak concentrate the spirit and develop these complex aromas.":"Muchos años en roble concentran el destilado y hacen nacer estos aromas complejos.","Fermentation mainly creates fresh fruity aromas, not evolved notes like leather. Double distillation keeps the grape aromas but does not create the aromas of age. Caramel, used properly, adds no aroma.":"La fermentación crea sobre todo aromas afrutados frescos, no notas evolucionadas como el cuero. La doble destilación conserva los aromas de la uva pero no crea los de la edad. El caramelo, bien usado, no añade aromas.","Which statement about Cognac is correct?":"¿Qué afirmación sobre el coñac es correcta?","Nearly all Cognacs are blends":"Casi todos los coñacs son mezclas","Nearly all Cognacs come from a single barrel":"Casi todos los coñacs proceden de una sola barrica","Cognac may never be blended":"El coñac nunca puede mezclarse","Cognac is only blended with vodka":"El coñac solo se mezcla con vodka","Combining spirits of different ages adds complexity, and nearly all Cognacs are blends.":"Unir destilados de distintas edades da complejidad, y casi todos los coñacs son mezclas.","Single-barrel Cognacs are the exception, not the rule. Blending is not forbidden; it is the norm. And Cognac spirits are blended with each other, not with other spirits such as vodka.":"Los coñacs de una sola barrica son la excepción, no la regla. Mezclar no está prohibido; es lo normal. Y se mezclan destilados de coñac entre sí, no con otros destilados como el vodka.","Which adjustments are common for Cognac before dilution and bottling?":"¿Qué retoques son habituales en el coñac antes de rebajar y embotellar?","A little caramel colouring and slight sweetening":"Un poco de caramelo colorante y un ligero endulzado","Adding herbs by maceration":"Añadir hierbas en maceración","A third distillation in a column":"Una tercera destilación en columna","Charcoal filtering to remove the colour":"El filtrado con carbón para quitar el color","Many producers use caramel to even out the colour and sweeten their Cognac slightly.":"Muchos productores usan caramelo para igualar el color y endulzan un poco su coñac.","Macerating herbs would turn Cognac into a flavoured spirit. Distillation happens only in pot stills, never columns. Stripping colour with charcoal would make no sense for a spirit valued precisely for the shade oak gives it.":"Macerar hierbas convertiría el coñac en un destilado aromatizado. La destilación solo se hace en alambique discontinuo, nunca en columna. Quitar el color con carbón no tendría sentido en un destilado que se aprecia precisamente por el tono que da el roble.","What does the term VS guarantee on a Cognac?":"¿Qué garantiza la mención VS en un coñac?","At least 2 years of ageing":"Al menos 2 años de envejecimiento","At least 4 years of ageing":"Al menos 4 años de envejecimiento","At least 10 years of ageing":"Al menos 10 años de envejecimiento","At least 6 months of ageing":"Al menos 6 meses de envejecimiento","VS matches the legal minimum: at least 2 years.":"VS corresponde al mínimo legal: al menos 2 años.","4 years is the minimum for VSOP and 10 years for XO. Six months is below the legal minimum: a spirit that young cannot even be called Cognac.":"4 años es el mínimo para VSOP y 10 años para XO. Seis meses están por debajo del mínimo legal: un destilado tan joven ni siquiera puede llamarse coñac.","What minimum age does VSOP guarantee?":"¿Qué edad mínima garantiza la mención VSOP?","4 years":"4 años","2 years":"2 años","6 years":"6 años","10 years":"10 años","VSOP guarantees the youngest spirit is at least 4 years old.":"VSOP garantiza que el destilado más joven tiene al menos 4 años.","2 years is VS and 10 years is XO. 6 years is not tied to any of the three terms: it sounds plausible but is made up.":"2 años corresponde a VS y 10 años a XO. 6 años no está ligado a ninguna de estas tres menciones: suena plausible pero es inventado.","A customer wants the Cognac with the longest minimum ageing. Which term should they look for?":"Un cliente busca el coñac con el envejecimiento mínimo más largo. ¿Qué mención debe buscar?","XO, at least 10 years":"XO, al menos 10 años","VSOP, at least 4 years":"VSOP, al menos 4 años","VS, at least 2 years":"VS, al menos 2 años","XO, at least 6 years":"XO, al menos 6 años","Of the three terms, XO guarantees the highest minimum age: 10 years.":"De las tres menciones, XO garantiza la edad mínima más alta: 10 años.","VSOP and VS guarantee 4 and 2 years respectively, so less. The last option names the right term with the wrong age: the XO minimum is 10 years.":"VSOP y VS garantizan 4 y 2 años respectivamente, es decir, menos. La última opción nombra la mención correcta con una edad equivocada: para XO el mínimo es de 10 años.","Which spirit does the age shown by VS, VSOP or XO refer to?":"¿A qué destilado se refiere la edad indicada por VS, VSOP o XO?","The youngest spirit in the blend":"Al destilado más joven de la mezcla","The oldest spirit in the blend":"Al destilado más viejo de la mezcla","The average age of the spirits":"A la edad media de los destilados","The years spent in the bottle":"A los años pasados en botella","The term guarantees a minimum age, which means the age of the youngest spirit.":"La mención garantiza la edad mínima, es decir, la del destilado más joven.","If the oldest spirit counted, a single old drop could lift the category. An average would also let very young spirits hide in the blend. Time in bottle does not count: ageing happens in barrel.":"Si contara el destilado más viejo, bastaría una gota antigua para subir de categoría. Una media también permitiría esconder destilados demasiado jóvenes. El tiempo en botella no cuenta: el envejecimiento ocurre en barrica.","A blend contains Cognacs aged 5, 8 and 15 years. What is the highest age term it can carry?":"Una mezcla contiene coñacs de 5, 8 y 15 años. ¿Qué mención de edad más alta puede llevar?","VSOP":"VSOP","XO":"XO","VS only":"Solo VS","No age term":"Ninguna mención","The youngest spirit counts, 5 years: that beats VSOP's 4 years but not XO's 10.":"Cuenta el destilado más joven, 5 años: supera los 4 de VSOP pero no los 10 de XO.","XO would need even the youngest spirit to be at least 10, and here it is only 5. VS would be allowed, but it is not the highest possible term. The blend is well past the 2-year minimum, so it can carry a term.":"XO exigiría que incluso el destilado más joven tuviera al menos 10 años, y aquí solo tiene 5. VS estaría permitido, pero no es la mención más alta posible. La mezcla supera de sobra los 2 años mínimos, así que puede llevar mención.","A wine spirit from the Cognac area, distilled by the rules, has spent 18 months in oak. Can it be sold as Cognac?":"Un destilado de vino de la zona de Cognac, destilado según las normas, ha pasado 18 meses en roble. ¿Se puede vender como coñac?","No, it needs at least two years in oak":"No, debe pasar al menos dos años en roble","Yes, as a VS":"Sí, como VS","Yes, as long as it was distilled twice":"Sí, basta con que se haya destilado dos veces","Yes, if caramel is added":"Sí, si se le añade caramelo","With less than two years in oak, the name Cognac is not allowed.":"Con menos de dos años en roble, el nombre coñac no está permitido.","VS is the youngest term but still requires at least 2 years. Double distillation is compulsory but does not replace ageing. Caramel only changes the colour, not the age.":"VS es la mención más joven, pero aun así exige al menos 2 años. La doble destilación es obligatoria pero no sustituye al envejecimiento. El caramelo solo cambia el color, no la edad.","What makes a spirit a vodka?":"¿Qué convierte un destilado en vodka?","Its distillation strength":"El grado de destilación","The raw material used":"La materia prima utilizada","The country of production":"El país de elaboración","The time spent in barrel":"El tiempo pasado en barrica","Vodka is defined by its very high distillation strength.":"El vodka se define por su grado de destilación, muy alto.","The raw material can be anything and vodka can be made in any country, so neither plant nor place defines it. Vodka does not go into barrels: it stays unaged.":"La materia prima puede ser cualquiera y el vodka se puede hacer en cualquier país, así que ni la planta ni el lugar lo definen. El vodka no pasa por barrica: queda sin envejecer.","Which raw material can vodka be made from?":"¿Con qué materia prima se puede hacer vodka?","Any plant-based raw material":"Con cualquier materia prima vegetal","Potatoes only":"Solo con patatas","Rye only":"Solo con centeno","Grapes only":"Solo con uva","Vodka has no required raw material: any plant will do.":"El vodka no tiene materia prima obligatoria: vale cualquier planta.","Potatoes and rye are favoured for premium vodka, but they are not compulsory. Grapes are possible too, but they are not the only choice: no ingredient is required.":"Las patatas y el centeno se valoran para el vodka de calidad, pero no son obligatorios. La uva también es posible, pero no es la única opción: ningún ingrediente es obligatorio.","Where can vodka be made?":"¿Dónde se puede elaborar vodka?","In any country in the world":"En cualquier país del mundo","Only in Russia and Poland":"Solo en Rusia y Polonia","Only in northern Europe":"Solo en el norte de Europa","Only where potatoes are grown":"Solo donde se cultivan patatas","Vodka has no required area of origin.":"El vodka no tiene zona de origen obligatoria.","Some countries have a long vodka tradition, but the law does not restrict production to them or to any region. And since the raw material is free, there is no need to grow potatoes to make it.":"Algunos países tienen una larga tradición de vodka, pero la ley no limita la elaboración a ellos ni a ninguna región. Y como la materia prima es libre, no hace falta cultivar patatas para hacerlo.","Which raw materials are often linked with premium vodka?":"¿Qué materias primas se asocian a menudo con los vodkas de mayor calidad?","Cereals such as barley, wheat and rye, and potatoes":"Cereales como cebada, trigo y centeno, y patatas","Sugar cane and molasses":"Caña de azúcar y melaza","Blue agave and corn":"Agave azul y maíz","Grapes and apples":"Uva y manzanas","Cereals, especially barley, wheat and rye, plus potatoes are the classic premium vodka raw materials.":"Los cereales, sobre todo cebada, trigo y centeno, y las patatas son las materias primas clásicas del vodka de calidad.","Sugar cane and molasses point to rum. Blue agave is Tequila's raw material. Grapes and apples can be used, but they are not the ones linked with premium vodka.":"La caña de azúcar y la melaza hacen pensar en el ron. El agave azul es la materia prima del tequila. La uva y las manzanas pueden usarse, pero no son las asociadas al vodka de calidad.","To what minimum strength must a neutral spirit be distilled?":"¿A qué grado mínimo debe destilarse un destilado neutro?","95% or 96% abv, depending on national law":"Al 95% o al 96% vol., según la ley del país","40% abv, as in the bottle":"Al 40% vol., como en botella","75% abv, as after double distillation":"Al 75% vol., como tras una doble destilación","60% abv in every country":"Al 60% vol. en todos los países","A neutral spirit must reach at least 95% or 96%, depending on local law.":"Un destilado neutro debe llegar al menos al 95% o al 96%, según la ley local.","40% is the strength after dilution, not the distillation strength. Around 75% is typical of double pot still distillation, with plenty of aroma. 60% is the lowest strength for newly made spirits, the most aromatic ones: the opposite of neutral.":"El 40% es el grado tras la dilución, no el de destilación. Alrededor del 75% es típico de la doble destilación en alambique discontinuo, con muchos aromas. El 60% es el grado más bajo de los destilados recién hechos, los más aromáticos: lo contrario de neutro.","Which type of still is essential for making vodka?":"¿Qué tipo de alambique es imprescindible para hacer vodka?","No still: fermentation is enough":"Ningún alambique: basta la fermentación","A new oak barrel":"Una barrica de roble nueva","Only a column still can reach the 95–96% needed for a neutral spirit.":"Solo la columna puede alcanzar el 95–96% que exige un destilado neutro.","Some producers use pot stills for part of the process, but on their own they cannot reach a neutral spirit. Fermentation stops at around 8–10%. A barrel is not a still, and vodka is not aged in oak.":"Algunos productores usan alambiques discontinuos en parte del proceso, pero por sí solos no llegan a un destilado neutro. La fermentación se detiene hacia el 8–10%. Una barrica no es un alambique, y el vodka no pasa por roble.","Why is the spirit behind vodka called neutral?":"¿Por qué el destilado base del vodka se llama neutro?","Because at that strength it has almost no aroma":"Porque a ese grado casi no tiene aroma","Because it contains no alcohol":"Porque no contiene alcohol","Because it has the same strength as water":"Porque tiene el mismo grado que el agua","Because it can be sold in any country":"Porque se puede vender en cualquier país","Distilled to 95–96%, the spirit loses almost all aroma and becomes neutral.":"Destilado al 95–96%, el alcohol pierde casi todos sus aromas y se vuelve neutro.","Neutral refers to aroma, not alcohol: in fact it is one of the strongest spirits. It has nothing to do with water or where it can be sold; it describes an almost absent smell.":"Neutro se refiere a los aromas, no al alcohol: de hecho, es uno de los destilados más fuertes. No tiene nada que ver con el agua ni con dónde se vende: describe un olor casi inexistente.","What happens to vodka after distillation?":"¿Qué ocurre con el vodka después de la destilación?","It stays unaged and is diluted, usually to 40% abv":"Queda sin envejecer y se rebaja, normalmente al 40% vol.","It ages for at least two years in oak":"Envejece al menos dos años en roble","It is bottled at 96% abv without dilution":"Se embotella al 96% vol. sin rebajar","It is always sweetened with sugar":"Siempre se endulza con azúcar","Vodka skips the barrel and is brought down to bottling strength with water.":"El vodka no pasa por barrica y se rebaja con agua al grado de embotellado.","Two years in oak describes Cognac, not vodka. At 96% it would be undrinkable, as such strong alcohol numbs the palate. Sweetening is not part of vodka's basic recipe.":"Los dos años en roble recuerdan al coñac, no al vodka. Al 96% sería imbebible: un alcohol tan fuerte adormece el paladar. El endulzado no forma parte de la receta básica del vodka.","Why is vodka so popular in mixed drinks and cocktails?":"¿Por qué el vodka es tan popular en combinados y cócteles?","Because its neutrality makes it versatile":"Porque su neutralidad lo hace versátil","Because it is sweeter than other spirits":"Porque es más dulce que otros destilados","Because it is lower in alcohol than other spirits":"Porque tiene menos grado que otros destilados","Because it has strong oak aromas":"Porque tiene aromas de roble muy marcados","With almost no aroma, vodka works with many ingredients without masking them.":"Casi sin aroma, el vodka encaja con muchos ingredientes sin taparlos.","Vodka is not sweet: like every spirit it leaves the still dry and is not normally sweetened. It is usually bottled at 40%, like many other spirits. And it is not aged in barrels, so it has no oak aromas.":"El vodka no es dulce: como todo destilado sale seco y normalmente no se endulza. Suele embotellarse al 40%, como muchos otros destilados. Y no pasa por barrica, así que no tiene aromas de roble.","A vodka shows a faint hint of grain on the nose. How should it be classed?":"Un vodka muestra en nariz un ligero toque de cereal. ¿Cómo se clasifica?","Still neutral, but with a little character":"Sigue siendo neutro, pero con algo de carácter","No longer vodka, because it is not neutral":"Ya no es vodka, porque no es neutro","A flavoured vodka":"Un vodka aromatizado","A young whisky":"Un whisky joven","Faint raw-material notes are allowed: the vodka is still correctly called neutral.":"Se admiten ligeras notas de materia prima: el vodka sigue siendo correctamente neutro.","Some vodkas keep a hint of character without ceasing to be vodka. A flavoured vodka has added flavourings, whereas here the grain note comes from the raw material. A whisky would be far more intense and aged in oak.":"Algunos vodkas conservan un toque de carácter sin dejar de ser vodka. Un vodka aromatizado lleva aromas añadidos, mientras que aquí el cereal viene de la materia prima. Un whisky tendría aromas mucho más intensos y pasaría por roble.","A bartender wants to make a fruit drink stronger without changing its taste. Which spirit fits best?":"En la barra se quiere hacer más alcohólica una bebida de fruta sin cambiar su sabor. ¿Qué destilado se elige?","A neutral vodka":"Un vodka neutro","An XO Cognac":"Un coñac XO","A peated malt whisky":"Un whisky de malta turbado","An aged Tequila":"Un tequila envejecido","Neutral vodka adds alcohol while adding almost no aroma.":"El vodka neutro aporta alcohol casi sin aportar aromas.","An XO Cognac has intense dried fruit, leather and oak aromas. A peated whisky brings smoke. An aged Tequila combines agave and oak: all of them would change the drink's flavour.":"Un coñac XO tiene aromas intensos de frutos secos, cuero y roble. El whisky turbado aporta notas de humo. Un tequila envejecido une agave y roble: todos cambiarían el sabor de la bebida.","A producer has only pot stills and distils several times. Can this produce vodka's neutral spirit?":"Un productor solo tiene alambiques discontinuos y destila varias veces. ¿Puede obtener el destilado neutro del vodka?","No, 95–96% can only be reached with a column still":"No, el 95–96% solo se alcanza con columna","Yes, three distillations are enough":"Sí, basta con destilar tres veces","Yes, if water is added afterwards":"Sí, si después rebaja con agua","Yes, if potatoes are the raw material":"Sí, si usa patatas como materia prima","However many times it is used, a pot still cannot reach neutral-spirit strength.":"Por muchas veces que se destile, el alambique discontinuo no llega al grado de un destilado neutro.","The number of passes is not enough: a column still is needed, possibly alongside pot stills for part of the process. Diluting lowers the strength rather than raising it. And the raw material does not change the still's limit.":"El número de pasadas no basta: hace falta columna, quizá junto a alambiques discontinuos en parte del proceso. Rebajar con agua baja el grado, no lo sube. Y la materia prima no cambia el límite del alambique.","Spirit":"Destilado","An alcoholic drink whose strength has been raised by distillation.":"Bebida alcohólica cuyo grado se ha subido mediante destilación.","The four steps":"Los cuatro pasos","Raw material, fermentation, distillation, post-distillation.":"Materia prima, fermentación, destilación, fase posterior a la destilación.","abv":"% vol.","Alcohol by volume: 40% abv means 40% of the liquid is alcohol.":"Porcentaje de alcohol en volumen: 40% vol. = el 40% es alcohol.","What does yeast do?":"¿Qué hacen las levaduras?","Eats sugar, making ethanol, carbon dioxide and fruity aromas.":"Se comen el azúcar y producen etanol, dióxido de carbono y aromas afrutados.","Strength after fermentation":"Grado tras la fermentación","Usually 8–10% abv.":"Normalmente entre un 8% y un 10% vol.","Distillation strength and aroma":"Grado de destilación y aromas","Lower strength = more aroma; higher strength = less; 96% = neutral.":"Grado bajo = más aromas; grado alto = menos; 96% = neutro.","Pot still":"Alambique discontinuo","Batch process, usually twice; low strength, lots of character.":"Trabaja por lotes, normalmente dos veces; grado bajo, mucho carácter.","Column still":"Alambique de columna","Continuous; short = flavourful, tall = light, tallest = neutral at 95–96%.":"Continuo; corta = aromático, alta = ligero, la más alta = neutro al 95–96%.","Newly made spirit":"Destilado recién hecho","Always colourless and dry, with no sugar.":"Siempre incoloro y seco, es decir, sin azúcar.","New oak barrel":"Barrica nueva","Never used: gives the most colour and aroma (vanilla, spice, coconut).":"Nunca usada: cede el máximo de color y aromas (vainilla, especias, coco).","Old oak barrel":"Barrica vieja","Already used: gives less aroma, and less again with each reuse.":"Ya usada: cede menos aromas, y menos aún con cada uso.","Blending":"Mezcla","Combining barrels for bottle-to-bottle consistency and for complexity.":"Unir varias barricas para lograr regularidad entre botellas y complejidad.","Caramel colouring":"Caramelo colorante","Evens out batch colour; used properly, not sweet and adds no aroma.":"Iguala el color de los lotes; bien usado, no es dulce ni aporta aromas.","Where does sweetness come from?":"¿De dónde viene el dulzor?","Always added after distillation, usually as sugar.":"Siempre se añade tras la destilación, normalmente como azúcar.","Final step: pure water, usually down to 40% abv; adds no flavour.":"Último paso: agua pura, normalmente hasta el 40% vol.; no aporta aromas.","Grape brandy":"Brandy de uva","Distilled wine; Cognac is the most famous example.":"Vino destilado; el coñac es el ejemplo más famoso.","Where does Cognac come from?":"¿Dónde nace el coñac?","Cognac distillation":"Destilación del coñac","By law: twice in a pot still.":"Por ley: dos veces en alambique discontinuo.","Cognac minimum ageing":"Envejecimiento mínimo del coñac","At least 2 years in oak; gives vanilla and toast.":"Al menos 2 años en roble; aporta vainilla y tostado.","VS":"VS","Youngest spirit: at least 2 years old.":"Destilado más joven: al menos 2 años.","Youngest spirit: at least 4 years old.":"Destilado más joven: al menos 4 años.","Youngest spirit: at least 10 years old.":"Destilado más joven: al menos 10 años.","What defines vodka?":"¿Qué define al vodka?","Distillation strength; raw material and place are open.":"El grado de destilación; la materia prima y el lugar son libres.","Neutral spirit":"Destilado neutro","At least 95% or 96% abv, column-distilled; almost no aroma.":"Al menos 95% o 96% vol., en columna; casi sin aromas.","Premium vodka raw materials":"Materias primas del vodka de calidad","Cereals (barley, wheat, rye) and potatoes.":"Cereales (cebada, trigo, centeno) y patatas.","Vodka after distillation":"Vodka tras la destilación","Unaged; usually diluted to 40% abv.":"Sin envejecer; rebajada normalmente al 40% vol.","Vodka with some character":"Vodka con algo de carácter","Faint raw-material notes, yet still neutral.":"Ligeras notas de materia prima, pero sigue siendo neutro.","From grain to sugar: malting":"Del grano al azúcar: el malteado","Whisky always starts with grain, and you can picture it as beer that has been through a still. There is one obstacle, though: a barley grain is dry, hard and packed with starch rather than sugar. Yeast cannot do anything with starch, so it has to be turned into sugar before any fermentation can happen. The classic method lets the barley do almost all of that work itself.":"El whisky nace siempre de cereales, y se puede imaginar como una cerveza que ha pasado por el alambique. Pero hay un obstáculo: un grano de cebada es seco, duro y está lleno de almidón, no de azúcar. Las levaduras no pueden hacer nada con el almidón, así que antes de fermentar hay que convertirlo en azúcar. El método clásico deja que la propia cebada haga casi todo el trabajo.","The first step is malting. The barley is allowed to start growing, and as it grows the grain makes enzymes, tiny chemical tools that can change starch. At the right moment hot air is blown through to stop the growth, and from then on it is called malted barley. The grain now carries everything it needs, but the sugar has not been released yet.":"El primer paso es el malteado. Se deja que la cebada empiece a germinar y, mientras crece, el grano produce enzimas, pequeñas herramientas químicas capaces de transformar el almidón. En el momento justo se aplica aire caliente para frenar el crecimiento: a partir de ahí se habla de cebada malteada. El grano ya tiene todo lo necesario, pero el azúcar aún no se ha liberado.","Next the malted barley is crushed into a rough flour, and other crushed grains can be added too. Everything is mixed with water, and in this bath the barley's enzymes get to work, converting the starch into sugar. The result is a sweet liquid ready for the yeast. From here the path is the one every spirit follows: fermentation, distillation, then what happens after the still.":"Después la cebada malteada se muele hasta obtener una harina gruesa, a la que se pueden añadir otros cereales molidos. Todo se mezcla con agua: en ese baño, las enzimas de la cebada se ponen a trabajar y convierten el almidón en azúcar. El resultado es un líquido dulce, listo para las levaduras. A partir de aquí el camino es el de cualquier destilado: fermentación, destilación y lo que ocurre después del alambique.","Each grain leaves its own signature in the glass. Barley brings cereal notes, corn recalls sweetcorn and rye adds a spicy, peppery edge. All whiskies then spend time in oak barrels, are blended and, where the law allows, have their colour adjusted with caramel. Most are bottled at 40% abv.":"Cada cereal deja su firma en la copa. La cebada aporta notas de cereal, el maíz recuerda al maíz dulce y el centeno da un toque especiado y picante. Después, todos los whiskies pasan por barricas de roble, se mezclan y, si la ley lo permite, se ajusta su color con caramelo. Casi siempre se embotellan al 40 % vol.","Whisky is made only from grain: think of it as distilled beer.":"El whisky se hace solo con cereales: es como una cerveza destilada.","Grains hold starch, not sugar, so it must be converted before fermentation.":"Los cereales contienen almidón, no azúcar: hay que convertirlo antes de fermentar.","Malting: barley sprouts, makes enzymes, then hot air stops the growth.":"Malteado: la cebada germina, crea enzimas y el aire caliente detiene el crecimiento.","Crushed malt + water: the enzymes turn starch into sugar.":"Cebada molida + agua: las enzimas convierten el almidón en azúcar.","The rules every Scotch follows":"Las reglas comunes a todo el Scotch","Scotch is the name for whisky from Scotland, and it is more than a loose geographical label. To carry the name, a whisky must be distilled in Scotland and then aged in Scotland for at least three years. Both conditions matter: a Scottish spirit sent to mature across the border loses the right to the name, even if everything else about it is identical.":"Scotch es el nombre del whisky escocés, y no es una simple indicación geográfica. Para llevar ese nombre, un whisky debe destilarse en Escocia y envejecer después en Escocia durante al menos tres años. Las dos condiciones cuentan: un destilado escocés que se lleva a madurar al otro lado de la frontera pierde el derecho al nombre, aunque sea idéntico en todo lo demás.","Time in oak is therefore compulsory, and it leaves its mark. The barrels give colour and aromas, and over the years the spirit becomes more concentrated as a little water and alcohol escape through the wood. Older whiskies can show notes of fruit cake and sweet spice. After maturation the whisky is blended, its colour adjusted if needed, and it is diluted.":"El paso por roble es, por tanto, obligatorio, y deja huella. Las barricas aportan color y aromas, y con el tiempo el destilado se concentra porque un poco de agua y alcohol se evapora a través de la madera. En los whiskies más viejos pueden aparecer notas de bizcocho de frutas y especias dulces. Tras la maduración se mezcla, se ajusta el color si hace falta y se diluye.","Scotch splits into two big families worth knowing well: Single Malt and Blended. The difference is not about prestige or age but about three simple questions: which grains it is made from, what kind of still it was distilled in, and how many distilleries it comes from. Answer those three and you can place any bottle of Scotch.":"El Scotch se divide en dos grandes familias que conviene conocer bien: el Single Malt y el Blended. La diferencia no está en el prestigio ni en la edad, sino en tres preguntas sencillas: con qué cereales se hace, en qué tipo de alambique se destila y de cuántas destilerías procede. Con esas tres respuestas se puede situar cualquier botella de Scotch.","Scotch: distilled and aged in Scotland.":"Scotch: destilado y envejecido en Escocia.","Minimum ageing: three years, always in Scotland.":"Envejecimiento mínimo: tres años, siempre en Escocia.","Two main families: Single Malt and Blended Scotch.":"Dos grandes familias: Single Malt y Blended Scotch.","What separates them: grains, type of still, number of distilleries.":"Las distingue la receta: cereales, alambique y número de destilerías.","Single Malt and peat smoke":"El Single Malt y el humo de turba","A Single Malt Scotch meets three requirements. It is made only from malted barley, with no other grains. It is distilled in pot stills, the kind that work one batch at a time. And it comes from a single distillery. That is what 'single' refers to: one place of production, not one barrel.":"Un Single Malt Scotch cumple tres requisitos. Se elabora solo con cebada malteada, sin otros cereales. Se destila en alambiques, los que trabajan por lotes, uno cada vez. Y procede de una sola destilería. A eso se refiere 'single': a un único lugar de producción, no a una única barrica.","Pot stills produce a spirit of fairly low strength that is full of character. That is why Single Malts are expressive whiskies: on the nose and palate you find cereal, fruit, flowers and honey and, with time in the barrel, fruit cake and sweet spice. Two Single Malts from different distilleries can taste very different from each other.":"Los alambiques dan un destilado de graduación relativamente baja y con mucho carácter. Por eso los Single Malt son whiskies expresivos: en nariz y en boca aparecen cereal, fruta, flores y miel y, con el tiempo en barrica, bizcocho de frutas y especias dulces. Dos Single Malt de destilerías distintas pueden parecerse muy poco.","Some Single Malts carry one extra aroma: smoke. It comes from peat, a natural fuel that is burned when the barley is heated at the end of malting. The smoke wraps around the grains and flavours them, and that flavour travels all the way to the glass. These whiskies are a minority, though: only a few Single Malts are peaty, some of them very strongly.":"Algunos Single Malt tienen un aroma más: el humo. Procede de la turba, un combustible natural que se quema cuando se calienta la cebada al final del malteado. El humo envuelve los granos y los perfuma, y ese aroma llega hasta la copa. Pero son una minoría: solo unos pocos Single Malt son turbados, algunos de forma muy intensa.","Single Malt: 100% malted barley, pot stills, one distillery.":"Single Malt: 100 % cebada malteada, alambiques, una sola destilería.","Typical aromas: cereal, fruit, flowers, honey, fruit cake, sweet spice.":"Aromas típicos: cereal, fruta, flores, miel, bizcocho de frutas, especias dulces.","Smoke comes from peat burned while the malted barley is heated.":"El humo viene de la turba quemada al calentar la cebada malteada.","Only a few Single Malts are peaty.":"Solo unos pocos Single Malt son turbados.","Blended Scotch and grain whisky":"El Blended Scotch y el whisky de grano","Alongside malt there is a second kind of Scottish whisky: grain whisky. It is made from malted barley together with other grains and distilled in a column still rather than a pot still. The result is a spirit with a light aroma and a smooth texture. It rarely reaches the shelf on its own, because its real job lies elsewhere.":"Junto al malta existe un segundo tipo de whisky escocés: el whisky de grano. Se elabora con cebada malteada y otros cereales y se destila en columna, no en alambique. El resultado es un destilado de aroma ligero y textura suave. Casi nunca llega solo a las estanterías: su verdadera función es otra.","That job is Blended Scotch, the most widespread category. A blend brings together malt whiskies and grain whiskies from different distilleries. Think of an orchestra: the malts, intense and characterful, are the soloists, while the light, smooth grain whisky is the section that holds everything together. Whiskies of different ages also go into the mix to add variety.":"Esa función es el Blended Scotch, la categoría más extendida. Un Blended reúne whiskies de malta y whiskies de grano de distintas destilerías. Se puede pensar en una orquesta: las maltas, intensas y con personalidad, son las solistas; el whisky de grano, ligero y suave, es la sección que lo une todo. En la mezcla también entran whiskies de distintas edades para sumar variedad.","Why blend? For two reasons. The first is consistency: every barrel is slightly different, and people expect a bottle to taste the same as last time. The second is complexity: combining spirits with different characters is the easiest way to build depth. A tiny amount of caramel then helps keep the colour identical from one batch to the next.":"¿Por qué mezclar? Por dos razones. La primera es la regularidad: cada barrica es un poco distinta, y quien compra una botella espera el mismo sabor que la vez anterior. La segunda es la complejidad: unir destilados de caracteres distintos es la forma más sencilla de crear profundidad. Una pequeña dosis de caramelo ayuda luego a mantener el mismo color de un lote a otro.","Blends vary a great deal. Some have medium intensity and a simple style, ideal for mixing; others are pronounced and complex. Thanks to the grain whisky they are usually smoother than Single Malts. So there is no reason to see them as second-rate: they are the work of a real craft, the craft of blending.":"Los Blended son muy variados. Algunos tienen una intensidad media y un estilo sencillo, perfectos para combinar; otros son intensos y complejos. En general, gracias al whisky de grano, resultan más suaves que los Single Malt. No hay por qué verlos como whiskies de segunda: son fruto de un oficio preciso, el del mezclador.","Grain whisky: malted barley + other grains, column still, light and smooth.":"Whisky de grano: cebada malteada + otros cereales, columna, ligero y suave.","Blended Scotch: malt + grain whiskies from different distilleries.":"Blended Scotch: malta + grano de distintas destilerías.","Blending gives consistency and complexity.":"Se mezcla para lograr regularidad y complejidad.","Usually smoother than Single Malts; from simple to complex.":"Suele ser más suave que los Single Malt; de sencillo a complejo.","Bourbon: corn and new barrels":"Bourbon: maíz y barricas nuevas","Bourbon is the best-known American whiskey. Many people link it to Kentucky, and that is indeed the state that makes the most, but the law allows it to be made anywhere in the United States. Its style comes down to three clear choices: the grain recipe, the way it is distilled and the type of barrel.":"El Bourbon es el whiskey estadounidense más famoso. Mucha gente lo asocia a Kentucky, y de hecho es el estado que más produce, pero la ley permite elaborarlo en cualquier lugar de Estados Unidos. Su estilo depende de tres decisiones concretas: la receta de cereales, la forma de destilar y el tipo de barrica.","First choice: at least 51% of the grain must be corn, usually topped up with barley and rye. Corn brings sweetcorn notes. Second choice: it is normally distilled in a column still, but only to a low strength, so the spirit keeps plenty of character. A column still does not have to make a light spirit; it all depends on how high the strength goes.":"Primera decisión: al menos el 51 % del cereal debe ser maíz, completado normalmente con cebada y centeno. El maíz aporta notas de maíz dulce. Segunda decisión: suele destilarse en columna, pero hasta una graduación baja, para que el destilado conserve mucho carácter. Una columna no da por fuerza un destilado ligero: todo depende de la graduación que se busque.","Third choice: the barrels must be new oak, charred on the inside. A barrel that has never been used gives the most colour and aroma, and the charring adds even more intensity. The result is a pronounced, complex whiskey with notes of sweetcorn, cereal, fruit, vanilla and coconut.":"Tercera decisión: las barricas deben ser de roble nuevo, quemado por dentro. Una barrica que nunca se ha usado es la que más color y aromas cede, y el quemado añade aún más intensidad. El resultado es un whiskey intenso y complejo, con notas de maíz dulce, cereal, fruta, vainilla y coco.","A common trap: people often call Bourbon 'sweet'. In fact it has no added sugar and is dry. The impression of sweetness comes from the vanilla, fruit and coconut aromas, which the nose links with desserts. In tasting language, 'sweet' refers only to the taste of sugar, felt on the palate.":"Una trampa habitual: se suele decir que el Bourbon es 'dulce'. En realidad no lleva azúcar añadido y es seco. La impresión de dulzor viene de los aromas de vainilla, fruta y coco, que la nariz asocia a los postres. En cata, 'dulce' se refiere solo al sabor del azúcar, que se percibe en boca.","Bourbon: at least 51% corn; made anywhere in the USA, mostly Kentucky.":"Bourbon: al menos 51 % de maíz; se hace en todo EE. UU., sobre todo en Kentucky.","Usually column-distilled to a low strength.":"Suele destilarse en columna a baja graduación.","New charred oak barrels: lots of colour and aroma.":"Barricas de roble nuevo quemado: mucho color y aroma.","Sweetcorn, vanilla, coconut, fruit; no added sugar, so it is dry.":"Maíz dulce, vainilla, coco, fruta; sin azúcar añadido: es seco.","Tennessee whiskey: through the charcoal":"Tennessee whiskey: el paso por el carbón","Tennessee whiskey is a close relative of Bourbon. It is made the same way, with the same majority of corn, the same distillation and the same new charred barrels. There are two differences. The first is geography: unlike Bourbon, it can only be made in the state of Tennessee. The second is one extra step that happens before the barrel.":"El Tennessee whiskey es pariente cercano del Bourbon. Se elabora igual, con la misma mayoría de maíz, la misma destilación y las mismas barricas nuevas quemadas. Hay dos diferencias. La primera es geográfica: a diferencia del Bourbon, solo puede producirse en el estado de Tennessee. La segunda es un paso adicional que tiene lugar antes de la barrica.","As soon as it leaves the still, the new spirit is passed through a bed of maple charcoal. It is not a very fine filter, but it holds back some impurities. The effect is a whiskey with a smoother character. This step adds no flavour at all: no maple, no smoke. It takes something away rather than putting anything in.":"Nada más salir del alambique, el destilado se hace pasar por una capa de carbón de madera de arce. No es un filtro muy fino, pero retiene parte de las impurezas. El efecto es un whiskey de carácter más suave. Este paso no añade ningún sabor: ni arce ni humo. Quita algo, no aporta nada.","One image makes it easy to remember: Tennessee whiskey is a Bourbon that takes a shower before going into the barrel. Watch the order of the steps: the filtering is done on the new, colourless spirit, not on whiskey that has already aged. After that, the path is the same as Bourbon's, with new charred barrels giving colour and aroma.":"Para recordarlo basta una imagen: el Tennessee whiskey es un Bourbon que se da una ducha antes de entrar en la barrica. Atención al orden de los pasos: el filtrado se hace sobre el destilado nuevo e incoloro, no sobre el whiskey ya envejecido. Después, el camino vuelve a ser el del Bourbon, con barricas nuevas quemadas que dan color y aromas.","Made only in the state of Tennessee.":"Solo se produce en Tennessee.","Same recipe and barrels as Bourbon.":"Misma receta y mismas barricas que el Bourbon.","Extra step: maple charcoal filtering before the barrel.":"Paso extra: filtrado con carbón de arce antes de la barrica.","Removes impurities, adds smoothness, adds no flavour.":"Elimina impurezas, aporta suavidad, no añade sabor.","Rye whiskey: the spicy grain":"Rye whiskey: el centeno especiado","American Rye whiskey is Bourbon's spicy twin. The rules are the same in every way except one: the main grain. Instead of corn, at least 51% of the recipe must be rye. So you still find low-strength column distillation and ageing in new charred oak barrels.":"El Rye whiskey estadounidense es el gemelo especiado del Bourbon. Las reglas son las mismas en todo salvo en una cosa: el cereal principal. En lugar de maíz, al menos el 51 % de la receta debe ser centeno. Se mantienen, por tanto, la destilación en columna a baja graduación y el envejecimiento en barricas de roble nuevo quemado.","That change of grain is enough to change the character. Rye brings spicy, peppery aromas that show clearly on both nose and palate. Where Bourbon recalls sweetcorn and coconut, Rye has a livelier, sharper profile. The vanilla notes from the new barrel are still there, but they sit behind the spice.":"Ese cambio de cereal basta para cambiar el carácter. El centeno aporta aromas especiados y picantes, bien presentes en nariz y en boca. Donde el Bourbon recuerda al maíz dulce y al coco, el Rye tiene un perfil más vivo y picante. Las notas de vainilla de la barrica nueva siguen ahí, pero quedan detrás de las especias.","A simple way to fix the three American whiskeys is to look at the grain and the filter. Mostly corn: Bourbon. Mostly corn, plus maple charcoal, made only in Tennessee: Tennessee whiskey. Mostly rye: Rye. Anyone looking for an American whiskey with a peppery kick, for example in a cocktail, should think of Rye.":"Una forma sencilla de fijar los tres whiskeys estadounidenses es fijarse en el cereal y el filtro. Mayoría de maíz: Bourbon. Mayoría de maíz, más carbón de arce y solo en Tennessee: Tennessee whiskey. Mayoría de centeno: Rye. Si se busca un whiskey estadounidense con un toque picante, por ejemplo para un cóctel, se piensa en el Rye.","Rye: at least 51% rye.":"Rye: al menos 51 % de centeno.","Otherwise made like Bourbon: column still and new charred barrels.":"Por lo demás se hace como el Bourbon: columna y barricas nuevas quemadas.","Spicy, peppery aromas.":"Aromas especiados y picantes.","Ireland, Canada and Japan":"Irlanda, Canadá y Japón","In Ireland, most whiskeys are made by combining pot-still and column-still spirits. The typical style is light and smooth, easy to drink. There are also Irish whiskeys made only in pot stills, and some use an unusual ingredient: unmalted barley. This gives an oily texture and a nutty character.":"En Irlanda, la mayoría de los whiskeys nacen de unir destilados de alambique y destilados de columna. El estilo típico es ligero y suave, fácil de beber. También hay whiskeys irlandeses destilados solo en alambique, y algunos usan un ingrediente poco común: la cebada sin maltear, que aporta una textura oleosa y un carácter a frutos secos, como la avellana.","Canada uses many different grains and usually blends high-strength spirits, which are lighter, with low-strength spirits, which have more flavour. The result is balanced, versatile whiskies. In the best Canadian whiskies, though, there is one common thread: rye. It is the signature flavour, spicy and peppery.":"Canadá usa muchos cereales distintos y suele mezclar destilados de alta graduación, más ligeros, con destilados de baja graduación, más sabrosos. Así se obtienen whiskies equilibrados y versátiles. Pero en los mejores whiskies canadienses hay un hilo conductor: el centeno, que les da su firma especiada y picante.","Japan built its whisky industry using Scotland as the model. That is why you find both malt and blended whiskies there, just as with Scotch. The traditional style is elegant and refined, precise in its details. In recent years, though, many Japanese producers have been exploring new styles and flavours, and the category keeps evolving.":"Japón construyó su industria del whisky tomando Escocia como modelo. Por eso allí hay whiskies de malta y blended, igual que en el Scotch. El estilo tradicional es elegante y refinado, cuidado hasta el detalle. Sin embargo, en los últimos años muchos productores japoneses exploran estilos y sabores nuevos, y la categoría no deja de evolucionar.","Ireland: mostly pot + column blends, light and smooth.":"Irlanda: sobre todo mezclas de alambique + columna, ligeras y suaves.","Unmalted barley: nutty notes and an oily texture.":"Cebada sin maltear: notas de frutos secos y textura oleosa.","Canada: many grains, high + low strength blends; rye is the signature.":"Canadá: muchos cereales, mezclas de alta + baja graduación; firma del centeno.","Japan: Scottish model, elegant malts and blends.":"Japón: modelo escocés, maltas y blended elegantes.","Cane juice or molasses":"Jugo de caña o melaza","Rum is made from sugar cane, a plant that loves heat. That is why production is centred on hot countries, and its historic heartland is the Caribbean. The region is a patchwork of small countries, though, each with its own traditions and rules. Sorting rum by colour or by the language spoken works poorly; it is far more useful to follow the four stages of production.":"El ron nace de la caña de azúcar, una planta que adora el calor. Por eso su producción se concentra en países cálidos, y su cuna histórica es el Caribe. Pero la región es un mosaico de pequeños países, cada uno con sus tradiciones y sus normas. Clasificar el ron por color o por idioma funciona mal: resulta mucho más útil seguir las cuatro fases de producción.","The first choice is the raw material. Freshly cut cane can be crushed and its sweet juice fermented straight away. Rums made from cane juice often have a very pronounced grassy, herbaceous flavour, like freshly mown grass. The best examples are rhum agricole, which in the Caribbean must come from Martinique or Guadeloupe.":"La primera decisión es la materia prima. Se puede prensar la caña recién cortada y fermentar enseguida su jugo dulce. Los rones de jugo de caña suelen tener un sabor herbáceo y vegetal muy marcado, como a hierba recién cortada. Los mejores ejemplos son los rhum agricole, que en el Caribe deben proceder de Martinica o Guadalupe.","Most Caribbean distillers, however, use molasses. It is a black, sticky substance, the by-product of the industry that turns cane juice into sugar. It has to be mixed with water before fermentation can start. Molasses rums have flavours of caramel and brown sugar, a rounder profile than the grassy freshness of cane juice.":"Sin embargo, la mayoría de los destiladores caribeños usa melaza. Es una sustancia negra y pegajosa, el subproducto de la industria que convierte el jugo de caña en azúcar. Antes de fermentar hay que mezclarla con agua. Los rones de melaza tienen sabores de caramelo y azúcar moreno: un perfil más redondo que la frescura herbácea del jugo de caña.","Rum is made from sugar cane, which grows in hot climates.":"El ron se hace con caña de azúcar, que crece en climas cálidos.","Understand it through the four stages, not colour or language.":"Mejor entenderlo por las cuatro fases que por el color o el idioma.","Cane juice: grassy; rhum agricole from Martinique and Guadeloupe.":"Jugo de caña: herbáceo; rhum agricole de Martinica y Guadalupe.","Molasses (the most common choice): caramel and brown sugar.":"Melaza (la opción más común): caramelo y azúcar moreno.","Fermentation and tropical fruit":"La fermentación y la fruta tropical","In every spirit, fermentation turns sugar into alcohol, but it also does something else: it creates aromas. Yeast in particular produces fruity scents. In rum this work can take centre stage. By managing fermentation in a certain way, distillers get tropical fruit aromas, such as banana or pineapple, which can become very pronounced.":"En cualquier destilado, la fermentación convierte el azúcar en alcohol, pero hace algo más: crea aromas. Son sobre todo las levaduras las que producen perfumes afrutados. En el ron, este trabajo puede convertirse en protagonista. Gestionando la fermentación de cierta manera, se obtienen aromas de fruta tropical, como plátano o piña, que a veces son muy intensos.","Pushing the flavour created during fermentation as far as it will go produces intensely fruity rums, almost explosive on the nose. Jamaican distillers are famous for exactly this style. When you meet a rum with a very concentrated tropical fruit aroma, the likely cause is a fermentation managed with that aim, not an added flavouring.":"Si se lleva al máximo el sabor creado en la fermentación, se obtienen rones intensamente afrutados, casi explosivos en nariz. Los destiladores de Jamaica son famosos precisamente por este estilo. Ante un ron con un aroma de fruta tropical muy concentrado, lo más probable es que detrás haya una fermentación trabajada con ese objetivo, no un aroma añadido.","This stage shows clearly why the four steps help more than colour. Two rums that are both colourless can be worlds apart: one light and discreet, the other loaded with tropical fruit. Asking what it was made from, how it was fermented and distilled and what happened afterwards tells you far more about the glass than its shade does.":"Esta fase muestra bien por qué las cuatro etapas ayudan más que el color. Dos rones incoloros pueden ser muy distintos: uno ligero y discreto, el otro cargado de fruta tropical. Preguntarse de qué materia prima viene, cómo se fermentó y destiló y qué pasó después dice mucho más de la copa que su tono.","Fermentation creates alcohol and fruity aromas too.":"La fermentación crea alcohol y también aromas afrutados.","In rum it can give very pronounced tropical fruit aromas.":"En el ron puede dar aromas de fruta tropical muy intensos.","Jamaica is known for this intensely fruity style.":"Jamaica es famosa por este estilo intensamente afrutado.","Pot or column: intensity to order":"Alambique o columna: intensidad a medida","In the Caribbean nearly every distiller can choose their still, and that choice decides how intense the rum will be. For a pronounced spirit full of character, a pot still is an option. Another is a short column with few sections, which also gives a flavourful spirit; this is how rhum agricole is made.":"En el Caribe casi todos los destiladores pueden elegir el tipo de alambique, y esa elección decide la intensidad del ron. Para un destilado intenso y con mucho carácter se puede usar el alambique. Otra opción es la columna corta, con pocas secciones, que también da un destilado sabroso: es el caso del rhum agricole.","At the opposite end are rums with a light aroma. They are made in tall column stills with many sections and distilled to a high strength. The higher the strength, the less aroma remains in the spirit. Examples of this style come from Cuba and Puerto Rico: delicate rums that work very well in cocktails.":"En el extremo opuesto están los rones de aroma ligero. Se elaboran en columnas altas, con muchas secciones, y se destilan a una graduación elevada. Cuanto más alta es la graduación, menos aroma queda en el destilado. Hay ejemplos de este estilo en Cuba y Puerto Rico: rones delicados, muy cómodos en cócteles.","Many Caribbean distilleries own both pot stills and column stills and make several spirits of different intensities. It is like a painter's palette: one light spirit, one pronounced, one fruity. Later, at the blending stage, this variety lets them compose rums in very different styles from the same distillery.":"Muchas destilerías caribeñas tienen a la vez alambiques y columnas, y producen varios destilados de intensidades distintas. Es como una paleta de pintor: un destilado ligero, uno intenso, uno afrutado. Más adelante, al mezclar, esta variedad permite componer rones de estilos muy diferentes desde una misma destilería.","Pot still: pronounced, characterful rum.":"Alambique: ron intenso y con carácter.","Short column: also flavourful; used for rhum agricole.":"Columna corta: también sabrosa; usada para el rhum agricole.","Tall column, high strength: light rums (Cuba, Puerto Rico).":"Columna alta, alta graduación: rones ligeros (Cuba, Puerto Rico).","Many distilleries own both types of still.":"Muchas destilerías tienen los dos tipos de alambique.","After the still: oak, filters, sugar and colour":"Después del alambique: barrica, filtros, azúcar y color","A rum can be aged or not. Time in oak adds vanilla and sweet spice aromas, as well as colour. In some Caribbean countries a period in the barrel is a legal requirement. Unaged rum, by contrast, rests in steel tanks: it stays colourless and keeps the aromas of the freshly distilled spirit.":"Un ron puede envejecerse o no. El paso por roble añade aromas de vainilla y especias dulces, además de color. En algunos países caribeños es obligatorio por ley un periodo en barrica. El ron sin envejecer, en cambio, reposa en depósitos de acero: sigue incoloro y conserva los aromas del destilado recién hecho.","What if a country requires oak but the producer wants a white rum? The answer is charcoal filtering, which removes the colour taken from the wood. The result is a colourless rum that has actually spent time in oak. This is one reason why colour alone cannot tell you how a rum was made.":"¿Y si un país exige barrica pero se quiere un ron blanco? La solución es filtrarlo con carbón, que elimina el color tomado de la madera. Se obtiene así un ron incoloro que en realidad ha pasado un tiempo en roble. Es uno de los motivos por los que el color, por sí solo, no cuenta cómo se hizo un ron.","Then comes blending. Blenders can combine pot-still and column-still spirits, of different ages and even from different distilleries, to build the style of each product. Finally, some rums are sweetened: this is common in Central and South America, while some countries forbid it. Many rums also receive caramel for colour, sometimes almost all of their colour.":"Después se mezcla. Se pueden combinar destilados de alambique y de columna, de distintas edades e incluso de distintas destilerías, para construir el estilo de cada producto. Por último, algunos rones se endulzan: es habitual en América Central y del Sur, mientras que en ciertos países está prohibido. Muchos rones reciben también caramelo para el color, a veces casi todo su color.","The last step, as for nearly every spirit, is dilution with pure water down to bottling strength. The result is a hugely varied family, from light, discreet white rum to dark, intense, spicy rum. To find your way, simply walk back through the four stages: raw material, fermentation, distillation and what happens afterwards.":"Último paso, como en casi todos los destilados: la dilución con agua pura hasta la graduación de embotellado. El resultado es una familia riquísima, que va del ron blanco ligero y discreto al oscuro, intenso y especiado. Para orientarse basta con recorrer de nuevo las cuatro fases: materia prima, fermentación, destilación y lo que ocurre después.","Oak gives vanilla, sweet spice and colour; required in some countries.":"El roble da vainilla, especias dulces y color; obligatorio en algunos países.","White rum: steel tanks (unaged) or charcoal filtering (aged).":"Ron blanco: acero (sin envejecer) o filtrado con carbón (envejecido).","Blending of different styles, ages and distilleries.":"Mezcla de estilos, edades y destilerías distintas.","Sugar: common in Central and South America, banned in some countries; caramel is common.":"Azúcar: habitual en América Central y del Sur, prohibido en algunos países; caramelo frecuente.","What raw material is whisky made from?":"¿Con qué materia prima se hace el whisky?","Grains":"Cereales","Grapes":"Uva","Sugar cane":"Caña de azúcar","Potatoes":"Patatas","By definition, whisky is an oak-aged spirit made from grain.":"Por definición, el whisky es un destilado de cereales envejecido en roble.","Whisky can be pictured as distilled beer: it starts from grains such as barley, corn or rye. Grapes are the base of brandies like Cognac, and sugar cane is the base of rum. Potatoes can be used for vodka, but not for whisky.":"El whisky se puede imaginar como una cerveza destilada: se parte de cereales como la cebada, el maíz o el centeno. La uva es la base de brandis como el coñac, y la caña de azúcar la del ron. Las patatas pueden servir para el vodka, pero no para el whisky.","Why do grains need processing before fermentation?":"¿Por qué hay que tratar los cereales antes de fermentar?","They hold starch, which must be turned into sugar":"Contienen almidón, que hay que convertir en azúcar","They hold too much sugar for the yeast":"Contienen demasiado azúcar para las levaduras","They already hold alcohol, which must be removed":"Ya contienen alcohol, que hay que eliminar","They hold acids that stop the yeast working":"Contienen ácidos que bloquean las levaduras","Yeast feed on sugar, but dry grains mostly contain starch.":"Las levaduras se alimentan de azúcar, pero los cereales secos contienen sobre todo almidón.","Grains are hard, dry and full of starch. Without converting it to sugar, the yeast would have nothing to turn into alcohol. The problem is not too much sugar, since sugar is actually missing, nor alcohol, which only appears during fermentation.":"Los granos son duros, secos y están llenos de almidón. Sin convertirlo en azúcar, las levaduras no tendrían nada que transformar en alcohol. El problema no es un exceso de azúcar, que de hecho falta, ni la presencia de alcohol, que solo aparece con la fermentación.","During malting, what does barley produce as it grows?":"Durante el malteado, ¿qué produce la cebada al germinar?","Enzymes that can convert starch":"Enzimas capaces de transformar el almidón","Yeast that starts the fermentation":"Levaduras que inician la fermentación","Small amounts of alcohol":"Pequeñas cantidades de alcohol","Natural smoky aromas":"Aromas ahumados naturales","As it sprouts, the grain makes enzymes that later convert starch into sugar.":"Al germinar, el grano crea enzimas que después convertirán el almidón en azúcar.","The enzymes really get to work once the crushed barley is mixed with water. Yeast, by contrast, is added later to the sugary liquid. Smoke does not come from sprouting: it only appears if peat is burned while the barley is heated.":"Las enzimas actúan de verdad cuando la cebada molida se mezcla con agua. Las levaduras, en cambio, se añaden después al líquido azucarado. El humo no procede de la germinación: solo aparece si se quema turba al calentar la cebada.","How is the barley's growth stopped at the end of malting?":"¿Cómo se detiene el crecimiento de la cebada al final del malteado?","With hot air":"Con aire caliente","With ice-cold water":"Con agua helada","By adding yeast":"Añadiendo levaduras","By charcoal filtering":"Filtrando con carbón","Heat dries the grain and halts sprouting, giving malted barley.":"El calor seca el grano y frena la germinación: así se obtiene la cebada malteada.","This heating stage is exactly when some distilleries burn peat to add smoke. Water comes in later, when the crushed barley is mixed to release its sugar. Yeast and charcoal filtering belong to other stages of production altogether.":"Es precisamente en este calentamiento cuando algunas destilerías queman turba para aportar humo. El agua interviene más tarde, cuando la cebada molida se mezcla para liberar el azúcar. Las levaduras y el filtrado con carbón pertenecen a otras fases de la producción.","What is the minimum ageing for any Scotch whisky?":"¿Cuál es el envejecimiento mínimo de cualquier Scotch whisky?","Three years, in Scotland":"Tres años, en Escocia","Two years, in any country":"Dos años, en cualquier país","Three years, anywhere in the UK":"Tres años, en cualquier lugar del Reino Unido","Ten years, in Scotland":"Diez años, en Escocia","All Scotch is distilled in Scotland and aged there for at least three years.":"Todo Scotch se destila en Escocia y envejece allí al menos tres años.","Where the whisky ages matters as much as how long: maturing elsewhere in the UK is not enough. Two years is the minimum for Cognac, not Scotch. Ten years recalls the XO term for Cognac and is not a rule for Scotch.":"El lugar del envejecimiento cuenta tanto como la duración: madurar en otra parte del Reino Unido no basta. Dos años es el mínimo del coñac, no del Scotch. Diez años recuerda la mención XO del coñac y no es una obligación para el whisky escocés.","Which combination defines a Single Malt Scotch whisky?":"¿Qué combinación define un Single Malt Scotch whisky?","100% malted barley, pot stills, one distillery":"100 % cebada malteada, alambiques, una sola destilería","Malted barley and other grains, column still, one distillery":"Cebada malteada y otros cereales, columna, una destilería","100% malted barley, pot stills, several distilleries":"100 % cebada malteada, alambiques, varias destilerías","At least 51% barley, any still, one distillery":"Al menos 51 % de cebada, cualquier alambique, una destilería","A Single Malt uses only malted barley, pot stills and one distillery.":"Un Single Malt solo usa cebada malteada, alambiques y una única destilería.","All three conditions must be true together. Other grains and a column still describe grain whisky. Malts from several distilleries would no longer be 'single'. The 51% threshold belongs to American rules such as those for Bourbon.":"Las tres condiciones deben cumplirse a la vez. Otros cereales y la columna describen el whisky de grano. Maltas de varias destilerías ya no serían 'single'. El umbral del 51 % pertenece a las reglas estadounidenses, como la del Bourbon.","Where does the smoky flavour of some Single Malts come from?":"¿De dónde viene el sabor ahumado de algunos Single Malt?","Peat burned while the malted barley is heated":"De la turba quemada al calentar la cebada malteada","New barrels charred on the inside":"De las barricas nuevas quemadas por dentro","Finished whisky exposed to smoke":"Del whisky terminado expuesto al humo","A charcoal filter after distillation":"De un filtro de carbón tras la destilación","Peat smoke flavours the grains during the final heating of malting.":"El humo de turba perfuma los granos durante el calentamiento final del malteado.","The smoke enters the whisky before fermentation even begins, through the barley. New charred barrels are typical of Bourbon and give vanilla and coconut, not peat. The charcoal filtering of Tennessee whiskey removes impurities and adds no flavour.":"El humo entra en el whisky antes incluso de la fermentación, a través de la cebada. Las barricas nuevas quemadas son típicas del Bourbon y aportan vainilla y coco, no turba. El filtrado con carbón del Tennessee whiskey elimina impurezas y no añade sabor.","Which statement about peaty Single Malts is true?":"¿Qué afirmación sobre los Single Malt turbados es cierta?","Only a few exist, and some are very smoky":"Son pocos, y algunos tienen un humo muy marcado","The law requires peat in every Single Malt":"La ley exige turba en todos los Single Malt","Almost every Single Malt is peaty":"Casi todos los Single Malt son turbados","Peat is added in the bottle as a flavouring":"La turba se añade en la botella como aroma","Only a minority of Single Malts are peaty, sometimes intensely.":"Solo una minoría de Single Malt es turbada, a veces con intensidad.","Smoke is a famous trait but not the rule: most Single Malts show cereal, fruit, flowers and honey with no smoky notes. No law makes peat compulsory. And peat is not a flavouring added later; it is burned during malting.":"El humo es un rasgo famoso, pero no la norma: la mayoría de los Single Malt muestran cereal, fruta, flores y miel sin notas ahumadas. Ninguna ley obliga a usar turba. Y la turba no es un aroma que se añade: se quema durante el malteado.","How is Scottish grain whisky best described?":"¿Cómo se describe el whisky de grano escocés?","Column-distilled, light and smooth":"Destilado en columna, ligero y suave","Pot-distilled, intense and peaty":"Destilado en alambique, intenso y turbado","Made only from malted barley, very aromatic":"Hecho solo con cebada malteada, muy aromático","Unaged and bottled straight away":"Sin envejecer y embotellado enseguida","Grain whisky comes off the column still with a light aroma and smooth texture.":"El whisky de grano sale de la columna con aroma ligero y textura suave.","It is made from malted barley plus other grains, so not from malted barley alone like Single Malt. The intensity and character of pot stills belong to the malts. And because it is Scotch, it must age for at least three years, so it cannot be bottled straight away.":"Se elabora con cebada malteada y otros cereales, así que no solo con cebada malteada como el Single Malt. La intensidad y el carácter del alambique pertenecen a las maltas. Y al ser Scotch debe envejecer al menos tres años, así que no puede embotellarse enseguida.","What is a Blended Scotch whisky?":"¿Qué es un Blended Scotch whisky?","Malt and grain whiskies from different distilleries":"Maltas y whiskies de grano de distintas destilerías","Several malts from the same distillery":"Varias maltas de una misma destilería","Grain whiskies only, of various ages":"Solo whiskies de grano de varias edades","Scotch mixed with Irish whiskey":"Scotch mezclado con whiskey irlandés","A blend combines both types of Scottish whisky from several distilleries.":"El Blended une los dos tipos de whisky escocés, procedentes de varias destilerías.","Both parts are essential: malts bring character, grain whisky brings lightness and smoothness. Several malts from one distillery do not make a Blended Scotch. And to be Scotch, every part must be distilled and aged in Scotland, so Irish whiskey cannot be included.":"Las dos partes son imprescindibles: las maltas aportan carácter y el whisky de grano, ligereza y suavidad. Varias maltas de una sola destilería no forman un Blended Scotch. Y para ser Scotch, cada componente debe destilarse y envejecer en Escocia, así que nada de whiskey irlandés.","A customer wants a smooth, easy-going Scotch with no smoke. What is usually the best suggestion?":"Un cliente pide un Scotch suave y fácil, sin humo. ¿Qué conviene proponer normalmente?","A Blended Scotch whisky":"Un Blended Scotch whisky","A heavily peated Single Malt":"Un Single Malt muy turbado","An old, intense Single Malt":"Un Single Malt viejo e intenso","A pot-distilled whisky":"Un whisky destilado en alambique","Thanks to grain whisky, blends are usually smoother than Single Malts.":"Gracias al whisky de grano, los Blended suelen ser más suaves que los Single Malt.","The light, smooth grain whisky softens the whole blend. A peaty malt brings exactly the smoke the customer wants to avoid. Old, intense malts, like pot-still spirits in general, aim for character and power rather than smoothness.":"El whisky de grano, ligero y suave, suaviza el conjunto. Una malta turbada aporta justo el humo que el cliente quiere evitar. Las maltas viejas e intensas, como los destilados de alambique en general, buscan carácter y potencia más que suavidad.","What is Scottish grain whisky mainly used for?":"¿Para qué se usa sobre todo el whisky de grano escocés?","Making Blended Scotch":"Para elaborar los Blended Scotch","Being sold as Single Malt":"Para venderse como Single Malt","Giving smoke to peaty malts":"Para dar humo a las maltas turbadas","Diluting Scotch before bottling":"Para diluir el Scotch antes de embotellar","Rarely sold on its own, grain whisky is the light backbone of blends.":"Casi nunca se vende solo: el whisky de grano es la base ligera de los Blended.","It cannot be a Single Malt, because it contains other grains and is column-distilled. Smoke comes from peat, not from another whisky. Dilution before bottling is done with pure water, not with another spirit.":"No puede ser un Single Malt, porque lleva otros cereales y se destila en columna. El humo viene de la turba, no de otro whisky. La dilución antes de embotellar se hace con agua pura, no con otro destilado.","Which set of aromas is typical of an unpeated Single Malt?":"¿Qué grupo de aromas es típico de un Single Malt no turbado?","Cereal, fruit, flowers, honey, sweet spice":"Cereal, fruta, flores, miel, especias dulces","Fresh grass, vegetal and cane notes":"Hierba fresca, notas vegetales y de caña","Juniper, citrus and roots":"Enebro, cítricos y raíces","Almost no aroma, a neutral style":"Casi ningún aroma, estilo neutro","Single Malt is expressive, with cereal, fruit, flower, honey and spice notes.":"El Single Malt es expresivo, con notas de cereal, fruta, flores, miel y especias.","With age in the barrel, fruit cake notes join them too. Grassy cane notes describe rum made from cane juice, and juniper is the signature of gin. A neutral style belongs to vodka, distilled to a very high strength.":"Con la edad en barrica se suman también notas de bizcocho de frutas. Las notas herbáceas de caña describen el ron de jugo de caña y el enebro es la firma de la ginebra. El estilo neutro es el del vodka, destilado a graduación altísima.","A whisky is distilled in Scotland, then aged four years in England. Can it be called Scotch?":"Un whisky se destila en Escocia y luego envejece cuatro años en Inglaterra. ¿Puede llamarse Scotch?","No: the ageing must also take place in Scotland":"No: el envejecimiento también debe hacerse en Escocia","Yes: only the place of distillation counts":"Sí: solo cuenta el lugar de destilación","Yes, as long as it is made from malted barley":"Sí, siempre que sea de cebada malteada","No: Scotch must age for ten years":"No: el Scotch debe envejecer diez años","Scotch must be both distilled and aged in Scotland, for at least three years.":"El Scotch debe destilarse y envejecer en Escocia, al menos tres años.","Four years would be long enough, but the place is wrong. The grain used does not change this rule, which applies to every Scotch. The minimum is three years, not ten: the only problem here is geography.":"Cuatro años bastarían en duración, pero el lugar no es el correcto. El cereal usado no cambia esta regla, que vale para todo Scotch. El mínimo es de tres años, no de diez: aquí el problema es solo geográfico.","A label reads 'Single Malt Scotch Whisky'. What can you be sure of?":"Una etiqueta dice 'Single Malt Scotch Whisky'. ¿Qué se puede afirmar con certeza?","It comes from one distillery and only malted barley":"Procede de una sola destilería y solo de cebada malteada","It comes from a single barrel, with no blending":"Procede de una única barrica, sin mezclas","It has a smoky peat flavour":"Tiene sabor ahumado a turba","It has been aged at least ten years":"Ha envejecido al menos diez años","'Single' means one distillery; 'Malt' means only malted barley, pot-distilled.":"'Single' significa una destilería; 'Malt', solo cebada malteada destilada en alambique.","A Single Malt can still be a blend of many barrels from the same distillery: 'single' does not mean one barrel. Only a few Single Malts are peaty, so smoke is not guaranteed. The minimum age is three years, as for every Scotch.":"Un Single Malt puede ser una mezcla de muchas barricas de la misma destilería: 'single' no significa una sola barrica. Solo unos pocos Single Malt son turbados, así que el humo no está garantizado. La edad mínima es de tres años, como en todo Scotch.","Why do Blended Scotch producers combine whiskies from different barrels and distilleries?":"¿Por qué quienes elaboran Blended Scotch mezclan whiskies de distintas barricas y destilerías?","To achieve consistency and complexity":"Para lograr regularidad y complejidad","To raise the final alcohol strength":"Para aumentar la graduación final","To make the whisky colourless":"Para que el whisky sea incoloro","To shorten the required ageing time":"Para acortar el envejecimiento obligatorio","Blending keeps each batch like the last and adds depth.":"La mezcla hace que cada lote se parezca al anterior y aporta profundidad.","Every barrel is unique, so blending is the way to a consistent taste, and combining different characters creates complexity. Strength is adjusted with water, not by blending. Blending does not remove colour, and the three-year minimum still applies to every component.":"Cada barrica es única, así que solo mezclando se logra un sabor constante, y unir caracteres distintos crea complejidad. La graduación se ajusta con agua, no mezclando. El color no desaparece al mezclar, y los tres años mínimos siguen siendo obligatorios para cada componente.","Why is whisky often described as 'distilled beer'?":"¿Por qué se suele describir el whisky como una 'cerveza destilada'?","Because a fermented grain liquid is distilled":"Porque se destila un líquido fermentado de cereales","Because beer is added before bottling":"Porque se añade cerveza antes de embotellar","Because it ages in old beer barrels":"Porque envejece en barricas usadas para cerveza","Because it has the same strength as beer":"Porque tiene la misma graduación que la cerveza","Like beer, whisky starts from fermented grain; that liquid is then distilled.":"Como la cerveza, el whisky parte de cereales fermentados; después ese líquido se destila.","The image describes the process: sugar from grain, fermentation, distillation. No beer is added to finished whisky, and the phrase says nothing about barrels. After distilling and diluting, whisky is far stronger than any beer, usually 40% abv.":"La imagen describe el proceso: azúcar obtenido de cereales, fermentación y destilación. No se añade cerveza al whisky terminado, y la expresión no habla de barricas. Tras destilar y diluir, el whisky es mucho más fuerte que cualquier cerveza, normalmente 40 % vol.","A blender adds a tiny amount of caramel to a batch of Scotch. What is the purpose?":"Quien mezcla un Scotch añade una cantidad mínima de caramelo. ¿Con qué fin?","To keep the colour the same from batch to batch":"Mantener el mismo color de un lote a otro","To make the whisky slightly sweet":"Hacer el whisky ligeramente dulce","To add a toffee aroma":"Añadir un aroma de tofe","To speed up ageing in the barrel":"Acelerar el envejecimiento en barrica","Caramel colour is used only to even out colour between batches.":"El colorante caramelo solo sirve para igualar el color entre lotes.","Each barrel gives a slightly different colour, and caramel corrects those differences. Used correctly it is not sweet and adds no aroma, so it brings neither sugar nor toffee notes. It has no effect on maturation, which depends on wood and time.":"Cada barrica da un color algo distinto, y el caramelo corrige esas diferencias. Bien usado no es dulce ni añade aromas, así que no aporta azúcar ni notas de tofe. No influye en la maduración, que depende de la madera y del tiempo.","Which grain must make up at least 51% of a Bourbon's recipe?":"¿Qué cereal debe suponer al menos el 51 % de la receta de un Bourbon?","Corn":"Maíz","Rye":"Centeno","Barley":"Cebada","Wheat":"Trigo","Bourbon is a corn-majority whiskey, at least 51%.":"El Bourbon es un whiskey con mayoría de maíz, al menos el 51 %.","Barley and rye often appear in the recipe, but only as secondary grains. If rye reaches 51%, the whiskey becomes a Rye. 100% malted barley is the rule for Scottish Single Malt.":"La cebada y el centeno aparecen a menudo en la receta, pero solo como cereales secundarios. Si el centeno llega al 51 %, el whiskey pasa a ser un Rye. La cebada malteada al 100 % es la regla del Single Malt escocés.","Where can Bourbon be made?":"¿Dónde se puede producir Bourbon?","Anywhere in the USA":"En cualquier lugar de EE. UU.","Only in Kentucky":"Solo en Kentucky","Only in Kentucky and Tennessee":"Solo en Kentucky y Tennessee","Anywhere in North America":"En cualquier lugar de Norteamérica","Bourbon can be made across the USA, though Kentucky leads production.":"El Bourbon puede hacerse en todo EE. UU., aunque Kentucky lidera la producción.","The link with Kentucky is strong because most Bourbon is made there, but it is not a requirement. It is Tennessee whiskey that is tied to one state. Outside the USA, in Canada for example, Bourbon cannot be made.":"La asociación con Kentucky es fuerte porque allí se produce la mayor parte, pero no es obligatoria. Es el Tennessee whiskey el que está ligado a un solo estado. Fuera de Estados Unidos, por ejemplo en Canadá, no se puede hacer Bourbon.","What barrels must Bourbon be aged in?":"¿En qué barricas debe envejecer el Bourbon?","New charred oak":"Roble nuevo quemado","Previously used oak":"Roble ya usado","Former Cognac barrels":"Antiguas barricas de coñac","New uncharred oak":"Roble nuevo sin quemar","The law requires new oak barrels charred on the inside.":"La ley exige barricas de roble nuevo, quemadas por dentro.","Used barrels give less aroma each time they are used, so they are not allowed for Bourbon. Even a new barrel is not enough unless it is charred. This choice explains Bourbon's deep colour and strong vanilla and coconut notes.":"Las barricas usadas ceden menos aroma con cada uso, así que no se admiten para el Bourbon. Ni siquiera una barrica nueva basta si no está quemada. Esta elección explica el color intenso y las marcadas notas de vainilla y coco del Bourbon.","Which aromas are typical of a Bourbon?":"¿Qué aromas son típicos de un Bourbon?","Sweetcorn, vanilla, coconut, fruit":"Maíz dulce, vainilla, coco, fruta","Peat smoke, cereal, honey":"Humo de turba, cereal, miel","Grass, vegetal, fresh cane":"Hierba, vegetal, caña fresca","Agave, pepper, olive":"Agave, pimienta, aceituna","Corn gives sweetcorn notes; new charred barrels give vanilla and coconut.":"El maíz da notas de maíz dulce; las barricas nuevas quemadas, vainilla y coco.","Peat smoke belongs to some Scottish Single Malts. Grassy cane notes are typical of rum made from cane juice. Agave, pepper and olive describe Tequila.":"El humo de turba pertenece a algunos Single Malt escoceses. Las notas herbáceas de caña son típicas del ron de jugo de caña. Agave, pimienta y aceituna describen el tequila.","How is Bourbon usually distilled?":"¿Cómo se destila normalmente el Bourbon?","In a column still, to a low strength":"En columna, hasta una graduación baja","In a column still, up to 96% abv":"En columna, hasta 96 % vol","Twice in a pot still, by law":"Dos veces en alambique, por ley","In a short column, then charcoal filtered":"En columna corta y luego filtrado con carbón","A column still is normal, but stopped at low strength to keep flavour.":"Se suele usar columna, pero a baja graduación para conservar el sabor.","At 96% abv you would get a neutral spirit like vodka's, and Bourbon would lose its pronounced character. Compulsory double pot distillation is the rule for Cognac. Maple charcoal filtering is the signature step of Tennessee whiskey.":"A 96 % vol se obtendría un destilado neutro como el del vodka, y el Bourbon perdería su carácter intenso. La doble destilación obligatoria en alambique es la regla del coñac. El filtrado con carbón de arce es el paso distintivo del Tennessee whiskey.","A customer says Bourbon 'tastes sweet'. Which explanation is correct?":"Un cliente dice que el Bourbon 'sabe dulce'. ¿Qué explicación es correcta?","It has no added sugar; vanilla and fruit aromas create that impression":"No lleva azúcar añadido: la vainilla y la fruta dan esa impresión","Sugar is always added after ageing":"Siempre se añade azúcar tras el envejecimiento","Sugar from the corn survives distillation":"El azúcar del maíz sobrevive a la destilación","New barrels release sugar into the whiskey":"Las barricas nuevas ceden azúcar al whiskey","Bourbon is dry: the perceived 'sweetness' comes from aromas, not sugar.":"El Bourbon es seco: el 'dulzor' percibido viene de aromas, no de azúcar.","Every spirit is dry when it comes off the still, and no sugar is added to Bourbon afterwards. Barrels give colour and aromas such as vanilla and coconut, which the nose links with desserts, but not sugar.":"Todo destilado sale seco del alambique, y al Bourbon no se le añade azúcar después. Las barricas ceden color y aromas como la vainilla y el coco, que la nariz asocia a los postres, pero no azúcar.","Compared with a used barrel, a new barrel gives a spirit...":"Frente a una barrica ya usada, una barrica nueva cede al destilado...","more colour and more aroma":"más color y más aroma","less colour and less aroma":"menos color y menos aroma","more sugar and sweetness":"más azúcar y más dulzor","only colour, no aroma":"solo color, sin aroma","A never-used barrel gives the most; each reuse weakens its effect.":"Una barrica nunca usada es la que más cede; cada reutilización reduce su efecto.","That is why Bourbon, which must use new barrels, shows such clear oak colour and aromas. Barrels do not add sugar: sweetness only comes from sugar added after distillation. And a new barrel always brings aromas too, such as vanilla and coconut.":"Por eso el Bourbon, que debe usar barricas nuevas, muestra un color y unos aromas de roble tan marcados. Las barricas no añaden azúcar: el dulzor solo viene del azúcar añadido tras la destilación. Y una barrica nueva siempre aporta también aromas, como vainilla y coco.","What sets Tennessee whiskey apart from Bourbon in production?":"¿Qué distingue al Tennessee whiskey del Bourbon en la producción?","Maple charcoal filtering before the barrel":"Un filtrado con carbón de arce antes de la barrica","A recipe with at least 51% rye":"Una receta con al menos un 51 % de centeno","Ageing in previously used barrels":"El envejecimiento en barricas ya usadas","Double distillation in a pot still":"La doble destilación en alambique","The new spirit runs through maple charcoal before it goes into the barrel.":"El destilado nuevo pasa por carbón de arce antes de entrar en barrica.","Otherwise Tennessee whiskey follows Bourbon's rules: mostly corn, low-strength column distillation, new charred barrels. 51% rye defines Rye whiskey. Used barrels and double pot distillation are not part of its rules.":"Por lo demás, el Tennessee whiskey sigue las reglas del Bourbon: mayoría de maíz, columna a baja graduación y barricas nuevas quemadas. El 51 % de centeno define el Rye. Las barricas usadas y la doble destilación en alambique no forman parte de sus reglas.","What does the maple charcoal filtering of Tennessee whiskey do?":"¿Qué efecto tiene el filtrado con carbón de arce del Tennessee whiskey?","Removes impurities and smooths it, adding no flavour":"Elimina impurezas y lo suaviza, sin añadir sabor","Adds a light maple syrup flavour":"Añade un ligero sabor a sirope de arce","Adds smoky, peat-like notes":"Añade notas ahumadas parecidas a la turba","Removes all the colour from the barrel":"Elimina todo el color de la barrica","The charcoal holds back some impurities and smooths, but adds no aroma.":"El carbón retiene parte de las impurezas y suaviza, pero no aporta aromas.","The word 'maple' is misleading: the charcoal passes on no syrup or smoke flavour. Also, the filtering happens before the barrel, on a spirit that is still colourless, so it cannot remove colour that is not there yet.":"La palabra 'arce' confunde: el carbón no transmite sabor a sirope ni a humo. Además, el filtrado se hace antes de la barrica, sobre un destilado aún incoloro, así que no puede quitar un color que todavía no existe.","Where can Tennessee whiskey be made?":"¿Dónde se puede producir el Tennessee whiskey?","Only in the state of Tennessee":"Solo en el estado de Tennessee","In Tennessee or Kentucky":"En Tennessee o en Kentucky","Anywhere, if maple charcoal filtered":"En cualquier sitio, si se filtra con carbón de arce","The name is tied to the state: it can only be made in Tennessee.":"El nombre está ligado al estado: solo se elabora en Tennessee.","It is Bourbon that can be made anywhere in the USA. Kentucky is the heart of Bourbon, not of Tennessee whiskey. Charcoal filtering is necessary but not enough: without the right place, the name cannot be used.":"Es el Bourbon el que puede producirse en todo EE. UU. Kentucky es el corazón del Bourbon, no del Tennessee whiskey. El filtrado con carbón es necesario pero no suficiente: sin el lugar correcto no se puede usar el nombre.","What defines an American Rye whiskey?":"¿Qué define un Rye whiskey estadounidense?","At least 51% rye; spicy, peppery aromas":"Al menos 51 % de centeno; aromas especiados y picantes","100% rye and smoky notes":"100 % centeno y notas ahumadas","At least 51% corn; coconut notes":"Al menos 51 % de maíz; notas de coco","At least 51% rye; grassy cane notes":"Al menos 51 % de centeno; notas herbáceas de caña","Rye has at least 51% rye grain, giving a spicy, peppery character.":"El Rye lleva al menos un 51 % de centeno, que le da un carácter especiado y picante.","The threshold is 51%, not 100%, and smoke has nothing to do with it. 51% corn defines Bourbon. Grassy cane notes belong to rum made from cane juice, not to a grain whiskey.":"El umbral es el 51 %, no el 100 %, y el humo no tiene nada que ver. El 51 % de maíz define el Bourbon. Las notas herbáceas de caña pertenecen al ron de jugo de caña, no a un whiskey de cereales.","A bartender wants an American whiskey with a spicy, peppery character. Which should they choose?":"En la barra se busca un whiskey estadounidense especiado y picante. ¿Cuál elegir?","Rye whiskey":"Un Rye whiskey","Bourbon":"Un Bourbon","Tennessee whiskey":"Un Tennessee whiskey","A light Irish whiskey":"Un whiskey irlandés ligero","Rye grain, the main grain in Rye whiskey, gives spicy, peppery aromas.":"El centeno, cereal principal del Rye, aporta aromas especiados y picantes.","Bourbon and Tennessee whiskey are mostly corn, so they lean towards sweetcorn, vanilla and coconut. A light, smooth Irish whiskey is not American and does not have this peppery profile.":"El Bourbon y el Tennessee whiskey llevan sobre todo maíz, así que tiran más a maíz dulce, vainilla y coco. Un whiskey irlandés ligero y suave no es estadounidense ni tiene este perfil picante.","What is the only rule that separates American Rye whiskey from Bourbon?":"¿Cuál es la única regla que separa el Rye whiskey estadounidense del Bourbon?","The main grain in the recipe":"El cereal principal de la receta","The type of barrel used":"El tipo de barrica usada","The type of still used":"El tipo de alambique usado","The state where it is made":"El estado donde se produce","Rye is made exactly like Bourbon, but with rye instead of corn.":"El Rye se hace exactamente como el Bourbon, pero con centeno en lugar de maíz.","Both use new charred oak barrels and usually low-strength column distillation. Neither is tied to one state; it is Tennessee whiskey that has a geographical limit. Only the grain that makes up 51% changes.":"Los dos usan barricas de roble nuevo quemado y, normalmente, columna a baja graduación. Ninguno está ligado a un solo estado: es el Tennessee whiskey el que tiene un límite geográfico. Solo cambia el cereal que supera el 51 %.","How are most Irish whiskeys made?":"¿Cómo se elabora la mayoría de los whiskeys irlandeses?","By blending pot-still and column-still spirits":"Mezclando destilados de alambique y de columna","Only from malted barley and peat":"Solo con cebada malteada y turba","With 51% corn in new barrels":"Con 51 % de maíz en barricas nuevas","Without any oak ageing":"Sin envejecimiento en roble","Most Irish whiskeys combine pot-still and column-still spirits.":"La mayoría de los whiskeys irlandeses unen destilados de alambique y de columna.","The typical result is a light, smooth whiskey. Peat belongs to some Scottish Single Malts, and 51% corn with new barrels to Bourbon. Like all whiskies, Irish whiskeys are aged in oak.":"El resultado típico es un whiskey ligero y suave. La turba se asocia a algunos Single Malt escoceses, y el 51 % de maíz con barricas nuevas al Bourbon. Como todos los whiskies, los irlandeses envejecen en roble.","What character does unmalted barley give some Irish pot-still whiskeys?":"¿Qué carácter da la cebada sin maltear a algunos whiskeys irlandeses de alambique?","Nutty notes and an oily texture":"Notas de frutos secos y textura oleosa","Smoky, medicinal notes":"Notas ahumadas y medicinales","Spicy, peppery notes":"Notas especiadas y picantes","Sweetcorn and coconut notes":"Notas de maíz dulce y coco","Unmalted barley brings a nutty character and an oily texture.":"La cebada sin maltear aporta carácter a frutos secos y textura oleosa.","It is an unusual ingredient, used only in some Irish whiskeys made in pot stills. Smoke comes from peat, pepper from rye, and sweetcorn and coconut from corn and new barrels as in Bourbon.":"Es un ingrediente poco común, que solo usan algunos whiskeys irlandeses destilados en alambique. El humo viene de la turba, la pimienta del centeno, y el maíz dulce y el coco del maíz y las barricas nuevas, como en el Bourbon.","What is the signature flavour of the best Canadian whiskies?":"¿Cuál es el sabor distintivo de los mejores whiskies canadienses?","Peat":"La turba","Unmalted barley":"La cebada sin maltear","Spicy, peppery rye is the signature of the best Canadian whiskies.":"El centeno, especiado y picante, es la firma de los mejores whiskies canadienses.","Canada uses many different grains, but rye gives the most recognisable character. Peat is typical of some Scottish malts. Corn dominates Bourbon, and unmalted barley is an Irish speciality.":"Canadá usa muchos cereales distintos, pero es el centeno el que da el carácter más reconocible. La turba es típica de algunas maltas escocesas. El maíz domina en el Bourbon, y la cebada sin maltear es una particularidad irlandesa.","Which description fits a typical Canadian whisky?":"¿Qué descripción corresponde a un whisky canadiense típico?","Many grains; a blend of high- and low-strength spirits":"Muchos cereales; mezcla de destilados de alta y baja graduación","Malted barley only, pot still, one distillery":"Solo cebada malteada, alambique, una destilería","51% corn and maple charcoal filtering":"51 % de maíz y filtrado con carbón de arce","Neutral spirit at 96%, unaged":"Destilado neutro al 96 % y sin envejecer","Canada uses several grains and blends lighter and more flavourful spirits.":"Canadá usa varios cereales y mezcla destilados ligeros y más sabrosos.","Malted barley only from one distillery describes a Single Malt. Corn plus maple charcoal is the profile of Tennessee whiskey. An unaged neutral spirit is the base of vodka, while every whisky spends time in oak.":"Solo cebada malteada de una destilería describe un Single Malt. Maíz más carbón de arce es el perfil del Tennessee whiskey. Un destilado neutro sin envejecer es la base del vodka, mientras que todo whisky pasa por roble.","Which country was Japanese whisky production modelled on?":"¿En qué país se inspiró la industria del whisky japonés?","Scotland":"Escocia","The USA":"Estados Unidos","Ireland":"Irlanda","Canada":"Canadá","Japanese whisky follows the Scottish model, with malts and blends.":"El whisky japonés sigue el modelo escocés, con maltas y blended.","As in Scotland, Japan makes malt whiskies and blended whiskies. The USA has a different model based on corn or rye and new barrels. Ireland and Canada have their own traditions of blending different spirits.":"Como en Escocia, Japón produce whiskies de malta y blended. Estados Unidos tiene otro modelo, basado en maíz o centeno y barricas nuevas. Irlanda y Canadá tienen tradiciones propias, con mezclas de destilados distintos.","How is the traditional style of Japanese whisky described?":"¿Cómo se describe el estilo tradicional del whisky japonés?","Elegant and refined":"Elegante y refinado","Very sweet from added sugar":"Muy dulce por el azúcar añadido","Peppery and rye-based":"Picante, a base de centeno","Neutral, with almost no aroma":"Neutro, casi sin aromas","Traditionally, Japanese whiskies are elegant and refined.":"Tradicionalmente, los whiskies japoneses son elegantes y refinados.","Today many producers are also exploring new styles, but the classic hallmark remains elegance. Added sugar is not part of the typical profile. Rye is the signature of Canada and American Rye, and a neutral style describes vodka.":"Hoy muchos productores exploran también estilos nuevos, pero el sello clásico sigue siendo la elegancia. El azúcar añadido no forma parte del perfil típico. El centeno es la firma de Canadá y del Rye estadounidense, y un estilo neutro describe el vodka.","A Kentucky whiskey: 70% corn, low-strength column still, new charred oak, no charcoal filtering. What is it?":"Un whiskey de Kentucky: 70 % de maíz, columna a baja graduación, roble nuevo quemado, sin filtrado con carbón. ¿Qué es?","A Bourbon":"Un Bourbon","A Tennessee whiskey":"Un Tennessee whiskey","A Rye whiskey":"Un Rye whiskey","A Canadian whisky":"Un whisky canadiense","Mostly corn, new charred barrels, made in the USA: every Bourbon rule is met.":"Mayoría de maíz, barricas nuevas quemadas y hecho en EE. UU.: cumple todas las reglas del Bourbon.","To be Tennessee whiskey it would need maple charcoal filtering and to be made in Tennessee; both are missing here. With 70% corn it cannot be a Rye, which needs 51% rye. And Kentucky is not in Canada.":"Para ser Tennessee whiskey necesitaría el filtrado con carbón de arce y producirse en Tennessee: aquí faltan las dos cosas. Con un 70 % de maíz no puede ser un Rye, que exige un 51 % de centeno. Y Kentucky no está en Canadá.","What is the raw material of rum?":"¿Cuál es la materia prima del ron?","Blue agave":"El agave azul","Rum comes from sugar cane, used as juice or as molasses.":"El ron se obtiene de la caña de azúcar, como jugo o como melaza.","Grains are the base of whisky, blue agave of Tequila and grapes of brandies such as Cognac. Cane can be used fresh, by crushing out its juice, or in the form of molasses.":"Los cereales son la base del whisky, el agave azul la del tequila y la uva la de brandis como el coñac. La caña puede usarse fresca, prensando su jugo, o en forma de melaza.","Why is rum production centred on places like the Caribbean?":"¿Por qué la producción de ron se concentra en zonas como el Caribe?","Sugar cane grows in hot climates":"La caña de azúcar crece en climas cálidos","Column stills are only allowed there":"Solo allí se permiten las columnas","The law bans rum outside the Caribbean":"La ley prohíbe el ron fuera del Caribe","Heat speeds up ageing":"El calor acelera el envejecimiento","Rum is made where cane grows, which means hot countries.":"El ron se produce donde crece la caña, es decir, en países cálidos.","The reason is agricultural: the raw material needs heat. No law reserves rum for the Caribbean, and column stills are used all over the world. The idea of faster ageing is not why rum is made in these areas.":"La razón es agrícola: la materia prima necesita calor. Ninguna ley reserva el ron al Caribe, y las columnas se usan en todo el mundo. La idea de un envejecimiento más rápido no explica por qué el ron nace en estas zonas.","What is molasses?":"¿Qué es la melaza?","A black, sticky by-product of sugar-making":"Un subproducto negro y espeso de la fabricación de azúcar","The fresh juice of just-crushed cane":"El jugo fresco de la caña recién prensada","A cane wine that has already fermented":"Un vino de caña ya fermentado","The caramel colouring used in rums":"El colorante caramelo usado en los rones","Molasses is left over when cane juice is turned into sugar.":"La melaza queda cuando se convierte el jugo de caña en azúcar.","It is black and sticky and must be mixed with water before fermentation. Fresh juice is the other raw material, used for rhum agricole. Molasses is not already fermented, and it should not be confused with caramel, which is only used to adjust colour.":"Es negra y pegajosa y hay que mezclarla con agua antes de fermentar. El jugo fresco es la otra materia prima, la de los rhum agricole. No está ya fermentada, y no debe confundirse con el caramelo, que solo se usa para ajustar el color.","What flavour do cane-juice rums often have?":"¿Qué sabor suelen tener los rones de jugo de caña?","Very pronounced grassy, herbaceous":"Herbáceo y vegetal, muy marcado","Caramel and brown sugar":"Caramelo y azúcar moreno","Juniper and citrus":"Enebro y cítricos","Fresh cane juice gives rum a grassy, herbaceous character.":"El jugo de caña fresco da a los rones un carácter herbáceo y vegetal.","Caramel and brown sugar are the mark of molasses rums, the most common choice in the Caribbean. Peat smoke belongs to some Scotch whiskies, while juniper and citrus are typical of gin.":"Caramelo y azúcar moreno son la marca de los rones de melaza, la opción más común en el Caribe. El humo de turba pertenece a algunos whiskies escoceses, y el enebro y los cítricos son típicos de la ginebra.","In the Caribbean, where must rhum agricole come from?":"En el Caribe, ¿de dónde debe proceder el rhum agricole?","Martinique or Guadeloupe":"Martinica o Guadalupa","Jamaica or Cuba":"Jamaica o Cuba","Puerto Rico or Jamaica":"Puerto Rico o Jamaica","Any Caribbean island":"De cualquier isla del Caribe","In the Caribbean, rhum agricole must come from Martinique or Guadeloupe.":"En el Caribe, el rhum agricole debe proceder de Martinica o Guadalupa.","Rhum agricole is the best example of a cane-juice rum. Jamaica is known for very fruity rums, Cuba and Puerto Rico for light rums from tall columns. Simply being a Caribbean island is not enough to use this name.":"El rhum agricole es el mejor ejemplo de ron de jugo de caña. Jamaica es conocida por sus rones muy afrutados, y Cuba y Puerto Rico por sus rones ligeros de columna alta. No basta con ser una isla del Caribe para usar este nombre.","Which raw material do most Caribbean distillers use?":"¿Qué materia prima usa la mayoría de los destiladores caribeños?","Molasses":"La melaza","Fresh cane juice":"El jugo de caña fresco","Refined white sugar":"El azúcar blanco refinado","Honey":"La miel","Molasses is the choice of most Caribbean distillers.":"La melaza es la opción de la mayoría de los destiladores del Caribe.","Fresh juice is used mainly for rhum agricole, a smaller share of production. Refined sugar is the main product of the industry that leaves molasses behind, not rum's raw material. Honey has nothing to do with rum.":"El jugo fresco se usa sobre todo para el rhum agricole, una parte menor de la producción. El azúcar refinado es el producto principal de la industria de la que sale la melaza, no la materia prima del ron. La miel no tiene que ver con el ron.","Which flavours are typical of a molasses rum?":"¿Qué sabores son típicos de un ron de melaza?","Fresh grass and vegetal notes":"Hierba fresca y notas vegetales","Sweetcorn and coconut":"Maíz dulce y coco","Agave, olive and pepper":"Agave, aceituna y pimienta","Molasses brings caramel and brown sugar notes to rum.":"La melaza aporta al ron notas de caramelo y azúcar moreno.","Grassy, vegetal notes are typical of fresh cane juice. Sweetcorn and coconut recall Bourbon, and agave, olive and pepper recall Tequila. Each raw material leaves its own set of aromas.":"Las notas herbáceas y vegetales son típicas del jugo de caña fresco. Maíz dulce y coco recuerdan al Bourbon, y agave, aceituna y pimienta al tequila. Cada materia prima deja su propio conjunto de aromas.","What must be done to molasses before it can ferment?":"¿Qué hay que hacer con la melaza antes de que pueda fermentar?","Mix it with water":"Mezclarla con agua","Let it sprout":"Hacerla germinar","Cook it in ovens":"Cocerla en hornos","Filter it through charcoal":"Filtrarla con carbón","Molasses is too thick: it must be mixed with water to ferment.":"La melaza es demasiado espesa: hay que diluirla con agua para que fermente.","Sprouting belongs to malting grain for whisky. Cooking in ovens is how sugar is created from agave cores for Tequila. Charcoal filtering comes after distillation, for example to remove colour from rum.":"La germinación pertenece al malteado de los cereales para el whisky. La cocción en hornos sirve para crear azúcar a partir de los corazones de agave para el tequila. El filtrado con carbón se usa después de destilar, por ejemplo para quitar color al ron.","Which stage mainly creates the intense tropical fruit aromas of some rums?":"¿De qué fase proceden sobre todo los intensos aromas de fruta tropical de algunos rones?","Fermentation":"La fermentación","Oak ageing":"El envejecimiento en roble","Charcoal filtering":"El filtrado con carbón","Dilution with water":"La dilución con agua","During fermentation, yeast can create intense tropical fruit aromas.":"Durante la fermentación, las levaduras pueden crear intensos aromas de fruta tropical.","Oak adds vanilla and sweet spice instead. Charcoal filtering removes colour; it does not add fruit. The water used for dilution is pure and brings no flavour.":"El roble aporta más bien vainilla y especias dulces. El filtrado con carbón quita color, no añade fruta. El agua de dilución es pura y no aporta sabor.","Which rum style are Jamaican distillers famous for?":"¿Por qué estilo de ron son famosos los destiladores de Jamaica?","Intensely fruity rums":"Rones intensamente afrutados","Light rums from tall columns":"Rones ligeros de columna alta","Grassy cane-juice rums":"Rones herbáceos de jugo de caña","Neutral rums at 96% abv":"Rones neutros al 96 % vol","In Jamaica, fermentation is used to create rums loaded with tropical fruit.":"En Jamaica se aprovecha la fermentación para crear rones cargados de fruta tropical.","Light rums from tall columns are linked to Cuba and Puerto Rico. Grassy cane-juice rums are the rhum agricole of Martinique and Guadeloupe. A neutral rum at 96% would have almost no aroma, the opposite of the Jamaican style.":"Los rones ligeros de columna alta se asocian a Cuba y Puerto Rico. Los rones herbáceos de jugo de caña son los rhum agricole de Martinica y Guadalupa. Un ron neutro al 96 % casi no tendría aroma, lo contrario del estilo jamaicano.","How are the light-aroma rums of Cuba and Puerto Rico made?":"¿Cómo se elaboran los rones de aroma ligero de Cuba y Puerto Rico?","In tall columns, to a high strength":"En columnas altas, a alta graduación","In pot stills, to a low strength":"En alambiques, a baja graduación","In short columns, like rhum agricole":"En columnas cortas, como el rhum agricole","With no distillation, only fermented":"Sin destilar, solo fermentados","Tall columns and high strength give rums with a light aroma.":"Columnas altas y graduación elevada dan rones de aroma ligero.","The higher the distillation strength, the less aroma remains. Pot stills and short columns give flavourful, characterful spirits instead. Without distillation you would not have rum at all, just a low-strength fermented liquid.":"Cuanto más alta es la graduación de destilación, menos aroma queda. El alambique y la columna corta dan, en cambio, destilados sabrosos y con carácter. Sin destilación no habría ron, sino un líquido fermentado de baja graduación.","A distillery wants a pronounced, characterful rum. Which still could it choose?":"Una destilería quiere un ron intenso y con mucho carácter. ¿Qué alambique puede elegir?","A pot still":"Un alambique","A tall column run to high strength":"Una columna alta a alta graduación","A column still taken to 96% abv":"Una columna hasta 96 % vol","None: charcoal filtering is enough":"Ninguno: basta con filtrar con carbón","A pot still gives a low-strength, pronounced, characterful spirit.":"El alambique da un destilado de baja graduación, intenso y con carácter.","A short column could also work, but among these options only the pot still points the right way. Tall columns and 96% abv lead to light or neutral spirits. Charcoal filtering does not create character; if anything, it removes colour.":"Una columna corta también podría servir, pero entre estas opciones solo el alambique va en la buena dirección. Las columnas altas y el 96 % llevan a destilados ligeros o neutros. El filtrado con carbón no crea carácter: más bien quita color.","What type of still is typically used for rhum agricole?":"¿Con qué tipo de alambique se destila normalmente el rhum agricole?","A short column still":"Una columna corta","A compulsory double pot still":"Un doble alambique obligatorio","A pot still with a maple filter":"Un alambique con filtro de arce","Rhum agricole is distilled in short columns, which give a flavourful spirit.":"El rhum agricole se destila en columnas cortas, que dan un destilado sabroso.","A short column with few sections keeps plenty of intensity, similar to a pot still. Very tall columns are used for light rums. Compulsory double pot distillation is the rule for Cognac, and maple charcoal belongs to Tennessee whiskey.":"Una columna corta, con pocas secciones, conserva mucha intensidad, parecida a la de un alambique. Las columnas muy altas sirven para los rones ligeros. La doble destilación obligatoria en alambique es la regla del coñac, y el carbón de arce está ligado al Tennessee whiskey.","In a country where rum must be oak-aged, how can a colourless rum be made?":"En un país donde el ron debe envejecer en barrica, ¿cómo se obtiene un ron incoloro?","By charcoal filtering it after the barrel":"Filtrándolo con carbón tras la barrica","By adding caramel":"Añadiendo caramelo","By diluting it with more water":"Diluyéndolo con más agua","By adding sugar":"Añadiendo azúcar","Charcoal filtering removes the colour picked up from the wood.":"El filtrado con carbón elimina el color tomado de la madera.","Caramel adds colour rather than removing it. Water lowers the strength but leaves the colour almost unchanged, and sugar changes sweetness, not shade. The other way to get a white rum, where the law allows, is not to age it and to keep it in steel.":"El caramelo añade color en lugar de quitarlo. El agua baja la graduación pero deja el color casi igual, y el azúcar cambia el dulzor, no el tono. La otra forma de obtener un ron blanco, donde la ley lo permite, es no envejecerlo y guardarlo en acero.","Many Caribbean distilleries own both pot stills and columns. Why is that useful?":"Muchas destilerías caribeñas tienen alambiques y columnas. ¿Por qué es útil?","To have spirits of different intensities to blend":"Para tener destilados de distinta intensidad que mezclar","Because the law requires two distillations":"Porque la ley exige dos destilaciones","Because columns are used for ageing":"Porque las columnas sirven para envejecer","Because the pot still is used to sweeten":"Porque el alambique sirve para endulzar","Two kinds of still give light and pronounced spirits for building different styles.":"Dos tipos de alambique dan destilados ligeros e intensos para componer estilos distintos.","With several types of spirit, blenders can create very different products, also combining different ages and distilleries. No general Caribbean rule requires two distillations. Columns are for distilling, not ageing, and sugar is added afterwards, not in the still.":"Con varios tipos de destilado se pueden crear productos muy distintos, combinando también edades y destilerías diferentes. Ninguna regla general del Caribe exige dos destilaciones. Las columnas sirven para destilar, no para envejecer, y el azúcar se añade después, no en el alambique.","Which aromas does oak ageing add to a rum?":"¿Qué aromas añade el envejecimiento en roble a un ron?","Vanilla and sweet spice":"Vainilla y especias dulces","Intense tropical fruit":"Fruta tropical intensa","Oak gives rum vanilla and sweet spice, as well as colour.":"El roble cede al ron vainilla y especias dulces, además de color.","Grassy notes come from cane juice, the raw material. Intense tropical fruit is born in fermentation. Peat smoke is created while malting grain, so it has nothing to do with rum.":"Las notas herbáceas vienen del jugo de caña, es decir, de la materia prima. La fruta tropical intensa nace en la fermentación. El humo de turba se crea al maltear cereales, así que no tiene que ver con el ron.","Which statement about adding sugar to rum is correct?":"¿Qué afirmación sobre añadir azúcar al ron es correcta?","Common in Central and South America, banned in some countries":"Es habitual en América Central y del Sur, prohibido en algunos países","Required for every Caribbean rum":"Es obligatorio para todos los rones caribeños","Banned everywhere in the world":"Está prohibido en todo el mundo","Happens on its own during ageing":"Ocurre sola durante el envejecimiento","Some rums are sweetened: common in Central and South America, but not allowed everywhere.":"Algunos rones se endulzan: práctica común en América Central y del Sur, pero no permitida en todas partes.","The rules change from country to country, so neither a requirement nor a ban applies everywhere. Every spirit is dry when it leaves the still: sweetness only comes from sugar added after distillation, not from the barrel.":"Las reglas cambian de un país a otro, así que ni la obligación ni la prohibición valen en todas partes. Todo destilado sale seco del alambique: el dulzor solo viene del azúcar añadido tras la destilación, no de la barrica.","A rum has a deep amber colour. What can you conclude for certain?":"Un ron tiene un color ámbar oscuro. ¿Qué se puede deducir con seguridad?","Nothing about age: the colour may come from caramel":"Nada sobre la edad: el color puede venir del caramelo","That it was aged at least ten years":"Que ha envejecido al menos diez años","That it was made from fresh cane juice":"Que está hecho con jugo de caña fresco","That it was distilled in a pot still":"Que se destiló en alambique","Many rums get caramel, sometimes for almost all their colour, so shade proves nothing about age.":"Muchos rones reciben caramelo, a veces casi todo su color, así que el tono no demuestra la edad.","This is why sorting rum by colour works badly. Colour also says nothing about the raw material or the type of still: those depend on the production stages, not on the shade in the glass.":"Por eso clasificar el ron por color funciona mal. El color tampoco dice nada sobre la materia prima ni sobre el tipo de alambique: eso depende de las fases de producción, no del tono en la copa.","Malting":"Malteado","Barley sprouts and makes enzymes; hot air then stops the growth.":"La cebada germina y crea enzimas; el aire caliente detiene el crecimiento.","What do barley enzymes do?":"¿Para qué sirven las enzimas de la cebada?","In water, they turn the grain's starch into sugar yeast can ferment.":"En el agua convierten el almidón de los cereales en azúcar fermentable.","Scotch: the basic rule":"Scotch: regla básica","Distilled in Scotland and aged there for at least three years.":"Destilado en Escocia y envejecido allí al menos tres años.","Single Malt Scotch":"Single Malt Scotch","100% malted barley, pot stills, one distillery.":"100 % cebada malteada, alambiques, una sola destilería.","Fuel burned while heating malted barley; gives smoke to a few Single Malts.":"Combustible quemado al calentar la cebada malteada: da humo a pocos Single Malt.","Grain whisky":"Whisky de grano","Malted barley plus other grains, column-distilled: light, smooth, rarely sold alone.":"Cebada malteada y otros cereales, en columna: ligero, suave, rara vez se vende solo.","Blended Scotch":"Blended Scotch","Malt plus grain whiskies from different distilleries; usually smoother.":"Maltas y whiskies de grano de distintas destilerías; suele ser más suave.","Bourbon: grain rule":"Bourbon: cereal","At least 51% corn, usually with some barley and rye.":"Al menos 51 % de maíz, normalmente con algo de cebada y centeno.","Bourbon: barrels":"Bourbon: barricas","New charred oak: vanilla, coconut and deep colour.":"Roble nuevo quemado: vainilla, coco y color intenso.","Where is Bourbon made?":"¿Dónde se hace el Bourbon?","Anywhere in the USA; Kentucky is the leading state.":"En cualquier lugar de EE. UU.; Kentucky es el estado principal.","Like Bourbon, but made only in Tennessee and maple-charcoal filtered before the barrel.":"Como el Bourbon, pero solo en Tennessee y filtrado con carbón de arce antes de la barrica.","American Rye whiskey":"Rye whiskey estadounidense","Made like Bourbon but with at least 51% rye: spicy and peppery.":"Hecho como el Bourbon pero con al menos 51 % de centeno: especiado y picante.","Irish whiskey":"Whiskey irlandés","Mostly pot + column blends, light and smooth; sometimes unmalted barley.":"Sobre todo alambique + columna, ligero y suave; a veces cebada sin maltear.","Canadian whisky":"Whisky canadiense","Many grains, high- and low-strength blend; rye is the signature.":"Muchos cereales, mezcla de alta y baja graduación; firma del centeno.","Japanese whisky":"Whisky japonés","Scottish model: malts and blends, traditionally elegant and refined.":"Modelo escocés: maltas y blended, tradicionalmente elegantes y refinados.","Black, sticky sugar by-product; mixed with water; gives caramel and brown sugar.":"Subproducto negro y espeso del azúcar; se diluye con agua; da caramelo y azúcar moreno.","Cane-juice rum":"Ron de jugo de caña","Fresh juice fermented at once: very pronounced grassy, herbaceous flavour.":"Jugo fresco fermentado enseguida: sabor herbáceo y vegetal muy marcado.","Rhum agricole":"Rhum agricole","Cane juice, short column; in the Caribbean, only Martinique or Guadeloupe.":"Jugo de caña, columna corta; en el Caribe, solo Martinica o Guadalupa.","Jamaican rum":"Ron de Jamaica","Known for intense tropical fruit aromas created during fermentation.":"Famoso por sus intensos aromas de fruta tropical, creados en la fermentación.","Light rums of Cuba and Puerto Rico":"Rones ligeros de Cuba y Puerto Rico","Tall columns, high strength: light aroma.":"Columnas altas, alta graduación: aroma ligero.","Charcoal filtering in rum":"Filtrado con carbón en el ron","Removes oak colour, giving a white rum even after ageing.":"Quita el color del roble: da un ron blanco aunque esté envejecido.","Sweetened rum":"Ron endulzado","Common in Central and South America; not allowed in some countries.":"Habitual en América Central y del Sur; prohibido en algunos países.","From blue agave to sweet juice":"Del agave azul al jugo dulce","Tequila is a Mexican spirit with a very clear identity: it can only be made in certain Mexican states named by law, and only from blue agave, a plant native to Mexico. It is not a cactus, even if it looks a bit like one: long, spiky leaves fan out around a large, hard core. That core is the part the distiller actually wants.":"El Tequila es un destilado mexicano con una identidad muy clara: solo puede elaborarse en determinados estados de México fijados por ley y únicamente a partir del agave azul, una planta originaria de ese país. No es un cactus, aunque lo parezca: sus largas hojas puntiagudas rodean un gran corazón duro. Ese corazón es lo que de verdad le interesa al destilador.","At harvest the leaves are cut away, leaving only the core. As with grains, a freshly harvested agave core has no sugar ready to ferment: it has to be processed first. The cores are cooked slowly in ovens until they turn soft and sugars form inside them. Think of a hard potato that you can mash with a fork once it has been cooked: the idea is much the same.":"En la cosecha se cortan las hojas y solo queda el corazón. Como ocurre con los cereales, el corazón recién cosechado no tiene azúcares listos para fermentar: hay que transformarlo. Se cuece lentamente en hornos hasta que se ablanda y en su interior se forman azúcares. Piensa en una patata dura que, una vez cocida, se aplasta con un tenedor: la idea es parecida.","Once cooked, the cores are crushed and give up a sweet juice. That juice carries the very recognisable aromas of blue agave: herbaceous and vegetal notes, hints of olive and earth, and a touch of pepper. These aromas are what set Tequila so clearly apart from rum or whisky, and the producer will try to protect them through the following steps.":"Una vez cocidos, los corazones se trituran y sueltan un jugo dulce. Ese jugo lleva los aromas muy reconocibles del agave azul: notas herbáceas y vegetales, matices de aceituna y de tierra, y un toque de pimienta. Son esos aromas los que separan con claridad el Tequila de un ron o de un whisky, y el productor intentará conservarlos en las etapas siguientes.","Blue agave only, made only in certain Mexican states.":"Solo agave azul, solo en ciertos estados de México.","The core is used; the leaves are cut away.":"Se usa el corazón; las hojas se cortan.","Oven cooking softens the core and creates sugars; then it is crushed.":"La cocción en horno ablanda el corazón y crea azúcares; después se tritura.","Agave aromas: herbaceous, vegetal, olive, earthy, peppery.":"Aromas del agave: herbáceos, vegetales, aceituna, tierra, pimienta.","Tequila or Tequila 100% agave?":"¿Tequila o Tequila 100% agave?","The agave juice is mixed with water to make a sugary liquid ready for fermentation. At this point the producer has a choice: other sugars, not from agave, may be added too. The law sets a clear floor, though: at least 51% of the sugars fermented must come from blue agave. In other words, more than half must always be agave.":"El jugo de agave se mezcla con agua para obtener un líquido azucarado listo para fermentar. En este punto el productor puede elegir: también puede añadir otros azúcares que no proceden del agave. Eso sí, la ley fija un mínimo claro: al menos el 51% de los azúcares fermentados debe venir del agave azul. Es decir, más de la mitad siempre tiene que ser agave.","When a label says ‘100% agave’, it means only blue agave was used to make the sugary liquid, with no other sugars at all. The result tends to show a more pronounced agave character. Every other Tequila, the ones that use the option of adding other sugars, is simply labelled ‘Tequila’, with nothing more.":"Cuando la etiqueta dice «100% agave», significa que solo se usó agave azul para preparar el líquido azucarado, sin ningún otro azúcar. El resultado suele tener un carácter de agave más marcado. Todos los demás Tequilas, los que aprovechan la posibilidad de añadir otros azúcares, se llaman simplemente «Tequila», sin más.","Be careful not to mix this up with ageing: it is only about where the sugars came from. An unaged Tequila can be ‘100% agave’ or not, and the same is true of an oak-aged one. So, in front of a shelf, it pays to read two separate pieces of information: how much agave went in, and how long the spirit has rested.":"Ojo con no confundir esta distinción con el envejecimiento: solo se refiere al origen de los azúcares. Un Tequila sin envejecer puede ser «100% agave» o no, y lo mismo ocurre con uno que ha pasado por barrica. Así que, delante de una estantería, conviene leer dos datos por separado: cuánto agave lleva y cuánto tiempo ha reposado.","Agave juice is mixed with water before fermentation.":"El jugo de agave se mezcla con agua antes de fermentar.","At least 51% of the sugars must come from blue agave.":"Al menos el 51% de los azúcares debe venir del agave azul.","‘100% agave’ = no other sugars, more pronounced agave character.":"«100% agave» = ningún otro azúcar, carácter de agave más marcado.","Any style, aged or unaged, can be ‘Tequila’ or ‘100% agave’.":"Cualquier estilo, envejecido o no, puede ser «Tequila» o «100% agave».","Distilling to keep the agave":"Destilar para conservar el agave","After fermentation comes distillation. Tequila can be made in column stills, but the best ones take another route: they are distilled twice in pot stills and stopped at a notably low strength. Remember the general rule: the lower the distillation strength, the more of the raw material's aromas stay in the spirit.":"Después de la fermentación llega la destilación. El Tequila puede hacerse en columnas, pero los mejores siguen otro camino: se destilan dos veces en alambiques de cobre tradicionales y se detienen a una graduación notablemente baja. Recuerda la regla general: cuanto más baja es la graduación de destilación, más aromas de la materia prima conserva el destilado.","The result is a spirit with real personality, putting the herbaceous, peppery notes of blue agave front and centre, easy to spot from the first sip. It is the exact opposite of a neutral spirit such as vodka, which is pushed through a column to very high strength precisely to strip out almost all aroma.":"El resultado es un destilado con mucha personalidad, que pone en primer plano las notas herbáceas y picantes del agave azul, reconocibles desde el primer sorbo. Es justo lo contrario de un destilado neutro como el vodka, que se lleva en columna hasta graduaciones altísimas precisamente para eliminar casi todos los aromas.","A simple way to lock the idea in: pot still, double distillation and low strength mean ‘more agave in the glass’. If a question asks how the most expressive Tequilas are made, the answer lies here, not with tall columns and high strengths. Columns are still allowed, but they generally give Tequilas with less pronounced character.":"Una forma sencilla de fijar la idea: alambique tradicional, doble destilación y graduación baja significan «más agave en la copa». Si una pregunta plantea cómo se consiguen los Tequilas más expresivos, la respuesta está aquí, no en las columnas altas ni en las graduaciones elevadas. Las columnas siguen estando permitidas, pero suelen dar Tequilas con un carácter menos marcado.","Columns are allowed, but the best Tequilas are double distilled in pot stills.":"Se permiten columnas, pero los mejores Tequilas se destilan dos veces en alambique tradicional.","Low distillation strength = more agave aroma.":"Graduación de destilación baja = más aroma de agave.","Result: a characterful, herbaceous, peppery spirit.":"Resultado: destilado con carácter, herbáceo y picante.","Blanco, Joven, Reposado, Añejo":"Blanco, Joven, Reposado, Añejo","After distillation the producer decides whether to age the Tequila or leave it as it is. There are two unaged versions. Blanco, also called Silver, is colourless and prized for showing agave at its purest. Joven, also called Oro or Gold, has an attractive golden colour but has never seen a barrel: the colour comes from caramel, and other additives soften its texture.":"Tras la destilación, el productor decide si envejece el Tequila o lo deja tal cual. Hay dos versiones sin envejecer. El Blanco, también llamado Silver, es incoloro y se aprecia porque expresa el agave de la forma más pura. El Joven, también llamado Oro o Gold, tiene un bonito color dorado, pero no ha pasado por barrica: el color viene del caramelo, y otros aditivos suavizan su textura.","There are also two oak-aged versions. Reposado (‘rested’) spends between 2 and 12 months in oak: it comes out softer, but the wood rarely shows strongly and the agave aromas stay pronounced. Añejo (‘aged’) spends at least 12 months in barrel and combines agave aromas with oak notes such as vanilla and spice.":"Las versiones envejecidas en roble también son dos. El Reposado pasa entre 2 y 12 meses en madera: sale más suave, pero la madera rara vez se nota mucho y los aromas de agave siguen siendo intensos. El Añejo permanece al menos 12 meses en barrica y combina los aromas del agave con los del roble, como la vainilla y las especias.","Why do aged Tequilas spend fairly little time in barrel? Because the producer is looking for balance: some vanilla and spice, without burying the agave character that makes Tequila unique. Aged versions are then blended and may receive caramel to even out the colour, before being diluted with water and bottled.":"¿Por qué los Tequilas envejecidos pasan relativamente poco tiempo en barrica? Porque el productor busca equilibrio: algo de vainilla y especias, sin tapar el carácter del agave que hace único al Tequila. Después, las versiones envejecidas se mezclan y pueden recibir caramelo para igualar el color, antes de diluirse con agua y embotellarse.","Blanco/Silver: unaged, agave at its purest.":"Blanco/Silver: sin envejecer, agave en estado puro.","Joven/Oro/Gold: unaged, coloured with caramel.":"Joven/Oro/Gold: sin envejecer, coloreado con caramelo.","Reposado: 2–12 months in oak, softer, agave still in the lead.":"Reposado: de 2 a 12 meses en roble, más suave, el agave sigue mandando.","Añejo: at least 12 months in oak, agave plus oak.":"Añejo: al menos 12 meses en roble, agave más madera.","Three ways to flavour a spirit":"Tres formas de aromatizar un destilado","With flavoured spirits the starting point is different: the producer usually grows and ferments nothing, but buys in a ready-made spirit. In the vast majority of cases it is the same neutral spirit that becomes vodka once diluted with water. Now and then the base is a rum, whisky or brandy instead. The real work starts afterwards: adding flavours other than those from oak.":"En los destilados aromatizados el punto de partida es distinto: el productor normalmente no cultiva ni fermenta nada, sino que compra un destilado ya hecho. En la gran mayoría de los casos es el mismo destilado neutro que, diluido con agua, se convierte en vodka. A veces se parte de un ron, un whisky o un brandy. El trabajo de verdad empieza después: añadir sabores distintos de los de la madera.","The best products use natural ingredients such as fruits, seeds, herbs and spices, known as botanicals. The first method is redistillation: diluted neutral spirit and botanicals go into a pot still together and are distilled. What comes out is fragrant and colourless. The second is maceration: the botanicals steep in the spirit, like a cold herbal tea, giving up flavour and colour too.":"Los mejores productos usan ingredientes naturales como frutas, semillas, hierbas y especias, llamados botánicos. El primer método es la redestilación: el destilado neutro diluido y los botánicos se meten juntos en un alambique tradicional y se destilan. Sale un destilado aromático e incoloro. El segundo es la maceración: los botánicos reposan en el alcohol, como una infusión en frío, y le ceden sabor y también color.","Maceration can last a few days or several months: the longer it goes on, the more flavour is drawn out, and gentle heating speeds things up. The third method is the simplest: adding bought-in flavourings, natural or artificial, which are very concentrated and used in small amounts. It is usually chosen for cost reasons, instead of real botanicals.":"La maceración puede durar unos días o varios meses: cuanto más larga, más sabor se extrae, y un calentamiento suave acelera el proceso. El tercer método es el más sencillo: añadir aromas comprados ya hechos, naturales o artificiales, muy concentrados, en pequeñas cantidades. Normalmente se elige por motivos de coste, en lugar de usar botánicos de verdad.","Typical base: bought-in neutral spirit (sometimes rum, whisky or brandy).":"Base típica: destilado neutro comprado (a veces ron, whisky o brandy).","Botanicals = fruits, seeds, herbs and spices.":"Botánicos = frutas, semillas, hierbas y especias.","Redistillation: flavoured and colourless. Maceration: flavoured and coloured.":"Redestilación: aromatizado e incoloro. Maceración: aromatizado y coloreado.","Bought-in flavourings: concentrated, used in small doses, often to save cost.":"Aromas comprados: concentrados, en pequeñas dosis, a menudo para ahorrar costes.","Flavoured vodka and gin":"Vodka aromatizado y ginebra","Flavoured vodka is the most intuitive case: a neutral base given one clear flavour. The options are endless: vanilla, fruits such as apple or lemon, even spices like pepper. Most producers simply add bought-in flavourings to their neutral vodka, although some use redistillation. The result is easy to spot on the nose: one flavour, clean and direct.":"El vodka aromatizado es el caso más intuitivo: una base neutra a la que se da un sabor concreto. Las opciones son muchísimas: vainilla, frutas como la manzana o el limón, incluso especias como la pimienta. Casi siempre los productores añaden aromas comprados a su vodka neutro, aunque algunos recurren a la redestilación. El resultado se reconoce fácilmente en nariz: un solo aroma, limpio y directo.","Gin is a flavoured spirit with one essential rule: juniper must be the leading flavour, with its resinous, piney notes. Alongside juniper you often find coriander seed, angelica root, orris root and citrus peel. The base is usually neutral spirit, although other distilled spirits are allowed in the USA. A typical gin is colourless and unaged.":"La ginebra es un destilado aromatizado con una regla fundamental: el sabor dominante debe ser el del enebro, con sus notas resinosas de pino. Junto al enebro suelen aparecer semillas de cilantro, raíz de angélica, raíz de lirio y piel de cítricos. La base suele ser un destilado neutro, aunque en Estados Unidos se admiten otros destilados. La ginebra típica es incolora y no envejecida.","The best gins are usually redistilled with their botanicals, although some very delicate flavours are added afterwards. Other producers simply add bought-in flavourings. On a label, ‘London Dry Gin’ means the flavours were added during redistillation. Despite the name, it is not a place: a London Dry Gin can be made anywhere in the world.":"Las mejores ginebras suelen redestilarse con sus botánicos, aunque algunos aromas muy delicados se añaden después. Otros productores se limitan a añadir aromas comprados. En la etiqueta, la mención «London Dry Gin» indica que los aromas se aportaron durante la redestilación. Pese al nombre, no indica un lugar: un London Dry Gin puede elaborarse en cualquier parte del mundo.","Flavoured vodka: neutral base + usually bought-in flavourings (sometimes redistillation).":"Vodka aromatizado: base neutra + normalmente aromas comprados (a veces redestilación).","Gin: juniper must lead.":"Ginebra: el enebro debe dominar.","Other classic botanicals: coriander, angelica, orris, citrus peel.":"Otros botánicos clásicos: cilantro, angélica, lirio, piel de cítricos.","London Dry = flavours added by redistillation; can be made anywhere.":"London Dry = aromas aportados al redestilar; se puede elaborar en cualquier lugar.","Bitter spirits, cocktail bitters and spiced rum":"Amargos, bitters de cóctel y ron especiado","Bitter spirits contain at least one bitter botanical, such as gentian, quinine or bitter orange. A curious detail: bitterness only shows up in the mouth, because the nose cannot detect it. The aromas come from the bitter botanicals but also from many other ingredients. These spirits were traditionally drunk before or after a meal; today they end up mostly in cocktails.":"Los destilados amargos contienen al menos un botánico amargo, como la genciana, la quinina o la naranja amarga. Un detalle curioso: el amargor solo se percibe en boca, porque la nariz no lo detecta. Los aromas vienen de los botánicos amargos, pero también de muchos otros ingredientes. Tradicionalmente se tomaban al principio o al final de una comida; hoy acaban sobre todo en cócteles.","Cocktail bitters are something else: highly concentrated, intensely bitter spirits that nobody drinks on their own. They are used by the drop, a few dashes in a cocktail, to add complexity, rather like salt and pepper in cooking. A small bottle lasts a long time behind the bar precisely because so little is needed.":"Los bitters de cóctel son otra cosa: destilados muy concentrados e intensamente amargos que nadie toma solos. Se usan a gotas, unos golpes en un cóctel, para aportar complejidad, un poco como la sal y la pimienta en la cocina. Un frasquito dura mucho tras la barra precisamente porque hace falta muy poco.","Spiced rum, finally, is a very varied family, both in its base rum and in the flavourings added. Many start from a light, unaged rum that is flavoured and coloured with caramel; only a handful use an oak-aged rum. Both real botanicals and other flavourings are used. So be careful: an amber colour does not necessarily mean years in a barrel.":"El ron especiado, por último, es una familia muy variada, tanto por el ron de base como por los aromas añadidos. Muchos parten de un ron ligero y sin envejecer, que se aromatiza y se colorea con caramelo; solo unos pocos usan un ron envejecido en roble. Se emplean tanto botánicos de verdad como otros aromas. Así que cuidado: un color ámbar no significa necesariamente años de barrica.","Bitter spirits: at least one bitter botanical (gentian, quinine, bitter orange).":"Destilados amargos: al menos un botánico amargo (genciana, quinina, naranja amarga).","Bitterness is felt only on the palate, not the nose.":"El amargor solo se nota en boca, no en nariz.","Cocktail bitters: very concentrated, never drunk alone, used in dashes.":"Bitters de cóctel: muy concentrados, nunca se toman solos, se usan a gotas.","Spiced rum: often light unaged rum + flavourings + caramel.":"Ron especiado: a menudo ron ligero sin envejecer + aromas + caramelo.","Liqueurs: flavoured and sweet":"Licores: aromatizados y dulces","A liqueur is a flavoured spirit that has also been sweetened. That is the key difference from a gin or a flavoured vodka, which stay dry. Sugar goes in after the flavouring, and the law sets a minimum level of sweetness: without reaching it, a product cannot be called a liqueur.":"Un licor es un destilado aromatizado al que además se le ha añadido azúcar. Esa es la diferencia clave frente a una ginebra o un vodka aromatizado, que siguen siendo secos. El azúcar se añade después de aromatizar, y la ley exige un nivel mínimo de dulzor: si no lo alcanza, un producto no puede llamarse licor.","Most liqueurs are made from neutral spirit, but some start from more characterful spirits such as brandy, rum or whisky. Beyond that, freedom is almost complete: any flavour and any method of adding it. Think citrus or coffee, herbs or hazelnuts. Some liqueurs even contain a surprising ingredient: cream, which gives them a soft, velvety texture.":"La mayoría de los licores parten de un destilado neutro, pero algunos se basan en destilados con más carácter, como el brandy, el ron o el whisky. Por lo demás, la libertad es casi total: cualquier sabor y cualquier método para añadirlo. Pueden ir de los cítricos al café, de las hierbas a la avellana. Algunos licores llevan incluso un ingrediente sorprendente: la nata, que les da una textura suave y aterciopelada.","Many liqueurs are coloured as well. Natural colour from maceration is attractive but tends to fade quickly, so artificial colourings, which are more stable, are widely used. They also offer a much wider range of shades, which is why shelves show liqueurs in bright green, electric blue or vivid red.":"Muchos licores también llevan color. El color natural que da la maceración es bonito, pero tiende a apagarse pronto, por eso se usan mucho los colorantes artificiales, más estables. Además ofrecen una gama de tonos mucho más amplia: por eso en las estanterías se ven licores verde intenso, azul eléctrico o rojo vivo.","Liqueur = flavoured spirit + sugar.":"Licor = destilado aromatizado + azúcar.","The law requires a minimum sweetness.":"La ley exige un dulzor mínimo.","Neutral or characterful base; any flavour, even cream.":"Base neutra o con carácter; cualquier sabor, incluso nata.","Artificial colours: stable colour and brighter shades.":"Colorantes artificiales: color estable y tonos más vivos.","The four building blocks of an aromatised wine":"Los cuatro componentes de un vino aromatizado","Aromatised wines are not spirits, yet every bar has them because they are so useful in cocktails: a single ingredient brings sweetness, bitterness and acidity. The category is varied, but the basic recipe never changes. There are four components: a base wine, flavourings that always include something bitter, sugar and a little spirit. Caramel is sometimes added too.":"Los vinos aromatizados no son destilados, pero están en todas las barras porque en coctelería son muy valiosos: en un solo ingrediente aportan dulzor, amargor y acidez. La categoría es variada, y aun así la receta básica es siempre la misma. Hay cuatro componentes: un vino base, unos aromas que siempre incluyen algo amargo, azúcar y un poco de destilado. A veces también se añade caramelo.","The base wine is nearly always white, often fairly neutral, so it works as a blank canvas for the added flavours; some producers prefer aromatic wines and balance them with their recipe, and some use red or rosé wine. Flavourings go straight into the wine or are added as flavoured spirits. Recipes vary a lot, but all of them include bitter botanicals such as wormwood, gentian or quinine.":"El vino base es casi siempre blanco, a menudo bastante neutro, para que sirva de lienzo a los aromas añadidos; algunos productores prefieren vinos aromáticos y los equilibran con su receta, y otros usan vino tinto o rosado. Los aromas se añaden directamente al vino o en forma de destilados aromatizados. Las recetas varían mucho, pero todas incluyen botánicos amargos como el ajenjo, la genciana o la quinina.","The spirit, nearly always neutral, is added in a small amount to raise the alcohol and give the product a longer life, especially once the bottle is open. Almost no aromatised wine is fully dry: sweetness can come from the wine itself or from added sugar. Caramel is optional and used for colour; in red products made from white wine it can also add caramel notes.":"El destilado, casi siempre neutro, se añade en pequeña cantidad para subir la graduación y alargar la vida del producto, sobre todo una vez abierta la botella. Casi ningún vino aromatizado es completamente seco: el dulzor puede venir del propio vino o del azúcar añadido. El caramelo es opcional y sirve para dar color; en los productos rojos hechos con vino blanco también puede aportar notas de caramelo.","Four components: base wine, flavourings with something bitter, sugar, spirit.":"Cuatro componentes: vino base, aromas con algo amargo, azúcar, destilado.","Base wine usually white and fairly neutral.":"Vino base normalmente blanco y bastante neutro.","The spirit (usually neutral) raises alcohol and extends shelf life.":"El destilado (normalmente neutro) sube la graduación y alarga la conservación.","Almost never fully dry; caramel optional for colour.":"Casi nunca del todo secos; caramelo opcional para el color.","Vermouth":"El vermut","Aromatised wines can be made anywhere in the world, but two areas are especially famous: south-east France and north-west Italy. In both countries the most widely made type is vermouth. Two rules define it: it is made from a white wine base, and it must be flavoured with wormwood, a botanical with a strongly bitter taste.":"Los vinos aromatizados pueden elaborarse en cualquier parte del mundo, pero hay dos zonas especialmente famosas: el sureste de Francia y el noroeste de Italia. En ambos países el tipo más extendido es el vermut. Dos reglas lo definen: se elabora con un vino blanco y debe aromatizarse con ajenjo, un botánico de sabor claramente amargo.","Watch the labels: a vermouth marked ‘dry’ nearly always contains added sugar, just less of it. Red vermouths, on the other hand, are usually heavily sweetened. And their colour? Since the base is a white wine, the red shade usually comes from caramel, which can also add a light caramel aroma.":"Ojo con las etiquetas: un vermut «dry» (seco) casi siempre lleva azúcar añadido, aunque en menor cantidad. Los vermuts rojos, en cambio, suelen estar muy endulzados. ¿Y su color? Como la base es un vino blanco, el tono rojo suele venir del caramelo, que además puede aportar un ligero aroma a caramelo.","Behind the bar, vermouth is a real all-rounder. A dry vermouth can add dryness and perfume to a gin-based drink, while a red one, sweet with a bitter edge, rounds out a whiskey cocktail. Either way it does the same job: balancing sweetness, bitterness and acidity in one pour. That is why it pays to know its style and sweetness before reaching for the bottle.":"Detrás de la barra, el vermut es un auténtico comodín. Un vermut seco puede secar y perfumar una bebida a base de ginebra, mientras que uno rojo, dulce y amargo a la vez, redondea un cóctel a base de whiskey. En los dos casos hace el mismo trabajo: equilibrar dulzor, amargor y acidez de un solo gesto. Por eso conviene conocer bien su estilo y su dulzor antes de usarlo.","Best-known areas: south-east France and north-west Italy.":"Zonas más conocidas: sureste de Francia y noroeste de Italia.","Vermouth = white wine base + wormwood, by rule.":"Vermut = vino blanco de base + ajenjo obligatorio.","Even ‘dry’ nearly always has sugar; red is very sweet.":"Incluso el «dry» casi siempre lleva azúcar; el rojo es muy dulce.","Red vermouth usually gets its colour from caramel.":"El color del vermut rojo suele venir del caramelo.","Which plant is Tequila made from?":"¿De qué planta se obtiene el Tequila?","Potato":"Patata","By law, Tequila must be made from blue agave, a plant native to Mexico.":"Por ley, el Tequila debe elaborarse con agave azul, planta originaria de México.","Blue agave is the only plant allowed and gives Tequila its herbaceous, peppery aromas. Sugar cane is the raw material of rum, corn is the main grain in Bourbon, and potato is one of the classic raw materials for vodka.":"El agave azul es la única planta permitida y da al Tequila sus aromas herbáceos y picantes. La caña de azúcar es la materia prima del ron, el maíz es el cereal principal del Bourbon y la patata una de las materias primas clásicas del vodka.","Where can Tequila be made?":"¿Dónde puede elaborarse el Tequila?","Only in certain states of Mexico":"Solo en ciertos estados de México","In any state of Mexico":"En cualquier estado de México","Anywhere in Central America":"En toda Centroamérica","Wherever blue agave grows":"Donde crezca el agave azul","The law limits production to certain named Mexican states.":"La ley limita la producción a determinados estados mexicanos.","Being in Mexico is not enough: only certain states are allowed. Growing blue agave elsewhere does not earn the name Tequila, and Central America is outside the zone. This is a key difference from vodka, which can be made anywhere.":"No basta con estar en México: solo algunos estados están autorizados. Cultivar agave azul en otro lugar no da derecho al nombre Tequila, y Centroamérica queda fuera. Es una gran diferencia con el vodka, que puede elaborarse en cualquier parte.","Why are agave cores cooked in ovens?":"¿Por qué se cuecen en horno los corazones de agave?","To soften them and create sugars":"Para ablandarlos y crear azúcares","To give them a smoky aroma":"Para darles un aroma ahumado","To remove their colour":"Para eliminar su color","To kill the natural yeasts":"Para matar las levaduras naturales","Cooking softens the core and forms the sugars needed for fermentation.":"La cocción ablanda el corazón y forma los azúcares necesarios para fermentar.","Like grains, freshly harvested agave has no sugar ready to use: without cooking there would be nothing to ferment. Smoke is not the goal (that is more the peat in some Scotch whiskies), colour is irrelevant, and yeast is needed right afterwards for fermentation.":"Como los cereales, el agave recién cosechado no tiene azúcares listos: sin cocción no habría nada que fermentar. El humo no es el objetivo (eso recuerda más a la turba de algunos whiskies escoceses), el color no tiene nada que ver y las levaduras se necesitan justo después, para fermentar.","A Tequila label says ‘Silver’. What does that tell you?":"Una etiqueta de Tequila dice «Silver». ¿Qué indica?","It is an unaged Tequila, the same as Blanco":"Que es un Tequila sin envejecer, como el Blanco","It has been aged for 2 to 12 months":"Que ha envejecido entre 2 y 12 meses","It is made from 100% agave":"Que está hecho con un 100% de agave","It has been coloured with caramel":"Que se ha coloreado con caramelo","Silver is another name for Blanco: unaged Tequila.":"Silver es otro nombre del Blanco: Tequila sin envejecer.","Blanco and Silver name the same style, colourless with a pure agave profile. The 2–12 month period belongs to Reposado; ‘100% agave’ is a separate piece of information, and caramel is typical of Joven/Oro instead.":"Blanco y Silver designan el mismo estilo, incoloro y con un perfil de agave puro. El periodo de 2 a 12 meses corresponde al Reposado; «100% agave» es un dato aparte, y el caramelo es típico del Joven/Oro.","What minimum share of the sugars in any Tequila must come from blue agave?":"¿Qué proporción mínima de los azúcares de cualquier Tequila debe proceder del agave azul?","51%":"51%","25%":"25%","75%":"75%","100%":"100%","At least 51% of the fermented sugars must come from blue agave.":"Al menos el 51% de los azúcares fermentados debe proceder del agave azul.","The producer may add other sugars, but agave must stay in the majority. 100% is not compulsory: it is the condition for writing ‘100% agave’ on the label. The 25% and 75% figures match no rule.":"El productor puede añadir otros azúcares, pero el agave debe seguir siendo mayoritario. El 100% no es obligatorio: es la condición para poder poner «100% agave» en la etiqueta. Las cifras de 25% y 75% no corresponden a ninguna regla.","What does ‘100% agave’ on a Tequila label guarantee?":"¿Qué garantiza la mención «100% agave» en un Tequila?","No sugar other than blue agave was used":"Ningún azúcar distinto del agave azul","Distillation in pot stills only":"Destilación solo en alambique tradicional","A minimum period in oak":"Un envejecimiento mínimo en roble","No caramel or other additives":"La ausencia de caramelo y aditivos","It means only blue agave was used to make the sugary liquid.":"Significa que solo se usó agave azul para preparar el líquido azucarado.","The term is only about where the sugars came from. It says nothing about the type of still or about ageing: there are both unaged and aged ‘100% agave’ Tequilas. Nor does it promise no caramel, which may be used in aged versions.":"La mención solo se refiere al origen de los azúcares. No dice nada del tipo de alambique ni del envejecimiento: hay Tequilas «100% agave» tanto sin envejecer como envejecidos. Tampoco garantiza la ausencia de caramelo, que puede usarse en las versiones envejecidas.","A customer wants the purest possible expression of agave. Which Tequila would you suggest?":"Un cliente busca el Tequila con la expresión de agave más pura posible. ¿Cuál le propondrías?","A Blanco labelled 100% agave":"Un Blanco 100% agave","An Añejo labelled 100% agave":"Un Añejo 100% agave","A Joven/Oro":"Un Joven/Oro","A Reposado with no other label terms":"Un Reposado sin más menciones","Blanco sees no oak, and ‘100% agave’ rules out other sugars: agave has the stage to itself.":"El Blanco no pasa por madera y el «100% agave» excluye otros azúcares: el agave es el protagonista absoluto.","Two choices point the same way: no oak and only agave sugars. Añejo adds oak notes, Joven/Oro has caramel and additives that soften its texture, and a Reposado without ‘100% agave’ may contain other sugars on top of its time in oak.":"Dos elecciones van en la misma dirección: nada de madera y solo azúcares de agave. El Añejo añade notas de roble, el Joven/Oro lleva caramelo y aditivos que suavizan su textura, y un Reposado sin la mención «100% agave» puede contener otros azúcares además de su paso por madera.","How are the best Tequilas distilled?":"¿Cómo se destilan los mejores Tequilas?","Twice in pot stills, to a low strength":"Dos veces en alambique tradicional, a baja graduación","Once in a tall column, to 96% abv":"Una vez en columna alta, al 96% vol.","Three times in columns, to a high strength":"Tres veces en columna, a alta graduación","Once in a pot still, then charcoal filtered":"Una vez en alambique y luego filtrados con carbón","Double pot distillation to a low strength keeps the agave aromas.":"La doble destilación en alambique a baja graduación conserva los aromas del agave.","The lower the strength, the more aroma stays in the spirit. A tall column reaching 96% abv makes a neutral spirit, the opposite of what is wanted. Charcoal filtering is not part of the typical Tequila method; it belongs rather to Tennessee whiskey or some white rums.":"Cuanto más baja es la graduación, más aroma conserva el destilado. Una columna alta que llega al 96% vol. da un destilado neutro, justo lo contrario de lo que se busca. El filtrado con carbón no forma parte del método típico del Tequila: es más propio del whiskey de Tennessee o de algunos rones blancos.","Which aromas are typical of blue agave?":"¿Qué aromas son típicos del agave azul?","Herbaceous, earthy and peppery":"Herbáceos, terrosos y picantes","Cereal, honey and smoke":"Cereal, miel y humo","Vanilla, coconut and sweetcorn":"Vainilla, coco y maíz dulce","Blue agave brings herbaceous, vegetal, olive, earthy and peppery notes.":"El agave azul aporta notas herbáceas, vegetales, de aceituna, de tierra y de pimienta.","Every raw material leaves its signature. Cereal, honey and smoke point to a peated Scotch single malt, caramel and brown sugar to a molasses rum, and vanilla, coconut and sweetcorn to a Bourbon aged in new oak.":"Cada materia prima deja su firma. Cereal, miel y humo recuerdan a un single malt escocés con turba, caramelo y azúcar moreno a un ron de melaza, y vainilla, coco y maíz dulce a un Bourbon criado en roble nuevo.","How long is a Reposado Tequila aged in oak?":"¿Cuánto tiempo envejece en roble un Tequila Reposado?","Between 2 and 12 months":"Entre 2 y 12 meses","At least 12 months":"Al menos 12 meses","At least 2 years":"Al menos 2 años","It is not aged at all":"No envejece en absoluto","Reposado rests in oak for 2 to 12 months.":"El Reposado reposa en roble entre 2 y 12 meses.","At least 12 months is the Añejo rule; no ageing applies to Blanco and Joven. At least 2 years recalls the Cognac minimum (VS), not a Tequila rule.":"Al menos 12 meses es la regla del Añejo; sin envejecimiento son el Blanco y el Joven. Al menos 2 años recuerda al mínimo del Coñac (VS), no a una regla del Tequila.","Which Tequila style spends at least 12 months in oak?":"¿Qué estilo de Tequila pasa al menos 12 meses en roble?","Añejo":"Añejo","Reposado":"Reposado","Joven":"Joven","Blanco":"Blanco","Añejo is aged for at least 12 months and combines agave and oak.":"El Añejo envejece al menos 12 meses y combina agave y roble.","Reposado stops at between 2 and 12 months. Blanco and Joven are unaged: Joven may look mature because of its golden colour, but that colour comes from caramel, not from a barrel.":"El Reposado se queda entre 2 y 12 meses. El Blanco y el Joven no se envejecen: el Joven puede parecer maduro por su color dorado, pero ese color viene del caramelo, no de la barrica.","Where does the golden colour of a Joven (Oro) Tequila come from?":"¿De dónde viene el color dorado de un Tequila Joven (Oro)?","Added caramel":"Del caramelo añadido","A few months in oak":"De unos meses en roble","A golden variety of agave":"De una variedad de agave dorada","A longer cooking time":"De una cocción más larga","Joven is unaged: it is coloured with caramel and softened with other additives.":"El Joven no se envejece: se colorea con caramelo y se suaviza con otros aditivos.","It is a classic trap: the golden look suggests wood, but Joven never goes into a barrel. Tequila is made only from blue agave, not a ‘golden’ variety, and cooking creates sugars rather than colour; the spirit always leaves the still colourless.":"Es una trampa clásica: el aspecto dorado hace pensar en madera, pero el Joven no pasa por barrica. El Tequila se elabora solo con agave azul, no con una variedad «dorada», y la cocción sirve para crear azúcares, no para dar color a un destilado que siempre sale incoloro del alambique.","Which statement about Reposado Tequila is true?":"¿Qué afirmación sobre el Tequila Reposado es correcta?","It is softer, but agave stays in the lead":"Es más suave, pero el agave sigue mandando","Oak flavours dominate the agave":"El sabor de la madera domina sobre el agave","It is always made from 100% agave":"Siempre se elabora con 100% agave","It spends at least two years in barrel":"Pasa al menos dos años en barrica","Its short time in oak softens it without erasing the agave.":"Su breve paso por madera lo suaviza sin borrar el agave.","With 2–12 months in oak, the wood rarely takes over, so the agave stays pronounced; two years would be well beyond the limit. A Reposado can be ‘100% agave’ or plain ‘Tequila’, like any other style.":"Con 2 a 12 meses en roble, la madera rara vez se impone, así que el agave sigue intenso; dos años superarían con creces el límite. Un Reposado puede ser «100% agave» o simplemente «Tequila», como cualquier otro estilo.","Why are aged Tequilas rarely matured for very long?":"¿Por qué los Tequilas envejecidos rara vez pasan mucho tiempo en barrica?","To keep oak from masking the agave character":"Para que la madera no tape el carácter del agave","Because the law forbids more than a year in oak":"Porque la ley prohíbe más de un año en barrica","Because agave ruins the barrels":"Porque el agave estropea las barricas","Because the Mexican climate evaporates it all":"Porque el clima mexicano lo evapora todo","Producers want a balance between oak's vanilla and spice and the agave.":"El productor busca un equilibrio entre la vainilla y las especias del roble y el agave.","It is a style choice, not a ban: Añejo, for example, has a 12-month minimum and no maximum. The other two answers have no basis: the aim is for oak to support the agave, not dominate it.":"Es una elección de estilo, no una prohibición: el Añejo, por ejemplo, solo tiene un mínimo de 12 meses y ningún máximo. Las otras dos respuestas no tienen fundamento: el objetivo es que el roble acompañe al agave sin dominarlo.","Which statement about Tequila labels is true?":"¿Qué afirmación sobre las etiquetas de Tequila es correcta?","Any style can be ‘Tequila’ or ‘100% agave’":"Cualquier estilo puede ser «Tequila» o «100% agave»","Only Añejo can be ‘100% agave’":"Solo el Añejo puede ser «100% agave»","Blanco must always be ‘100% agave’":"El Blanco siempre debe ser «100% agave»","A ‘100% agave’ Tequila must be aged":"Un «100% agave» debe estar envejecido","Sugar source and ageing are two independent pieces of information.":"El origen de los azúcares y el envejecimiento son dos datos independientes.","Blanco, Joven, Reposado and Añejo can all be either ‘100% agave’ or plain ‘Tequila’. The other answers wrongly tie the sugar term to one style or to ageing, which the law does not do.":"Blanco, Joven, Reposado y Añejo pueden ser todos «100% agave» o simplemente «Tequila». Las otras respuestas vinculan por error la mención sobre los azúcares a un estilo o al envejecimiento, cosa que la ley no hace.","What is the correct order of the first steps in making Tequila?":"¿Cuál es el orden correcto de las primeras etapas de elaboración del Tequila?","Cut the leaves, cook, crush, ferment":"Cortar las hojas, cocer, triturar, fermentar","Crush, cook, cut the leaves, ferment":"Triturar, cocer, cortar las hojas, fermentar","Cut the leaves, ferment, cook, crush":"Cortar las hojas, fermentar, cocer, triturar","Cook, ferment, crush, cut the leaves":"Cocer, fermentar, triturar, cortar las hojas","The core is freed, cooked to create sugars, crushed to release juice, then fermented.":"Se separa el corazón, se cuece para crear azúcares, se tritura para sacar el jugo y luego se fermenta.","Logic helps: fermentation needs a sugary liquid, so the sugars must already exist (cooking) and be extracted (crushing). A raw core is too hard to crush usefully, and fermenting before cooking would leave no sugar to work on.":"La lógica ayuda: la fermentación necesita un líquido azucarado, así que los azúcares deben existir ya (cocción) y estar extraídos (trituración). Un corazón crudo es demasiado duro para triturarlo con provecho, y fermentar antes de cocer no dejaría azúcares que transformar.","What does a flavoured-spirit producer usually start from?":"¿De qué parte normalmente un productor de destilados aromatizados?","A bought-in neutral spirit":"De un destilado neutro comprado","Fruit harvested and fermented on site":"De fruta cosechada y fermentada en casa","An oak-aged brandy":"De un brandy envejecido en roble","A mash of malted grain":"De un mosto de cereales malteados","Most buy in the same neutral spirit that becomes vodka.":"La mayoría compra el mismo destilado neutro que se convierte en vodka.","These spirits do not need to start from a raw material: the work lies in the flavouring. Rum, whisky or brandy are only occasionally used as a base, and fermenting fruit or grain in-house is not the norm.":"Para estos destilados no hace falta partir de una materia prima: el trabajo está en la aromatización. El ron, el whisky o el brandy solo se usan de vez en cuando como base, y fermentar fruta o cereales por cuenta propia no es lo habitual.","What do you get by redistilling neutral spirit with botanicals?":"¿Qué se obtiene al redestilar un destilado neutro con botánicos?","A flavoured, colourless spirit":"Un destilado aromatizado e incoloro","A flavoured, coloured spirit":"Un destilado aromatizado y coloreado","A sweet, coloured spirit":"Un destilado dulce y coloreado","A spirit that is neutral again":"Un destilado de nuevo neutro","The vapour carries the botanicals' aromas but not their colour.":"El vapor arrastra los aromas de los botánicos, pero no su color.","Everything that leaves a still is colourless and dry, so there is no colour and no sweetness. Colour comes from maceration, sweetness from added sugar. The aromas do come through, though, so the result is far from neutral.":"Todo lo que sale de un alambique es incoloro y seco: ni color ni dulzor. El color llega con la maceración y el dulzor con el azúcar añadido. Los aromas, en cambio, sí pasan: por eso el resultado no es en absoluto neutro.","What is maceration?":"¿Qué es la maceración?","Steeping botanicals in the spirit":"Dejar los botánicos en infusión en el alcohol","Distilling the spirit with botanicals":"Destilar el alcohol junto con los botánicos","Adding concentrated essences":"Añadir esencias concentradas","Ageing the spirit in used barrels":"Envejecer el alcohol en barricas usadas","In maceration the botanicals soak and release flavour and colour.":"En la maceración los botánicos quedan sumergidos y ceden sabor y color.","Distilling with botanicals is redistillation, and adding essences is the third method, bought-in flavourings. Time in barrel is ageing: it gives oak aromas, not those of fruit, herbs and spices.":"Destilar con botánicos es la redestilación, y añadir esencias es el tercer método, el de los aromas comprados. El paso por barrica es envejecimiento: da aromas de madera, no de fruta, hierbas y especias.","A producer wants to extract more flavour, faster, during maceration. What can they do?":"Un productor quiere extraer más sabor, más rápido, durante la maceración. ¿Qué puede hacer?","Gently heat the spirit":"Calentar ligeramente el alcohol","Chill the spirit":"Enfriar el alcohol","Add caramel":"Añadir caramelo","Gentle heat speeds up flavour extraction.":"Un calor suave acelera la extracción del sabor.","As with tea, heat helps extraction and cold slows it. Caramel adds colour but no flavour, and charcoal filtering removes things (impurities or colour) rather than adding aroma.":"Como con el té, el calor ayuda a extraer y el frío frena. El caramelo da color pero no sabor, y el filtrado con carbón sirve para quitar algo (impurezas o color), no para añadir aromas.","Why do some producers use bought-in flavourings instead of botanicals?":"¿Por qué algunos productores usan aromas comprados en lugar de botánicos?","Mostly for reasons of cost":"Sobre todo por motivos de coste","Because the law requires it for gin":"Porque la ley lo exige para la ginebra","To give the spirit colour":"Para dar color al destilado","Because they raise the strength":"Porque aumentan la graduación","Concentrated bought-in flavourings are usually a cost-driven choice.":"Los aromas comprados, muy concentrados, suelen ser una elección económica.","The law does not make gin use them: in fact the best gins are redistilled with real botanicals. Flavourings are used in small doses for taste, not colour, and have nothing to do with strength.":"La ley no obliga a la ginebra a usarlos: al contrario, las mejores ginebras se redestilan con botánicos de verdad. Los aromas se usan en pequeñas dosis por el sabor, no por el color, y no tienen nada que ver con la graduación.","What are ‘botanicals’?":"¿Qué se entiende por «botánicos»?","Fruits, seeds, herbs and spices used for flavour":"Frutas, semillas, hierbas y especias para aromatizar","Highly concentrated artificial flavours":"Aromas artificiales muy concentrados","The yeasts that start fermentation":"Las levaduras que inician la fermentación","The plants used to make barrels":"Las plantas con las que se hacen las barricas","They are the natural ingredients that flavour flavoured spirits.":"Son los ingredientes naturales que dan sabor a los destilados aromatizados.","Artificial flavours are the alternative to botanicals, not the same thing. Yeast turns sugar into alcohol and barrel oak gives ageing aromas: neither fits the definition.":"Los aromas artificiales son precisamente la alternativa a los botánicos, no lo mismo. Las levaduras convierten el azúcar en alcohol y el roble de las barricas da aromas de envejecimiento: ninguno encaja en la definición.","Which flavour must lead in a gin?":"¿Qué sabor debe dominar en una ginebra?","Juniper":"Enebro","Coriander":"Cilantro","Lemon peel":"Piel de limón","Gentian":"Genciana","By definition, gin must have juniper as its main flavour.":"Por definición, la ginebra debe tener el enebro como sabor predominante.","Coriander and citrus peel are common gin botanicals, but they play supporting roles. Gentian is a classic bitter botanical, typical of bitter spirits and aromatised wines, not the heart of gin.":"El cilantro y la piel de cítricos son botánicos habituales en la ginebra, pero tienen un papel secundario. La genciana es un botánico amargo clásico, típico de los destilados amargos y los vinos aromatizados, no el corazón de la ginebra.","What does the term ‘London Dry Gin’ tell you?":"¿Qué indica la mención «London Dry Gin»?","The flavours were added by redistillation":"Que los aromas se aportaron por redestilación","The gin was made in London":"Que la ginebra se elaboró en Londres","The gin has been aged in oak":"Que la ginebra ha envejecido en roble","The gin contains no juniper":"Que la ginebra no contiene enebro","It is a method term: flavours added during redistillation.":"Es una indicación de método: aromas aportados durante la redestilación.","The name is misleading, but it is not a place: it can be made anywhere. Typical gin is unaged, and a gin without leading juniper would not be gin at all.":"El nombre engaña, pero no es un lugar: puede elaborarse en cualquier sitio. La ginebra típica no se envejece, y una ginebra sin enebro dominante no sería ginebra.","Which group lists typical gin botanicals besides juniper?":"¿Qué grupo enumera botánicos típicos de la ginebra además del enebro?","Coriander, angelica, orris, citrus peel":"Cilantro, angélica, lirio, piel de cítricos","Gentian, quinine, wormwood, bitter orange":"Genciana, quinina, ajenjo, naranja amarga","Mint, lime, cane sugar, cream":"Menta, lima, azúcar de caña, nata","Coriander seed, angelica root, orris root and citrus peel are classic gin botanicals.":"Semillas de cilantro, raíz de angélica, raíz de lirio y piel de cítricos son botánicos clásicos de la ginebra.","The second group is made of bitter botanicals, typical of bitter spirits and aromatised wines. Vanilla, cinnamon, cloves and coconut recall the aromas oak gives. The fourth group looks like cocktail ingredients or a cream liqueur.":"El segundo grupo reúne botánicos amargos, típicos de los amargos y los vinos aromatizados. Vainilla, canela, clavo y coco recuerdan a los aromas que da el roble. El cuarto grupo parece una lista de ingredientes de cóctel o de licor de nata.","What is a typical gin like?":"¿Cómo suele ser una ginebra?","Colourless and unaged":"Incolora y sin envejecer","Golden and oak-aged":"Dorada y envejecida en roble","Colourless and sweetened":"Incolora y azucarada","Amber and coloured with caramel":"Ámbar y coloreada con caramelo","Typical gin sees no oak and stays clear.":"La ginebra típica no pasa por madera y se mantiene transparente.","A golden or amber colour would suggest oak or caramel, neither of which belongs to typical gin. A colourless but sweetened gin would be closer to a liqueur: sweetness is not a feature of gin.":"Un color dorado o ámbar haría pensar en barrica o caramelo, que no forman parte de la ginebra típica. Una ginebra incolora pero azucarada se acercaría más a un licor: el dulzor no es un rasgo de la ginebra.","How are flavoured vodkas usually made?":"¿Cómo se elaboran normalmente los vodkas aromatizados?","Neutral vodka plus bought-in flavourings":"Vodka neutro más aromas comprados","Long maceration in oak barrels":"Maceración larga en barricas de roble","Distilling the fruit directly":"Destilación directa de la fruta","Adding sugar and caramel":"Añadiendo azúcar y caramelo","Most add bought-in flavourings to neutral vodka; some redistil.":"Casi siempre se añaden aromas comprados a un vodka neutro; algunos redestilan.","The base is the same neutral vodka, not a fruit spirit. Oak plays no part, and sugar plus caramel would lead to a coloured liqueur, not a flavoured vodka.":"La base es el mismo vodka neutro, no un destilado de fruta. El roble no interviene, y el azúcar y el caramelo llevarían a un licor coloreado, no a un vodka aromatizado.","What do all bitter spirits have in common?":"¿Qué tienen en común todos los destilados amargos?","At least one bitter botanical, such as gentian":"Al menos un botánico amargo, como la genciana","A minimum time in oak":"Un envejecimiento mínimo en roble","A dark rum base":"Una base de ron oscuro","A legal minimum sugar level":"Un nivel mínimo de azúcar por ley","Gentian, quinine or bitter orange provide the bitterness.":"La genciana, la quinina o la naranja amarga aportan el amargor.","No oak or rum base is needed. The legal minimum sweetness is the rule for liqueurs, not for bitter spirits.":"No hace falta paso por madera ni base de ron. El dulzor mínimo por ley es la regla de los licores, no de los destilados amargos.","When tasting a bitter spirit, where is the bitterness detected?":"En una cata, ¿dónde se percibe el amargor de un destilado amargo?","Only on the palate":"Solo en boca","Only on the nose":"Solo en nariz","On both nose and palate":"Tanto en nariz como en boca","Already from the colour":"Ya por el color","Bitterness is a taste: it is felt in the mouth, not smelled.":"El amargor es un sabor: se nota en boca, no con el olfato.","On the nose you pick up the aromas of the botanicals, bitter or not, but not the bitterness itself. Colour reveals nothing about taste: a bitter spirit can be coloured like any other.":"En nariz se captan los aromas de los botánicos, amargos o no, pero no el amargor en sí. El color no revela el sabor: un destilado amargo puede tener color como cualquier otro.","A bartender wants to add complexity to a drink with just a few drops. What do they reach for?":"Un bartender quiere añadir complejidad a un cóctel con solo unas gotas. ¿Qué usa?","Cocktail bitters":"Un bitter de cóctel","A cream liqueur":"Un licor de nata","A spiced rum":"Un ron especiado","A London Dry Gin":"Una ginebra London Dry","Cocktail bitters are so concentrated that a few dashes are enough.":"Los bitters de cóctel están tan concentrados que bastan unos golpes.","Cream liqueur, spiced rum and gin are used in normal measures and can be drunk on their own. Cocktail bitters are never drunk neat: they are there only to add depth to a drink.":"El licor de nata, el ron especiado y la ginebra se usan en cantidades normales y pueden tomarse solos. Los bitters de cóctel nunca se toman solos: solo sirven para dar profundidad a una bebida.","When were bitter spirits traditionally drunk?":"¿Cuándo se tomaban tradicionalmente los destilados amargos?","At the start or end of a meal":"Al principio o al final de una comida","Only with breakfast":"Solo en el desayuno","Only as a cooking ingredient":"Solo como ingrediente de cocina","Only diluted in hot water":"Solo diluidos en agua caliente","Traditionally they opened or closed a meal; today they are mostly used in cocktails.":"Tradicionalmente abrían o cerraban una comida; hoy se usan sobre todo en cócteles.","Their classic place was around a meal, as an aperitif or digestif. The other answers describe invented habits: today their main use is in mixing.":"Su lugar clásico era alrededor de la comida, como aperitivo o digestivo. Las otras respuestas describen costumbres inventadas: hoy su uso principal es en coctelería.","Which statement about spiced rum is true?":"¿Qué afirmación sobre el ron especiado es correcta?","It often starts from a light, unaged rum":"A menudo parte de un ron ligero sin envejecer","It must always start from an aged rum":"Siempre debe partir de un ron envejecido","It may only be flavoured with botanicals":"Solo puede aromatizarse con botánicos","Its colour always comes from oak":"Su color siempre viene del roble","Many spiced rums use a light unaged rum, flavoured and coloured with caramel.":"Muchos rones especiados usan un ron ligero sin envejecer, aromatizado y coloreado con caramelo.","Only a handful of spiced rums start from an oak-aged rum. Both botanicals and other flavourings are used, and the colour often comes from caramel: an amber look does not prove long ageing.":"Solo unos pocos rones especiados parten de un ron envejecido en roble. Se usan tanto botánicos como otros aromas, y el color suele venir del caramelo: un aspecto ámbar no demuestra un envejecimiento largo.","What sets a liqueur apart from a plain flavoured spirit?":"¿Qué distingue un licor de un simple destilado aromatizado?","It has also been sweetened":"También se ha endulzado","It has been aged in oak":"Ha envejecido en roble","It always contains cream":"Siempre contiene nata","It has a higher strength":"Tiene una graduación más alta","Liqueur = flavoured spirit plus sugar.":"Licor = destilado aromatizado más azúcar.","Ageing is not part of the definition. Cream appears only in some liqueurs, not all. And no rule demands a higher strength: what matters is the sweetness.":"El envejecimiento no forma parte de la definición. La nata solo aparece en algunos licores, no en todos. Y ninguna regla exige una graduación más alta: lo que cuenta es el dulzor.","What does the law say about sugar in liqueurs?":"¿Qué establece la ley sobre el azúcar en los licores?","There must be a minimum level of sweetness":"Que haya un nivel mínimo de dulzor","Sugar is not allowed":"Que el azúcar esté prohibido","Sugar is optional":"Que el azúcar sea opcional","Sugar may only come from fruit":"Que el azúcar solo proceda de la fruta","To be called a liqueur, a spirit must reach a minimum sweetness.":"Para llamarse licor, un destilado debe alcanzar un dulzor mínimo.","Sugar is not just allowed but required, so it cannot be banned or optional. It is added after flavouring and does not have to come from fruit.":"El azúcar no solo está permitido, es obligatorio, así que no puede estar prohibido ni ser opcional. Se añade después de aromatizar y no tiene por qué proceder de la fruta.","Which ingredient, unusual for a spirit, is found in some liqueurs?":"¿Qué ingrediente, poco habitual en un destilado, se encuentra en algunos licores?","Cream":"La nata","Yeast":"La levadura","Red wine":"El vino tinto","Sea water":"El agua de mar","Some liqueurs contain cream, a notable ingredient in this category.":"Algunos licores contienen nata, un ingrediente notable en esta categoría.","Yeast is for fermentation, before distillation, and is not added to a liqueur. Wine as a base belongs to aromatised wines, a different category. Sea water plays no part.":"La levadura sirve para fermentar, antes de destilar, y no se añade a un licor. El vino como base es propio de los vinos aromatizados, otra categoría. El agua de mar no tiene ningún papel.","Why do many liqueurs use artificial colourings?":"¿Por qué muchos licores usan colorantes artificiales?","Natural colour fades quickly":"El color natural se apaga pronto","They make the liqueur sweeter":"Hacen el licor más dulce","The law bans natural colours":"La ley prohíbe los colorantes naturales","They add fruity aromas":"Añaden aromas de fruta","Artificial colours keep the colour stable and offer more shades.":"Los colorantes artificiales mantienen el color estable y ofrecen más tonos.","Natural colour from maceration is allowed, but it loses its brightness: so more stable colourings are preferred, which also allow very vivid shades. Colourings add neither sweetness nor aroma; those come from sugar and flavouring.":"El color natural de la maceración está permitido, pero pierde viveza: por eso se prefieren colorantes más estables, que además permiten colores muy llamativos. Los colorantes no aportan dulzor ni aromas: eso viene del azúcar y de la aromatización.","What is an aromatised wine?":"¿Qué es un vino aromatizado?","A wine with flavourings, sugar and a little spirit":"Un vino con aromas, azúcar y un poco de destilado","A wine spirit aged in oak":"Un destilado de vino envejecido en roble","A liqueur based on neutral spirit":"Un licor a base de destilado neutro","A wine left to oxidise in barrel":"Un vino que se deja oxidar en barrica","It is wine-based, not a spirit, with flavourings, sugar and a little spirit added.":"Es un producto a base de vino, no un destilado, con aromas, azúcar y algo de destilado.","An aged wine spirit is a brandy, such as Cognac. A liqueur starts from a spirit, not a wine. Oxidation in barrel is not part of the definition: what counts is the flavourings, always including something bitter.":"Un destilado de vino envejecido es un brandy, como el Coñac. Un licor parte de un destilado, no de un vino. La oxidación en barrica no forma parte de la definición: lo que cuenta son los aromas, que siempre incluyen algo amargo.","Which list gives the four components of every aromatised wine?":"¿Qué lista recoge los cuatro componentes de todo vino aromatizado?","Wine, flavourings incl. a bitter, sugar, spirit":"Vino, aromas con un amargo, azúcar, destilado","Wine, flavourings, caramel, soda water":"Vino, aromas, caramelo, agua con gas","Spirit, sugar, cream, colourings":"Destilado, azúcar, nata, colorantes","Wine, fruit juice, sugar, yeast":"Vino, zumo de fruta, azúcar, levadura","Base wine, flavourings (always with something bitter), sugar and a little spirit.":"Vino base, aromas (siempre con algo amargo), azúcar y un poco de destilado.","Caramel is only optional and soda water does not belong. Spirit, cream and colourings describe a cream liqueur instead. Juice and yeast are not part of the recipe, and that list leaves out the spirit, which is required.":"El caramelo es solo opcional y el agua con gas no pinta nada. Destilado, nata y colorantes describen más bien un licor de nata. El zumo y la levadura no forman parte de la receta, y en esa lista falta el destilado, que es obligatorio.","Why is a little spirit added to an aromatised wine?":"¿Por qué se añade un poco de destilado a un vino aromatizado?","To raise the alcohol and make it keep longer":"Para subir la graduación y que se conserve más","To give it a darker colour":"Para darle un color más oscuro","To make it sweeter":"Para hacerlo más dulce","To add oak notes":"Para añadir notas de roble","The spirit raises alcohol and extends shelf life, even once opened.":"El destilado sube el alcohol y alarga la vida del producto, incluso abierto.","A neutral spirit is nearly always used, so it brings no colour or oak notes. Spirits are dry: sweetness comes from the wine or added sugar, and any colour from caramel.":"Casi siempre se usa un destilado neutro, así que no aporta color ni notas de madera. Un destilado es seco: el dulzor viene del vino o del azúcar añadido, y el color, en su caso, del caramelo.","Which type of spirit is nearly always used in aromatised wines?":"¿Qué tipo de destilado se usa casi siempre en los vinos aromatizados?","A neutral spirit":"Un destilado neutro","An aged brandy":"Un brandy envejecido","A peated whisky":"Un whisky con turba","A dark rum":"Un ron oscuro","Neutral spirit raises the strength without clashing with the chosen flavours.":"El destilado neutro sube la graduación sin estorbar a los aromas elegidos.","A characterful spirit would bring its own aromas, such as oak, peat or molasses, competing with the recipe. Here the spirit's role is technical, not aromatic.":"Un destilado con carácter aportaría aromas propios, como madera, turba o melaza, que competirían con la receta. Aquí el papel del destilado es técnico, no aromático.","Which group lists bitter botanicals used in aromatised wines?":"¿Qué grupo enumera botánicos amargos usados en los vinos aromatizados?","Wormwood, gentian, quinine":"Ajenjo, genciana, quinina","Juniper, coriander, angelica":"Enebro, cilantro, angélica","Vanilla, coconut, cinnamon":"Vainilla, coco, canela","Mint, lime, ginger":"Menta, lima, jengibre","Every recipe includes a bitter, such as wormwood, gentian or quinine.":"Toda receta incluye un amargo, como el ajenjo, la genciana o la quinina.","Juniper, coriander and angelica are gin classics, and they are not bitter. Vanilla, coconut and cinnamon recall oak aromas. Mint, lime and ginger suggest a long drink, not an aromatised wine recipe.":"Enebro, cilantro y angélica son clásicos de la ginebra y no son amargos. Vainilla, coco y canela recuerdan a los aromas del roble. Menta, lima y jengibre hacen pensar en un trago largo, no en la receta de un vino aromatizado.","Which botanical must vermouth be flavoured with?":"¿Con qué botánico debe aromatizarse un vermut?","Wormwood":"Ajenjo","Bitter orange":"Naranja amarga","Quinine":"Quinina","Wormwood is required in vermouth.":"El ajenjo es obligatorio en el vermut.","Juniper is gin's signature. Bitter orange and quinine are bitter botanicals that may appear in aromatised wines and bitter spirits, but the vermouth rule is specifically about wormwood.":"El enebro es la firma de la ginebra. La naranja amarga y la quinina son botánicos amargos que pueden aparecer en vinos aromatizados y destilados amargos, pero la regla del vermut se refiere concretamente al ajenjo.","A red vermouth is made from white wine. Where does its colour usually come from?":"Un vermut rojo se elabora con vino blanco. ¿De dónde suele venir su color?","Caramel":"Del caramelo","Black grape skins":"De los hollejos de uva tinta","Long ageing in oak":"De un largo envejecimiento en roble","Macerated juniper":"Del enebro macerado","With a white base, the red colour usually comes from caramel.":"Con una base blanca, el rojo suele venir del caramelo.","If the base is white, black grape skins play no part. Long oak ageing is not part of the recipe, and juniper is a gin botanical that does not turn things red. Caramel can also add a light caramel aroma.":"Si la base es blanca, los hollejos de uva tinta no intervienen. Un largo envejecimiento en roble no forma parte de la receta, y el enebro es un botánico de la ginebra que no tiñe de rojo. El caramelo también puede aportar un ligero aroma a caramelo.","A customer orders a ‘dry’ vermouth thinking it has no sugar. What is the correct reply?":"Un cliente pide un vermut «dry» pensando que no tiene azúcar. ¿Qué es correcto responderle?","It nearly always contains added sugar":"Que casi siempre lleva azúcar añadido","By law it contains no sugar at all":"Que por ley no lleva azúcar","It is sweeter than a red vermouth":"Que es más dulce que un vermut rojo","It is made without wine":"Que se elabora sin vino","Even ‘dry’ vermouths nearly always have some added sugar.":"Incluso los vermuts «dry» casi siempre llevan algo de azúcar añadido.","Almost no aromatised wine is fully dry, and no rule bans sugar in ‘dry’. It is red vermouth that is usually heavily sweetened. And every vermouth starts from a white wine.":"Casi ningún vino aromatizado es completamente seco, y ninguna regla prohíbe el azúcar en el «dry». Es el vermut rojo el que suele estar muy endulzado. Y todo vermut parte de un vino blanco.","Which areas are best known for aromatised wines?":"¿Cuáles son las zonas más conocidas por sus vinos aromatizados?","South-east France and north-west Italy":"El sureste de Francia y el noroeste de Italia","Northern France and southern Italy":"El norte de Francia y el sur de Italia","Scotland and Ireland":"Escocia e Irlanda","Mexico and the Caribbean":"México y el Caribe","They are made everywhere, but the famous areas are south-east France and north-west Italy.":"Se elaboran en todas partes, pero las zonas famosas son el sureste francés y el noroeste italiano.","The second answer flips the directions. Scotland and Ireland point to whisky, Mexico and the Caribbean to Tequila and rum: those are spirits, while this is about wine-based products.":"La segunda respuesta invierte las direcciones. Escocia e Irlanda remiten al whisky, México y el Caribe al Tequila y al ron: son destilados, mientras que aquí se habla de productos a base de vino.","Why are aromatised wines so useful in cocktails?":"¿Por qué los vinos aromatizados son tan útiles en coctelería?","They bring sweetness, bitterness and acidity at once":"Aportan a la vez dulzor, amargor y acidez","They are the strongest spirit in the drink":"Son la base alcohólica más fuerte de la bebida","They add colour without changing the taste":"Solo dan color sin cambiar el sabor","They replace ice for dilution":"Sustituyen al hielo en la dilución","One ingredient adds sweetness, bitterness and acidity to the drink.":"Un solo ingrediente añade dulzor, amargor y acidez al cóctel.","They are wines with a little spirit, so far weaker than the base spirit, which is usually 40% abv or more. They clearly change the taste, and dilution is still the job of ice and non-alcoholic ingredients.":"Son vinos con un poco de destilado, así que mucho menos fuertes que la base alcohólica, que suele tener un 40% vol. o más. Cambian claramente el sabor, y la dilución sigue siendo cosa del hielo y de los ingredientes sin alcohol.","Blue agave core":"Corazón de agave azul","Leaves cut off; cooked in ovens to create sugars, then crushed.":"Se cortan las hojas, se cuece en horno para crear azúcares y luego se tritura.","Tequila vs Tequila 100% agave":"Tequila vs Tequila 100% agave","At least 51% agave sugars, or agave sugars only.":"Al menos un 51% de azúcares de agave, o solo azúcares de agave.","Twice in pot stills to a low strength: lots of agave character.":"Dos veces en alambique tradicional, a baja graduación: mucho carácter de agave.","Blanco / Silver":"Blanco / Silver","Unaged and colourless: agave at its purest.":"Sin envejecer e incoloro: el agave en su forma más pura.","Joven / Oro / Gold":"Joven / Oro / Gold","Unaged; colour from caramel, texture softened by additives.":"Sin envejecer; color de caramelo, textura suavizada con aditivos.","Reposado vs Añejo":"Reposado vs Añejo","Reposado: 2–12 months in oak. Añejo: at least 12 months.":"Reposado: de 2 a 12 meses en roble. Añejo: al menos 12 meses.","Botanicals":"Botánicos","Natural flavouring ingredients: fruits, seeds, herbs and spices.":"Ingredientes naturales que aromatizan: frutas, semillas, hierbas y especias.","Neutral spirit and botanicals distilled together in a pot still: flavoured, colourless.":"Destilado neutro + botánicos destilados juntos en alambique: aromatizado e incoloro.","Botanicals steeped for days or months; give flavour and colour. Heat speeds it up.":"Botánicos en infusión días o meses; dan sabor y color. El calor acelera.","Gin":"Ginebra","Flavoured spirit led by juniper; usually colourless and unaged.":"Destilado aromatizado dominado por el enebro; normalmente incoloro y sin envejecer.","London Dry Gin":"London Dry Gin","Flavours added by redistillation. Can be made anywhere, not just London.":"Aromas aportados al redestilar. Puede elaborarse en cualquier lugar, no solo en Londres.","Bitter spirit":"Destilado amargo","At least one bitter botanical (gentian, quinine, bitter orange); bitterness felt only on the palate.":"Al menos un botánico amargo (genciana, quinina, naranja amarga); amargor solo en boca.","Very concentrated and very bitter; never drunk alone, a few drops add complexity.":"Muy concentrados y muy amargos; nunca solos, unas gotas aportan complejidad.","Flavoured, sweetened spirit with a legal minimum sweetness; often coloured.":"Destilado aromatizado y endulzado, con dulzor mínimo por ley; a menudo coloreado.","Aromatised wine":"Vino aromatizado","Base wine + flavourings with a bitter + sugar + a little spirit.":"Vino base + aromas con un amargo + azúcar + un poco de destilado.","Why add spirit?":"¿Por qué se añade destilado?","To raise alcohol and extend shelf life, even after opening.":"Para subir el alcohol y conservar más tiempo, incluso tras abrir.","White wine base flavoured with wormwood; France and Italy.":"Vino blanco de base aromatizado con ajenjo; Francia e Italia.","‘Dry’ vermouth":"Vermut «dry»","Nearly always has added sugar, just less than red.":"Casi siempre lleva azúcar añadido, solo menos que el rojo.","Red vermouth colour":"Color del vermut rojo","Usually from caramel, as the base is a white wine.":"Normalmente del caramelo, porque la base es un vino blanco.","Setting the scene and choosing the glass":"Preparar el lugar y la copa","Tasting a spirit means looking at it closely, and doing that well needs a method you repeat the same way every time. If every sample is treated identically, the notes you write today can be compared with the ones you write next month. Before pouring anything, though, it pays to prepare the setting: a good tasting depends as much on what surrounds the glass as on the liquid inside it.":"Catar un destilado es observarlo con atención, y para hacerlo bien hace falta un método que se repita siempre igual. Si cada muestra se trata de la misma manera, las notas de hoy se podrán comparar con las de dentro de un mes. Pero antes de servir nada conviene preparar el entorno: una buena cata depende tanto de lo que rodea la copa como del líquido que contiene.","The room should be free of distracting smells: no strong perfume, cooking or scented candles. You need good natural light and a white surface, such as a sheet of paper or a tablecloth, to hold the glass against so the colour can be judged without misleading reflections. The taster matters too: a clean palate with no lingering toothpaste or coffee, and a well-hydrated body.":"La sala debe estar libre de olores que distraigan: nada de perfumes fuertes, cocina ni velas aromáticas. Hace falta buena luz natural y una superficie blanca, como una hoja o un mantel, sobre la que mirar la copa para juzgar el color sin reflejos engañosos. Quien cata también cuenta: boca limpia, sin restos de pasta de dientes ni de café, y el cuerpo bien hidratado.","Then comes the glass. The ideal shape has a wide bowl that narrows towards the rim, a little like a tulip. The wide part gives the aromas room to rise, while the narrower opening gathers them and channels them straight to your nose. In a straight, open tumbler, by contrast, the scents drift away and the spirit seems less expressive than it really is.":"Después viene la copa. La forma ideal tiene un cuerpo ancho que se estrecha hacia el borde, un poco como un tulipán. La parte ancha deja espacio para que los aromas se liberen, y la boca más estrecha los concentra y los lleva directos a la nariz. En un vaso recto y abierto, en cambio, los aromas se dispersan y el destilado parece menos expresivo de lo que es.","A consistent method makes your notes comparable over time.":"Un método siempre igual hace que las notas sean comparables con el tiempo.","No stray smells, natural light and a white surface for colour.":"Sala sin olores, luz natural y superficie blanca para el color.","A clean palate (no toothpaste or coffee) and good hydration.":"Boca limpia (sin pasta de dientes ni café) y buena hidratación.","A wide bowl narrowing at the top concentrates the aromas.":"Copa ancha que se estrecha arriba: concentra los aromas.","The method step by step":"El método paso a paso","Even though the distiller has already diluted it before bottling, a spirit is still a very strong drink. At 40% abv the alcohol stings the nose and warms the mouth, hiding many details. That is why you work with a small sample of about 1.5 cL, roughly a tablespoon. It gives you everything you need without tiring your senses.":"Aunque el productor ya lo haya rebajado antes de embotellarlo, un destilado sigue siendo una bebida muy fuerte. A 40 % vol, el alcohol pica en la nariz y calienta la boca, tapando muchos matices. Por eso se trabaja con una muestra pequeña, de unos 1,5 cL, más o menos una cucharada. Es suficiente para todo lo que hace falta sin cansar los sentidos.","The route is simple. First you look at the sample and smell it neat. Then you add the same amount of water, another 1.5 cL, which halves its strength. You smell again: aromas the alcohol was hiding often appear, like opening a window in a crowded room. Only then do you move on to tasting.":"El recorrido es sencillo. Primero se mira la muestra y se huele tal cual. Luego se añade la misma cantidad de agua, otros 1,5 cL, con lo que su fuerza se reduce a la mitad. Se vuelve a oler: a menudo aparecen aromas que el alcohol escondía, como al abrir una ventana en una sala llena de gente. Solo entonces se pasa a probar.","In the mouth, you roll the liquid around for a few seconds, look for the flavours and then spit it out. Spitting is not rude: it lets you taste several samples while staying clear-headed and judge the last one as carefully as the first. In short: small sample, eyes and nose, equal water, nose again, palate, spit.":"En boca, se mueve el líquido unos segundos, se buscan los sabores y después se escupe. Escupir no es de mala educación: permite probar varias muestras con la cabeza despejada y juzgar la última con la misma atención que la primera. En resumen: muestra pequeña, vista y nariz, la misma cantidad de agua, otra vez nariz, boca y escupir.","Small sample: about 1.5 cL.":"Muestra pequeña: unos 1,5 cL.","Look and smell before adding any water.":"Se mira y se huele antes de añadir agua.","Add an equal amount of water, then smell again.":"Se añade la misma cantidad de agua y se vuelve a oler.","Taste, then spit.":"Se prueba y después se escupe.","What to write down":"Qué anotar","Your notes follow the order of the tasting: eyes, nose, palate. For appearance, colour is all you need. Many unaged spirits are colourless, while those that have spent time in wood range from lemon to gold, amber and brown. Some flavoured products, especially liqueurs, can be vivid: pink, red, green, blue, even black. Colour is a first clue, not proof.":"Las notas siguen el orden de la cata: vista, nariz y boca. Para el aspecto basta con el color. Muchos destilados sin envejecer son incoloros, mientras que los que han pasado por madera van del amarillo limón al dorado, al ámbar y al marrón. Algunos productos aromatizados, sobre todo los licores, pueden tener colores vivos: rosa, rojo, verde, azul e incluso negro. El color es una primera pista, no una prueba.","On the nose, you first judge intensity: a spirit can be neutral, with almost no smell like many vodkas, or light, medium or pronounced. Then you describe the aromas grouped by where they come from: the raw material, such as fruit or grain; the way it was made; and the oak and maturation, such as vanilla, spice or toasty notes. Asking 'where does this smell come from?' helps you sort your thoughts.":"En nariz se juzga primero la intensidad: un destilado puede ser neutro, casi sin olor como muchos vodkas, o bien ligero, medio o pronunciado. Después se describen los aromas agrupándolos por su origen: los de la materia prima, como fruta o cereal; los que vienen de la elaboración; y los de la madera y el envejecimiento, como vainilla, especias o tostados. Preguntarse «¿de dónde viene este olor?» ayuda a ordenar las ideas.","On the palate you find the same groups of flavours, plus two useful observations: how much sugar you can sense and what the texture is like, thin or richer. After spitting, you measure the finish, meaning how long the flavours linger: short, medium or long. Finally, you judge complexity, from neutral to simple, up to very complex when there are many flavours that keep changing.":"En boca se encuentran los mismos grupos de sabores, más dos observaciones útiles: cuánto azúcar se percibe y qué textura tiene el líquido, fluida o más rica. Tras escupir se mide el final, es decir, cuánto tiempo permanecen los sabores: corto, medio o largo. Por último se valora la complejidad, de neutro a simple, hasta muy complejo cuando hay muchos sabores que van cambiando.","Appearance: colour, from colourless to brown, or vivid shades in flavoured products.":"Aspecto: el color, de incoloro a marrón, o tonos vivos en productos aromatizados.","Nose: intensity (neutral, light, medium, pronounced) and aromas by source.":"Nariz: intensidad (neutra, ligera, media, pronunciada) y aromas por origen.","Aroma sources: raw material, processing, oak and maturation.":"Origen de los aromas: materia prima, elaboración, madera y envejecimiento.","Palate: flavours, sugar, texture; then finish (short, medium, long) and complexity.":"Boca: sabores, azúcar, textura; después final (corto, medio, largo) y complejidad.","Strong versus weak":"Fuerte frente a suave","Good ingredients and the right tools help, but what turns a decent cocktail into a memorable one is balance. Picture two sets of scales. The first weighs the strong part against the weak part; the second weighs sweet against bitter and sour. Together they give four points of balance, and every classic cocktail is built from exactly these four elements.":"Los buenos ingredientes y las herramientas adecuadas ayudan, pero lo que convierte un cóctel correcto en uno memorable es el equilibrio. Se puede imaginar como dos balanzas. La primera pone lo fuerte en un platillo y lo suave en el otro; la segunda enfrenta lo dulce con lo amargo y lo ácido. Juntas dan cuatro puntos de equilibrio, y todo cóctel clásico se construye con estos cuatro elementos.","The strong part is the base spirit, usually 40% abv or more. It is the heart of the flavour: rum in a Daiquiri, gin in a Martini. Change the spirit and you change the drink. Even switching to another product from the same category alters the result, and replacing the base entirely creates a variation, such as an Old Fashioned made with rum instead of whiskey.":"Lo fuerte es el destilado base, normalmente de 40 % vol o más. Es el corazón del sabor: el ron en un Daiquiri, la ginebra en un Martini. Si se cambia el destilado, cambia el cóctel. Incluso pasar a otro producto de la misma categoría modifica el resultado, y sustituir del todo la base crea una variante, como un Old Fashioned hecho con ron en lugar de whiskey.","The weak part softens the power of the alcohol. One source is always there: ice, which melts a little as you stir or shake and adds water. Others are optional and non-alcoholic: fruit juices, cream or milk, sodas, club soda and tonic. Think of a gin and tonic: the gin is the strong part, and the tonic and ice balance it.":"Lo suave suaviza la fuerza del alcohol. Hay una fuente que siempre está: el hielo, que se funde un poco al remover o agitar y añade agua. Otras son opcionales y sin alcohol: zumos de fruta, nata o leche, refrescos, soda y tónica. Piensa en un gin-tonic: la ginebra es lo fuerte, y la tónica y el hielo hacen de contrapeso.","Two scales: strong vs weak, and sweet vs bitter and/or sour.":"Dos balanzas: fuerte frente a suave, dulce frente a amargo y/o ácido.","Strong = the base spirit, usually 40% abv or more.":"Fuerte = destilado base, normalmente 40 % vol o más.","Weak = dilution from ice, plus juices, dairy, sodas or tonic.":"Suave = dilución del hielo, más zumos, lácteos, refrescos o tónica.","Swapping the base spirit creates a variation of the drink.":"Cambiar el destilado base crea una variante del cóctel.","Sweet versus bitter and sour":"Dulce frente a amargo y ácido","Many cocktails are first sweetened and then 'seasoned' with another ingredient, called a modifier, which brings a bitter note, a sour note or both. Sweetness can come in several forms: sugar, simple syrup (sugar dissolved in water) or a liqueur. Sweetness rounds things off and binds them together, but on its own it tires the palate: a cocktail that is too sweet tastes cloying and heavy.":"Muchos cócteles primero se endulzan y luego se «sazonan» con otro ingrediente, llamado modificador, que aporta una nota amarga, ácida o ambas. El dulzor puede llegar de varias formas: azúcar, jarabe simple, es decir, azúcar disuelto en agua, o un licor. El dulzor redondea y une, pero solo cansa: un cóctel demasiado dulce resulta empalagoso y pesado.","The counterweight is acidity or bitterness. Sourness comes mainly from citrus: a little lime or lemon juice makes the sip lively. Bitterness comes most obviously from cocktail bitters, used by the dash, but also from bitter spirits. It is just like cooking: a pinch of salt or a squeeze of lemon lifts a dish that seemed flat.":"El contrapeso es la acidez o el amargor. Lo ácido viene sobre todo de los cítricos: un poco de zumo de lima o de limón hace el trago más vivo. Lo amargo llega de forma clara con los bitters de cóctel, que se usan por gotas, y también con los destilados amargos. Es como en la cocina: una pizca de sal o un chorrito de limón despiertan un plato que parecía soso.","A single ingredient can play several roles. Aromatised wines such as vermouth bring sweetness, bitterness and acidity all at once; a liqueur brings both alcohol and sweetness. The goal is a cohesive whole in which no part dominates the others: if the drink tastes only of sugar, lemon or alcohol, it is not balanced yet.":"Un solo ingrediente puede cumplir varios papeles. Los vinos aromatizados, como el vermut, aportan a la vez dulzor, amargor y acidez; un licor aporta alcohol y dulzor. El objetivo es un conjunto coherente, en el que ninguna parte domine a las demás: si el cóctel solo sabe a azúcar, a limón o a alcohol, todavía no está equilibrado.","Sweetness comes from sugar, simple syrup or liqueurs.":"El dulzor viene del azúcar, el jarabe simple o los licores.","Too sweet = cloying.":"Demasiado dulce = empalagoso.","The modifier brings sour (citrus) and/or bitter (bitters).":"El modificador aporta ácido (cítricos) y/o amargo (bitters).","Aromatised wines can add sweet, bitter and sour at once.":"Los vinos aromatizados pueden aportar dulce, amargo y ácido a la vez.","Short drinks and long drinks":"Tragos cortos y tragos largos","Hundreds of cocktails can look like a maze, but one first split is enough to find your way: short drinks and long drinks. Short drinks have few ingredients and a small volume. Their weak part comes almost entirely from the water released by ice while stirring or shaking; they are then served in a small glass, concentrated and intense.":"Cientos de cócteles pueden parecer un laberinto, pero basta una primera división para orientarse: tragos cortos y tragos largos. Los cortos tienen pocos ingredientes y poco volumen. Su parte suave viene casi solo del agua que suelta el hielo al remover o agitar; después se sirven en un vaso pequeño, concentrados e intensos.","Short drinks include two families: spirit-forward cocktails, where the spirit leads, such as the Manhattan, and short sours, which combine spirit, citrus and sweetness, such as the Daiquiri. Long drinks have a larger volume: their weak part comes from sodas, juices, dairy or other non-alcoholic drinks. This is where highballs and long sours belong.":"Entre los tragos cortos hay dos familias: los cócteles «spirit-forward», donde manda el destilado, como el Manhattan, y los sours cortos, que combinan destilado, cítricos y dulzor, como el Daiquiri. Los tragos largos tienen más volumen: su parte suave llega de refrescos, zumos, lácteos u otras bebidas sin alcohol. Aquí están los highballs y los sours largos.","An example shows the link. A short gin sour, shaken and served in a small glass, becomes a long drink if you pour it over ice and top it with club soda. The core ingredients stay the same; what changes is the amount of the weak part, and with it the strength, the volume and the moment you might drink it.":"Un ejemplo ayuda a ver la relación. Un gin sour corto, agitado y servido en un vaso pequeño, se convierte en un trago largo si se sirve sobre hielo y se completa con soda. Los ingredientes básicos son los mismos; lo que cambia es la cantidad de la parte suave, y con ella la fuerza, el volumen y el momento en que se bebe.","Short drinks: few ingredients, diluted only by ice during mixing.":"Tragos cortos: pocos ingredientes, diluidos solo por el hielo al prepararlos.","Short families: spirit-forward and short sours.":"Familias cortas: spirit-forward y sours cortos.","Long drinks: bigger volume, lengthened with sodas, juices or dairy.":"Tragos largos: más volumen, alargados con refrescos, zumos o lácteos.","Long families: highballs and long sours.":"Familias largas: highballs y sours largos.","Spirit-forward cocktails":"Los cócteles spirit-forward","These are the strongest cocktails, the ones that put the spirit on show. In their simplest form they combine a spirit with sugar and bitters, or a spirit with a liqueur; in more elaborate versions, sweetness and bitterness come from mixes of sugar, aromatised wines and bitters. They are built in the glass or stirred, and the ice both chills and dilutes.":"Son los cócteles con más alcohol, los que ponen el destilado en primer plano. En su forma más sencilla combinan un destilado con azúcar y bitters, o un destilado con un licor; en las versiones más elaboradas, el dulce y el amargo llegan de mezclas de azúcar, vinos aromatizados y bitters. Se preparan directamente en el vaso o removiendo, y el hielo sirve tanto para enfriar como para diluir.","The Old Fashioned is the template: American whiskey, a sugar cube and Angostura bitters. The Manhattan uses rye or Bourbon with the same bitters, but swaps the sugar for sweet red vermouth, which makes it more complex. The Sazerac starts from Cognac or rye, with sugar, Peychaud's bitters and a touch of absinthe. The Rusty Nail is the simplest: Scotch whisky and Drambuie, a liqueur.":"El Old Fashioned es el modelo: whiskey americano, un terrón de azúcar y bitters Angostura. El Manhattan usa rye o Bourbon con los mismos bitters, pero cambia el azúcar por vermut rojo dulce, lo que lo hace más complejo. El Sazerac parte de Cognac o rye, con azúcar, bitters Peychaud's y un toque de absenta. El Rusty Nail es el más sencillo: Scotch whisky y Drambuie, un licor.","Gin gives two great classics. The Martini pairs gin with dry vermouth, which on its own provides both the sweet and the bitter note. The Negroni combines gin, sweet red vermouth and Campari, a red bitter spirit: three ingredients, three clear roles. Finally, adding cream to this kind of drink creates the Alexander family, such as the Brandy Alexander.":"Con la ginebra nacen dos grandes clásicos. El Martini combina ginebra y vermut seco, que aporta por sí solo la nota dulce y la amarga. El Negroni une ginebra, vermut rojo dulce y Campari, un destilado amargo rojo: tres ingredientes, tres papeles claros. Por último, al añadir nata a este tipo de bebida nace la familia de los Alexander, como el Brandy Alexander.","Spirit-forward: the strongest drinks, built or stirred.":"Spirit-forward: los más alcohólicos, preparados en el vaso o removidos.","Old Fashioned and Manhattan: whiskey and Angostura; the Manhattan adds sweet vermouth.":"Old Fashioned y Manhattan: whiskey y Angostura; el Manhattan añade vermut dulce.","Sazerac: Cognac or rye, Peychaud's and absinthe; Rusty Nail: Scotch and Drambuie.":"Sazerac: Cognac o rye, Peychaud's y absenta; Rusty Nail: Scotch y Drambuie.","Martini: gin and dry vermouth; Negroni: gin, sweet vermouth, Campari. With cream: Alexander.":"Martini: ginebra y vermut seco; Negroni: ginebra, vermut dulce, Campari. Con nata: Alexander.","Short sours":"Los sours cortos","The short sour rests on a trio: strong, sour, sweet. The basic recipe is a spirit, a citrus juice and an unflavoured sweetener such as simple syrup. These drinks are shaken: the shaker chills, mixes, dilutes a little and gives a light, airy, almost frothy texture. It is the family behind a huge number of successful cocktails.":"El sour corto se apoya en un trío: fuerte, ácido y dulce. La receta básica lleva un destilado, un zumo de cítricos y un endulzante neutro como el jarabe simple. Estas bebidas se agitan: la coctelera enfría, mezcla, diluye un poco y da una textura ligera y aireada, casi espumosa. Es la familia de la que nacen muchísimos cócteles de éxito.","Three classics show the pure pattern. The Daiquiri: rum, lime and simple syrup. The Whiskey Sour: Bourbon or rye, lemon and syrup, with optional egg white and bitters. The Pisco Sour: pisco, lime and syrup, plus one egg white and a dash of bitters. Here the egg white is essential: it creates a foam head and a silky texture. Many bars now use aquafaba, the water chickpeas are cooked in, as a vegan alternative.":"Tres clásicos muestran el esquema puro. El Daiquiri: ron, lima y jarabe simple. El Whiskey Sour: Bourbon o rye, limón y jarabe, con clara de huevo y bitters opcionales. El Pisco Sour: pisco, lima y jarabe, más una clara y unas gotas de bitters. Aquí la clara es imprescindible: crea una capa de espuma y una textura sedosa. Muchos bares usan hoy el aquafaba, el agua de cocción de los garbanzos, como alternativa vegana.","Variations change the sweetener, the sour ingredient or both. In the Sidecar, Cognac meets lemon and triple sec, an orange liqueur that replaces the syrup. The Margarita uses tequila, lime and triple sec, with an optional salt rim. The Clover Club brings together gin, lemon and raspberry syrup, with egg white and optionally a little vermouth: the same pattern, a completely different colour.":"Las variantes cambian el endulzante, el ácido o ambos. En el Sidecar, el Cognac se encuentra con limón y triple sec, un licor de naranja que sustituye al jarabe. La Margarita usa tequila, lima y triple sec, con el borde de sal opcional. El Clover Club une ginebra, limón y jarabe de frambuesa, con clara y, si se quiere, un poco de vermut: el mismo esquema, un color muy distinto.","Short sour = spirit + citrus + sweetener, shaken.":"Sour corto = destilado + cítrico + endulzante, agitado.","Daiquiri: rum and lime; Whiskey Sour: whiskey and lemon; Pisco Sour: pisco, lime and egg white.":"Daiquiri: ron y lima; Whiskey Sour: whiskey y limón; Pisco Sour: pisco, lima y clara.","Egg white: foam and a silky texture; vegan alternative: aquafaba.":"Clara: espuma y textura sedosa; alternativa vegana: aquafaba.","Variations: Sidecar (Cognac), Margarita (tequila), Clover Club (gin, raspberry).":"Variantes: Sidecar (Cognac), Margarita (tequila), Clover Club (ginebra, frambuesa).","Highballs":"Los highballs","The highball is the simplest of all mixed drinks: a spirit and a non-alcoholic mixer, served long over cubed ice. Gin and tonic, vodka and tonic, whisky and soda are examples almost everyone knows without realising they form a family. The rule is clear: little work, plenty of volume, and the weak part handed over to the mixer.":"El highball es la más sencilla de todas las mezclas: un destilado y una bebida sin alcohol, servidos en vaso alto con hielo en cubitos. Gin-tonic, vodka con tónica o whisky con soda son ejemplos que casi todo el mundo conoce sin saber que forman una familia. La regla es clara: poco trabajo, mucho volumen y la parte suave en manos del refresco o el zumo.","Some highballs have their own names. The Cuba Libre is rum and cola with lime. The Greyhound is vodka and grapefruit juice: the slightly bitter, sour juice acts as the modifier. These are summer-afternoon drinks, easy to make at home with ingredients found anywhere, yet built on the same logic of balance as more complex cocktails.":"Algunos highballs tienen nombre propio. El Cuba Libre es ron y cola con lima. El Greyhound es vodka y zumo de pomelo: el zumo, ligeramente amargo y ácido, hace de modificador. Son bebidas de tarde de verano, fáciles de preparar en casa con ingredientes que se encuentran en cualquier parte, pero construidas con la misma lógica de equilibrio que los cócteles más complejos.","Other highballs add a detail. The Horse's Neck combines Cognac, ginger ale and bitters: a highball with a bitter accent on top of spirit and mixer. The Americano has a split base: its alcoholic part is Campari and sweet red vermouth together, topped with club soda. Lighter than a Negroni, it is almost a lengthened version of it without the gin.":"Otros highballs añaden un detalle. El Horse's Neck combina Cognac, ginger ale y bitters: un highball con una nota amarga además del destilado y el refresco. El Americano, en cambio, tiene una base dividida: su parte alcohólica son Campari y vermut rojo dulce juntos, completados con soda. Menos alcohólico que un Negroni, es casi una versión alargada de este sin ginebra.","Highball: spirit + non-alcoholic mixer, served long over ice.":"Highball: destilado + bebida sin alcohol, en vaso alto con hielo.","Cuba Libre: rum, cola and lime. Greyhound: vodka and grapefruit juice.":"Cuba Libre: ron, cola y lima. Greyhound: vodka y zumo de pomelo.","Horse's Neck: Cognac, ginger ale and bitters.":"Horse's Neck: Cognac, ginger ale y bitters.","Americano: split base of Campari and sweet vermouth, plus club soda.":"Americano: base dividida de Campari y vermut dulce, más soda.","Long sours":"Los sours largos","The long sour covers several sub-families: Collinses, Slings and sparkling sours. In its simplest form it is a short sour made long with club soda. The Tom Collins is the perfect example: gin, lemon juice and simple syrup, poured over ice and topped with soda. It is refreshing and thirst-quenching, and shows clearly how one recipe can change its outfit.":"El sour largo reúne varias subfamilias: los Collins, los Sling y los sours espumosos. En su forma más simple es un sour corto alargado con soda. El Tom Collins es el ejemplo perfecto: ginebra, zumo de limón y jarabe simple, servidos sobre hielo y completados con soda. Es refrescante, quita la sed y muestra muy bien cómo una misma receta puede cambiar de aspecto.","Instead of club soda you can use a flavoured soda or Champagne. The Paloma combines tequila and lime with a Mexican-style grapefruit soda, which brings sweetness and bubbles at once; alternatively, grapefruit juice and soda water are used. The French 75 starts from Cognac or gin, lemon and simple syrup, and is topped with Champagne: an elegant sparkling sour.":"En lugar de soda se puede usar un refresco aromatizado o Champagne. La Paloma combina tequila y lima con un refresco de pomelo de estilo mexicano, que aporta a la vez dulzor y burbujas; como alternativa se usan zumo de pomelo y soda. El French 75 parte de Cognac o ginebra, limón y jarabe simple, y se completa con Champagne: un sour espumoso y elegante.","Some long sours are enriched with extra ingredients. The Mojito stays simple: rum, lime and sugar or syrup, with mint leaves that make it fresh and fragrant. The Singapore Sling is more complex: gin and lime, sweetened with a cherry liqueur and a herbal liqueur, with a dash of Angostura bitters and a final top of club soda.":"Algunos sours largos se enriquecen con ingredientes extra. El Mojito sigue siendo sencillo: ron, lima y azúcar o jarabe, con hojas de menta que lo hacen fresco y aromático. El Singapore Sling es más complejo: ginebra y lima, endulzadas con un licor de cereza y un licor de hierbas, con unas gotas de bitters Angostura y un toque final de soda.","Long sour = a lengthened short sour; sub-families: Collins, Sling, sparkling sour.":"Sour largo = sour corto alargado; subfamilias: Collins, Sling, sours espumosos.","Tom Collins: gin, lemon, syrup, club soda.":"Tom Collins: ginebra, limón, jarabe, soda.","Paloma: tequila, lime, grapefruit soda. French 75: Cognac or gin, lemon, syrup, Champagne.":"Paloma: tequila, lima, refresco de pomelo. French 75: Cognac o ginebra, limón, jarabe, Champagne.","Mojito: rum, lime, sugar and mint. Singapore Sling: gin, lime, liqueurs, bitters, soda.":"Mojito: ron, lima, azúcar y menta. Singapore Sling: ginebra, lima, licores, bitters, soda.","Why is water added to the sample when tasting a spirit?":"¿Por qué se añade agua a la muestra al catar un destilado?","Because at 40% abv it is hard to judge accurately":"Porque a 40 % vol es difícil juzgarlo con precisión","Because water changes the colour and makes it easier to read":"Porque el agua cambia el color y lo hace más fácil de leer","Because water adds sugar and softens the sip":"Porque el agua añade azúcar y suaviza el trago","Because the spirit has never been diluted before":"Porque el destilado nunca se ha rebajado antes","The strength of the alcohol hides many aromas; diluting reveals them.":"La fuerza del alcohol tapa muchos aromas; al diluir se perciben mejor.","A bottled spirit has already been diluted by the producer, but at around 40% abv it is still very strong: the alcohol stings the nose and masks the details. Adding water makes it easier to judge. Water adds no sugar and is not used to assess colour, which is looked at before diluting.":"Un destilado embotellado ya ha sido rebajado por el productor, pero a unos 40 % vol sigue siendo muy fuerte: el alcohol pica en la nariz y tapa los matices. Añadir agua lo hace más fácil de juzgar. El agua no aporta azúcar ni sirve para valorar el color, que se observa antes de diluir.","How much spirit is usually poured as a tasting sample?":"¿Cuánto destilado se sirve normalmente como muestra de cata?","About 1.5 cL":"Unos 1,5 cL","About 15 cL":"Unos 15 cL","About 5 cL":"Unos 5 cL","About 0.1 cL":"Unos 0,1 cL","A sample of about 1.5 cL is enough to look, smell and taste.":"Una muestra de unos 1,5 cL basta para mirar, oler y probar.","1.5 cL is roughly a tablespoon: enough for every step, small enough not to tire your senses. 5 cL is already a drinking measure and 15 cL a full glass, while 0.1 cL would be just a few drops, too little to work with.":"1,5 cL equivale más o menos a una cucharada: suficiente para todas las fases y poco para no cansar los sentidos. 5 cL ya es una dosis para beber y 15 cL un vaso entero, mientras que 0,1 cL serían solo unas gotas, demasiado poco para trabajar.","Which glass shape is best for tasting a spirit?":"¿Qué forma de copa es la más adecuada para catar un destilado?","A wide bowl that narrows towards the top":"Cuerpo ancho que se estrecha hacia arriba","A short, straight, wide-open tumbler":"Vaso bajo y recto, muy abierto","A flat, wide saucer like a sparkling-wine coupe":"Copa plana y ancha como la de espumoso","A tall, narrow glass with a flared rim":"Vaso alto y estrecho con el borde abierto","The wide bowl releases the aromas and the narrow top concentrates them.":"El cuerpo ancho libera los aromas y la boca estrecha los concentra.","A tulip-shaped glass is designed to gather the scents. In very open glasses, such as a flat coupe or a tumbler, the aromas escape at once. A flared rim has the same effect: it widens the opening instead of narrowing it.":"Una copa en forma de tulipán está pensada para reunir los aromas. En los recipientes muy abiertos, como la copa plana o el vaso bajo, los aromas se escapan enseguida. Un borde abierto produce el mismo efecto: ensancha la boca en lugar de estrecharla.","What is a white surface used for during a tasting?":"¿Para qué sirve una superficie blanca durante la cata?","To judge the colour of the spirit better":"Para valorar mejor el color del destilado","To work out how long the finish is":"Para saber cuánto dura el final","To reduce the smells in the room":"Para reducir los olores de la sala","To keep the sample at the right temperature":"Para mantener la muestra a la temperatura correcta","A white background lets you see the colour without distractions.":"Un fondo blanco permite ver el color sin distracciones.","Holding the glass against white paper or a white tablecloth, in good natural light, lets you read the colour reliably. The surface has no effect on smells, temperature or finish: those depend on the room, the sample and the palate.":"Si se coloca la copa delante de una hoja o un mantel blanco, con buena luz natural, el color se lee con fiabilidad. La superficie no influye en los olores, la temperatura ni el final: eso depende de la sala, de la muestra y de la boca.","Just before a tasting, which of these habits is best avoided?":"Justo antes de una cata, ¿qué costumbre conviene evitar?","Brushing your teeth or drinking coffee":"Lavarse los dientes o tomar un café","Drinking a glass of still water":"Beber un vaso de agua sin gas","Sitting near a bright window":"Sentarse junto a una ventana luminosa","Putting a white sheet on the table":"Poner una hoja blanca en la mesa","Toothpaste and coffee leave lingering flavours that distort the tasting.":"La pasta de dientes y el café dejan sabores persistentes que falsean la cata.","Your palate should be clean and neutral, with no lingering flavours. The other three habits actually help: water keeps you hydrated, while natural light and white paper help you see the colour properly.":"La boca debe estar limpia y neutra, sin sabores que perduren. Las otras tres costumbres, en cambio, ayudan: el agua mantiene la hidratación, y la luz natural y la hoja blanca sirven para observar bien el color.","What is the correct order of steps when tasting a spirit?":"¿Cuál es el orden correcto de las fases de cata de un destilado?","Eyes and nose, water, nose again, palate, spit":"Vista y nariz, agua, otra vez nariz, boca, escupir","Water, eyes and nose, palate, nose again, spit":"Agua, vista y nariz, boca, otra vez nariz, escupir","Palate, eyes and nose, water, palate again, spit":"Boca, vista y nariz, agua, otra vez boca, escupir","Eyes and nose, palate, spit, water, nose again":"Vista y nariz, boca, escupir, agua, otra vez nariz","Look and smell neat, dilute, smell again, then taste and spit.":"Se mira y se huele solo, se diluye, se vuelve a oler, luego se prueba y se escupe.","The first look and sniff are on the neat spirit, to get a starting impression. Water comes next, so you can compare the nose before and after dilution. Tasting comes last, on the diluted sample, which is easier to judge; tasting before the water or smelling after spitting breaks this logic.":"El primer examen se hace con el destilado solo, para tener una impresión inicial. Después llega el agua, para comparar la nariz antes y después de diluir. La boca va al final, con la muestra diluida, más fácil de juzgar; probar antes del agua u oler después de escupir rompe esta lógica.","After adding water and smelling again, new aromas appear. Why does this happen?":"Tras añadir agua y volver a oler, aparecen aromas nuevos. ¿Por qué ocurre?","The alcohol, now weaker, no longer masks some aromas":"El alcohol, ahora menos fuerte, ya no tapa algunos aromas","The water itself brings fruit and floral aromas":"El agua aporta por sí misma aromas de fruta y flores","The sample has warmed up and started to age":"La muestra se ha calentado y ha empezado a envejecer","The glass has released aromas from the previous sample":"La copa ha soltado los aromas de la muestra anterior","With less alcoholic strength, hidden aromas become noticeable.":"Con menos fuerza alcohólica, aromas antes ocultos se vuelven perceptibles.","Diluting with an equal amount of water halves the strength of the sample: the sting of the alcohol fades and lets hidden details come through. Water has no aroma of its own, and a few minutes in a glass do not age a spirit. A dirty glass would be a preparation mistake, not the normal effect of dilution.":"Diluir a partes iguales reduce a la mitad la fuerza de la muestra: el picor del alcohol se suaviza y deja salir matices que antes estaban tapados. El agua no tiene aroma propio, y unos minutos en la copa no envejecen un destilado. Una copa sucia sería un error de preparación, no el efecto normal de la dilución.","A vodka has almost no smell at all. Which nose intensity do you record?":"Un vodka casi no tiene olor. ¿Qué intensidad en nariz se anota?","Light":"Ligera","Short":"Corta","Simple":"Simple","'Neutral' is the lowest intensity level, for an almost absent nose.":"«Neutra» es el nivel más bajo de intensidad, para una nariz casi ausente.","Nose intensity runs from neutral to light, medium and pronounced. 'Light' means there is some aroma, however delicate. 'Short' describes the finish and 'simple' refers to complexity: real terms, but used in a different part of the note.":"La intensidad en nariz va de neutra a ligera, media y pronunciada. «Ligera» indica que hay algo de aroma, aunque sea delicado. «Corto» describe el final y «simple» se refiere a la complejidad: son términos reales, pero se usan en otra parte de la nota.","In an aged brandy you notice vanilla and sweet spice. Where do these aromas most likely come from?":"En un brandy envejecido se notan vainilla y especias dulces. ¿De dónde vienen probablemente estos aromas?","From the oak and maturation":"De la madera y el envejecimiento","From the grapes used as raw material":"De la uva usada como materia prima","From the water added in the glass":"Del agua añadida en la copa","Vanilla and spice are typical aromas given by oak during maturation.":"La vainilla y las especias son aromas típicos que aporta la madera durante el envejecimiento.","Aromas are grouped by source: raw material, processing, and oak and maturation. Grapes tend to give fruity notes, not vanilla. Water has no smell, and sugar, if present, shows up as sweetness on the palate rather than as a spicy aroma.":"Los aromas se agrupan por su origen: materia prima, elaboración, y madera y envejecimiento. La uva suele dar notas afrutadas, no vainilla. El agua no tiene olor y el azúcar, si lo hay, se nota como dulzor en boca más que como un aroma especiado.","In a tasting note, what does the 'finish' describe?":"En una nota de cata, ¿qué describe el «final»?","How long the flavours linger after spitting":"Cuánto tiempo permanecen los sabores tras escupir","The colour of the liquid at the bottom of the glass":"El color del líquido en el fondo de la copa","The last aroma noticed before adding water":"El último aroma percibido antes de añadir agua","The alcoholic strength shown on the label":"La graduación alcohólica indicada en la etiqueta","The finish measures how long flavours persist: short, medium or long.":"El final mide la persistencia de los sabores: corto, medio o largo.","The finish is the last observation on the palate: after spitting, you note how long the flavours last. A long finish is often a sign of quality. Colour belongs to appearance, aromas to the nose, and alcoholic strength is label information, not a tasting observation.":"El final es la última observación en boca: tras escupir, se mide cuánto duran los sabores. Un final largo suele ser señal de calidad. El color pertenece al aspecto, los aromas a la nariz, y la graduación es un dato de la etiqueta, no una observación de cata.","In a cocktail, what makes up the 'strong' element?":"En un cóctel, ¿qué constituye la parte «fuerte»?","The base spirit":"El destilado base","The citrus juice":"El zumo de cítricos","The sugar syrup":"El jarabe de azúcar","The ice used for chilling":"El hielo usado para enfriar","The base spirit is the strong element and the heart of the flavour.":"El destilado base es la parte fuerte y el corazón del sabor.","The strong element brings the alcohol and the main character of the drink. Citrus gives acidity, syrup gives sweetness and ice gives dilution, which belongs to the weak side: they are counterweights, not the base.":"La parte fuerte aporta el alcohol y el carácter principal de la bebida. Los cítricos dan acidez, el jarabe dulzor y el hielo dilución, que pertenece a la parte suave: son contrapesos, no la base.","What is the typical strength of a cocktail's base spirit?":"¿Cuál es la graduación típica del destilado base de un cóctel?","Usually 40% abv or higher":"Normalmente 40 % vol o más","Usually between 12 and 15% abv":"Normalmente entre 12 y 15 % vol","Usually around 20% abv":"Normalmente en torno al 20 % vol","Usually above 90% abv":"Normalmente más de 90 % vol","A cocktail's strong base is generally a spirit at 40% abv or more.":"La base fuerte de un cóctel suele ser un destilado de 40 % vol o más.","Strengths of 12–15% abv are typical of wine, and around 20% you find lighter products such as some aromatised wines. Above 90% abv you are looking at neutral spirit for production, not a spirit ready for mixing.":"Las graduaciones de 12–15 % vol son propias del vino, y en torno al 20 % hay productos más ligeros como algunos vinos aromatizados. Por encima del 90 % vol se trata de alcohol neutro para producción, no de un destilado listo para mezclar.","In a short drink stirred with ice and served with nothing added, where does the 'weak' element come from?":"En un trago corto removido con hielo y servido sin añadidos, ¿de dónde viene la parte «suave»?","From water as the ice melts during stirring":"Del agua del hielo que se funde al remover","From the bitters added by the dash":"De los bitters añadidos por gotas","From the base spirit":"Del destilado base","From the citrus peel used as a garnish":"De la piel de cítrico usada como decoración","Stirring with ice adds meltwater and softens the alcohol.":"Al remover con hielo, el deshielo añade agua y suaviza el alcohol.","In short drinks, dilution comes almost entirely from ice during mixing, by stirring or shaking. Bitters are a bitter accent, the spirit is the strong part and a citrus peel adds scent, but none of them really lengthens the drink.":"En los tragos cortos, la dilución viene casi solo del hielo durante la preparación, al remover o agitar. Los bitters son una nota amarga, el destilado es la parte fuerte y una piel de cítrico perfuma, pero ninguno alarga realmente la bebida.","What is the ingredient called that brings a bitter and/or sour note to balance sweetness?":"¿Cómo se llama el ingrediente que aporta una nota amarga y/o ácida para equilibrar el dulzor?","The modifier":"El modificador","The garnish":"La decoración","The sweetener":"El endulzante","The modifier 'seasons' the drink with bitterness and/or sourness.":"El modificador «sazona» el cóctel con amargor y/o acidez.","A cocktail is often sweetened first and then balanced by a modifier, such as citrus juice or bitters. A garnish is mainly decorative or aromatic, the base spirit is the strong part, and the sweetener is exactly what the modifier has to offset.":"A menudo un cóctel se endulza primero y luego se equilibra con un modificador, como zumo de cítricos o bitters. La decoración es sobre todo visual o aromática, el destilado base es la parte fuerte y el endulzante es justo lo que el modificador debe compensar.","What is simple syrup?":"¿Qué es un jarabe simple?","Sugar dissolved in water":"Azúcar disuelto en agua","Sweetened lemon juice":"Zumo de limón endulzado","An orange liqueur":"Un licor de naranja","Vermouth reduced over heat":"Vermut reducido al fuego","Simple syrup is just sugar and water, an unflavoured sweetener.":"El jarabe simple es solo azúcar y agua, un endulzante sin aroma.","Dissolving sugar in water makes it easy to mix into a cold cocktail. Lemon juice is a sour ingredient, orange liqueur is a flavoured, alcoholic sweetener and vermouth is an aromatised wine: none of them is 'simple'.":"Disolver el azúcar en agua permite mezclarlo fácilmente en un cóctel frío. El zumo de limón es un ingrediente ácido, el licor de naranja un endulzante aromatizado y con alcohol, y el vermut un vino aromatizado: ninguno es «simple».","A bartender tastes a cocktail and finds it cloying and too sweet. Which fix makes most sense?":"Un barman prueba un cóctel y lo encuentra empalagoso, demasiado dulce. ¿Qué corrección es la más adecuada?","Add a little citrus juice or a dash of bitters":"Añadir un poco de zumo de cítricos o unas gotas de bitters","Add a spoonful of simple syrup":"Añadir una cucharada de jarabe simple","Swap the spirit for a liqueur":"Sustituir el destilado por un licor","Serve it warmer, without ice":"Servirlo más caliente, sin hielo","Sourness or bitterness balances too much sweetness.":"La acidez o el amargor equilibran un exceso de dulzor.","On the sweet-versus-bitter-and-sour scale, you offset too much sugar by adding weight to the other side. More syrup or a liqueur would add even more sweetness. Removing the ice reduces dilution and does nothing about the sweetness.":"En la balanza dulce frente a amargo y ácido, para compensar el exceso de azúcar se refuerza el otro platillo. Más jarabe o un licor añadirían aún más dulzor. Quitar el hielo reduce la dilución y no resuelve el problema del dulzor.","Which ingredient can bring sweetness, bitterness and acidity to a cocktail on its own?":"¿Qué ingrediente puede aportar por sí solo dulzor, amargor y acidez a un cóctel?","An aromatised wine such as vermouth":"Un vino aromatizado como el vermut","Simple syrup":"El jarabe simple","Club soda":"La soda","A neutral spirit such as vodka":"Un destilado neutro como el vodka","Aromatised wines combine sweet, bitter and sour in one ingredient.":"Los vinos aromatizados reúnen dulce, amargo y ácido en un solo ingrediente.","Vermouth starts from wine, so it has acidity, it contains bitter botanicals and almost always some sugar: that is why it is so useful in cocktails. Syrup gives only sweetness, club soda only dilution and vodka mainly alcoholic strength.":"El vermut parte de un vino, así que tiene acidez, contiene botánicos amargos y casi siempre azúcar: por eso es tan útil en coctelería. El jarabe solo da dulzor, la soda solo dilución y el vodka sobre todo fuerza alcohólica.","Which two cocktail families are short drinks?":"¿Qué dos familias de cócteles son tragos cortos?","Spirit-forward and short sours":"Spirit-forward y sours cortos","Highballs and long sours":"Highballs y sours largos","Highballs and spirit-forward":"Highballs y spirit-forward","Short sours and long sours":"Sours cortos y sours largos","Spirit-forward drinks and short sours are the two short groups.":"Los spirit-forward y los sours cortos son los dos grupos de tragos cortos.","Short drinks have few ingredients and are diluted only by ice, as with a Manhattan or a Daiquiri. Highballs and long sours are long drinks, lengthened with sodas or juices. The mixed options pair a short group with a long one.":"Los tragos cortos tienen pocos ingredientes y solo se diluyen con hielo, como el Manhattan o el Daiquiri. Los highballs y los sours largos son tragos largos, alargados con refrescos o zumos. Las opciones mixtas combinan un grupo corto con uno largo.","In long drinks, where does most of the 'weak' element usually come from?":"En los tragos largos, ¿de dónde suele venir la mayor parte de lo «suave»?","From sodas, juices or dairy":"De refrescos, zumos o lácteos","From a second spirit added to the base":"De un segundo destilado añadido a la base","From a few dashes of bitters":"De unas gotas de bitters","From a sweet liqueur":"De un licor dulce","Non-alcoholic mixers such as sodas and juices lengthen the drink.":"Las bebidas sin alcohol como refrescos y zumos alargan la bebida.","What sets a long drink apart is its bigger volume, achieved with non-alcoholic ingredients: tonic, club soda, juice, milk or cream. A second spirit would raise the strength instead of lowering it, bitters are used by the dash and a liqueur mainly adds sugar and alcohol.":"Lo que distingue un trago largo es su mayor volumen, conseguido con ingredientes sin alcohol: tónica, soda, zumos, leche o nata. Un segundo destilado aumentaría la fuerza en lugar de reducirla, los bitters se usan por gotas y un licor aporta sobre todo azúcar y alcohol.","An Old Fashioned made with rum instead of whiskey is an example of what?":"Un Old Fashioned hecho con ron en lugar de whiskey, ¿de qué es un ejemplo?","A variation made by changing the strong element":"Una variante obtenida al cambiar la parte fuerte","A variation made by changing the modifier":"Una variante obtenida al cambiar el modificador","A way of turning it into a long drink":"Una forma de convertirlo en un trago largo","A way of making it a short sour":"Una forma de convertirlo en un sour corto","The base spirit, the strong element, is replaced.":"Se sustituye el destilado base, es decir, la parte fuerte.","Knowing the four points of balance lets you change a recipe in a targeted way. Swapping whiskey for rum leaves the sugar and bitters, the sweet part and the modifier, unchanged. The volume stays the same, so it does not become a long drink, and with no citrus it is not a sour.":"Conociendo los cuatro puntos de equilibrio, se puede modificar una receta de forma precisa. Cambiar el whiskey por ron deja igual el azúcar y los bitters, es decir, el dulce y el modificador. El volumen no cambia, así que no se convierte en un trago largo, y sin cítricos no es un sour.","What is the base spirit of a Negroni?":"¿Cuál es el destilado base del Negroni?","Vodka":"Vodka","Rum":"Ron","The Negroni is built on gin.":"El Negroni se construye sobre la ginebra.","The Negroni combines gin, sweet red vermouth and Campari in a spirit-forward drink. Vodka lacks gin's botanical character, rum is the base of the Daiquiri and Mojito, and Bourbon appears in drinks such as the Old Fashioned or Whiskey Sour.":"El Negroni une ginebra, vermut rojo dulce y Campari en un trago spirit-forward. El vodka no tiene el carácter botánico de la ginebra, el ron es la base del Daiquiri y del Mojito, y el Bourbon aparece en bebidas como el Old Fashioned o el Whiskey Sour.","In a Negroni, which ingredient mainly provides the bitter note?":"En el Negroni, ¿qué ingrediente aporta sobre todo la nota amarga?","Campari":"El Campari","Sweet red vermouth":"El vermut rojo dulce","A sugar cube":"El terrón de azúcar","Campari, a red bitter spirit, is the Negroni's bitter element.":"El Campari, un destilado amargo rojo, es el elemento amargo del Negroni.","Each Negroni ingredient has a role: gin is the strong part, sweet red vermouth brings sweetness and Campari the bitterness. The sugar cube belongs to the Old Fashioned, not the Negroni.":"Cada ingrediente del Negroni tiene un papel: la ginebra es la parte fuerte, el vermut rojo dulce aporta el dulzor y el Campari el amargor. El terrón de azúcar pertenece al Old Fashioned, no al Negroni.","The Old Fashioned and the Manhattan both use whiskey and Angostura bitters. What makes the Manhattan different?":"El Old Fashioned y el Manhattan usan whiskey y bitters Angostura. ¿Qué diferencia al Manhattan?","Sweet red vermouth instead of sugar":"Vermut rojo dulce en lugar de azúcar","Lemon juice instead of bitters":"Zumo de limón en lugar de bitters","Club soda that makes it a long drink":"La soda que lo convierte en trago largo","Cream that makes it smooth":"La nata que lo suaviza","In the Manhattan, sweetness comes from sweet red vermouth, which is more complex than sugar.":"En el Manhattan, el dulzor viene del vermut rojo dulce, más complejo que el azúcar.","Both drinks share the whiskey base and Angostura bitters; the Manhattan replaces the sugar cube with vermouth, which also brings bitter and sour nuances. It remains a short spirit-forward drink: no citrus, soda or cream, which belong to sours, long drinks and the Alexander family respectively.":"Ambos comparten la base de whiskey y los bitters Angostura; el Manhattan cambia el terrón de azúcar por vermut, que también aporta matices amargos y ácidos. Sigue siendo un trago corto spirit-forward: sin cítricos, soda ni nata, que corresponden a los sours, los tragos largos y los Alexander.","Which combination provides the bitter note in a Sazerac?":"¿Qué combinación aporta la nota amarga en un Sazerac?","Peychaud's bitters and absinthe":"Bitters Peychaud's y absenta","Angostura bitters and dry vermouth":"Bitters Angostura y vermut seco","Campari and sweet red vermouth":"Campari y vermut rojo dulce","Grapefruit juice and ginger ale":"Zumo de pomelo y ginger ale","The Sazerac stands out for Peychaud's bitters and a touch of absinthe.":"El Sazerac destaca por los bitters Peychaud's y un toque de absenta.","The Sazerac uses Cognac or rye, sugar and, as its bitter element, Peychaud's bitters with absinthe. Angostura and dry vermouth appear in other classics (Old Fashioned, Manhattan, Martini), Campari and sweet vermouth are the Negroni and Americano pair, and grapefruit and ginger ale are highball mixers.":"El Sazerac usa Cognac o rye, azúcar y, como elemento amargo, bitters Peychaud's con absenta. Angostura y vermut seco aparecen en otros clásicos (Old Fashioned, Manhattan, Martini), Campari y vermut dulce son la pareja del Negroni y el Americano, y el pomelo y el ginger ale son refrescos de highball.","A customer wants a simple drink of Scotch whisky sweetened with a liqueur. Which classic do you suggest?":"Un cliente quiere un trago sencillo de Scotch whisky endulzado con un licor. ¿Qué clásico se le propone?","Rusty Nail":"Rusty Nail","Sazerac":"Sazerac","Sidecar":"Sidecar","Horse's Neck":"Horse's Neck","The Rusty Nail is Scotch whisky with Drambuie, a liqueur.":"El Rusty Nail es Scotch whisky con Drambuie, un licor.","It is the simplest example of a spirit-forward drink made of spirit plus liqueur. The Sazerac uses Cognac or rye with sugar, bitters and absinthe; the Sidecar is a Cognac sour with lemon; the Horse's Neck is a Cognac highball with ginger ale.":"Es el ejemplo más sencillo de spirit-forward con destilado y licor. El Sazerac usa Cognac o rye con azúcar, bitters y absenta; el Sidecar es un sour de Cognac con limón; el Horse's Neck es un highball de Cognac con ginger ale.","What are the ingredients of a classic Martini?":"¿Cuáles son los ingredientes de un Martini clásico?","Gin and dry vermouth":"Ginebra y vermut seco","Gin and sweet red vermouth":"Ginebra y vermut rojo dulce","Vodka and lemon juice":"Vodka y zumo de limón","Gin, Campari and club soda":"Ginebra, Campari y soda","The Martini pairs gin with dry vermouth.":"El Martini combina ginebra y vermut seco.","In the Martini, dry vermouth does two jobs at once: it brings a hint of sweetness (even 'dry' vermouth has a little sugar) and a bitter note. Sweet vermouth goes into the Manhattan and Negroni; vodka and lemon suggest a sour, and Campari with soda points to the highball family.":"En el Martini, el vermut seco hace dos cosas a la vez: aporta un punto de dulzor (incluso el «seco» lleva algo de azúcar) y una nota amarga. El vermut dulce va en el Manhattan y el Negroni; vodka y limón recuerdan a un sour, y Campari con soda remite a los highballs.","What do you get by adding cream to a spirit-forward cocktail?":"¿Qué se obtiene al añadir nata a un cóctel spirit-forward?","The Alexander family, such as the Brandy Alexander":"La familia de los Alexander, como el Brandy Alexander","The Collins family, such as the Tom Collins":"La familia de los Collins, como el Tom Collins","The Sling family, such as the Singapore Sling":"La familia de los Sling, como el Singapore Sling","The sour family, such as the Pisco Sour":"La familia de los sours, como el Pisco Sour","Cream turns the drink into an Alexander.":"La nata convierte la bebida en un Alexander.","Alexanders are a twist on spirit-forward drinks in which cream makes everything rounder and velvety. Collinses and Slings are long sours topped with soda, and the Pisco Sour is a short sour whose smoothness comes from egg white, not cream.":"Los Alexander son una variación de los spirit-forward en la que la nata lo hace todo más redondo y aterciopelado. Collins y Sling son sours largos alargados con soda, y el Pisco Sour es un sour corto cuya suavidad viene de la clara, no de la nata.","How are spirit-forward cocktails usually prepared?":"¿Cómo se preparan normalmente los cócteles spirit-forward?","Built in the glass or stirred, with ice to chill and dilute":"Directamente en el vaso o removidos, con hielo para enfriar y diluir","Shaken with egg white to create a foam":"Agitados con clara para crear espuma","Topped with plenty of club soda in a tall glass":"Alargados con mucha soda en un vaso alto","Served warm, with no ice or dilution":"Servidos calientes, sin hielo ni dilución","They are built or stirred; the ice chills and dilutes.":"Se preparan en el vaso o se remueven; el hielo enfría y diluye.","Stirring keeps the drink clear and dense, ideal for showcasing the spirit. Shaking with egg white is typical of short sours, and soda in a tall glass of long drinks. Without ice you would lose the very weak element that makes such a strong drink pleasant to sip.":"Remover deja la bebida limpia y densa, ideal para destacar el destilado. La coctelera con clara es típica de los sours cortos, y la soda en vaso alto de los tragos largos. Sin hielo faltaría justo la parte suave que hace agradable una bebida tan alcohólica.","What are the three elements of a classic short sour?":"¿Cuáles son los tres elementos de un sour corto clásico?","Spirit, citrus juice, simple syrup":"Destilado, zumo de cítricos, jarabe simple","Spirit, vermouth, bitters":"Destilado, vermut, bitters","Spirit, cream, liqueur":"Destilado, nata, licor","Spirit, tonic, ice":"Destilado, tónica, hielo","The short sour balances strong, sour and sweet: spirit, citrus, syrup.":"El sour corto equilibra fuerte, ácido y dulce: destilado, cítrico, jarabe.","The basic formula uses an unflavoured sweetener such as simple syrup and a citrus fruit such as lime or lemon. Spirit, vermouth and bitters describe a spirit-forward drink; cream and liqueur lead to the Alexander family; tonic gives a highball.":"La fórmula básica usa un endulzante sin aroma, como el jarabe simple, y un cítrico como la lima o el limón. Destilado, vermut y bitters describen un spirit-forward; con nata y licor se va hacia los Alexander; con tónica se obtiene un highball.","Which recipe is a Daiquiri?":"¿Qué receta corresponde al Daiquiri?","Rum, lime, simple syrup":"Ron, lima, jarabe simple","Rum, cola, lime":"Ron, cola, lima","Tequila, lime, triple sec":"Tequila, lima, triple sec","Rum, lime, sugar, mint":"Ron, lima, azúcar, menta","The Daiquiri is the classic rum-based short sour.":"El Daiquiri es el sour corto clásico a base de ron.","The Daiquiri follows the pure sour pattern: rum, lime and syrup, shaken. Rum, cola and lime is the Cuba Libre, a highball; tequila, lime and triple sec is the Margarita; add mint and a long format and you reach the Mojito.":"El Daiquiri sigue el esquema puro del sour: ron, lima y jarabe, agitados. Ron, cola y lima es el Cuba Libre, un highball; tequila, lima y triple sec es la Margarita; con menta y formato largo se llega al Mojito.","In which cocktail is egg white considered essential?":"¿En qué cóctel se considera imprescindible la clara de huevo?","Pisco Sour":"Pisco Sour","Daiquiri":"Daiquiri","Margarita":"Margarita","The Pisco Sour always calls for an egg white.":"El Pisco Sour siempre lleva una clara.","In the Pisco Sour, egg white creates a foam head and a silky texture and is an integral part of the recipe. It is optional in the Whiskey Sour and included in the Clover Club, while the Daiquiri, Sidecar and Margarita are normally made without it.":"En el Pisco Sour, la clara crea una capa de espuma y una textura sedosa, y forma parte de la receta. En el Whiskey Sour es opcional y en el Clover Club está prevista, mientras que el Daiquiri, el Sidecar y la Margarita se hacen normalmente sin ella.","Which recipe is a Sidecar?":"¿Qué receta corresponde al Sidecar?","Cognac, lemon, triple sec":"Cognac, limón, triple sec","Cognac, ginger ale, bitters":"Cognac, ginger ale, bitters","Cognac, lemon, syrup, Champagne":"Cognac, limón, jarabe, Champagne","Cognac, sugar, Peychaud's, absinthe":"Cognac, azúcar, Peychaud's, absenta","The Sidecar is a Cognac sour sweetened with triple sec.":"El Sidecar es un sour de Cognac endulzado con triple sec.","The Sidecar is a sour variation in which triple sec, an orange liqueur, takes the place of syrup. Every option contains Cognac, but Cognac, ginger ale and bitters is the Horse's Neck; with Champagne it is the French 75; with Peychaud's and absinthe, the Sazerac.":"El Sidecar es una variante del sour en la que el triple sec, un licor de naranja, sustituye al jarabe. Todas las opciones llevan Cognac, pero Cognac, ginger ale y bitters es el Horse's Neck; con Champagne, el French 75; con Peychaud's y absenta, el Sazerac.","In a Margarita, which ingredient provides the sweetness?":"En la Margarita, ¿qué ingrediente aporta el dulzor?","Triple sec":"El triple sec","The salt rim":"La sal del borde","Lime juice":"El zumo de lima","Grapefruit soda":"El refresco de pomelo","Triple sec, an orange liqueur, is the Margarita's sweetener.":"El triple sec, licor de naranja, es el endulzante de la Margarita.","The Margarita is tequila, lime and triple sec: the lime is the sour part, not the sweet one. The salt rim is optional and lifts the flavours. Grapefruit soda belongs to the Paloma, another tequila drink, but a long one.":"La Margarita es tequila, lima y triple sec: la lima es la parte ácida, no la dulce. El borde de sal es opcional y realza los sabores. El refresco de pomelo pertenece a la Paloma, otro trago de tequila, pero largo.","Which short sour uses gin, lemon and raspberry syrup?":"¿Qué sour corto usa ginebra, limón y jarabe de frambuesa?","Clover Club":"Clover Club","Tom Collins":"Tom Collins","Singapore Sling":"Singapore Sling","French 75":"French 75","The Clover Club is the gin variation with raspberry syrup.":"El Clover Club es la variante de ginebra con jarabe de frambuesa.","The Clover Club is a short sour with a flavoured sweetener, plus egg white and optionally a little vermouth. The other three contain gin but are long sours: the Tom Collins with simple syrup and soda, the Singapore Sling with liqueurs and soda, and the French 75 with Champagne.":"El Clover Club es un sour corto con un endulzante aromatizado, más clara y, si se quiere, algo de vermut. Los otros tres llevan ginebra pero son sours largos: el Tom Collins con jarabe simple y soda, el Singapore Sling con licores y soda, y el French 75 con Champagne.","The Whiskey Sour and the Pisco Sour are both classic sours. How do their citrus juices differ?":"El Whiskey Sour y el Pisco Sour son sours clásicos. ¿En qué se diferencian los cítricos que usan?","The Whiskey Sour uses lemon, the Pisco Sour lime":"El Whiskey Sour usa limón y el Pisco Sour lima","The Whiskey Sour uses lime, the Pisco Sour lemon":"El Whiskey Sour usa lima y el Pisco Sour limón","Both use grapefruit juice":"Ambos usan zumo de pomelo","Both use orange juice":"Ambos usan zumo de naranja","Lemon for the Whiskey Sour, lime for the Pisco Sour.":"Limón para el Whiskey Sour, lima para el Pisco Sour.","Of the three classic sours, only the Whiskey Sour uses lemon; the Pisco Sour and Daiquiri use lime. A memory tip: whiskey, like the Cognac in a Sidecar, goes with lemon. Grapefruit appears in the Greyhound and the Paloma, not in these sours.":"De los tres sours clásicos, solo el Whiskey Sour usa limón; el Pisco Sour y el Daiquiri usan lima. Un truco para recordarlo: el whiskey, como el Cognac del Sidecar, va con limón. El pomelo aparece en el Greyhound y la Paloma, no en estos sours.","What is a Greyhound?":"¿Qué es un Greyhound?","Vodka and grapefruit juice":"Vodka y zumo de pomelo","Rum and cola with lime":"Ron y cola con lima","Gin and tonic water":"Ginebra y tónica","Tequila and grapefruit soda":"Tequila y refresco de pomelo","The Greyhound is a highball of vodka and grapefruit juice.":"El Greyhound es un highball de vodka y zumo de pomelo.","It is one of the highballs with its own name, as simple as the rest of the family. Rum, cola and lime is the Cuba Libre; gin and tonic has no special name; tequila and grapefruit soda with lime is the Paloma, which is a long sour.":"Es uno de los highballs con nombre propio, tan sencillo como los demás de la familia. Ron, cola y lima es el Cuba Libre; la ginebra con tónica no tiene nombre especial; tequila y refresco de pomelo con lima es la Paloma, que en realidad es un sour largo.","A customer asks for a Cognac highball with ginger ale and a few dashes of bitters. What do you make?":"Un cliente pide un highball de Cognac con ginger ale y unas gotas de bitters. ¿Qué se prepara?","A Horse's Neck":"Un Horse's Neck","A Sidecar":"Un Sidecar","A French 75":"Un French 75","An Americano":"Un Americano","The Horse's Neck is Cognac, ginger ale and bitters.":"El Horse's Neck es Cognac, ginger ale y bitters.","It is an example of a highball that adds bitters to the spirit and mixer. The Sidecar and French 75 contain Cognac but are sours, with lemon; the Americano is a highball with no Cognac, made with Campari, sweet vermouth and soda.":"Es un ejemplo de highball que añade bitters al destilado y al refresco. El Sidecar y el French 75 llevan Cognac pero son sours, con limón; el Americano es un highball sin Cognac, con Campari, vermut dulce y soda.","Why is the Americano said to have a 'split base'?":"¿Por qué se dice que el Americano tiene una «base dividida»?","Its alcoholic part is Campari and sweet vermouth together":"Su parte alcohólica son Campari y vermut dulce juntos","It is served half in a short glass and half in a tall one":"Se sirve la mitad en vaso corto y la mitad en vaso alto","It uses two different gins":"Usa dos ginebras distintas","It mixes lemon juice and lime juice":"Mezcla zumo de limón y zumo de lima","Campari and sweet red vermouth share the role of the strong element.":"Campari y vermut rojo dulce se reparten el papel de parte fuerte.","Instead of a single spirit, the Americano uses two alcoholic ingredients that together form the base, then lengthened with club soda. It contains no gin and no citrus: think of a Negroni without the gin, made long with soda.":"En lugar de un solo destilado, el Americano usa dos ingredientes alcohólicos que juntos forman la base, y luego se alarga con soda. No lleva ginebra ni cítricos: es como un Negroni sin ginebra alargado con soda.","How is a short sour turned into a Tom Collins?":"¿Cómo se convierte un sour corto en un Tom Collins?","By using gin and topping with club soda":"Usando ginebra y alargando con soda","By using rum and adding mint leaves":"Usando ron y añadiendo hojas de menta","By using Cognac and topping with Champagne":"Usando Cognac y completando con Champagne","By using tequila and grapefruit soda":"Usando tequila y refresco de pomelo","The Tom Collins is a gin sour lengthened with club soda.":"El Tom Collins es un sour de ginebra alargado con soda.","Gin, lemon and simple syrup make a sour; topped with soda over ice it becomes a Collins, the simplest long sour. Rum and mint lead to the Mojito, Cognac and Champagne to the French 75, and tequila with grapefruit soda to the Paloma.":"Ginebra, limón y jarabe simple forman un sour; al añadir soda sobre hielo se convierte en un Collins, el sour largo más sencillo. Ron y menta llevan al Mojito, Cognac y Champagne al French 75, y tequila con refresco de pomelo a la Paloma.","What is a French 75 topped with?":"¿Con qué se completa un French 75?","Champagne":"Champagne","Tonic water":"Tónica","Ginger ale":"Ginger ale","Cola":"Cola","The French 75 is a sparkling sour topped with Champagne.":"El French 75 es un sour espumoso completado con Champagne.","The base is Cognac or gin, lemon and simple syrup; Champagne replaces the soda and makes it a sparkling sour. Tonic is typical of highballs such as the gin and tonic, ginger ale of the Horse's Neck and cola of the Cuba Libre.":"La base es Cognac o ginebra, limón y jarabe simple; el Champagne sustituye a la soda y lo convierte en un sour espumoso. La tónica es típica de highballs como el gin-tonic, el ginger ale del Horse's Neck y la cola del Cuba Libre.","In a Paloma, what provides both sweetness and bubbles?":"En la Paloma, ¿qué aporta a la vez dulzor y burbujas?","A Mexican-style grapefruit soda":"Un refresco de pomelo de estilo mexicano","Grapefruit soda both sweetens and lengthens the Paloma.":"El refresco de pomelo endulza y alarga la Paloma.","The Paloma is tequila and lime topped with grapefruit soda; alternatively, grapefruit juice and soda water can be used. Triple sec sweetens the Margarita, Champagne tops the French 75 and ginger ale goes into the Horse's Neck.":"La Paloma es tequila y lima completados con refresco de pomelo; como alternativa se pueden usar zumo de pomelo y soda. El triple sec endulza la Margarita, el Champagne completa el French 75 y el ginger ale va en el Horse's Neck.","Which extra ingredient sets the Mojito apart from a plain rum sour?":"¿Qué ingrediente extra distingue al Mojito de un simple sour de ron?","Mint leaves":"Las hojas de menta","Egg white":"La clara de huevo","A salt rim":"El borde de sal","Mint, with the lime, makes the Mojito fresh and fragrant.":"La menta, con la lima, hace que el Mojito sea fresco y aromático.","The Mojito is rum, lime and sugar or syrup, enriched with mint: a long sour with one simple extra ingredient. Egg white is typical of the Pisco Sour, salt of the Margarita and cream of the Alexander family.":"El Mojito es ron, lima y azúcar o jarabe, enriquecido con menta: un sour largo con un ingrediente extra sencillo. La clara es típica del Pisco Sour, la sal de la Margarita y la nata de los Alexander.","Sample size for tasting a spirit":"Muestra para catar un destilado","About 1.5 cL, roughly a tablespoon.":"Unos 1,5 cL, más o menos una cucharada.","How much water to add?":"¿Cuánta agua añadir?","The same amount as the sample, after the first look and sniff.":"La misma cantidad que la muestra, tras el primer examen de vista y nariz.","Ideal tasting glass":"Copa de cata ideal","Wide bowl narrowing at the top, to concentrate the aromas.":"Cuerpo ancho que se estrecha arriba, para concentrar los aromas.","Nose intensity levels":"Niveles de intensidad en nariz","Neutral, light, medium, pronounced.":"Neutra, ligera, media, pronunciada.","Two palate observations besides flavours":"Dos observaciones en boca además de los sabores","Sugar level and the texture of the liquid.":"Nivel de azúcar y textura del líquido.","The four points of balance":"Los cuatro puntos de equilibrio","Strong, weak, sweet, bitter and/or sour.":"Fuerte, suave, dulce, amargo y/o ácido.","Sugar dissolved in water: an unflavoured sweetener.":"Azúcar disuelto en agua: un endulzante sin aroma.","Modifier":"Modificador","Ingredient that balances sweetness with bitter and/or sour, like citrus or bitters.":"Ingrediente que equilibra el dulzor con amargo y/o ácido, como cítricos o bitters.","Short drink":"Trago corto","Few ingredients, diluted by ice when stirred or shaken.":"Pocos ingredientes, diluido por el hielo al remover o agitar.","Long drink":"Trago largo","Bigger volume, lengthened with sodas, juices or dairy.":"Más volumen, alargado con refrescos, zumos o lácteos.","Old Fashioned":"Old Fashioned","Whiskey (usually Bourbon), sugar cube, Angostura bitters.":"Whiskey (normalmente Bourbon), terrón de azúcar, bitters Angostura.","Manhattan":"Manhattan","Rye or Bourbon, sweet red vermouth, Angostura bitters.":"Rye o Bourbon, vermut rojo dulce, bitters Angostura.","Brandy Alexander":"Brandy Alexander","Example of the Alexander family: a spirit-forward drink with cream added.":"Ejemplo de la familia Alexander: un spirit-forward enriquecido con nata.","Whiskey Sour":"Whiskey Sour","Bourbon or rye, lemon, simple syrup; optional egg white and bitters.":"Bourbon o rye, limón, jarabe simple; clara y bitters opcionales.","Aquafaba":"Aquafaba","Chickpea cooking water: a vegan alternative to egg white for foam.":"Agua de cocción de garbanzos: alternativa vegana a la clara para la espuma.","Highball":"Highball","The simplest mixed drink: spirit and mixer, served long over cubed ice.":"La mezcla más sencilla: destilado y refresco, en vaso alto con cubitos.","Cuba Libre":"Cuba Libre","Highball of rum and cola with lime.":"Highball de ron y cola con lima.","Cognac or gin, lemon, simple syrup, topped with Champagne.":"Cognac o ginebra, limón, jarabe simple, completado con Champagne.","Gin, lime, cherry and herbal liqueurs, Angostura bitters, club soda.":"Ginebra, lima, licor de cereza y de hierbas, bitters Angostura, soda.","Long sour sub-families":"Subfamilias del sour largo","Collins, Sling and sparkling sour.":"Collins, Sling y sours espumosos.","Four steps and two stills":"Los cuatro pasos y los alambiques","Flavour, sweetness and colour":"Sabor, dulzor y color","Cognac":"Coñac","Scotch whisky":"Whisky escocés","American and other whiskies":"Whiskey americano y otros whiskies","Caribbean rum":"Ron del Caribe","Tequila":"Tequila","Flavoured spirits and liqueurs":"Destilados aromatizados y licores","Aromatised wines":"Vinos aromatizados","Tasting a spirit":"Catar un destilado","A balanced cocktail":"El cóctel equilibrado","Cocktail families":"Familias de cócteles","How a spirit is made":"Cómo se hace un destilado","The main spirit families":"Las grandes familias de destilados","Taste and mix":"Catar y mezclar"});Object.assign(window.TWG_ESX.ar,{"The strength reached during distillation matters a lot. A newly made spirit can range from about 60% up to 96% abv. The lower the strength, the more intense the aromas; the higher the strength, the less aroma survives. At 96% abv a spirit has so little smell that it is called neutral. Picture a radio: the louder the alcohol, the fainter the music of the aromas.":"El grado al que se destila importa mucho. Un destilado recién hecho puede ir de un 60% a un 96% vol. aproximadamente. Cuanto más bajo es el grado, más intensos son los aromas; cuanto más alto, menos aroma queda. A 96% el destilado tiene tan poco olor que se le llama neutro. Imaginá una radio: cuanto más sube el volumen del alcohol, menos se oye la música de los aromas.","The higher the vapour climbs in the column, the higher its alcohol level: the bottom section holds the weakest liquid, the top section the strongest, and that is where the spirit leaves the still. Because the distillations happen simultaneously and the column never needs emptying, production is continuous and fast. Think of an escalator that never stops, compared with the stop-start lift of the pot still.":"Cuanto más sube el vapor por la columna, más alto es su grado: la sección de abajo tiene el líquido menos alcohólico, la de arriba el más alcohólico, y de ahí sale el destilado. Como las destilaciones ocurren a la vez y no hay que vaciar la columna, el trabajo es continuo y rápido. Pensá en una escalera mecánica que nunca se detiene, frente al ascensor de viajes sueltos del alambique discontinuo.","An unaged spirit rests briefly in stainless steel, a material that gives nothing away: it stays clear and keeps the aromas born in the still. Oak, on the other hand, does real work. A barrel adds colour in a sequence that goes from lemon to gold, then amber and, very rarely, brown. The newer the barrel and the longer the spirit stays in it, the deeper the colour.":"Un destilado sin envejecer reposa poco tiempo en acero inoxidable, un material que no cede nada: seguí transparente y conserva los aromas nacidos en el alambique. El roble, en cambio, trabaja. Una barrica aporta color siguiendo una secuencia que va del limón al oro, luego al ámbar y, muy rara vez, al marrón. Cuanto más nueva es la barrica y más tiempo pasa dentro el destilado, más profundo es el color.","Since every spirit leaves the still dry, any sweetness you notice in the mouth was added afterwards, usually simply as sugar. Watch the wording: here, sweet refers only to the taste of sugar. A whiskey with vanilla and fruity aromas may seem sweet on the nose, but with no added sugar it is still dry. A sweet-smelling nose and a sweet palate are not the same thing.":"Como todo destilado sale seco del alambique, cualquier dulzor que notes en boca se ha añadido después, casi siempre con azúcar. Ojo con las palabras: acá dulce se refiere solo al sabor del azúcar. Un whiskey con aromas de vainilla y fruta puede parecer dulce en nariz, pero si no lleva azúcar añadido sigue siendo seco. Una nariz golosa y un paladar dulce no son lo mismo.","A grape brandy is simply wine that has been distilled, and Cognac is the most famous of them all. It comes from south-west France, from a clearly defined area north of the town of Bordeaux. Only grapes grown there can become Cognac: as with many products tied to a place, the name is a precise address rather than a recipe that can be copied elsewhere.":"Un brandy de uva no es más que vino destilado, y el coñac es el más famoso de todos. Nace en el suroeste de Francia, en una zona bien delimitada al norte de Burdeos. Solo la uva cultivada allá puede convertirse en coñac: como en muchos productos ligados a un territorio, el nombre es una dirección concreta y no una simple receta que se pueda copiar en otro lugar.","The grapes from this area give Cognac its basic aromas, fruity and floral. After harvest they are pressed to release their juice, which is full of sugar and so needs no complicated processing: it is fermented straight away. The result is a wine, and it is this wine, not the grapes, that goes into the still. Before it is a spirit, then, Cognac is a wine.":"Las uvas de esta zona dan al coñac sus aromas de base, afrutados y florales. Tras la vendimia se prensan para liberar el jugo, que es rico en azúcar y por eso no necesita transformaciones complicadas: se pone a fermentar enseguida. El resultado es un vino, y es ese vino, no la uva, lo que entra en el alambique. Antes de ser un destilado, el coñac es, por tanto, un vino.","Grapes pressed, juice fermented straight away into wine.":"Uvas prensadas, jugo fermentado enseguida en vino.","Three label terms show the age, and they always refer to the youngest spirit in the blend. VS guarantees at least 2 years, VSOP at least 4 years, XO at least 10 years. Picture a staircase with three steps: 2, 4 and 10. If a blend contains a 5-year-old and a 20-year-old spirit, it is the 5 that counts.":"En la etiqueta, tres menciones indican la edad, y siempre se refieren al destilado más joven de la mezcla. VS garantiza al menos 2 años, VSOP al menos 4 años y XO al menos 10 años. Imaginá una escalera de tres peldaños: 2, 4 y 10. Si una mezcla lleva un destilado de 5 años y otro de 20, cuenta el de 5.","After distillation, vodka does not go into barrels: it stays unaged and clear. It is then diluted with pure water to bottling strength, typically 40% abv. Think of it as a blank canvas: the producer's whole effort goes into taking away rather than adding, so that what reaches the glass is a clean spirit with almost no smell.":"Tras la destilación, el vodka no pasa por barrica: queda sin envejecer y transparente. Después se rebaja con agua pura hasta el grado de embotellado, normalmente el 40% vol. Pensá en un lienzo en blanco: todo el trabajo del productor busca quitar, no añadir, para que en la copa quede un alcohol limpio y casi sin olor.","A spirit has spent several decades in barrel. Which aromas are most likely?":"Un destilado pasó varias décadas en barrica. ¿Qué aromas es más probable encontrar?","Grape juice distilled without fermentation":"Jugo de uva destilado sin fermentar","Grape juice is fermented into wine, and that wine is distilled.":"El jugo de uva fermenta en vino, y ese vino se destila.","Without fermentation there is no alcohol to distil, so the juice must first become wine. Adding spirit to a wine is not distilling it. And Cognac is made from grapes, not flavoured grain spirit.":"Sin fermentación no hay alcohol que destilar, así que el jugo primero debe convertirse en vino. Añadir alcohol a un vino no es destilarlo. Y el coñac nace de la uva, no de cereales aromatizados.","What happens to the freshly pressed juice destined for Cognac?":"¿Qué ocurre con el jugo recién prensado destinado al coñac?","Grape juice is already full of sugar, so it is fermented into wine right away.":"El jugo de uva ya es rico en azúcar, así que fermenta enseguida en vino.","Distilling before fermentation would leave no alcohol to concentrate. Cooking to create sugar is for raw materials like agave, not grapes. The two years in oak apply to the spirit after distillation, not to the juice.":"Destilar antes de fermentar no daría alcohol que concentrar. La cocción para crear azúcares es para materias primas como el agave, no para la uva. Los dos años en roble se aplican al destilado, tras el alambique, no al jugo.","It adds colour and sweetness by itself":"Agregá por sí solo color y dulzor","From the fermentation of the juice":"De la fermentación del jugo","XO would need even the youngest spirit to be at least 10, and here it is only 5. VS would be allowed, but it is not the highest possible term. The blend is well past the 2-year minimum, so it can carry a term.":"XO exigiría que incluso el destilado más joven tuviera al menos 10 años, y acá solo tiene 5. VS estaría permitido, pero no es la mención más alta posible. La mezcla supera de sobra los 2 años mínimos, así que puede llevar mención.","A wine spirit from the Cognac area, distilled by the rules, has spent 18 months in oak. Can it be sold as Cognac?":"Un destilado de vino de la zona de Cognac, destilado según las normas, pasó 18 meses en roble. ¿Se puede vender como coñac?","Neutral refers to aroma, not alcohol: in fact it is one of the strongest spirits. It has nothing to do with water or where it can be sold; it describes an almost absent smell.":"Neutro se refiere a los aromas, no al alcohol: de hecho, es uno de los destilados más fuertes. No tiene nada que ver con el agua ni con dónde se vende: describí un olor casi inexistente.","Still neutral, but with a little character":"Seguí siendo neutro, pero con algo de carácter","Some vodkas keep a hint of character without ceasing to be vodka. A flavoured vodka has added flavourings, whereas here the grain note comes from the raw material. A whisky would be far more intense and aged in oak.":"Algunos vodkas conservan un toque de carácter sin dejar de ser vodka. Un vodka aromatizado lleva aromas añadidos, mientras que acá el cereal viene de la materia prima. Un whisky tendría aromas mucho más intensos y pasaría por roble.","Whisky always starts with grain, and you can picture it as beer that has been through a still. There is one obstacle, though: a barley grain is dry, hard and packed with starch rather than sugar. Yeast cannot do anything with starch, so it has to be turned into sugar before any fermentation can happen. The classic method lets the barley do almost all of that work itself.":"El whisky nace siempre de cereales, y se puede imaginar como una cerveza que pasó por el alambique. Pero hay un obstáculo: un grano de cebada es seco, duro y está lleno de almidón, no de azúcar. Las levaduras no pueden hacer nada con el almidón, así que antes de fermentar hay que convertirlo en azúcar. El método clásico deja que la propia cebada haga casi todo el trabajo.","Next the malted barley is crushed into a rough flour, and other crushed grains can be added too. Everything is mixed with water, and in this bath the barley's enzymes get to work, converting the starch into sugar. The result is a sweet liquid ready for the yeast. From here the path is the one every spirit follows: fermentation, distillation, then what happens after the still.":"Después la cebada malteada se muele hasta obtener una harina gruesa, a la que se pueden añadir otros cereales molidos. Todo se mezcla con agua: en ese baño, las enzimas de la cebada se ponen a trabajar y convierten el almidón en azúcar. El resultado es un líquido dulce, listo para las levaduras. A partir de acá el camino es el de cualquier destilado: fermentación, destilación y lo que ocurre después del alambique.","Japan built its whisky industry using Scotland as the model. That is why you find both malt and blended whiskies there, just as with Scotch. The traditional style is elegant and refined, precise in its details. In recent years, though, many Japanese producers have been exploring new styles and flavours, and the category keeps evolving.":"Japón construyó su industria del whisky tomando Escocia como modelo. Por eso allá hay whiskies de malta y blended, igual que en el Scotch. El estilo tradicional es elegante y refinado, cuidado hasta el detalle. Sin embargo, en los últimos años muchos productores japoneses exploran estilos y sabores nuevos, y la categoría no deja de evolucionar.","In every spirit, fermentation turns sugar into alcohol, but it also does something else: it creates aromas. Yeast in particular produces fruity scents. In rum this work can take centre stage. By managing fermentation in a certain way, distillers get tropical fruit aromas, such as banana or pineapple, which can become very pronounced.":"En cualquier destilado, la fermentación convierte el azúcar en alcohol, pero hace algo más: creá aromas. Son sobre todo las levaduras las que producen perfumes afrutados. En el ron, este trabajo puede convertirse en protagonista. Gestionando la fermentación de cierta manera, se obtienen aromas de fruta tropical, como plátano o piña, que a veces son muy intensos.","A rum can be aged or not. Time in oak adds vanilla and sweet spice aromas, as well as colour. In some Caribbean countries a period in the barrel is a legal requirement. Unaged rum, by contrast, rests in steel tanks: it stays colourless and keeps the aromas of the freshly distilled spirit.":"Un ron puede envejecerse o no. El paso por roble añade aromas de vainilla y especias dulces, además de color. En algunos países caribeños es obligatorio por ley un periodo en barrica. El ron sin envejecer, en cambio, reposa en depósitos de acero: seguí incoloro y conserva los aromas del destilado recién hecho.","What if a country requires oak but the producer wants a white rum? The answer is charcoal filtering, which removes the colour taken from the wood. The result is a colourless rum that has actually spent time in oak. This is one reason why colour alone cannot tell you how a rum was made.":"¿Y si un país exige barrica pero se quiere un ron blanco? La solución es filtrarlo con carbón, que elimina el color tomado de la madera. Se obtiene así un ron incoloro que en realidad pasó un tiempo en roble. Es uno de los motivos por los que el color, por sí solo, no cuenta cómo se hizo un ron.","All Scotch is distilled in Scotland and aged there for at least three years.":"Todo Scotch se destila en Escocia y envejece allá al menos tres años.","Four years would be long enough, but the place is wrong. The grain used does not change this rule, which applies to every Scotch. The minimum is three years, not ten: the only problem here is geography.":"Cuatro años bastarían en duración, pero el lugar no es el correcto. El cereal usado no cambia esta regla, que vale para todo Scotch. El mínimo es de tres años, no de diez: acá el problema es solo geográfico.","The link with Kentucky is strong because most Bourbon is made there, but it is not a requirement. It is Tennessee whiskey that is tied to one state. Outside the USA, in Canada for example, Bourbon cannot be made.":"La asociación con Kentucky es fuerte porque allá se produce la mayor parte, pero no es obligatoria. Es el Tennessee whiskey el que está ligado a un solo estado. Fuera de Estados Unidos, por ejemplo en Canadá, no se puede hacer Bourbon.","Adds a light maple syrup flavour":"Agregá un ligero sabor a sirope de arce","Adds smoky, peat-like notes":"Agregá notas ahumadas parecidas a la turba","To be Tennessee whiskey it would need maple charcoal filtering and to be made in Tennessee; both are missing here. With 70% corn it cannot be a Rye, which needs 51% rye. And Kentucky is not in Canada.":"Para ser Tennessee whiskey necesitaría el filtrado con carbón de arce y producirse en Tennessee: acá faltan las dos cosas. Con un 70 % de maíz no puede ser un Rye, que exige un 51 % de centeno. Y Kentucky no está en Canadá.","Column stills are only allowed there":"Solo allá se permiten las columnas","Distilled in Scotland and aged there for at least three years.":"Destilado en Escocia y envejecido allá al menos tres años.","At harvest the leaves are cut away, leaving only the core. As with grains, a freshly harvested agave core has no sugar ready to ferment: it has to be processed first. The cores are cooked slowly in ovens until they turn soft and sugars form inside them. Think of a hard potato that you can mash with a fork once it has been cooked: the idea is much the same.":"En la cosecha se cortan las hojas y solo queda el corazón. Como ocurre con los cereales, el corazón recién cosechado no tiene azúcares listos para fermentar: hay que transformarlo. Se cuece lentamente en hornos hasta que se ablanda y en su interior se forman azúcares. Pensá en una patata dura que, una vez cocida, se aplasta con un tenedor: la idea es parecida.","Be careful not to mix this up with ageing: it is only about where the sugars came from. An unaged Tequila can be ‘100% agave’ or not, and the same is true of an oak-aged one. So, in front of a shelf, it pays to read two separate pieces of information: how much agave went in, and how long the spirit has rested.":"Ojo con no confundir esta distinción con el envejecimiento: solo se refiere al origen de los azúcares. Un Tequila sin envejecer puede ser «100% agave» o no, y lo mismo ocurre con uno que pasó por barrica. Así que, delante de una estantería, conviene leer dos datos por separado: cuánto agave lleva y cuánto tiempo ha reposado.","After fermentation comes distillation. Tequila can be made in column stills, but the best ones take another route: they are distilled twice in pot stills and stopped at a notably low strength. Remember the general rule: the lower the distillation strength, the more of the raw material's aromas stay in the spirit.":"Después de la fermentación llega la destilación. El Tequila puede hacerse en columnas, pero los mejores siguen otro camino: se destilan dos veces en alambiques de cobre tradicionales y se detienen a una graduación notablemente baja. Recordá la regla general: cuanto más baja es la graduación de destilación, más aromas de la materia prima conserva el destilado.","A simple way to lock the idea in: pot still, double distillation and low strength mean ‘more agave in the glass’. If a question asks how the most expressive Tequilas are made, the answer lies here, not with tall columns and high strengths. Columns are still allowed, but they generally give Tequilas with less pronounced character.":"Una forma sencilla de fijar la idea: alambique tradicional, doble destilación y graduación baja significan «más agave en la copa». Si una pregunta plantea cómo se consiguen los Tequilas más expresivos, la respuesta está acá, no en las columnas altas ni en las graduaciones elevadas. Las columnas siguen estando permitidas, pero suelen dar Tequilas con un carácter menos marcado.","After distillation the producer decides whether to age the Tequila or leave it as it is. There are two unaged versions. Blanco, also called Silver, is colourless and prized for showing agave at its purest. Joven, also called Oro or Gold, has an attractive golden colour but has never seen a barrel: the colour comes from caramel, and other additives soften its texture.":"Tras la destilación, el productor decide si envejece el Tequila o lo deja tal cual. Hay dos versiones sin envejecer. El Blanco, también llamado Silver, es incoloro y se aprecia porque expresa el agave de la forma más pura. El Joven, también llamado Oro o Gold, tiene un bonito color dorado, pero no pasó por barrica: el color viene del caramelo, y otros aditivos suavizan su textura.","Wine, fruit juice, sugar, yeast":"Vino, jugo de fruta, azúcar, levadura","Caramel is only optional and soda water does not belong. Spirit, cream and colourings describe a cream liqueur instead. Juice and yeast are not part of the recipe, and that list leaves out the spirit, which is required.":"El caramelo es solo opcional y el agua con gas no pinta nada. Destilado, nata y colorantes describen más bien un licor de nata. El jugo y la levadura no forman parte de la receta, y en esa lista falta el destilado, que es obligatorio.","A characterful spirit would bring its own aromas, such as oak, peat or molasses, competing with the recipe. Here the spirit's role is technical, not aromatic.":"Un destilado con carácter aportaría aromas propios, como madera, turba o melaza, que competirían con la receta. Acá el papel del destilado es técnico, no aromático.","The second answer flips the directions. Scotland and Ireland point to whisky, Mexico and the Caribbean to Tequila and rum: those are spirits, while this is about wine-based products.":"La segunda respuesta invierte las direcciones. Escocia e Irlanda remiten al whisky, México y el Caribe al Tequila y al ron: son destilados, mientras que acá se habla de productos a base de vino.","In the mouth, you roll the liquid around for a few seconds, look for the flavours and then spit it out. Spitting is not rude: it lets you taste several samples while staying clear-headed and judge the last one as carefully as the first. In short: small sample, eyes and nose, equal water, nose again, palate, spit.":"En boca, se mueve el líquido unos segundos, se buscan los sabores y después se escupe. Escupir no es de mala educación: permití probar varias muestras con la cabeza despejada y juzgar la última con la misma atención que la primera. En resumen: muestra pequeña, vista y nariz, la misma cantidad de agua, otra vez nariz, boca y escupir.","The weak part softens the power of the alcohol. One source is always there: ice, which melts a little as you stir or shake and adds water. Others are optional and non-alcoholic: fruit juices, cream or milk, sodas, club soda and tonic. Think of a gin and tonic: the gin is the strong part, and the tonic and ice balance it.":"Lo suave suaviza la fuerza del alcohol. Hay una fuente que siempre está: el hielo, que se funde un poco al remover o agitar y añade agua. Otras son opcionales y sin alcohol: zumos de fruta, nata o leche, refrescos, soda y tónica. Pensá en un gin-tonic: la ginebra es lo fuerte, y la tónica y el hielo hacen de contrapeso.","The counterweight is acidity or bitterness. Sourness comes mainly from citrus: a little lime or lemon juice makes the sip lively. Bitterness comes most obviously from cocktail bitters, used by the dash, but also from bitter spirits. It is just like cooking: a pinch of salt or a squeeze of lemon lifts a dish that seemed flat.":"El contrapeso es la acidez o el amargor. Lo ácido viene sobre todo de los cítricos: un poco de jugo de lima o de limón hace el trago más vivo. Lo amargo llega de forma clara con los bitters de cóctel, que se usan por gotas, y también con los destilados amargos. Es como en la cocina: una pizca de sal o un chorrito de limón despiertan un plato que parecía soso.","Short drinks include two families: spirit-forward cocktails, where the spirit leads, such as the Manhattan, and short sours, which combine spirit, citrus and sweetness, such as the Daiquiri. Long drinks have a larger volume: their weak part comes from sodas, juices, dairy or other non-alcoholic drinks. This is where highballs and long sours belong.":"Entre los tragos cortos hay dos familias: los cócteles «spirit-forward», donde manda el destilado, como el Manhattan, y los sours cortos, que combinan destilado, cítricos y dulzor, como el Daiquiri. Los tragos largos tienen más volumen: su parte suave llega de refrescos, zumos, lácteos u otras bebidas sin alcohol. Acá están los highballs y los sours largos.","The short sour rests on a trio: strong, sour, sweet. The basic recipe is a spirit, a citrus juice and an unflavoured sweetener such as simple syrup. These drinks are shaken: the shaker chills, mixes, dilutes a little and gives a light, airy, almost frothy texture. It is the family behind a huge number of successful cocktails.":"El sour corto se apoya en un trío: fuerte, ácido y dulce. La receta básica lleva un destilado, un jugo de cítricos y un endulzante neutro como el jarabe simple. Estas bebidas se agitan: la coctelera enfría, mezcla, diluye un poco y da una textura ligera y aireada, casi espumosa. Es la familia de la que nacen muchísimos cócteles de éxito.","Three classics show the pure pattern. The Daiquiri: rum, lime and simple syrup. The Whiskey Sour: Bourbon or rye, lemon and syrup, with optional egg white and bitters. The Pisco Sour: pisco, lime and syrup, plus one egg white and a dash of bitters. Here the egg white is essential: it creates a foam head and a silky texture. Many bars now use aquafaba, the water chickpeas are cooked in, as a vegan alternative.":"Tres clásicos muestran el esquema puro. El Daiquiri: ron, lima y jarabe simple. El Whiskey Sour: Bourbon o rye, limón y jarabe, con clara de huevo y bitters opcionales. El Pisco Sour: pisco, lima y jarabe, más una clara y unas gotas de bitters. Acá la clara es imprescindible: creá una capa de espuma y una textura sedosa. Muchos bares usan hoy el aquafaba, el agua de cocción de los garbanzos, como alternativa vegana.","The highball is the simplest of all mixed drinks: a spirit and a non-alcoholic mixer, served long over cubed ice. Gin and tonic, vodka and tonic, whisky and soda are examples almost everyone knows without realising they form a family. The rule is clear: little work, plenty of volume, and the weak part handed over to the mixer.":"El highball es la más sencilla de todas las mezclas: un destilado y una bebida sin alcohol, servidos en vaso alto con hielo en cubitos. Gin-tonic, vodka con tónica o whisky con soda son ejemplos que casi todo el mundo conoce sin saber que forman una familia. La regla es clara: poco trabajo, mucho volumen y la parte suave en manos del refresco o el jugo.","Some highballs have their own names. The Cuba Libre is rum and cola with lime. The Greyhound is vodka and grapefruit juice: the slightly bitter, sour juice acts as the modifier. These are summer-afternoon drinks, easy to make at home with ingredients found anywhere, yet built on the same logic of balance as more complex cocktails.":"Algunos highballs tienen nombre propio. El Cuba Libre es ron y cola con lima. El Greyhound es vodka y jugo de pomelo: el jugo, ligeramente amargo y ácido, hace de modificador. Son bebidas de tarde de verano, fáciles de preparar en casa con ingredientes que se encuentran en cualquier parte, pero construidas con la misma lógica de equilibrio que los cócteles más complejos.","Cuba Libre: rum, cola and lime. Greyhound: vodka and grapefruit juice.":"Cuba Libre: ron, cola y lima. Greyhound: vodka y jugo de pomelo.","The long sour covers several sub-families: Collinses, Slings and sparkling sours. In its simplest form it is a short sour made long with club soda. The Tom Collins is the perfect example: gin, lemon juice and simple syrup, poured over ice and topped with soda. It is refreshing and thirst-quenching, and shows clearly how one recipe can change its outfit.":"El sour largo reúne varias subfamilias: los Collins, los Sling y los sours espumosos. En su forma más simple es un sour corto alargado con soda. El Tom Collins es el ejemplo perfecto: ginebra, jugo de limón y jarabe simple, servidos sobre hielo y completados con soda. Es refrescante, quita la sed y muestra muy bien cómo una misma receta puede cambiar de aspecto.","Instead of club soda you can use a flavoured soda or Champagne. The Paloma combines tequila and lime with a Mexican-style grapefruit soda, which brings sweetness and bubbles at once; alternatively, grapefruit juice and soda water are used. The French 75 starts from Cognac or gin, lemon and simple syrup, and is topped with Champagne: an elegant sparkling sour.":"En lugar de soda se puede usar un refresco aromatizado o Champagne. La Paloma combina tequila y lima con un refresco de pomelo de estilo mexicano, que aporta a la vez dulzor y burbujas; como alternativa se usan jugo de pomelo y soda. El French 75 parte de Cognac o ginebra, limón y jarabe simple, y se completa con Champagne: un sour espumoso y elegante.","The citrus juice":"El jugo de cítricos","A cocktail is often sweetened first and then balanced by a modifier, such as citrus juice or bitters. A garnish is mainly decorative or aromatic, the base spirit is the strong part, and the sweetener is exactly what the modifier has to offset.":"A menudo un cóctel se endulza primero y luego se equilibra con un modificador, como jugo de cítricos o bitters. La decoración es sobre todo visual o aromática, el destilado base es la parte fuerte y el endulzante es justo lo que el modificador debe compensar.","Sweetened lemon juice":"Jugo de limón endulzado","Dissolving sugar in water makes it easy to mix into a cold cocktail. Lemon juice is a sour ingredient, orange liqueur is a flavoured, alcoholic sweetener and vermouth is an aromatised wine: none of them is 'simple'.":"Disolver el azúcar en agua permite mezclarlo fácilmente en un cóctel frío. El jugo de limón es un ingrediente ácido, el licor de naranja un endulzante aromatizado y con alcohol, y el vermut un vino aromatizado: ninguno es «simple».","Add a little citrus juice or a dash of bitters":"Añadir un poco de jugo de cítricos o unas gotas de bitters","Lemon juice instead of bitters":"Jugo de limón en lugar de bitters","Both drinks share the whiskey base and Angostura bitters; the Manhattan replaces the sugar cube with vermouth, which also brings bitter and sour nuances. It remains a short spirit-forward drink: no citrus, soda or cream, which belong to sours, long drinks and the Alexander family respectively.":"Ambos comparten la base de whiskey y los bitters Angostura; el Manhattan cambia el terrón de azúcar por vermut, que también aporta matices amargos y ácidos. Seguí siendo un trago corto spirit-forward: sin cítricos, soda ni nata, que corresponden a los sours, los tragos largos y los Alexander.","Grapefruit juice and ginger ale":"Jugo de pomelo y ginger ale","Vodka and lemon juice":"Vodka y jugo de limón","Spirit, citrus juice, simple syrup":"Destilado, jugo de cítricos, jarabe simple","Lime juice":"El jugo de lima","Both use grapefruit juice":"Ambos usan jugo de pomelo","Both use orange juice":"Ambos usan jugo de naranja","Vodka and grapefruit juice":"Vodka y jugo de pomelo","The Greyhound is a highball of vodka and grapefruit juice.":"El Greyhound es un highball de vodka y jugo de pomelo.","It mixes lemon juice and lime juice":"Mezcla jugo de limón y jugo de lima","The Paloma is tequila and lime topped with grapefruit soda; alternatively, grapefruit juice and soda water can be used. Triple sec sweetens the Margarita, Champagne tops the French 75 and ginger ale goes into the Horse's Neck.":"La Paloma es tequila y lima completados con refresco de pomelo; como alternativa se pueden usar jugo de pomelo y soda. El triple sec endulza la Margarita, el Champagne completa el French 75 y el ginger ale va en el Horse's Neck."});
